key', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff7cf16-c065-5f78-bea7-18d046cd894d', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff7cf16-c065-5f78-bea7-18d046cd894d'}, {'abstract': 'Situated within walking distance of the Fairfield train station, the Brasserie has loads of character and comfortably spaced tables.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/01/nyregion/the-brasserie-in-fairfield-cheerful-and-french.html', 'snippet': 'Situated within walking distance of the Fairfield train station, the Brasserie has loads of character and comfortably spaced tables.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE BRASSERIE is a cheerful, attractive French restaurant within walking distance of the Fairfield train station. It has loads of character: exposed brick walls and a large blackboard listing handwritten specials. Tables are comfortably spaced, and the single-page menu offers a variety of appealing choices — French and not-so-French — like tapas, burgers, frog’s legs, bouillabaisse and short ribs. But as I watched the restaurant fill almost to capacity on a recent Saturday evening, I wondered if the rest of the room knew something I didn’t.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/01/nyregion/01DINECT1/01DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/01/nyregion/01DINECT1/01DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/01/nyregion/01DINECT1/01DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', '