irector.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/theater/arian-moayed-is-acclaimed-for-bengal-tiger-and-waterwell.html', 'snippet': 'Arian Moayed, appearing on Broadway in “Bengal Tiger at the Baghdad Zoo,” also has his hand in many other projects, including productions at Waterwell, where he is artistic director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arian Moayed is busy — like James Franco busy. Eight times a week he takes to the stage at the Richard Rodgers Theater, playing Musa, an Iraqi translator, with Robin Williams in “Bengal Tiger at the Baghdad Zoo,” Mr. Moayed’s Broadway debut. In between shows he squeezes in time with his girlfriend, Krissy Shields, and their daughters, 2-year-old Olive Joon and 3-month-old Ivy Shireen. Sleep is not exactly a priority.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/sub-waterwall/sub-waterwall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/sub-waterwall/sub-waterwall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/sub-waterwall/sub-waterwall-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Starry-Eyed to Star', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Starry-Eyed to Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waterwell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-01T22:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname