 labyrinthine paths of the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four bodies were discarded and hidden in the deep brush along Ocean Parkway on Long Island over a three-year period. They were all women, thought to have been killed by the same person.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/yjpcraigslist1/yjpcraigslist1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pursuit of Killer, Police Mine Online Clues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Pursuit Of Killer, Police Mine Online Clues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Craigslist', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Suffolk County (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T02:19:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae2d9bbe-1a5e-5909-aa35-8b50fe300366', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae2d9bbe-1a5e-5909-aa35-8b50fe300366'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cohen, a filmmaker, photographer and poet, ranged from his artists’ salon on the Lower East Side to pilgrimages to Marrakesh, Katmandu and the banks of the Ganges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/arts/ira-cohen-an-artist-and-a-touchstone-dies-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cohen, a filmmaker, photographer and poet, ranged from his artists’ salon on the Lower East Side to pilgrimages to Marrakesh, Katmandu and the banks of the Ganges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ira Cohen made phantasmagorical films that became cult classics. He developed a way of taking photographs in mesmerizing, twisting colors, including a famous one of Jimi Hendrix. He published works by authors like William Burroughs and the poet Gregory Corso. He wrote thousands of poems himself. He wrote “The Hashish Cookbook” under the name Panama Rose. He called himself “the conscience of Planet Earth.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/cohen-obit/cohen-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/cohen-obit/cohen-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/cohen-obit/cohen-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ira Cohen, an Artist and a Touchstone, Dies at 76', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ira Cohen Is Dead at 76; An Artist and a Touchstone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Ira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T02:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff2e35d-d6d2-58f6-b52c-b38655a16d11', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff2e35d-d6d2-58f6-b52c-b38655a16d11'}, {'abstract': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/business/02ahead.html', 'snippet': 'Economic reports, corporate earnings and hearings this week in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include the Institute for Supply Management manufacturing index for April, and construction spending for March (Monday); vehicle sales for April and factory orders for March (Tuesday); the ADP employment report and I.S.M. service index for April (Wednesday); same-store retail sales for April, first-quarter productivity and weekly jobless claims (Thursday); and unemployment for April and consumer credit for March \xa0(Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Ahead to Economic Reports This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'LOOKING AHEAD', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T02:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'per