er a rambling speech from Colonel Qaddafi on state television on Saturday in which he insisted that his forces were not killing civilians, evidence to the contrary was found in Misurata.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MISURATA, Libya — On the night he would die, Muhammad Abdulhamid Sbikhee, a night watchman at a local school, was at home with his wife and their seven children. They shared a small, ground-floor apartment that opened to a tiny yard that opened in turn to an urban dirt alley.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/world/MISURATA-1/MISURATA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/02/world/MISURATA-1/MISURATA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/world/MISURATA-1/MISURATA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/world/MISURATA-1/MISURATA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/02/world/MISURATA-1/MISURATA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shell in Misurata Adds to a City’s Grim Toll', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Libya’s Denials, Rising Toll in Misurata', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Misurata (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T02:39:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a47a3aef-0991-5310-957a-21890b5bb782', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a47a3aef-0991-5310-957a-21890b5bb782'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede presents a live video stream from the White House Web site of President Barack Obama’s upcoming address to the American people, said to concern national security.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/01/live-video-of-president-obamas-address/', 'snippet': 'The Lede presents a live video stream from the White House Web site of President Barack Obama’s upcoming address to the American people, said to concern national security.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:44 p.m. Update: President Obama’s remarks have now concluded. As soon as an archived copy of the video is available, it will be posted on The Lede. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Video of President Obama’s Address', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T02:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization'