aring the same message that had just been transmitted to the White House press corps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Bin Laden Announcement Leaked Out', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pfeiffer, Daniel H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T03:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6fdd3a9-2426-5123-b78e-a2c128c63f24', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6fdd3a9-2426-5123-b78e-a2c128c63f24'}, {'abstract': 'Osama bin Laden has been killed, a United States official said Sunday night. President Obama is expected to make an announcement on Sunday night, almost 10 years after the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/01/bin-laden-dead-u-s-official-says/', 'snippet': 'Osama bin Laden has been killed, a United States official said Sunday night. President Obama is expected to make an announcement on Sunday night, almost 10 years after the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON —President Obama announced late Sunday that Osama bin Laden, the leader of Al Qaeda responsible for the Sept. 11 attacks, was killed in a firefight during an operation he ordered Sunday inside Pakistan, ending a 10-year manhunt for the world’s most wanted terrorist. American officials were in possession of his body, he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Announces Killing of Osama bin Laden', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T03:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2263d234-4595-535a-bbee-ca629953ad48', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2263d234-4595-535a-bbee-ca629953ad48'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats and Republicans agree on the need for controls on deficit spending but struggle over what they should be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/us/politics/02congress.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats and Republicans agree on the need for controls on deficit spending but struggle over what they should be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With Congress returning this week to confront an administration demand to raise the federal debt limit, Democrats and Republicans are in general agreement that the step should be accompanied by new controls on deficit spending but face a wrenching struggle over what those controls should be.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 