52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62cbae9-db7c-5682-9601-376212eab700'}, {'abstract': 'Within moments of President Obama completing his statement Sunday night, lawmakers and two former presidents offer their reactions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/after-killing-of-bin-laden-reaction-pours-in/', 'snippet': 'Within moments of President Obama completing his statement Sunday night, lawmakers and two former presidents offer their reactions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within moments of President Obama‘s statement late Sunday night announcing the death of Osama bin Laden, reaction from across the globe began to pour in:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Killing of Bin Laden, Official Reaction Pours In', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T04:32:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/be2e6725-cb71-5053-90c1-d8404a3d8032', 'word_count': 1553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be2e6725-cb71-5053-90c1-d8404a3d8032'}, {'abstract': 'Crowds chanted in Washington and Times Square, while officers raised their fists near the World Trade Center site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/nyregion/amid-cheers-a-message-they-will-be-caught.html', 'snippet': 'Crowds chanted in Washington and Times Square, while officers raised their fists near the World Trade Center site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the midnight darkness, the crowds gathered, chanting and cheering, waving American flags, outside the front gates of the White House. In Times Square, tourists poured out of nearby hotels and into the streets early Monday morning to celebrate with strangers. And in the shadow of the World Trade Center site, as the news of Osama bin Laden’s killing by American special forces spread, a police car drove north on Church Street blaring the sound of bagpipes from open windows. Officers raised clenched fists in the air. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/react/react-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/react/react-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/react/react-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/react/react-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/react/react-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Cheers, a Message: ‘They Will Be Caught’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Cheers, a Message: ‘They Will Be Caught’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-