ASHINGTON -- President Obama’s announcement late Sunday that Osama bin Laden had been killed delivered not only a long-awaited prize to the United States, but also a significant victory for Mr. Obama, whose foreign policy has been the subject of persistent criticism by his rivals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President’s Vow Fulfilled', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President&#8217;s Vow Fulfilled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T04:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba17d5c2-ece7-5afa-a0da-17504288b84a', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba17d5c2-ece7-5afa-a0da-17504288b84a'}, {'abstract': 'News of Osama bin Laden’s death was broken in a Twitter post by the chief of staff for Donald Rumsfeld, the former defense secretary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/business/media/02media.html', 'snippet': 'News of Osama bin Laden’s death was broken in a Twitter post by the chief of staff for Donald Rumsfeld, the former defense secretary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The terse announcement came just after 9:45 p.m. Sunday from Dan Pfeiffer, the White House communications director. “Potus to address the nation tonight at 10:30 PM Eastern Time,” he wrote on Twitter, sharing the same message that had just been transmitted to the White House press corps.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Social Networking Sites, Presidential Mystery Does Not Wait for the President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Social Networking Sites, Presidential Mystery Does Not Wait for the President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T04:51:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7e91d8-4bc1-5935-a5fb-000eb47fd4cb', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7e91d8-4bc1-5935-a5fb-000eb47fd4cb'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama announced Sunday night that Osama bin Laden, the leader of Al Qaeda responsible for the Sept. 11 attacks, had been killed. (Video via MSNBC)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000000799358/obama-announces-death-of-osama-bin-laden.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama announced Sunday night that Osama bin Laden, the leader of Al Qaeda responsible for the Sept. 11 attacks, had been killed. (Video via MSNBC)', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama announced S