tracked to a compound so secure that officials guessed it was built to hide someone far more important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/world/asia/02reconstruct-capture-osama-bin-laden.html', 'snippet': 'After eight months of intelligence work, Osama bin Laden’s most trusted courier was tracked to a compound so secure that officials guessed it was built to hide someone far more important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After years of dead ends and promising leads gone cold, the big break came last August. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detective Work on Courier Led to Breakthrough on Bin Laden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detective Work on Courier Led to Breakthrough on Bin Laden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuwaiti, Abu Ahmed al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abbottabad (Pakistan)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T06:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti and Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1426133-4bd0-5c4b-a307-a7c0d4d06d59', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1426133-4bd0-5c4b-a307-a7c0d4d06d59'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department issued a warning to “U.S. citizens traveling and residing abroad to the enhanced potential for anti-American violence.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/world/02warning-americans-abroad-.html', 'snippet': 'The State Department issued a warning to “U.S. citizens traveling and residing abroad to the enhanced potential for anti-American violence.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States government warned American expatriates and travelers abroad early Monday of possible reprisals against them over the killing of Osama bin Laden, who was shot to death in a firefight with American forces in Pakistan on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Warns Americans Abroad of Possible Reprisals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Warns Americans Abroad of Possible Reprisals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T06:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d576c358-f6a2-5f09-aa86-d5b64e388554', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d576c358-f6a2-5f09-aa86-d5b64e388554'}, {'abstract': 'Osama bin Laden, the mastermind of the most devastating attack on American soil in modern times and the most hunted man in the world, was killed in a firefight with United States forces in Pakistan on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/02/world/20110502-osama-timeline.html', 'snippet': 'Osama bin Laden, the mastermind of the most devastating attack on American soil in modern times and the most hunted man in the world, was killed in a firefight with United States forces in Pakistan on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Osama bin Laden, the mastermind of the most devastating attack on American soil in modern times and the most hunted man in the world, was killed in a firefight with United States forces in Pakistan on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milestones: Osama Bin Laden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T06:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f6b66482-6772-57e7-8370-96594b759d95', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f6b66482-6772-57e7-8370-96594b759d95'}, {'abstract': 'Senior political figures cautioned that the killing did not necessarily mean an immediate victory over the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/asia/03afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Senior political figures cautioned that the killing did not necessarily mean an immediate victory over the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — In Afghanistan, where Osama bin Laden was based for many years and where Al Qaeda helped to train and pay insurgents, there was relief and uncertainty about how his death would play out in the fraught regional power politics now shaping the war. While senior political figures welcomed the news of his death, they cautioned that it did not necessarily translate into an immediate military victory over the Taliban, and urged the United States and NATO not to use it as a reason to withdraw. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghans Fear West May See Death as the End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghans Fear U.S. and NATO May View Bin Laden’s Death as the End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zawahri, Ayman Al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omar, Muhammad (Taliban Leader)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Taiba', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T07:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a35aad1-193a-54d2-87eb-abf4352f4f0e', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a35aad1-193a-54d2-87eb-abf4352f4f0e'}, {'abstract': 'In the charged world of top-level soccer, a royal wedding tribute sewn onto the shirt of the Glasgow Rangers