nt': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/504c2ea3-b3d5-5c09-b314-88852fb17756'}, {'abstract': 'The economic recovery in the United States has not revived the job market — and may not, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/super-sad-true-jobs-story/', 'snippet': 'The economic recovery in the United States has not revived the job market — and may not, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy Folbre is an economics professor at the University of Massachusetts Amherst.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Super Sad True Jobs Story', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Immelt, Jeffrey R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on Jobs and Competitiveness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T10:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Folbre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Folbre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/63253952-c74d-5880-ad11-6ab9bfc5027b', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63253952-c74d-5880-ad11-6ab9bfc5027b'}, {'abstract': 'Though Ai Weiwei, the detained Chinese artist, was absent from the Gallery Weekend Berlin, his exhibition will continue into June is at Galerie Neugerriemschneider.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/berlin-gallery-spotlights-ai-weiwei-detained-chinese-artist/', 'snippet': 'Though Ai Weiwei, the detained Chinese artist, was absent from the Gallery Weekend Berlin, his exhibition will continue into June is at Galerie Neugerriemschneider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual Gallery Weekend Berlin, which just finished its seventh iteration, welcomed a deluge of collectors, curators and artists to the city for a three-day marathon of 44 official openings and countless other events. One important artist was absent from the festivities: Ai Weiwei, the detained Chinese artist, whose exhibition will continue into June\xa0 at Galerie Neugerriemschneider.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Berlin Gallery Spotlights Ai Weiwei, Detained Chinese Artist', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T10:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emilie Trice', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emilie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trice', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/913e5616-c60e-5106-ac9a-2ed6872852d9', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/913e5616-c60e-5106-ac9a-2ed6872852d9'}, {'abstract': 'The ghosts of “Studio 60″: Why is someone gently skewering a failed show that was canceled four years ago?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/the-ghost-and-cult-of-studio-60-on-the-sunset-strip/', 'snippet': 'The ghosts of “Studio 60″: Why is someone gently skewering a failed show that was canceled four years ago?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2006, “Studio 60 on the Sunset Strip” made its debut on NBC, and the show was intriguing for several reasons. One, it was created by arguably TV’s most revered auteur at the time, Aaron Sorkin, who was more-or-less fresh off “The West Wing,” a paragon of snappy-pattered, makes-you-feel-smart-just-for-watching television. Two, “Studio 60″ was about comedy: specifically, late-night comedy and, presumably, “Saturday Night Live.” (“Studio 60″ was the name of a fictional, live, late-night sketch-comedy show produced out of Los Angeles.) Third, in a weird coincidence, “Studio 60″ premiered the same year, on the same network, as the similarly numerically titled “30 Rock,” which is also sort-of about “Saturday Night Live” and is written by the ex-“S.N.L.” head writer Tina Fey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ghost, and Cult, of ‘Studio 60 on the Sunset Strip’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T10:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6949eb79-4f3a-52bb-b662-fa8e3375578b', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6949eb79-4f3a-52bb-b662-fa8e3375578b'}, {'abstract': 'May 2, 2011 - Mark Mazzetti on how U.S. intelligence agencies tracked and then killed the founder of the Al Qaeda terrorist network.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/100000000799521/timescast--the-search-for-bin-laden.html', 'snippet': 'May 2, 2011 - Mark Mazzetti on how U.S. intelligence agencies tracked and then killed the founder of the Al Qaeda terrorist network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 2, 2011 - Mark Mazzetti on 