'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee76f64d-392a-5f5b-a836-55d32150763f', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee76f64d-392a-5f5b-a836-55d32150763f'}, {'abstract': 'Mixed prospects for a more liberal Arab world.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/how-hot-will-the-arab-summer-be/', 'snippet': 'Mixed prospects for a more liberal Arab world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a nice piece by Asef Bayat in Foreign Affairs last week on “The Post-Islamist Revolutions.” Bayat — born and raised in Iran, educated in Britain, professor at Leiden then the University of Illinois — makes the first convincing (rather than wishful) argument I’ve seen that the Arab Spring is likely to usher in relatively liberal, though religiously inflected, societies. The article makes a nice pairing with another recent Foreign Affairs piece by Michael Scott Doran, which takes Iran and Syria seriously as a kind of “anticolonialist” bloc single-mindedly focused on undermining the United States. It is perhaps a slightly paranoid or excited piece, but it is paranoid about something that the United States, as a noncolonial and indeed anticolonial power, habitually underestimates in its foreign policy, namely the enduring political power of anticolonial feeling in a post-colonial world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Hot Will the Arab Summer Be?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Gideon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tepperman, Jonathan D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Malcomson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malcomson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/589ee01f-7795-5684-8902-a551d13dc565', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/589ee01f-7795-5684-8902-a551d13dc565'}, {'abstract': 'Send us photos of bird habitats in your local park, neighborhood, on your window ledge or fire escape.  No nest is too small, too fancy, or overgrown.   Five boroughs only, please.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/bird-week-send-us-photos-of-nyc-bird-habitats/', 'snippet': 'Send us photos of bird habitats in your local park, neighborhood, on your window ledge or fire escape.  No nest is too small, too fancy, or overgrown.   Five boroughs only, please.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bird Week | Send Us Photos of New York City Habitats', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e59b9af6-8d83-5232-8e8a-5929023fb331', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e59b9af6-8d83-5232-8e8a-5929023fb331'}, {'abstract': 'The deal for the biopharmaceutical company comes just weeks after Cephalon rejected a $5.7 billion takeover bid from Valeant Pharmaceuticals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/teva-to-buy-cephalon-for-6-8-billion/', 'snippet': 'The deal for the biopharmaceutical company comes just weeks after Cephalon rejected a $5.7 billion takeover bid from Valeant Pharmaceuticals.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:30 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teva to Buy Cephalon for $6.8 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cephalon Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/56b400ca-a9b0-5b62-b5ba-f9b47852f15e', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56b400ca-a9b0-5b62-b5ba-f9b47852f15e'}, {'abstract': 'Students 13 and older: Please share your reactions to the killing of Osama bin Laden by American forces.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/what-is-your-reaction-to-the-death-of-osama-bin-laden/', 'snippet': 'Students 13 and older: Please share your reactions to the killing of Osama bin Laden by American forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president announced last night that al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden was killed in a United States military operation. What is your response to the news? Do you think it means that the United States is safer now from terrorism? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Your Reaction to the Death of Osama bin Laden?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:37:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbc0a70-7b23-5f4d-9d0b-9d0467d8ff71', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbc0a70-7b23-5f4d-9d0b-9d0467d8ff71'}, {'abstract': 'In a speech almost 18 months before he assumed the presidency, Barack Obama made a statement that was eerily prescient.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/in-bin-laden-announcement-echoes-of-2007-obama-speech/', 'snippet': 'In a speech almost 18 months before he assumed the presidency, Barack Obama made a statement that was eerily prescient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a speech almost 18 months before he assumed the presidency, Barack Obama issued a blunt warning to President Pervez Musharaff of Pakistan: “If we have actionable intelligence about high-value terrorist targets and President Musharraf won’t act, we will.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bin Laden Announcement, Echoes of 2007 Obama Speech', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9569c67d-247b-5c77-8fb9-66c08c651765', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9569c67d-247b-5c77-8fb9-66c08c651765'}, {'abstract': 'Community Health Systems on Monday increased its bid for Tenet Healthcare to $7.25 a share from $6, in the latest effort to win over the reluctant company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/community-health-raises-bid-for-tenet/', 'snippet': 'Community Health Systems on Monday increased its bid for Tenet Healthcare to $7.25 a share from $6, in the latest effort to win over the reluctant company.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:42 a.m. | Updated Community Health Systems on Monday increased its bid for Tenet Healthcare to $7.25 a share from $6, in the latest effort to win over the reluctant company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Community Health Raises Bid for Tenet', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0af2304b-85ee-55e1-a389-2e55aaff0314', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0af2304b-85ee-55e1-a389-2e55aaff0314'}, {'abstract': 'A man who once vowed to liberate the Arab world was reduced to a footnote in the revolutions and uprisings remaking a region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/middleeast/03arab.html', 'snippet': 'A man who once vowed to liberate the Arab world was reduced to a footnote in the revolutions and uprisings remaking a region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The words were not uncommon in angry Arab capitals a decade ago. Osama bin Laden was hero, sheik, even leader to some. After his death Monday, a man who once vowed to liberate the Arab world was reduced to a footnote in the revolutions and uprisings remaking a region that he and his men had struggled to understand.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/03arab/03arab-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Arab World, Bin Laden’s Confused Legacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Arab World, Now a Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T11:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af0bdb84-b895-5d25-a6c3-43edbf2a2d65', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af0bdb84-b895-5d25-a6c3-43edbf2a2d65'}, {'abstract': 'How has your life been affected? And what do you think America and its allies should do now, in Afghanistan, Pakistan, Iraq and elsewhere?', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/thoughts-on-bin-ladens-death-after-10-years-at-war/', 'snippet': 'How has your life been affected? And what do you think America and its allies should do now, in Afghanistan, Pakistan, Iraq and elsewhere?', 'lead_paragraph': ' It has been nearly a decade since Osama bin Laden’s Al Qaeda carried out the most devastating attack on American soil. Many of our readers are in the armed forces and have had their lives changed profoundly since that day in September 2001. We would like to hear from you. Share your thoughts about the news of Bin Laden’s death and how the post-9/11 world has affected your life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thoughts on Bin Laden’s Death After 10 Years at War', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T12:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10a5f54-de8c-538b-b713-45af0932c683', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10a5f54-de8c-538b-b713-45af0932c683'}, {'abstract': 'Chants of “U-S-A! U-S-A!” rang out well past midnight from the rowdy crowd gathered at Vesey and Church Streets, near the World Trade Center site.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/morning-buzz-celebration-and-vigilance-after-bin-ladens-death/', 'snippet': 'Chants of “U-S-A! U-S-A!” rang out well past midnight from the rowdy crowd gathered at Vesey and Church Streets, near the World Trade Center site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cloudy with a chance of afternoon showers. The high temperature will be about 64 degrees. A good day to spend reading some good news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Celebration, and Vigilance, After Bin Laden’s Death', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T12:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Tomassini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tomassini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c296abae-a87c-5d06-a7aa-2595c83f624f', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c296abae-a87c-5d06-a7aa-2595c83f624f'}, {'abstract': 'The takeover would create one of the largest coal producers in the world and a powerhouse in the production of steel-making coal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/arch-coal-to-acquire-icg-in-3-4-billion-deal/', 'snippet': 'The takeover would create one of the largest coal producers in the world and a powerhouse in the production of steel-making coal.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:40 p.m. | Updated Arch Coal said on Monday that it would buy the International Coal Group for $3.4 billion in cash, creating one of the world’s largest coal producers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arch Coal to Buy International Coal for $3.4 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCH COAL INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value':