 terrorist was the truly fundamental nature of his motive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thing that scared us most about Osama bin Laden, I think, was what seemed to be his — and many of his acolytes’ — rational mega-murderousness. In American action thrillers, the bad guys sometimes used what appeared to be blind terrifying terrorism as a guise for merely felonious behavior. (The “Die Hard” franchise nearly always centered on that construction.) But here were engineers and others with advanced degrees whose obsession was an end to modernism and a return to primal law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Thing That Scared Us', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T12:46:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5453994-39a4-5827-a4d3-ddb97c49214f', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5453994-39a4-5827-a4d3-ddb97c49214f'}, {'abstract': 'Why is this a surprise?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/a-commodity-peak/', 'snippet': 'Why is this a surprise?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WSJ: Commodity Surprise: Some Are Now Heading Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Commodity Peak?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T12:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bebf36ab-9257-536c-bbd0-9cabf6d930fe', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bebf36ab-9257-536c-bbd0-9cabf6d930fe'}, {'abstract': 'The new documentary about Yves Saint Laurent and Pierre Bergé, including this hilarious clip where the designer takes a Proust questionnaire.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/yves-and-pierre-crazy-in-love/', 'snippet': 'The new documentary about Yves Saint Laurent and Pierre Bergé, including this hilarious clip where the designer takes a Proust questionnaire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many moments to love in “L’Amour Fou,” the new documentary about Yves Saint Laurent and Pierre Bergé, including every time that Betty Catroux opens her mouth and Bergé’s poetic recollections of his life with Saint Laurent, a 52-year relationship that he refers to as “une grande histoire d’amour.” Directed by Pierre Thoretton, the film also features rare archival footage, not the least of which is this hilarious video interview in which an uncharacteristically unguarded (and frisky) Saint Laurent takes a Proust questionnaire. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yves and Pierre, Crazy in Love', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Horacio Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Horacio', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/22fe2824-0201-5377-a359-20649fb0222a', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22fe2824-0201-5377-a359-20649fb0222a'}, {'abstract': 'Rent the Runway, a New York start-up that lets women rent designer dresses, has grown to a million members and recently began turning a profit.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/rent-the-runway-takes-flight/', 'snippet': 'Rent the Runway, a New York start-up that lets women rent designer dresses, has grown to a million members and recently began turning a profit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Rent the Runway, a New York start-up hoping to make high-end fashion as accessible as renting a movie from Netflix, first introduced its service in late 2009, it wasn’t clear how successful the venture would be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rent the Runway Takes Flight', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rent the Runway', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T13:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5fc13a8-f5e6-51e2-ab1c-7437c8ebfbba', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5fc13a8-f5e6-51e2-ab1c-7437c8ebfbba'}, {'abstract': 'Lot18, a New York start-up that sells wine online, announced on Monday that it had raised money to expand its business, particularly to scout wine overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/lot18-raises-more-cash-to-sell-wine-online/', 'snippet': 'Lot18, a New York start-up that sells wine online, announced on Monday that it had raised money to expand its business, particularly to scout wine overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The online sample sale model that has helped bolster companies like Gilt, ideeli, HauteCouture and RueLaLa, isn’t limited to luxury clothing and jewelry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lot18 Raises More Cash to Sell Wine Online', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T13:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d92f47da-035f-5eab-8602-56c8dd8c466a', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d92f47da-035f-5eab-8602-56c8dd8c466a'}, {'abstract': 'More falsehoods in the Ryan plan.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/the-fehb-deception/', 'snippet': 'More falsehoods in the Ryan plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Pear:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The FEHB Deception', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T13:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c665a01b-be87-59e4-b864-ea910c222a02', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c665a01b-be87-59e4-b864-ea910c222a02'}, {'abstract': 'Karsan’s ouster leaves the city’s Taxi of Tomorrow competition with two contenders, the Ford Transit Connect and the Nissan NV200 vans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/nyregion/karsan-from-turkey-is-rejected-as-new-york-taxi.html', 'snippet': 'Karsan’s ouster leaves the city’s Taxi of Tomorrow competition with two contenders, the Ford Transit Connect and the Nissan NV200 vans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Karsan V1, an oblong Turkish van vying to become the exclusive vehicle of the New York City taxi fleet, has features that would make a Crown Victoria weep: London-style jump seats; a moon roof for panoramic views; even a pledge to build the cars in Brooklyn. (The Crown Vic, the fleet’s old mainstay, was made in Canada.)', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/taxi/taxi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/taxi/taxi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/taxi/taxi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/taxi/taxi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/02/nyregion/taxi/taxi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Contest for New Y