n more than 20 deceased players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The suicide of the former Chicago Bears star Dave Duerson became more alarming Monday,\xa0when Boston University researchers announced that his brain had developed the same trauma-induced disease recently found in more than 20 deceased players.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/01/sports/football/0duersonpix/0duersonpix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/01/sports/football/0duersonpix/0duersonpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/01/sports/football/0duersonpix/0duersonpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Duerson’s Brain Trauma Diagnosed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Duerson’s Brain Trauma Diagnosed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duerson, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Traumatic Encephalopathy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T15:17:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1362924c-eaca-5ccd-9ac1-da6a9e22fe0d', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1362924c-eaca-5ccd-9ac1-da6a9e22fe0d'}, {'abstract': 'With the Ohio River rising, officials blew a gap in a levee, sending 550,000 cubic feet of water a second across 130,000 acres of farmland to try to save one Illinois town from flooding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/us/03levee.html', 'snippet': 'With the Ohio River rising, officials blew a gap in a levee, sending 550,000 cubic feet of water a second across 130,000 acres of farmland to try to save one Illinois town from flooding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST PRAIRIE, Mo. — Ruben Bennett, his back bent and his fingers gnarled from a lifetime of labor, has lived all of his 88 years on an expanse of rich farmland here, just below where the Ohio River pours into the Mississippi. He survived his share of floods — including the record-setting one that swept away his boyhood home — but he has never run from one, until now. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/us/jp-LEVEE/jp-LEVEE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/us/jp-LEVEE/jp-LEVEE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w