s', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolin, Neal S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T15:39:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c9dfbf-7642-5322-a2f7-c869136c23d7', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c9dfbf-7642-5322-a2f7-c869136c23d7'}, {'abstract': 'What to tell the children when there are no words?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/raising-the-911-generation/', 'snippet': 'What to tell the children when there are no words?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parenting is about preserving the past and facing the future. There’s little time to think in those lofty terms during the tumult of a usual day, of course. But every so often we have a day like today, a reminder of how all “where were you when” moments are about our children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising the 9/11 Generation', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T15:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbe10934-5938-52ff-8086-eb64a4f624c2', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbe10934-5938-52ff-8086-eb64a4f624c2'}, {'abstract': 'Many bankers were wary of making A.R.C. loans, and their fears now appear well founded.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/a-r-c-loans-gone-but-hardly-forgotten/', 'snippet': 'Many bankers were wary of making A.R.C. loans, and their fears now appear well founded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Small Business Administration‘s special stimulus-funded loan program, known as America’s Recovery Capital, may be gone, but the controversy surrounding it lingers. In March, the agency’s independent Inspector General released a report estimating that of the 4,559 A.R.C. loans made through January 2010, nearly half “were not originated and closed in compliance with S.B.A.’s policies and procedures, resulting in approximately $66.5 million in inappropriate loan approvals.” If those loans default, the report warns, the banks that made them should not expect to be fully repaid by the S.B.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.R.C. Loans Gone But Hardly Forgotten', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/894a7e7b-d40b-55f0-8bef-392d00a5f1df', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/894a7e7b-d40b-55f0-8bef-392d00a5f1df'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Scott Brown says he is headed to Afghanistan for training as part of his service in the Massachusetts National Guard.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/scott-brown-headed-to-afghanistan-for-national-guard-duty/', 'snippet': 'Senator Scott Brown says he is headed to Afghanistan for training as part of his service in the Massachusetts National Guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Scott Brown, Republican of Massachusetts, said Monday that he was headed to Afghanistan for training as part of his service in the National Guard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scott Brown Headed to Afghanistan for National Guard Training', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b04685f4-76f6-5679-a24a-3a875cf3e3bf', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b04685f4-76f6-5679-a24a-3a875cf3e3bf'}, {'abstract': 'ABC News on Monday aired a short video segment that it said depicts scenes from inside the compound where Osama Bin Laden was killed.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/abc-says-video-shows-bin-laden-compound/', 'snippet': 'ABC News on Monday aired a short video segment that it said depicts scenes from inside the compound where Osama Bin Laden was killed.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:05 p.m. | Updated ABC News scored the first big exclusive in the story behind the raid that killed Osama bin Laden with a short video segment it said was shot from inside the compound where the battle took place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Says Video Shows Bin Laden Compound', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:02:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c2e217f-a005-5038-a247-2f12d336e7e5', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c2e217f-a005-5038-a247-2f12d336e7e5'}, {'abstract': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden may complicate the G.O.P.’s 2012 narrative that the president is naïve and indecisive when it comes to foreign policy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/bin-laden-operation-may-complicate-g-o-p-message-on-national-security/', 'snippet': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden may complicate the G.O.P.’s 2012 narrative that the president is naïve and indecisive when it comes to foreign policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama‘s Republican critics, especially his potential 2012 rivals, have been assembling a campaign-season narrative that seeks to label him as weak and indecisive on national security matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden Raid Complicates G.O.P. Message for 2012', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeb7b8ce-5988-5c6e-aeae-3ccae9dca74f', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeb7b8ce-5988-5c6e-aeae-3ccae9dca74f'}, {'abstract': 'Faced with protests, Kid Rock said that his use of the flag in his act was a tribute to Lynyrd Skynyrd and that he had “never flown that flag with any hate in my heart.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/at-n-a-a-c-p-event-kid-rock-defends-use-of-confederate-flag/', 'snippet': 'Faced with protests, Kid Rock said that his use of the flag in his act was a tribute to Lynyrd Skynyrd and that he had “never flown that flag with any hate in my heart.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Kid Rock received an award from the Detroit branch of the N.A.A.C.P. on Sunday night despite the protests of picketers outside the ceremony who said he should not be using the Confederate flag during his performances. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At N.A.A.C.P. Event, Kid Rock Defends Use of Confederate Fl