Long Time Coming', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africans Greet News With Relief And Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/205a917e-5180-581b-a0e3-d30148c44086', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/205a917e-5180-581b-a0e3-d30148c44086'}, {'abstract': 'Amid a report of a proposal from ConAgra, the maker of Post Cereals says it is not in any talks about a sale of the company.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/ralcorp-says-it-received-a-takeover-approach/', 'snippet': 'Amid a report of a proposal from ConAgra, the maker of Post Cereals says it is not in any talks about a sale of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ralcorp Holdings, the maker of Post Cereals and private-brand food products, confirmed on Monday that it had received an unsolicited offer from an unidentified party in March. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ralcorp Says It Received a Takeover Approach', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ralcorp Holdings Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cba8719-b6ed-5b24-9f08-bcb9d76ef7da', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cba8719-b6ed-5b24-9f08-bcb9d76ef7da'}, {'abstract': 'A new private showroom for the fine jewelry line opens on Santa Monica’s Main Street.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/linked-in-hoorsenbuhs/', 'snippet': 'A new private showroom for the fine jewelry line opens on Santa Monica’s Main Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the 1941 Quonset hut that housed Hoorsenbuhs’s Santa Monica atelier was scheduled for demolition, the first reaction of the fine jewelry line’s founders, Robert Keith and Kether Parker, was resistance; after all, the iron structure’s rustic feel was the perfect complement to Keith’s opulent industrial designs, favored by style savvy celebs like David Beckham, Katie Holmes, Mary Kate Olsen and Rihanna. But soon the two men, who became fast friends on a Malibu beach 20 years ago and started Hoorsenbuhs in 2005, decided that an upgrade was in order. The new private showroom opened this week in a former bungalow on Santa Monica’s Main Street, with fittings from the old space, like dark wood sliding doors, industrial lamps and jewelry cases offset with heavy maritime chains. (The Hoorsenbuhs name comes from a Dutch trading ship sailed by Keith’s ancestors.). The new space is an airy, light-filled room that will soon open to an outdoor area with a fire pit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Linked In | Hoorsenbuhs', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steffie Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steffie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b106503-39fa-52d3-be59-d8afbe2eceec', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b106503-39fa-52d3-be59-d8afbe2eceec'}, {'abstract': 'Low- and middle-income tenants occupy buildings that abut those of luxury condominium owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nyregion/brooklyn-neighbors-share-landlord-but-not-amenities.html', 'snippet': 'Low- and middle-income tenants occupy buildings that abut those of luxury condominium owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rare is the New Yorker not afflicted by real estate envy. In this city of dreams and dissatisfactions, where public housing and squished tenements sit an air shaft away from multimillion-dollar apartments, coveting thy neighbor’s home is as common as breathing in exhaust.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/APPRAISAL/APPRAISAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Brooklyn Renters, Look but Don’t Swim', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Brooklyn Renters, Look but Don’t Swim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21fbc770-799d-56aa-bc68-b2a1251f85ff', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21fbc770-799d-56aa-bc68-b2a1251f85ff'}, {'abstract': 'The death of Bin Laden and the Arab revival.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/osamas-long-goodbye/', 'snippet': 'The death of Bin Laden and the Arab revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did you grow up with the notion that you should never cheer at the death of a person, even a tyrant? I did. I suppose it has to do with that very subtle business of distinguishing yourself from your enemies. So I felt some slight ambivalence when a force that was much stronger than my ambivalence took me into my daughter’s bedroom this morning to wake her and show her the local newspaper, then on the same errand into my son’s room, waiting while he rubbed the sleep out of his eyes and focused on the Page 1 headline in great, black type: BIN LADEN DEAD. I exult in the death of my enemy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Osama’s Long Goodbye', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Malcomson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malcomson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed3e4d3c-4819-5003-b3df-69e4c37aef20', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed3e4d3c-4819-5003-b3df-69e4c37aef20'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters examined the way sports became a backdrop for the news that the United States had located and killed Osama bin Laden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/sports/baseball/03leading.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters examined the way sports became a backdrop for the news that the United States had located and killed Osama bin Laden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Usually, the sports world’s intersections with the real one are awkward and embarrassing, perspective not generally being a strong suit of people who paint their faces and erupt in streams of profanity over a referee’s call. Inevitably, the news could be Armageddon and someone will be upset that it interrupted the baseball scores crawling at the bottom of the screen. There will be at least one inappropriate headline like, “N.F.L. draft takes backseat to news of Osama bin Laden’s death.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big News at the Ballpark', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big News at the Ballpark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Randolph, Zach', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T16:29:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa8ab48-7850-5b04-9a94-406beb42eb00', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa8ab48-7850-5b04-9a94-406beb42eb00'}, {'abstract': 'Based on the Intrade odds on whether Osama bin Laden would be caught by September 2011, it appears someone made a lot of money yesterday.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/bin-laden-and-inefficient-markets/', 'snippet': 'Based on the Intrade odds on whether Osama bin Laden would be caught by September 2011, it appears someone made a lot of money yesterday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someone else could have made a killing yesterday. Here’s a look at the odds on Intrade, the prediction markets site, on whether Osama bin Laden would be “captured/neutralised before midnight ET on 30 Sep 2011″:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden and Inefficient M