ovies stars like James Earl Jones (“Driving Miss Daisy”), Al Pacino (“The Merchant of Venice”), and Robin Williams (“Bengal Tiger”); and widely admired actors Bobby Cannavale (“Hat”) and Mark Rylance (“Jerusalem,” “La Bête”) are all more-than-plausible as nominees. To that end, will Mr. Rylance be competing against himself at the Tonys ceremony? And which shows were blanked among the nominees? Who wuz robbed?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tune In for the Tony Nominations', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bedford, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantello, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rylance, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drama Desk', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T17:41:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4c82f62-1ab9-5610-a510-0db06a27aaef', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4c82f62-1ab9-5610-a510-0db06a27aaef'}, {'abstract': 'There are thousands of years of history in Cairo and that history can be seen in the people themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2008/02/03/travel/0203-36HOURS_index.html', 'snippet': 'There are thousands of years of history in Cairo and that history can be seen in the people themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are thousands of years of history in Cairo and that 