bt limit fight as well as efforts by House Republicans and Senate Democrats to try to score quick political victories on rising gas prices.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/week-ahead-debt-ceiling-and-gas-prices-still-focus-of-congress/', 'snippet': 'Congress is expected to focus on the debt limit fight as well as efforts by House Republicans and Senate Democrats to try to score quick political victories on rising gas prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden will dominate Congressional conversations this week, but top aides said Monday that lawmakers still intended to pursue their planned agenda as members of the House and Senate return from spring break.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week Ahead: Debt Ceiling and Gas Prices Still Focus of Congress', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T18:25:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b25718ce-1384-53da-9a9f-481f62647b34', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b25718ce-1384-53da-9a9f-481f62647b34'}, {'abstract': 'One pleasure of the sixth floor — right now I mean the offices, not the blog — is getting to walk past the prints of some of the photos we’ve published in the magazine over the years.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/obscura-cool/', 'snippet': 'One pleasure of the sixth floor — right now I mean the offices, not the blog — is getting to walk past the prints of some of the photos we’ve published in the magazine over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One pleasure of the sixth floor — right now I mean the offices, not the blog — is getting to walk past the prints of some of the photos we’ve published in the magazine over the years. They’re big, and they’re full of fun or beauty or mystery or some mix of all these and other qualities. I’m no art critic — I know, shocking, right? — but one in particular has struck me as subtler than the rest, harder to “read” at a glance, easier to pass by on a daily basis without fully seeing what’s going on. That’s how it has been for me, anyway. The photo is a black-and-white camera obscura image of Times Square by Abelardo Morell. It ran in the magazine in 1997,\xa0and is reproduced above.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obscura Cool', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T18:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1620cf5-8019-5b26-818e-4d7a88e4c059', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1620cf5-8019-5b26-818e-4d7a88e4c059'}, {'abstract': 'Details emerged about the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, whose body was dropped into the North Arabian Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/asia/osama-bin-laden-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Details emerged about the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, whose body was dropped into the North Arabian Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Calling it a “good day for America,” President Obama said on Monday that the