ion_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4c44263-6bba-5416-90cf-1282aaf1c1f9', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4c44263-6bba-5416-90cf-1282aaf1c1f9'}, {'abstract': 'The 10 Most Wanted list now has a vacancy, but it is not immediately apparent who will fill it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/us/03wanted.html', 'snippet': 'The 10 Most Wanted list now has a vacancy, but it is not immediately apparent who will fill it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A red banner declaring “Deceased” was splashed across Osama bin Laden’s photograph on the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s 10 Most Wanted list on Monday, ending his 10-year sojourn among America’s most sought-after public enemies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Famous List of the Infamous, Now in Need of an Update', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Famous List of the Infamous, Now in Need of an Update', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e276a2c-dc51-5869-a903-65b5777e43f0', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e276a2c-dc51-5869-a903-65b5777e43f0'}, {'abstract': 'Men with the highest blood D.H.A. levels were more likely to develop high-grade prostate cancer than those with the lowest D.H.A. blood levels, researchers have found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/health/research/03patterns.html', 'snippet': 'Men with the highest blood D.H.A. levels were more likely to develop high-grade prostate cancer than those with the lowest D.H.A. blood levels, researchers have found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Omega-3 fatty acids have anti-inflammatory effects that may help protect against heart disease, studies have shown. But men with high blood levels of the omega-3 fat docosahexaenoic acid, or D.H.A., were at significantly greater risk for aggressive prostate cancer, a large study has found.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patterns: An Omega-3 Fatty Acid Shows a Risky Side', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PATTERNS: An Omega-3 Fatty Acid Shows a Risky Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Gland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb140603-2159-5996-9628-aafc51a64acb', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb140603-2159-5996-9628-aafc51a64acb'}, {'abstract': 'In “A Singular Woman,” the author Janny Scott goes beyond what we know about Barack Obama’s mother — a “white woman from Kansas” — to portray a woman who took a more difficult path than her peers’.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/books/in-a-singular-woman-janny-scott-portrays-obamas-mother.html', 'snippet': 'In “A Singular Woman,” the author Janny Scott goes beyond what we know about Barack Obama’s mother — a “white woman from Kansas” — to portray a woman who took a more difficult path than her peers’.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pieces of the story of Ann Dunham, the mother of Barack Obama, we know already. A “white woman from Kansas,” as he referred to her at the Democratic convention in 2008, who married an African intellectual and had a son with him. A strict mother who roused that son before dawn to study. An anthropologist who spent years studying in Indonesian villages, several of those years without her son. A 52-year-old woman whose last year before succumbing to cancer was spent in part trying to convince the Cigna insurance company that she should not be disqualified from benefits by virtue of a “pre-existing condition.” These are the parts of her life that resonate with our cultural anxieties about good mothering, access to health care and, of course, race.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/JPBOOK2/JPBOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Journey and Legacy of Obama’s Mother', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Journey and Legacy Of Obama’s Mother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunham, Stanley Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Janny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Lutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/32e14acc-aaa8-5999-8c2e-4de2d4a0dddf', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32e14acc-aaa8-5999-8c2e-4de2d4a0dddf'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Galassi will be stepping down in July.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/chief-photography-curator-retiring-from-moma/', 'snippet': 'Peter Galassi will be stepping down in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Galassi, the chief curator of photography at the Museum of Modern Art, will retire in July, the museum announced. Mr. Galassi, 60, who first worked for the museum as a curatorial intern in 1974, will leave to devote time to other projects, including writing, according to a statement from the museum. He joined MoMA’s photography department as a staff member in 1981 and was made chief curator 10 years later. Under his direction the museum expanded its exhibition style to include not just documentary but also post-modern works. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chief Photography Curator Retiring From MoMA', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galassi, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowry, Glenn D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Cindy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steichen, Edward', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3288cafb-ec72-5d04-9ba8-32fb8694464d', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3288cafb-ec72-5d04-9ba8-32fb8694464d'}, {'abstract': 'Since 9/11, there’s been an outpouring of books about Osama bin Laden, Al Qaeda, the September 11th attacks and the war in Afghanistan. Here is an annotated list of some of the more useful books on those subjects.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/a-survey-of-books-about-osama-bin-laden-and-al-qaeda/', 'snippet': 'Since 9/11, there’s been an outpouring of books about Osama bin Laden, Al Qaeda, the September 11th attacks and the war in Afghanistan. Here is an annotated list of some of the more useful books on those subjects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 9/11, there has been an outpouring of books aboutOsama bin Laden, Al Qaeda, the Sept. 11 attacks and the war in Afghanistan. Below is an annotated list of some of the more useful ones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Survey of Books About Osama bin Laden and Al Qaeda', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:15:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/299b6c1d-8154-5bf8-85e9-1c738bc58b51', 'word_count': 1496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/299b6c1d-8154-5bf8-85e9-1c738bc58b51'}, {'abstract': 'White House officials decided that if American troops killed Osama bin Laden, they would bury him at sea in order to prevent his grave from becoming a shrine for his followers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/asia/03burial.html', 'snippet': 'White House officials decided that if American troops killed Osama bin Laden, they would bury him at sea in order to prevent his grave from becoming a shrine for his followers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'White House officials decided before Monday’s firefight in northern Pakistan that if American troops killed Osama bin Laden, they would bury him at sea in order to prevent his grave from becoming a shrine for his followers, a White House official said Monday. They planned to include all rites associated with Muslim burials, the official added. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamic Scholars Split Over Sea Burial for Bin Laden', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'pr