some money. I bet people didn’t know poetry involved such high stakes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/03flierpix/03flierpix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/business/03flierpix/03flierpix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/03flierpix/03flierpix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/03flierpix/03flierpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/business/03flierpix/03flierpix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Poetic Job That Invites Conversation', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Poetic Job That Invites Conversation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirby, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kirby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kirby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e089897-b92f-5f7e-812b-e9f9d2619999', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e089897-b92f-5f7e-812b-e9f9d2619999'}, {'abstract': 'Three marine scientists respond to critics of their paper on declining plankton and rising temperatures.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/researchers-defend-study-finding-plankton-decline/', 'snippet': 'Three marine scientists respond to critics of their paper on declining plankton and rising temperatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study in Nature Climate Change,\xa0“Revaluating ocean warming impacts on global\xa0phytoplankton,”\xa0has shown that the method used to calculate phytoplankton loss in the 2010 research greatly overstated plankton losses because of a missing vital factor. Read New Scientist for the details.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Researchers Defend Study Finding Plankton Decline', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marine Biology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worm, Boris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:43:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc820cd-889a-5e14-90d4-8f37c65921a9', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc820cd-889a-5e14-90d4-8f37c65921a9'}, {'abstract': 'The founders of the Webster Miami suggest some must-haves for travel for the staff at T Magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/the-webster-sends-t-packing/', 'snippet': 'The founders of the Webster Miami suggest some must-haves for travel for the staff at T Magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Laure Heriard Dubreuil and Frederic Dechnik, founders of the Webster Miami, have a penchant for sun, and lots of it. It’s reflected in what they buy for their store but also in their personal itineraries, which have them jet-setting from Egypt and Greece to St. Tropez and Mallorca. Come June the duo will head to Venice (for the Art Biennale) and to Mexico’s Costa Careyes for the wild beaches, Las Alamandas resort and the banana forest. With their astute knowledge of all climates — and immaculate taste — The Moment put Dubreul and Dechnik to work to send T’s editors packing. “I guess it’s very French, but August is off,” Dechnik says. “I will never compromise.” We can dream.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Webster Sends T Packing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/77395bcd-21c2-58e1-a3c4-037e073590b0', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77395bcd-21c2-58e1-a3c4-037e073590b0'}, {'abstract': 'Ticketing on intercontinental trips is smoother, but some travelers blamed reduced competition on some routes for higher fares.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/business/03alliances.html', 'snippet': 'Ticketing on intercontinental trips is smoother, but some travelers blamed reduced competition on some routes for higher fares.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Global airline alliances used to be little more than marketing agreements among carriers, and travelers had only a dim awareness of them. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/Alliances/Alliances-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Clout of Air Alliances', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Clout of Air Alliances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c1767d7-b3fe-5a30-b8e8-ab2f39997756', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c1767d7-b3fe-5a30-b8e8-ab2f39997756'}, {'abstract': 'A recall study of rhesus monkeys suggests that language is not necessary — either for having the ability to recall, or for proving it to an experimenter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/science/03obmonkeys.html', 'snippet': 'A recall study of rhesus monkeys suggests that language is not necessary — either for having the ability to recall, or for proving it to an experimenter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monkeys can recognize an object they have seen before, but now scientists have shown that they are also capable of a much more sophisticated form of memory: They can hold in mind an object without actually seeing it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03obmonkeys/03obmonkeys-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03obmonkeys/03obmonkeys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03obmonkeys/03obmonkeys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Monkeys’ Memories Can Stretch Beyond What’s in Front of Them', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Monkeys’ Memories Can Stretch Beyond What’s in Front of Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T19:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5839247-5f82-5391-b590-e83ecba7f609', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5839247-5f82-5391-b590-e83ecba7f609'}, {'abstract': 'Retro and proud of it, Beastie Boys give their hip-hop time machine another ride into the 1980s on “Hot Sauc