 false positives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A questionnaire that parents can fill out in five minutes while waiting for the pediatrician can detect autism and other delays in 1-year-olds, a new study has found. But the test has a high false-positive rate that may cause unnecessary alarm.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Screening: An Autism Questionnaire at Checkup Time', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SCREENING: An Autism Questionnaire at Checkup Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db3c1c89-7902-58ac-bfa8-c5754e6a130c', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db3c1c89-7902-58ac-bfa8-c5754e6a130c'}, {'abstract': 'No, the successful raid in Pakistan didn’t put the 2012 election in Mr. Obama’s pocket. But that doesn’t mean voters will ignore it.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/second-thoughts-about-obama-and-bin-laden-its-not-just-the-economy-stupid/', 'snippet': 'No, the successful raid in Pakistan didn’t put the 2012 election in Mr. Obama’s pocket. But that doesn’t mean voters will ignore it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first heard the news about the American military operation that killed Osama bin Laden, I was pretty certain that the popular press was going to overstate its impact on Barack Obama’s re-election chances. I wrote an article to that effect last night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second Thoughts About Obama and Bin Laden: It’s Not Just the Economy, Stupid', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/27f851a5-e9d0-50e1-86d5-85f6371a2e6d', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27f851a5-e9d0-50e1-86d5-85f6371a2e6d'}, {'abstract': 'Consumer Reports teams with Billshrink to offer service comparison tools.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/consumer-reports-offers-new-comparison-tool/', 'snippet': 'Consumer Reports teams with Billshrink to offer service comparison tools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consumer Reports has long offered rankings and comparisons of products as diverse as cars, vacuum cleaners and televisions. Now the magazine’s online counterpart, consumerreports.org, has teamed up with the bill comparison site Billshrink.com to help shoppers evaluate the services that go along with some of those products.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumer Reports Offers New Comparison Tool', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e12ab067-b23f-5442-9b16-67fcc40a5766', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e12ab067-b23f-5442-9b16-67fcc40a5766'}, {'abstract': 'Michael D. Shear responded to comments and questions about Osama bin Laden’s death and its political ramifications.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/facebook-transcript-live-chat-on-bin-laden-death/', 'snippet': 'Michael D. Shear responded to comments and questions about Osama bin Laden’s death and its political ramifications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday afternoon, Michael D. Shear, the chief correspondent for The Caucus, participated in a live chat on The Times’s Facebook page, responding to comments and questions about Osama bin Laden’s death and its political ramifications. The following is a transcript of the questions Mr. Shear addressed and the answers he posted on Facebook. Thanks to everyone who participated; we hope to bring you more Facebook chats like this in the future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Transcript: Live Chat on Bin Laden Death', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/daeef94f-b2a8-5165-8896-8c0f103d268c', 'word_count': 1670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daeef94f-b2a8-5165-8896-8c0f103d268c'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Tragical Life of Cheeseboy,” Finegan Kruckemeyer’s play at the Duke on 42nd Street, a Dickensian storyteller relates the adventures of a boy made of cheese.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/theater/reviews/the-tragical-life-of-cheeseboy-at-duke-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Tragical Life of Cheeseboy,” Finegan Kruckemeyer’s play at the Duke on 42nd Street, a Dickensian storyteller relates the adventures of a boy made of cheese.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Tragical Life of Cheeseboy,” Finegan Kruckemeyer’s play presented by the New Victory Theater, begins with a bearded storyteller (Stephen Sheehan) in a top hat approaching some children sitting on the floor in the front row: “Are you prepared to be saddened?” he asks. “Are you prepared to laugh? Are you prepared to be dazzled?” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/TRAGIC/TRAGIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/TRAGIC/TRAGIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/TRAGIC/TRAGIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Orphan’s Adventures, Ripe for the Telling', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Tragical Life of Cheeseboy'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Orphan’s Adventures, Ripe for the Telling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/68b57d91-2f0d-584e-ab44-42af5d5a4f7d', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68b57d91-2f0d-584e-ab44-42af5d5a4f7d'}, {'abstract': 'Better than a flipped coin, I am.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/prognosticate-that/', 'snippet': 'Better than a flipped coin, I am.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ahem: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prognosticate That!', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f29f9d-5917-5af2-8d2b-821b74e39e1d', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f29f9d-5917-5af2-8d2b-821b74e39e1d'}, {'abstract': 'Classical music, suffering from the advent of digital technology and from the aging of its audience, is reaching as far out as to correctional institutions and the military to attract new fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/01/arts/music/classical-music-finds-ways-to-reach-way-out.html', 'snippet': 'Classical music, suffering from the advent of digital technology and from the aging of its audience, is reaching as far out as to correctional institutions and the military to attract new fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, during his consultancy to the Chicago Symphony Orchestra, the celebrated cellist Yo-Yo Ma visited the Illinois Youth Center, a correctional institution in Warrenville. He accompanied the female inmates as they rehearsed a musical show based on their life experiences, as part of the C.S.O.’s program to reach communities far from Symphony Center.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '37A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Music Finds Ways to Reach (Way) Out', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical Music Finds Ways to Reach (Way) Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyric Opera of Chicago', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:41:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Tesser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tesser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542c0202-2e7d-59e1-aa11-442c405d91db', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542c0202-2e7d-59e1-aa11-442c405d91db'}, {'abstract': 'Interviews provide a grim look at abuses occurring in Iraq and their crushing effects on individuals and families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/health/03torture.html', 'snippet': 'Interviews provide a grim look at abuses occurring in Iraq and their crushing effects on individuals and families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMMAN, Jordan — The first time the Iraqi Army arrested him, he said, soldiers burst into his shop in Baghdad, dragged him out in handcuffs and a blindfold, and took him to a filthy, overcrowded prison. Beatings, rape, hunger and disease were rampant, and he expected at any moment to be killed. He was held for four months, until December 2008. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03torturespan/03torturespan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03torturespan/03torturespan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03torturespan/03torturespan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03torturespan/03torturespan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03torturespan/03torturespan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tugging at Threads to Unspool Stories of Torture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tugging at Threads to Unspool Stories of Torture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', '