vers being hacked last week.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/sony-declines-to-testify-at-upcoming-data-hearing/', 'snippet': 'Sony on Monday declined to testify at a Congressional hearing on data breaches and their affect on consumers. An earlier deadline has been placed on Sony to answer questions about its servers being hacked last week.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:00 p.m. | Updated Added comment from Sony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Declines to Testify at Congressional Hearing', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca1d3b29-1fc6-55ee-86dc-d7a8d645c66f', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca1d3b29-1fc6-55ee-86dc-d7a8d645c66f'}, {'abstract': 'In Internet forums, gatherings, and interviews, Al Qaeda and its affiliates vowed continue their struggle against the West and its allies following the death of Osama bin Laden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/03jihadi.html', 'snippet': 'In Internet forums, gatherings, and interviews, Al Qaeda and its affiliates vowed continue their struggle against the West and its allies following the death of Osama bin Laden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jihadis around the world reacted on Monday to the news of Osama bin Laden’s death with a mix of sorrow, disbelief and determination that Al Qaeda and its affiliates would continue their struggle against the West and its allies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jihadis Voice Grief and Determination at Death of Their Inspiration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jihadis Voice Grief and Determination at Death of Their Inspiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:46:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9416b6b-d5b5-5510-9e85-5daa0664ac57', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9416b6b-d5b5-5510-9e85-5daa0664ac57'}, {'abstract': 'U.S. Citizens traveling abroad are warned of the “enhanced potential for anti-American violence” following Bin Laden’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/worldwide-travel-alert/', 'snippet': 'U.S. Citizens traveling abroad are warned of the “enhanced potential for anti-American violence” following Bin Laden’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the killing of Osama bin Laden, the State Department has issued a worldwide travel alert, warning United States citizens of “the enhanced potential for anti-American violence given recent counter-terrorism activity in Pakistan.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Worldwide Travel Alert', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7585e2b-601f-584d-9668-ef82fdc36404', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7585e2b-601f-584d-9668-ef82fdc36404'}, {'abstract': 'Careful Asia, careless West.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/whos-over-leveraged-now/', 'snippet': 'Careful Asia, careless West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I wrote the first edition of The Return of Depression Economics, I was reacting in large part to the Asian financial crisis, which I thought could presage similarly difficult crises here in America. Sadly, I was right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s Over-leveraged Now?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/06aff24b-88d6-51bb-be2a-e390ca927518', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06aff24b-88d6-51bb-be2a-e390ca927518'}, {'abstract': 'The commissioner says the authorities “know of no specific plot against New York,” but have added shifts and increased officers’ public profile nonetheless.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/police-step-up-efforts-on-news-of-bin-ladens-death/', 'snippet': 'The commissioner says the authorities “know of no specific plot against New York,” but have added shifts and increased officers’ public profile nonetheless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As New Yorkers made their way through the city on Monday, they were greeted with an increased police presence in the city’s transit system, at the area’s bridges and tunnels and at other key sites like Times Square and the financial district — part of a coordinated security plan put in place as soon as Osama bin Laden’s death was reported by President Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Step Up Efforts on News of Bin Laden’s Death', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T20:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Zraick and Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zraick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type