’s interview with its correspondent Lara Logan on “60 Minutes” in which she recounted details of her sexual assault in Cairo topped the Nielsen ratings on Sunday. The program drew 10.6 million viewers during the 7 p.m. hour, lifting CBS to No. 1 for the night, according to preliminary estimates, which were somewhat imprecise because of interruptions in Western time zones for President Obama’s announcement of the death of Osama bin Laden. Although CBS also appeared to lead the 8 p.m. time slot with “The Amazing Race” (9.7 million), at 9 and 10, CBS’s “Undercover Boss” (8.8 million) and “CSI: Miami” (9 million) lagged slightly behind ABC’s “Desperate Housewives” (10.1 million) and the second half of NBC’s two-hour installment of “Celebrity Apprentice” (9.1 million). ABC ranked second for the night over all, garnering 9.6 million viewers in the 8 o’clock hour for “Extreme Makeover: Home Edition.” NBC was third with “Dateline” at 7 (5.5 million) and “America’s Next Great Restaurant” at 8 (6 million). Fox finished in fourth place with mostly reruns.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lara Logan Interview Leads Sunday Ratings', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lara Logan Interview Leads Sunday Ratings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T21:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0d9be9-6b76-512c-9b51-07c8c2c2966e', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0d9be9-6b76-512c-9b51-07c8c2c2966e'}, {'abstract': 'A newlywed learns to grieve after her husband dies in “Be a Good Little Widow” at Ars Nova.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/theater/reviews/be-a-good-little-widow-at-ars-nova-review.html', 'snippet': 'A newlywed learns to grieve after her husband dies in “Be a Good Little Widow” at Ars Nova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Zimmerman’s set for “Be a Good Little Widow” is the perfect reflection of the lead character in Bekah Brunstetter’s funny-sad play about loss at Ars Nova. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/widow/widow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/widow/widow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/widow/widow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Learning to Grieve in a Grown-Up World', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Be a Good Little Widow'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Learning to Grieve in a Grown-Up World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brunstetter, Bekah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T21:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Rooney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/59107d33-c536-5082-ad86-f3033cfe2b5d', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59107d33-c536-5082-ad86-f3033cfe2b5d'}, {'abstract': 'Activists describe a campaign of intimidation, with arbitrary detentions, particularly in Dara’a and near the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/middleeast/03syria.html', 'snippet': 'Activists describe a campaign of intimidation, with arbitrary detentions, particularly in Dara’a and near the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian security forces have escalated an arrest campaign in the country’s most rebellious regions, detaining hundreds over the past few days in the besieged city of Dara’a and towns on the outskirts of the capital, Damascus, activists said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Syria, Reports of Arrests Proliferate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Syria, Reports Of Arrests Proliferate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T21:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9037e455-3243-5d62-a696-a3676fbeb40f', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt: