s', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db396819-9baa-585c-8442-2928837b2d38', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db396819-9baa-585c-8442-2928837b2d38'}, {'abstract': 'The French newspaper Le Monde editorializes on Bin Laden’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/media-react-le-monde-notes-historys-timing/', 'snippet': 'The French newspaper Le Monde editorializes on Bin Laden’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — “Chance sometimes does things well,”\xa0 Le Monde, widely viewed as France’s newspaper of record, wrote in an editorial. “The man who embodied international jihadism dies at the moment when the ‘Arab spring’ has just given a blow to this totalitarian fantasy. As soon as Arab peoples revolted in the name of democracy and not Islamism or the return to the caliphate preached by Al Qaeda, Osama bin Laden was politically moribund.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Media React: Le Monde Notes History’s Timing', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Monde', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41a97dbf-6dc2-5e82-a250-9c5cb1779910', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41a97dbf-6dc2-5e82-a250-9c5cb1779910'}, {'abstract': 'Senator John Ensign of Nevada apologized to his colleagues and attributed his personal and ethical lapses to an arrogance developed as a member of Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/ensign-apologizes-in-farewell-speech/', 'snippet': 'Senator John Ensign of Nevada apologized to his colleagues and attributed his personal and ethical lapses to an arrogance developed as a member of Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator John Ensign apologized to his colleagues on Monday in an unusual farewell speech in which he attributed his personal and ethical lapses to an arrogance developed as a member of Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ensign Apologizes in Farewell Speech', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ensign, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/725ac7f3-88d6-538c-a9dc-3dc2c22e3720', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725ac7f3-88d6-538c-a9dc-3dc2c22e3720'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers lately have learned that serotonin plays an impressive number of critical roles throughout the body.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/science/03angier.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers lately have learned that serotonin plays an impressive number of critical roles throughout the body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just when you thought that serotonin was passé, and you’d tossed all your half-used bottles of S.S.R.I.-type antidepressants because the ones that didn’t give you nausea or smother your libido left you wondering whether you were in the placebo arm of a clinical trial, here comes a raft of new discoveries that sweeps the small, evolutionarily ancient and slyly powerful signaling molecule back on to center stage.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03angier/03angier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03angier/03angier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/science/03angier/03angier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Description Grows for Our Utility Hormone', 'kicker': 'Basics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Job Description Grows For Our Utility Hormone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serotonin (Chemical)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natal