': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/443fd880-77c0-5bb4-95c9-7c3bdbd2315f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/443fd880-77c0-5bb4-95c9-7c3bdbd2315f'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Bartok formed the core of a recital by Christian Tetzlaff and Antje Weithaas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/arts/music/christian-tetzlaff-and-antje-weithaas-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Bartok formed the core of a recital by Christian Tetzlaff and Antje Weithaas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you spent long childhood hours locked in practice rooms, it can be hard to believe that the dry études that once plagued you might actually have been, well, music. But in 1930 Bela Bartok was asked to make a contribution to an anthology for student violinists. Rather than arrange pre-existing works, the composer created his multifaceted 44 short Violin Duos.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/christian/christian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Violinists Wander Into Bartok, and Well Off the Beaten Path', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violinists Wander Into Bartok, and Well Off the Beaten Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tetzlaff, Christian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:06:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2374dba3-3726-5cfe-94cb-2a2bacad0554', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2374dba3-3726-5cfe-94cb-2a2bacad0554'}, {'abstract': 'This two-time host of the Winter Olympics knows how to stay cool in the off-season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2007/08/10/travel/20070810_PLACID_SLIDESHOW_index.html', 'snippet': 'This two-time host of the Winter Olympics knows how to stay cool in the off-season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This two-time host of the Winter Olympics knows how to stay cool in the off-season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2007/08/10/travel/10placid75.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2007/08/10/travel/10placid75.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wintry Summer in Lake Placid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ab1f462f-0098-577e-bea5-0bf4ca0b4e8d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ab1f462f-0098-577e-bea5-0bf4ca0b4e8d'}, {'abstract': 'The Boston Ballet stages works by William Forsythe, Helen Pickett and Jiri Kylian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/arts/dance/boston-ballets-bella-figura-with-a-forsythe-work-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Boston Ballet stages works by William Forsythe, Helen Pickett and Jiri Kylian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The stage, washed in white light, looks enormous when the curtain goes up on William Forsythe’s “Second Detail,” the opening piece on the Boston Ballet triple bill at the opera house here. Twelve dancers, dressed in the palest gray leotards and tights — some facing the audience, some with their backs to us — are arrayed in lines and diagonals, their bodies etched against the space with cut-glass clarity. Thom Willem’s electronic score offers a hesitant, knocking rhythm, and then a 13th dancer, a woman, walks on quietly and takes her place in a line.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/Sub-Figura/Sub-Figura-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/Sub-Figura/Sub-Figura-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/arts/Sub-Figura/Sub-Figura-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building on the Mastery of What Came Before', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building on the Mastery of What Came Before', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kylian, Jiri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'FORSYTHE, WILLIAM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-02T22:08:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'last