Northwest cringed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To start with, a confession: I want to root for the Oklahoma City Thunder. I like the players. I like the team. I like the way it plays. The Thunder is easily one of the most likable teams in pro basketball. I get that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Pacific Northwest, a Playoff Matchup Stings', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle SuperSonics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Grizzlies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c662bd9-0d74-5c80-a9b0-fca2811601d2', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c662bd9-0d74-5c80-a9b0-fca2811601d2'}, {'abstract': 'Federal officials said DNA analysis helped confirm Osama bin Laden’s identity with 99.9 percent accuracy, which scientific experts said would result from a match with a close relative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/science/03dna.html', 'snippet': 'Federal officials said DNA analysis helped confirm Osama bin Laden’s identity with 99.9 percent accuracy, which scientific experts said would result from a match with a close relative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While federal officials said that analysis of DNA from several relatives helped confirm that it was Osama bin Laden who was killed in the military raid on Sunday, they have not yet disclosed the relationships of the family members whose DNA was used.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Experts Say DNA Match Is Likely a Parent or Child', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experts Say DNA Match Is Likely a Parent or Child', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr. and Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97200710-8101-534b-94fd-1da51103a0d5', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97200710-8101-534b-94fd-1da51103a0d5'}, {'abstract': 'At dinner with members of Congress from both parties, the president speaks of moments that bring Americans together.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/obama-emphasizes-sense-of-unity/', 'snippet': 'At dinner with members of Congress from both parties, the president speaks of moments that bring Americans together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama told members of Congress on Monday that because of the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, America on Sunday “experienced the same sense of unity that prevailed on 9/11.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Emphasizes ‘Sense of Unity’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0565f804-7610-5c99-8e76-18c0849a8c5a', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0565f804-7610-5c99-8e76-18c0849a8c5a'}, {'abstract': 'Desi Bouterse, a former military ruler who has been convicted of drug trafficking and is still on trial for official killings in the 1980s, is once again Suriname’s leader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/americas/03suriname.html', 'snippet': 'Desi Bouterse, a former military ruler who has been convicted of drug trafficking and is still on trial for official killings in the 1980s, is once again Suriname’s leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARAMARIBO, Suriname — Desi Bouterse has been a soldier, a coup plotter, the military ruler of this former Dutch colony, a convicted drug trafficker and, for more than a decade, a fugitive from Interpol. He remains on trial here for the killing of 15 top opponents by his military government in the 1980s. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/03suriname1/03suriname1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name