’s thinking on how to handle a lieutenant’s questionable stock trades.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/warren-buffett-lets-the-facts-bury-sokol/', 'snippet': 'At the Berkshire Hathaway shareholder meeting, coming to an understanding of Warren E. Buffett’s thinking on how to handle a lieutenant’s questionable stock trades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — In Warren E. Buffett’s view, he was as ruthless as ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buffett Lets the Facts Bury Sokol', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokol, David L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:32:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/93c12052-522f-5ddd-98e9-2f2cdbfe7211', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93c12052-522f-5ddd-98e9-2f2cdbfe7211'}, {'abstract': 'A new federal effort intended to increase access to health care for the poor would make it much more difficult for states to cut Medicaid payments to doctors and hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/us/politics/03medicaid.html', 'snippet': 'A new federal effort intended to increase access to health care for the poor would make it much more difficult for states to cut Medicaid payments to doctors and hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a new effort to increase access to health care for poor people, the Obama administration is proposing a rule that would make it much more difficult for states to cut Medicaid payments to doctors and hospitals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rule Would Discourage States’ Cutting Medicaid Payments to Providers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rule Would Discourage States’ Cutting Medicaid Payments to Providers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3319388-4d5e-5b69-bf41-b68433efdbe2', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3319388-4d5e-5b69-bf41-b68433efdbe2'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican ousted an Australian bishop, William Morris, who had called on the church to consider ordaining women and married men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/world/europe/03briefs-ART-vatican.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican ousted an Australian bishop, William Morris, who had called on the church to consider ordaining women and married men.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Vatican ousted an Australian bishop on Monday who had called on the church to consider ordaining women and married men. In a statement, the Vatican said that it had “removed from pastoral care” Bishop William Morris, left, the bishop of Toowoomba, Australia. The statement was particularly strong; normally the Vatican urges bishops to resign and then announces that it has accepted their resignation. Australian media reported that Bishop Morris had recently published an open letter saying that he was being removed for having argued in 2006 that the church should consider ordaining women and married men in order to fight a shortage of priests, prompting Pope Benedict XVI to open an investigation into his diocese. In the letter, Bishop Morris said he that he refused to resign, but would take early retirement because the pope had decided “that the diocese would be better served by the leadership of a new bishop.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/03briefs-morris/03briefs-morris-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 998, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/03briefs-morris/03briefs-morris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/world/03briefs-morris/03briefs-morris-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vatican: Bishop Who Broached New Rules for Priests Is Ousted', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vatican: Bishop Who Broached New Rules for Priests Is Ousted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T00:35:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e621100-d5ce-505a-846a-4412bb88df05', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e621100-d5ce-505a-846a-4412bb88df05'}, {'abstract': 'The arrest of Paul Sigmund IV is the latest crisis to hit the administration of Mayor Tony Mack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nyregion/drug-and-assault-charges-for-trentons-deputy-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'The arrest of Paul Sigmund IV is the latest crisis to hit the administration of Mayor Tony Mack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second-ranking city official in Trenton was arrested on Monday and charged with heroin possession and assaulting two police officers, the latest blow to an administration that has lurched from crisis to crisis since taking office in July.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/TRENTON/TRENTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 622, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/TRENTON/TRENTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/TRENTON/TRENTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'h