/04664fab-fb99-5aa1-8760-5ada133e8a60', 'word_count': 1260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04664fab-fb99-5aa1-8760-5ada133e8a60'}, {'abstract': 'SUNY’s four research campuses want to set their own rates, but many Assembly Democrats fear the plan could exclude low-income students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nyregion/cuomo-backs-higher-tuition-at-top-suny-colleges.html', 'snippet': 'SUNY’s four research campuses want to set their own rates, but many Assembly Democrats fear the plan could exclude low-income students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said Monday that he would support allowing the flagship campuses of the State University of New York to charge higher tuition than the rest of the system, a stance that could pit him against fellow Democrats who worry that lower-income students could be priced out of the top schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/suny/suny-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/suny/suny-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/suny/suny-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Backs Higher Tuition at Top SUNY Campuses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo Backs Higher Tuition at Top SUNY Campuses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T01:51:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65c642e2-2817-5141-8019-6460e0020d85', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65c642e2-2817-5141-8019-6460e0020d85'}, {'abstract': 'At the World Trade Center site and other gatherings in New York, there was joy, but also more subdued scenes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nyregion/joy-at-bin-ladens-death-is-mixed-with-sober-reflection.html', 'snippet': 'At the World Trade Center site and other gatherings in New York, there was joy, but also more subdued scenes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were, of course, the joyous celebrations, the honking horns, cheering crowds and waving flags, as if war had been won and tyranny ended. But word that Osama bin Laden had at last been killed brought out other voices on Monday as well: sober, reflective, wounded still and vengeful, but also articulate in hope.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/jp-YORK5/jp-YORK5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/jp-YORK5/jp-YORK5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/jp-YORK5/jp-YORK5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra