print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5691f3d6-fe3b-5d1b-b9ed-2a09b532626b', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5691f3d6-fe3b-5d1b-b9ed-2a09b532626b'}, {'abstract': 'A special election to replace a Republican about to be appointed to the United States Senate should be open to all candidates, Nevada’s secretary of state ruled on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/us/politics/03brfs-SENATERACEIS_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'A special election to replace a Republican about to be appointed to the United States Senate should be open to all candidates, Nevada’s secretary of state ruled on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A special election to replace Representative Dean Heller, a Republican about to be appointed to the United States Senate, should be open to all candidates, not just those selected by the two major political parties, Nevada’s secretary of state ruled on Monday. The decision improves the prospects of Sharron Angle, the Tea Party-backed Republican who ran for Senate last year and whom state Republicans had signaled that they did not want to run for this seat. The secretary of state, Ross J. Miller, a Democrat, ruled against an interpretation of the law that would limit the ballot to just candidates chosen by the major parties. “Pleased to announce an open-ballot-access election,” Mr. Miller posted on his Twitter account. “Freedom for all to run; let the people decide rather than politically elite power brokers.” Mr. Heller’s Second Congressional District is, normally, solidly Republican; the decision appears to put the Sept. 13 election in flux. Mr. Heller would replace John Ensign, a Republican, whose resignation is effective today.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nevada: House Race Is Thrown Open to All', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nevada: Senate Race Is Thrown Open to All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heller, Dean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/111543a0-50bf-58bd-987d-49b908386562', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/111543a0-50bf-58bd-987d-49b908386562'}, {'abstract': 'An Israeli publication reports on the Bin Laden killing.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/media-react-haaretz-weighs-in/', 'snippet': 'An Israeli publication reports on the Bin Laden killing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Web site for the Israeli publication Haaretz led its coverage with a map of the compound where Osama\xa0bin Laden was found, with the headline: “U.S. Had No Choice but to Kill Bin Laden, Says U.S. Defense Official.” Other content on the home page included a slide show of Americans celebrating the killing and an article featuring the results of a survey conducted by the Pew Research Center Global Attitudes Project. According to the article, the data found that support for Bin Laden had declined among Muslims worldwide. While the publication’s lead editorial focused on the commemoration of Holocaust Martyrs and Heroes Day, an editorial titled “The Road to Bin Laden Ran Through Guantánamo Bay,” by Yossi Melman, extolled the merits of the United States’ war on terror, including the cost to American taxpayers. “It turned out that it was worth every cent.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Media React: Haaretz Weighs In', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haaretz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b53b5a-5d0d-54ca-a081-06ac1626455f', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b53b5a-5d0d-54ca-a081-06ac1626455f'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 3, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/pageoneplus/corrections.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on May 3, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b8a2a43-82c6-5cc0-bfce-89b64bd02144', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b8a2a43-82c6-5cc0-bfce-89b64bd02144'}, {'abstract': 'The bureaucratic logjam for veterans pursuing benefit claims has gotten so huge that judges are having to work nights and weekends as they decide more than 600 cases each annually.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/opinion/03tue3.html', 'snippet': 'The bureaucratic logjam for veterans pursuing benefit claims has gotten so huge that judges are having to work nights and weekends as they decide more than 600 cases each annually.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bureaucratic logjam for veterans pursuing benefit claims has gotten so huge that judges — in Dickensian fashion — are having to work nights and weekends as they decide more than 600 cases each annually. The little-noticed court for appealing rejected claims is about to be even more overwhelmed by the caseloads from the Iraq and Afghanistan wars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slogging on the Home Front', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slogging on the Home Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5910176e-f937-55e3-b0b2-3a86922403e6', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5910176e-f937-55e3-b0b2-3a86922403e6'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than cut early child care, which benefits disadvantaged children, Mayor Bloomberg should consider other ways to save money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/opinion/03tue4.html', 'snippet': 'Rather than cut early child care, which benefits disadvantaged children, Mayor Bloomberg should consider other ways to save money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Bernanke, the Federal Reserve chairman, made a strong argument for good early childhood care. In a speech in New York City, he argued that the value can be especially high for disadvantaged children with a strong payoff for the economy. These programs can increase high school graduation rates, and graduates earn more, pay more taxes, and rely less on state-provided health care. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Real, Unnecessary Crisis for Families', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Real, Unnecessary Crisis for Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1a1c3e-8c76-5493-8d10-9bfb5dd9f7c7', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1a1c3e-8c76-5493-8d10-9bfb5dd9f7c7'}, {'abstract': 'Bartolo Colon turned in another fine start in place of Phil Hughes, who learned that he does not have thoracic outlet syndrome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/sports/baseball/03yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Bartolo Colon turned in another fine start in place of Phil Hughes, who learned that he does not have thoracic outlet syndrome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The most encouraging element for the Yankees on Monday occurred not at Comerica Park, where they scored the winning runs in the ninth inning of their 5-3 victory against the Tigers, but at a doctor’s office 450 miles away in St. Louis. That was where Phil Hughes learned that he did not have a rare neurovascular condition that could have sidelined him for the season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/sports/pins/pins-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/03/sports/pins/pins-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/sports/pins/pins-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/sports/pins/pins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/sports/pins/pins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Hughes and Yankees, News Is All Good', 'kicker': 'Yankees 5, Tigers 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relief for Hughes, Then Revelry for the Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T02:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/055fef13-55b1-5afe-a995-3ed5e662591c', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/055fef13-55b1-5afe-a995-3ed5e662591c'}, {'abstract': 'The Boston Globe received nine Pulitzer Prizes under his leadership, and he negotiated the sale of the paper to The New York Times Company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/business/media/03taylor.html', 'snippet': 'The Boston Globe received nine Pulitzer Prizes under his leadership, and he negotiated the sale of the paper to The New York Times Company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William O. Taylor II, a former publisher of The Boston Globe and the fourth member of his family to run that newspaper, died on Sunday at his home in Boston. Mr. Taylor, who oversaw the sale of The Globe to The New York Times Company in 1993, was 78.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/media/03taylor1/03taylor1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/business/media/03taylor1/03taylor1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/business/media/03taylor1/03taylor1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'William Taylor II, Ex-Publisher of Boston Globe, Dies at 78', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'William Osgood Taylor II, 78, Ex-Publisher of Boston Globe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Globe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, William O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T03:17:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/60a1e70f-022d-5276-94df-1251f90079d5', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60a1e70f-022d-5276-94df-1251f90079d5'}, {'abstract': 'Sony said Monday that it had discovered credit card information and customer profiles had been compromised during an attack on the Sony Online Entertainment servers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/02/other-divisions-of-sony-attacked-last-week/', 'snippet': 'Sony said Monday that it had discovered credit card information and customer profiles had been compromised during an attack on the Sony Online Entertainment servers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sony said Monday that it had discovered that more credit card information and customer profiles had been compromised during an attack on its servers last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Finds More Cases of Hacking of Its Servers', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T03:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/73868570-0c66-586d-8948-c9841ac656b8', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73868570-0c66-586d-8948-c9841ac656b8'}, {'abstract': 'The guests at the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s annual Costume Institute gala on Monday night honored the late designer Alexander McQueen by arriving in daring dress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nyregion/costume-institute-gala-goers-honor-alexander-mcqueen.html', 'snippet': 'The guests at the Metropolitan Museum of Art’s annual Costume Institute gala on Monday night honored the late designer Alexander McQueen by arriving in daring dress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rihanna looked half naked in a black lace Stella McCartney gown with a sheer panel on one side. Beyoncé wore a form-fitting Pucci the shape of a pepper mill. Renée Zellweger’s gold lace dress, by Carolina Herrera, seemed demure by comparison, until she turned around to reveal the back, which plunged all the way into plumber territory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/GALA1/GALA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 704, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/GALA1/GALA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/nyregion/GALA1/GALA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Neoprene and Kilts, Remembering a Risk Taker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Neoprene And Kilts, Remembering A Risk Taker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costume Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T03:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro',