ry, Scientific American was amazed. “The announcement of the success of the electric carriages created some surprise, as it has been thought lately that motors using some form of petroleum were best adapted for horseless carriage use,” it reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Deep Sleep, an E.V. Ancestor Awaits a Jolt', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford, Henry, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific American', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Society of Automotive Engineers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westport (Conn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T10:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e56c234-9071-5111-847a-1e56ae9039f8', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e56c234-9071-5111-847a-1e56ae9039f8'}, {'abstract': 'Every spring art galleries in the Saint-Germain-des-Pres neighborhood of Paris, long famed as home to artists, writers and musicians, open their doors to the public, in a block party called Art Saint-Germain-des-Pres. This year’s event, from May 19 to 22, will include at least 60 galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/an-art-themed-block-party-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'Every spring art galleries in the Saint-Germain-des-Pres neighborhood of Paris, long famed as home to artists, writers and musicians, open their doors to the public, in a block party called Art Saint-Germain-des-Pres. This year’s event, from May 1...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every spring art galleries in the Saint-Germain-des-Pres neighborhood, long famed as home to artists, writers and musicians, open their doors to the public, in a block party called Art Saint-Germain-des-Pres. With what might be the highest concentration of galleries in the world, it’s an ideal area to find a variety of art, from primitive to contemporary and sculpture and painting to photography, jewelry and antiques. This year’s event, from May 19 to 22, will include at least 60 galleries. As an example of the event’s breadth, La Galerie Artco-France will show works by the Surrealist René Magritte and La Galerie Frédéric Got Fine Art photographs by Elliott Erwitt. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art-Themed Block Party in Paris', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T10:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b45444f-4ca4-5ac2-b879-bdaaa0b3a5e7', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b45444f-4ca4-5ac2-b879-bdaaa0b3a5e7'}, {'abstract': 'Help City Room and WNYC create an interactive map of bird-watching spots in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/where-do-you-watch-bird-in-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'Help City Room and WNYC create an interactive map of bird-watching spots in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bird Week | Where Do You Watch Birds in New York?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T10:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times and WNYC', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3b0d4ad-2bfc-55dd-b09d-8b9537e444ab', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3b0d4ad-2bfc-55dd-b09d-8b9537e444ab'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s leader denied Western accusations that his nation lacked “vitality” in combating terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/04risk.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan’s leader denied Western accusations that his nation lacked “vitality” in combating terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of Osama bin Laden inspired many questions, but fewer answers on Tuesday: Could it lead to further erosion of support for foreign troops in Afghanistan and, subsequently, a faster withdrawal by NATO? And how should outside powers deal with Pakistan, whose president denied Western accusations that his nuclear-armed nation lacked what he called “vitality” in combating terrorism?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions Focus on Pakistan’s Role in Terror Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concerns Come to Fore Globally After Bin Laden Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Force