f97e16b-d9be-5426-9ca1-737540615232'}, {'abstract': 'In anticipation of attacks from Al Qaeda in the wake of Bin Laden’s death, additional security forces patrolled Iraq’s streets on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/bin-ladens-death-expected-to-have-little-impact-on-al-qaeda-in-iraq/', 'snippet': 'In anticipation of attacks from Al Qaeda in the wake of Bin Laden’s death, additional security forces patrolled Iraq’s streets on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' BAGHDAD — Eight years ago Osama bin Laden called on his followers to head to Iraq to fight the United States. Within months, Al Qaeda in Mesopotamia took form, eventually allying itself with militants from the country’s Sunni minority. The group took a leading role in the insurgency that plunged Iraq into a bloody sectarian war. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden’s Death Expected to Have Little Impact on Al Qaeda in Iraq', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T10:48:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6492a912-83f8-5ed0-a374-d624c8875931', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6492a912-83f8-5ed0-a374-d624c8875931'}, {'abstract': 'Adani Enterprises of India is acquiring the Abbott Point Coal Terminal in Queensland, Australia, for 1.8 billion Australian dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/indias-adani-to-buy-australian-port-for-2-billion/', 'snippet': 'Adani Enterprises of India is acquiring the Abbott Point Coal Terminal in Queensland, Australia, for 1.8 billion Australian dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adani Enterprises of India said on Tuesday that it would acquire the Abbott Point Coal Terminal in the state of Queensland in northeast Australia for 1.8 billion Australian dollars, or roughly $2 billion, giving a boost to an area still recovering from a series of floods last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adani of India to Buy Australian Port for $2 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T10:55:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dc1bf80-ceee-5368-9d35-73dd553c2cb9', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dc1bf80-ceee-5368-9d35-73dd553c2cb9'}, {'abstract': 'For Osama bin Laden, New York was a frequent theme in the messages he broadcast from his hideout after Sept. 11, 2001.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/bin-laden-on-new-york-in-his-own-words/', 'snippet': 'For Osama bin Laden, New York was a frequent theme in the messages he broadcast from his hideout after Sept. 11, 2001.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For Osama bin Laden, New York was a recurring theme in speeches and interviews after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon