0-c9ed819c4ef6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/d6eea7de-06d2-574e-b220-c9ed819c4ef6'}, {'abstract': '“The Scottsboro Boys” received 12 nominations, second to “The Book of Mormon,” which led, as expected, with 14. Check back here for more updates throughout the day.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/live-blogging-the-tony-award-nominations-3/', 'snippet': '“The Scottsboro Boys” received 12 nominations, second to “The Book of Mormon,” which led, as expected, with 14. Check back here for more updates throughout the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nominees for the 65th annual Tony Awards were announced this morning. Updates and analysis from the announcement, and developments as they unfolded, are below. A slide show of the nominees for best musical can be found here and a slide show for the nominees for best play can be found here. Make sure to fill out the interactive ballot here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Book of Mormon’ and ‘Scottsboro Boys’ Lead Tony Nominations', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T11:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/35ec7bd7-5935-51d3-bb44-b7568027709d', 'word_count': 3515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35ec7bd7-5935-51d3-bb44-b7568027709d'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian Albert Brooks, who publishes his debut comic novel, “2030,” next Tuesday, finds humor amid misery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/books/albert-brooks-the-novelist-relishes-his-worries-in-2030.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian Albert Brooks, who publishes his debut comic novel, “2030,” next Tuesday, finds humor amid misery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — For a guy who just wrote a whole book about the myriad catastrophes that could befall the United States in the next 20 years, Albert Brooks says he’s not interested in end-of-the-world scenarios and, more to the point, he’s too nervous to contemplate them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/brooks/brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/brooks/brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/02/arts/brooks/brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Comedian Laughs All the Way to Dystopia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Comedian Laughs All the Way To Dystopia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Albert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T12:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/966b9083-1e3e-5c9b-abe2-981dbc152396', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/966b9083-1e3e-5c9b-abe2-981dbc152396'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan of Turkey, a key regional power broker, made his harshest comments to date about Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/africa/04libya.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan of Turkey, a key regional power broker, made his harshest comments to date about Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — In his harshest comments to date on the situation in Libya, Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdogan of Turkey, a regional power broker, told reporters here on Tuesday that Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi had chosen “blood, tears, oppression” and that he must “immediately step down.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/LIBYA_span/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/LIBYA_span/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/LIBYA_span/LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/LIBYA_span/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/LIBYA_span/LIBYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkish Leader Says Qaddafi Must Step Down Immediately', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkish Prime Minister Says Qaddafi Must Leave Now', 