good point on my Keynes post:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In The Long Run, Keynes Is Dead', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T13:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a609f345-6cce-54b6-bbec-6e5261ccfd6e', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a609f345-6cce-54b6-bbec-6e5261ccfd6e'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously proposed chat-up lines.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/want-to-be-my-co-vocabularist/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously proposed chat-up lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists have generously proposed chat-up lines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Be My Co-Vocabularist?', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T13:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/90dff4a0-e963-5de4-ae68-d330e7dcf38c', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90dff4a0-e963-5de4-ae68-d330e7dcf38c'}, {'abstract': 'A desire to make a different photograph in Tahrir Square taught Jacopo Quaranta, 27, that he doesn’t have to pretend to be what he isn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/during-egyptian-uprising-a-scene-of-hope/', 'snippet': 'A desire to make a different photograph in Tahrir Square taught Jacopo Quaranta, 27, that he doesn’t have to pretend to be what he isn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacopo Quaranta, 27, an Italian native and a graduate of the International Center of Photography school, spent a week in Egypt during the uprising. He spoke with Kerri MacDonald last week in New York. Their conversation, part of the Turning Point series, has been edited and condensed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'During Egyptian Uprising, a Scene of Hope', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hartmann, Erich', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T13:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e078b000-b0df-51d5-b3e1-d79c58486225', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e078b000-b0df-51d5-b3e1-d79c58486225'}, {'abstract': 'Efforts to prevent an Illinois town from flooding appeared to be working hours after a levee was breached.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/us/04levee.html', 'snippet': 'Efforts to prevent an Illinois town from flooding appeared to be working hours after a levee was breached.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST PRAIRIE, Mo. — Last-ditch