: 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T13:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael H. Krimminger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Krimminger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e07824ce-982d-5b3e-b08b-e6981f612643', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e07824ce-982d-5b3e-b08b-e6981f612643'}, {'abstract': 'The government says the bank and its mortgage unit lied about loans included in a program to insure mortgages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/business/04mortgage.html', 'snippet': 'The government says the bank and its mortgage unit lied about loans included in a program to insure mortgages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States government sued Deutsche Bank on Tuesday, accusing it of lying about the quality of home loans it handled under a government program and demanding that the bank repay hundreds of millions of dollars of losses on those loans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/business/04mortgagePicA/04mortgagePicA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/04/business/04mortgagePicA/04mortgagePicA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/business/04mortgagePicA/04mortgagePicA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/business/04mortgagePicA/04mortgagePicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/business/04mortgagePicA/04mortgagePicA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Sues Deutsche Bank Over Loan Practices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Sues Big Bank Over Loan Practices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:03:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Story', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Story', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f0213c7-6c31-592e-9359-e6c5155dfa47', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f0213c7-6c31-592e-9359-e6c5155dfa47'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers at Penn State University found that adding vegetable puree to various recipes didn’t change the flavor much but did lead to big reductions in the amount of calories consumed.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/recipes-to-curb-appetites/', 'snippet': 'Researchers at Penn State University found that adding vegetable puree to various recipes didn’t change the flavor much but did lead to big reductions in the amount of calories consumed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I explain in today’s Well column, “Adding Food and Subtracting Calories, “ researchers at Penn State University found that adding vegetable purée to various recipes didn’t change the flavor much but did lead to big reductions in the amount of calories consumed. The result was that diners felt full after eating fewer calories, allowing the vegetable purée mixtures to act as natural appetite suppressants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recipes to Curb Appetites', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:07:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d45b0d57-b504-5eec-aa0c-768f0554d2c1', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d45b0d57-b504-5eec-aa0c-768f0554d2c1'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors say the bank “repeatedly lied” in order to be allowed to participate in a Federal Housing Administration program that insures mortgages', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/government-sues-deutsche-bank-over-mortgages/', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors say the bank “repeatedly lied” in order to be allowed to participate in a Federal Housing Administration program that insures mortgages', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal prosecutors on Tuesday filed a civil mortgage fraud lawsuit against Deutsche Bank and its MortgageIT unit, accusing the bank of “reckless lending practices.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Sues Deutsche Bank Over Mortgages', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7385eef6-fb3d-5bd2-8619-8cae7179b395', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7385eef6-fb3d-5bd2-8619-8cae7179b395'}, {'abstract': 'Toby’s Corner, winner of the Wood Memorial and a leading contender for the Kentucky Derby, injured his left hind leg and will not run in the race on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/tobys-corner-is-out-of-the-derby/', 'snippet': 'Toby’s Corner, winner of the Wood Memorial and a leading contender for the Kentucky Derby, injured his left hind leg and will not run in the race on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toby’s Corner, winner of the Wood Memorial and a leading contender for the Kentucky Derby, is lame in his left hind leg and will not run in Saturday’s Derby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toby’s Corner Is Out of the Derby', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Goetz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goetz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bdb6141-2607-5cd4-b46c-4c5eec7de256', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bdb6141-2607-5cd4-b46c-4c5eec7de256'}, {'abstract': 'Much of the tilapia farmed in China for export is frozen and then treated with carbon monoxide, a gas that prevents meat and seafood from discoloring as it ages; when it is thawed, it looks like new.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/when-fresh-fish-is-really-frozen/', 'snippet': 'Much of the tilapia farmed in China for export is frozen and then treated with carbon monoxide, a gas that prevents meat and seafood from discoloring as it ages; when it is thawed, it looks like new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tilapia arrayed between the salmon steaks and flounder filets at an upscale supermarket down the block from my home in Manhattan looks as if it were plucked out of the water yesterday, and it costs far less than those other fish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When ‘Fresh’ Fish is Really Frozen', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Monoxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frozen Foods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tilapia (Fish)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b419ba16-b51e-5722-a0e2-2daae2684d53', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b419ba16-b51e-5722-a0e2-2daae2684d53'}, {'abstract': 'The Nissan NV200 van has won New York City’s Taxi of Tomorrow competition.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/nissan-chosen-as-the-taxi-of-tomorrow/', 'snippet': 'The Nissan NV200 van has won New York City’s Taxi of Tomorrow competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 12:25 p.m. | Sliding doors. Charging stations for mobile devices. Reading lights. Even passenger airbags.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nissan Chosen as the Taxi of Tomorrow', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/84685f4a-d328-5aa6-812f-00a0bb0487bd', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84685f4a-d328-5aa6-812f-00a0bb0487bd'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Haynes discusses shooting a concert film in the indie band’s hometown, Louisville, Ky.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/todd-haynes-to-make-film-of-my-morning-jacket-show/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Haynes discusses shooting a concert film in the indie band’s hometown, Louisville, Ky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last couple of years, in a series called Unstaged, American Express has entrusted the direction of its online concert broadcasts to a handful of accomplished filmmakers, coming up with some interesting combinations: Terry Gilliam and Arcade Fire. John Legend (and the Roots) and Spike Lee. Duran Duran and David Lynch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Todd Haynes to Make Film of My Morning Jacket Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T14:34:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9c53dc-a029-58e3-a242-03c0701f32b8', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9c53dc-a029-58e3-a242-03c0701f32b8'}, {'abstract': 'The upheaval in Arab countries is driving up oil prices, creating a windfall for oil producers and new economic challenges for their oil-importing neighbors, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/uneven-prospects-for-the-arab-world/', 'snippet': 'The upheaval in Arab countries is driving up oil prices, creating a windfall for oil producers and new economic challenges for their oil-importing neighbors, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The popular uprisings across the Arab world are defining a new order in the region. But as the transition continues, the area’s economies are diverging sharply, posing added challenges to leaders as they seek to cultivate greater stability.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uneven Prospects for the Arab World', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )',