roblem with air bags that deploy so forcefully they can injure or kill a driver. The automaker said that cars involved in crashes may not have been repaired with the proper air-bag assemblies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its fourth action to fix a problem with an air bag that deploys so forcefully it can injure or kill a driver, Honda announced late on Monday that it was recalling 833,000 more vehicles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honda Expands Air-Bag Recall to 833,000 Additional Vehicles', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T16:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c2b999c-4b15-54e6-96c2-b14761534b48', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c2b999c-4b15-54e6-96c2-b14761534b48'}, {'abstract': 'A reminder that most of our daily struggles are real luxuries.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/save-the-mothers/', 'snippet': 'A reminder that most of our daily struggles are real luxuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While you make your brunch plans, and search through racks of cards praising Mom, take a moment to remember that there are many places where it is dangerous to be a mother.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Save the Mothers', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Save the Children', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T16:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/69ff8fe8-4c82-5bbb-8ac0-95ddd0de10c3', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69ff8fe8-4c82-5bbb-8ac0-95ddd0de10c3'}, {'abstract': 'White House officials said they were still weighing whether releasing a photo of Osama Bin Laden’s body would do more harm than good.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/white-house-weighs-the-photo/', 'snippet': 'White House officials said they were still weighing whether releasing a photo of Osama Bin Laden’s body would do more harm than good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To release or not to release?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Weighs Whether to Release ‘the Photo’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T16:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/008f5bd1-083a-5ef4-a035-00f111f99129', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/008f5bd1-083a-5ef4-a035-00f111f99129'}, {'abstract': 'After difficult talks, City Ballet and its dancers agree on a contract.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/city-ballet-reaches-accord-with-dancers/', 'snippet': 'After difficult talks, City Ballet and its dancers agree on a contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dancers with the New York City Ballet voted 63-1 on Tuesday to accept a contract after contentious negotiations over issues like overtime and salary. “I’m pretty excited,” said Devin Alberda, a member of the company’s corps de ballet who serves on the dancers’ six-member negotiating committee. “I don’t think we got everything we wanted, but we made a lot of progress in terms of our work conditions.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Ballet Reaches Accord With Dancers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T16:43:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a338f0-05d6-51a3-9bbe-4146b32eb1ca', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a338f0-05d6-51a3-9bbe-4146b32eb1ca'}, {'abstract': '“Spouse vs. House,” a home-decorating reality show that contrasts the visions of husband and wife, begins on Wednesday on TLC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/arts/television/spouse-vs-house-on-tlc-review.html', 'snippet': '“Spouse vs. House,” a home-decorating reality show that contrasts the visions of husband and wife, begins on Wednesday on TLC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Bravo is the network devoted to baroque expressions of coastal affluence, TLC exists as its spirit cousin and opposition: a cable channel committed to the ostensibly bizarre habits of non-elites. Producers take us from Pennsylvania to Arkansas to Utah and to other places that are neither West Hollywood nor East Hampton to uncover overbreeders (“19 Kids and Counting,” “Kate Plus 8”), polygamists (“Sister Wives”), addicts of household flotsam (“Hoarding: Buried Alive”) and the strange people who submit their young children to spray tans (“Toddlers & Tiaras”). Bravo ridicules the world of the well to do; TLC, instead, implicitly makes fun of the idea that those hoping to avoid encounters with creepiness or bad taste are safe beyond the realm of four-ply cashmere.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/spouse/spouse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/spouse/spouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/spouse/spouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Say Man Cave, I Say Good Taste', 'kicker': 'Television Review | ‘Spouse vs. House’ ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Say Man Cave, I Say Good Taste', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1,