gers-next/', 'snippet': 'The Mavericks owner Mark Cuban might be interested in adding the Dodgers to his portfolio if the team goes up for sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dallas Mavericks owner Mark Cuban has said he’s “done chasing” baseball teams he wants to purchase, without quite ruling out a run at the troubled Dodgers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuban May Pursue Dodgers Next', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T17:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/772f8222-8853-5940-8f55-4461798ffd55', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/772f8222-8853-5940-8f55-4461798ffd55'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Bergen, the author of three books about terrorism, will write a book about the manhunt for Osama bin Laden for Crown Publishers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/peter-bergen-to-write-book-on-bin-laden-manhunt/', 'snippet': 'Peter Bergen, the author of three books about terrorism, will write a book about the manhunt for Osama bin Laden for Crown Publishers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than 48 hours after Osama bin Laden’s death, the book deals have begun. Peter Bergen will write the “definitive” book on the hunt for Bin Laden, his publisher said on Tuesday. Crown Publishers, part of Random House, said it had acquired a new book by Mr. Bergen that it described as “an immersive, definitive account of the operation that killed the world’s most wanted man.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Bergen to Write Book on Bin Laden Manhunt', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergen, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T17:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4976d74f-7e63-5659-a3b8-fb6684a0848a', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4976d74f-7e63-5659-a3b8-fb6684a0848a'}, {'abstract': 'A pastry shop in Paris’s Marais neighborhood is devoted exclusively to pâte à choux, or cream puffs.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/let-them-eat-choux/', 'snippet': 'A pastry shop in Paris’s Marais neighborhood is devoted exclusively to pâte à choux, or cream puffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Popelini, the pastry shop Lauren Koumetz opened this month in Paris’s Marais neighborhood, is devoted exclusively to choux à la crème, or cream puffs, the bite-size flavor shots that offer a sugar lover an alternative to France’s superstar macaron. On any given day, the choux are lined up in a half dozen flavors including dark chocolate, lemon praline, salted butter caramel, Madagascar vanilla and rose; some have an additional confit filling of passion fruit or raspberry. And then there’s the choux du jour, dreamed up by the pastry chef Alice Barday, which might be strawberry-litchi, Earl Grey tea, pear, or tiramisu, inspired by the Italian dessert with whipped cream, almonds and crunchy chocolate sprinkles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let Them Eat Choux', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T17:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Voight', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voight', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c01c652-e7ea-53ca-bc30-21076c52f08b', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c01c652-e7ea-53ca-bc30-21076c52f08b'}, {'abstract': 'If you follow your company’s expense policy, you shouldn’t be held liable for your corporate card balance.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/troubled-employers-and-your-company-charge-card/', 'snippet': 'If you follow your company’s expense policy, you shouldn’t be held liable for your corporate card balance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buried near the end of a lengthy New York magazine profile of voluptuous financier Lynn Tilton was a nugget that caught our eye here at Bucks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Troubled Employers and Your Company Charge Card', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 