thor of the Year” at last night’s Children’s Choice Book Awards, to tell us about three of his own childhood favorites. Here they are, in his words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today marks the publication date of “The Throne of Fire,” the second in Rick Riordan’s latest mega-series, “The Kane Chronicles,” for which Disney has announced an initial print run of 1.5 million copies. Mr. Riordan is probably best known for his #1 best-selling “Percy Jackson and the Olympians,” also for middle grade readers, though he writes novels for adults as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Riordan’s Favorite Childhood Books', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T19:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff02cc35-4b53-5cfd-8ab5-62f0e562b6d3', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff02cc35-4b53-5cfd-8ab5-62f0e562b6d3'}, {'abstract': 'The Puig Beauty and Fashion Group, a Spanish company whose primary focus is perfumes, is acquiring a controlling 60 percent share of the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/business/global/04iht-fashion04.html', 'snippet': 'The Puig Beauty and Fashion Group, a Spanish company whose primary focus is perfumes, is acquiring a controlling 60 percent share of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jean Paul Gaultier, the French designer whose fashion house has been in partnership with Hermès since 1999, said Tuesday that the Puig Beauty and Fashion Group, a Spanish company whose primary focus is perfumes, was acquiring a controlling 60 percent share of the company. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hermès Is Selling Its Stake in Gaultier’s Fashion House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hermès Is Selling Its Stake In Gaultier’s Fashion House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T19:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzy Menkes and David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Menkes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a2f5659-4fcb-5e86-9aa6-35827a542526', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a2f5659-4fcb-5e86-9aa6-35827a542526'}, {'abstract': 'With firmness in the right, as God gives us to see the right.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/how-should-we-think-of-the-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'With firmness in the right, as God gives us to see the right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Brad DeLong, Ta-Nehisi Coates argues that the Civil War wasn’t tragic in the way it’s so often portrayed. The human losses were terrible — but the war marked the end of the far greater horror of slavery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline'