': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Double Take: There Are Recipes, Too', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Torrisi Italian Specialties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T19:43:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf1fd50a-1b87-5a19-84db-1310afa84c3e', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf1fd50a-1b87-5a19-84db-1310afa84c3e'}, {'abstract': 'Every year, members of the Kalaidzhi, a group of seminomadic Roma, gather in a field outside the town of Stara Zagora to conduct the complex negotiations on a bride price that traditionally lead to marriage. However, support for marriage traditions is waning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/04/world/europe/04iht-letter04-roma-ss.html', 'snippet': 'Every year, members of the Kalaidzhi, a group of seminomadic Roma, gather in a field outside the town of Stara Zagora to conduct the complex negotiations on a bride price that traditionally lead to marriage. However, support for marriage tradition...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, members of the Kalaidzhi, a group of seminomadic Roma, gather in a field outside the town of Stara Zagora to conduct the complex negotiations on a bride price that traditionally lead to marriage. However, support for marriage traditions is waning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/world/europe/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/world/europe/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/world/europe/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6/04iht-letter04-roma-ss-slide-AXY6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bulgaria, a Tradition Meets New Realities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bulgaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Romani People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T19:50:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f87d1a57-4e66-56fe-8ff9-44990fa27a43', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f87d1a57-4e66-56fe-8ff9-44990fa27a43'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco-based group wins the Avery Fisher Prize and shares the Polar Music Prize with Patti Smith.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/kronos-quartet-honored-with-two-awards/', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco-based group wins the Avery Fisher Prize and shares the Polar Music Prize with Patti Smith.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the San Francisco-based Kronos Quartet prepared for a European tour, beginning on Thursday in Athens, its bags became a little heavier on Tuesday with two major awards. Kronos will receive the Avery Fisher Prize, awarded in New York to individuals or chamber ensembles for outstanding achievement and excellence in music, as well as the Polar Music Prize, awarded in Stockholm (not on the quartet’s current itinerary), also intended to recognize exceptional achievement in music. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kronos Quartet Honored with Two Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kronos Quartet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stockholm (Sweden)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T19:50:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/769296b7-ad7a-5271-b579-39a7204e97a6', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/769296b7-ad7a-5271-b579-39a7204e97a6'}, {'abstract': 'In his last days, bin Laden was not surrounded by a circle of heavily armed Arab bodyguards or mujahedeen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/asia/04compound.html', 'snippet': 'In his last days, bin Laden was not surrounded by a circle of heavily armed Arab bodyguards or mujahedeen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABBOTTABAD, Pakistan — In his last days, Osama bin Laden was not surrounded by a circle of heavily armed Arab bodyguards or mujahedeen who had fought with him in Afghanistan against the Soviet Union. Rather, he relied on two Pakistanis, one of whom, according to American officials, was his most trusted courier. Both men died with him in the American raid on their compound.', 'print_s