_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/board-disciplines-3-doctors/', 'snippet': 'The doctors had failed to disclose their financial ties to the development of an artificial disk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Board of Medical Examiners in New Jersey, which is responsible for licensing doctors practicing in the state, said on Tuesday that it had disciplined three orthopedic surgeons because they did not disclose their personal financial interests in the success of an artificial spinal disk they were studying in clinical trials that were used by federal regulators to approve the disk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Board Disciplines 3 Doctors', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spine (Body Part)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T20:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/99072df3-849c-5bf6-a419-cfd38092a081', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99072df3-849c-5bf6-a419-cfd38092a081'}, {'abstract': 'The USA Network sent out the stars of its series to speak about the cable channel’s plans for the 2011-12 season.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/usa-networks-twist-on-upfront-puts-stars-up-front/', 'snippet': 'The USA Network sent out the stars of its series to speak about the cable channel’s plans for the 2011-12 season.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:50 a.m. | Updated The executives at the USA Network cable channel decided to have some fun with the first large-scale presentation to advertisers, agencies and reporters of their coming season by sending out the stars of USA series to speak in their place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'USA Network’s Twist on ‘Upfront’ Puts Stars Up Front', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T20:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcbe3626-9614-5ac5-b71c-ecc998a93835', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcbe3626-9614-5ac5-b71c-ecc998a93835'}, {'abstract': 'Two engineers involved in past scandals are working in the sport again.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/scandal-scarred-formula-one-men-return/', 'snippet': 'Two engineers involved in past scandals are working in the sport again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After disappointing performances by the Williams Formula One car in the first three races, the team announced on Tuesday that its technical director, Sam Michael, and its chief aerodynamicist, Jon Tomlinson, had resigned, effective at the end of the season. The team also announced that Mike Coughlan, the race car designer behind a spying scandal four years ago, would join the team in June as chief engineer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scandal-Scarred Formula One Men Return', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T20:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/240ffad3-17c8-5165-be9d-684281fe7f5b', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/240ffad3-17c8-5165-be9d-684281fe7f5b'}, {'abstract': 'Two engineers involved in past scandals are working in the sport again.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/scandal-scarred-formula-one-men-return/', 'snippet': 'Two engineers involved in past scandals are working in the sport again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After disappointing performances by the Williams Formula One car in the first three races, the team announced on Tuesday that its technical director, Sam Michael, and its chief aerodynamicist, Jon Tomlinson, had resigned, effective at the end of the season. The team also announced that Mike Coughlan, the race car designer behind a spying scandal four years ago, would join the team in June as chief engineer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scandal-Scarred Formula One Men Return', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T20:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/726e6860-090c-5ba3-9448-6b78d21ddcd3', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/726e6860-090c-5ba3-9448-6b78d21ddcd3'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors don’t often make it to Germantown Avenue, which makes for a great low-cost historic detour if you’re in town from elsewhere, or an economical day trip from as far away as Washington or New York.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/off-the-beaten-path-history-in-philadelphia/', 'snippet': 'Visitors don’t often make it to Germantown Avenue, which makes for a great low-cost historic detour if you’re in town from elsewhere, or an economical day trip from as far away as Washington or New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The No. 23 city bus running along the cobblestones is still known as the “trolley,”and you can take it to visit the house where a young Benjamin Franklin stopped for advice on books or to other homes where Revolutionary War battles left powder marks and bloodstains. George Washington slept here, a lot, and decades later so did runaway slaves at a well-preserved stop on the Underground Railroad. There’s also a homey lunch spot known for its veggie burger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Beaten Path, History in Philadelphia', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T20:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/efed81a6-df05-5a35-9dd9-182a8f33113f', 'word_count': 1406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efed81a6-df05-5a35-9dd9-182a8f33113f'}, {'abstract': 'A demonstration by the farmer Tim Huppe of how to yoke a pair of oxen for work in the field, fro