': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/8968b744-80c1-5aab-9876-ebe98407401b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/8968b744-80c1-5aab-9876-ebe98407401b'}, {'abstract': 'The New Democrats, stuck in a distant third place for years, broke through systemic disadvantages on Monday to become the main opposition party in Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/analyzing-a-sea-change-in-canada/', 'snippet': 'The New Democrats, stuck in a distant third place for years, broke through systemic disadvantages on Monday to become the main opposition party in Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even for observers who were the most optimistic about the New Democratic Party’s chances, the results of Monday’s general election in Canada were nothing short of astounding. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analyzing a Sea Change in Canada', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Democratic Party (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'British Columbia (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ontario (Canada)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T21:21:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renard Sexton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sexton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '