he window for them to hatch has closed.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/there-will-be-no-baby-hawks/', 'snippet': 'For more than a month, a red-tailed hawk has tended her eggs in a nest overlooking Washington Square Park, devotedly but fruitlessly. And now, experts say, the window for them to hatch has closed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Violet the red-tailed hawk has been sitting on those eggs for a very long while. But sometimes, eggs don’t hatch. This appears to be one of those times. Read more »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barring a Miracle, There Will Be No Baby Hawks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T21:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc14f0f-c568-5ade-b430-39758cbc8178', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc14f0f-c568-5ade-b430-39758cbc8178'}, {'abstract': '“Extraordinary Stories,” by the Argentine director Mariano Llinás, is a contagiously playful and thrillingly inventive work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/movies/extraordinary-stories-directed-by-mariano-llinas-review.html', 'snippet': '“Extraordinary Stories,” by the Argentine director Mariano Llinás, is a contagiously playful and thrillingly inventive work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The independent Argentine film “Extraordinary Stories” interweaves the obscurely circuitous story lines of three cryptically named and decidedly unextraordinary characters: H (Agustín Mendilaharzu, the film’s cinematographer), a visibly bored civil engineer; X (Mariano Llinás, the director), a frustrated architect slumming as a land surveyor; and Z (Walter Jakob), a midlevel bureaucrat in a provincial agricultural agency.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/EXTRAORDINARY/EXTRAORDINARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/EXTRAORDINARY/EXTRAORDINARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/EXTRAORDINARY/EXTRAORDINARY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/EXTRAORDINARY/EXTRAORDINARY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/arts/EXTRAORDINARY/EXTRAORDINARY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'H Plus X Plus Z, Formula for 3 Intersecting Lives', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Extraordinary Stories'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'H Plus X Plus Z, Formula For 3 Intersecting Lives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T21:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Brunick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brunick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9981b250-0cd9-5728-ab1a-fc5536083af0', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9981b250-0cd9-5728-ab1a-fc5536083af0'}, {'abstract': 'The Webby Awards, which recognize excellence in online and mobile applications, Web design, video, and a number of other categories, announced the judges’ picks and the winners of the “People’s Voice” awards.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/funny-or-die-webby-awards-choose-funny/', 'snippet': 'The Webby Awards, which recognize excellence in online and mobile applications, Web design, video, and a number of other categories, announced the judges’ picks and the winners of the “People’s Voice” awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Justin Bieber lost out on the Grammy Award for best new artist this year, all his fans could do was complain (and hack the Wikipedia page of the winner, Esperanza Spalding).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Funny or Die: Webby Awards Choose Funny', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galifianakis, Zach', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kudrow, Lisa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCADE FIRE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foursquare', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T21:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/038a818e-b14f-5b2b-b2c4-a58af7b2c37c', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/038a818e-b14f-5b2b-b2c4-a58af7b2c37c'}, {'abstract': 'The caretaker prime minister, José Sócrates, suggested the plan involved more lenient conditions than those agreed to by Greece and Ireland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/business/global/04portugal.html', 'snippet': 'The caretaker prime minister, José Sócrates, suggested the plan involved more lenient conditions than those agreed to by Greece and Ireland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Portugal agreed on Tuesday to accept an international aid plan of 78 billion euros ($116 billion) that the country’s caretaker prime minister, José Sócrates, suggested would involve more lenient conditions than those imposed on Greece and Ireland in return for similar bailouts. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/business/4PORTUGAL/4PORTUGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Portugal Agrees to a $116 Billion Bailout', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Portugal Agrees to a $116 Billion Bailout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Socrates, Jose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N