blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/a-new-first-stop-for-homeless-families/', 'snippet': 'The city’s new intake center in the South Bronx replaces the old center at the same location, where families often had to spend the night sleeping on hard benches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city’s Department of Homeless Services on Tuesday opened a new intake center in the South Bronx, a $65.5 million building designed to greet families seeking shelter with much more of a smile than in the old days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New First Stop for Homeless Families', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeless Services Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T22:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a605462d-9ced-5561-94ff-40c873b58027', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a605462d-9ced-5561-94ff-40c873b58027'}, {'abstract': 'With much of the port city of Misurata reclaimed, part of the rebels’ success has roots in the network of hidden metal workshops, where the uprising’s killing tools have been assembled and pushed out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/03/world/africa/20110504_MISURATA.html', 'snippet': 'With much of the port city of Misurata reclaimed, part of the rebels’ success has roots in the network of hidden metal workshops, where the uprising’s killing tools have been assembled and pushed out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With much of the port city of Misurata reclaimed, part of the rebels’ success has roots in the network of hidden metal workshops, where the uprising’s killing tools have been assembled and pushed out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/africa/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/03/world/africa/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/03/world/africa/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O/20110504_MISURATA-slide-XD0O-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The Libyan Rebels’ Hidden Weapons Shops', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T22:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3d3ee9e6-3c39-5f82-a2af-0d2f115c7db8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3d3ee9e6-3c39-5f82-a2af-0d2f115c7db8'}, {'abstract': 'A video clip on how to yoke oxen.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/teamwork/', 'snippet': 'A video clip on how to yoke oxen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, driven to a rustic frenzy by the Northeast’s oxen craze, you’ve just bought a pair of brawny bovines and are ready to put them to work in your garden. But you have no idea how to do that. For $29.95 you can buy the DVD “Training Oxen,” made in 2003 by Drew Conroy, a professor at the University of New Hampshire who is known in draft-power circles as “the ox guru.” Or, to get started, you can take a look at this clip from the DVD with Tim Huppe of BerryBrook Ox Supply, in Farmington, N.H.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teamwork', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T22:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7285afe3-31c1-56f9-a36f-f43008a3ccb2', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7285afe3-31c1-56f9-a36f-f43008a3ccb2'}, {'abstract': 'A study that examined the elbow joints of dozens of predators concluded that “Tasmanian tiger” is an apt name for a creature that became extinct in the last century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/science/10obtasmania.html', 'snippet': 'A study that examined the elbow joints of dozens of predators concluded that “Tasmanian tiger” is an apt name for a creature that became extinct in the last century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was known as the Tasmanian tiger, for its striped coat, or the Tasmanian wolf, for its doglike appearance. But new research indicates the bone structure and hunting habits of Thylacinus cynocephalus may make the “tiger” designation more apt.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype