eline.html', 'snippet': 'A federal prosecutor said the penalty was a wake-up call as the Gulf of Mexico spill inquiry is being conducted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — BP will pay $25 million in civil fines to settle charges arising from two spills from its network of pipelines in Alaska in 2006 and from a willful failure to comply with a government order to properly maintain the pipelines to prevent corrosion, federal officials announced on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BP Is Fined $25 Million for ’06 Spills at Pipelines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BP Is Fined $25 Million For ’06 Spills At Pipelines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80e7a1cb-af33-5e8f-8e47-a69b510d7620', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80e7a1cb-af33-5e8f-8e47-a69b510d7620'}, {'abstract': 'Toby’s Corner, the winner of the Wood Memorial, is pulled from the race, further diluting a now-weak field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/sports/04racing.html', 'snippet': 'Toby’s Corner, the winner of the Wood Memorial, is pulled from the race, further diluting a now-weak field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — There will be 20 horses in the gate Saturday for the 137th running of the Kentucky Derby, but it is a stretch to say that they are the cream of this 3-year-old crop. The field lost another contender Tuesday when Toby’s Corner, the winner of the Wood Memorial, came up lame in his left hind leg and was declared out of the race.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-RACING/Y-RACING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-RACING/Y-RACING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-RACING/Y-RACING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 845, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-RACING/Y-RACING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-RACING/Y-RACING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Once-Promising Field Gets Weaker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loss of One Derby Hopeful; Intrigue About Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Motion, Graham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:45:44+