Threats', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A National Security Strategy That Doesn’t Focus on Threats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc612664-831d-5eb3-8cbf-462f228af8ea', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc612664-831d-5eb3-8cbf-462f228af8ea'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Asmus advocated the inclusion of such nations as Poland, Hungary and the Czech Republic into the alliance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/europe/04asmus.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Asmus advocated the inclusion of such nations as Poland, Hungary and the Czech Republic into the alliance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronald D. Asmus, an early proponent of expanding the Atlantic alliance to include Eastern European nations and a key figure in the Clinton administration’s realization of that vision, died April 30 in Belgium. He was 53.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/04asmus-1/04asmus-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/04asmus-1/04asmus-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/04asmus-1/04asmus-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ronald D. Asmus, Official Who Favored Expanded NATO, Dies at 53', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ronald D. Asmus, 53; Favored Expanded NATO', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asmus, Ronald D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21e873c-bb55-540c-b427-9b3875a34413', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21e873c-bb55-540c-b427-9b3875a34413'}, {'abstract': 'China’s top internal security official called for building a database containing information on each of China’s 1.34 billion residents to manage public dissent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/asia/04briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'China’s top internal security official called for building a database containing information on each of China’s 1.34 billion residents to manage public dissent.', 'lead_paragraph': ' China’s top internal security official called for building a database containing information on each of China’s 1.34 billion residents to improve “social management,” a term that encompasses the state’s efforts to manage public dissent and head off protests in the name of maintaining stability. The official, Zhou Yongkang, said the system should be based on the resident identity cards issued to every Chinese citizen, and should include such details as each person’s tax record and history of education and employment, as well as what property and vehicles he or she owns. Writing in Qiushi, a Communist Party magazine, Mr. Zhou said that a comprehensive database would help neighborhood watchmen enforce stability. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Database on Each Citizen Is Urged', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Database on Each Citizen Is Urged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3005ef-3744-51e9-b914-4c418e54340e', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3005ef-3744-51e9-b914-4c418e54340e'}, {'abstract': 'A new government study says nearly one in 10 children and almost one in 12 Americans of all ages now has asthma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/health/research/04asthma.html', 'snippet': 'A new government study says nearly one in 10 children and almost one in 12 Americans of all ages now has asthma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are suffering from asthma in record numbers, according to a study released Tuesday by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Nearly one in 10 children and almost one in 12 Americans of all ages now has asthma, government researchers said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asthma Rate Rises Sharply in U.S., Government Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asthma Rate Rises Sharply in U.S., Government Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-03T23:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26b4980-7b4c-5bc5-bd38-e0cd2e60ba5f', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26b4980-7b4c-5bc5-bd38-e0cd2e60ba5f'}, {'abstract': 'The Cue r1 radio, from Cue Acoustics, looks retro, but sounds pretty up to date.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/the-cue-r1-alarm-clock-is-a-time-machine/', 'snippet': 'The Cue r1 radio, from Cue Acoustics, looks retro, but sounds pretty up to date.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Throwback” is a word the Cue r1 clock radio brings to mind. For one thing, it’s a clock radio, by which it has an AM/FM radio built in and which is tied to the clock’s alarm timer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cue r1 Alarm Clock Is a Time Machine', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPod', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speakers (Audio)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T00:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/145b2a0a-8c66-579c-90f6-3e1f49590ecf', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/145b2a0a-8c66-579c-90f6-3e1f49590ecf'}, {'abstract': 'The entire collection is to be published by 2022.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/end-in-sight-for-darwin-letters-project-thanks-to-8-2-million-in-grants/', 'snippet': 'The entire collection is to be published by 2022.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teams of scholars have spent nearly 30 years tracking down, researching and editing the more than 15,000 letters written by or to Charles Darwin. Now, thanks to $8.2 million in grants from the Evolution Education Trust, the Andrew W. Mellon Foundation, the Alfred P. Sloan Foundation, and the Isaac Newton Trust, the entire collection will be published in full by 2022. Texts of some 6,000 letters and information on 9,000 more are already available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'End in Sight for Darwin Letters Project Thanks to $8.2 Million in Grants', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darwin, Charles Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Council of Learned Societies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cambridge University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mellon Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sloan, Alfred P, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T00:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab92b2a8-31ce-5d85-94a3-d444ecce5ae9', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab92b2a8-31ce-5d85-94a3-d444ecce5ae9'}, {'abstract': 'After last season’s surprising playoff collapse against the Flyers, no series lead seems safe for the Bruins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/sports/hockey/04hockey.html', 'snippet': 'After last season’s surprising playoff collapse against the Flyers, no series lead seems safe for the Bruins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Many hockey fans would be pleased if their team had taken a two-games-to-none lead in a playoff series, especially if those victories came on the road. But not Boston Bruins fans, judging from the radio call-in shows Tuesday morning, only hours after the Bruins had won Game 2 of their second-round series, 3-2, in overtime. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-HOCKEY/Y-HOCKEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-HOCKEY/Y-HOCKEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/sports/Y-HOCKEY/Y-HOCKEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruins Have a Lead, but Not Peace of Mind', 'kicker': 'Hockey | Stanley Cup Playoffs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bruins Have Lead, But Peace of Mind Seems to Be Missing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laviolette, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T00:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80005299-23a1-5fd7-9837-1bfd1d1317e9', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80005299-23a1-5fd7-9837-1bfd1d1317e9'}, {'abstract': 'More than a dozen soldiers have been killed in clashes in Sudan’s contested Abyei area, Sudanese officials said on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/africa/04briefs-Sudan.html', 'snippet': 'More than a dozen soldiers have been killed in clashes in Sudan’s contested Abyei area, Sudanese officials said on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More than a dozen soldiers have been killed in clashes in Sudan’s contested Abyei area, Sudanese officials said on Tuesday. The fighting broke out Sunday afternoon when a convoy of northern Sudanese troops tried to enter the specially demarcated Abyei area, which straddles the border of northern and southern Sudan and is administered jointly. Southern Sudanese policemen traded fire with the northern troops; each side says the other one started it. Southern Sudan is preparing to split off from northern Sudan this summer, but Abyei’s status is unresolved. Both sides have been beefing up their military forces in Abyei, raising fears of an all-out border war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan: Deadly Clashes in Disputed Border Territory', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan: Deadly Clashes in Disputed Border Territory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T00:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5329c70-ce2e-50c7-9ab2-536ac1fcd78b', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5329c70-ce2e-50c7-9ab2-536ac1fcd78b'}, {'abstract': 'Despite some questions, the “Facebook of China” is expected to generate significant interest among American investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/03/renren-shares-are-set-for-market-debut/', 'snippet': 'Despite some questions, the “Facebook of China” is expected to generate significant interest among American investors