, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4710ad33-eb7c-5e4f-b237-80ec43c52c6a', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4710ad33-eb7c-5e4f-b237-80ec43c52c6a'}, {'abstract': 'A $700,000 red-brick, five-stall barn near the zoo will house horses for parks department patrol officers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/nyregion/horse-stable-to-open-in-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'A $700,000 red-brick, five-stall barn near the zoo will house horses for parks department patrol officers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Central Park is laced with bridle paths and dotted with pastures, and its plants were once fertilized with manure. But though carriage horses trot through it, police horses occasionally patrol it, and wooden steeds gallop around the carousel, horses have not called the park home for more than 100 years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/nyregion/STABLE1/STABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/04/nyregion/STABLE1/STABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/nyregion/STABLE1/STABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/04/nyregion/STABLE1/STABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/04/nyregion/STABLE1/STABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Central Park, Built for and With the Help of Horses, Will Again Offer Them a Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Central Park, Built for and With the Help of Horses, Will Again Offer Them a Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barns', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benepe, Adrian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Park Conservancy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T01:19:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f1043cd-a1e5-5294-8e42-503f530bd1e7', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f1043cd-a1e5-5294-8e42-503f530bd1e7'}, {'abstract': 'With Osama bin Laden’s death, federal prosecutors in Manhattan are expected to close the case against the leader of Al Qaeda that began with an indictment in 1998.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/nyregion/with-bin-ladens-death-seeking-the-dismissal-of-all-charges.html', 'snippet': 'With Osama bin Laden’s death, federal prosecutors in Manhattan are expected to close the case against the leader of Al Qaeda that began with an indictment in 1998.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It should happen with little or no fanfare, but it will still represent a moment that some thought might never occur: federal prosecutors in Manhattan are expected to file court papers this week that will formally ask a judge to 