'New research suggests that the Japanese language is not descended from that of the hunter-gatherers who first inhabited the islands some 30,000 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers studying the various dialects of Japanese have concluded that all are descended from a founding language taken to the Japanese islands about 2,200 years ago. The finding sheds new light on the origin of the Japanese people, suggesting that their language is descended from that of the rice-growing farmers who arrived in Japan from the Korean Peninsula, and not from the hunter-gatherers who first inhabited the islands some 30,000 years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding on Dialects Casts New Light on the Origins of the Japanese People', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding on Dialects Casts New Light on the Origins of the Japanese People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T04:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a43b268-bbbb-5379-989d-0b8ae54b83d4', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a43b268-bbbb-5379-989d-0b8ae54b83d4'}, {'abstract': 'Three explosions shook the neighborhood of Dora in south Baghdad on Tuesday, killing at least 10 and wounding 28, according to a local security official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/world/middleeast/04briefs-Iraq.html', 'snippet': 'Three explosions shook the neighborhood of Dora in south Baghdad on Tuesday, killing at least 10 and wounding 28, according to a local security official.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Three explosions shook the neighborhood of Dora in south Baghdad on Tuesday, killing at least 10 and wounding 28, according to a local security official. It was the third straight day in which Dora had been attacked. Dora is predominantly Sunni, although the attack on Tuesday evening occurred in a Shiite area. Improvised explosive devices and magnetic bombs were detonated on Sunday and Monday, injuring 12 people, including four police officers and a government official. Members of Al Qaeda in Mesopotamia have said they would increase attacks after Osama bin Laden’s death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Third Day of Blasts in Baghdad Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Third Day of Blasts in Baghdad Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T04:24:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e777fde3-cecc-583c-aa0e-8a4206a730a0', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e777fde3-cecc-583c-aa0e-8a42