low-salt diet, how credit card data is stolen and sold and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/wednesday-reading-honda-widens-airbag-recall/', 'snippet': 'Honda expands an air-bag recall, study stirs debate over low-salt diet, how credit card data is stolen and sold and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet .', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Honda Widens Air-Bag Recall', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T12:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/46ca0c1a-8e11-5ae6-978e-c728e6dea5a1', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46ca0c1a-8e11-5ae6-978e-c728e6dea5a1'}, {'abstract': 'Rising interest rates a day after a huge bailout show that Portugal’s troubles are not over.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/business/global/05portugal.html', 'snippet': 'Rising interest rates a day after a huge bailout show that Portugal’s troubles are not over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day after agreeing to a $115.5 billion rescue package, Portugal was forced to offer higher interest rates on its debt, spurring fears that, as in Greece and Ireland after their aid deals, financing costs in the country will continue to escalate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source':