 job performance approval rating among both Republican and Democratic voters, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/bin-ladens-killing-helps-presidents-poll-numbers/', 'snippet': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden has given President Obama a sharp bump in his job performance approval rating among both Republican and Democratic voters, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our colleagues James Dao and Dalia Sussman report that the operation in Pakistan that killed Osama bin Laden has given President Obama a sharp bump in his job performance approval rating among both Republican and Democratic voters, climbing to 57 percent from 46 percent in April. Many more Americans now approve of the job he is doing as president and of the way he is handling foreign policy, the war in Afghanistan and the threat of terrorism, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden’s Killing Helps President’s Poll Numbers', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T12:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/80506c4e-88a4-5db3-9642-d7b4a5b96b9e', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80506c4e-88a4-5db3-9642-d7b4a5b96b9e'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: a symposium on legal representation for immigrants, the cab of the future, the beginnin