value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/370db631-8059-5576-ba14-1dbe0ec6040a', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/370db631-8059-5576-ba14-1dbe0ec6040a'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a meal’s brightest star is found between the big numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/now-serving-egg-cream-at-eleven-madison-park/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a meal’s brightest star is found between the big numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, fine dining isn’t so much a three-act play of starter/main/dessert as a three-hour spectacular that starts with a couple of rounds of amuse-bouches and ends with the chocolates and dime-size cookies that appear some time after dessert and before the check. The headliners are still foie gras, langoustines and steak from an extremely expensive steer, but sometimes a meal’s brightest star is found between the big numbers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Serving | Egg Cream at Eleven Madison Park', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ab6fe8d-4694-5764-85f3-30cbe8c51c0a', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ab6fe8d-4694-5764-85f3-30cbe8c51c0a'}, {'abstract': 'The State Internet Information Office will regulate every corner of the nation’s vast Internet community, a move that appeared to complement a continuing crackdown on political dissidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/world/asia/05china.html', 'snippet': 'The State Internet Information Office will regulate every corner of the nation’s vast Internet community, a move that appeared to complement a continuing crackdown on political dissidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A powerful arm of China’s government said Wednesday that it had created a new central agency to regulate every corner of the nation’s vast Internet community, a move that appeared to complement a continuing crackdown on political dissidents and other social critics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Creates New Agency for Patrolling the Internet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Creates New Agency For Patrolling The Internet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/980f5ceb-a1b6-5ac7-af53-a04612b7d5a2', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980f5ceb-a1b6-5ac7-af53-a04612b7d5a2'}, {'abstract': 'Two years after it fell out of the sky, the main part of the wreckage has been located at the bottom of the Atlantic Ocean. But will the mystery of the crash ever be solved?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/magazine/mag-08Plane-t.html', 'snippet': 'Two years after it fell out of the sky, the main part of the wreckage has been located at the bottom of the Atlantic Ocean. But will the mystery of the crash ever be solved?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late on the morning of April 3, the expedition ship Alucia rocked violently on the South Atlantic Ocean in the middle of a squall. On the aft deck, the crew huddled together in rain slickers and gazed across the heaving seas to a yellow blur on the horizon. This was an unmanned reconnaissance submarine carrying 15,000 photographs that they were nearly desperate to see. But it had buoyed to the surface just as the squall sprang up, and with 30-knot winds and four-foot swells that splashed over the stern, it was too dangerous to retrieve the sub. So they watched and waited.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/08plane2/08plane2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/08plane2/08plane2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/08plane2/mag-08Plane-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/08plane2/08plane2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/08plane2/08plane2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened to Air France Flight 447?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE DEEPEST END', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airplane Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wil S. Hylton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wil', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Hylton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de957974-10ce-5ccd-b67a-6f25f29e10ce', 'word_count': 7468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de957974-10ce-5ccd-b67a-6f25f29e10ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate majority leader, Harry Reid of Nevada, took a spill on the rainy streets of Washington, but was quickly released from the hospital to head to work as usual.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/reid-dislocates-shoulder-during-morning-run/', 'snippet': 'The Senate majority leader, Harry Reid of Nevada, took a spill on the rainy streets of Washington, but was quickly released from the hospital to head to work as usual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Reid, the United States Senate majority leader, took a spill on the rainy streets of Washington on Wednesday, leaving the Democrat from Nevada with a dislocated right shoulder and golf ball-sized bump above his left eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reid Dislocates Shoulder During Morning Run', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e7e720b-19a4-54e1-b30d-f11451d23080', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e7e720b-19a4-54e1-b30d-f11451d23080'}, {'abstract': 'What Mom wants on Sunday … and all year.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/why-moms-should-quit/', 'snippet': 'What Mom wants on Sunday … and all year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, in the middle of what I now refer to as my “On the Couch” period, I gave my younger son a list. I don’t remember what exactly was on it, but I clearly recall his response. His expression said he was about to protest. He opened his mouth, closed it again, thought for a moment, then said: “All this is the stuff you usually do around here but I don’t notice, right?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Moms Should Quit', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5030412-59bb-58fa-83ab-f4d70d6483bf', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5030412-59bb-58fa-83ab-f4d70d6483bf'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/morning-take-out-236/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T15:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f049641c-16b0-5ec9-a3b4-e6f2afb7fc97', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f049641c-16b0-5ec9-a3b4-e6f2afb7fc97'}, {'abstract': 'Despite celebrations of Osama bin Laden’s death in America, the military’s work continues in Afghanistan, where a new spring offensive has begun.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/in-afghanistan-no-time-to-celebrate/', 'snippet': 'Despite celebrations of Osama bin Laden’s death in America, the military’s work continues in Afghanistan, where a new spring offensive has begun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Osama bin Laden is dead. The news was announced in tickers, as I entered my office at Bagram Airfield in Afghanistan on Monday morning. Everyone was gathered around the television, intently sitting on the edge of their black swivel chairs. “All right, let’s pack up now — it’s time to go home,” one of the sergeants in the room said. “I want to see a death certificate,” our chiseled former infantry first sergeant said. “We all know Donald Trump is going to demand to see one.” The blond newscaster described how Bin Laden had been hiding in a luxurious compound 60 miles outside of Islamabad. She exclaimed, “Who would have thought he would be hiding in Pakistan all along?” One sergeant jumped up, muttering, “I would have thought that.” We all laughed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Afghanistan, No Time to Celebrate', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Lt. Holly Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/15476f99-8571-57e1-a407-2e9a0f8bdbee', 'word_count': 1214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15476f99-8571-57e1-a407-2e9a0f8bdbee'}, {'abstract': 'The list of Republican candidates who will take the stage at the Fox News debate on Thursday in South Carolina will be a short one.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/stage-is-set-for-first-republican-debate/', 'snippet': 'The list of Republican candidates who will take the stage at the Fox News debate on Thursday in South Carolina will be a short one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The contrast with four years ago is likely to be striking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stage Is Set for First Republican Debate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Simi Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ce1846e-8d04-5e90-8f6d-bded242880e1', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ce1846e-8d04-5e90-8f6d-bded242880e1'}, {'abstract': 'In a coup for the Big Board, LinkedIn said on Wednesday that it would be listing its shares on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol LNKD.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/shunning-nasdaq-linkedin-prepares-for-an-i-p-o-on-the-big-board/', 'snippet': 'In a coup for the Big Board, LinkedIn said on Wednesday that it would be listing its shares on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol LNKD.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a coup for the New York Stock Exchange, the business-oriented social networking site LinkedIn said in a filing on Wednesday that it would list its new shares on the Big Board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shunning Nasdaq, LinkedIn Prepares a Big Board I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nasdaq Composite Index', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IntercontinentalExchange Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nasdaq Stock Market', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or