'The four men and their company, Lehr Construction, were indicted on charges that they inflated costs as they built corporate offices across Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/nyregion/four-lehr-construction-executives-charged-with-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'The four men and their company, Lehr Construction, were indicted on charges that they inflated costs as they built corporate offices across Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four veteran construction executives were arraigned Wednesday on charges that they systemically stole tens of millions of dollars from investment firms, insurance companies and law firms as they built corporate offices in buildings across Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/CONSTRUCT1/CONSTRUCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 483, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Construction Executives Are Charged With Fraud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '4 Construction Executives Accused of Stealing Millions in Work on Office Interiors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Todd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehr Construction', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lazar, Jeffrey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:09:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993b4bf5-ecb4-568a-b30b-5cc732dfc3f3', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993b4bf5-ecb4-568a-b30b-5cc732dfc3f3'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of Rikki Reich’s haunting photographs taken from the Jersey City waterfront.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/911-and-the-silence-of-shock/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of Rikki Reich’s haunting photographs taken from the Jersey City waterfront.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our friends on the Lens blog are marking Bin Laden Week, which is what this seems to be turning into, with a remarkable series of Sept. 11 photos this morning. They’re by Rikki Reich and were shot from the Jersey City waterfront over the course of the unfolding nightmare. As David Dunlap writes on Lens, Ms. Reich’s pictures “convey an awful tranquility, a suspension of everyday existence, the silence of shock.” View the slide show on Lens. »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '9/11 and the Silence of Shock', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:11:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f038f933-2524-559f-b242-17433b5035cb', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f038f933-2524-559f-b242-17433b5035cb'}, {'abstract': 'While several dozen colleges turned away far more applicants than they accepted this year, hundreds of others are still accepting applications for their freshman classes.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/space-survey/', 'snippet': 'While several dozen colleges turned away far more applicants than they accepted this year, hundreds of others are still accepting applications for their freshman classes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regular visitors to The Choice know that we try, whenever the opportunity presents itself, to remind readers that in sharp contrast to the competitive admissions landscape at some colleges, hundreds of other universities struggle every year to fill their freshman classes. For some of those institutions, the sluggish economy has only added to the challenge of completing the freshman class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Room for Freshmen at Many Colleges', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/feba318c-5490-58f7-a06b-438c8096e02d', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feba318c-5490-58f7-a06b-438c8096e02d'}, {'abstract': 'With only two strikeouts, the Twins’ Francisco Liriano needed a lot of help in recording his no-hitter Tuesday and improving to 2-4.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/sports/05leading.html', 'snippet': 'With only two strikeouts, the Twins’ Francisco Liriano needed a lot of help in recording his no-hitter Tuesday and improving to 2-4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard not to love no-hitters. They usually contain so much of what is charming about baseball: the mastery of a locked-in pitcher, superstitious teammates avoiding him in the dugout, dramatic defensive plays and nervous moments in the late innings, the emotional spillover when it is finally in the books. Francisco Liriano’s no-hitter for the Twins on Tuesday night, however? Maybe only a mother could love that one. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Still a No-Hitter in the Record Book', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Still a No-Hitter in the Box Score', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laviolette, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liriano, Francisco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Frank H Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selig, Bud', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67cfa41e-4ce6-5fb1-a9b7-0b1f57fb15aa', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67cfa41e-4ce6-5fb1-a9b7-0b1f57fb15aa'}, {'abstract': 'A jury can rule whether Edie’s exit from the ABC prime-time soap opera was a cost-cutting move or an act of retaliation against Nicollette Sheridan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/sheridans-suit-against-desperate-housewives-can-go-to-trial-judge-says/', 'snippet': 'A jury can rule whether Edie’s exit from the ABC prime-time soap opera was a cost-cutting move or an act of retaliation against Nicollette Sheridan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the producers of “Desperate Housewives” who decided to kill off Edie, the much-married Wisteria Lane resident whom Nicollette Sheridan had played on the prime-time ABC soap opera since its 2004 debut. But it is a California jury that will decide whether the character’s death, in a car accident during the show’s fifth season, was a fair exit for Ms. Sheridan, who has sued for damages for wrongful termination, among other matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheridan’s Suit Against ‘Desperate Housewives’ Can Go to Trial, Judge Says', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheridan, Nicollette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cab5b80-c154-5184-b7cf-d94598a572ba', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cab5b80-c154-5184-b7cf-d94598a572ba'}, {'abstract': 'Grand Central Publishing, part of the Hachette Book Group, announced on Wednesday that it would publish  “The Family Corleone,” a book based on a screenplay by Mario Puzo, in June of next year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/the-godfather-before-he-was/', 'snippet': 'Grand Central Publishing, part of the Hachette Book Group, announced on Wednesday that it would publish  “The Family Corleone,” a book based on a screenplay by Mario Puzo, in June of next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How did the Don become the Don? A new prequel to “The Godfather” promises to explain the “unknown history” of how Vito Corleone rose to power\xa0in Depression-era New York. Grand Central Publishing, part of the Hachette Book Group, announced\xa0on Wednesday that it would publish\xa0 “The Family Corleone,” a book based on a screenplay by Mario Puzo, in June\xa0of next year. \xa0Mr. Puzo died in 1999, but the book has the blessing of his\xa0estate. “The Family Corleone” was written by Ed Falco, the author of three novels and the winner of a Pushcart Prize. “The Godfather” was first published in 1969 and has sold more than 21 million copies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Godfather, Before He Was', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Puzo, Mario', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Central Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T16:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3152dde8-e151-5673-9186-3165f22cb96a', 'word_count': 108,