ation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/276eebde-2937-5eed-9526-961b524c09cc', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/276eebde-2937-5eed-9526-961b524c09cc'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate votes to have a confirmation vote on a nominee from Rhode Island who has been attacked as being hostile to business.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/senate-thwarts-filibuster-on-judge/', 'snippet': 'The Senate votes to have a confirmation vote on a nominee from Rhode Island who has been attacked as being hostile to business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defying highly unusual opposition by business groups and the Senate minority leader, the Senate on Wednesday voted to proceed with a confirmation vote for a nominee for federal district\xa0 court, thwarting a threatened filibuster and signaling an apparent unwillingness among many Republicans to hinder judicial appointments without extraordinary cause.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Thwarts Filibuster on Judge', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T19:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/28d596ce-a796-533d-adaf-5fcd71f5aa30', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28d596ce-a796-533d-adaf-5fcd71f5aa30'}, {'abstract': 'Michael D. Shear reports on the debate over pulling troops out of Afghanistan in the wake of the killing of Bin Laden. President Obama’s self imposed deadline to begi