/05/04/at-galleon-calm-in-the-face-of-market-turmoil/', 'snippet': 'A wiretapped phone call between Raj Rajaratnam and a trader provides a window into the unique lingo of a Wall Street trading floor and the calm before the Lehman Brothers storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As DealBook reported earlier on Wednesday, jury deliberations in the trial of Raj Rajaratnam, the founder of the Galleon Group, hit a snag after a juror dropped out for medical reasons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Galleon, Calm in the Face of Market Turmoil', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T19:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb3f587-d013-543f-8ac9-a2dc0f31bcb4', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb3f587-d013-543f-8ac9-a2dc0f31bcb4'}, {'abstract': 'A pop-up shop on Elizabeth Street, inspired by happenstance.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/chance-encounter/', 'snippet': 'A pop-up shop on Elizabeth Street, inspired by happenstance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julia Leach doesn’t strike you as the type of person who would leave anything to chance. A veteran of the ad agency Chiat/Day, Paper Magazine and Kate Spade, Leach is a prolific and meticulous storyboarder. Ideas seem to spill out of her head fully formed, including graphic sensibility, visual collateral and even potential plot twists. But when she struck out to start her own 360-degree lifestyle brand, she left ample room for serendipity. And as if to drive the concept home — or simply to remind herself that nothing ever really comes out exactly as you plan it — she named the venture Chance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chance Encounter', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T19:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2de98c7a-fee8-551f-9548-b8902df7e8db', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2de98c7a-fee8-551f-9548-b8902df7e8db'}, {'abstract': 'Chase ended a test of higher A.T.M. fees in two states.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/chase-ends-test-of-5-a-t-m-fees/', 'snippet': 'Chase ended a test of higher A.T.M. fees in two states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase quietly ended a test in which it was charging a hefty $4 or $5 fee for non-Chase customers in two states for access to its A.T.M.’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chase Ends Test of $5 A.T.M. Fees', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumerist, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam