ou-glee-goes-3-d-in-new-concert-movie/', 'snippet': 'The “Glee Live! In Concert!” series will be filmed this summer for a 3-D movie that will be released in theaters on Aug. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The “Glee” franchise isn’t all about indulging the 1970s nostalgia of its creators and structuring entire episodes around “The Rocky Horror Picture Show” or Fleetwood Mac’s “Rumours” album; that hit Fox musical comedy has a few modern-day tricks up its sleeve, too. For instance: its “Glee Live! In Concert!” series will be filmed this summer for a 3-D movie that will feature 14 members of the television series and utilize whatever remaining exclamation points Fox possesses. On Wednesday, Twentieth Century Fox’s film and television divisions said that the “Glee Live! 3D!” movie will be released in theaters on Aug. 12 and run for two weeks. The film, directed by Kevin Tancharoen (director of the 2009 remake of “Fame,” and the online series “Mortal Kombat: Legacy”) will feature “Glee” stars like Lea Michele, Chris Colfer, Heather Morris and Darren Criss performing numbers like “I’m a Slave 4 U,” “Raise Your Glass” and “Teenage Dream.” (No word about the “Glee” star Matthew Morrison, whose cleft chin would seem tailor-made for the 3-D format.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slushies Coming at You: ‘Glee’ Goes 3-D in  Concert Movie', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michele, Lea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T19:39:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualif