acecraft)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stamps (Postal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shepard, Alan B Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Postal Service (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Canaveral (Fla)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dayton (Ohio)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T19:59:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/635907c5-cc43-53b6-8c66-bcceb4f8fb62', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/635907c5-cc43-53b6-8c66-bcceb4f8fb62'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago guard Kyle Korver is often criticized for his defense, but his performance on that end may not be as poor as his reputation suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/bulls-korver-shadowed-by-defensive-reputation/', 'snippet': 'Chicago guard Kyle Korver is often criticized for his defense, but his performance on that end may not be as poor as his reputation suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the course of his career, Chicago guard Kyle Korver has developed a reputation for being both one of the league’s top outside shooters and one of its lesser perimeter defenders. The former is unquestionably true: Korver is a career 41.1 percent 3-point marksman, and has connected on a whopping 61.9 percent of his attempts in these playoffs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulls’ Korver Shadowed by Defensive Reputation', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thibodeau, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/36df180d-500f-550d-87a8-2470ad58b7eb', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36df180d-500f-550d-87a8-2470ad58b7eb'}, {'abstract': 'Jean Shrimpton tells The Guardian why she likes Kate Moss.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/quote-unquote-small-wonder/', 'snippet': 'Jean Shrimpton tells The Guardian why she likes Kate Moss.', 'lead_paragraph': '– Jean Shrimpton tells The Guardian why she likes Kate Moss. Of course “the shrimp” gets along with “the waif.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quote Unquote | Small Wonder', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Kate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Leon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/12366913-0b8c-5425-b5b6-a33cc6a39bc5', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12366913-0b8c-5425-b5b6-a33cc6a39bc5'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Edward Whitfield, Republican of Kentucky, and Senator Tom Udall, Democrat of New Mexico, introduced legislation Wednesday to end the use of performance-enhancing drugs in horse racing.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/legislation-targets-drug-use-in-horse-racing/', 'snippet': 'Representative Edward Whitfield, Republican of Kentucky, and Senator Tom Udall, Democrat of New Mexico, introduced legislation Wednesday to end the use of performance-enhancing drugs in horse racing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Edward Whitfield, Republican of Kentucky, and Senator Tom Udall, Democrat of New Mexico, introduced legislation Wednesday to regulate the use of performance-enhancing drugs in horse racing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legislation Targets Drug Use in Horse Racing', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/30fa520c-e36a-5a45-8fa2-a98e089577a8', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30fa520c-e36a-5a45-8fa2-a98e089577a8'}, {'abstract': 'The films of Hayao Miyazaki are amazing, unlike anything else. And yet, the music.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/adorable-anime-characters-go-speed-metal/', 'snippet': 'The films of Hayao Miyazaki are amazing, unlike anything else. And yet, the music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The films of Hayao Miyazaki — “Ponyo,” “Spirited Away,” “Princess Mononoke” — are unlike anything else. The animation is amazing, but it’s the tone of the films that sets them apart. They are suffused with a mysterious sense of wonderment that is impossible to describe. And yet, the music: why? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adorable Anime Characters Go Speed Metal', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miyazaki, Hayao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wm. Ferguson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4762d17-8613-5ae8-bce7-fcc7ce61a7df', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4762d17-8613-5ae8-bce7-fcc7ce61a7df'}, {'abstract': 'New apps make it easy to share video by automating uploads, reformatting clips for multiple phones and computers and tying into Facebook and Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/technology/personaltech/05basics.html', 'snippet': 'New apps make it easy to share video by automating uploads, reformatting clips for multiple phones and computers and tying into Facebook and Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the video shot in the world today is recorded on mobile phones. That annoying guy who walked around parties with a camcorder has been replaced with an army of annoying people who whip out their phones to capture the moment. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/technology/05basics-web/05basics-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/technology/05basics-web/05basics-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/technology/05basics-web/05basics-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/technology/05basics-web/05basics-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/technology/05basics-web/05basics-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Apps to Post Videos With Ease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Apps To Post Videos With Ease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Boutin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boutin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c7c95b-1474-5ca7-9d40-2cc66635e7e3', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c7c95b-1474-5ca7-9d40-2cc66635e7e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Ogallala was first pumped 100 years ago to irrigate farms and ranches. Man is draining it faster than nature can recharge it, especially in the most arid areas, like Boise City, Okla.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/aquifers-depletion-poses-sweeping-threat/', 'snippet': 'The Ogallala was first pumped 100 years ago to irrigate farms and ranches. Man is draining it faster than nature can recharge it, especially in the most arid areas, like Boise City, Okla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The small town of Boise City, Okla., which I wrote about in Wednesday’s Times, survived the environmental disaster of the Dust Bowl in the 1930s. But now it faces a confluence of dangers that could push it to the edge of extinction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aquifer’s Depletion Poses Sweeping Threat', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irrigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/04d81396-abea-5585-be