es destinations for you, and shares the details later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise! American Express Picks Your Destination for You', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Express Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8065f08b-b8fd-5836-ae23-a0ac05ff9d27', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8065f08b-b8fd-5836-ae23-a0ac05ff9d27'}, {'abstract': 'The 43-year-old French director discusses the crazy love between Yves Saint Laurent and his partner, Pierre Bergé.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/asked-answered-pierre-thoretton/', 'snippet': 'The 43-year-old French director discusses the crazy love between Yves Saint Laurent and his partner, Pierre Bergé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the past few years, there have been a number of documentaries about iconic fashion designers, from the critically acclaimed “Valentino: The Last Emperor” to the wayward “Ultrasuede: In Search of Halston.” But none seems as delicately composed and poignant as Pierre Thoretton’s “L’Amour Fou,” which had its United States premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival last month and will be out in theaters on May 13. Thoretton hangs the film on the spectacular $480 million art collection that the French-Algerian couturier Yves Saint Laurent and his partner, Pierre Bergé, amassed during their 50 years together and its symbolism for the love they had for one another. Still it’s hard not to wonder if it was Bergé, as much as Thoretton, who called the shots in the film much as he did in Saint Laurent’s life and image. Here, the 43-year-old French director discusses the crazy love between the two men and the filmmaking techniques he chose to tell the story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Pierre Thoretton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T20:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joy Dietrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dietrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/34ce7ab7-8709-5610-8608-3fa745d9c0ab', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34ce7ab7-8709-5610-8608-3fa745d9c0ab'}, {'abstract': 'Beige, the fashion-y, mostly-but-not-all-gay party held every Tuesday at the B Bar on the Bowery, is coming to an end after noise complaints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige.html', 'snippet': 'Beige, the fashion-y, mostly-but-not-all-gay party held every Tuesday at the B Bar on the Bowery, is coming to an end after noise complaints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOLLY PARTON and Gloria Gaynor singing an impromptu duet. Britney Spears supposedly skipping out on her check. Jocelyne Wildenstein showing off her nip and tuck. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige-span/05beige-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige-span/05beige-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige-span/05beige-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige-span/05beige-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/fashion/05beige-span/05beige-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beige Never Looked So Bright', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beige Never Looked So Bright', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T21:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/982af3a0-af7b-5da5-bc0f-5d7c4d66efd3', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/982af3a0-af7b-5da5-bc0f-5d7c4d66efd3'}, {'abstract': 'The crumbling tennis stadium in Queens where legends like Ashe and Laver won Open titles now faces an even more uncertain future.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/forest-hills-stadium-loses-bid-to-be-a-landmark/', 'snippet': 'The crumbling tennis stadium in Queens where legen