tion_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab1be67-1afc-5635-bb12-ab3597ed83db', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab1be67-1afc-5635-bb12-ab3597ed83db'}, {'abstract': 'The morning-line favorite at 4-1 is the Florida Derby winner Dialed In, who will break from the No. 8 post.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/dialed-in-is-early-derby-favorite-at-4-1/', 'snippet': 'The morning-line favorite at 4-1 is the Florida Derby winner Dialed In, who will break from the No. 8 post.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uncle Mo may or may not show up for the 137th running of the Kentucky Derby on Saturday, but if he does he will break from the No. 18 hole as the 9-2 morning-line second favorite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dialed In Is Early Derby Favorite at 4-1', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/81ff9047-9b7c-54d2-ba62-d0d17c5544ff', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81ff9047-9b7c-54d2-ba62-d0d17c5544ff'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet’s spring season began Tuesday night with Balanchine Black & White Week, consisting of a dozen of his works that offered a modernist simplicity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-opens-with-balanchine-review.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet’s spring season began Tuesday night with Balanchine Black & White Week, consisting of a dozen of his works that offered a modernist simplicity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music starts. The curtain rises. There is no scenery, just a backdrop that implies the infinite sky. Yet the stage is far from empty: it features a central tableau of dancers, braced for action. When they start to move, they do so in sharply alive meters. It’s as if they had been waiting for the music to ignite their motors. That little transition from standstill to motion always carries something of the drama of the moment when the sculptor Pygmalion’s statue Galatea comes to life.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/SQUARE1/SQUARE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stripped Down to Black and White, Revealing Balanchine at His Core', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stripped Down to Black and White, Revealing Balanchine at His Core', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:08:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd3626f-fee3-5abf-a9bf-716477c669ad', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd3626f-fee3-5abf-a9bf-716477c669ad'}, {'abstract': 'The Nyfos Next series focused on experimental works, including some set to texts by Hunter S. Thompson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/arts/music/nyfos-next-at-the-baryshnikov-arts-center-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Nyfos Next series focused on experimental works, including some set to texts by Hunter S. Thompson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The enterprising New York Festival of Song has presented plenty of new music and even some pop at times (most notably, evenings of Beatles tunes and musical theater pieces). So it would not be entirely correct to suggest that its latest series, Nyfos Next, is an attempt to address a serious deficit in the festival’s purview. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/MOVADO1/MOVADO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Off-the-Edge Songs, Placed Front and Center', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Off-the-Edge Songs, Placed Front and Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Festival of Song', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcd934f5-9fc7-5ea5-9a86-ddc6f38d4746', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcd934f5-9fc7-5ea5-9a86-ddc6f38d4746'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s attorney general, Eric Schneiderman, issued three subpoenas to Sony on Tuesday asking for information about its security measures after an attack last week.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/new-york-attorney-general-subpoenas-sony/', 'snippet': 'New York’s attorney general, Eric Schneiderman, issued three subpoenas to Sony on Tuesday asking for information about its security measures after an attack last week.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:47 p.m. | Updated Added comment from Sony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Attorney General Subpoenas Sony', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bfa9e07-8f26-5932-9d06-f108df0cf0f3', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bfa9e07-8f26-5932-9d06-f108df0cf0f3'}, {'abstract': 'A house on the tiny Isle of Coll was built on the remains of one abandoned 150 years earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/05/greathomesanddestinations/20110504-scotland.html', 'snippet': 'A house on the tiny Isle of Coll was built on the remains of one abandoned 150 years earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A house on the tiny Isle of Coll was built on the remains of one abandoned 150 years earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Scotland, a Modern Farmhouse Rises From Ruins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/22a03a15-3fce-5c5b-83cb-97cb4c038776', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/22a03a15-3fce-5c5b-83cb-97cb4c038776'}, {'abstract': 'The ratings for NBC’s new singing competition “The Voice” grew 10 percent over its impressive debut a week ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/arts/television/voice-grows-stronger.html', 'snippet': 'The ratings for NBC’s new singing competition “The Voice” grew 10 percent over its impressive debut a week ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ratings for NBC’s new singing competition “The Voice” grew 10 percent over its impressive debut a week ago, leading Tuesday night’s ratings over all by a wide margin among viewers 18 to 49, and drawing 12.4 million over all. But in total viewers for the night NBC finished in third place, according to Nielsen’s estimates. CBS had the most viewers, garnering 17.3 million for “NCIS” at 8 p.m. and 14 million for “NCIS: Los Angeles” at 9. ABC ranked second over all, earning its best ratings at 9 for a “Dancing With the Stars” results episode (15.6 million), but at 10, its “Body of Proof” (10.4 million) trailed “The Good Wife” on CBS (12.3 million). Fox finished in fourth place for the night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Voice’ Grows Stronger', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Voice’ Grows Stronger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:14:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/093d4caa-3d45-5d29-a3b9-0d82c4ed10f3', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/093d4caa-3d45-5d29-a3b9-0d82c4ed10f3'}, {'abstract': 'As an “American Idol” judge, Jennifer Lopez understands the star-making businesses, a talent reflected in her new album, “Love?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/arts/music/jennifer-lopez-and-the-star-making-machinery-of-idol.html', 'snippet': 'As an “American Idol” judge, Jennifer Lopez understands the star-making businesses, a talent reflected in her new album, “Love?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steven Tyler may operate on a bizarre frequency, and Jimmy Iovine may be the ruthless engine behind the scenes, but no one has kept “American Idol” afloat this year more than Jennifer Lopez.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/JLOALT/JLOALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 446, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/JLOALT/JLOALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/JLOALT/JLOALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An ‘Idol’ Judge Heeds Her Tips', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An ‘Idol’ Judge Heeds Her Tips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1543915c-9f28-5ba4-8790-8bcfd9e2ccaa', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1543915c-9f28-5ba4-8790-8bcfd9e2ccaa'}, {'abstract': 'Christian R. Bartholomew will become the head of the law firm’s S.E.C. enforcement and litigation practice in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/onetime-s-e-c-enforcement-lawyer-joins-weil-gotshal/', 'snippet': 'Christian R. Bartholomew will become the head of the law firm’s S.E.C. enforcement and litigation practice in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christian R. Bartholomew, a former senior enforcement lawyer at the Securities and Exchange Commission, has joined Weil, Gotshal & Manges as head of the law firm’s S.E.C. enforcement and litigation practice in Washington. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Onetime S.E.C. Enforcement Lawyer Joins Weil Gotshal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weil Gotshal & Manges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:28:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ee7e24b-4a12-5f1a-a984-e38f0fccd383', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ee7e24b-4a12-5f1a-a984-e38f0fccd383'}, {'abstract': '“It was Monday afternoon when he drove the white van up the driveway and stopped it at the side door of the house.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/books/excerpt-the-informant-by-thomas-perry.html', 'snippet': '“It was Monday afternoon when he drove the white van up the driveway and stopped it at the side door of the house.”', 'lead_paragraph': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Informant’', 'kicker': 'Excerpt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Perry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'First Chapter', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0d176e1-070a-5649-af4e-51b822640fd1', 'word_count': 2255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0d176e1-070a-5649-af4e-51b822640fd1'}, {'abstract': 'The Butcher’s Boy, Thomas Perry’s unflappable hired killer, is forced out of retirement to settle old scores in “The Informant.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/books/the-informant-by-thomas-perry-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Butcher’s Boy, Thomas Perry’s unflappable hired killer, is forced out of retirement to settle old scores in “The Informant.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Perry won the Mystery Writers of America’s Edgar Award for  “The Butcher’s Boy,” his 1982 debut novel about an extremely unflappable hired killer. He checks in on the character after long intervals, so the steel-nerved assassin showed up in the 1992 “Sleeping Dogs.” Now the Butcher’s Boy is back at full blast in “The Informant,” a book-length war of nerves that accentuates the best of Mr. Perry’s gift for using pure logic and gamesmanship to generate breathless nonstop suspense.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hired Killer, Forced Out of Retirement, Says Hello Again to an Old Adversary', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hired Killer, Forced Out of Retirement, Says Hello Again to an Old Adversary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T22:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e172830-88bf-5e40-a3fe-73d7b5d7044f', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e172830-88bf-5e40-a3fe-73d7b5d7044f'}, {'abstract': 'New state laws will expand charter schools, end teacher tenure and introduce a voucher system.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/daniels-happy-with-action-on-indiana-schools/', 'snippet': 'New state laws will expand charter schools, end teacher tenure and introduce a voucher system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as he was noncommittal about entering the 2012 presidential race on Wednesday, Gov. Mitch Daniels of Indiana was characteristically low key in discussing his sweeping, even landmark changes for schools in his state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniels Happy With Action on Indiana Schools', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Mitchell E Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '201