00-ded35790fe42', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e0c374c5-7674-571b-b100-ded35790fe42'}, {'abstract': 'The gallery, which specializes in functional designs by visual artists, now has a 2,300-square-foot space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/garden/05open.html', 'snippet': 'The gallery, which specializes in functional designs by visual artists, now has a 2,300-square-foot space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After five years in the West Village, Artware Editions has moved to a 2,300-square-foot space on the Bowery — one large enough to display the range of products offered by the gallery, which specializes in functional designs by visual artists. “The space allows us to show pieces in the context of each other,” said Rebecca Kong, a founder of the company. “We can show the Klein table with a couch, so you can see it’s something you can live with.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05open-span/05open-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05open-span/05open-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05open-span/Currents-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05open-span/05open-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05open-span/05open-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Artware Editions Moves to the Bowery', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bridging the Worlds of Art and Commerce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T23:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5a303e-598c-5d07-9d74-20af4c3b7872', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5a303e-598c-5d07-9d74-20af4c3b7872'}, {'abstract': 'The Oasis collection from the Swedish furniture company Offecct offers a new way to add plant life to interiors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/garden/05furniture.html', 'snippet': 'The Oasis collection from the Swedish furniture company Offecct offers a new way to add plant life to interiors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Oasis collection from the Swedish furniture company Offecct offers a new way to add plant life to interiors, by merging furniture with flowerpots. “Plants and flowers enhance the quality of the air,” said David Lerdell, a spokesman for the company, but some people don’t like the look of ordinary plant containers. With Oasis, he said, you can have vegetation and “the feeling of the interior that you want.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05furniture/05furniture-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 931, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '