en.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lighting designer shopped for good-looking toys that would appeal to adults as well as children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for Toys With David Weeks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-04T23:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/458ae802-71be-5a23-a1f3-66ab266a9ca4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/458ae802-71be-5a23-a1f3-66ab266a9ca4'}, {'abstract': 'Discounts on furniture, flatware, crystal and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/garden/05deals.html', 'snippet': 'Discounts on furniture, flatware, crystal and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The  Housing Works Design on a Dime event opens Thursday night with a preview party, with merchandise 50 to 70 percent off (a Bunny Williams turquoise lamp, originally $800, will be $350; a Jonathan Adler Lampert sofa, regularly $3,200, will be $1,600); tickets are $250 at the door, at (347) 473-7457 or at housingworks.org. Design on a Dime continues Friday and Saturday at the Metropolitan Pavilion, 125 West 18th Street (Sixth Avenue).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05deals-span/05deals-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/garden/05deals-span