cations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T00:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e769e35-5046-59fd-af3a-d3832ec3b3bf', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e769e35-5046-59fd-af3a-d3832ec3b3bf'}, {'abstract': 'While wealthy travelers still often prefer the most high-end seats, many international carriers are concentrating on just business class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/business/05LUXE.html', 'snippet': 'While wealthy travelers still often prefer the most high-end seats, many international carriers are concentrating on just business class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO the question, what does a person get when spending upward of $16,000 for a first-class international airline ticket, the answer is: more than ever. Private lounges with hot food and drink, spalike bathrooms and concierge services. Courteous guards to help passengers through a separate security checkpoint and a private car to whisk them to the plane. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/business/LUX-1/LUX-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/business/LUX-1/LUX-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u