onnecticut of liability in a patient’s suicide has been overturned by an appeals court that said the judge should have tried to determine if jurors were prejudiced by a newspaper article published just before the trial began.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jury Verdict for Hospital in Suicide Case Is Set Aside', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jury Verdict for Hospital In Suicide Case Is Set Aside', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westport (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Hill Hospital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:22:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa29108f-8ba8-56bb-a71c-29c24976500a', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa29108f-8ba8-56bb-a71c-29c24976500a'}, {'abstract': 'Among the ideas being discussed is a “trigger” that would force spending cuts if the government goes over a prescribed debt level.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/us/politics/05congress.html', 'snippet': 'Among the ideas being discussed is a “trigger” that would force spending cuts if the government goes over a prescribed debt level.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As bipartisan negotiations were to begin over how to limit the spread of federal red ink, Senator Max Baucus, chairman of the Finance Committee, said Wednesday that he was open to imposing a “trigger” that would force spending cuts if the government exceeded prescribed deficit levels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 525, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers’ Challenge: A Plan to Lower the Deficit, and Make It Stick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers’ Challenge: A Plan to Lower the Deficit, and Make It Stick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:24:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99d7e90c-1b72-5282-af92-d5eb3979a934', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99d7e90c-1b72-5282-af92-d5eb3979a934'}, {'abstract': 'If the valuation of Renren, China’s social networking giant, were applied to Facebook, the American company’s value would be $200 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/business/05views.html', 'snippet': 'If the valuation of Renren, China’s social networking giant, were applied to Facebook, the American company’s value would be $200 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs got a steal of a deal on its Facebook stake. That’s if Renren is anything to go by. Shares in Renren, China’s answer to the social networking giant, surged more than 25 percent on their first day of trading on Wednesday. That meant it was valued at nearly 100 times last year’s revenue. On that basis, Facebook is worth about $200 billion. Goldman bought in at just a quarter of that. With some bubbly assumptions, the higher figure can almost be supported.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 973, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Renren May Skew Facebook’s Value', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Renren May Skew Facebook’s Value', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:28:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Goldfarb, Hugo Dixon and Neil Unmack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Unmack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7271b96c-40b4-50b4-9090-2ea6173f064e', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7271b96c-40b4-50b4-9090-2ea6173f064e'}, {'abstract': 'Time to put an end to an unsustainable rate of soil erosion caused by farm policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/opinion/05thu2.html', 'snippet': 'Time to put an end to an unsustainable rate of soil erosion caused by farm policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To an untrained eye, the fields of Iowa have a reassuring solidity. You cannot tell that the state has lost half its topsoil in the past century. According to a new report from the Environmental Working Group, Iowa’s soil is washing away at rates far higher than anyone realized.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washing Away the Fields of Iowa', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Washing Away the Fields of Iowa: Time to put an end to an unsustainable rate of soil erosion caused by farm policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Working Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/56334b38-4c80-5d0f-b8ad-256038f5d7d6', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56334b38-4c80-5d0f-b8ad-256038f5d7d6'}, {'abstract': 'How can I leave the city I love?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/goodbye-to-all-that-2/', 'snippet': 'How can I leave the city I love?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My first New York apartment was a 9-by-5-foot room on 20th Street between Seventh and Eighth Avenues. It was an all-female boarding house, or S.R.O. (single room occupancy) as they were called before my time. The eight women on my floor all lived in cell-like rooms, and shared the two tiny bathrooms in the hallway, one with nothing but a toilet, the other with a moldy shower. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodbye to All That', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Febos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Febos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aef33cc2-f67d-5aaa-9731-12d838f9d2d0', 'word_count': 1874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aef33cc2-f67d-5aaa-9731-12d838f9d2d0'}, {'abstract': 'Unless all of the state universities have a more rational budgeting process, the system will continue its decline, and New York’s students will suffer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/opinion/05thu3.html', 'snippet': 'Unless all of the state universities have a more rational budgeting process, the system will continue its decline, and New York’s students will suffer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the fiscal crisis, the New York State Legislature was doing a terrible job of managing the State University of New York System. Lawmakers who voted to cut financing to the 64-campus system also starved it by forbidding reasonable tuition increases and then hijacked tuition revenue for use in the general state budget. In recent years, administrators have had to cut class offerings, limit enrollment and rely far too much on part-time faculty. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Rebuild SUNY', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chance to Rebuild SUNY', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:31:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a57388-3f0c-5708-ae1a-75666608f750', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a57388-3f0c-5708-ae1a-75666608f750'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit, which names A.I.G., Goldman Sachs and Deutsche Bank, says two Federal Reserve loans to A.I.G. were improper because no high-quality collateral was pledged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/business/05aig.html', 'snippet': 'The lawsuit, which names A.I.G., Goldman Sachs and Deutsche Bank, says two Federal Reserve loans to A.I.G. were improper because no high-quality collateral was pledged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first known whistle-blower lawsuit to assert that the taxpayers were defrauded when the federal government bailed out the American International Group was unsealed on Friday, joining a number of suits seeking to settle the score on losses related to the financial crisis of 2008. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/business/AIG/AIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 833, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Claiming Fraud in A.I.G. Bailout, Whistle-Blower Lawsuit Names 3 Companies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Claiming Fraud in A.I.G. Bailout, Whistle-Blower Lawsuit Names 3 Companies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:31:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d872a14b-2ed7-5c6f-929f-e0117e7049fd', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d872a14b-2ed7-5c6f-929f-e0117e7049fd'}, {'abstract': 'Marina Abramovic, known for using nudity in her performance art, was among the guests at an event for Francis Alÿs at the Museum of Modern Art. She regaled with a tale about learning to drive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/nyregion/at-a-moma-art-party-baring-all-while-remaining-dressed.html', 'snippet': 'Marina Abramovic, known for using nudity in her performance art, was among the guests at an event for Francis Alÿs at the Museum of Modern Art. She regaled with a tale about learning to drive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We saw relatively little of Marina Abramovic at the Museum of Modern Art on Tuesday night because, unlike in some of her shows elsewhere, she wasn’t naked.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST/NOCTURNALIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At an Art Party, Baring All While Remaining Dressed', 'kicker': 'Nocturnalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Art Party, Baring All but Remaining Fully Clothed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Julie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dawson, Rosario', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'P