/www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/opinion/05thu4.html', 'snippet': 'Kings Point, N.Y., wants to run criminal checks on every car that enters its placid realm by installing license-plate cameras hooked up to police computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kings Point, N.Y., on Long Island’s gilded North Shore, wants to do criminal checks on every car that enters its placid realm. It has the technology — license-plate cameras hooked up to police computers — and is borrowing the money to install 44 of them. For about a million dollars, it will get what village trustees say is the snuggest security blanket money can buy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Brother Goes to West Egg', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Suburban Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Brother Goes to West Egg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cameras', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T01:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9111344-a9a8-5067-8e76-30b05952169f', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9111344-a9a8-5067-8e76-30b05952169f'}, {'abstract': 'If she is approved, Cami Anderson faces choices about how to use a $200 million windfall to help address problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/nyregion/next-newark-schools-chief-faces-challenges.html', 'snippet': 'If she is approved, Cami Anderson faces choices about how to use a $200 million windfall to help address problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the new superintendent of the Newark schools, Cami Anderson faces the monumental task of rescuing an urban school system that has long been mired in low achievement, high turnover and a culture of failure, despite decades of state intervention.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NEWARK/NEWARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NEWARK/NEWARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NEWARK/NEWARK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NEWARK/NEWARK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/NEWARK/NEWARK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Next Chief of Newark Schools, Hard Choices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awaiting Newark’s Next Schools Chief: Big Challenges and Money to Spend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pe