puzzle’s grid provide a hint to the four longest Down answers.” Now that you have the hint, proceed in an orderly fashion through the puzzle and upon finishing, please wait until this post has come to a full and complete stop to exit the blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday: City Known as the Big Guava', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T02:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b5cf94-d1f7-5fd9-bbfa-f8c913244dca', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b5cf94-d1f7-5fd9-bbfa-f8c913244dca'}, {'abstract': 'Trevin T. Smith had been sought after a killing in Springfield, Mass., and the shooting of two police officers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/nyregion/suspect-surrenders-to-bishop-after-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Trevin T. Smith had been sought after a killing in Springfield, Mass., and the shooting of two police officers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The suspect, Trevin T. Smith, was waiting in the rain with his sister on a Brooklyn street corner on Wednesday morning. The clergyman, Bishop Gerald G. Seabrooks, pulled up alone, as agreed, in his brown four-door car. Then the three set out on a 15-minute ride to Rehoboth Cathedral to meet the police.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Suspect’s Surrender, Eased by a Clergy Program to Curtail Black-on-Black Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Suspect’s Surrender, Eased by a Clergy Program to Curtail B