voters. He has not said whether he will join the race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Gov. Mitch Daniels of Indiana called the leisurely pace of the 2012 presidential campaign “a blessing” for voters. Whether he plans to take advantage of it is another question, which he did not answer as he paid a visit here Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/us/DANIELS-1304554716807/DANIELS-1304554716807-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 815, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/us/DANIELS-1304554716807/DANIELS-1304554716807-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/us/DANIELS-1304554716807/DANIELS-1304554716807-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Potential Candidate in No Rush for a Race', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Potential Candidate In No Rush for a Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Mitchell E Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T03:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d9bb0ea-2e92-5fce-8511-d5266eabc3a9', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d9bb0ea-2e92-5fce-8511-d5266eabc3a9'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Pat Quinn has withdrawn the state from a federal program that runs immigration checks on fingerprints of everyone arrested by the state and local police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/us/05brfs-Illinois.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Pat Quinn has withdrawn the state from a federal program that runs immigration checks on fingerprints of everyone arrested by the state and local police.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Gov. Pat Quinn has withdrawn the state from a federal program that runs immigration checks on fingerprints of everyone arrested by the state and local police. In a letter to Immigration and Customs Enforcement, Mr. Quinn, a Democrat, said he was canceling Illinois’ participation in the program, known as Secure Communities, because of “a conflict” between its stated purpose and its results. Although officials had said the program would deport immigrants who were convicted criminals, Mr. Quinn wrote, fewer than 20 percent of immigrants deported under the program had serious convictions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: State Leaves Immigration Program', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | MIDWEST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: State Leaves Immigration Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Patrick J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T03:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e89a0d8e-1191-59c5-a70b-18d01601efa2', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e89a0d8e-1191-59c5-a70b-18d01601efa2'}, {'abstract': 'Sales at the Wednesday night auction in Manhattan totaled $156 million, below its low estimate. Sotheby’s sale on Tuesday was also on the low side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/arts/vlaminck-and-monet-tie-for-top-sale-at-christies.html', 'snippet': 'Sales at the Wednesday night auction in Manhattan totaled $156 million, below its low estimate. Sotheby’s sale on Tuesday was also on the low side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An early sighting of Leonardo DiCaprio trying to hide under a navy-blue baseball cap and sitting next to his actor pal Lukas Haas added a bit of Hollywood flavor to a generally lively sale of Impressionist and modern art at Christie’s on Wednesday night. Although neither man could be seen raising his hand, others certainly did, though in a controlled, price-conscious fashion. Blue-chip names including Monet, Matisse and Picasso brought solid prices — even if the works were far from their best — a day after auction season got off to a bumpy start at Sotheby’s.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vlaminck and Monet Tie for Top Sale at Christie’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vlaminck and Monet Tie for Top Sale at Christie&#8217;s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phillips de Pury & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T03:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ba2c54d-cab5-5cbc-afa3-9d357f0e8bbb', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ba2c54d-cab5-5cbc-afa3-9d357f0e8bbb'}, {'abstract': 'On a 251-to-175 vote, the House approved a bill prohibiting federal money to be used for insurance plans that cover abortions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/us/politics/05brfs-Abortion.html', 'snippet': 'On a 251-to-175 vote, the House approved a bill prohibiting federal money to be used for insurance plans that cover abortions.', 'lead_paragraph': ' House Republicans continued Wednesday with their efforts to dismantle the health care law. On a 251-to-175 vote, the House approved a bill prohibiting federal money to be used for insurance plans that cover abortions. The bill goes beyond current federal law, which prohibits the use of federal funds for abortions. It would also wipe out tax breaks for private employers who provide coverage if their plans offer abortion services and would eliminate the ability to pay for an abortion with pretax dollars from a flexible spending plan. Voting 235 to 191, the House blocked money for construction of school-based health centers that had been earmarked in the health care act. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Votes to Limit Access to Abortion', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | WASHINGTON', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Votes to Limit Access to Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T03:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a48bbc-1f97-59a4-b117-715bb4b825d0', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a48bbc-1f97-59a4-b117-715bb4b825d0'}, {'abstract': 'Varied views on population paths from now through 2100.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/04/shaping-human-path-to-15-or-6-billion-by-2100/', 'snippet': 'Varied views on population paths from now through 2100.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following up on the latest United Nations projections for population growth through 2100, Room for Debate, drawing on some familiar Dot Earth voices, has elicited five fascinating takes on alternative human futures:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shaping Human Path to 15, or 6, Billion by 2100', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, David E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Joel E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for the Future', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rockefeller University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T03:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9fc0b13-e48d-57bc-ab24-f91792913f66', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9fc0b13-e48d-57bc-ab24-f91792913f66'}, {'abstract': 'Pet hotels near airports offer pampering for animals, including spacious rooms, plush bedding, spa treatments and a swimming pool.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/business/05PET.html', 'snippet': 'Pet hotels near airports offer pampering for animals, including spacious rooms, plush bedding, spa treatments and a swimming pool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spacious rooms, plush bedding, spa treatments, a large swimming p