': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hetherington, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hondros, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T08:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6af352d-b90f-5e4a-a419-51a48a847df8', 'word_count': 1898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6af352d-b90f-5e4a-a419-51a48a847df8'}, {'abstract': 'A fish-eater; one whose food is fish.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/daily-lexeme-ichthyophagist/', 'snippet': 'A fish-eater; one whose food is fish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s word, in association with the dependable Oxford English Dictionary, is', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Lexeme: Ichthyophagist', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T08:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbcc7176-e039-53bc-a620-c3a153c0b319', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbcc7176-e039-53bc-a620-c3a153c0b319'}, {'abstract': 'The United States needs to start debating anew how to redistribute wealth, rather than the size of federal debt, an e