tps://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/global/06euro.html', 'snippet': 'Taking a cautious approach in the face of slow economic growth, central banks in Europe will leave their rates unchanged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The European Central Bank left its benchmark interest rate unchanged Thursday, and signaled that it would probably wait until July before it made another move.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/global/06euro-span/06euro-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 586, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/global/06euro-span/06euro-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/business/global/06euro-span/06euro-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Central Banks Stand Pat on Rates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Concerns About Inflation, European Banks Leave Rates Unchanged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T11:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4ecbda-6c61-59c8-8b4d-6e6bec528f0d', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4ecbda-6c61-59c8-8b4d-6e6bec528f0d'}, {'abstract': '“We don’t trot out this stuff as trophies,” President Obama said of his decision not to release photos of Osama bin Laden.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/obama-blocks-release-of-graphic-photos-for-second-time/', 'snippet': '“We don’t trot out this stuff as trophies,” President Obama said of his decision not to release photos of Osama bin Laden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice since assuming office, President Obama has been confronted with the question of whether to release grisly photographs depicting the results of American actions overseas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Blocks Release of Graphic Photos for Second Time', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T11:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/366ffe0f-85f7-5a05-8c24-780c73938b4f', 'word_count': 950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366ffe0f-85f7-5a05-8c24-780c73938b4f'}, {'abstract': 'An alternative history: what if Jerry Brown had become president and Linda Ronstadt was first lady?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/linda-ronstadt-first-lady-of-california/', 'snippet': 'An alternative history: what if Jerry Brown had become president and Linda Ronstadt was first lady?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s magazine, the New York Times reporter Adam Nagourney writes about Gov. Jerry Brown as he wrestles with California’s budget. Linda Ronstadt makes a cameo appearance as Brown’s former girlfriend. But for me, Ronstadt is always the main event. Seeing her perform in her Cub Scouts uniform at Pine Knob outside Detroit in the late 1970s (or early ’80s; it’s a bit hazy) was a formative experience. With a few not-inconceivable twists of fate, it’s possible (at least to me) to imagine Brown as president and Ronstadt as first lady. That this didn’t happen might have marked the moment when things started to go wrong. Or maybe that was when Johnny Carson retired. Anyway, this clip of “My Boyfriend’s Back” (date uncertain but probably filmed sometime during the campaign for the 1980 Democratic nomination) gives a hint of what we missed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Linda Ronstadt, First Lady of California', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronstadt, Linda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T11:47:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Dickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b565ab67-ec0f-54e7-8b8e-4e6789658108', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b565ab67-ec0f-54e7-8b8e-4e6789658108'}, {'abstract': 'Gap’s retail sales in North America have been trending downward, with same-store sales in March down 9 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/06gap.html', 'snippet': 'Gap’s retail sales in North America have been trending downward, with same-store sales in March down 9 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gap announced on Thursday that it had dismissed its star designer, Patrick Robinson, in an acknowledgement that its problems run deeper than the company had previously indicated.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Gap/Gap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Gap/Gap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Gap/Gap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Gap/Gap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Gap/Gap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gap Dismisses Design Chief as Brand’s Slow Sales Persist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gap Dismisses Design Chief As Brand’s Slow Sales Persist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject'