— in children’s literature over the last century.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/new-study-finds-gender-bias-in-childrens-books/', 'snippet': 'According to a new study published in the April issue of “Gender and Society,” there has been a bias  toward male characters — men, boys and, yes, animals — in children’s literature over the last century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Babar, Peter Rabbit, Curious George … conspiracy?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Study Finds Gender Bias in Children’s Books', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T13:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/46b416c2-62d7-5186-ae35-7ef937e41830', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46b416c2-62d7-5186-ae35-7ef937e41830'}, {'abstract': 'The lead singer, Lovefoxxx, surfed the crowd at the Brazilian pop band’s all-ages show at the Glass House.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/notes-from-the-underground-cansei-de-ser-sexy/', 'snippet': 'The lead singer, Lovefoxxx, surfed the crowd at the Brazilian pop band’s all-ages show at the Glass House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Brazilian pop band Cansei de Ser Sexy (CSS) kicked off its current American tour with a star turn at Coachella, then stepped off the stage and went straight to Pomona, Calif., and an all-ages show at the Glass House the following night. Fans mobbed the barricades to get a closer look at the lead singer, Lovefoxxx (pictured here). Dressed in a sequined bolero ensemble and Doc Martens boots, she turned cartwheels and surfed the crowd. The audience read like a throng of exultant misfits, gathered to hail their beloved leaders. Lovefoxxx gave a shout-out to someone watching that night, who had written the band an e-mail explaining how they had inspired him to come out and be honest about who he was with his family and friends, and later she brought several teenage girls to the stage to dance alongside her. CSS will perform three nights in New York City in May.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Cansei de Ser Sexy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T13:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/63baec2f-4dc5-5489-b3fc-965f53e56661', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63baec2f-4dc5-5489-b3fc-965f53e56661'}, {'abstract': 'Aggregate demand disorder.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/new-keynesian-misconceptions-wonkish-and-trivial/', 'snippet': 'Aggregate demand disorder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noah Smith tries to sorta-kinda defend Casey Mulligan, arguing that New Keynesian economics as you might have read it in Woodford’s book might correspond to what Mulligan does.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Keynesian Misconceptions 