e in commodities in almost two years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slide in Commodities Adds to Markets’ Woes', 'kicker': 'Stocks & Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slide in Commodities Adds to Markets’ Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T13:49:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c19663d-8e5f-5a0d-85a4-0d3e820480b6', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c19663d-8e5f-5a0d-85a4-0d3e820480b6'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday, The Lede continues to track new details on the killing of Osama Bin Laden, and reactions to his death from around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/updates-on-bin-ladens-death-may-5/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday, The Lede continues to track new details on the killing of Osama Bin Laden, and reactions to his death from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, as new details about the killing of Osama Bin Laden continue to emerge, and the debate about the legality and ethics of the operation intensifies, The Lede provides updates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on the Killing of Bin Laden, May 5', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T13:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3062a66-f65e-5e16-97be-07210baee6f5', 'word_count': 4711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3062a66-f65e-5e16-97be-07210baee6f5'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Judd’s son opens up about his father and discusses a major exhibit of his father’s work at David Zwirner gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/asked-answered-flavin-judd/', 'snippet': 'Donald Judd’s son opens up about his father and discusses a major exhibit of his father’s work at David Zwirner gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Donald Judd died in 1994, he had a couple thousand dollars in the bank but was millions of dollars in debt. The task of sorting out his estate was left to his two children, Rainer and Flavin, who persevered against what many considered insurmountable odds, resulting in the creation of the now seemingly solid Judd Foundation. Judd’s daughter, Rainer, is the president of the board of the foundation and the more public of the two while his son, Flavin, is vice president (but referred to himself as the “curatorial consultant”). Despite being very involved in the day-to-day running of the foundation, he remains relatively out of the public eye. T recently caught up with Flavin Judd, who was in town to oversee the installation of a major exhibit of his father’s work at David Zwirner gallery. “Donald Judd,” which opens on Friday, features nine aluminum boxes originally shown in a 1989 exhibition at Staatliche Kunsthalle Baden-Baden. It is the first time since that such a large number pieces from that show have been installed in one place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Flavin Judd', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b4970a7-3114-57bc-a3aa-1c2f490f96c3', 'word_count': 1765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b4970a7-3114-57bc-a3aa-1c2f490f96c3'}, {'abstract': 'This week we pair the poem “I Am,” written by an 8-year-old, with a Home and Garden article, “Mom, You’re One Tough Art Critic.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/poetry-pairing-may-5-2011/', 'snippet': 'This week we pair the poem “I Am,” written by an 8-year-old, with a Home and Garden article, “Mom, You’re One Tough Art Critic.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our weekly “Poetry Pairing” series, we collaborate with the Poetry Foundation to feature a work from its American Life in Poetry project alongside content from The Times that somehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | May 5, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 