': 'Updates from ground zero and elsewhere as the president comes to New York to mark Bin Laden’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the killing of Osama bin Laden, President Obama  came to New York Thursday to lay a wreath at the 9/11 Memorial and meet with families of Sept. 11 victims and, along the way, to meet with firefighters at a Midtown firehouse that lost 15 men on Sept. 11 and police officers at the station house near ground zero. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blog: Obama Visits New York', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T14:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca5eeb9-1457-5f95-8038-c36c4587f5cf', 'word_count': 4423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca5eeb9-1457-5f95-8038-c36c4587f5cf'}, {'abstract': 'The Portuguese finance minister forecast that the economy would contract 2 percent both this year and next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/global/06portugal.html', 'snippet': 'The Portuguese finance minister forecast that the economy would contract 2 percent both this year and next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bailout negotiated for Portugal should give it enough breathing space to overhaul its economy and restore investor confidence before having to return to the bond market, the country’s financial rescuers said Thursday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Portugal/Portugal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images