ount': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57ca73a-aea7-5692-aa50-d666b6ba474d'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets’ dim chances have relieved the writer of his worries about winning and losing, allowing him to enjoy just being at the park.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/stress-free-days-in-the-upper-deck-are-here-again/', 'snippet': 'The Mets’ dim chances have relieved the writer of his worries about winning and losing, allowing him to enjoy just being at the park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long-suffering Mets fans like to brag about how bad the team was when they were growing up, how crowds were sparse during the team’s many losing seasons and how pathetic some of its star players were.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stress-Free Days in the Upper Deck Are Here Again', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shea Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T14:42:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/391e770b-b5bd-52f7-b0d7-e37323d5355a', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391e770b-b5bd-52f7-b0d7-e37323d5355a'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times Company’s Research and Development Lab released a free Web-based tool that creates an research database of anonymized location data from iPhones and iPads.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/a-tool-to-harvest-iphone-location-data/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times Company’s Research and Development Lab released a free Web-based tool that creates an research database of anonymized location data from iPhones and iPads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot people got upset about Apple collecting location data on iPads and iPhones. The company just issued an update to the devices’ software in part to tamp down the reaction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tool to Harvest iPhone Location Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T15:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/484c76fd-5848-50d3-a0b5-b76882881ef4', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/484c76fd-5848-50d3-a0b5-b76882881ef4'}, {'abstract': 'The biggest buzz from Austin is coming from the 2nd Street District, a small area in a formerly unglamorous part of downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/dispatch-austins-new-hot-hood/', 'snippet': 'The biggest buzz from Austin is coming from the 2nd Street District, a small area in a formerly unglamorous part of downtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South by Southwest may be over, but Austin still hums along to its own quirky beat. And while there’s always something happening in the many hip hubs in this laid-back Texas town — a young singer-songwriter at the Continental Club on South Congress, a new art exhibit on the once gritty East Side — the biggest buzz lately is coming from the 2nd Street District, a recently designated three-by-two block area in a formerly unglamorous part of downtown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dispatch | Austin’s New Hot Hood', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T15:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jill Fergus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fergus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b4d831f-2ae6-56d5-a310-604ac9770781', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b4d831f-2ae6-56d5-a310-604ac9770781'}, {'abstract': 'Toby’s Corner galloped like a train Saturday, worked to precision Sunday. Monday, he couldn’t trot without limping. Off in his left hind. Veterinarians are thus far stumped for a conclusive reason.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/for-tobys-corner-life-goes-on/', 'snippet': 'Toby’s Corner galloped like a train Saturday, worked to precision Sunday. Monday, he couldn’t trot without limping. Off in his left hind. Veterinarians are thus far stumped for a conclusive reason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Steeplechase Times talked with the connections of Toby’s Corner at the Fair Hill Training Center in the wake of his withdrawal from the Kentucky Derby: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Toby’s Corner, Life Goes On', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'p