he Washington Capitals are more than a top seed being swept in the N.H.L. playoffs; they are a four-year story of promise gone haywire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even if you are not a Washington Capitals fan, please feel free to boo them. It may seem unfair — and a little weird if you’re nowhere near Washington and, say, in a business meeting — but go ahead anyway. The Capitals are more than a No. 1 seed bounced from the Stanley Cup playoffs in a gruesome second-round sweep, they are a four-year story of promise gone haywire. They boast a handful of the game’s most exhilarating players — Alex Ovechkin, Alexander Semin, Nicklas Backstrom and Mike Green — who treat the big stage of the playoffs like children being forced to eat overcooked cabbage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Capitals Exit', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Capitals Exit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, Sidney', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boudreau, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Semin, Alexander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Pau', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ovechkin, Alex', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T16:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e893a9a-