cting-this-weeks-oil-price-tumble/', 'snippet': 'Nationwide, most drivers have not changed their habits much, which suggests that prices will advance again before long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a saying in the oil business: The best cure for high oil prices is high oil prices. In other words, when prices are high, consumers are supposed to buy less at the pump and oil companies are supposed to produce more because it is more profitable to do so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissecting This Week’s Oil Price Tumble', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T17:27:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5a5093-0f4a-5fcb-af25-89e58f84b826', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5a5093-0f4a-5fcb-af25-89e58f84b826'}, {'abstract': 'The sentencing of Habib el-Adli, the once-feared former interior minister, ended the first in a series of corruption trials of top figures in the government of Hosni Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/world/middleeast/06egypt.html', 'snippet': 'The sentencing of Habib el-Adli, the once-feared former interior minister, ended the first in a series of corruption trials of top figures in the government of Hosni Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — An Egyptian court sentenced the once feared former interior minister, Habib el-Adly, to 12 years in prison on Thursday and fined him about $4 million, setting a template for a series of high-profile corruption trials of senior figures in the government of the ousted president, Hosni Mubarak, that could include Mr. Mubarak himself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Feared Egypt Official Gets 12 Years and Fine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Feared Egypt Official Gets 12 Years and Fine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adly, Habib el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T17:29:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ef1f8c2-6511-5e8e-bae5-2da2f69619f1', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ef1f8c2-6511-5e8e-bae5-2da2f69619f1'}, {'abstract': 'A day after celebrating a pact for Palestinian unity, Khaled Meshal declined to swear off violence or agree that a Palestinian state would produce an end to the conflict with Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/world/middleeast/06palestinians.html', 'snippet': 'A day after celebrating a pact for Palestinian unity, Khaled Meshal declined to swear off violence or agree that a Palestinian state would produce an end to the conflict with Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — One day after celebrating a landmark reconciliation accord for Palestinian unity, Khaled Meshal, the Hamas leader, said on Thursday that he was fully committed to working for a two-state solution but declined to swear off violence or agree that a Palestinian state would produce an end to the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hamas Leader Calls for Two-State Solution, but Refuses to Renounce Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hamas Leader Calls for Two-State Solution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meshal, Khaled', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fatah, Al', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T17:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': No