': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f065ac2b-5044-5e68-af77-128149a57c4d', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f065ac2b-5044-5e68-af77-128149a57c4d'}, {'abstract': 'A (most informal) measure of filial love around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/call-your-mother/', 'snippet': 'A (most informal) measure of filial love around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will you be spending Mother’s Day with your mother? If not, will you be giving her a call?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Call Your Mother', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T18:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f232e4-df7f-5f62-aab7-d763b7322319', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f232e4-df7f-5f62-aab7-d763b7322319'}, {'abstract': 'More than 20 million people watched the five finalists in a 90-minute episode of “American Idol.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/fox-with-idol-leads-the-pack/', 'snippet': 'More than 20 million people watched the five finalists in a 90-minute episode of “American Idol.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last five finalists faced off on “American Idol” on Wednesday night as 20.6 million viewers tuned in to the 90-minute episode of the Fox reality show, according to Nielsen’s estimates. Fox led the night over all by a wide margin even as its 9:30 p.m. sitcom, “Breaking In,” drew a much more modest audience of 7.3 million viewers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox, With ‘Idol,’ Leads the Pack', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/964045cf-dc80-5b01-8c28-da9964ca211b', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964045cf-dc80-5b01-8c28-da9964ca211b'}, {'abstract': 'This year, however, some luxury hotels in the Caribbean are offering even better deals than the 2010 low season. Here are four where an off-peak stay costs less than it did last year.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/caribbean-summer-deals-better-than-ever/', 'snippet': 'This year, however, some luxury hotels in the Caribbean are offering even better deals than the 2010 low season. Here are four where an off-peak stay costs less than it did last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Caribbean is a staple winter destination for travelers looking for a warm weather getaway, but through the summer and fall, the threat of rain and hurricanes can mean fewer visitors and dramatically lower prices at many upscale properties. This year, however, some luxury hotels are offering even better deals than the 2010 low season. Here are four where an off-peak stay costs less than it did last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caribbean Summer Deals, Better Than Ever', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahama Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab173ee-97c5-5544-b814-1ca2f4e7c17d', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab173ee-97c5-5544-b814-1ca2f4e7c17d'}, {'abstract': 'Every time someone asks me how I feel about calling the Kentucky Derby, I say it’s a dream come true. It sounds cliche, but it is the truth.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/calling-the-derby-my-dream-my-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Every time someone asks me how I feel about calling the Kentucky Derby, I say it’s a dream come true. It sounds cliche, but it is the truth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Larry Collmus, the announcer at Monmouth Park, will call his first Kentucky Derby for NBC on Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling the Derby: My Dream, My Challenge', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Collmus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collmus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/065158cf-0cff-5532-b1d9-a9cbcb108880', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/065158cf-0cff-5532-b1d9-a9cbcb108880'}, {'abstract': 'Self-consumed mothers, office tattletales and hot versus lukewarm for a prom date.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/fashion/08Social.html', 'snippet': 'Self-consumed mothers, office tattletales and hot versus lukewarm for a prom date.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever I see my mother (which I do as little as possible), we fall into a terrible rut. She asks me a question. I get out a few words of reply. Then she interrupts me and starts talking about herself. This makes me feel much worse than you would think. I haven’t brought it up with her because she doesn’t take criticism well, and I don’t feel like defending myself. I know I should see her on Mother’s Day, but I really don’t want to. Any advice? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/02/21/fashion/21social-1/21social-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s All About My Mother', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s All About My Mother', 'name': None,