', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d5d0998-c492-5a97-bf38-249d317a5806', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d5d0998-c492-5a97-bf38-249d317a5806'}, {'abstract': 'Holding a Socratic seminar to discuss the importance and role of truth in writers’ memoirs, and then crafting personal memoirs and comparing them with others’ recollections.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/in-service-of-the-story-exploring-questions-of-truth-in-memoir/', 'snippet': 'Holding a Socratic seminar to discuss the importance and role of truth in writers’ memoirs, and then crafting personal memoirs and comparing them with others’ recollections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is the role of truth in memoir? Is it O.K. to manipulate facts in the service of conveying a story? In this lesson, students participate in a Socratic seminar to consider questions of truth and fiction in memoir raised by allegations about the veracity of Greg Mortenson’s “Three Cups of Tea.” They also write their own six-word memoirs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Service of the Story? Exploring Questions of Truth in Memoir', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Christy Brown and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': 'Christy', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/904fab96-4420-5c7c-8fc9-82baefccab54', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/904fab96-4420-5c7c-8fc9-82baefccab54'}, {'abstract': 'My profile of Jerry Brown will be in the magazine on Sunday. Here’s an interview I did with The Times, discussing the behind-the-scenes process in reporting a story like this and how Brown compares with other politicians I’ve written about.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/adam-nagourney-talks-about-jerry-brown/', 'snippet': 'My profile of Jerry Brown will be in the magazine on Sunday. Here’s an interview I did with The Times, discussing the behind-the-scenes process in reporting a story like this and how Brown compares with other politicians I’ve written about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My profile of Jerry Brown, the California governor who is making a return engagement in Sacramento, will be in the magazine on Sunday. Here’s an interview I did with The Times, discussing the behind-the-scenes process in reporting a story like this and how Brown compares with other politicians I’ve written about over the years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adam Nagourney Talks About Jerry Brown', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagourney, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c130e09d-8f5e-5a54-a494-6373d032a085', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c130e09d-8f5e-5a54-a494-6373d032a085'}, {'abstract': 'Most flights out of Israel’s international airport were grounded Thursday as a safety precaution, according to Israeli officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/world/middleeast/06israel.html', 'snippet': 'Most flights out of Israel’s international airport were grounded Thursday as a safety precaution, according to Israeli officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Most flights out of Israel’s international airport were grounded Thursday as a safety precaution after the airport’s fuel supply was found to be tainted, Israeli officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tainted Fuel Grounds Israeli Planes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tainted Fuel Grounds Israeli Planes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f51663-1350-5978-9cfa-7431a156bd1a', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f51663-1350-5978-9cfa-7431a156bd1a'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at the general-interest magazine led by Tina Brown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/08/magazine/talk-covers.html', 'snippet': 'A look back at the general-interest magazine led by Tina Brown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look back at the general-interest magazine led by Tina Brown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/talk-covers-slide-HB6D/talk-covers-slide-HB6D-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 785, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/talk-covers-slide-HB6D/talk-covers-slide-HB6D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/magazine/talk-covers-slide-HB6D/talk-covers-slide-HB6D-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two-Plus Years of Talk, in 25 Covers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Tina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:25:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bcf9c014-a678-54de-83ba-bc67fa2ea5f6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bcf9c014-a678-54de-83ba-bc67fa2ea5f6'}, {'abstract': 'An extraordinary, active empathy pervades every one of Tony Kushner’s plays, extended even to those who would not appear to be his allies.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/theater-talkback-the-honorable-tony-kushner/', 'snippet': 'An extraordinary, active empathy pervades every one of Tony Kushner’s plays, extended even to those who would not appear to be his allies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have neither the background nor the inclination to hold forth on Tony Kushner’s political views on the Middle East. But I was deeply saddened to read of the City University of New York’s initial decision, now being reconsidered, to rescind an honorary degree for Mr. Kushner, after a trustee at CUNY said the playwright had made disparaging remarks about the State of Israel, particularly in regard to Israel’s policy toward Palestinians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Tony Kushner and the Art of Empathy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kushner, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/03805f5e-b2f1-5f9c-8edc-1ad2bda047d5', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03805f5e-b2f1-5f9c-8edc-1ad2bda047d5'}, {'abstract': 'Oil prices plummeted by almost 9 percent on Thursday as traders worried that American drivers were beginning to balk at the price of gasoline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/06oil.html', 'snippet': 'Oil prices plummeted by almost 9 percent on Thursday as traders worried that American drivers were beginning to balk at the price of gasoline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Oil prices closed below $100