f a cover-up by the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the $7 billion fraud case against the jailed Texas financier R. Allen Stanford drags on, a whistle-blower says he is concerned about the possibility of a cover-up by the government. In this video interview, CNBC speaks to a former Stanford employee, Charlie Rawl, about the case and the information that he has.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s the Holdup in the Stanford Case?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi Schemes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanford, Robert Allen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford Financial Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f125ee57-2cb5-52c6-9aa9-f39516afefef', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f125ee57-2cb5-52c6-9aa9-f39516afefef'}, {'abstract': 'The body, which was still strapped in its seat on the Air France plane that crashed on June 1, 2009, was raised early Thursday from a debris field 3,900 meters below the surface of the Atlantic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/world/europe/06iht-france06.html', 'snippet': 'The body, which was still strapped in its seat on the Air France plane that crashed on June 1, 2009, was raised early Thursday from a debris field 3,900 meters below the surface of the Atlantic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — An underwater salvage team on Thursday began the grisly task of recovering the remains of the victims of an Air France jet that crashed in the Atlantic two years ago, retrieving the first of possibly dozens of bodies from the wreckage as experts gather evidence that they hope will shed more light on what happened in the flight’s final moments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Body in Jet Wreckage Is Retrieved From Sea Bottom', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: 2 Years After Jet Crash, Body Is Retrieved From the Ocean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ce233d-b271-501b-bfd0-5eab80e62173', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ce233d-b271-501b-bfd0-5eab80e62173'}, {'abstract': 'Lucien Smith and Jack Siegel have created a show on false memories of the past.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/now-recalling-imagined-nostalgia/', 'snippet': 'Lucien Smith and Jack Siegel have created a show on false memories of the past.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I wanted to create objects from a childhood that I never experienced firsthand,” Lucien Smith says, explaining the background of “Imagined Nostalgia,” which opens May 6 at 41 Cooper Gallery. The show is a collaboration between Smith, 22, and Jack Siegel, 24, who shared studio space at Cooper Union (where Smith is enrolled and set to graduate this month). The work is based on how our imaginations create false memories of what actually happened in the past — how we remember something from the past and embellish it to make it seem worse or better, larger than life, different. Highlights include yearbook-style photographs from familiar New York faces like the filmmaker Austin Peters and the artist Brenden Lynch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Recalling | ‘Imagined Nostalgia’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T19:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Moonves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moonves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/39cfae9e-7846-5af5-9f72-626a4ded0d0b', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39cfae9e-7846-5af5-9f72-626a4ded0d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Surely if there is uncertainty about the health of Uncle Mo this close to the race, there will be uncertainty on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/scratch-uncle-mo/', 'snippet': 'Surely if there is uncertainty about the health of Uncle Mo this close to the race, there will be uncertainty on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is only three days before the Kentucky Derby and Uncle Mo, the 2-year-old champion who had his only defeat as the 1-10 favorite in the Wood Memorial, is only 50-50 to start in the Kentucky Derby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scratch Uncle Mo', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, '