r job growth, like economic growth, has slowed.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/5-questions-about-fridays-jobs-report/', 'snippet': 'The jobs report for April, to be released on Friday, will shed light on whether job growth, like economic growth, has slowed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Below, we pose five questions to ask about Friday’s jobs report, much as we did a month ago. The big picture is that job growth has been picking up in recent months — but the job market is still a long way from being healthy, and the last month or so has offered new reason for concern.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '5 Questions About Friday’s Jobs Report', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T20:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/abf6bab1-315d-5f50-ab02-9517e2084980', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abf6bab1-315d-5f50-ab02-9517e2084980'}, {'abstract': 'Heading into negotiations, both sides emphasize their broad agreement on the goals, but they remain far apart on specifics.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/biden-calls-first-deficit-meeting-productive/', 'snippet': 'Heading into negotiations, both sides emphasize their broad agreement on the goals, but they remain far apart on specifics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. said he and six Congressional negotiators had “a good, productive first meeting” on Thursday morning in what is likely to be a prolonged effort to forge some agreement on long-term deficit reduction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Calls First Deficit Meeting ‘Productive’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T20:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e93eebb-440a-50e2-8889-67e0bfb58bcd', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e93eebb-440a-50e2-8889-67e0bfb58bcd'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Popcast, Jon Caramanica discusses the evolution and career prospects of Tyler, the Creator, and Dana Jennings discusses Emmylou Harris.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/popcast-can-tyler-create-a-career/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Popcast, Jon Caramanica discusses the evolution and career prospects of Tyler, the Creator, and Dana Jennings discusses Emmylou Harris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a prodigiously profane mixtape and YouTube sensation cross over into something like mainstream success? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Can Tyler Create a Career?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {