leasing Foodies And Regular Joes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T21:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1226faf8-05b8-58eb-8c61-635a7d939498', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1226faf8-05b8-58eb-8c61-635a7d939498'}, {'abstract': 'The Alexander McQueen retrospective at the Metropolitan Museum of Art set an attendance record for the opening day of a Costume Institute exhibition — and nearly for the entire museum.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/mcqueen-almost-as-good-as-van-gogh/', 'snippet': 'The Alexander McQueen retrospective at the Metropolitan Museum of Art set an attendance record for the opening day of a Costume Institute exhibition — and nearly for the entire museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Alexander McQueen retrospective at the Metropolitan Museum of Art set an attendance record for the opening day of a Costume Institute exhibition — and nearly for the entire museum. The show had 5,100 visitors on Wednesday, beating out popular shows like the Jacqueline Kennedy and Chanel exhibitions, though time will tell if the numbers hold up for the duration of the show. The crowd was so large that the Met had to temporarily suspend its guided tours, a spokeswoman said. The museum sold 600 catalogs that day in its gift shop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McQueen Almost as Good as Van Gogh', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': 