: 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Court of Human Rights', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T21:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c22aec1b-91aa-5f35-82d8-4f1d3f86efe7', 'word_count': 1441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c22aec1b-91aa-5f35-82d8-4f1d3f86efe7'}, {'abstract': 'A depressed toy manufacturer fails to commit suicide and begins communicating through a hand puppet. Nasty and brutish, the beaver owns the film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/the-beaver-with-mel-gibson-and-jodie-foster-review.html', 'snippet': 'A depressed toy manufacturer fails to commit suicide and begins communicating through a hand puppet. Nasty and brutish, the beaver owns the film.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Beaver,” a dysfunctional-family melodrama about depression, and the ties that bind and throttle, and the tears that trickle but dry in the warm glow of said family, has a card up (or actually on) its sleeve, and it isn’t entirely Mel Gibson. Directed by Jodie Foster, who has unwisely given herself a supporting role as a weepy little woman, the film involves a depressed toy manufacturer, Walter Black (Mr. Gibson), who, after failing to commit suicide, begins communicating through a hand puppet. Nasty, brutish and as cuddly as a crusty old sock fished out of a sewer, the beaver or the beav, as I like to think of him, owns the film.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06BEAVER-span/SUB-BEAVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06BEAVER-span/SUB-BEAVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06BEAVER-span/SUB-BEAVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06BEAVER-span/SUB-BEAVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06BEAVER-span/SUB-BEAVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leave It to the Beaver to Do All the Talking', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Beaver'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leave It to the Beaver To Do All the Talking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Mel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Jodie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T21:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'n