ed by the plaintiffs on Thursday, three months after it was filed. The plaintiffs in the class-action suit had argued that Mr. Carter’s “Palestine: Peace Not Apartheid,” about the Arab-Israeli conflict, was falsely marketed as “absolute truth.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/plaintiffs-drop-suit-over-jimmy-carter-book/', 'snippet': 'A $5 million lawsuit against Simon & Schuster over a book by former President Jimmy Carter was dropped by the plaintiffs on Thursday, three months after it was filed. The plaintiffs in the class-action suit had argued that Mr. Carter’s “Palestine:...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $5 million lawsuit against Simon & Schuster over a book by former President Jimmy Carter was dropped by the plaintiffs on Thursday, three months after it was filed. The plaintiffs in the class-action suit had argued that Mr. Carter’s “Palestine: Peace Not Apartheid,” about the Arab-Israeli conflict, was falsely marketed as “absolute truth.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plaintiffs Drop Suit Over Jimmy Carter Book', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon & Schuster Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T21:57:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c35af4d-ab49-5c36-a709-fdc930661ddc', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c35af4d-ab49-5c36-a709-fdc930661ddc'}, {'abstract': 'As exciting as these playoffs have been, they nonetheless will be an afterthought. Once they are completed, the players will almost certainly be locked out, perhaps for a full season.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/looking-to-europe-as-lockout-looms/', 'snippet': 'As exciting as these playoffs have been, they nonetheless will be an afterthought. Once they are completed, the players will almost certainly be locked out, perhaps for a full season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As exciting as these playoffs have been, they nonetheless will be an afterthought. Once they are completed, the players will almost certainly be locked out, perhaps for a full season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking to Europe as Lockout Looms', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Deeks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deeks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/373a0677-fbce-56d0-8c3a-eaeb30aee4cc', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/373a0677-fbce-56d0-8c3a-eaeb30aee4cc'}, {'abstract': 'Artopolis Bakery, in the corner of a shopping complex in Astoria, Queens, has a clientele that includes bohemians, families pushing strollers and old men in black suits.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/artopolis-bakery/', 'snippet': 'Artopolis Bakery, in the corner of a shopping complex in Astoria, Queens, has a clientele that includes bohemians, families pushing strollers and old men in black suits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It all started with a sweet, cinnamon-tinted whiff. The subway roaring above, I crossed the street and followed my curiosity to the Greek bakery tucked in the corner of a shopping complex in Astoria, Queens. That afternoon, on the first of my many visits to Artopolis Bakery, on 31st Street and 23rd Avenue, there were bohemians, families pushing strollers, and old men in black suits lined up against the counter or crowded at the few wrought-iron tables, dunking cookies in the darkest coffee I’d ever seen.Read the Full Article »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pastries and Aromas of Greece', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Astoria (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvie Bigar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bigar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/608c8ab8-e5bb-5e2c-809a-93851fd1ece2', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/608c8ab8-e5bb-5e2c-809a-93851fd1ece2'}, {'abstract': 'The South Carolina governor said the contenders should talk about what they would do right, and not dwell on President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/haley-to-g-o-p-candidates-its-go-time/', 'snippet': 'The South Carolina governor said the contenders should talk about what they would do right, and not dwell on President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, S.C. — As five candidates prepared to take the stage here Thursday night for the first debate of the Republican presidential nominating contest — barely a quorum of the field that may ultimately shape the race — the fretting about whether the party will find someone strong enough to defeat President Obama intensified.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haley to G.O.P. Candidates: ‘It’s Go Time’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bc9c5b0-7157-5218-9e97-6e61c3b09e3b', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bc9c5b0-7157-5218-9e97-6e61c3b09e3b'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to pop, rock, hip-hop, folk and other performances in New York and the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/music/pop-and-rock-listings-for-may-6-12.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to pop, rock, hip-hop, folk and other performances in New York and the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pop', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop and Rock Listings for May 6-12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prudential Center (Newark)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:10:29+0000', 'document_typ