hives and MoMA looks at the San Francisco Bay Area as humming hub for great avant-garde film and video makers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/radical-light-alternative-film-in-san-francisco-area.html', 'snippet': 'The Radical Light series at Anthology Film Archives and MoMA looks at the San Francisco Bay Area as humming hub for great avant-garde film and video makers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is geography destiny? Or, to put it another way, why did the San Francisco Bay Area become a humming hub for so many great avant-garde film and video makers, a veritable crossroads of the alternative world? ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06RADICAL-span/RADICAL-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06RADICAL-span/RADICAL-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06RADICAL-span/RADICAL-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06RADICAL-span/RADICAL-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06RADICAL-span/RADICAL-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco, the Crossroads of the Avant-Garde', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'San Francisco, the Crossroads of the Avant-Garde', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTHOLOGY FILM ARCHIVES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peterson, Sidney', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fa46981-a669-54a6-b922-7adbd92cb0a1', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fa46981-a669-54a6-b922-7adbd92cb0a1'}, {'abstract': 'Sudden and swift.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/the-republican-descent-into-economic-darkness/', 'snippet': 'Sudden and swift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Avent listens to Paul Ryan’s ideas on macroeconomic policy, and is appalled: it’s all spending cuts and tight money, which would be a recipe for another recession.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Republican Descent Into Economic Darkness', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d64c082a-839a-5265-a70b-f5ce953a800f', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d64c082a-839a-5265-a70b-f5ce953a800f'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York and the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/music/jazz-listings-for-may-6-12.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to jazz performances in New York and the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jazz', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Listings for May 6-12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a6e2612-87fb-5d0c-88b1-aa6f6df77989', 'word_count': 2126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a6e2612-87fb-5d0c-88b1-aa6f6df77989'}, {'abstract': 'The latest story collection from Julian Barnes is filled with both gems and should-have-been discards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/books/pulse-short-stories-by-julian-barnes-review.html', 'snippet': 'The latest story collection from Julian Barnes is filled with both gems and should-have-been discards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As his many novels and earlier short stories have demonstrated, Julian Barnes is one of those confident literary decathletes, proficient at old-fashioned storytelling, dialogue-driven portraiture, postmodern collage, and political allegory and farce. He’s a true literary professional whose most compelling work showcases his musical prose, his ear for the chattering class’s chatter (“Talking It Over”), his ability to create narratives with both surface brio and finely calibrated philosophical subtexts (“Flaubert’s Parrot,” “The Porcupine”). His weaker efforts, however, can be overly cerebral and contrived, with bloodless characters and story lines that have been cut and pasted into pretentious blueprints (“Arthur & George,” “Love, Etc.”). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06book/BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06book/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06book/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love, Loss, Change and Being English', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love, Loss, Change And Being English', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnes, Julian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/99d35de0-9346-5fa9-a141-8b12f199b83c', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99d35de0-9346-5fa9-a141-8b12f199b83c'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to dance performances in New York and the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/dance/dance-listings-for-may-6-12.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to dance performances in New York and the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan