, 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/33f8cb4e-3756-56e3-8664-2e32bab654f6'}, {'abstract': 'Peering into her crystal ball, a writer imagines the two Ivies’ continuing to reject almost all who apply, but with tuition too high for anyone to come.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/crimson-bulldog/', 'snippet': 'Peering into her crystal ball, a writer imagines the two Ivies’ continuing to reject almost all who apply, but with tuition too high for anyone to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will the day soon come when Shanghai University buys Princeton, an online Bill Gates University (B.G.U.) boasts six Rhodes Scholars, and Harvard and Yale, in an effort to stem dwindling enrollment and shrinking endowments, merge?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imagining a Harvard-Yale Merger', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T22:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5719b6e6-c7bf-56fd-bfa3-d5ac50e8237b', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5719b6e6-c7bf-56fd-bfa3-d5ac50e8237b'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/design/museum-and-gallery-listings-for-may-6-12.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to the visual arts in New York and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum and Gallery Listings for May 6-12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':