 full of revelations revolving around class conflict between the two bridal families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Farce and melodrama are two sides of the same coin, a coin that “Jumping the Broom” tosses in the air, spins on its rim, drops on the floor and loses between the cushions of the couch. The director, Salim Akil, a television veteran, handles an awful lot of hectic business with suavity and restraint, which is a mixed blessing. It might have been better to embrace the chaos rather than underplay it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06JUMPING/JUMPING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06JUMPING/06JUMPING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06JUMPING/06JUMPING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Families Put Asunder Just Before the ‘I Dos’', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Jumping the Broom'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Families Put Asunder Just Before the ‘I Dos’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bassett, Angela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epps, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-0