ernment bailout that weighed heavily on its financial results.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/a-i-g-s-1st-quarter-net-income-tumbles-85/', 'snippet': 'The American International Group recorded charges tied to the Japan earthquake in March and to restructuring its government bailout that weighed heavily on its financial results.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:56 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.I.G.’s 1st-Quarter Profit Tumbles 85%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SunAmerica Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/42e5b944-c90f-5a55-b3d0-7d786a1c1f79', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42e5b944-c90f-5a55-b3d0-7d786a1c1f79'}, {'abstract': 'Angus MacLise, an original member of the Velvet Underground, didn’t achieve the prominence of others in that group, but a new exhibition suggests he was an influential force in the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/music/angus-maclise-of-velvet-underground-in-dreamweapon.html', 'snippet': 'Angus MacLise, an original member of the Velvet Underground, didn’t achieve the prominence of others in that group, but a new exhibition suggests he was an influential force in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A\u2002YOUNG man stands slouching on the stoop of a crumbling Lower East Side tenement. His back is turned, but he cocks his head toward the camera, his eyes hidden behind dark shades. Beside him, staring straight ahead, are three other young men who will soon become famous. Yet 46 years later the fourth is still a sphinx.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06MACLISE-span/JP-MACLISE-1-1304620050024-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06MACLISE-span/JP-MACLISE-1-1304620050024-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 254}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06MACLISE-span/JP-MACLISE-1-1304620050024-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06MACLISE-span/06MACLISE-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06MACLISE-span/06MACLISE-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Velvet Unknown, Now Emerging', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Velvet Unknown, Now Emerging', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Velvet Underground', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/642f72cc-344b-5750-9102-97be8c43fb9f', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/642f72cc-344b-5750-9102-97be8c43fb9f'}, {'abstract': '“Octubre,” a Peruvian film, shows how life changes for a shabby moneylender in Lima when an infant is left on his bed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/octubre-by-daniel-and-diego-vega-review.html', 'snippet': '“Octubre,” a Peruvian film, shows how life changes for a shabby moneylender in Lima when an infant is left on his bed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you first meet Clemente, the humble, eventually humbled moneylender who becomes something of a reluctant hero in the unassuming, low-key charmer “Octubre,” he’s counting pennies instead of blessings. You can scarcely blame him. Unsmiling, seemingly friendless, he lives and works out of a run-down apartment in Lima, Peru, that — with its peeling wallpaper and badly scarred walls, and its passing parade of men and women hocking bits of their lives — makes a fitting setting for this hard stone of a man. The specter of his admired dead father hovers here, a twin perhaps to the images of Jesus seen everywhere else.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06OCTUBRE-span/OCTUBRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06OCTUBRE-span/OCTUBRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06OCTUBRE-span/OCTUBRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06OCTUBRE-span/OCTUBRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06OCTUBRE-span/OCTUBRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Difference a Baby Can Make', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Octubre'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Difference a Baby Can Make', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:12:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aa79b14-e976-5070-a0b8-a8a078450b0f', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aa79b14-e976-5070-a0b8-a8a078450b0f'}, {'abstract': 'Nature is wild but proportioned at the new Azalea Garden, which reflects a particular philosophy of garden display, at the New York Botanical Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/design/azalea-garden-at-new-york-botanical-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Nature is wild but proportioned at the new Azalea Garden, which reflects a particular philosophy of garden display, at the New York Botanical Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stand at an overlook along the mile of paths winding through the enchanting 11-acre Azalea Garden that opens on Saturday at the New York Botanical Garden in the Bronx, and look down over the lush plantings. Broad sprays of white, pale pink and lavender seem almost haphazardly arrayed. Some flowers are just beginning to reveal themselves; others are extravagantly pronounced, sweeping across the hill in bands, punctuated by coarse foliated rock formations and tall trees that have yet to display robust signs of spring. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06AZALEAS-span/AZALEAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06AZALEAS-span/AZALEAS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06AZALEAS-span/AZALEAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06AZALEAS-span/AZALEAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06AZALEAS-span/AZALEAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Method Behind All the Wildness', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Method Behind All the Wildness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Botanical Garden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/218a13cc-ea41-5a3a-8c43-207ca155d9c6', 'word_count': 1383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/218a13cc-ea41-5a3a-8c43-207ca155d9c6'}, {'abstract': 'At the Jewish Museum “Collecting Matisse and Modern Masters” presents a selection of works from the collection of the Baltimore sisters Etta and Claribel Cone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/design/collecting-matisse-at-jewish-museum-review.html', 'snippet': 'At the Jewish Museum “Collecting Matisse and Modern Masters” presents a selection of works from the collection of the Baltimore sisters Etta and Claribel Cone.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Collecting Matisse and Modern Masters: The Cone Sisters of Baltimore,” at the Jewish Museum, samples the extraordinary trove of European art amassed by two American spinsters in the first half of the 20th century. The Baltimore Museum of Art owns their collection — all 3,000 pieces, including some 500 Matisses — but others are free to tell the Cones’ story.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/MATISSE/MATISSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What They Loved and What They Bought', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What They Loved and What They Bought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matisse, Henri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Museum (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article