Osama bin Laden’s killing were a matter of “pure existential release,” a social psychologist said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/health/06revenge.html', 'snippet': 'Raucous rallies that broke out in New York and Washington after news of Osama bin Laden’s killing were a matter of “pure existential release,” a social psychologist said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some Americans celebrated the killing of Osama bin Laden loudly, with chanting and frat-party revelry in the streets. Others were appalled — not by the killing, but by the celebrations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/world/05revenge2/05revenge2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/world/05revenge2/05revenge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/world/05revenge2/05revenge2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating a Death: Ugly, Maybe, but Only Human', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating a Death: Ugly, Maybe, but Only Human', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/0568e2a4-b26e-50da-95aa-bb002b5903ae', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0568e2a4-b26e-50da-95aa-bb002b5903ae'}, {'abstract': 'A noir-flavored reverie directed by Mitch Glazer and starring Mickey Rourke and Bill Murray, “Passion Play” is metaphysically ambitious but barely palatable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/passion-play-with-mickey-rourke-review.html', 'snippet': 'A noir-flavored reverie directed by Mitch Glazer and starring Mickey Rourke and Bill Murray, “Passion Play” is metaphysically ambitious but barely palatable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a hard-living loser with the face of a smashed pumpkin find redemption in the arms of a real-life earth angel? That is the silly question floating through “Passion Play,” a fatuous noir-flavored reverie with allegorical pretensions written and directed by Mitch Glazer. Set in the desert at places with portentous names like the Dream Lounge, “Passion Play” wants desperately to be something like an artier, more metaphysically ambitious answer to mood pieces like Alan Rudolph’s “Trouble in Mind.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/movies/06passion-span/06passion-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/movies/06passion-span/06passion-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/movies/06passion-span/06passion-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': Non