sit on Sept. 14, 2001.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Doug Mills was last at ground zero, he was working for The Associated Press. The sky was overcast. The World Trade Center lay in ruin. And Osama bin Laden had only one day earlier been implicated as the prime suspect in the attack by the administration of President George W. Bush, whom Mr. Mills accompanied to New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doug Mills at Ground Zero, 10 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mills, Doug', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-05T23:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/64266977-2f5c-57db-829e-2380707112d2', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64266977-2f5c-57db-829e-2380707112d2'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of classical music performances in the United States this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/arts/music/classical-music-in-the-us-this-summer.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of classical music performances in the United States this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arizona', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/CLASSICAL-1/CLASSICAL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei