imedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bf2076ef-ec1d-53ff-a5fa-678cd18f54ad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bf2076ef-ec1d-53ff-a5fa-678cd18f54ad'}, {'abstract': 'A response to an article about the reduction of pensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/opinion/lweb06pension.html', 'snippet': 'A response to an article about the reduction of pensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying for Public Pension Mistakes', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paying for Public Pension Mistakes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T00:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eac1b3e2-12f0-5c04-8c49-ebabb515167d', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eac1b3e2-12f0-5c04-8c49-ebabb515167d'}, {'abstract': 'San Francisco’s public employee unions want to change accounting procedures for the pension fund, but experts say their plan is legally dubious and would cost millions of dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/us/06bcdeal.html', 'snippet': 'San Francisco’s public employee unions want to change accounting procedures for the pension fund, but experts say their plan is legally dubious and would cost millions of dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a final push to get a consensus pension-reform measure on the ballot this fall, San Francisco’s public-employee unions are lobbying hard for a change in accounting procedures that experts say is legally dubious and would cost the city hundreds of millions of dollars in the long run.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Experts See Peril for City in Union Pension Proposal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experts See Peril for City In Union Pension Proposal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T00:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Lesly Stevens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'Lesly', 'lastname': 'Stevens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229f47ea-97ee-510d-9eb0-4fbfce811a3c', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229f47ea-97ee-510d-9eb0-4fbfce811a3c'}, {'abstract': 'In his autobiographical show at Feinstein’s, Peter Asher, the Peter of Peter and Gordon, tells tales of his life at the center of the British music scene in the 1960s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/arts/music/peter-ashers-musical-memoir-at-feinsteins-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his autobiographical show at Feinstein’s, Peter Asher, the Peter of Peter and Gordon, tells tales of his life at the center of the British music scene in the 1960s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Asher, a red-headed pixie at 66, has enjoyed at least three lives in the music business: as a singer and guitarist, as an executive for the Beatles’ Apple Records, and as a manager and producer of James Taylor and Linda Ronstadt. Although these overlapping identities are covered in Mr. Asher’s entertaining, autobiographical show, “A Musical Memoir of the 60s and Beyond,” at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, the show’s musical heart belongs to mid-’60s British Invasion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06ASHER/ASHER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06ASHER/ASHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06ASHER/ASHER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Inside Take on the British Invasion', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Inside Take on the British Invasion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T00:08:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41fe541b-0a08-5021-9f89-322787556c9f', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41fe541b-0a08-5021-9f89-322787556c9f'}, {'abstract': 'A vanguard of public officials around the Bay Area are pushing sophisticated traffic and parking solutions built on the theory of congestion pricing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/us/06bccongestion.html', 'snippet': 'A vanguard of public officials around the Bay Area are pushing sophisticated traffic and parking solutions built on the theory of congestion pricing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jay Primus’s small office at the San Francisco Municipal Transportation Agency could be mistaken for that of a science professor. The walls are covered with giant maps and colorful charts, all aimed at helping to illuminate one of the big mysteries in the life of any city dweller: how to find a parking space.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/us/06BCCONGESTION2/06BCCONGESTION2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/us/06BCCONGESTION2/06BCCONGESTION2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/us/06BCCONGESTION2/06BCCONGESTION2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/us/06BCCONGESTION2/06BCCONGESTION2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/us/06BCCONGESTION2/06BCCONGESTION2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Want to Add to Congestion? Then It’s Going to Cost You', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Want to Add To Congestion? Then It’s Going To Cost You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francis