lead_paragraph': 'Only weeks ago, top Democrats appeared to have all but written off a special election for a Congressional seat in the suburbs of Buffalo. After all, Republican voters vastly outnumber Democrats in the district, and the Republican candidate, Jane L. Corwin, a well-liked state assemblywoman, seemed to be a shoo-in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/Cong-SF/Cong-SF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/Cong-SF/Cong-SF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/Cong-SF/Cong-SF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Medicare Plan Shakes Up Race for House Seat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicare Plan Shakes Up Race For House Seat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buffalo (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T00:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f0faadd-f953-5642-ba98-44b8e22ec412', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f0faadd-f953-5642-ba98-44b8e22ec412'}, {'abstract': 'The overall traditional path to the Derby has also been altered. Trainers have to be conscious of their graded earnings. They have to train aggressively into each race, because each race actually is totally meaningful and no longer a prep. We have traditionally called prestigious races like the Gotham, Wood, Florida Derby and many others, Derby preps.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/earnings-are-king-on-the-road-to-the-derby/', 'snippet': 'The overall traditional path to the Derby has also been altered. Trainers have to be conscious of their graded earnings. They have to train aggressively into each race, because each race actually is totally meaningful and no longer a prep. We have...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruno De Julio has been a workout analyst and thoroughbred owner for the past 20 years. He is the author of “Bruno on Workouts: Exposing the Mystery” and can be found daily at Racing With Bruno and Grade One Racing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earnings Are King on the Road to the Derby', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruno De Julio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruno', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Julio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2e8da6-93f9-5aa0-b5bb-00c239e6994e', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2e8da6-93f9-5aa0-b5bb-00c239e6994e'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Keller talks with Joao Silva and Greg Marinovich about what animates — and terrifies — combat photographers.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/the-inner-lives-of-wartime-photographers/', 'snippet': 'Bill Keller talks with Joao Silva and Greg Marinovich about what animates — and terrifies — combat photographers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Bill Keller, the executive editor of The New York Times, met with the photographers Joao Silva and Greg Marinovich at Walter Reed Army Medical Center, where Mr. Silva is recovering from the grave injuries he suffered — including the loss of his legs — when a land mine exploded under him in Afghanistan. Mr. Marinovich and Mr. Silva are the authors of “The Bang-Bang Club” (2000), an account of the tumultuous end of apartheid in South Africa that was made into a movie in 2010. Their conversation, which served as the basis for Mr. Keller’s column in The Times Magazine this week, is presented here in full, with minor editing and condensing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘To Be on the Edge of History’', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e0a6e0-72f7-5fed-a4b5-f888e2f02cc7', 'word_count': 8064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e0a6e0-72f7-5fed-a4b5-f888e2f02cc7'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas Legislature’s biennial session is winding down. Time is crucial and important bills are often held up by lawmakers’ attention to less serious matters, like sexy cheerleaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/us/06ttramsey.html', 'snippet': 'The Texas Legislature’s biennial session is winding down. Time is crucial and important bills are often held up by lawmakers’ attention to less serious matters, like sexy cheerleaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s tense at the Texas Capitol. It’s May — the last month of the session. Deadlines are arriving daily. Bills are dying. Legislative wish lists are drying up and blowing away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Really Important Bills? Sorry, the Puppies Ate Them', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Really Important Bills? Sorry, the Puppies Ate Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53bc4a82-6ab2-559e-b648-de75e39ecc71', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53bc4a82-6ab2-559e-b648-de75e39ecc71'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Batiste stars in this “Lord Byron,” which was made for less than $1,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/lord-byron-from-zack-godshall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Batiste stars in this “Lord Byron,” which was made for less than $1,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite his literary moniker, the eponymous hero of “Lord Byron” is unlikely to be accused of being mad, bad or dangerous to know. Not by his lady friends, who are numerous and devoted; nor by his ex-wife and her two daughters, with whom he lives in comfortable dysfunction.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06lord-span/ROUNDUP-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06lord-span/ROUNDUP-5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06lord-span/ROUNDUP-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06lord-span/ROUNDUP-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06lord-span/ROUNDUP-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Life of a Searcher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Lord Byron'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cc3e305-4680-5941-bce2-28a1759071af', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cc3e305-4680-5941-bce2-28a1759071af'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission hasn’t done enough to forestall a recurrence of the brief, terrifying stock market plunge of May 6, 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/opinion/06kaufman.html', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission hasn’t done enough to forestall a recurrence of the brief, terrifying stock market plunge of May 6, 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE year ago, the stock market took a brief and terrifying nose-dive.\xa0Almost a trillion dollars in wealth momentarily vanished. Shares in blue-chip companies were traded at absurdly low prices. High-frequency traders, who use computers to look for microscopic price differences in stocks on different exchanges and other trading venues, stopped trading, while others immediately sold whatever they bought, mainly to each other, in what has been called “hot potato” trading. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preventing the Next Flash Crash', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Preventing the Next Flash Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By EDWARD E. KAUFMAN Jr. AND CARL M. LEVIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'KAUFMAN', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a586c1-e78a-57e7-bc58-f3ef12884fe1', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a586c1-e78a-57e7-bc58-f3ef12884fe1'}, {'abstract': 'In a documentary, Kevin Tostado follows people obsessed with the board game Monopoly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/crazy-for-thimbles.html', 'snippet': 'In a documentary, Kevin Tostado follows people obsessed with the board game Monopoly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the end of this perky, quirky documentary by Kevin Tostado, you might think that Monopoly, the durable board game, ranks right up there with the Bible in cultural and spiritual importance. It doesn’t, of course, but don’t tell that to any of the people who appear in this film; they are obsessed with the game beyond all reason and seem darned happy to be so.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06under/ROUNDUP-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06under/ROUNDUP-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06under/ROUNDUP-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crazy for Thimbles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Under the Boardwalk: The Monopoly Story'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:07:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firs