75-5fe6-8a5d-fd9843e7fff5'}, {'abstract': 'The 42 players who made their major league debuts in March and April have been putting up abysmal numbers at the plate.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/in-the-majors-young-players-are-still-teething-at-the-plate/', 'snippet': 'The 42 players who made their major league debuts in March and April have been putting up abysmal numbers at the plate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Through the first month of the season, baseball’s new major leaguers have started off as the worst-hitting bunch ever. While offense is slightly off throughout baseball, the 42 players who made their debut in March or April have all failed to contribute to their teams at the plate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Majors, Young Players Are Still Teething at the Plate', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belt, Brandon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Lance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holliday, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:13:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Forman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb44f0a-62c3-54fd-b1e8-b7ee92e4d8fa', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb44f0a-62c3-54fd-b1e8-b7ee92e4d8fa'}, {'abstract': 'In the Andean region of Colombia, people are menaced on one side by guerrillas and on the other by paramilitary groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/the-colors-of-the-mountain-set-in-colombia-review.html', 'snippet': 'In the Andean region of Colombia, people are menaced on one side by guerrillas and on the other by paramilitary groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A soccer ball marooned in a minefield is the central image of Carlos César Arbeláez’s quietly assured debut feature film, “The Colors of the Mountain,” set in a remote village in the Andean region of Colombia. And it’s a neat enough symbol for the characters’ lives, which are menaced on one side by guerrillas and on the other by paramilitary groups.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06colors/BROUNDUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06colors/BROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06colors/BROUNDUP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggles in Colombia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'The Colors of the Mountain'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:14:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3eea6f8-996e-5d28-b48a-95c837348c7a', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3eea6f8-996e-5d28-b48a-95c837348c7a'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion companies leapt into action to copy Kate Middleton’s wedding gown, but surprisingly, customers want copies of the bridesmaid’s gown, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/06dress.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion companies leapt into action to copy Kate Middleton’s wedding gown, but surprisingly, customers want copies of the bridesmaid’s gown, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly before the start of the royal wedding last Friday, designers and bridal boutiques planning knockoff dresses went into action when they got their first glimpse of the gown.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/06dress3_inline/06dress3_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/06dress3_inline/06dress3_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/business/06dress3_inline/06dress3_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Last, a Reason to Be Always the Bridesmaid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Last, a Reason to Be Always the Bridesmaid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82d46e3d-e87a-536a-a515-8edbeab73502', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82d46e3d-e87a-536a-a515-8edbeab73502'}, {'abstract': 'The news that the Duke and Duchess of Cambridge will visit has inspired some suggestions for their itinerary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/us/06california.html', 'snippet': 'The news that the Duke and Duchess of Cambridge will visit has inspired some suggestions for their itinerary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — It is, in many ways, a match made in heaven: California and the royal newlyweds. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/us/CALIFORNIA-2/CALIFORNIA-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/us/CALIFORNIA-2/CALIFORNIA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/us/CALIFORNIA-2/CALIFORNIA-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California, Here They Come: Tips for the Royal Newlyweds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California, Here They Come: Tips for the Royal Newlyweds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charles, Prince of Wales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e88e727d-def1-59e8-814f-c86decc0e7b5', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e88e727d-def1-59e8-814f-c86decc0e7b5'}, {'abstract': 'A woman faces her husband, just returned from the Sino-Japanese wars limbless and deaf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/movies/caterpillar-a-war-story-from-japan-review.html', 'snippet': 'A woman faces her husband, just returned from the Sino-Japanese wars limbless and deaf.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Caterpillar” is a slight deviation for its director, Koji Wakamatsu, who began his long career as a sexual-political provocateur by churning out the soft-core films known as pinku eiga. Here, his usual sledgehammer critique of Japanese nationalism, militarism and male domination is delivered without his usual degree of stylistic filigree (though there is some grisly, fascinating World War II-era footage of battle in China and of Japanese war criminals being hanged). The bulk of the film looks like a quiet domestic melodrama involving a Japanese villager and her husband, just returned from the Sino-Japanese wars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06cater-span/06cater-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06cater-span/06cater-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06cater-span/06cater-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06cater-span/06cater-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/06cater-span/06cater-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the War, a Tense Rehabilitation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Caterpillar'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wakamatsu, Koji', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a6047a-baf3-5988-92c3-45073fe13eb6', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a6047a-baf3-5988-92c3-45073fe13eb6'}, {'abstract': 'The second round of the Stanley Cup playoffs has exposed weaknesses not fully evident in teams earlier — like the Washington Capitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/sports/hockey/06hockey.html', 'snippet': 'The second round of the Stanley Cup playoffs has exposed weaknesses not fully evident in teams earlier — like the Washington Capitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The second round of the Stanley Cup playoffs is turning out to be as one-sided as the first round was close. And for the teams that have lost or are in danger of losing in four games, the consequences of being swept could be significant.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/sports/y-nhl/y-nhl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 972, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/sports/y-nhl/y-nhl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/sports/y-nhl/y-nhl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Losers, Sweeps May Have Big Consequences', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Losers, Sweeps May Have Big Consequences', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boudreau, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subjec