e New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/LAURENTS2-obit/LAURENTS2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/LAURENTS2-obit/LAURENTS2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/arts/LAURENTS2-obit/LAURENTS2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arthur Laurents, Playwright and Director on Broadway, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arthur Laurents, Playwright and Director on Broadway, Dies at 93', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laurents, Arthur', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:28:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Berkvist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkvist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/137d5552-4580-5415-8d42-87561a782346', 'word_count': 2323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/137d5552-4580-5415-8d42-87561a782346'}, {'abstract': 'What role did the U.S. Coast Survey play in West Virginia’s decision to stick with the Union?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/how-a-map-divided-virginia/', 'snippet': 'What role did the U.S. Coast Survey play in West Virginia’s decision to stick with the Union?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The secession crisis created tremendous turmoil in Virginia. The state initially considered leaving the Union in February, and then again in early April, but on both occasions the proposal was defeated. This was partly a matter of geography: slavery was relatively rare in the western counties, and as the crisis intensified residents there began to see secession as primarily driven by the interests of slaveholders. As easterners became more strident about their rights, those in the west began to see themselves as a separate group with fundamentally different interests. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Map Divided Virginia', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/475b64bf-faea-557f-b48f-c0f8e6541406', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/475b64bf-faea-557f-b48f-c0f8e6541406'}, {'abstract': 'Five presidential candidates are participating in the debate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/republicans-debate-in-south-carolina/', 'snippet': 'Five presidential candidates are participating in the debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, S.C. — Five candidates are taking part Thursday night in the first debate of the Republican presidential nominating contest. They are Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota; Rick Santorum, a former senator from Pennsylvania; Representative Ron Paul of Texas; Herman Cain, the former chief executive of Godfather’s Pizza; and Gary Johnson, the former governor of New Mexico. The Caucus is watching the debate and is providing updates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Debate in South Carolina', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:34:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4be39e-e149-578b-94b7-fcbd2bdafab3', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4be39e-e149-578b-94b7-fcbd2bdafab3'}, {'abstract': 'A group’s method for researching a cure for multiple sclerosis could be a model for others fighting diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/05/fostering-a-team-approach-to-drug-cures/', 'snippet': 'A group’s method for researching a cure for multiple sclerosis could be a model for others fighting diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, I reported on the Myelin Repair Foundation (M.R.F.), an organization that is working to develop a novel treatment for multiple sclerosis, a degenerative disease that currently has no cure. Over the past four decades, despite extraordinary advances in bioscience, cures for many chronic diseases have remained elusive. As Norman from New York City (17) noted, the survival rates for many cancers have not changed much since the launch of the nation’s war on cancer during the Nixon administration: “The death rate has only declined by 3.3 percent or less in colon cancer, breast cancer, prostate cancer, and leukemia.” In response, groups like the M.R.F. have begun exploring new models to accelerate research and hasten the development of new treatments for disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fostering a Team Approach to Drug Cures', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:34:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/906b2fa8-86df-5721-b241-d724c6ce519f', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/906b2fa8-86df-5721-b241-d724c6ce519f'}, {'abstract': 'For reasons not well understood, commodities have become more volatile, increasing the costs of the futures and options that protect companies against such changes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/economy/06commodities.html', 'snippet': 'For reasons not well understood, commodities have become more volatile, increasing the costs of the futures and options that protect companies against such changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The extreme volatility of commodities prices and the unpredictability that comes with it is increasing the cost of doing business for everyone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/6COMMODITIES/6COMMODITIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Companies Hedge Bets at a Cost to Consumers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Moving Target', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley and William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3891788-6b79-5f91-a463-2bb6759d9c8f', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3891788-6b79-5f91-a463-2bb6759d9c8f'}, {'abstract': 'Fear of an economic slowdown in the United States and the rest of the world pushes down prices for commodities like oil, sugar, coffee and silver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/06prices.html', 'snippet': 'Fear of an economic slowdown in the United States and the rest of the world pushes down prices for commodities like oil, sugar, coffee and silver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commodities prices fell sharply on Thursday, led by the steepest drop in oil prices since the fall of 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Prices/Prices-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ending Run, Investors Abandon Commodities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ending Run, Investors Abandon Commodities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Silver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T01:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley and Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'ny