publicans are backing away from their plan to privatize Medicare after it proved to be wildly unpopular among core groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All but seven House Republicans voted for a budget plan last month that would eliminate Medicare’s guarantee to the elderly. It was always bad policy. But now that the vote has proved to be wildly unpopular, the party is suddenly running in the opposite direction. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Could It Have Been the Polls?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Could It Have Been the Polls?: Republicans are backing away from their plan to privatize Medicare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Ways and Means', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camp, David L', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T02:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b874da2-0ad0-5e10-8477-5cef05adf81d', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b874da2-0ad0-5e10-8477-5cef05adf81d'}, {'abstract': 'CVS Caremark is a $50 billion company that could be worth $13 billion more it if were split in two.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/business/06views.html', 'snippet': 'CVS Caremark is a $50 billion company that could be worth $13 billion more it if were split in two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The merger that created CVS Caremark never made much sense. Combining the drugstore chain and pharmacy benefit manager resulted in lost contracts and Federal Trade Commission scrutiny. It has hurt investors, too. The fall in first-quarter profit reported on Thursday emphasizes the point. The $50 billion company could be worth $13 billion more carved up.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pharmacy Tie-Up Without Benefits', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pharmacy Tie-Up Without Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CVS Caremark Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T02:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran and Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of