f_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3e6e7d9-e902-51d6-8dbe-5f2bbad0d628', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3e6e7d9-e902-51d6-8dbe-5f2bbad0d628'}, {'abstract': 'Many energy experts and economists say that oil prices are bound to rebound again because the fundamentals of the global market have not changed very much.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/skidding-oil-prices-a-blip-or-a-trend/', 'snippet': 'Many energy experts and economists say that oil prices are bound to rebound again because the fundamentals of the global market have not changed very much.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Oil prices have plunged this week like they haven’t since the fall of 2008, when Lehman Brothers failed and a hurricane closed so many refineries that demand for crude dried up for more than a week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Skidding Oil Prices: A Blip or a Trend?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T12:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c03f42b4-ee96-5075-bf42-71a1628337bf', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c03f42b4-ee96-5075-bf42-71a1628337bf'}, {'abstract': 'Also in the news: a campaign to block same-sex marriage, opposition to a wheelchair lift for a child with cerebral palsy, a buyer for the Metropolitan Life clock tower, and other regional developments.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/morning-buzz-obama-at-ground-zero/', 'snippet': 'Also in the news: a campaign to block same-sex marriage, opposition to a wheelchair lift for a child with cerebral palsy, a buyer for the Metropolitan Life clock tower, and other regional developments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This lovely weather will last through the day, with a high near 70, but showers will return tonight and tomorrow before things straighten out for Mother’s Day, which should be kind of like today, except with more people calling their mothers. Your seasonal allergies are brought to you this weekend by the mulberry tree. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Buzz | Obama at Ground Zero', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T12:24:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb96d25e-3944-547d-a66e-14f4769633fc', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb96d25e-3944-547d-a66e-14f4769633fc'}, {'abstract': 'Heaven Hill distillers comes out with five different versions of unaged whiskeys.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/the-palette-of-moonshines-expands/', 'snippet': 'Heaven Hill distillers comes out with five different versions of unaged whiskeys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the past two years, many an American distillery has hopped on the moonshine bandwagon, releasing its own unaged, just-off-the-still “white dogs.” But few are taking it as far as Heaven Hill, the large, family-owned, Kentucky outfit that produces a wide line of whiskeys. They are going to have five different versions of white lighting. Why? Because they can.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Palette of Moonshines Expands', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T12:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c079d58-28e2-5fed-b49b-16fd68aa8da1', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c079d58-28e2-5fed-b49b-16fd68aa8da1'}, {'abstract': 'The private sector powered a gain in jobs but the unemployment rate actually nudged up to 9 percent, from 8.8 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/business/economy/07jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The private sector powered a gain in jobs but the unemployment rate actually nudged up to 9 percent, from 8.8 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For three straight months, the nation’s employers have delivered solid job growth, easing some concerns that the economy could be stalling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': '