64460d-76c0-5b61-abc7-638f1202a85d', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e64460d-76c0-5b61-abc7-638f1202a85d'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of protesters gathered in dozens of cities and towns as the government deployed security forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/world/middleeast/07syria.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of protesters gathered in dozens of cities and towns as the government deployed security forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Security forces fired on demonstrators in six Syrian towns and cities in a day of protests that activists declared a “Friday of Defiance.” Twenty-six people died, but a withering crackdown subdued the most restive town and prevented many protesters from gathering in larger demonstrations, activists and human rights groups said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07syria/07syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07syria/07syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07syria/07syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07syria/07syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07syria/07syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Across Syria Despite Military Presence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On ‘Friday of Defiance,’ Syrian Forces Fire on Demonstrators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T12:50:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7f3d28-90c3-5194-b692-2bce4a50a78d', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7f3d28-90c3-5194-b692-2bce4a50a78d'}, {'abstract': 'The latest disclosure may raise additional questions about the culture and practices at SAC Capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/prosecutors-looking-at-steven-cohens-account/', 'snippet': 'The latest disclosure may raise additional questions about the culture and practices at SAC Capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trades made for an account of Steven A. Cohen, the founder of the hedge fund giant SAC Capital, have come under scrutiny as part of the government’s sweeping investigation into insider trading on Wall Street. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutors Looking at Steven Cohen’s Account', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Steven A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SAC Capital Advisors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T12:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Cane and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f4ea35e-6ea0-5476-a5e4-cf7b54c1dfe3', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f4ea35e-6ea0-5476-a5e4-cf7b54c1dfe3'}, {'abstract': 'Gully Wells, the jet-setting features director of Condé Nast Traveler, on fashionable lessons learned from her mother, Dee.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/gullys-travels/', 'snippet': 'Gully Wells, the jet-setting features director of Condé Nast Traveler, on fashionable lessons learned from her mother, Dee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Gully Wells left London for New York City in the mid-’80s, she was shocked to discover that New York women were uniformly dressed in short skirts and Manolo Blahniks. Wells, who is now the jet-setting features director of Condé Nast Traveler, is no stranger to the vagaries of style — her mother was Dee Wells, the author and columnist whose home, located between Toulon and Marseille, France, was the scene of many salacious exploits (summer affairs, teeny bikini contests) often involving her fabulous friends (Christopher Hitchens and Antonia Fraser). Wells recounts these tales and fashionable lessons her mother taught her in her coming memoir, “The House in France,” to be published in June by Knopf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gully’s Travels', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c95092d1-6fdd-5bf2-8162-7bc5abc85e35', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c95092d1-6fdd-5bf2-8162-7bc5abc85e35'}, {'abstract': 'Job growth is up. So is the jobless rate. Which should you believe?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/correcting-the-picture-on-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Job growth is up. So is the jobless rate. Which should you believe?', 'lead_paragraph': '11:29 a.m. | Updated This is one of those months when it’s impossible to tell a consistent story about the jobs report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Correcting the Picture on Jobs', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5dbc98e-4359-5578-a6dd-841aefb78564', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5dbc98e-4359-5578-a6dd-841aefb78564'}, {'abstract': 'The investment bank’s chief executive, Lloyd C. Blankfein, faced questions on executive compensation and business practices during the shareholder meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/live-blogging-goldmans-annual-meeting/', 'snippet': 'The investment bank’s chief executive, Lloyd C. Blankfein, faced questions on executive compensation and business practices during the shareholder meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Goldman Sachs’s annual meetings are usually eventful, this one will make history. For the first time, shareholders are trekking to Jersey City for the gathering. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blogging Goldman’s Annual Meeting', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:02:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/55a5ff0b-f19e-55ee-81bb-502a6e5ceb6e', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55a5ff0b-f19e-55ee-81bb-502a6e5ceb6e'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Samberg, Jorma Taccone and Akiva Schaffer talk about their new album, their “Saturday Night Live” skits and working with collaborators like Nicki Minaj and Michael Bolton.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/real-beats-fake-m-c-s-a-conversation-with-the-guys-of-the-lonely-island/', 'snippet': 'Andy Samberg, Jorma Taccone and Akiva Schaffer talk about their new album, their “Saturday Night Live” skits and working with collaborators like Nicki Minaj and Michael Bolton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They’re the hilarious trio of rap-rock-R&B innovators who are back on the scene with a new album after an all-too-long hiatus – but hey, enough about the Beastie Boys. The Lonely Island, the comedy team of Andy Samberg, Jorma Taccone and Akiva Schaffer, whose Internet skits and parodies got them gigs on “Saturday Night Live” and the status that comes from the authorship of enduring digital shorts like “Lazy Sunday” and “Two Worlds Collide ft. Reba McEntire”, have a new record of their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Beats, Fake M.C.’s: A Conversation With the Guys of The Lonely Island', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samberg, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lonely Island', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:05:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41511656-cb7c-555c-acd3-5302af4763ff', 'word_count': 1659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41511656-cb7c-555c-acd3-5302af4763ff'}, {'abstract': 'The Churchill Downs oddsmaker Mike Battaglia set the morning line for Saturday’s race, and Joe Drape has listed the horses in order of preference.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/joe-drapes-kentucky-derby-picks-2/', 'snippet': 'The Churchill Downs oddsmaker Mike Battaglia set the morning line for Saturday’s race, and Joe Drape has listed the horses in order of preference.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:37 p.m. | Update Uncle Mo has been scratched.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe Drape’s Kentucky Derby Picks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffd43e3-b316-563c-acac-d673c2fb6994', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffd43e3-b316-563c-acac-d673c2fb6994'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Capa’s famous advice to younger photographers — “Get closer” — translates in combat to “get more vulnerable,” both literally and emotionally.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/the-inner-lives-of-wartime-photographers/', 'snippet': 'Robert Capa’s famous advice to younger photographers — “Get closer” — translates in combat to “get more vulnerable,” both literally and emotionally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Keller, the executive editor of The New York Times, has interviewed Times war photographer Joao Silva, who lost both his legs to a land mine while he was photographing an American patrol near Kandahar, Afghanistan last October.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Inner Lives of Wartime Photographers', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:24:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c76c3b9a-5ec0-5a6f-820f-40dbd0905f9e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c76c3b9a-5ec0-5a6f-820f-40dbd0905f9e'}, {'abstract': 'Uncle Mo could not shake a gastrointestinal infection fast enough to be ready for the biggest race of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/07racing.html', 'snippet': 'Uncle Mo could not shake a gastrointestinal infection fast enough to be ready for the biggest race of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — Once the Kentucky Derby favorite, Uncle Mo was scratched from the race Friday after his owner and trainer decided the colt had not recovered sufficiently from a gastrointestinal infection that was diagnosed in the days after his first defeat, in the Wood Memorial last month.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/jp-racing/jp-racing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 630, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/jp-racing/jp-racing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/jp-racing/jp-racing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncle Mo, Once the Favorite, Is Scratched From the Derby', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uncle Mo, Once the Favorite, Is Scratched From the Derby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pletcher, Todd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Repole, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:32:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c8a3bde-3cff-5c32-ba88-b2683980c0bd', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c8a3bde-3cff-5c32-ba88-b2683980c0bd'}, {'abstract': 'Luxury Caribbean hotels offer great summer deals, taking children to pricey Broadway shows, Al Gore invents a cool e-book and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/friday-reading-caribbean-hotels-offer-summer-deals/', 'snippet': 'Luxury Caribbean hotels offer great summer deals, taking children to pricey Broadway shows, Al Gore invents a cool e-book and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Caribbean Hotels Offer Summer Deals', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5816959d-f654-5328-a110-c58beedf8b5a', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5816959d-f654-5328-a110-c58beedf8b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Al Qaeda released a statement on militant Web sites Friday confirming the death of Osama bin Laden, news agencies reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/world/asia/07qaeda.html', 'snippet': 'Al Qaeda released a statement on militant Web sites Friday confirming the death of Osama bin Laden, news agencies reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Qaeda released a statement on militant Web sites Friday confirming the death of Osama bin Laden, according to the SITE Intelligence Group, which monitors jihadi Web sites. The lengthy statement, dated May 3 and signed by Al Qaeda’s General Command, warned of new attacks and called on the Pakistani people to rebel against their government to protest its relations with the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Qaeda Confirms Bin Laden’s Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Al Qaeda Confirms Bin Laden’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8c02c3f-eada-5a42-9cb3-22b5a650afc0', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8c02c3f-eada-5a42-9cb3-22b5a650afc0'}, {'abstract': 'Nature doesn’t always listen to the experts. A red-tailed hawk baby emerged Friday morning from the severely overdue eggs on a nest high above Washington Square Park.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/hawk-cam-miracles-do-happen/', 'snippet': 'Nature doesn’t always listen to the experts. A red-tailed hawk baby emerged Friday morning from the severely overdue eggs on a nest high above Washington Square Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never have we been so ecstatic to be wrong. Days after we wrote that the hatch-by date had expired on Violet the red-tailed hawk’s eggs, an eyas (that’s what baby hawks are called) emerged on Friday morning. Go to Updates from the Nest for live Hawk Cam video, a Q-and-A on what to expect in the days to come, and the latest developments, or to post a comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Miracles Do Happen', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:55:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6af178-de97-5900-9aeb-eed9daedb16c', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6af178-de97-5900-9aeb-eed9daedb16c'}, {'abstract': 'Videos – often elaborate and usually shot in one take – of people lip-synching to a song.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/lip-dub/', 'snippet': 'Videos – often elaborate and usually shot in one take – of people lip-synching to a song.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Videos – often elaborate and usually shot in one take – of people lip-synching to a song.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lip Dub', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T13:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'repo