system to match students and high schools, and 10 percent of eighth graders recently learned the hard way how dizzying and disappointing the process can be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/nyregion/in-applying-for-high-school-some-8th-graders-find-a-maze.html', 'snippet': 'New York City uses a complex system to match students and high schools, and 10 percent of eighth graders recently learned the hard way how dizzying and disappointing the process can be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON the last day in March, when most eighth graders in New York City learned where they would be going to high school in the fall, Radcliffe Saddler watched the majority of his classmates rip open thin envelopes and celebrate. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBUNMATCHED1/08SUBUNMATCHED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBUNMATCHED1/08SUBUNMATCHED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBUNMATCHED1/08SUBUNMATCHED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBUNMATCHED1/08SUBUNMATCHED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBUNMATCHED1/08SUBUNMATCHED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in the School Choice Maze', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost in the School Choice Maze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aead3d04-ccd4-5f5d-a46b-126e9df31b1a', 'word_count': 2597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aead3d04-ccd4-5f5d-a46b-126e9df31b1a'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/morning-take-out-238/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fervor Roils Markets as Companies Beat a Path to Go Public \xa0|\xa0 Companies are lining up to go public. Market conditions are favorable. Investor appetite is strong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:06:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb7294ba-e39d-509a-8884-29b3dc156dcf', 'word_count': 2325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb7294ba-e39d-509a-8884-29b3dc156dcf'}, {'abstract': 'The number of long-term unemployed workers is coming down, at long last.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/a-more-normal-job-market/', 'snippet': 'The number of long-term unemployed workers is coming down, at long last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the surface, the jobs report today was as confused as ever. The household survey looked bad (the unemployment rate went up) and the employer survey looked good (the economy added 268,000 private sector jobs in April). More private-sector jobs — 760,000 — have been gained over the last three months than over any comparable period in five years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A More Normal Job Market?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a116f749-7af6-5c84-b914-a3bce7366287', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a116f749-7af6-5c84-b914-a3bce7366287'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott on the new wave of Romanian cinema.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2008/01/18/magazine/20080120_ROMANIAN_FEATURE.html', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott on the new wave of Romanian cinema.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. O. Scott on the new wave of Romanian cinema.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romanian Cinema Rising', 'kicker': 'Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MOTION PICTURES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/5806f6e1-c5c9-59c4-adcd-70d29872dcf7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/5806f6e1-c5c9-59c4-adcd-70d29872dcf7'}, {'abstract': 'In this sympathetically witty novel, which spans 30 years, a Midwestern family struggles for economic and emotional stability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/books/review/book-review-the-year-we-left-home-by-jean-thompson.html', 'snippet': 'In this sympathetically witty novel, which spans 30 years, a Midwestern family struggles for economic and emotional stability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a third of the way into “The Year We Left Home,” Jean Thompson’s 10th book of fiction, the \xadErickson family of Grenada, Iowa, attends — along with much of the town — the funeral of a beloved great aunt. Torrie, the Erickson’s 17-year-old daughter, arrives late to the church, an offense she knows will strain her already volatile relations with her mother; by the time she gets there, the only empty seats are up in the choir loft. From that height, as the pastor delivers the eulogy, she can see her family in the pews below, angry and worried over her seeming absence, but they cannot see her:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/bkr-Dee-t_CA0/bkr-Dee-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, '