definitive edition of Friedrich A. Hayek’s “Constitution of Liberty” coincides with the unexpected best-seller status of his earlier book “The Road to Serfdom” as a result of its promotion by the conservative talk-show host Glenn Beck. In an age when many on the right are worried that the Obama administration’s reform of health care is leading us toward socialism, Hayek’s warnings from the mid-20th century about society’s slide toward despotism, and his principled defense of a minimal state, have found strong political resonance. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/FUKUYAMA/FUKUYAMA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/FUKUYAMA/FUKUYAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/FUKUYAMA/FUKUYAMA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Friedrich A. Hayek, Big-Government Skeptic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big-Government Skeptic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis Fukuyama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fukuyama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/62e85bc0-2fde-5a42-8cb6-c95e354d8418', 'word_count': 1143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62e85bc0-2fde-5a42-8cb6-c95e354d8418'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/what-were-reading-177/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b804ca43-f751-5766-942b-058047e23a57', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b804ca43-f751-5766-942b-058047e23a57'}, {'abstract': 'After an avalanche, a couple on a skiing holiday notice changes to their existence, in this eerie fantasy of isolation, marital love and the afterworld.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/books/review/book-review-the-silent-land-by-graham-joyce.html', 'snippet': 'After an avalanche, a couple on a skiing holiday notice changes to their existence, in this eerie fantasy of isolation, marital love and the afterworld.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a first and last paragrapher. I never read a book until I’ve taken some time to examine the beginning and the end. Allowing the frame to orient my gaze to the painting — that’s how I think of it. Granted, the technique has its disadvantages: now and then I have bought books that decorated their borders with more artistry than their interiors, and occasionally the final lines of a story will contain some ruinous premature revelation. But knowing how a book arranges itself answers a few essential questions: What are its rhythms? What is its emotional tenor? Can I feel comfortable relinquishing myself to its authority? How will it go about removing me from and then reintroducing me to the trajectory of my life?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/Brockmeier/Brockmeier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/Brockmeier/Brockmeier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/Brockmeier/Brockmeier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Death and Afterlife on the Slopes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twilight on the Slopes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, Graham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:46:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Brockmeier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brockmeier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1acad71a-df89-5529-8037-faa2dd2ff81e', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1acad71a-df89-5529-8037-faa2dd2ff81e'}, {'abstract': 'A home buyer with a down payment of less than 20 percent may face higher mortgage fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/realestate/08mort.html', 'snippet': 'A home buyer with a down payment of less than 20 percent may face higher mortgage fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE increased cost of F.H.A. mortgages has shifted the math a bit for would-be borrowers.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/08mortgages-graphic/08mortgages-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/08mortgages-graphic/08mortgages-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/08mortgages-graphic/08mortgages-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/08mortgages-graphic/08mortgages-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/08mortgages-graphic/08mortgages-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With Higher Costs of F.H.A. Loans', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dealing With Higher Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T14:54:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maryann Haggerty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maryann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haggerty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2a5d5e-d448-5bee-830e-53ee4d919846', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2a5d5e-d448-5bee-830e-53ee4d919846'}, {'abstract': 'A history of the founding fathers’ passion for agriculture and botany, and how those pursuits reflected their political ideas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/books/review/book-review-founding-gardeners-by-andrea-wulf.html', 'snippet': 'A history of the founding fathers’ passion for agriculture and botany, and how those pursuits reflected their political ideas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1961, when John F. Kennedy asked Rachel Lambert Mellon to design the Rose Garden at the White House, the commission established a strong link with America’s botanical past. And so, much more recently, has Michelle Obama’s organic vegetable garden, elsewhere on the grounds. As Andrea Wulf reminds us in her illuminating and engrossing new book, “Founding Gardeners,” the first four presidents were passionate botanists whose country seats became laboratories for their grander vision of an independent agrarian republic in the New World.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/Dietz/Dietz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/books/review/Dietz/Dietz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheigh