gic National Arts Alumni Project based at Indiana University, which tracks the lives and careers of arts graduates, has recently released one. The results of the 2010 online survey include responses from more than 13,500 students who were in fine arts, theater, dance, music, creative writing, media arts, film, design and architecture programs and graduated in the past 15 or so years from 154 arts high schools, undergraduate and graduate institutions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Survey Suggests Employment Prospects for Arts Graduates Are About the Same as for Others', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T17:25:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb07873-580e-5b25-9ba2-61b29e6a1eb1', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb07873-580e-5b25-9ba2-61b29e6a1eb1'}, {'abstract': 'The luxury swimwear house is  setting up shop in America’s playground of the rich and fabulous, the Hamptons.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/eres-in-the-swim-of-things/', 'snippet': 'The luxury swimwear house is  setting up shop in America’s playground of the rich and fabulous, the Hamptons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From St. Tropez to Porto Cervo, Capri to Cannes, few brands are as at home in the world’s most glamorous settings as Eres — and come this weekend, the luxury swimwear house is setting up shop in America’s playground of the rich and fabulous, the Hamptons. “In America, having stores in resort locations is a must,” explains Eres’s swim and lingerie designer, Valerie Delafoss. But unlike the Eres boutiques in Palm Beach and Los Angeles, this latest venture, at 55 Main Street in East Hampton, will feature more beachy attire — ocean-blue maillots with a flirty tassel belts, color-blocked boy-short bikinis and cotton jersey wide-leg cover-up pants — than delicate lingerie. Our opinion? Either way, it’s a good excuse to go to the Hamptons!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eres, in the Swim of Things', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T17:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec24a46-4be1-5537-863c-ccf01d1c8ae7', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec24a46-4be1-5537-863c-ccf01d1c8ae7'}, {'abstract': 'After the squall about Princess Beatrice’s royal wedding hat, could the hype spawn a trend stateside?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/fashion/08noticed.html', 'snippet': 'After the squall about Princess Beatrice’s royal wedding hat, could the hype spawn a trend stateside?', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEVER has a hat stirred such a squall. Moments after the royal wedding, images of Princess Beatrice’s spiraling Band-Aid-hued headpiece had gone viral. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '5', 's