 the first labor union to formally endorse President Obama’s re-election bid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Education Association took a major step on Friday toward becoming the first labor union to formally endorse President Obama‘s re-election bid, announcing that its political action committee approved a recommendation for the union to back Mr. Obama and for its 3.2 million members to vote for him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.E.A. Advances Endorsement for Obama in 2012', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Education Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T17:37:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dbc1b91-0672-58e0-93fb-2b5601d9534f', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dbc1b91-0672-58e0-93fb-2b5601d9534f'}, {'abstract': 'A new report faults the Bay Delta Conservation Plan as little more than a list of tactics with no overall strategic purpose.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/can-a-water-plan-work-without-an-environmental-goal/', 'snippet': 'A new report faults the Bay Delta Conservation Plan as little more than a list of tactics with no overall strategic purpose.', '