: 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7ec16be0-724c-5f7a-a0e6-3f1f1d3ce227', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7ec16be0-724c-5f7a-a0e6-3f1f1d3ce227'}, {'abstract': 'The center, in midtown Manhattan, is looking downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/international-center-of-photography-seeking-a-new-bigger-home/', 'snippet': 'The center, in midtown Manhattan, is looking downtown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The International Center of Photography in Manhattan is looking for a new home that can accommodate both its museum and its school, its director, Willis E. Hartshorn, said on Friday. The school and museum are across the street from each other on the Avenue of the Americas near 43rd Street. Mr. Hartshorn said the center was in the “early phases” of evaluating various sites below 26th Street, including buildings in Lower Manhattan and Chelsea. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'International Center of Photography Seeking a New, Bigger Home', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Center of Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:42:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b710e412-1b9f-5593-9e8b-09e7db31e9c8', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b710e412-1b9f-5593-9e8b-09e7db31e9c8'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers with security freezes report their own experiences thawing and refreezing their credit reports.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/security-freezes-how-theyve-worked-out-for-you/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers with security freezes report their own experiences thawing and refreezing their credit reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s “Your Money” column, I write about security freezes, also known as credit freezes, in the wake of the big customer data breach at Sony.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Freezes: How They’ve Worked Out for You', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Fraud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:47:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b189b86-b448-566a-80e4-817cb5d8da11', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b189b86-b448-566a-80e4-817cb5d8da11'}, {'abstract': 'As the endgame begins, both bidders — Deutsche Börse, and Nasdaq and its partner, the IntercontinentalExchange — are preparing for the NYSE Euronext shareholders meeting in July.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/handicapping-the-battle-over-nyse-euronext/', 'snippet': 'As the endgame begins, both bidders — Deutsche Börse, and Nasdaq and its partner, the IntercontinentalExchange — are preparing for the NYSE Euronext shareholders meeting in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The endgame in the Nasdaq’s bid for NYSE Euronext has begun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Handicapping the Battle Over NYSE Euronext', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Borse AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IntercontinentalExchange Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYSE Euronext', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/35574130-ee4c-5658-a3d6-721391ec8d0d', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35574130-ee4c-5658-a3d6-721391ec8d0d'}, {'abstract': 'A credit report monitoring service will alert you only after the damage is done. Instituting a credit freeze will prevent anyone from opening an account in your name.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/your-money/identity-theft/07money.html', 'snippet': 'A credit report monitoring service will alert you only after the damage is done. Instituting a credit freeze will prevent anyone from opening an account in your name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, Sony’s chairman and chief executive, Howard Stringer, finally got around to apologizing for the security breach that left the personal data of 77 million customers vulnerable to hackers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/lieber-75/lieber-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/lieber-75/lieber-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'ID Theft Tool That Sony Isn’t Using', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ID Theft Tool That Sony Isn’t Using', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Fraud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:48:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Identify Theft', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ee601a-5cb6-53b0-94b8-781b865be1ba', 'word_count': 1301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ee601a-5cb6-53b0-94b8-781b865be1ba'}, {'abstract': 'A place to get quirky, responsibly sourced Chinese food, on Mission Street in San Francisco.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/the-selby-danny-bowien-of-mission-chinese/', 'snippet': 'A place to get quirky, responsibly sourced Chinese food, on Mission Street in San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hole-in-the-wall at 2234 Mission Street in San Francisco looks more like a greasy spoon where General Tso’s chicken is ordered by number than a cult outpost offering quirky, responsibly sourced Chinese food. Inside, it’s both. Danny Bowien and Anthony Myint, who ran the pop-up Mission Street Food out of Lung Shan restaurant, are now cooking here permanently with Mission Chinese Food. Alongside Lung Shan’s menu, you can now indulge in what Mr. Bowien calls “whimsical Chinese” — sizzling cumin lamb, ma po tofu, barbecued brisket braised with a Mexican/Coca-Cola gastrique. “It’s not fusion,” he said. “It’s not fine dining. It’s not authentic. It’s not from one region. We’re just trying to do everything backwards.” Go to interactive feature >> ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Danny Bowien of Mission Chinese', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c776495-f6e2-5dda-b17f-c1468338c738', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c776495-f6e2-5dda-b17f-c1468338c738'}, {'abstract': 'Producing a sequel to a star car, like the Mercedes-Benz CLS, is a formidable task for a designer, but updating already updated cars may be the hardest task of all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/automobiles/08SEQUEL.html', 'snippet': 'Producing a sequel to a star car, like the Mercedes-Benz CLS, is a formidable task for a designer, but updating already updated cars may be the hardest task of all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN clandestine photos of the redesigned 2012 Volkswagen Beetle turned up on the Internet last fall, two words appeared repeatedly in online critiques: squashed and squished. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/automobiles/SEQU-4/SEQU-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/automobiles/SEQU-4/SEQU-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/automobiles/SEQU-4/SEQU-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Designing Successful Sequel Is Exercise in Restraint', 'kicker': 'Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Designing the Successful Sequel Is an Exercise in Restraint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T19:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f6e2efe-7f89-5073-bb75-e55bd67810ec', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f6e2efe-7f89-5073-bb75-e55