ation by RR Donnelly in Lancaster, Pennsylvania.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times daily newspaper is printed at multiple locations across the globe to ensure timely delivery. The entire run of The New York Times Magazine, however, is printed every week at RR Donnelly, a press in Lancaster, Pa. They have been printing our magazine for almost 30 years. We here in New York deliver the last of the files every Friday to them, and they print over 1.5 million copies of the publication for delivery nine days later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Makes Our Magazine?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By HILARY GREENBAUM', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GREENBAUM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b42a26-4d2f-5979-adb4-8c8d761094d0', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b42a26-4d2f-5979-adb4-8c8d761094d0'}, {'abstract': 'Developers of the video game “L.A. Noire” bet on an audience for sniffing out suspects in 1940s Hollywood, with actors along for the ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/arts/video-games/la-noire-from-rock-star-games.html', 'snippet': 'Developers of the video game “L.A. Noire” bet on an audience for sniffing out suspects in 1940s Hollywood, with actors along for the ride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/NOIRE-Jp-1/NOIRE-Jp-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/NOIRE-Jp-1/NOIRE-Jp-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/NOIRE-Jp-1/NOIRE-Jp-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/NOIRE-Jp-1/NOIRE-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/arts/NOIRE-Jp-1/NOIRE-Jp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Game to Play in Vintage Gumshoes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Video Game to Play In Vintage Gumshoes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d623fc9-9da2-51f0-ad43-1f096c0b09d0', 'word_count': 1876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d623fc9-9da2-51f0-ad43-1f096c0b09d0'}, {'abstract': 'We wanted to photograph where Air France Flight 447 went down. But on the chosen day, a combination of vague coordinates — French authorities refused to provide the precise location of the ship — and cloud cover prevented us from getting any usable image.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/how-to-photograph-the-cover/', 'snippet': 'We wanted to photograph where Air France Flight 447 went down. But on the chosen day, a combination of vague coordinates — French authorities refused to provide the precise location of the ship — and cloud cover prevented us from getting any usabl...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this week’s article on the crash of Air France Flight 447, we considered several photographic treatments for the cover. First we considered having a photographer charter a plane and fly over the recovery ship, the Alucia, while it was still near the spot where its crew located the plane in early April. \xa0We decided that option was too costly, so next we tried to take a satellite picture of the Alucia. \xa0But on the chosen day, a combination of vague coordinates — French authorities refused to provide the precise location of the ship — and cloud cover prevented us from getting any usable image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Photograph the Cover', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacey Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ced5ede-c813-5e76-bd73-7de17c420dc2', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ced5ede-c813-5e76-bd73-7de17c420dc2'}, {'abstract': 'Within the last couple of years a new batch of neighborhood bakeries has risen in Minneapolis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-minneapolis-bakeries.html', 'snippet': 'Within the last couple of years a new batch of neighborhood bakeries has risen in Minneapolis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a recent Saturday morning there was a line out the door at Patisserie 46 in Minneapolis’s emerging Kingfield neighborhood, as folks waited to get their daily baked goods. The bakery (4552 Grand Avenue South; 612-354-3257; patisserie46.com) hasn’t yet been open a year and already has achieved cultlike status for its French-style offerings: the croissants are crisp and light as air, the macarons evaporate in the mouth.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-span/08headsup-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-span/08headsup-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-span/08-HEADS-UP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-span/08headsup-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08headsup-span/08headsup-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bakeries Spring Up in the Twin Cities', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bakeries Spring Up in the Twin Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Paul (Minn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Davila', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davila', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be735a33-0a71-5663-9036-745cf8e054d3', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be735a33-0a71-5663-9036-745cf8e054d3'}, {'abstract': 'A Sicilian social movement is organizing trips that patronize only businesses that do not pay protection money to the Mafia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08sicily.html', 'snippet': 'A Sicilian social movement is organizing trips that patronize only businesses that do not pay protection money to the Mafia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a thick summer afternoon in the Sicilian town of Corleone, beneath palm trees in the small central piazza, the old men in their rimmed caps watched us. They rolled their eyes over our touristy selves (cameras and sunhats), and my husband and I scarfed our gelato a little faster.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08sicily-span/08sicily-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08sicily-span/08sicily-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 326}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08sicily-span/Sicily-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':