idth': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08choice-span/08choice-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08choice-span/08choice-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlanta Serves Sophisticated Southern', 'kicker': 'Choice Tables', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Atlanta Serves Sophisticated Southern', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbb2e09d-aab7-5fff-9ab3-bf48f44fd1d3', 'word_count': 1689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbb2e09d-aab7-5fff-9ab3-bf48f44fd1d3'}, {'abstract': 'Finding spice, color and moments of unexpected silence in the pulsating center of Indonesia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08cover-lost-in-java.html', 'snippet': 'Finding spice, color and moments of unexpected silence in the pulsating center of Indonesia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 15 years of traveling to Asia, I have seen and done a number of strange things. I have eaten writhing octopus tentacles in Seoul, and I’ve been shepherded into a Phnom Penh nightclub by a Cambodian dwarf in a tuxedo. At this point, little surprises me. But when I arrived in the city of Malang, in the cool hills of inland East Java, I discovered something I never imagined existed.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08java-span/Java-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08java-span/Java-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08java-span/Java-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08java-span/08java-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08java-span/08java-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in Java', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost in Java', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79258ce6-d799-575b-8953-f439b6ee030b', 'word_count': 3358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79258ce6-d799-575b-8953-f439b6ee030b'}, {'abstract': 'The magnetic strip on charge cards can pose problems in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08letters-CHARGEITPLEA_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': 'The magnetic strip on charge cards can pose problems in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: The article “Picking the Best Credit Card” (April 24) was helpful but did not address the common problem that credit cards issued in the United States have a magnetic strip, not the chip found in European cards. This is an inconvenience, as United States cards are rejected at some kiosks all over Europe, and even for some counter purchases.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Charge It, Please?', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charge It, Please?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a82b193a-783f-56ec-bb7a-a7d2b79d1e4e', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a82b193a-783f-56ec-bb7a-a7d2b79d1e4e'}, {'abstract': 'The Jacksonville area has much to offer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08letters-FLORIDAHEREW_LETTERS.html', 'snippet': 'The Jacksonville area has much to offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Re “A Post-Spring Break Jaunt to Florida’s Beaches” (April 19): The area around Jacksonville is great. You can camp at Kathryn Abbey Hanna Park. Jax Beach, Neptune Beach and Atlantic Beach are great to visit. Just south of town, on your way to St. Augustine on Route A1A, is Mickler’s Landing and Beach. It’s a great beach, with lots of friendly locals, surfers and families, plus lots of free parking. My favorite place is Cocoa Beach. It’s a relatively small town, with small-town prices. The beach is great, and there’s an even better one south of town at Patrick Air Force Base (lots of free parking). The stretch from Jacksonville to Cocoa Beach is a great part of Florida. You’re guaranteed to enjoy your time there. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Florida, Here We Come', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida, Here We Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5536db3-0201-5547-ad15-40009e1109b8', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5536db3-0201-5547-ad15-40009e1109b8'}, {'abstract': 'Shepherd’s huts, old circus wagons, converted wool mills and train cars are a few of the choices you’ll have while traveling here.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/travel/08pers-wales.html', 'snippet': 'Shepherd’s huts, old circus wagons, converted wool mills and train cars are a few of the choices you’ll have while traveling here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are a few constants on the Pen-y-Wyrlod farm in southeast Wales: the sheep, the rain, the mud, the Black Mountains. And at the top of a small hill, beyond an unmarked gate, across from a medieval church, a Gypsy caravan barely large enough to hold a bed, a wood-burning stove and a paying guest — me. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08journeys-span/08journeys-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/travel/08journeys-span/08jou