119cc63e3bf'}, {'abstract': 'Correcting for an aging population doesn’t help.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/demography-and-jobs-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Correcting for an aging population doesn’t help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Catherine Rampell raises the question of how many jobs we need to keep up with population growth, given the aging of the population. I’d been thinking about it a different way. We know that the employment-population ratio has been flat since late 2009; would things look better if we looked at the employment ratio for prime-age workers?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demography and Jobs (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdb232f8-7e86-5332-8e61-270ecf1eb5f0', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb232f8-7e86-5332-8e61-270ecf1eb5f0'}, {'abstract': '“The Ernie Kovacs Collection,” new on DVD, gives the contemporary viewer an opportunity to admire Kovacs, a seminal television comedian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/arts/television/the-ernie-kovacs-collection-new-on-dvd.html', 'snippet': '“The Ernie Kovacs Collection,” new on DVD, gives the contemporary viewer an opportunity to admire Kovacs, a seminal television comedian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELEVISION in the 1950s was still something relatively new and strange. But nowhere was it stranger — or funnier — than in the shows of Ernie Kovacs. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia'