sponse to Garry Wills’s review of “A Thousand Times More Fair: What Shakespeare’s Plays Teach Us About Justice,” by Kenji Yoshino.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/books/review/shakespeare-in-context.html', 'snippet': 'Letter in response to Garry Wills’s review of “A Thousand Times More Fair: What Shakespeare’s Plays Teach Us About Justice,” by Kenji Yoshino.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shakespeare in Context', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shakespeare In Context', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d48f4e-dadb-5a5b-beff-f2081ccde7f7', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d48f4e-dadb-5a5b-beff-f2081ccde7f7'}, {'abstract': 'The wedding of Sir Paul and Nancy Shevell was first reported in People magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/in-agency-news-m-t-a-board-member-to-wed-paul-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'The wedding of Sir Paul and Nancy Shevell was first reported in People magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the annals of Metropolitan Transportation Authority history, it has not been customary for transit officials to be caught up in a celebrity wedding. Their work has focused more on the construction of the No. 7 line extension, say, than on bridal gown designers, floral arrangement preferences or what the bridesmaids will wear. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Agency News, M.T.A. Board Member to Wed (Paul McCartney)', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shevell, Nancy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:43:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/98dede4d-8fee-5927-b4a0-7bffec16adcf', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98dede4d-8fee-5927-b4a0-7bffec16adcf'}, {'abstract': 'NBC’s coverage of President Obama’s speech last Sunday attracted the most viewers overall of any of the broadcast or cable channels that carried the event.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/most-tuned-to-nbc-for-address-on-bin-laden/', 'snippet': 'NBC’s coverage of President Obama’s speech last Sunday attracted the most viewers overall of any of the broadcast or cable channels that carried the event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ratings arrived Friday for President Obama’s address to the nation last Sunday, and NBC affirmed its status as the biggest draw for news viewers – though Donald Trump might have been a significant reason on that night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Most Tuned to NBC for Address on Bin Laden', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/08549eac-e198-5749-8648-9926fc1bf470', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08549eac-e198-5749-8648-9926fc1bf470'}, {'abstract': 'A Times reporter observed firsthand how E.V.’s are proving their worth, and their mettle, on the quake-damaged streets of northeastern Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/electric-vehicles-aid-relief-efforts-in-japan/', 'snippet': 'A Times reporter observed firsthand how E.V.’s are proving their worth, and their mettle, on the quake-damaged streets of northeastern Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tragedy unfolding in Japan since March 11 has been stunning, compelling and sad. But recovery efforts, which receive far less publicity, have been no less interesting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electric Vehicles Aid Relief Efforts in Japan', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Bel