20:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d27c2cb-dc83-5e29-a932-84a4ec33bfca', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d27c2cb-dc83-5e29-a932-84a4ec33bfca'}, {'abstract': 'Sonny and Cher’s daughter, now a man, is the subject of a documentary of his transition from female to male.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/fashion/08CHAZ.html', 'snippet': 'Sonny and Cher’s daughter, now a man, is the subject of a documentary of his transition from female to male.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the Sundance Film Festival earlier this year, I wheedled a ticket to “Becoming Chaz,” a documentary about the sex change of Chastity Bono. Having long admired the Fenton Bailey and Randy Barbato World of Wonder productions — slyly edu-taining films like “The Eyes of Tammy Faye” and oodles of just-louche-enough-for-reality-TV shows like “RuPaul’s Drag Race” — I anticipated their usual mix of human interest, alternative lifestyle and salacious tabloid.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/fashion/CHAZ/CHAZ-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reluctant Transgender Role Model', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Reluctant Transgender Role Model', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bono, Chastity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cintra Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cintra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b72923a-98a9-5be6-a471-5a662effd558', 'word_count': 1688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b72923a-98a9-5be6-a471-5a662effd558'}, {'abstract': 'Avon Products could easily spend $250 million on legal costs for an internal investigation of whether its employees violated the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/the-high-price-of-internal-investigations/', 'snippet': 'Avon Products could easily spend $250 million on legal costs for an internal investigation of whether its employees violated the Foreign Corrupt Practices Act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The old saying that crime doesn’t pay applies especially to corporations caught up in investigations by the Justice Department and Securities and Exchange Commission for possible violations of federal law. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The High Price of Internal Inquiries', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (1977)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avon Products Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/db3b692c-48e4-510a-9c31-dc5318aabb44', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db3b692c-48e4-510a-9c31-dc5318aabb44'}, {'abstract': 'Eight months of images from the fighting between rebels and forces loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi in Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/world/africa/2011-libya-index.html', 'snippet': 'Eight months of images from the fighting between rebels and forces loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi in Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eight months of images from the fighting between rebels and forces loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi in Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle for Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/31236ba4-6baf-583c-9b6a-deafa9aa54c6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/31236ba4-6baf-583c-9b6a-deafa9aa54c6'}, {'abstract': 'The mom-daughter team of the blog Stylelikeu have released a book of the same name just in time for Mother’s Day.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/stylelikeu-mother-and-daughter-sartorialists/', 'snippet': 'The mom-daughter team of the blog Stylelikeu have released a book of the same name just in time for Mother’s Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Target is offering matching dresses for moms and babies from its new Calypso collaboration. Lucky magazine recently introduced a back-page feature called “My Mom, the Style Icon.” But for most of us, there was a period, in between teetering in Mom’s high heels and aching to steal her vintage blouses, during which we’d balk at anything —\xa0anything — she liked. Not so for Lily Mandelbaum, a student at N.Y.U. who has collaborated with her mother, the fashion editor and stylist Elisa Goodkind, on the style blog Stylelikeu since 2008. The popular site features closet tours, style mantras and video interviews with their fashion muses, both known (the fashion designer LaQuan Smith) and unknown (Virginie Sommet, who makes art out of Indian candy and fennel). Now, just in time for Mother’s Day, they’ve released a book of the same name, full of beautiful images of sartorial inspiration, including collages of hands garnished with jaw-dropping gems, club kids posing in their bedrooms and little old ladies who refuse to hang up the toreador pants. As Tziporah Salamon,\xa0one such senior, happily explained: “Every single day you get a chance to invent yourself. How fun is that?” Happy Mother’s Day!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Stylelikeu’ | Mother and Daughter Sartorialists', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T20:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce494842-3381-5a4f-a980-cd75c95a6011', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce494842-3381-5a4f-a980-cd75c95a6011'}, {'abstract': 'A design project descends on Levittown.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/suburbia-what-a-concept/', 'snippet': 'A design project descends on Levittown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no more iconic suburb than Levittown, the postwar planned community built by the developer William Levitt in the late 1940s, so it is understandable that in launching Open House, a collaborative project to imagine a “future suburbia,” the Dutch design collective Droog in collaboration with Diller Scofidio + Renfro architects would make it the focus of their inquiry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suburbia: What a Concept', 'kicker': 'Allison Arieff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T21:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Arieff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arieff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a37e0c88-4afa-5c2c-a56c-4b8b1c32063d', 'word_count': 2321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a37e0c88-4afa-5c2c-a56c-4b8b1c32063d'}, {'abstract': 'Both efforts address the collection of online data by marketers without people’s knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/do-not-track-privacy-bill-appears-in-congress/', 'snippet': 'Both efforts address the collection of online data by marketers without people’s knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And the privacy legislation just keeps on coming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Do Not Track’ Privacy Bill Appears in Congress', 'k