sicians for two evenings at Weill Recital Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brilliant German violinist Christian Tetzlaff has demonstrated his versatility and imagination in a wide range of repertory during his Perspectives series at Carnegie Hall this season. In recent programs he has focused on chamber music, performing a concert with the Tetzlaff Quartet (of which he is first violinist) and a duo recital with the violinist Antje Weithaas. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/sub-christian/sub-christian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Violin and Piano, in an Evening’s Conversation', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violin and Piano, in an Evening’s Conversation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tetzlaff, Christian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T21:49:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2afe76c-b93e-55d2-8151-4ac2305f0b41', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2afe76c-b93e-55d2-8151-4ac2305f0b41'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Oscar Larson, an auditor and family man during the week, chronicled life in New York City through the lens of his Rolleiflex camera on the weekends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/08/nyregion/20110508VISUALss.html', 'snippet': 'Frank Oscar 