2'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from the past week in New York City and the region, including a Sikh Day festival, a stable in Central Park and President Obama’s visit to ground zero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/06/nyregion/20110506WIP.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from the past week in New York City and the region, including a Sikh Day festival, a stable in Central Park and President Obama’s visit to ground zero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from the past week in New York City and the region, including a Sikh Day festival, a stable in Central Park and President Obama’s visit to ground zero.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/nyregion/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX/20110506WIP-slide-KVNX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for May 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T23:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/81af47d5-2908-5957-8ea5-47e96d6ce8c5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/81af47d5-2908-5957-8ea5-47e96d6ce8c5'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Muna Tseng pays homage to her mother in “Stella.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/arts/dance/muna-tseng-presents-stella-at-danspace.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Muna Tseng pays homage to her mother in “Stella.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1999 the choreographer Muna Tseng paid homage to her brother, the photographer Tseng Kwong Chi, who had died of AIDS. That work, “SlutForArt,” was created in collaboration with the theater artist Ping Chong. Now, in “Stella,” Ms. Tseng tries to get under the skin of her mother, a stylish woman who had a sharp tongue. Stella cared about clothes — included in the show is an exhibition of her luxurious couture dresses — and said memorable things like, “The biggest waste in life is time.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/stella/stella-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/stella/stella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/stella/stella-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling and Quoting Her Mother', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recalling And Quoting Her Mother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tseng, Muna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T23:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1be96c-edf5-5c33-b0e3-fbf4605aceb3', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1be96c-edf5-5c33-b0e3-fbf4605aceb3'}, {'abstract': 'Endangered Blood and Starlicker, musicians of new jazz, reach back to the roots of their sound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/arts/music/endangered-blood-and-starlicker-review.html', 'snippet': 'Endangered Blood and Starlicker, musicians of new jazz, reach back to the roots of their sound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the late 1990s, jazz outside the straight-ahead mainstream was looking around itself and worrying. Outlasting a flicker of interest from major-record labels, anticipating audience decline as the “downtown jazz” scene grew diffuse and undefinable, it went in search of its parents and looked backward and Eastward: to Ornette Coleman, Lennie Tristano, Jimmy Giuffre, early fusion and progressive rock, the Art Ensemble of Chicago and Balkan and cantorial music. A whole field of bands gravitated toward intense polyphony, liturgical melodies and the clank: drummers playing roughed-up rhythm, rushing time and forestalling your pleasure, vexing you on purpose. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/star/star-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/star/star-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/star/star-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/star/star-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/star/star-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jazz That Keeps an Ear Trained on the Past', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Jazz That Keeps an Ear Trained on the Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T23:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b7d39b-6cbf-5bee-b43e-6680ca127695', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b7d39b-6cbf-5bee-b43e-6680ca127695'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet had a fresh opening to its spring season with its Balanchine Black and White Week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/arts/dance/chase-finlay-in-city-ballets-apollo-review.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet had a fresh opening to its spring season with its Balanchine Black and White Week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Stravinsky-Balanchine “Apollo,” the world itself is young. The boy god Apollo, the first musician, discovers art by creating it in the open air. On Thursday night at New York City Ballet, the title role was danced by Chase Finlay, who had not even graduated from the School of American Ballet when this piece was last performed, in 2008. Afterward the audience would not release the performers until Mr. Finlay had taken a solo bow in front of the curtain. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/movement-1/movement-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/movement-1/movement-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/movement-1/movement-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Youth, Balanchine and Fans Are Served', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Youth, Balanchine And Fans Are Served', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-06T23:29:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bfd85b9-099d-57ff-9229-faad67d888e3', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bfd85b9-099d-57ff-9229-faad67d888e3'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/the-week-in-culture-pictures-may-7-2/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'le