7a7-9bb3-53b4-84ef-c721af6a5034', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6ee347a7-9bb3-53b4-84ef-c721af6a5034'}, {'abstract': 'For Mother’s Day, Nahid Sabet, an Iranian living in Texas, told her 13-year-old daughter about being persecuted in her homeland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/us/07religion.html', 'snippet': 'For Mother’s Day, Nahid Sabet, an Iranian living in Texas, told her 13-year-old daughter about being persecuted in her homeland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — On a blustery night the week before Mother’s Day, a woman and her daughter sat together on the sofa at a hair salon here. Nica Sabet had come to the beauty parlor after school, because it was where her mother, Nahid Sabet, worked. By this time, past 8 o’clock, the doors were locked and the customers gone, and Mrs. Sabet could tell the story that Nica had never heard in its entirety.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/SUB-RELIGION/SUB-RELIGION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/SUB-RELIGION/SUB-RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/SUB-RELIGION/SUB-RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman’s Persecution, and a Daughter’s Deliverance', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hardship of an Iranian Bahai and Her Daughter’s Deliverance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of