000808664/block-by-block.html', 'snippet': 'Sights and sounds from West 14th to West 23rd Street including the Buddakan nightclub, the grounds of the General Theological Seminary, Le Grainne Cafe and Moonstruck diner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sights and sounds from West 14th to West 23rd Street including the Buddakan nightclub, the grounds of the General Theological Seminary, Le Grainne Cafe and Moonstruck diner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/06/realestate/video-block-chelsea/video-block-chelsea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/06/realestate/video-block-chelsea/video-block-chelsea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Block by Block', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T00:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'Judy Tong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2521b190-9765-5669-b827-eecc56e6658b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2521b190-9765-5669-b827-eecc56e6658b'}, {'abstract': 'The emotional Mark Cuban is doing his part to stay noncontroversial as the Mavericks continue their march against the Lakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/basketball/07mavericks.html', 'snippet': 'The emotional Mark Cuban is doing his part to stay noncontroversial as the Mavericks continue their march against the Lakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — Mark Cuban is not an owner who merely watches his Dallas Mavericks. He seems to internalize the action while outwardly cheering and complaining. When his emotions are released — and they frequently are — the result is often a fine leveled at Cuban by the N.B.A. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/y-mavericks/y-mavericks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/y-mavericks/y-mavericks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/y-mavericks/y-mavericks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/y-mavericks/y-mavericks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/y-mavericks/y-mavericks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Dallas Leading, Outspoken Owner Lowers the Volume', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Dallas Leading, Outspoken Owner Lowers the Volume', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T00:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34945f47-9487-5a7d-aa78-72b00cd03912', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34945f47-9487-5a7d-aa78-72b00cd03912'}, {'abstract': 'Nikita Tikhonov was sentenced to life in prison, Russia’s most stringent punishment, on Friday for fatally shooting a human rights lawyer and a young journalist two years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/world/europe/07briefs-Russia.html', 'snippet': 'Nikita Tikhonov was sentenced to life in prison, Russia’s most stringent punishment, on Friday for fatally shooting a human rights lawyer and a young journalist two years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A young nationalist was sentenced to life in prison, Russia’s most stringent punishment, on Friday for fatally shooting a human rights lawyer and a young journalist two years ago on a busy street near the Kremlin. His common-law wife, who prosecutors said acted as a lookout, was sentenced to 18 years as an accomplice. The sentence brings to a close a case that deeply shook Russian human rights circles, which have been dogged by a series of high-profile killings. Last week, the couple, Nikita Tikhonov, 30, and Yevgenia Khasis, 26, were found guilty. Defense lawyers appealed the sentence on Friday, saying the judge had sided with prosecutors. “This can be qualified in whatever way you like, a costume ball, a farce, a reprisal, but not a trial,” Aleksandr Vasilyev, Mr. Tikhonov’s lawyer, told the Interfax news service. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Lawyer’s Killer Gets Life Term', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Lawyer’s Killer Gets Life Term', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tikhonov, Nikita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khasis, Yevgenia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T00:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9228d953-968c-530f-88f7-8d1b1fd2b6e4', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9228d953-968c-530f-88f7-8d1b1fd2b6e4'}, {'abstract': 'Just beyond the reach of the meatpacking district, Ninth Avenue from West 14th to West 23rd Street, has its own vibe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/realestate/08block.html', 'snippet': 'Just beyond the reach of the meatpacking district, Ninth Avenue from West 14th to West 23rd Street, has its own vibe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POOR Ninth Avenue. You could dismiss the stretch from West 14th to West 23rd Street as the northern hinterlands of the greater meatpacking district. Or you could pity it, there in the shadow of 10th, the glamorous sister avenue whose profile has been transformed by famous art galleries, starred restaurants and the coursing aorta that is the High Line. But no need to disparage in any way: These blocks in West Chelsea form a self-contained little quarter, with a thriving life all their own. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/SUB-block-3/SUB-block-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/SUB-block-3/SUB-block-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/SUB-block-3/SUB-block-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/SUB-block-3/SUB-block-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/realestate/SUB-block-3/SUB-block-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sort of Cool, Not Yet Hot', 'kicker': 'Block by Block', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sort of Cool, Not Yet Hot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T00:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian L. Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/773b37b3-5a04-5a09-9859-e6dfe76b8046', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/773b37b3-5a04-5a09-9859-e6df