in the Garden State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN “Jersey Rocks: A History of Rock & Roll in the Garden State,” a new exhibition at the Morris Museum in Morristown that will run through Sept. 5, the background music may be as interesting for some visitors as the 400 or so objects on display. “Stacy’s Mom,” the 2003 hit by the pop band Fountains of Wayne, whose front man, Adam Schlesinger, grew up in Montclair, was followed recently by “Walk on By,” the 1960s classic made famous by Dionne Warwick, who was raised in Newark and now lives in South Orange. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBSPOTNJ/08SUBSPOTNJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBSPOTNJ/08SUBSPOTNJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBSPOTNJ/08SUBSPOTNJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBSPOTNJ/08SUBSPOTNJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08SUBSPOTNJ/08SUBSPOTNJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey Rock History: More Than Big Hair and the Boss', 'kicker': 'Spotlight | Morris Township', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Jersey Rock History: More Than Big Hair and the Boss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morris Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major':