bType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/opinion/07oped-art/07oped-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Philosopher in Love', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Philosopher in Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hume, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T01:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Zaretsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaretsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/32acb9ad-a8f0-592f-8b1e-1e7ce3536ccb', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32acb9ad-a8f0-592f-8b1e-1e7ce3536ccb'}, {'abstract': 'The country needs a serious energy policy, not more pandering to the oil industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/opinion/07sat1.html', 'snippet': 'The country needs a serious energy policy, not more pandering to the oil industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the country again facing $4-a-gallon gasoline, the time would seem ripe for a grown-up conversation on energy. What we are getting instead is a mindless rerun of the drill-baby-drill operatics of the 2008 campaign, when gas was also at $4 a gallon. Then, as now, opportunistic politicians insisted that vastly expanded oil drilling would bring relief at the pump and reduced dependence on foreign oil. Then, as now, these arguments were bogus. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Return of ‘Drill, Baby, Drill’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Return of ‘Drill, Baby, Drill’: The country needs a serious energy policy, not more pandering to the oil industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T01:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef8e5a1-05de-522e-8f7f-20beb33a5106', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ef8e5a1-05de-522e-8f7f-20beb33a5106'}, {'abstract': 'Contradictory employment data raise questions about the economy’s momentum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/opinion/07sat2.html', 'snippet': 'Contradictory employment data raise questions about the economy’s momentum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jobs data can be hard to read. When an economy is emerging from recession, a rising jobless rate can be a good sign if it reflects an increase in the people actively looking for work. Sadly, that was not the case with the April employment numbers reported on Friday. The jobless rate rose because the people who lost or left their jobs outnumbered those who found new work. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Hand Clapping', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Hand Clapping: Contradictory employment data raise questions about the economy’s momentum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T01:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/123a5b7c-4f15-5aa8-83d2-710912fe1c78', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/123a5b7c-4f15-5aa8-83d2-710912fe1c78'}, {'abstract': 'Analysts on both sides have anticipated that the league would get the full stay of the injunction, but the lengthy delay has some scratching their heads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/football/07nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Analysts on both sides have anticipated that the league would get the full stay of the injunction, but the lengthy delay has some scratching their heads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With silence from a federal appeals court, the N.F.L. headed into another weekend in limbo, with business shut down and players wondering when — or if — they will go back to work. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Legal Fight Continues for N.F.L.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Legal Fight Continues For N.F.L.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doty, David S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'},