d and participate in counseling to deter cyberbullying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW BRUNSWICK, N.J. — One of two former Rutgers University students accused of spying on another student with a webcam just days before he committed suicide will be allowed to avoid a conviction if she continues to provide information about her co-defendant, prosecutors said Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/nyregion/RUTGERS/RUTGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Fallout of Suicide by Student, a Plea Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Fallout Of Suicide By Student, A Plea Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravi, Dharun', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clementi, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wei, Molly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T01:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aec7dfb4-c22b-54bf-bf56-63fcb100193a', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aec7dfb4-c22b-54bf-bf56-63fcb100193a'}, {'abstract': 'The power struggle between Iranian President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad and the supreme leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei is continuing to escalate, even interrupting Friday Prayer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/world/middleeast/07iran.html', 'snippet': 'The power struggle between Iranian President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad and the supreme leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei is continuing to escalate, even interrupting Friday Prayer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unprecedented power struggle between the two most powerful leaders in Iran deepened Friday, spilling out into Tehran’s public prayers where the mullah leading the service indirectly criticized President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad while the crowd chanted “Death to opponents of the supreme leader!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/world/07iran/07iran-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 857, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power Struggle in Iran Enters the Mosque', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power Struggle In Iran Enters The Mosque', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mottaki, Manouchehr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2