f trading Thursday that its sales rose to $356.4 million, and profit rose to 59 cents a share, topping the 49 cents analysts had expected. Stock in Hansen, which is based in Corona, Calif., rose $2.80, to $64.74 a share. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales Surge 50% for Maker of Monster Energy Drinks', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Beverages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sales Surge 50% for Maker of Monster Energy Drinks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hansen Natural Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T02:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/67345cff-f4c8-5c7e-aea7-42a7c7118c97', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67345cff-f4c8-5c7e-aea7-42a7c7118c97'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation into mortgage-linked securities gained momentum after Goldman Sachs admitted a “mistake” and paid $550 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/business/07bank.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation into mortgage-linked securities gained momentum after Goldman Sachs admitted a “mistake” and paid $550 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company is in negotiations to resolve its role in a Securities and Exchange Commission investigation into how mortgage-linked securities were packaged and sold as the housing market came apart. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan in Talks to Settle