. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Adjust to Loss of the Versatile Chavez', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Adjust to Loss of the Versatile Chavez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T02:29:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffa0f5ef-7386-5c99-ae7a-99019402c71c', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffa0f5ef-7386-5c99-ae7a-99019402c71c'}, {'abstract': 'Suspected militants were killed by missiles from the pilotless aircraft, a security official said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/world/asia/07drone.html', 'snippet': 'Suspected militants were killed by missiles from the pilotless aircraft, a security official said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Missiles believed to have been fired by an American drone killed at least eight suspected militants and wounded four in Pakistan’s tribal regions on Friday, according to a Pakistani security official and a resident in the area of the strike. Later, seven more bodies were recovered, bringing the death toll to 15, the resident said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drone Strike Said to Kill at Least 8 in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drone Strike Said to Kill At Least 8 In Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T02:32:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pir Zubair Shah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pir', 'middlename': 'Zubair', 'lastname': 'Shah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a8c36a-6254-5317-9785-5e28edbf954f', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a8c36a-6254-5317-9785-5e28edbf954f'}, {'abstract': 'Andre Ethier has hit safely in 30 straight games, but Jason Pridie’s home run was decisive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/baseball/07mets.html', 'snippet': 'Andre Ethier has hit safely in 30 straight games, but Jason Pridie’s home run was decisive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just 13 pitches into Friday’s game, the big question of the day was answered virtually without suspense. Andre Ethier, the third batter of the evening, belted a 3-0 fastball into center field for a base hit, and with that his hitting streak moved up a level. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/citifield-1/citifield-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 781, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/citifield-1/citifield-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/citifield-1/citifield-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethier Extends Streak, but Mets Win the Day', 'kicker': 'Mets 6, Dodgers 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethier Extends Streak, but Mets Win the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ethier, Andre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T03:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbfe4dcb-9b41-5b3d-8726-072dcf246742', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbfe4dcb-9b41-5b3d-8726-072dcf246742'}, {'abstract': 'Misha Erwitt talks with his father, Elliott Erwitt.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/06/elliott-erwitts-best-picture-the-next-one/', 'snippet': 'Misha Erwitt talks with his father, Elliott Erwitt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, the Magnum photographer and filmmaker Elliott Erwitt, 82, will receive the Infinity Award for Lifetime Achievement from the International Center of Photography, which will exhibit his favorite pictures as “Personal Best,” beginning May 20. For the occasion, he agreed to let his son Misha Erwitt, a photographer himself, present him with a list of questions that family members have long wanted to ask.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elliott Erwitt’s Best Picture? The Next One.', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capa, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cartier-Bresson, Henri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erwitt, Elliott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnum Photos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T03:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Misha Erwitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Misha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erwitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/763a51f3-4087-5e07-b7f4-0800399ecb9c', 'word_count': 2494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/763a51f3-4087-5e07-b7f4-0800399ecb9c'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the day in sports, from the opening ceremony of the Giro d’Italia cycling race to the morning workouts at Churchill Downs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/