collapse against the same team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/hockey/07bruins.html', 'snippet': 'With the defeat of the Flyers, the Bruins — who have not won a Stanley Cup since 1972 — nullified the bitter memory of last year’s playoff collapse against the same team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The Bruins exorcised some very persistent demons Friday night. It is too soon to tell if they have done so as thoroughly as the Red Sox did when they overcame nearly a century of futility by rallying from three games down in a playoff series against the Yankees in 2004.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/bruins/bruins-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/bruins/bruins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/bruins/bruins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruins Finish Off Flyers, Leaving Bad Taste Behind', 'kicker': 'Bruins 5, Flyers 1 ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bruins Bury the Flyers, and Some Bad Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T03:37:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c738822-3e2f-5e68-9e27-3a8ac499ef06', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c738822-3e2f-5e68-9e27-3a8ac499ef06'}, {'abstract': 'With his sinker working, Ivan Nova allowed just two hits and a run in seven and a third innings, his deepest outing in 12 career starts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sports/baseball/07yankees.html', 'snippet': 'With his sinker working, Ivan Nova allowed just two hits and a run in seven and a third innings, his deepest outing in 12 career starts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Ignore the detail that the Texas Rangers were playing without the sluggers Josh Hamilton and Nelson Cruz, and that their flight from Seattle arrived Friday morning after the newspapers had hit the driveways. Just consider the facts. On a muggy night, in a stadium where the ball travels well, and facing a lineup still loaded with power and speed, Ivan Nova dominated like no other starter for the Yankees this season.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/yankees/yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/yankees/yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/sports/yankees/yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nova Finds His Pitch, Leaving Rangers Helpless', 'kicker': 'Yankees 4, Rangers 1 ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nova Finds His Pitch, Leaving Rangers Helpless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granderson, Curtis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nova, Ivan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T03:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/415886c8-d1ba-5e76-9205-2fc1d8fa5a19', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/415886c8-d1ba-5e76-9205-2fc1d8fa5a19'}, {'abstract': 'With just 71 babies born on average for every 100 deaths, Brooke County, in West Virginia, has the largest such gap in the nation among counties in metropolitan areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/us/07aging.html', 'snippet': 'With just 71 babies born on average for every 100 deaths, Brooke County, in West Virginia, has the largest such gap in the nation among counties in metropolitan areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEIRTON, W. Va. — Life in this industrial area has slowed to a shuffle along with the steel mills that used to power it. Young people have moved away, leaving an aging population that no longer has the energy to put on street fairs or holiday parades. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/us/JP-AGING-2/JP-AGING-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/07/us/JP-AGING-2/JP-AGING-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/us/JP-AGING-2/JP-AGING-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/us/JP-AGING-2/JP-AGING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/us/JP-AGING-2/JP-AGING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Death Outpacing Birth, a County Slows to a Shuffle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Balance of Births and Deaths Upset by County&#8217;s Hard Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BIRTHS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T03:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise and Robert Gebeloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gebeloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58cfb340-987f-5dbb-9b73-cefee8bfd805', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58cfb340-987f-5dbb-9b73-cefee8bfd805'}, {'abstract': '“Friday Night Lights,” which has been so entrenched in ideas surrounding absent fathers, is spending its final season in the territory of paternal healing.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/friday-night-lights-watch-save-the-children/', 'snippet': '“Friday Night Lights,” which has been so entrenched in ideas surrounding absent fathers, is spending its final season in the territory of paternal healing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are covering the final season of “Friday Night Lights” according to the NBC schedule. We ask that readers who have already seen the season on DirecTV or on DVD to please refrain from giving away future plot points in the comments section.Can this child be saved? That was the underlying theme of the latest episode of “Friday Night Lights,” as we watched Epyck lash out, fight and get suspended and Buddy’s son roll into town with his quasi-vegan-induced anger and disillusionment. Who among us wouldn’t become cranky if subjected to a step-parent mandated diet of seitan? It seems to take Buddy Jr. about 10 seconds of being in Dillon to steal his father’s credit card and break into the booze and another 20 for everyone to figure that the cure for what ails Buddy is going to be two-a-days. I’m already feeling too optimistic about Buddy’s future, and I don’t want to feel optimistic. I hope for more screeching engines and rebellion, a challenge to Buddy’s narrowly circumscribed gridiron view of the world.', 'source': 'The N