s most memorable games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECAUCUS, N.J. — It was the most magical night a pitcher has ever had, an extra-inning shutout to win the World Series, and Jack Morris wishes he could share it with you. If every person could experience one moment like that, he says, and reach a goal in extraordinary circumstances, think of the positive energy it could bring to the world.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/series2/series2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/series2/series2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/series2/series2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strong Arms, Long Memories for Smoltz and Morris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Memories of Game That Strong Arms Ruled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Jack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smoltz, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T15:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7588113-5d40-5441-9d7b-84d401ced34c', 'word_count': 1465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7588113-5d40-5441-9d7b-84d401ced34c'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers’ Sean Avery became one of only a few active athletes in American team sports to voice support for gay rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/hockey/08avery.html', 'snippet': 'The Rangers’ Sean Avery became one of only a few active athletes in American team sports to voice support for gay rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since September, advocates for same-sex marriage in New York have released 30-second videos of celebrities endorsing their cause. More than 30 have taken part, including the actors Julianne Moore and Sam Waterston, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg and the former first daughter Barbara Bush. On Thursday, former President Bill Clinton released a written statement of support, too. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-AVERY3/Y-AVERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-AVERY3/Y-AVERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-AVERY3/Y-AVERY3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-AVERY3/Y-AVERY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-AVERY3/Y-AVERY3-t