first collective bargaining agreement with team owners. Miller’s own new deal raised the minimum salary to $10,000 from $6,000, the first increase since the 1940s. (It’s now $414,000.)', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/tellem3/tellem3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/tellem3/tellem3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/tellem3/tellem3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Players Union Doesn’t Help the Players', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Players Union Doesn’t Help the Players', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League Players Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Players Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGENTS (BUSINESS)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date':