no hit a leadoff single, and Phillies Manager Charlie Manuel called for a hit-and-run. He knew he could trust the hitter, Placido Polanco.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Phillies’ Polanco, It’s the Little Things', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polanco, Placido', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T15:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1c5332a-bc51-500d-b57c-d02317983a2c', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1c5332a-bc51-500d-b57c-d02317983a2c'}, {'abstract': 'Starting this month, commercial fishing vessels that drop long lines in the Gulf of Mexico must use lightweight, circular hooks that allow bluefin tuna to swim free.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/business/08novel.html', 'snippet': 'Starting this month, commercial fishing vessels that drop long lines in the Gulf of Mexico must use lightweight, circular hooks that allow bluefin tuna to swim free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOST angling gear is designed to hold onto fish. But some new equipment is fine-tuned to be more selective — holding tight to some fish and letting go of others, especially if they are Atlantic bluefin tuna — a fish whose numbers have fallen sharply.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'