ish golfer who won the Masters twice and the British Open three times and helped propel Europe’s rise in the Ryder Cup competition with the United States, died early Saturday at his home in northern Spain, where his struggle with brain cancer had gained wide attention in the sports world. He was 54.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Share Your Memories of Seve Ballesteros', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballesteros, Seve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T16:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9e38c36-1236-5872-90ac-d66ec0966500', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9e38c36-1236-5872-90ac-d66ec0966500'}, {'abstract': 'The Lakers and Celtics, facing likely elimination, have combined for a majority of league championships and could even need a scandal to unify them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/basketball/08araton.html', 'snippet': 'The Lakers and Celtics, facing likely elimination, have combined for a majority of league championships and could even need a scandal to unify them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boston', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-JP-ARATON/Y-JP-ARATON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-JP-ARATON/Y-JP-ARATON-thumbStanda