 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27d70b23-0d89-5683-9c3d-3d59fdc29718'}, {'abstract': 'The West and the Taliban are grappling with how the struggle over who will control Afghanistan will change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/world/asia/08taliban.html', 'snippet': 'The West and the Taliban are grappling with how the struggle over who will control Afghanistan will change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — From the Taliban’s hidden mud compounds to NATO’s headquarters in Brussels and the Pentagon, combatants in a decade-long war are asking versions of the same question: How does Osama bin Laden’s death change the struggle over who will control Afghanistan? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/world/JP-TALIBAN/JP-TALIBAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden and the New Unknown in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bin Laden’s Death and the New Unknown in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omar, Muhammad (Taliban Leader)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date'