ves, casting new uncertainty on an issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Marijuana remains illegal under federal law, but that has not stopped a fuzzy industry of marijuana farms and dispensaries from rising to serve the 15 states that allow the drug to be used for medical purposes. Under President Obama, the federal government had seemed to make a point of paying little attention — until now.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/us/MARIJUANA/MARIJUANA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Federal Crackdown Confounds States That Allow Medical Marijuana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Federal Crackdown Confounds States That Allow Medical Marijuana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregoire, Christine O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-07T22:37:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 's