humbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/Y-LAKERS/Y-LAKERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lakers Face Early Exit, and the Potential for Many Off-Season Departures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lakers Face Early Exit, and the Potential for Many Off-Season Departures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T00:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83fc08e8-473e-54e6-8921-dd8ced41b080', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83fc08e8-473e-54e6-8921-dd8ced41b080'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor complements his print column with a series of graphics showing The Times’s late-night transformation in print and digital the night of President Obama’s announcement of the killing of Osama bin Laden.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/a-visual-look-at-the-times-in-overdrive/', 'snippet': 'The public editor complements his print column with a series of graphics showing The Times’s late-night transformation in print and digital the night of President Obama’s announcement of the killing of Osama bin Laden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column this week looks at the extraordinary efforts of Times staffers as they responded to the news of Osama Bin Laden’s death in a raid by Navy Seals. Because the news broke late on print deadlines, The Times took extraordinary measures to stop the presses, remake print pages and rush to get updated copies not only to New York readers but to many readers in major cities nationwide. On top of that, the Times mounted an intense global reporting effort aimed at delivering fresh stories through the night for publication on NYTimes.com, which became the key venue for breaking developments after the print edition closed at 12:45 a.m. Monday. The result was an outpouring of fresh copy that was published online-only and then superseded eventually by new stories on Monday, some of which ultimately fed a 10-page special print section titled “The Death of Bin Laden” that was delivered Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Visual Look at The Times in Overdrive', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T00:17:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd5469e9-4f77-5371-903e-b06d7a958606', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd5469e9-4f77-5371-903e-b06d7a958606'}, {'abstract': 'For the comedian, who is finishing his ninth season on “Saturday Night Live,” Sunday is a day for video games, record-shopping and watching TV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/nyregion/for-fred-armisen-the-fish-comes-first-on-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'For the comedian, who is finishing his ninth season on “Saturday Night Live,” Sunday is a day for video games, record-shopping and watching TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man of many morphs, Fred Armisen, 44, formerly the drummer for the band Trenchmouth and the male half of the comedy duo ThunderAnt, is winding up his ninth season on “Saturday Night Live,” where his goofily earnest impression of President Obama is a staple. He was a creator, writer and star of the cult hit “Portlandia” this year on IFC, and is gearing up to write Season 2. Twice divorced, he spends much, if not all, of Sunday in the Upper West Side apartment he shares with Fischie, a red cap oranda.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE-SPAN/08ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE-SPAN/08ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE-SPAN/08ROUTINE-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE-SPAN/08ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE-SPAN/08ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Things First: Feed the Fish', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Things First: Feed the Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armisen, Fred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T00:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75247fe4-8433-5897-8f5e-2092d7436db8', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75247fe4-8433-5897-8f5e-2092d7436db8'}, {'abstract': '“Beyond Therapy,” Christopher Durang’s absurdist comedy about searching for a love connection through the personals, is the season-opener at the Westport Country Playhouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/nyregion/in-beyond-therapy-romance-via-the-personals-review.html', 'snippet': '“Beyond Therapy,” Christopher Durang’s absurdist comedy about searching for a love connection through the personals, is the season-opener at the Westport Country Playhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prudence’s first date with Bruce does not go well. “He talked about my breasts,” she tells her psychiatrist, “he has a male lover, and he wept at the table.”', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08THEATCT1/08THEATCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/nyregion/08THEATCT1/08THEATCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/