80-fbba-54de-9d91-220f10110d75', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4db9e380-fbba-54de-9d91-220f10110d75'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s national security adviser, Thomas E. Donilon, appears on four talk shows to discuss Osama bin Laden.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/07/sunday-breakfast-menu-may-8/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s national security adviser, Thomas E. Donilon, appears on four talk shows to discuss Osama bin Laden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A week after President Obama announced Osama bin Laden had been killed, the Sunday talk shows are still buzzing about what his death means for the United States. Mr. Obama’s national security adviser, Thomas E. Donilon, appears on “Fox News Sunday,” ABC’s “This Week,” NBC’s “Meet the Press” and CNN’s “State of the Union” to talk about the raid that brought down the 9/11 mastermind who has eluded capture for years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, May 8', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T02:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/800f4ef0-e4dc-50ec-b1d7-f8fc0b6ed2ce', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/800f4ef0-e4dc-50ec-b1d7-f8fc0b6ed2ce'}, {'abstract': 'There’s something fishy about the victory of Andriy Slyusarchuk over Rybka 4, the strongest commercially available chess program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/crosswords/chess/08chess.html', 'snippet': 'There’s something fishy about the victory of Andriy Slyusarchuk over Rybka 4, the strongest commercially available chess program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been commonly accepted for about a decade that computers are better than people at chess. But a couple of weeks ago, a widely circulated story out of Ukraine suggested that a man who learned to play the game less than a year ago had beaten the world’s best chess program. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s All in the Programming: Computer Falls to a Beginner', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s All in the Programming: Computer Falls to a Beginner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasparov, Garry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T02:24:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c1a2c5b-1131-58df-8766-d41f47247941', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c1a2c5b-1131-58df-8766-d41f47247941'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 7, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T02:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/b220bfd0-7803-5bcc-9410-4fa265309f1a', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b220bfd0-7803-5bcc-9410-4fa265309f1a'}, {'abstract': 'Teams in the Cosmopolitan Soccer League are getting more cosmopolitan than they ever intended, as fielding a homogenous ethnic soccer team in New York has gotten harder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/soccer/08ethnicsoccer.html', 'snippet': 'Teams in the Cosmopolitan Soccer League are getting more cosmopolitan than they ever intended, as fielding a homogenous ethnic soccer team in New York has gotten harder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, it seems to be your average barren lot next to a railroad track, a sight not uncommon in the industrial neighborhood of Maspeth, Queens. But venture past the tall iron gates, at what is, oddly enough, considered the intersection of 59th and 60th Streets, and the Metropolitan Oval plays host to a good chunk of the city’s ethnic soccer teams. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethnic Soccer Teams Drift Toward Diversity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethnic Soccer Teams Drift Toward Diversity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cosmopolitan Soccer League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T02:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Belac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50acbdee-bfa8-55ec-a981-6ac88f055412', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50acbdee-bfa8-55ec-a981-6ac88f055412'}, {'abstract': 'Dillon Gee, pitching in place of Chris Young, worked into the sixth inning as the Mets beat the Dodgers and ended Andre Ethier’s hitting streak at 30 games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/baseball/08mets.html', 'snippet': 'Dillon Gee, pitching in place of Chris Young, worked into the sixth inning as the Mets beat the Dodgers and ended Andre Ethier’s hitting streak at 30 games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The person most disappointed to learn that Chris Young would not pitch Saturday might have been on the opposing bench. At 7:05 p.m., five minutes before the scheduled start of the game, the Mets announced that Young could not get loose in the bullpen warming up and would be replaced by the rookie right-hander Dillon Gee.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/mets-2/mets-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/mets-2/mets-