 into an epic tailspin. Star point guards generally need two arms to carry a team, or at least to keep their passes and shots on target.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/celtics/celtics-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/celtics/celtics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/celtics/celtics-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rondo Plays Through Pain as Celtics Hang On', 'kicker': 'Celtics 97, Heat 81', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rondo Plays Through Pain as Celtics Hang On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rondo, Rajon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T03:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d890fd-2750-52b8-a0b1-70c53acb682a', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d890fd-2750-52b8-a0b1-70c53acb682a'}, {'abstract': 'Julio Borbon’s suicide squeeze drove in the go-ahead run after the Yankees has rallied from a 5-0 deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/baseball/08yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Julio Borbon’s suicide squeeze drove in the go-ahead run after the Yankees has rallied from a 5-0 deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Much happens, and much is forgotten over the course of 162 games. A result may linger, but not the final score. A great play can stick in the memory bank, but not its participants. And then there are moments that endure because of their audacity as much as their impact. One such moment occurred at Rangers Ballpark last Sept. 12, in the Yankees’ final regular-season meeting with Texas, and save for a few insignificant details it all but happened again Saturday night. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/yankees-2/yankees-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/yankees-2/yankees-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/yankees-2/yankees-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/yankees-2/yankees-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/08/sports/yankees-2/yankees-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Fall to the Rangers On a Play They Saw Coming', 'kicker': 'Rangers 7, Yankees 5', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Fall to the Rangers On a Play They Saw Coming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T03:27:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa9563c-7e88-52fe-a605-f94606d19123', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa9563c-7e88-52fe-a605-f94606d19123'}, {'abstract': 'An on-call veterinarian said that Archarcharch’s fractured left foreleg was not a life-threatening injury.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/sports/08rail.html', 'snippet': 'An on-call veterinarian said that Archarcharch’s fractured left foreleg was not a life-threatening injury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. — Archarcharch was pulled up past the finish line of the 137th running of the Kentucky Derby on Saturday after fracturing his left front leg. The injury was not life-threatening, according to an on-call veterinarian, Dr. Larry Bramlage.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Archarcharch Fractures a Leg', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Archarcharch Fractures a Leg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'r