 that has gone wrong in the American thoroughbred breeding industry and everything that can save it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUSIVILLE, KY — Even though the winner has a Brazilian-bred sire and a German-bred dam, the 137th Kentucky Derby made a big run toward retaining its eminence as the world’s greatest race. The reasons are legion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Derby Winner Sets Shining Example for Wayward Industry', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breeding of Animals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Motion, Graham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANIMAL KINGDOM', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T18:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Squires', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Squires', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8014bc03-4e7d-572f-b141-ca41acd9d9ce', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8014bc03-4e7d-572f-b141-ca41acd9d9ce'}, {'abstract': 'The king of Bahrain said that the state of emergency he imposed to quell antigovernment protests would be ended on June 1st.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/world/middleeast/09bahrain.html', 'snippet': 'The king of Bahrain said that the state of emergency he imposed to quell antigovernment protests would be ended on June 1st.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The king of Bahrain said Sunday that the state of emergency he imposed in mid-March to quell antigovernment protests on that stra