 made it through eight and a half minutes of his first game action in more than two months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'O’Neal, No Stranger to Change, May Soon See More', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neal, Shaquille", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T21:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1488724d-5cc9-5f2e-8afc-19bac57383cc', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1488724d-5cc9-5f2e-8afc-19bac57383cc'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Armstrong says he has not lost faith that his overhaul of the company will reverse its decline.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/technology/09aol.html', 'snippet': 'Tim Armstrong says he has not lost faith that his overhaul of the company will reverse its decline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALO ALTO, Calif. — Tim Armstrong, AOL’s chief executive, will tell just about anyone who will listen that AOL is not some washed-up tech company from another era.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/business/Armstrong/Armstrong-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/09/business/Armstrong/Armstrong-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xla