e by a team from the Netherlands took some of the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The final 28-board session of the Cavendish Invitational Pairs was played on Sunday in Henderson, Nev., ending late in the day. (Results are at cavendish.bridgewinners.com.) Leading going into Sunday were Bobby Levin and Steve Weinstein, who were trying for a threepeat.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cavendish Craftiness', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cavendish Craftiness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T22:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/813262e7-a733-585a-9477-f51e785a0325', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/813262e7-a733-585a-9477-f51e785a0325'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s speech at the White House Correspondents’ Association dinner was watched more times last week than his announcement that Osama bin Laden had been killed.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/08/obamas-youtube-star-turn/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s speech at the White House Correspondents’ Association dinner was watched more times last week than his announcement that Osama bin Laden had been killed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama was a YouTube star twice over the last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s YouTube Star Turn', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T22:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/365f2bf0-515d-501e-8ebc-e21fbd0c2767', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/365f2bf0-515d-501e-8ebc-e21fbd0c2767'}, {'abstract': 'The Taiwan Stories series at the Film Society of Lincoln Center is an attempt to shine some light on this national cinema.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/movies/taiwan-stories-film-series-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Taiwan Stories series at the Film Society of Lincoln Center is an attempt to shine some light on this national cinema.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the turn of the century Taiwanese cinema had a moment, albeit a quiet one that the average American filmgoer probably missed. Edward Yang’s magnificent family drama “Yi Yi” was named the best film of 2000, in any language, by the National Society of Film Critics. Hou Hsiao-Hsien and Tsai Ming-Liang, Mr. Yang’s compatriots in the movement known as the Taiwanese New Wave or the New Taiwan Cinema, were at or near the peaks of their renown; Mr. Hou’s “Millennium Mambo” and Mr. Tsai’s “What Time Is It Over There?” were both released in 2001.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/arts/STORIES1/STORIES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/arts/STORIES1/STORIES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/arts/STORIES1/STORIES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting Light on Taiwanese Cinema', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Light on Taiwanese Cinema', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T22:14:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ec97e2b-626c-5c7a-8877-e6fe04797d92', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ec97e2b-626c-5c7a-8877-e6fe04797d92'}, {'abstract': 'Civilians led a march calling for an end to the bloodshed that has plagued the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/world/americas/09mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Civilians led a march calling for an end to the bloodshed that has plagued the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — Javier Sicilia, the poet who has become an unlikely hero in a movement calling for an end to Mexico’s drug war, asked for five minutes of silence at the end of a Sunday rally in this city’s giant central plaza.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/world/09mexico-inline1/09mexico-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/world/09mexico-inline1/09mexico-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/world/09mexico-inline1/09mexico-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tens of Thousands March in Mexico City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thousands in Mexico City March Against Drug War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T22:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0394b7b1-8b24-53a8-9a97-a8badcc4cfe3', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0394b7b1-8b24-53a8-9a97-a8badcc4cfe3'}, {'abstract': 'After going 259 at-bats without a home run, Derek Jeter hit two in three innings as the Yankees won at Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/sports/baseball/09yankees.html', 'snippet': 'After going 259 at-bats without a home run, Derek Jeter hit two in three innings as the Yankees won at Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — Divining the key to Derek Jeter’s success over 17 seasons is not difficult. He abides by a simple credo, believing that keeping things uncomplicated is the only way to live. As his Yankees teammates and coaches hailed his revival after Sunday’s 12-5 victory against the Rangers, Jeter offered a verbal shrug. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/08yankees-1/08yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/08yankees-1/08yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/08yankees-1/08yankees-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/08yankees-1/08yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/08yankees-1/08yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Finds Power Stroke, and Texas Pays', 'kicker': 'Yankees 12, Rangers 5', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeter Finds Power Stroke, And Texas Pays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank':