': 'Human Growth Hormone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-08T23:22:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d53083-5364-51bd-882f-15f1c4637588', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d53083-5364-51bd-882f-15f1c4637588'}, {'abstract': 'The joy in watching Seve Ballesteros was watching him escape from tangled rough or clumps of bushes or towering tree limbs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/sports/golf/09anderson.html', 'snippet': 'The joy in watching Seve Ballesteros was watching him escape from tangled rough or clumps of bushes or towering tree limbs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The joy of watching the world’s best golfers, especially Jack Nicklaus and Tiger Woods, involved their accuracy and precision. In the fairway off the tee, on the green in regulation, often with a makeable birdie putt. But with Seve Ballesteros, the dashing matador from Spain who died over the weekend with complications from a brain tumor, the joy was watching him escape from tangled rough or clumps of bushes or towering tree limbs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/anderson/anderson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im