 to find compelling matchups with fighters not named Floyd Mayweather Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Late Saturday, at his postfight news conference, Manny Pacquiao looked less like a combatant in a welterweight prize fight and more like a congressman emerging from a bargaining session. He appeared tired, but wore neither bandages nor bruises; his face was unmarked, his body unharmed, except, perhaps, for a touch of wounded pride.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/Y-BOXING1/Y-BOXING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/Y-BOXING1/Y-BOXING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/Y-BOXING1/Y-BOXING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/Y-BOXING1/Y-BOXING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/sports/Y-BOXING1/Y-BOXING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Ho-Hum Victory, Pacquiao Is Running Out of Challengers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After a Ho-Hum Victory, Pacquiao Is Running Out of Challengers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayweather, Floyd Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacquiao, Manny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosley, Shane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T00:24:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b7c002b-8e1b-5acc-9494-bfdacb5095c2', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b7c002b-8e1b-5acc-9494-bfdacb5095c2'}, {'abstract': 'Foreign groups in China are being subjected to scrutiny, reflecting growing fears of a Western-inspired revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/world/asia/09china.html', 'snippet': 'Foreign groups in China are being subjected to scrutiny, reflecting growing fears of a Western-inspired revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Chinese and American officials are polishing off scripts for a ritual that is set to unfold in Washington on Monday and Tuesday. During a meeting known as the Strategic and Economic Dialogue, they will smile across conference tables and talk about cooperating on a range of issues: trade, currency, North Korea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/world/CHINA/CHINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beijing Blames Foreigners for Its Fears of Unrest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beijing Blames Foreigners for Its Fears of Unrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T00:29:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong and Jonathan Ansfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ansfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ea7127-9b9e-51d8-9643-77344b8da910', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ea7127-9b9e-51d8-9643-77344b8da910'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Leet and her husband, Glen, started Trickle Up, one of the first nonprofits to provide microgrants to help poor people start their own businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/nyregion/mildred-robbins-leet-philanthropist-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Leet and her husband, Glen, started Trickle Up, one of the first nonprofits to provide microgrants to help poor people start their own businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mildred Robbins Leet, a philanthropist who was a co-founder of Trickle Up, one of the first nonprofits to provide microgrants, typically of $100, to help poor people start their own businesses, died on Tuesday in Manhattan. \xa0She was 88.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/nyregion/leet-obit/leet-obit-jumbo.jp