rter reported in The Times in late April, the writers have been given less than three weeks to come up with a newish version of their hit comedy. They are no doubt under just a teensy bit of pressure to produce something with the same award-winning, ratings-generating, money-raking-in qualities as the original, while also having to abruptly write out a major character, Charlie Harper, the jingle-writing cad brother played by Charlie Sheen until he was fired by Warner Brothers in March.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ten Ideas for ‘Two and a Half Men’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T10:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lia Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c806fcda-59af-53a4-b1c4-5499c8d9bc82', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c806fcda-59af-53a4-b1c4-5499c8d9bc82'}, {'abstract': 'Ayesha Khanna, director of the Hybrid Reality Institute, talks about the increasing intelligence of machines, and the importance of seeing technological development with a global perspective.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/one-on-one-ayesha-khanna-futurist/', 'snippet': 'Ayesha Khanna, director of the Hybrid Reality Institute, talks about the increasing intelligence of machines, and the importance of seeing technological development with a global perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ayesha Khanna is the director of the Hybrid Reality Institute, a think tank that explores the practical implications of what she refers to as “human-technology co-evolution in the Hybrid Age.” The following is an edited transcript of an interview with Ms. Khanna. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One on One: Ayesha Khanna, Futurist', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T10:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b0c5e4d-3cb1-5fad-bb4e-b91453234b49', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0c5e4d-3cb1-5fad-bb4e-b91453234b49'}, {'abstract': 'If this year’s Manchester United isn’t one of Alex Ferguson’s strongest title teams, then must this season be one of his best coaching jobs?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/could-this-be-alex-fergusons-finest-hour/', 'snippet': 'If this year’s Manchester United isn’t one of Alex Ferguson’s strongest title teams, then must this season be one of his best coaching jobs?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The only downside to coaching 12 league-title-winning teams, as Alex Ferguson is poised to do with Manchester United, is that there are people who sit back and compare them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Could This Be Alex Ferguson’s Finest Hour?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or