day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The big question in food-media circles last week was: Will he or she, or won’t he or she?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruth Bourdain Wins Humor Award, Invisibly', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beard, James, Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b84e331d-9360-5efd-b76f-4b51dbc45a56', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b84e331d-9360-5efd-b76f-4b51dbc45a56'}, {'abstract': 'Donna Douglas, who played Elly May Clampett on “The Beverly Hillbillies,” has sued Mattel over a Barbie doll she said uses her name and likeness without permission.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/feudin-and-fussin-over-a-beverly-hillbillies-barbie-doll/', 'snippet': 'Donna Douglas, who played Elly May Clampett on “The Beverly Hillbillies,” has sued Mattel over a Barbie doll she said uses her name and likeness without permission.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Y’all get a good intellectual property lawyer now, you hear? Come and listen to our story about a woman named Donna Douglas, an actress who for nine seasons kept herself fed by playing Elly May Clampett, the comely daughter of mountaineer Jed Clampett on “The Beverly Hillbillies.” But then one day, some 40 years after that hit comedy series went off the air, Ms. Douglas took notice of a Barbie doll designed to look like the Elly May character and filed suit against Barbie manufacturer Mattel, saying the toy uses her likeness without her permission, Reuters reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feudin’ and Fussin’ Over a ‘Beverly Hillbillies’ Barbie Doll', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbie (Doll)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mattel Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ca6b7d-b0de-52cd-9a22-961469d396f8', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ca6b7d-b0de-52cd-9a22-961469d396f8'}, {'abstract': 'According to a spokesman, Newt Gingrich will announce his candidacy on Wednesday with postings on Facebook and Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/gingrich-to-announce-candidacy-online-on-wednesday/', 'snippet': 'According to a spokesman, Newt Gingrich will announce his candidacy on Wednesday with postings on Facebook and Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trying to tap into the spontaneity of Twitter and Facebook, Newt Gingrich, the former speaker of the House, will announce his campaign for the Republican nomination for president on Wednesday by way of the two popular social networking sites, his spokesman, Rick Tyler, said in a Twitter post on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich to Announce Candidacy Online on Wednesday', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pr