aph': 'Representative Aaron Schock of Illinois, who already had the distinction of being the youngest member of the House, has a new feather in his cap (or maybe, his gym bag): he is the first member of Congress to appear shirtless on the cover of Men’s Health magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shirtless Schock on Cover of Men’s Health', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b52490-c43d-5c1a-9aa6-27f066c78b22', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b52490-c43d-5c1a-9aa6-27f066c78b22'}, {'abstract': 'Still images show six individual tigers and a mother with a cub; a video shows footage of another mother and three young cubs playfully chasing a leaf.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/on-our-radar-tigers-found-in-indonesian-logging-concession/', 'snippet': 'Still images show six individual tigers and a mother with a cub; a video shows footage of another mother and three young cubs playfully chasing a leaf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A video and photographs captured by the World Wide Fund for Nature show a dozen highly endangered tigers living within an Indonesian logging concession that could be cleared if a forest protection deal is not finalized, the group said in a statement. The Indonesian government has tentatively agreed to a two-year moratorium on new logging permits under a $1 billion deal with Norway to reduce the carbon emissions associated with deforestation, but the plan has yet to be signed into law. [Reuters]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Tigers Found in Indonesian Logging Concession', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/822f9bcd-5f0e-5c68-872b-360c69a4c492', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/822f9bcd-5f0e-5c68-872b-360c69a4c492'}, {'abstract': 'The Southern Baptist Convention volunteers are playing a central role in relief efforts for victims of tornadoes that struck Alabama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/09/us/20110509Baptist2.html', 'snippet': 'The Southern Baptist Convention volunteers are playing a central role in relief efforts for victims of tornadoes that struck Alabama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Southern Baptist Convention volunteers are playing a central role in relief efforts for victims of tornadoes that struck Alabama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/us/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/09/us/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/09/us/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223/20110509Baptist2-slide-K223-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Baptist Relief Effort', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:54:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/64647ee8-ca35-517c-8780-d3788d56923b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/64647ee8-ca35-517c-8780-d3788d56923b'}, {'abstract': 'Though Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo plans to embark on a statewide tour to promote the rights of gays to marry, he chose not to attend a rally on the issue in Albany.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/lieutenant-governor-not-cuomo-attends-gay-rights-rally/', 'snippet': 'Though Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo plans to embark on a statewide tour to promote the rights of gays to marry, he chose not to attend a rally on the issue in Albany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo was conspicuously absent on Monday as more than 1,000 New Yorkers gathered at the State Capitol for the annual lobby day in support of gay rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lieutenant Governor, Not Cuomo, Attends Gay Rights Rally', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duffy, Robert J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empire State Pride Agenda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T15:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dce86c9c-4c82-5b40-b7a8-5ba2ee8a8f29', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dce86c9c-4c82-5b40-b7a8-5ba2ee8a8f29'}, {'abstract': 'As a mother and small-business owner, I often find myself squeezed by the double whammy of guilt.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/battle-hymn-of-the-small-business-tiger-mother/', 'snippet': 'As a mother and small-business owner, I often find myself squeezed by the double whammy of guilt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As usual on this Mother’s Day, I found myself not only being waited on by my husband and two sons but also reflecting on my own experiences of motherhood and how I’m measuring up. As a mother and small- business owner, I often find myself squeezed by the double whammy of guilt: time spent in my business is time spent away from my kids, while time with my kids is time away from my business. They all need me, and the struggle to “be there” is ongoing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle Hymn of the Small-Business Tiger Mother', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/220d475f-4aa9-548f-80ba-18bd8fe1418f', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/220d475f-4aa9-548f-80ba-18bd8fe1418f'}, {'abstract': 'Too many people chase the very best investments and end up losing money in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/the-best-investment-advice-stop-losing-money/', 'snippet': 'Too many people chase the very best investments and end up losing money in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog and on his personal Web site, BehaviorGap.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Investment Advice: Stop Losing Money', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d462fa63-5f13-559a-b49b-bd8bff4f29f6', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d462fa63-5f13-559a-b49b-bd8bff4f29f6'}, {'abstract': 'At the Maryland high school, which is known for its championship sports programs, the music program has won so many awards that the school has run out of room for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/sports/10dematha.html', 'snippet': 'At the Maryland high school, which is known for its championship sports programs, the music program has won so many awards that the school has run out of room for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HYATTSVILLE, Md. — The new gym at DeMatha Catholic High is named for a Hall of Fame basketball coach and his wife, and its foyer is lined with championship banners for all the sports the school offers and usually dominates. On a recent afternoon, football players ran sprints under the gaze of coaches from Stanford, Virginia, West Virginia and Duke.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/DEMATHA3/DEMATHA3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/DEMATHA3/DEMATHA3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/DEMATHA3/DEMATHA3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At DeMatha, Sports and Music Play Well Together', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At DeMatha, Sports and Music Play Well Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3aaa09-3b8b-500d-a624-59e7cbbe83ba', 'word_count': 1332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3aaa09-3b8b-500d-a624-59e7cbbe83ba'}, {'abstract': 'War can strip those caught in its path to almost nothing, which is what happened to those who had gathered in a migrant workers’ camp set up in the Libyan city of Misurata.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/reporters-notebook-here-they-stood-until-they-ran/', 'snippet': 'War can strip those caught in its path to almost nothing, which is what happened to those who had gathered in a migrant workers’ camp set up in the Libyan city of Misurata.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MISURATA, Libya — The family photo albums, abandoned on the sand, lay open and fluttering in the desert wind. Around them were the personal items with which they had been packed: heaps of clothing, sandals, DVDs, combs, bottles of perfume, cooking utensils, razors, toothbrushes, several teapots, bundled blankets and a few biscuits, broken and dry. Every several yards a dropped suitcase rested on the dirt, looted bare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reporter’s Notebook: Here They Stood, Until They Ran', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migrant and Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Misurata (Libya)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4362e7ab-adae-5515-a522-601f2a4600ca', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4362e7ab-adae-5515-a522-601f2a4600ca'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Fay Greene, who wrote the Lives piece in yesterday’s magazine, was well qualified to fill the Mother’s Day slot. She and her husband have six sons and three daughters.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/nine-is-enough/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Fay Greene, who wrote the Lives piece in yesterday’s magazine, was well qualified to fill the Mother’s Day slot. She and her husband have six sons and three daughters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melissa Fay Greene, who wrote the Lives essay in yesterday’s magazine, was well qualified to fill the Mother’s Day slot. She and her husband have six sons and three daughters. Or four children by birth and five from foreign orphanages. Divide it however you want; it’s nine kids. This column isn’t about motherhood, exactly, but it shows the way a mother sees and, in Greene’s case, how much she loves seeing her athletically gifted son Fisseha run like the wind. (Her children could field their own baseball team, but Fisseha’s sport of choice is soccer.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Is Enough', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Mother's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greene, Melissa Fay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Glassie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glassie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f19ff9b-65f8-5cb6-b271-51f95f93690a', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f19ff9b-65f8-5cb6-b271-51f95f93690a'}, {'abstract': 'Officials are warning residents in low-lying areas to leave, as the Mississippi River approached a crest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/us/10flood.html', 'snippet': 'Officials are warning residents in low-lying areas to leave, as the Mississippi River approached a crest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMPHIS — The Mississippi River was approaching levels it has not reached in over 70 years as it rolled through here on Monday, attracting a festive crowd of spectators to its banks but also sending residents from their homes in some parts of the city as the river shoved its tributaries aside to make way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/us/FLOODING/FLOODING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/us/FLOODING/FLOODING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/us/FLOODING/FLOODING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/us/FLOODING/FLOODING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011