 to do that, I have to tell a story first.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Be a Jerk or a Human Being on Facebook?', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:20:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0c2e0b-a4a7-5329-bc53-62aa8dd4f0e4', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0c2e0b-a4a7-5329-bc53-62aa8dd4f0e4'}, {'abstract': 'Elderly patients with dementia are receiving feeding tubes without families getting adequate information about the drawbacks, a new study finds.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/feeding-tube-decisions-often-made-in-haste/', 'snippet': 'Elderly patients with dementia are receiving feeding tubes without families getting adequate information about the drawbacks, a new study finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote a few months back about one of the toughest decisions families face as their elders falter: whether to allow insertion of a feeding tube.\xa0\xa0 Somehow, this question seems to stir up even more doubt and anxiety than other medical interventions intended to prolong or improve life.\xa0When a senior nears death and cannot speak for herself, we may find it easier to say no to cardiopulmonary resuscitation or a ventilator than to say no to nutrition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Demented Patients Receive Feeding Tubes', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a7a7c86-2b99-5656-b3fc-d99a76047461', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a7a7c86-2b99-5656-b3fc-d99a76047461'}, {'abstract': 'An outright victory for Qaddafi is still possible.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/how-we-could-lose-in-libya/', 'snippet': 'An outright victory for Qaddafi is still possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From a Kenneth Pollack essay making the case for Western escalation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How We Could Lose in Libya', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/edc23348-d47b-5724-b5ef-cb5046066acd', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edc23348-d47b-5724-b5ef-cb5046066acd'}, {'abstract': 'In a phone interview, Geoffroy de la Bourdonnaye, chief executive at Chloé, shed a bit more light on Monday’s news about the replacement of Hannah MacGibbon.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/more-on-the-change-at-chloe/', 'snippet': 'In a phone interview, Geoffroy de la Bourdonnaye, chief executive at Chloé, shed a bit more light on Monday’s news about the replacement of Hannah MacGibbon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a phone interview, Geoffroy de la Bourdonnaye, chief executive at Chloé, shed a bit more light on Monday’s news. First, he praised Hannah MacGibbon, saying: “I think she’s been extremely good for the house. She put the house back on track, no question about it.” Ms. MacGibbon, who was promoted to creative director in 2008, helped restore attention to the feminine brand, which had briefly faltered under its previous designer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More on the Change at Chloé', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/51d86a00-cbba-574c-8f21-ce3e06833f4f', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51d86a00-cbba-574c-8f21-ce3e06833f4f'}, {'abstract': 'Many allergy sufferers believe that a daily spoonful of locally produced honey can act like a vaccine and alleviate symptoms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/10really.html', 'snippet': 'Many allergy sufferers believe that a daily spoonful of locally produced honey can act like a vaccine and alleviate symptoms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eating Local Honey Cures Allergies', 'kicker': 'Really?', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eating local honey cures allergies.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Honey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b85c469-b533-51cc-a0c5-cd81b210d01c', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b85c469-b533-51cc-a0c5-cd81b210d01c'}, {'abstract': 'Los Angeles exits the N.B.A. playoffs, and now finds itself without a coach or a clear way to rebuild.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/sports/10leading.html', 'snippet': 'Los Angeles exits the N.B.A. playoffs, and now finds itself without a coach or a clear way to rebuild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is not generally fair to compare teams’ fates across sports. They are different games and circumstances, ruled by entirely different committees of the sporting gods. That said, we’ll do it anyway because the Lakers and the Red Wings responded so remarkably differently this weekend when faced with the epitaph being written on their dynasties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lakers Go Out With a Thud', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lakers Go Out With a Thud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballesteros, Seve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thornton, Joe (1979- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosley, Shane', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verlander, Justin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bliss, Dave', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacquiao, Manny', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T16:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454a8789-8b8f-59b8-a28c-f32d0eba5235', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454a8789-8b8f-59b8-a28c-f32d0eba5235'}, {'abstract': 'The number of Americans with gout is rising steadily as the population ages, becomes heavier and is exposed to foods that can precipitate the disorder in susceptible people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/10brody.html', 'snippet': 'The number of Americans with gout is rising steadily as the population ages, becomes heavier and is exposed to foods that can precipitate the disorder in susceptible people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 55-year-old neighbor of mine was awakened in the wee hours of the morning recently with an excruciating pain in his right big toe that rendered him unable to walk. As happens in a classic attack of gout, the onset was sudden and the affected joint red and swollen. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10brody/10brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 936, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10brody/10brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 936}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10brody/10brody-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 657, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10brody/10brody-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 825, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10brody/10brody-thumbStandar