ice of Euro RSCG Worldwide by naming it to handle the creative duties for the introduction of Pucker, a flavored vodka.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/business/media/09adnewsletter3.html', 'snippet': 'Beam Global Spirits and Wine, Deerfield, Ill., expanded its relationship with the Chicago office of Euro RSCG Worldwide by naming it to handle the creative duties for the introduction of Pucker, a flavored vodka.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beam Global Spirits and Wine, Deerfield, Ill., expanded its relationship with the Chicago office of Euro RSCG Worldwide by naming it to handle the creative duties for the introduction of Pucker, a flavored vodka. Spending has not been determined. Euro RSCG Chicago already creates campaigns for Beam Global brands like Effen vodka and Sauza tequila. Beam Global is part of Fortune Brands and Euro RSCG Worldwide is part of the Havas Worldwide unit of Havas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T17:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7abffe2f-7220-54a9-899a-d7aecdea4e9f', 'word_count': 1343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7abffe2f-7220-54a9-899a-d7aecdea4e9f'}, {'abstract': 'Hertz has once again proved that “best and final offers” are often nothing of the sort, finally trumping Avis’s bid for Dollar Thrifty with a $2.24 billion offer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/hertz-gets-back-into-the-drivers-seat/', 'snippet': 'Hertz has once again proved that “best and final offers” are often nothing of the sort, finally trumping Avis’s bid for Dollar Thrifty with a $2.24 billion offer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not quite the action in the movie “Fast Five,” but the rental car wars just got interesting again. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hertz Gets Back Into the Driver’s Seat', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T17:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae631b0e-ee72-5348-b34b-ae7959d7a175', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae631b0e-ee72-5348-b34b-ae7959d7a175'}, {'abstract': 'The Thai prime minister said Monday he had received the king’s approval to dissolve Parliament seven months early , and he set elections for July 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/world/asia/10thailand.html', 'snippet': 'The Thai prime minister said Monday he had received the king’s approval to dissolve Parliament seven months early , and he set elections for July 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — The prime minister of Thailand said Monday that he had received the king’s approval to dissolve Parliament seven months early. He set elections for July 3. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thai Premier to Dissolve Parliament; Elections Set for July 3', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker