nyt://article/0b157c53-eb64-505f-84c6-418059d672a4'}, {'abstract': 'Finding out the shortest path between two points, in the presence of obstacles.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/numberplay-mission-shortest-path/', 'snippet': 'Finding out the shortest path between two points, in the presence of obstacles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the above problem, you had to determine the shortest distance, which, assuming that the speed of the vehicle was constant over the terrain, would also result in the shortest travel time. In the next mission, you have to specifically determine the path that takes the least time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Mission Shortest Path', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/664eee30-aa8e-5b10-9440-6bb84b68bdfa', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/664eee30-aa8e-5b10-9440-6bb84b68bdfa'}, {'abstract': 'YouTube confirmed reports that it will add thousands of new movies to its online video rental service to compete with services like Netflix.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/youtube-expands-video-rental-service/', 'snippet': 'YouTube confirmed reports that it will add thousands of new movies to its online video rental service to compete with services like Netflix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 5:48 p.m.: Adding details about the new movie rentals and correcting the spelling of Salar Kamangar, the head of YouTube’s, last name. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'YouTube Expands Video Rental Service', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/977e2624-3d11-50ad-ae94-cbce34777046', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977e2624-3d11-50ad-ae94-cbce34777046'}, {'abstract': 'A new study reports that breast cancers detected between screenings are more aggressive than tumors missed during a regular screening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/research/10screening-1.html', 'snippet': 'A new study reports that breast cancers detected between screenings are more aggressive than tumors missed during a regular screening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some breast cancers detected between regular screenings were simply missed on the patient’s last mammogram. But a majority found during the interim periods can’t be found on previous scans at all. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Screening: New Threat Rises Between Mammograms', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SCREENING: New Threat Rises Between Mammograms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9505bc-ce43-5fc3-926c-ac886fa9ccbf', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9505bc-ce43-5fc3-926c-ac886fa9ccbf'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly four in 10 voter (37 percent) said they had a unfavorable opinion of the former House speaker.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/recent-poll-shows-gingrich-has-work-to-do/', 'snippet': 'Nearly four in 10 voter (37 percent) said they had a unfavorable opinion of the former House speaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a former speaker of the House and contributor to Fox News, Newt Gingrich will enter the presidential race this week as one of the better-known Republicans on the list of possible contenders. But a New York Times/CBS News poll conducted last month found that that may not necessarily be to his advantage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recent Poll Shows Gingrich Has Work to Do', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/32dcd958-007f-58cd-aed5-64d5c01fb367', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32dcd958-007f-58cd-aed5-64d5c01fb367'}, {'abstract': 'Notebooks containing unauthorized notes offer insights into the debates over the Constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/sothebys-to-offer-a-founding-fathers-illicit-notebooks/', 'snippet': 'Notebooks containing unauthorized notes offer insights into the debates over the Constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the annals of injudicious disappearances from Manhattan’s mean streets, before there was Judge Crater there was Judge Lansing. And, before Judge John Lansing Jr. vanished in 1829, not so far from where Judge Joseph Force Crater went missing 99 years later, Judge Lansing was already famous — as a Founding Father and New York delegate to the Constitutional Convention in 1787. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sotheby’s to Offer a Founding Father’s Illicit Notebooks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2810d74b-5d14-5b04-bb40-088839ca1442', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2810d74b-5d14-5b04-bb40-088839ca1442'}, {'abstract': 'A game developer has created a replica of Osama bin Laden’s compound for a new level of the first-person shooter video game Counter-Strike.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/video-game-level-replicates-bin-laden-compound/', 'snippet': 'A game developer has created a replica of Osama bin Laden’s compound for a new level of the first-person shooter video game Counter-Strike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading the news coverage of Osama bin Laden’s death last week sometimes sounded like the narrative of a new video game. There were the secret radar-evading government helicopters, the highly trained war dog and the fearless members of Seal Team 6, the best of the best Navy Seal units, which\xa0stormed Bin Laden’s compound.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Game Level Replicates Bin Laden Compound', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abbottabad (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T18:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0a97dcd-330a-5f36-9c6b-9e36a365153f', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0a97dcd-330a-5f36-9c6b-9e36a365153f'}, {'abstract': 'Is a child’s ability to stay focused on TV or a video game, though not on anything else, a cause or an effect of attention problems — or both?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/views/10klass.html', 'snippet': 'Is a child’s ability to stay focused on TV or a video game, though not on anything else, a cause or an effect of attention problems — or both?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mother had brought in a note from her son’s elementary school teacher: Dear doctor, I think this child needs to be tested for attention deficit disorder.', 'print_section': 'D', 'p