ng to feature a more glittering lineup of stars than most Broadway shows. Meryl Streep, Amy Adams, Allison Janney, Liev Schreiber, David Morse and Bill Camp are among the actors coming together on June 1 at Alice Tully Hall to participate in a reading of a new play written by Alan Alda about the scientist Marie Curie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meryl Streep to Participate in Alan Alda’s Marie Curie Play', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alice Tully Hall (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDA, ALAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camp, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curie, Marie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janney, Allison', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morse, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schreiber, Liev', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:09:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ffa2f78-fc7e-5a28-82d2-4f9943961241', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ffa2f78-fc7e-5a28-82d2-4f9943961241'}, {'abstract': 'The agency announced that Sheila C. Bair will end her five-year term on July 8.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/business/10bair.html', 'snippet': 'The agency announced that Sheila C. Bair will end her five-year term on July 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheila C. Bair, one of the banking industry’s most influential regulators and outspoken critics during the financial crisis, said on Monday that she planned to step down as chairwoman of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation on July 8. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.I.C. Chairwoman to Leave in July', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chairwoman At F.D.I.C. Is Departing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:23:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Dash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58c77579-d463-5676-ae48-a38e7fe53abc', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58c77579-d463-5676-ae48-a38e7fe53abc'}, {'abstract': 'Some natural supplements for babies are of unknown effectiveness and may contain contaminants or spur allergies, a new study says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/research/10regimens.html', 'snippet': 'Some natural supplements for babies are of unknown effectiveness and may contain contaminants or spur allergies, a new study says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly one in 10 babies are given supplements or plant-based teas to soothe colic or help with teething during the first year of life, even though the products are unproven and may contain contaminants or spur allergies, a new study says.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regimens: Looking Twice at Supplements for Infants', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'REGIMENS: Looking Twice at Supplements for Infants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b464fdd-8780-5cc6-ba8c-2c0d41a670a8', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b464fdd-8780-5cc6-ba8c-2c0d41a670a8'}, {'abstract': 'Warhol is famous for it, but the Campbell’s Soup label is an icon on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/who-made-that-campbells-soup-label/', 'snippet': 'Warhol is famous for it, but the Campbell’s Soup label is an icon on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1962, Andy Warhol produced “Campbell’s Soup Cans”: 32 paintings, each representing a flavor of Campbell’s condensed soup. “With these works, Warhol took on the tradition of still-life painting, declaring a familiar household brand of packaged food a legitimate subject in the age of Post-War economic recovery,” according to Christie’s. Warhol appropriated the famous soup can and reinvented it as a work of art. He can be credited with converging the world of high art and supermarket branding, propelling the pop-art movement forward and possibly even boosting the sales of canned soup, but the label that he rode to stardom was not his design at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Campbell’s Soup Label?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorrance, John T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warhol, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Campbell Soup Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54971cdb-aee4-5c8c-9939-8a60b2452c62', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54971cdb-aee4-5c8c-9939-8a60b2452c62'}, {'abstract': 'New rules will make it hard for stay-at-home spouses to get credit in their own name.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/stay-at-home-moms-and-the-need-for-credit/', 'snippet': 'New rules will make it hard for stay-at-home spouses to get credit in their own name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are a stay-at-home mom (or dad) and want a credit card, you should consider applying for one, pronto. A pending change in the way card companies must evaluate applications will probably make it much harder for people who don’t have their own, independent income to get one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stay-at-Home Moms and the Need for Credit', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d24a0a4-22ca-5f8f-9937-dbe19123c79a', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d24a0a4-22ca-5f8f-9937-dbe19123c79a'}, {'abstract': 'Groupon is pairing with Live Nation Entertainment to create GrouponLive, a discount ticket seller. In an interview with CNBC, Groupon chief’s executive, Andrew Mason, and Live Nation’s chief executive, Michael Rapino, discuss the rationale behind the deal and their strategy to “grow the pie” of online event marketing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/inside-the-groupon-live-nation-deal/', 'snippet': 'Groupon is pairing with Live Nation Entertainment to create GrouponLive, a discount ticket seller. In an interview with CNBC, Groupon chief’s executive, Andrew Mason, and Live Nation’s chief executive, Michael Rapino, discuss the rationale behind ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The daily-deals site Groupon is pairing with Live Nation Entertainment, an online ticket seller, to create GrouponLive, a discount ticket seller. In an interview with CNBC, Groupon’s chief executive, Andrew Mason, and Live Nation’s chief executive, Michael Rapino, discuss the rationale behind the deal and their strategy to “grow the pie” of online event marketing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Groupon-Live Nation Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapino, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Live Nation Entertainment Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:29:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b3d60cd-2aab-5fa6-99f7-6bd99e642996', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b3d60cd-2aab-5fa6-99f7-6bd99e642996'}, {'abstract': 'Why is it that children with attention deficit problems at school can be held in rapt attention by a video game or television program?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/attention-problems-except-for-screens/', 'snippet': 'Why is it that children with attention deficit problems at school can be held in rapt attention by a video game or television program?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why is it that children with attention deficit problems at school can be held in rapt attention by a video game or television program?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attention Problems, Except for Screens', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/04569730-6527-5d0e-8bcc-17cd96966817', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04569730-6527-5d0e-8bcc-17cd96966817'}, {'abstract': 'A new T-shirt from Playtype serves two purposes: it’s the latest entry in the movement to free Ai Weiwei and it speaks volumes about free speech.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/hot-type/', 'snippet': 'A new T-shirt from Playtype serves two purposes: it’s the latest entry in the movement to free Ai Weiwei and it speaks volumes about free speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest entry in the movement to free Ai Weiwei, the Chinese dissident artist who has been detained since April, is this T-shirt, the heavy black bars of which speak volumes about free speech. It’s the creation of Playtype, a self-described “online type foundry” that was established by e-Types, a Copenhagen design agency, to showcase over 20 years of type design, including commissioned works for fonts “created out of pure passion and typographical heartache.” E-Types collaborated on the project with the architecture office Bjarke Ingels Group and V1 Gallery in Copenhagen. Late last year, Playtype opened a concept store — which will operate for one year only, until Dec. 1 — in Copenhagen’s trendy Vesterbro neighborhood, a former red-light district. The store’s wares, which include the aforementioned T-shirt and type-adorned notebooks, wine labels and ceramic mugs, are not sold online, alas, but inquiries are invited at info@playtype.com. You can also download the T-shirt graphic here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot Type', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:38:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/679d82f4-9aba-5c85-a9a0-5eb8d20011b4', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/679d82f4-9aba-5c85-a9a0-5eb8d20011b4'}, {'abstract': 'A pilot project costing only $20,244 saved the lives of 97 infants, the authors estimated, meaning that it cost just $208 per life saved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/health/10global.html', 'snippet': 'A pilot project costing only $20,244 saved the lives of 97 infants, the authors estimated, meaning that it cost just $208 per life saved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giving midwives simple training has already been shown to save newborns’ lives, and a new study in Zambia has found that it can be remarkably cost-effective as well. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10globalspan/10globalspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10globalspan/10globalspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10globalspan/10globalspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10globalspan/10globalspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/health/10globalspan/10globalspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Infant Deaths Drop After Midwives Undergo Inexpensive Training', 'kicker': 'Global Update', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ZAMBIA: Infant Deaths Drop After Midwives Undergo Inexpensive Training', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midwives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infant Mortality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BIRTHS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zambia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18283965-759d-5d17-a714-1012f29b5340', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18283965-759d-5d17-a714-1012f29b5340'}, {'abstract': 'Henry A. Kissinger’s fascinating, shrewd and sometimes perverse new book, “On China,” tries to show how the history of China has shaped its foreign policy and attitudes toward the West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/books/on-china-by-henry-kissinger-review.html', 'snippet': 'Henry A. Kissinger’s fascinating, shrewd and sometimes perverse new book, “On China,” tries to show how the history of China has shaped its foreign policy and attitudes toward the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been four decades since President Richard M. Nixon sent Henry A. Kissinger to Beijing to re-establish contact with China, an ancient civilization with which the United States, at that point, had had no high-level diplomatic contact for more than two decades. Since then the cold war has ended; the Soviet Union (a threat to both China and the United States and a spur to Sino-American cooperation) has come unwound; and economic reform in China has transformed a poverty-ridden, poorly educated nation into a great power that is playing an increasingly pivotal role in the globalized world. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 866, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Insider Views China, Past and Future', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Insider Views China, Past and Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kissinger, Henry A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T19:40:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9eceeb8-15b0-57c2-ab3f-e364436e8795', 'word_count': 1681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9eceeb8-15b0-57c2-ab3f-e364436e8795'}, {'abstract': 'Eman al-Obeidy, whose complaint to foreign journalists of being raped by security forces and subsequent forcible removal made her a symbol of Libya’s repression, says she has fled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/world/middleeast/10rape.html', 'snippet': 'Eman al-Obeidy, whose complaint to foreign journalists of being raped by security forces and subsequent forcible removal made her a symbol of Libya’s repression, says she has fled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A Libyan woman who became a symbol of her country’s repression after security forces tried to silence her accusations that Qaddafi militiamen had raped her said on Monday that she had escaped to neighboring Tunisia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Who Accused Militiamen of Rape Has Fled Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outspoken Victim Flees Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obeidy, Eman al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 