: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75ca7c3-bc74-505d-9972-ab731316dab0', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75ca7c3-bc74-505d-9972-ab731316dab0'}, {'abstract': 'The pop-up creators will open Co-Op Food & Drink next week in the Hotel on Rivington.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/guerrilla-culinary-brigade-finds-a-permanent-home/', 'snippet': 'The pop-up creators will open Co-Op Food & Drink next week in the Hotel on Rivington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Philips and Jason Apfelbaum, who have been running pop-up dinners in parking lots and similar venues with their company, Guerrilla Culinary Brigade, are settling down. Late next week they plan to open Co-Op Food & Drink in the space that had been Thor in the Hotel on Rivington. “This is my first real restaurant,” Mr. Philips said, “but I haven’t given up on the pop-up dinners either.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guerrilla Culinary Brigade Finds a Permanent Home', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T20:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba7ecc49-2b40-51f8-800e-bfee6b8a8ee0', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba7ecc49-2b40-51f8-800e-bfee6b8a8ee0'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by a classic pasta, this dish includes chicory, a bitter green much loved in southern Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/health/nutrition/11recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by a classic pasta, this dish includes chicory, a bitter green much loved in southern Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This dish is inspired by a classic oil and garlic pasta. I’ve added chicory, a bitter green that is much loved in southern Italy but underused here. It’s sold with lettuces in the supermarket, often called escarole or curly endive. Chicory contains a type of soluble fiber called inulin, which some studies suggest may have a positive effect on blood sugar levels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/11recipehealth/11recipehealth-thumbLarge.jp