 young as 29,000 years ago, suggesting there was extensive overlap between the two human species. This raised the question of whether there had been interbreeding between humans and Neanderthals, an issue that is still not resolved.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neanderthals and Early Humans May Not Have Mingled Much', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Neanderthals and Early Humans May Not Have Mingled Much', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neanderthal Man', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY AND ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T20:41:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6eb3051-5da4-56ed-ad91-f8580eee87f1', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6eb3051-5da4-56ed-ad91-f8580eee87f1'}, {'abstract': 'An interview with the president draws the most viewers on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/obama-on-bin-laden-mission-lifts-60-minutes/', 'snippet': 'An interview with the president draws the most viewers on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s interview on “60 Minutes” about the mission that killed Osama bin Laden helped lift the program to No. 1 in the ratings on Sunday night as 13.8 million people tuned in to the broadcast, according to Nielsen’s estimates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 