 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a72bff6-84ea-58c2-a6b6-4e731b768bf7', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a72bff6-84ea-58c2-a6b6-4e731b768bf7'}, {'abstract': 'What are the hidden gems in your favorite parks? In honor of spring, we’re asking readers to send us your favorite restaurants in parks, from the casual to the high-end experience.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/where-do-you-eat-at-the-park/', 'snippet': 'What are the hidden gems in your favorite parks? In honor of spring, we’re asking readers to send us your favorite restaurants in parks, from the casual to the high-end experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s spring in New York – a time when parks fill up with city dwellers who’ve been indoors, patiently waiting for the warm sun to show its face. Among the city’s great perks are its parks, and with parks come outdoor concerts, Frisbee matches, sunbathing, nature-watching and last but far from least, alfresco dining.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Do You Eat at the Park?', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Belopotosky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belopotosky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bb498ba-2d99-5f07-978f-3a99e1505d1d', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bb498ba-2d99-5f07-978f-3a99e1505d1d'}, {'abstract': 'Danza Contemporánea de Cuba prepares to perform in New York for the first time since it was formed in 1959.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/arts/dance/danza-contemporanea-de-cuba-at-the-joyce-on-first-us-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Danza Contemporánea de Cuba prepares to perform in New York for the first time since it was formed in 1959.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAVANA — At the humid, spare studios of Danza Contemporánea de Cuba here last week, two dozen dancers rolled their spines forward, turning their outstretched arms in their sockets as drummers beat a slow, syncopated song dedicated to the Yoruba deity Obatalá.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/DANZA/DANZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/DANZA/DANZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/DANZA/DANZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuban Dancers Complete a 5-Decade Trip to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuban Dancers Complete A 5-Decade Trip to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:17:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Burnett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burnett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d395ce61-8217-5ddf-b157-9f139bb11702', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d395ce61-8217-5ddf-b157-9f139bb11702'}, {'abstract': 'New research suggests computer assistants in cars could significantly reduce distracted-driving accidents.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/distracted-driving-an-answer-perhaps/', 'snippet': 'New research suggests computer assistants in cars could significantly reduce distracted-driving accidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are at least two irrefutable facts about the practice of people communicating by cellphones while driving cars. First, it is a big problem, with studies estimating that more than 500,000 traffic accidents and 2,600 deaths a year are caused by cellphone-distracted drivers. No one has documented the problem as thoroughly as my colleague, Matt Richtel. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Distracted Driving: An Answer Perhaps?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horvitz, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/28d2fafc-02d3-5e39-8d7f-22248b599835', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28d2fafc-02d3-5e39-8d7f-22248b599835'}, {'abstract': 'PBS is making changes to its Friday-night schedule this fall, trimming its public affairs programming and adding a nine-week run of arts performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/arts/television/pbs-revamps-schedule-of-friday-night-shows.html', 'snippet': 'PBS is making changes to its Friday-night schedule this fall, trimming its public affairs programming and adding a nine-week run of arts performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PBS is making changes to its Friday-night schedule this fall, trimming its public affairs programming and adding a nine-week run of arts performances, the public broadcaster announced on Monday. The Friday newsmagazine “Need to Know” will shrink to a half-hour, beginning Sept. 16, from an hour, and take on a new focus on issues related to the 2012 election. On Oct. 14 the new “PBS Arts Fall Festival” will start its run of offerings from around the country, including “The Little Mermaid From San Francisco Ballet”; “Women Who Rock,” based on an exhibition at the Rock ’n’ Roll Hall of Fame in Cleveland; and “Give Me the Banjo,” narrated by Steve Martin, exploring the roots of American music. Other changes this fall include the addition of a Wednesday broadcast for the Sunday-night staple “Nature.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PBS Revamps Schedule of Friday Night Shows', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PBS Revamps Schedule Of Friday Night Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a202e025-cdd8-5f4d-97b1-a21da41a456f', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a202e025-cdd8-5f4d-97b1-a21da41a456f'}, {'abstract': 'In life, the specimen weighed less than 70 pounds, compared with the six-ton weight of a full-grown T. bataar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/science/10obdinosaur.html', 'snippet': 'In life, the specimen weighed less than 70 pounds, compared with the six-ton weight of a full-grown T. bataar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers working in the western Gobi Desert in Mongolia have discovered the almost complete skeleton of a tyrannosaurid dinosaur that was less than 3 years old when it died, younger and smaller than any previously known. The animal, Tarbosaurus bataar, is the closest relative of Tyrannosaurus rex, the predator that lived at the same time in North America.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10obtrex/10obtrex-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10obtrex/10obtrex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10obtrex/10obtrex-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Featherweight Relative of the T. Rex Is Found', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Featherweight Relative Of the T. Rex Is Found', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac7d894-c2c4-55fc-90f6-4403cc1aed9c', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac7d894-c2c4-55fc-90f6-4403cc1aed9c'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Lucas has a wide-ranging body of work that has channeled musical traditions from Poland, China, Israel, India and elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/10/arts/design/LUCAS.html', 'snippet': 'Gary Lucas has a wide-ranging body of work that has channeled musical traditions from Poland, China, Israel, India and elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Lucas has a wide-ranging body of work that has channeled musical traditions from Poland, China, Israel, India and elsewhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/design/LUCAS-slide-FE1K/LUCAS-slide-FE1K-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/design/LUCAS-slide-FE1K/LUCAS-slide-FE1K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/design/LUCAS-slide-FE1K/LUCAS-slide-FE1K-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eclectic Virtuoso', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:36:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4e78da0f-148d-5121-9aac-a280e2ea856c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4e78da0f-148d-5121-9aac-a280e2ea856c'}, {'abstract': 'The music business has never quite known what to make of Gary Lucas, who has a new CD, “The Ordeal of Civility,” going on sale on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/arts/music/gary-lucas-has-a-new-cd-the-ordeal-of-civility.html', 'snippet': 'The music business has never quite known what to make of Gary Lucas, who has a new CD, “The Ordeal of Civility,” going on sale on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music business has never quite known what to make of Gary Lucas. Go to a site for streaming or downloading songs, and you may find his music consigned to a vague category called “other.” Look him up in standard reference works, and he’s likely to be referred to as a “legendary left-field guitarist” whose work is “eclectic” or just plain “eccentric.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/LUCAS/LUCAS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/LUCAS/LUCAS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/LUCAS/LUCAS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/LUCAS/LUCAS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/arts/LUCAS/LUCAS