b', 'word_count': 1464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/488fb195-b27b-55f7-8a5f-b603cb5ecd4b'}, {'abstract': 'Despite volcanic activity and many hot springs, Japan’s geothermal power plants account for only 0.3 percent of its electricity production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/business/energy-environment/10yenside.html', 'snippet': 'Despite volcanic activity and many hot springs, Japan’s geothermal power plants account for only 0.3 percent of its electricity production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANAIZU, Japan — As visitors to any of Japan’s thousands of hot springs know, this country is sitting on a lot of very hot water. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lot of Hot Water, but Not Much Is Being Used to Produce Electricity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lot of Hot Water, but Not Much Is Being Used to Produce Electricity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geothermal Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T21:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fe3d51-0d24-58a0-b283-2daf4a288690', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fe3d51-0d24-58a0-b283-2daf4a288690'}, {'abstract': 'The Pistons reacted poorly when they were swept by Phil Jackson’s Bulls on the way to their first of six titles in eight years.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/lakers-bitter-exit-evokes-1991-pistons/', 'snippet': 'The Pistons rea