 '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f48812a4-82a6-5474-ab34-cd07e735184a', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f48812a4-82a6-5474-ab34-cd07e735184a'}, {'abstract': 'A new study lends weight to the argument that online poker should be legal.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/poker-as-a-game-of-skill/', 'snippet': 'A new study lends weight to the argument that online poker should be legal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is poker a game of luck or skill? That’s the question the economists Steven D. Levitt (of “Freakonomics” fame) and Thomas J. Miles explore in a new working paper published with the National Bureau of Economic Research.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poker as a Game of Skill', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poker (Card Game)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levitt, Steven D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Bureau of Economic Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T22:07:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/994e2e9e-4fa8-5514-8290-141cfda9b484', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/994e2e9e-4fa8-5514-8290-141cfda9b484'}, {'abstract': 'Though not “a great flier,” Margery Mayer says conversations with seatmates can turn a routine business trip into a memorable experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/business/10flier.html', 'snippet': 'Though not “a great flier,” Margery Mayer says conversations with seatmates can turn a routine business trip into a memorable experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE been a business traveler for most of my career, but I started to fly what seems like nonstop about 15 years ago. I like to travel for business because I like meeting people, but I’m not a great flier. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Book Publisher Finds Ready Conversation', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Book Publisher Finds Ready Conversation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T22:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margery Mayer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mayer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2a159e4-a7af-5663-9802-7057090875e7', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2a159e4-a7af-5663-9802-7057090875e7'}, {'abstract': 'A newfound abundance of water in the solar system has inspired scientists who hope to find traces of life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/science/space/10water.html', 'snippet': 'A newfound abundance of water in the solar system has inspired scientists who hope to find traces of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those who hunt for life on other worlds, water in its liquid form is perhaps the leading indicator. Life as we know it on Earth is based on water and carbon. And if organisms can prosper here in nasty environments — in geysers, in the depths of the sea, in toxic waste, in water that is too hot, too cold, too acidic or too alkaline — why could they not prosper out there?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10life/10life-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 926, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10life/10life-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/10/science/10life/10life-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fountains of Optimism for Life Way Out There', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fountains of Optimism For Life Way Out There', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraterrestrial Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T22:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Gugliotta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gugliotta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08bf0b55-9b16-5f8a-93bb-840ea54a4bb5', 'word_count': 1626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08bf0b55-9b16-5f8a-93bb-840ea54a4bb5'}, {'abstract': 'Groups try to draw attention to the need to conserve areas like the Northeast Ecological Corridor near El Yunque National Forest.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/09/a-green-banner-for-puerto-rican-day/', 'snippet': 'Groups try to draw attention to the need to conserve areas like the Northeast Ecological Corridor near El Yunque National Forest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Puerto Rican Day Parade is going green.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Green Banner for Puerto Rican Day', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sierra Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Yunque (Puerto Rico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-09T22:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline'