rstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc5440e-0ad5-561a-b587-64e7ac6c7d09', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc5440e-0ad5-561a-b587-64e7ac6c7d09'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees general manager said he thought more about the team’s success, adding that Jeter’s struggles probably masked the fact that some of his teammates also were not hitting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/sports/baseball/10yankees.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees general manager said he thought more about the team’s success, adding that Jeter’s struggles probably masked the fact that some of his teammates also were not hitting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROE TOWNSHIP, N.J. — Brian Cashman, the Yankees’ general manager, showed up Monday morning in a golf shirt, slacks and shoes to play 18 holes at Forsgate Country Club, 54 miles down the New Jersey Turnpike from Yankee Stadium.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/10jeter-1/10jeter-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/10jeter-1/10jeter-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/10jeter-1/10jeter-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/10/sports/10jeter-1/10jeter-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':