 in “The Home Front” when 12-year-old Isaac Eisch almost lets down his brave-soldier demeanor as he speaks of his father, Sgt. First Class Brian Eisch, who is half a world away in Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tender Moments, a War’s High Cost', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Press Photo Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T09:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/39e7d357-b7af-5b3d-b1f5-8a3428510e86', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39e7d357-b7af-5b3d-b1f5-8a3428510e86'}, {'abstract': 'How do you tend to use Facebook?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/what-is-your-facebook-persona/', 'snippet': 'How do you tend to use Facebook?', 'lead_paragraph': 'People use Facebook in different ways and for different purposes — to connect with friends, to post clever observations, to find and share ideas and resources found elsewhere, to help others. If you are on Facebook, how do you use it? How would you characterize your “persona” there? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is Your Facebook Persona?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}