l in Tushka, Okla.; its superintendent talks about resuming classes and rebuilding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, Tushka, Okla., with a population of 312, was hit by a tornado that damaged much of the town, killed two people and virtually destroyed its school. Tushka, which is the Choctaw word for “warrior,” is finding its way back amid difficult circumstances. Bill Pennington, the town’s school superintendent, discusses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/04/17/us/SUB-17-TORNADO/SUB-17-TORNADO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/04/17/us/SUB-17-TORNADO/SUB-17-TORNADO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/04/17/us/SUB-17-TORNADO/SUB-17-TORNADO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/04/17/us/SUB-17-TORNADO/SUB-17-TORNADO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/04/17/us/SUB-17-TORNADO/SUB-17-TORNADO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Demolished School, Moving On and Looking Ahead', 'kicker': 'Asked And Answered', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Demolished School, Moving On and Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T14:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'b