stors, including a private equity firm, a pension fund and a venture capital firm, stand to benefit from Skype’s proposed deal with Microsoft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Skype is neither a start-up nor a stalwart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Winners in the Skype Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internet Telephony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Silver Lake Partners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skype Technologies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T15:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c89b90a-e154-5062-8a1c-9b86262744f2', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c89b90a-e154-5062-8a1c-9b86262744f2'}, {'abstract': 'Since Tunisian revolutionaries anointed their successful revolt the “Jasmine Revolution,” the flowering cousin of the olive tree has been branded a nefarious change-agent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/world/asia/11jasmine.html', 'snippet': 'Since Tunisian revolutionaries anointed their successful revolt the “Jasmine Revolution,” the flowering cousin of the olive tree has been branded a nefarious change-agent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAXING, China — Do not be lulled by its intoxicating fragrance or the dainty, starlike blossoms whose whiteness suggests innocence and purity. Jasmine, a stalwart of Chinese tea and the subject of a celebrated folk song often heard while on hold with provincial bureaucrats, is not what it seems. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/world/11jasmine_337cham/11jasmine_337cham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/11/world/11jasmine_337cham/11jasmine_337cham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/world/11jasmine_337cham/11jasmine_337cham-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/world/11jasmine_337cham/11jasmine_337cham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/world/11jasmine_337cham/11jasmine_337cham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Catching Scent of Revolution, China Moves to Snip Jasmine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catching Scent of Revolution, China Moves to Snip Jasmine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T15:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne