-10T15:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b30ed3eb-0221-5b9d-a0f0-2dea71dd6552', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b30ed3eb-0221-5b9d-a0f0-2dea71dd6552'}, {'abstract': 'Both sides hailed modest progress on economic issues even as they traded harsh words about China’s respect for human rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/world/asia/11china.html', 'snippet': 'Both sides hailed modest progress on economic issues even as they traded harsh words about China’s respect for human rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Two days of high-level talks between the United States and China wrapped up Tuesday with both sides hailing modest progress on economic issues even as they traded harsh words about China’s respect for human rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/world/CHINA/CHINA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/world/CHINA/CHINA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Hopes Than Gains At U.S.-China Meetings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Hopes Than Gains At U.S.-China Meetings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T16:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fc532aa-2c12-5716-bb01-3f902cc2a5c9', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fc532aa-2c12-5716-bb01-3f902cc2a5c9'}, {'abstract': 'For her latest collection, the jeweler Monique Péan went in search of sustainable pearls — and wound up working in a lagoon in the South Pacific.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/pearl-vision/', 'snippet': 'For her latest collection, the jeweler Monique Péan went in search of sustainable pearls — and wound up working in a lagoon in the South Pacific.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For her latest collection, the jeweler Monique Péan went in search of sustainable pearls — and wound up working in a lagoon in the South Pacific. Péan says she furthered her commitment to eco-minded jewelry during her CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund mentorship at Tiffany & Company; she and the company’s C.E.O., Michael Kowalski, share what he calls “an approach to precious materials that is sustainable and benefits the communities involved.” The quest led Péan to the Ahe atoll in French Polynesia, where the Kamoka Pearl Farm uses fish and sponges to clean its oyster shells. The farm harvests without chemicals, feeds its employees (“Raw oysters, fried oysters, oyster risotto, a lot of oysters!” Péan says) and turns the shells into beads. Péan’s line uses Kamoka’s keshi pearls in hues of blue, aubergine and gold for pieces like a ring set with delicate pavé-diamond tendrils (conflict-free, of course), which Péan says was inspired by Ahe’s “pollution-free midnight sky reflecting against the waves and the light.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pearl Vision', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6225288a-dc1c-5333-af45-fd9a61920a01', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6225288a-dc1c-5333-af45-fd9a61920a01'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney is often asked about health care. On Thursday, he will talk about it.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/romney-to-deliver-health-care-speech-in-michigan/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney is often asked about health care. On Thursday, he will talk about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney is often asked about health care. On Thursday, he will talk about it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney to Deliver Health Care Speech in Michigan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'p