ing for trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Filling your time during a cheap weekend in Rio de Janeiro would seem like a no-brainer: head to Ipanema beach on Saturday, spend a couple of bucks to rent a beach chair and a couple more on tempting snacks from roaming vendors. Rinse (in the on-beach showers) and repeat (on Sunday).', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '$100 Weekend in Rio de Janeiro', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Weekend in Rio de Janeiro for $100', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T19:38:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d5e67a-d84e-5121-9c33-8b19a95f0f51', 'word_count': 1530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d5e67a-d84e-5121-9c33-8b19a95f0f51'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing lasts forever — and that includes these far-flung destinations, which are changing as they balance their own needs with those of ever more curious travelers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/last-call/', 'snippet': 'Nothing lasts forever — and that includes these far-flung destinations, which are changing as they balance their own needs with those of ever more curious travelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nothing lasts forever — and that includes these far-flung destinations, which are changing as they balance their own needs with those of ever more curious travelers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last Call'