ovelist José Saramago. Saramago’s best books read like hallucinatory thrillers. They’re warm to the touch; they practically palpitate in your hands. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 987, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/BOOK1/BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cautious Memoirist Who Ends With a Laugh', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cautious Memoirist Who Ends With a Laugh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saramago, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Margaret Jull', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T20:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd0268f0-3add-519e-8624-56001d30f89e', 'word_count': 950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd0268f0-3add-519e-8624-56001d30f89e'}, {'abstract': 'During the Liberian Civil War, illegal logging flourished, but led to sanctions against the timber industry.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/on-our-radar-war-torn-liberia-signs-timber-deal-with-e-u/', 'snippet': 'During the Liberian Civil War, illegal logging flourished, but led to sanctions against the timber industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liberia, home to 45 percent of the rain forests in West Africa, signs a deal with the European Union to prevent illegal timber exports and develop a sustainable forestry industry. Illegal logging flourished during the country’s long civil war but led to crippling sanctions against the timber industry. [BBC]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: War-Torn Liberia Signs Timber Deal with E.U.', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T20:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/082341a6-ccee-501c-b9e3-d74c2b462ac3', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/082341a6-ccee-501c-b9e3-d74c2b462ac3'}, {'abstract': 'Gala NYC, a new series of classical music without borders, opened on Saturday at the Brooklyn Lyceum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/arts/music/gala-nyc-at-brooklyn-lyceum-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gala NYC, a new series of classical music without borders, opened on Saturday at the Brooklyn Lyceum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The border-hopping proclivities of classical composers and performers have become more pronounced in recent years, resulting in a freewheeling blend of genres and styles. Gala NYC, a new series (the name means Global Art, Local Audience) founded by Mike Block, a Juilliard-trained cellist and disciple of Yo-Yo Ma and the Silk Road Project, aims to promote this healthy eclecticism by combining performers from varying disciplines. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genres and Styles Without Borders, in a Brooklyn Series', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genres and Styles Without Borders, in a Brooklyn Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T20:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/576d706d-5398-5a2b-bd4a-9ceca35314d8', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/576d706d-5398-5a2b-bd4a-9ceca35314d8'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Drama Critics’ Circle awarded best play to “Good People,” by David Lindsay-Abaire, and best musical to “The Book of Mormon.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/deliberative-theater-critics-honor-good-people/', 'snippet': 'The New York Drama Critics’ Circle awarded best play to “Good People,” by David Lindsay-Abaire, and best musical to “The Book of Mormon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York theater critics had an awfully hard time on Monday selecting the best play of the year for their annual award. Four rounds of balloting by the New York Drama Critics’ Circle revealed strong preferences for three Broadway plays that have also been nominated for this year’s Tony Award for best play — “Good People,” “Jerusalem,” and “The ____________ with the Hat.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deliberative Theater Critics Honor ‘Good People’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butterworth, Jez', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Larry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindsay-Abaire, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rylance, Mark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Drama Critics Circle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T21:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b68689-a716-5e9d-a0db-503ded91c553', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b68689-a716-5e9d-a0db-503ded91c553'}, {'abstract': 'The chamber group Concertante performed at Merkin Hall on Monday, with replacement musicians sitting in for four of its six members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/arts/music/concertante-with-pinch-hitters-at-merkin-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The chamber group Concertante performed at Merkin Hall on Monday, with replacement musicians sitting in for four of its six members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The effect that substitute players can have on an ensemble’s character probably varies according to the size of the group in question. Orchestras use subs on a regular basis, sometimes for extended periods, with no great impact on corporate identity. But for full-time chamber groups, consistent chemistry is a key attribute. It would be hard to imagine a prominent string quartet, for instance, soldiering on for more than a few outings with a pinch-hitter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/concert/concert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/concert/concert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/concert/concert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Sextet’s Substitutes, a Chemistry Test', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Sextet’s Substitutes, a Chemistry Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Concertante', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merkin Concert Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T21:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/99895eee-022e-5f9f-9c83-2609003e3a94', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99895eee-022e-5f9f-9c83-2609003e3a94'}, {'abstract': 'At its developers conference in San Francisco, Google addressed criticism that its Android operating system has not been open enough, and announced a new operating system for cellphones, tablets and TVs.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/google-plans-to-streamline-android/', 'snippet': 'At its developers conference in San Francisco, Google addressed criticism that its Android operating system has not been open enough, and announced a new operating system for cellphones, tablets and TVs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Android phones have been a runaway success for Google — perhaps too runaway. Now Google is trying to add some order to the craziness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Plans to Streamline Android', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-10T21:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/907ddd81-aabd-5e06-be92-50aec98beb8d', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/907ddd81-aabd-5e06-be92-50aec98beb8d'}, {'abstract': 'The tenor Ian Bostridge leads a tour of 18th-century arias and voices with the Montreal ensemble Les Violons du Roy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/arts/music/les-violons-du-roy-with-ian-bostridge-review.html', 'snippet': 'The tenor Ian Bostridge leads a tour of 18th-century arias and voices with the Montreal ensemble Les Violons du Roy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Les Violons du Roy, a Quebec  ensemble led by Bernard Labadie, has a broad repertory that includes Romantic and contemporary works. But the ensemble is best known for its zesty performances of Baroque and Classical music, performed on modern instruments, and it played to its strengths on Sunday evening at Zankel Hall in a program devoted to Handel and his contemporaries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/ROY/ROY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/ROY/ROY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/ROY/ROY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/ROY/ROY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/arts/ROY/ROY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Tenor, Three Voices, in Arias From Handel’s Era', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Tenor, Three Voices, In Arias From Handel’s Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bostridge, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Labadie, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 