Tuesday in a British parliamentary inquiry into corruption at the highest levels of soccer.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/10/top-fifa-officials-are-named-in-bribery-investigation/', 'snippet': 'Jeré Longman writes about the testimony Tuesday in a British parliamentary inquiry into corruption at the highest levels of soccer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeré Longman writes about the testimony Tuesday in a British parliamentary inquiry into corruption at the highest levels of soccer. A former F.A. president and one-time leader of England’s failed World Cup bid, David Triesman, accused four top FIFA officials of soliciting bribes for their votes in bidding to host the World Cup. Read the article here, and come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top FIFA Officials Are Named in Bribery Investigation', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Triesman, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T01:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2994bcaf-69ae-53b6-8ac4-2a7153d9ae73', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2994bcaf-69ae-53b6-8ac4-2a7153d9ae73'}, {'abstract': 'A strong vow is made to move forward on immigration reform. But to make progress, he will have to do a lot more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/opinion/11wed1.html', 'snippet': 'A strong vow is made to move forward on immigration reform. But to make progress, he will have to do a lot more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama went to the border in El Paso on Tuesday and delivered a speech on immigration reform. He didn’t present a bill or issue any executive orders or set deadlines for action. Aides say his goal was to “create a pathway” and “a sense of urgency” to “move forward.” That is a start but not nearly enough. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama at the Border', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama at the Border: A strong vow to move forward on immigration reform, but no plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T01:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/579d01e7-b5a9-507d-bd34-ba2460ebcc64', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/579d01e7-b5a9-507d-bd34-ba2460ebcc64'}, {'abstract': 'Triple Five Group of Canada plans to invest $1 billion in American Dream@Meadowlands in New Jersey, hoping to replicate its success at the Mall of America in Minnesota.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/realestate/commercial/ghermezians-hope-to-bring-mall-of-america-magic-to-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'Triple Five Group of Canada plans to invest $1 billion in American Dream@Meadowlands in New Jersey, hoping to replicate its success at the Mall of America in Minnesota.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Ghermezian brothers, immigrants from Iran who had settled in western Canada, wanted to build the largest shopping center in the United States a quarter-century ago, they shipped a submarine that had been custom-built for them in Vancouver — and was an offbeat attraction at their mall in Edmonton — to Bloomington, Minn., and parked it in front of City Hall. Their company, Triple Five, won the development rights for what would become the Mall of America.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/business/Ghermezian1/Ghermezian1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/business/Ghermezian1/Ghermezian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/business/Ghermezian1/Ghermezian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Mall of America Magic to New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Square Feet', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bringing the Mall of America Magic to New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping Centers and Malls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Triple Five Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Meadowlands Xanadu (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T01:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terry Pristin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pristin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '