3, Royals 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Crucial Moment, Rodriguez Delivers for the Yankees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Royals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T02:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdb22c0a-5224-52a7-bc0d-a9bfe37cd52a', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb22c0a-5224-52a7-bc0d-a9bfe37cd52a'}, {'abstract': 'The spread of the disease since the 2010 earthquake is a reminder of the help that Haiti still needs and the consequences of continued neglect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/opinion/11wed3.html', 'snippet': 'The spread of the disease since the 2010 earthquake is a reminder of the help that Haiti still needs and the consequences of continued neglect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A United Nations report on the cholera outbreak that has sickened 300,000 Haitians since last fall, killing nearly 5,000, finds evidence to suggest that the disease may have originated at a United Nations military camp north of the capital, which spilled raw sewage into a tributary of the Artibonite River. The epidemic was able to spread so far only because of the chronic and horrible deficiencies in Haiti’s sanitation and health care systems, which long predate the 2010 earthquake. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti’s Continuing Cholera Outbreak', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti’s Continuing Cholera Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T02:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b05ff0f-8b11-5eef-8571-dff4a69862ad', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b05ff0f-8b11-5eef-8571-dff4a69862ad'}, {'abstract': 'Republican leaders called the changes modernization, while environmentalists called them a throwback to the 1970s and ’80s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/science/earth/11florida.html', 'snippet': 'Republican leaders called the changes modernization, while environmentalists called them a throwback to the 1970s and ’80s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Just before the Republican-led Florida Legislature finished up its session for the year, it gave developers a parting gift: It pushed through measures that would reverse 25 years of growth management law by loosening state oversight of builders and making it harder for people to challenge development. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/us/FLORIDA-1/FLORIDA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 898, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Legislature Votes to Ease Rules on Development', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida Legislature Votes to Ease Rules on Development', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T02:37:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f770c1-9fc4-55eb-b65a-81b3b80fc160', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f770c1-9fc4-55eb-b65a-81b3b80fc160'}, {'abstract': 'If the State Supreme Court calls for New Jersey to fund education, Mr. Christie will have to comply.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/opinion/11wed4.html', 'snippet': 'If the State Supreme Court calls for New Jersey to fund education, Mr. Christie will have to comply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey prides himself on his bluster and relishes the attention it garners in conservative circles beyond the state. He jumped the shark last month, suggesting he might defy the State Supreme Court if it orders him to make up a $1.6 billion shortfall of education financing that disproportionately punishes poorer districts and their students. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even for Gov. Christie, This One’s a Stretch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even for Gov. Christie, This One’s a Stretch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T02:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b49d8209-fd2b-579d-9a7e-5f61f7df74a2', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b49d8209-fd2b-579d-9a7e-5f61f7df74a2'}, {'abstract': 'The purchase has potential advantages, but Microsoft has a poor record on mergers and acquisitions and is paying a high price.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/business/11views.html', 'snippet': 'The purchase has potential advantages, but Microsoft has a poor record on mergers and acquisitions and is paying a high price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Microsoft has only recently embraced the Internet cloud. But from the perspective of its shareholders, that’s certainly where its $8.5 billion deal to buy Skype belongs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skype Deal Is Unlikely to P