yt://article/65cae9a1-74fc-506e-b12d-26bc5967c68d', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65cae9a1-74fc-506e-b12d-26bc5967c68d'}, {'abstract': 'A relic of Mumbai’s prohibition, some of which is still on the books, are so-called “permit rooms.” Here is a selection for the intrepid imbiber.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/a-drinkers-guide-to-mumbais-permit-rooms/', 'snippet': 'A relic of Mumbai’s prohibition, some of which is still on the books, are so-called “permit rooms.” Here is a selection for the intrepid imbiber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Considering Mumbai’s reputation as India’s night-life capital, it is something of an anomaly that the city is still technically under prohibition. Imposed by the state government shortly after India achieved Independence, prohibition has been gradually eased over the years but was never completely lifted. One of the remaining constraints is that anyone attempting to purchase or consume alcohol must obtain a “permit” declaring that they “continue to require foreign liquor and country liquor for preservation and maintenance of my health.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Drinker’s Guide to Mumbai’s ‘Permit Rooms’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T10:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leo Mirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6309c02-c75f-573f-bd17-2fac09b89a22', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6309c02-c75f-573f-bd17-2fac09b89a