ame': 'Celia', 'middlename': 'Watson', 'lastname': 'Seupel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/901a3d30-cc4d-5506-9dc0-b7ea86f4ad8b', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/901a3d30-cc4d-5506-9dc0-b7ea86f4ad8b'}, {'abstract': 'The lawyer of three Americans charged with espionage and illegal entry in Iran almost two years ago protested the delay on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/world/middleeast/12iran.html', 'snippet': 'The lawyer of three Americans charged with espionage and illegal entry in Iran almost two years ago protested the delay on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The trial of three Americans charged with espionage and illegal entry in Iran after their arrest almost two years ago near the border with Iraqi Kurdistan failed to resume in Tehran on Wednesday, and their Iranian lawyer said he had formally protested the delay.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial of American Hikers Charged With Espionage in Iran Is Unexpectedly Delayed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial of American Hikers Charged With Espionage in Iran Is Unexpectedly Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T11:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fcec504-3217-5330-b1d1-6e954bd6c734', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fcec504-3217-5330-b1d1-6e954bd6c734'}, {'abstract': 'Not happy with the U.S. exporting inflation to the rest of the world? Tough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/paul-krugman-how-the-financial-crisis-was-wasted.html', 'snippet': 'Not happy with the U.S. exporting inflation to the rest of the world? Tough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a way, I miss the months that followed Lehman’s failure. O.K., not really — but if it was a time of terror, it was also a time of clarity. The whole world was going to hell in a handbasket, and policy makers everywhere shared a common goal: stopping the plunge.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation and Economic Hooliganism', 'kicker': 'First', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ON ECONOMIC HOOLIGANISM', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f52bb3-21cb-5699-8e7e-342d50ff5eeb', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f52bb3-21cb-5699-8e7e-342d50ff5eeb'}, {'abstract': 'As economic uncertainty ignites the market for the most primitive form of wealth, a good old-fashioned gold rush is back on. A prospector’s tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15Gold-t.html', 'snippet': 'As economic uncertainty ignites the market for the most primitive form of wealth, a good old-fashioned gold rush is back on. A prospector’s tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first met Shawn Ryan and Cathy Wood, in 2005, they were living with their two young children in a small cabin outside Dawson City, at the northernmost end of the paved road system in Canada’s Yukon Territory. It was a beautiful site in the summertime, with clear water lapping the banks of the Klondike River and the sky still bright at midnight. But the sun hit their roof for the last time each year in early December and didn’t show up again for six weeks. Temperatures in the dead of winter could reach 50 below zero. Wood sometimes feared that their children would freeze. Back then Ryan and Wood already knew they had found gold, but they didn’t have proof.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/magazine/16gold-span/16gold-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/16/magazine/16gold-span/16gold-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/magazine/16gold-span/16gold-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/magazine/16gold-span/16gold-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/magazine/16gold-span/16gold-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gold Mania in the Yukon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘People Have Been Looking For This For 100 Years’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yukon Territory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Wolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e82304-5bf9-514d-8baa-620fcaa0d1e6', 'word_count': 6417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e82304-5bf9-514d-8baa-620fcaa0d1e6'}, {'abstract': 'The American International Group and the Treasury Department will sell roughly 300 million shares, in the insurer’s latest step toward regaining its independence from the government.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/a-i-g-lays-out-plan-for-share-sale/', 'snippet': 'The American International Group and the Treasury Department will sell roughly 300 million shares, in the insurer’s latest step toward regaining its independence from the government.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A.I.G. Outlines Share Sale Plan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:03:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c63a7c9-f55b-547e-b60c-d64781a0e7c1', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c63a7c9-f55b-547e-b60c-d64781a0e7c1'}, {'abstract': 'Woody Allen will attend the opening of the Cannes Film Festival, when his movie “Midnight in Paris” has its debut.  But one of his actors, Carla Bruni-Sarkozy, the first lady of France, will not attend.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/woody-allen-headlines-cannes-guest-list/', 'snippet': 'Woody Allen will attend the opening of the Cannes Film Festival, when his movie “Midnight in Paris” has its debut.  But one of his actors, Carla Bruni-Sarkozy, the first lady of France, will not attend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — As the film world and its attendant paparazzi and army of scribes descend upon the 64th Cannes Film Festival that begins today and runs through May 22, the French media has mused less about the plot of the opening film, Woody Allen’s “Midnight in Paris,” than over whether one of its cast members, Carla Bruni-Sarkozy, the first lady of France, would be one of those descending.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woody Allen Headlines Cannes Guest List', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAdams, Rachel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Carla', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Owen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9537add1-4750-5cce-8649-7cdbba0cfe31', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9537add1-4750-5cce-8649-7cdbba0cfe31'}, {'abstract': 'The former Mets clubhouse manager Charlie Samuels, 53, was charged Wednesday in connection with the theft of nearly $2.3 million in team equipment and memorabilia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/sports/baseball/arrest-of-mets-clubhouse-manager-to-be-announced.html', 'snippet': 'The former Mets clubhouse manager Charlie Samuels, 53, was charged Wednesday in connection with the theft of nearly $2.3 million in team equipment and memorabilia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Mets clubhouse manager Charlie Samuels was charged Wednesday in connection with the theft of nearly $2.3 million worth of team equipment and memorabilia — from hats, bats and balls to a full set of autographed 1986 World Series uniforms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/SUB-SAMUELS/SUB-SAMUELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/SUB-SAMUELS/SUB-SAMUELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/SUB-SAMUELS/SUB-SAMUELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Mets Employee Charged in Theft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Mets Employee Charged in Theft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuels, Charlie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:12:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By William K. Rashbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6552439b-8af4-5e84-b162-32347c22c862', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6552439b-8af4-5e84-b162-32347c22c862'}, {'abstract': 'David Chang replaces Momofuku Ssam Bar’s lunch service with an all-duck menu in the former Milk Bar space, which will also serve as a waiting area, with beer and cocktails, for dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/53863/', 'snippet': 'David Chang replaces Momofuku Ssam Bar’s lunch service with an all-duck menu in the former Milk Bar space, which will also serve as a waiting area, with beer and cocktails, for dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each of David Chang’s restaurant is a different animal, it seems. Momofuku Ssam Bar has a whole pork butt, Momofuku Noodle Bar serves a mountain of fried chicken, and Má Pêche does beef seven ways.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Duck Starts Here', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b5b9846-fbe2-5be5-830a-e086fb33f519', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5b9846-fbe2-5be5-830a-e086fb33f519'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Through a free service called PLAN, text messages will warn everyone of disaster. But what about people who are in the subway or the theater, or have really old mobile phones?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/duck-and-cover-and-check-your-cellphone/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Through a free service called PLAN, text messages will warn everyone of disaster. But what about people who are in the subway or the theater, or have really old mobile phones?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those of us old enough to remember “I Love Lucy” when it was a hot new thing on television are also old enough to remember civil defense drills that had us ducking under our desks at school. Received wisdom back then seemed to be that if the Russians ever dropped the big one, the desks would keep us from being vaporized like soldiers in the original “The Day the Earth Stood Still.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duck and Cover and Check Your Cellphone', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/63cc2dbf-bdcc-5242-aeb4-b8c056c1e8d4', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63cc2dbf-bdcc-5242-aeb4-b8c056c1e8d4'}, {'abstract': 'Karl Lagerfeld tells WWD about his latest project.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/quote-unquote-the-will-to-power-indeed/', 'snippet': 'Karl Lagerfeld tells WWD about his latest project.', 'lead_paragraph': '-Karl Lagerfeld tells WWD about his latest project: publishing the complete writings of Friedrich Nietzsche. Easy is totally a word I would use to describe Nietzsche’s writing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quote Unquote | The Will to Power Indeed', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T12:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Leon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/279d1437-1536-5d49-9489-5f3a3372cca7', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279d1437-1536-5d49-9489-5f3a3372cca7'}, {'abstract': 'Several recent restoration projects, both well financed and small-scale, are bringing a sense of localism back to the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/venice-reclaimed/', 'snippet': 'Several recent restoration projects, both well financed and small-scale, are bringing a sense of localism back to the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The common refrain about Venice, besides that it’s sinking, is that it is no longer a city for Venetians. The native population is declining (as is most of Italy’s), replaced by some 20 million tourists a year. But several recent restoration projects, both well financed and small-scale, are bringing a sense of localism back to the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Reclaimed', 