{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zandi, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T13:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d5c824c-b483-52e2-afd9-ee27af3b9746', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d5c824c-b483-52e2-afd9-ee27af3b9746'}, {'abstract': 'Antipsychotic drugs are overused in nursing homes, F.D.A. orders study of metal hip failures, a $100 weekend in Rio and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/wednesday-reading-antipsychotic-drugs-overused-in-nursing-homes/', 'snippet': 'Antipsychotic drugs are overused in nursing homes, F.D.A. orders study of metal hip failures, a $100 weekend in Rio and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Antipsychotic Drugs Overused in Nursing Homes', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T13:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c1a38b-4887-5909-9079-8add57dd1902', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c1a38b-4887-5909-9079-8add57dd1902'}, {'abstract': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel said in a newspaper interview that Mario Draghi embodies German ideas about economic stability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/business/global/12draghi.html', 'snippet': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel said in a newspaper interview that Mario Draghi embodies German ideas about economic stability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Germany moved Wednesday to reassure financial markets by supporting Mario Draghi as the next president of the European Central Bank, virtually assuring him of the job, but offered no quick end to uncertainty over the continuing Greek and Irish debt crises.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/business/subDraghi/subDraghi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/business/subDraghi/subDraghi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/business/subDraghi/subDraghi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merkel Signals Support for Italian to Lead E.C.B.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merkel Clears Way for Italian to Lead the European Central Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T13:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36e3c8eb-88ac-5735-90ec-c225a915ecb8', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36e3c8eb-88ac-5735-90ec-c225a915ecb8'}, {'abstract': 'The Tea Party Express, whose money and endorsements proved key to the victories of several Senate candidates in 2010, will back Jon Bruning, currently Nebraska’s attorney general, in his bid to unseat Senator Ben Nelson, a Democrat.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/tea-party-express-to-endorse-nelson-rival-in-nebraska/', 'snippet': 'The Tea Party Express, whose money and endorsements proved key to the victories of several Senate candidates in 2010, will back Jon Bruning, currently Nebraska’s attorney general, in his bid to unseat Senator Ben Nelson, a Democrat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tea Party Express, whose money and endorsements proved key to the victories of several Senate candidates in 2010, has made its first endorsement for 2012, backing Jon Bruning, a Republican who serves as Nebraska’s attorney general, in his bid to unseat Senator Ben Nelson, a Democrat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tea Party Express Endorses Nelson Rival in Nebraska', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T13:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {