bject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T14:25:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f92a3b9a-3e0b-5af2-a304-9e4430b30f70', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f92a3b9a-3e0b-5af2-a304-9e4430b30f70'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor was faulted by New Yorkers for his handling of the schools, in the poll by Quinnipiac University; they also said he had lost focus in his third term.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/bloomberg-given-poor-marks-in-new-poll/', 'snippet': 'The mayor was faulted by New Yorkers for his handling of the schools, in the poll by Quinnipiac University; they also said he had lost focus in his third term.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the schools, stupid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Given Poor Marks in New Poll', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T14:26:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/27b0b2f7-d0b9-5c10-a74f-57e478b32e0d', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27b0b2f7-d0b9-5c10-a74f-57e478b32e0d'}, {'abstract': 'The city’s 18th-century streets are home to superb coffee, pulled by baristas who are tremendously skilled and disarmingly sweet-natured.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/ristretto-in-philadelphia/', 'snippet': 'The city’s 18th-century streets are home to superb coffee, pulled by baristas who are tremendously skilled and disarmingly sweet-natured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philadelphia has plenty going for it: the best four-man rotation in baseball, art worth fighting over, a ruin so elegant and haunting it feels like Berlin. It also has superb coffee. Recently, I went on a coffee crawl that took me to a handful of shops where the baristas aren’t just tremendously skilled, they’re disarmingly sweet-natured. I found an energetic scene thriving outside the gravitational pull of the hometown giant La Colombe Torrefaction. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | In Philadelphia', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T14:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/194ccc99-e21d-5ca9-ba99-1820c94981d8', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/194ccc99-e21d-5ca9-ba99-1820c94981d8'}, {'abstract': 'New York State does well in tracking the on-time performance of different transit options and greenhouse gas emissions, a study finds, but it lags in measuring the availability of options for seniors and the disabled.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/a-report-card-on-transportation-spending/', 'snippet': 'New York State does well in tracking the on-time performance of different transit options and greenhouse gas emissions, a study finds, but it lags in measuring the availability of options for seniors and the disabled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study that examined how states account for billions of dollars spent annually on transportation found that most are not tracking how their investments are performing in six important areas, among them mitigating the effects of transportation on the environment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Report Card on Transportation Spending', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Center on the States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T14:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/43265330-a57c-5e37-bea6-d5b4d991ad93', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43265330-a57c-5e37-bea6-d5b4d991ad93'}, {'abstract': 'Bel Kaufman, the granddaughter of the great Yiddish storyteller Sholem Aleichem, taught a course on Jewish humor this year at Hunter College, where she graduated in 1934.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/nyregion/bel-kaufman-at-100-still-a-teacher-and-a-jokester.html', 'snippet': 'Bel Kaufman, the granddaughter of the great Yiddish storyteller Sholem Aleichem, taught a course on Jewish humor this year at Hunter College, where she graduated in 1934.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Bel Kaufman sits you down on her sofa and asks, “Are you comfortable?” the right answer, she reminds you, requires a Yiddish inflection, a shrug and the words, “I make a living.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/KAUFMAN1/KAUFMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/KAUFMAN1/KAUFMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/KAUFMAN1/KAUFMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/KAUFMAN1/KAUFMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/KAUFMAN1/KAUFMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At 100, Still a Teacher, and Quite a Character', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At 100, Still a Teacher, And Quite a Character', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufman, Bel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALEICHEM, SHOLEM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hunter College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank':