: 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T16:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c369da-de99-5f4d-bac3-ef1f380f0ae4', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c369da-de99-5f4d-bac3-ef1f380f0ae4'}, {'abstract': 'The artist on being a cultural worker in a late-capitalist economy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/the-lowdown-a-l-steiner/', 'snippet': 'The artist on being a cultural worker in a late-capitalist economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A. L. Steiner is as well known for her thought-provoking and politically charged work as she is for her witty art world mischief. Sharp of tongue and nimble of mind, Steiner often touches on feminist, sometimes lesbian themes, and she is never afraid to court controversy. Steiner’s critically acclaimed installation at last summer’s Greater New York show at MoMA P.S.1 featured a vast collage of images of naked women, nature and beaten body parts, in a somehow celebratory homage to queer culture. She recently completed a film — she likes to call it a “sociosexual” video, but the more usual term is “porno” — in collaboration with the artist A. K. Burns. Titled “Community Action Center,” the film explores queer sexuality and runs an almost impossibly hilarious 69 minutes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lowdown | A. L. Steiner', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T16:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e7d36ab-ca57-53f5-b2cc-5100d705fa22', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e7d36ab-ca57-53f5-b2cc-5100d705fa22'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Lopez’s role as a judge on “American Idol” did not seem to significantly help sales of her new album, which made its debut at No. 5 on the Billboard 200 chart.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/love-some-for-jennifer-lopez-but-more-for-beastie-boys-and-fleet-foxes/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Lopez’s role as a judge on “American Idol” did not seem to significantly help sales of her new album, which made its debut at No. 5 on the Billboard 200 chart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Lopez has had a prime television role as a judge on “American Idol” and plenty of airtime to promote her new album, “Love?” But it wasn’t enough for her to top new releases from the Beastie Boys and Fleet Foxes on this week’s Billboard 200 albums chart, Billboard reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Love? Some for Jennifer Lopez, but More for Beastie Boys and Fleet Foxes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sade', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sixx, Nikki', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soulchild, Musiq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beastie Boys', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fleet Foxes (Music Group)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mumford & Sons', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T16:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/385d1478-ae98-52d2-93d8-a5ed38540c93', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/385d1478-ae98-52d2-93d8-a5ed38540c93'}, {'abstract': 'Denver’s running game was poor, and the defense gave up too many big plays.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/2010-broncos-what-the-film-revealed/', 'snippet': 'Denver’s running game was poor, and the defense gave up too many big plays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we wonder whether there will be a 2011 season, this is part of a series looking back at the 2010 season, with the benefit of film analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2010 Broncos: What the Film Revealed', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T16:23:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b07e6423-d51f-591b-a56a-042162f69fd4', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b07e6423-d51f-591b-a56a-042162f69fd4'}, {'abstract': 'Two men from a Charlotte, N.C., swim club will go head to head Thursday to see which will compete at the world championships in the 50-meter freestyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/sports/swim-off-takes-toll-on-teammates-jones-and-schneider.html', 'snippet': 'Two men from a Charlotte, N.C., swim club will go head to head Thursday to see which will compete at the world championships in the 50-meter freestyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — For nine months, Cullen Jones and Josh Schneider have been training side by side for a 22-second duel. Their 50-meter freestyle swim-off Thursday is the sport’s version of musical chairs: when the clock stops, one of them will not have a seat on the plane to the world championships in Shanghai. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/12swimmerspix/12swimmerspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/12swimmerspix/12swimmerspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/12swimmerspix/12swimmerspix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/12swimmerspix/12swimmerspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/12swimmerspix/12swimmerspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 't