tical rhetoric” when it comes to their proposal on Medicare — even while admitting that their party took similar  liberties during the health care debate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/republicans-decry-tactics-the-party-used-in-200/', 'snippet': 'Republican freshmen in the House want Democrats to stop the “political rhetoric” when it comes to their proposal on Medicare — even while admitting that their party took similar  liberties during the health care debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, it’s true, Republican House freshmen say, our party did help storm town-hall-style meetings to protest changes in the Medicare plan during the debate over the health care overhaul. But they would appreciate it if Democrats did not take that page from their playbook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Decry Tactics the Party Used in 2009', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:16:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a36484-2757-5f09-8682-70868b3225c6', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a36484-2757-5f09-8682-70868b3225c6'}, {'abstract': 'A plan calls for the Metropolitan Museum to showcase its modern holdings at the site for at least eight years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/arts/design/the-met-to-take-over-whitneys-breuer-building.html', 'snippet': 'A plan calls for the Metropolitan Museum to showcase its modern holdings at the site for at least eight years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art will take over the Whitney Museum of American Art’s Marcel Breuer building in 2015, when the Whitney opens its new museum in Manhattan’s meatpacking district, according to the terms of a real estate agreement that the museum boards are pursuing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/jp-museum-1/jp-museum-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Plans to Occupy the Whitney’s Uptown Site', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Met Plans to Occupy the Whitney’s Uptown Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5405ce88-6e5a-55e5-a31f-6bec5d8e6a82', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5405ce88-6e5a-55e5-a31f-6bec5d8e6a82'}, {'abstract': 'A locavore’s food tour of Toronto.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/another-pre-dawn-flight/', 'snippet': 'A locavore’s food tour of Toronto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the hotel clerk recommended that I set my alarm at 3 a.m. for my 6:15 a.m. flight to Miami, I gasped. Why is it that arrangements that seemed so reasonable a month ago are now horrifying? Maybe I should just cancel, spend an extra day in Canada, tour a cattle farm, chill? But no: The Florida trip is important, and so there I was, dutifully, in a cab at 4 a.m., to join a couple of hundred other bleary-eyed travelers on a long customs line that lasted until 4:45 a.m. (or maybe it was 5 a.m.? Who can remember, even only a couple of hours later) and led to a series of steel shutters. The customs officers were not as eager as the rest of us. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Pre-Dawn Flight', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:26:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/66274d57-acdc-5997-8c6d-c28154473cd7', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66274d57-acdc-5997-8c6d-c28154473cd7'}, {'abstract': 'If Violet’s injuries are too serious to be treated on-site, she and her hatchling will be removed to the Bronx Zoo. An expert said that if that happens, the hatchling could never survive in the wild.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/hawk-cam-rescue-of-violet-planned-for-thursday/', 'snippet': 'If Violet’s injuries are too serious to be treated on-site, she and her hatchling will be removed to the Bronx Zoo. An expert said that if that happens, the hatchling could never survive in the wild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:33 p.m. | Help is on the way for Violet the red-tailed hawk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Rescue of Violet Is Planned for Thursday', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department of Environmental Conservation (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:26:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/934c873a-49b1-56a9-a8df-5221a75b7dbb', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934c873a-49b1-56a9-a8df-5221a75b7dbb'}, {'abstract': 'Now that the Royals have finally tied the knot we can focus on the real trend at hand: black diamond rings.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/black-is-the-new-blue/', 'snippet': 'Now that the Royals have finally tied the knot we can focus on the real trend at hand: black diamond rings.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#729", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black is the New Blue', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kavitha Surana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kavitha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Surana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7ac4e10-10b3-59ee-aa49-9b9b65bf9054', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7ac4e10-10b3-59ee-aa49-9b9b65bf9054'}, {'abstract': '“The New Girl,” a comedy starring Zooey Deschanel, is among the new programs that Fox will add to its fall schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/the-new-girl-in-chicago-code-and-lie-to-me-out-at-fox/', 'snippet': '“The New Girl,” a comedy starring Zooey Deschanel, is among the new programs that Fox will add to its fall schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of Zooey Deschanel, the star of “(500) Days of Summer” and lead singer of the band She & Him, will have something to look forward to on Fox’s fall season: she is set to star in “The New Girl,” a new comedy that the network plans to announce next week. And fans of the Fox shows “Lie to Me,” “The Chicago Code,” “Human Target,” “Breaking In” and “Traffic Light” will have more free time on their schedules: the network has canceled those series. Brian Stelter has more at Media Decoder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The New Girl’ Is in, ‘Chicago Code’ and ‘Lie to Me’ Are Out at Fox', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deschanel, Zooey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/de65c2d6-64b5-5cf4-b23a-5b8ad1f15acb', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de65c2d6-64b5-5cf4-b23a-5b8ad1f15acb'}, {'abstract': 'A British journalist who entered Syria posing as a tourist described his brief detention in the city of Homs in several interviews on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/reporter-witnessed-mass-arrests-in-syria/', 'snippet': 'A British journalist who entered Syria posing as a tourist described his brief detention in the city of Homs in several interviews on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Anthony Shadid reports, Syrian activists claim that the country’s security forces shelled the city of Homs on Wednesday and detained hundreds of people suspected of supporting protests. According to human rights groups, more than 10,000 people have been taken into custody in recent weeks, during a crackdown by the Syrian government on dissent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reporter Witnessed Mass Arrests in Syria', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T17:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b92cdd4-8ee4-5be0-9c32-1376b5325066', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b92cdd4-8ee4-5be0-9c32-1376b5325066'}, {'abstract': '“Grandma’s Wedding Album” depicts an album within a book; “A Photo for Greta” is about a bunny whose father is a photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/books/review/kids-and-cameras.html', 'snippet': '“Grandma’s Wedding Album” depicts an album within a book; “A Photo for Greta” is about a bunny whose father is a photographer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any parent who finds the time to cobble together an actual photo album these days knows how children love flipping through them — especially baby books and wedding albums. Good reason to take note of two heartfelt and personal picture books about family photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/books/review/11childrens-review-1/12childrens-review-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 239, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/11/books/review/11childrens-review-1/12childrens-review-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 239}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/books/review/11childrens-review-1/11childrens-review-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/books/review/11childrens-review-1/12childrens-review-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/books/review/11childrens-review-1/12childrens-review-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids and Cameras', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None,