roblems in the Rearview Mirror', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Constellation Energy Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Valley Authority', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toms River (NJ)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/24b4cba4-29f7-56b2-b3f5-441956849c47', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24b4cba4-29f7-56b2-b3f5-441956849c47'}, {'abstract': 'Some 50 Impressionist and Post-Impressionist French paintings from the National Gallery, one of the finest such collections in the world, are drawing a lot of attention at the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/national-gallery-treasures-making-a-splash-in-texas/', 'snippet': 'Some 50 Impressionist and Post-Impressionist French paintings from the National Gallery, one of the finest such collections in the world, are drawing a lot of attention at the Museum of Fine Arts, Houston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Vincent van Gogh’s self-portrait from 1889, the haunting oil on canvas of the troubled artist looking sallow in a blue smock, rarely travels from its home at the National Gallery of Art in Washington, D.C. Neither does Claude Monet’s “Japanese Footbridge” or Edgar Degas’ “Dancers Backstage.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Gallery Treasures Making a Splash in Texas', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Degas, Edgar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monet, Claude', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Gogh, Vincent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NATIONAL GALLERY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a1dec31-d05b-5f39-b5ee-3e2b8635df4f', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a1dec31-d05b-5f39-b5ee-3e2b8635df4f'}, {'abstract': 'The conviction of Raj Rajaratnam vindicates the aggressive prosecutorial tactics used in his insider trading case, but whether it will produce any meaningful change is unclear.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/prosecutors-hardball-tactics-produce-big-results-in-galleon-case/', 'snippet': 'The conviction of Raj Rajaratnam vindicates the aggressive prosecutorial tactics used in his insider trading case, but whether it will produce any meaningful change is unclear.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:31 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutors Hope Verdict Will Be a Deterrent to Others', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d677c0bd-e2e1-5f6b-bcf4-cfb64e69ae01', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d677c0bd-e2e1-5f6b-bcf4-cfb64e69ae01'}, {'abstract': 'Vashtie Kola, a downtown party hostess, fashion designer and music video director, is a kind of renaissance woman who moves easily among fashion, film and music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/fashion/vashtie-kola-role-model-for-young-tastemakers-up-close.html', 'snippet': 'Vashtie Kola, a downtown party hostess, fashion designer and music video director, is a kind of renaissance woman who moves easily among fashion, film and music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT long ago, Vashtie Kola — a downtown party hostess, fashion designer and music video director — started wearing a chambray shirt, which she would pair with cutoff denim jean shorts and tights. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/Z-UP-CLOSE/Z-UP-CLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Her Cool-Kid Clubhouse', 'kicker': 'Up Close', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Cool-Kid Clubhouse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:03:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Swerdloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swerdloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86cdc7a3-8e50-5a18-8054-3d362773a398', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86cdc7a3-8e50-5a18-8054-3d362773a398'}, {'abstract': 'Standing at the vulnerable fault line between autonomy and dependence.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/when-a-college-student-loses-a-parent/', 'snippet': 'Standing at the vulnerable fault line between autonomy and dependence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lori Eiler-Hunter was a dynamo, a leader, a force. She was the kind of woman who left instructions for her obituary: “In lieu of flowers Lori requested that you read to your children, call your mother, say please and thank you and mind your P’s and Q’s.” When her brain cancer was first diagnosed six years ago, she made it clear she planned to fight hard to hang in for her husband, Art, and their then middle-school-aged children. Statistics said she should never have had those six years, but Lori used them to see Max and Alexandra both get settled into life at college.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a College Student Loses a Parent', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0a6f8fd-d72a-5edb-974b-cfafd1f0ed79', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0a6f8fd-d72a-5edb-974b-cfafd1f0ed79'}, {'abstract': 'Governing Class: A “living wage” bill stirs passions in Albany, but the great vegetable debate is settled amicably.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/heated-debate-on-wages-and-less-so-on-corn/', 'snippet': 'Governing Class: A “living wage” bill stirs passions in Albany, but the great vegetable debate is settled amicably.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One side is accusing the Bloomberg administration of using tactics “straight out of the K.G.B.” The other side has screamed “job killing,” taking a page from the national debate over health care.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heated Debate on Wages, and Less So on Corn', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5aa5e4b9-c8d5-5446-b5f5-4fca7930a091', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5aa5e4b9-c8d5-5446-b5f5-4fca7930a091'}, {'abstract': 'An economic crisis deepened in the former Soviet republic as the Central Bank lifted restrictions on the exchange rate, setting off a collapse of the ruble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/world/europe/12belarus.html', 'snippet': 'An economic crisis deepened in the former Soviet republic as the Central Bank lifted restrictions on the exchange rate, setting off a collapse of the ruble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — An economic crisis in Belarus deepened Wednesday when its currency plunged in value after the Central Bank lifted restrictions on the exchange rate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12belarus/12belarus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12belarus/12belarus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12belarus/12belarus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus Economic Crisis Deepens as Currency Plunges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus Economic Crisis Deepens as Currency Plunges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commonwealth of Independent States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kudrin, Aleksei L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:08:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe73279f-cae5-5e0b-9ec7-8ce9126aabcb', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe73279f-cae5-5e0b-9ec7-8ce9126aabcb'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Spiegelman nearly sold a majority interest in his call center company, Beryl, in 2010, but he abandoned the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/business/smallbusiness/12sbiz.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Spiegelman nearly sold a majority interest in his call center company, Beryl, in 2010, but he abandoned the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many successful entrepreneurs, Paul Spiegelman often refers to his company as his “baby,” and he becomes emotional when he talks about issues relating to succession or the sale of all or part of his company — an opportunity he recently sought out.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/business/smallbusiness/12sbiz-span/12sbiz-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/business/smallbusiness/12sbiz-span/12sbiz-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/business/smallbusiness/12sbiz-span/12sbiz-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why It’s So Difficult for Entrepreneurs to Head for the Exit', 'kicker': 'Conversations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why It’s So Difficult For Entrepreneurs To Head for the Exit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darren Dahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/844cc922-dda1-54da-94aa-4acb3a83f570', 'word_count': 1243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/844cc922-dda1-54da-94aa-4acb3a83f570'}, {'abstract': 'Morning Line for Wednesday, May 11, 2011', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/morning-line-a-loss-in-a-racing-dynasty/', 'snippet': 'Morning Line for Wednesday, May 11, 2011', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday brings news of the death of the 24-year-old jockey Michael Baze. He was found dead in his car on the backside at Churchill Downs on Tuesday. Baze had been the fourth-leading rider at the Oaklawn Park meet, and he had ridden Nehro, the runner-up in the Kentucky Derby, to that horse’s only victory before being replaced. Daily Racing Form reports that “police have undertaken an investigation into the death,” and that an \xa0autopsy will be performed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: A Loss in a Racing Dynasty', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/75897f2d-d541-5314-ad71-8fdf96e33ac6', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75897f2d-d541-5314-ad71-8fdf96e33ac6'}, {'abstract': 'How do you balance finding an exit strategy with maintaining a positive work environment after the sale?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/what-do-you-owe-your-employees-when-you-sell/', 'snippet': 'How do you balance finding an exit strategy with maintaining a positive work environment after the sale?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a small-business conversation  we’ve just published, Paul Spiegelman talks about how he came very close to selling a controlling interest in his company, Beryl, an unusual call center based near Dallas. “I began to get nervous,” Mr. Spiegelman told Darren Dahl. “I felt like if we went down this road, it would have an irreversible negative impact on Beryl’s culture.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do You Owe Your Employees When You Sell?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1fd0b37-da02-56c4-b3f3-eb8b3c33cdf2', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1fd0b37-da02-56c4-b3f3-eb8b3c33cdf2'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya and Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/11/blogs/20110511POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya and Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/blogs/20110511POD-slide-TN6V/20110511POD-slide-TN6V-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Greece and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1a65f999-c05a-5444-943d-ebdca56786f0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1a65f999-c05a-5444-943d-ebdca56786f0'}, {'abstract': 'The Stephen Adly Guirgis play about the intertwined lives of a former drug dealer struggling with sobriety, his girlfriend and his sponsor will play through July 17.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/hat-with-chris-rock-extends-its-broadway-run/', 'snippet': 'The Stephen Adly Guirgis play about the intertwined lives of a former drug dealer struggling with sobriety, his girlfriend and his sponsor will play through July 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call your sponsor, hide your distinguishing headwear and find yourself a spot on Cousin Julio’s couch: “The ___________ With the Hat” is extending its run on Broadway. Press representatives for that Stephen Adly Guirgis play, about the intertwined lives of a former drug dealer struggling with sobriety, his girlfriend, his cousin, his sponsor and the sponsor’s wife, said that it will play at the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater through July 17; it was previously scheduled to end its run on June 25. While Chris Rock is making his Broadway debut in this dark, dark, dark comedy – did we mention it was dark? – most of the critical praise for the play, which opened on April 11, has been directed at the performances of Bobby Cannavale and Elizabeth Rodriguez. Last week, it was nominated for six Tony Awards, including best play, direction of a play (Anna D. Shapiro), leading actor in a play (Mr. Cannavale), featured actress in a play (Ms. Rodriguez) and featured actor in a play (Yul Vázquez).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Hat,’ With Chris Rock, Extends Its Broadway Run', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c774e45b-4086-51c5-a0b7-5be20549f1d5', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c774e45b-4086-51c5-a0b7-5be20549f1d5'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge decided that a case involving corporate misconduct should not even go to the jury.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/former-glaxo-lawyer-acquitted/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge decided that a case involving corporate misconduct should not even go to the jury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former GlaxoSmithKline lawyer who was indicted last year on charges of making false statements and obstructing a federal investigation into illegal drug marketing was acquitted on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Glaxo Lawyer Acquitted', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Lauren C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GlaxoSmithKline PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/878ffac7-327e-57d7-8d24-c719c8cd48dc', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/878ffac7-327e-57d7-8d24-c719c8cd48dc'}, {'abstract': 'An ambitious summer show features more than 1,000 pieces from 200 painters and sculptors working on the Riviera from 1951 to 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/cote-art-crawl/', 'snippet': 'An ambitious summer show features more than 1,000 pieces from 200 painters and sculptors working on the Riviera from 1951 to 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The days of the ‘easel’ painting are fading,” predicted the American artist Ellsworth Kelly, while living in the French fishing village of Sanary-sur-Mer in the 1950s. As Kelly experimented with color grids, dozens more artists followed suit, kicking off a contemporary art revolution on the Côte d’Azur.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Côte Art Crawl', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By LANIE GOODMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GOODMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 