ph': 'Raj Rajaratnam, the billionaire co-founder of the hedge fund Galleon Group, was found guilty on 14 counts of securities fraud and conspiracy today in federal court in Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/business/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/11/business/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/business/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/business/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict/video-db-rajaratnam-verdict-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guilty Verdict in Galleon Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2cd2a292-517f-599c-9f3e-89b99b44e15e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2cd2a292-517f-599c-9f3e-89b99b44e15e'}, {'abstract': 'The governor said he would not pursue a bill to legalize same-sex marriage unless there were enough votes in the Senate to assure its passage.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/cuomo-wants-more-support-on-same-sex-marriage-bill/', 'snippet': 'The governor said he would not pursue a bill to legalize same-sex marriage unless there were enough votes in the Senate to assure its passage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — In a suggestion of the uncertain odds surrounding the push to legalize same-sex marriage in New York, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo said Wednesday that he would hold off introducing legislation to allow gay couples to wed until he was confident that the measure would pass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo Wants More Support on Same-Sex Marriage Bill', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Donnell, Daniel J", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:38:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa225b52-e793-538d-8c00-c76b6da403f4', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa225b52-e793-538d-8c00-c76b6da403f4'}, {'abstract': 'So much about the race in New York’s 26th Congressional District this month is anomalous that the outcome is unlikely to tell us much of use about the broader political tides — though it will surely be spun that way anyhow.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/a-special-election-may-be-a-special-case/', 'snippet': 'So much about the race in New York’s 26th Congressional District this month is anomalous that the outcome is unlikely to tell us much of use about the broader political tides — though it will surely be spun that way anyhow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m generally skeptical about the predictive value of special elections. They occur, by definition, under special circumstances — after a Congressman has died or left office unexpectedly. There may be unusual rules for nominating candidates; turnout is usually low; and they occur in isolation. Any one race can only tell you so much about the mood of the country, since there are always idiosyncrasies related both to the candidates and the district.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Special Election May Be a Special Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/08cb3458-b027-5c48-8dbd-9b2bd8be2971', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08cb3458-b027-5c48-8dbd-9b2bd8be2971'}, {'abstract': 'The conviction of Raj Rajaratnam sets the stage for post-trial wrangling and an appeal by the defense that is expected to last at least until next year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/the-galleon-case-is-nowhere-near-over/', 'snippet': 'The conviction of Raj Rajaratnam sets the stage for post-trial wrangling and an appeal by the defense that is expected to last at least until next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the conviction of Raj Rajaratnam on 14 counts of conspiracy and securities fraud, the Galleon Group insider trading case moves to its next phase.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Galleon Case Is Nowhere Near Over', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e960898-accc-542c-bd2c-d534628d55fe', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e960898-accc-542c-bd2c-d534628d55fe'}, {'abstract': 'American publishers have always given away their work in hopes of building up huge audiences that they can sell advertising against. Are they making a mistake in replicating that model on the iPad and other tablets?', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/are-publisher-replicating-the-original-sin-on-digital-platforms/', 'snippet': 'American publishers have always given away their work in hopes of building up huge audiences that they can sell advertising against. Are they making a mistake in replicating that model on the iPad and other tablets?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last few days, there have been a flurry of deals that suggest that a level of détente  between Apple and the Big Three Manhattan publishers (Condé Nast, Time Inc. and Hearst) has finally been reached. For veteran industry watchers, the announcement that Condé had finally agreed to release an iPad version of The New Yorker seemed like the signing of the Salt treaty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the iPad Just a  New Way to Give Away Magazines?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nast, Conde', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T18:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef3b4251-a8c7-5968-b4ae-7b9d2be01498', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef3b4251-a8c7-5968-b4ae-7b9d2be01498'}, {'abstract': 'A four-bedroom condo in a Queen Anne in Princeton, N.J.; a contemporary house in Virginia’s Loudoun Valley; and a 1905 house set on 17 wooded acres in Pine, Colo.', 