dynamic rookie guard Rodrigue Beaubois down the stretch in a potential elimination game against the San Antonio Spurs. At the time, the mistake appeared fatal, as Dallas’ season ended while Beaubois, who had scored 16 points in just 21 minutes in that game, sat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rise of the Mavericks, and the Fall of Beaubois', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlisle, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/75863901-87a3-563e-8312-0715bf2f7406', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75863901-87a3-563e-8312-0715bf2f7406'}, {'abstract': 'Eight of the 24 members of FIFA’s executive committee have been accused of seeking or accepting bribes in return for World Cup votes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/sports/soccer/reform-for-fifa-is-long-overdue.html', 'snippet': 'Eight of the 24 members of FIFA’s executive committee have been accused of seeking or accepting bribes in return for World Cup votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Sepp Blatter could begin reforming soccer with brilliant ideas, like his suggestion that women should wear tighter shorts and lower necklines, he first had to run for president of FIFA in 1998.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/soccer/12onsoccerpic/12onsoccerpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/soccer/12onsoccerpic/12onsoccerpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/soccer/12onsoccerpic/12onsoccerpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'FIFA Develops a Salt Lake City Look, Without Doorknobs', 'kicker': 'On Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'FIFA Develops a Salt Lake City Look, Without Doorknobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2022 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2018 (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22473cec-1438-5b6c-9303-f9a0f7ec98d5', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22473cec-1438-5b6c-9303-f9a0f7ec98d5'}, {'abstract': 'Nine activity ideas and resources for learning about birds.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/on-the-fly-studying-bird-migration-and-behavior/', 'snippet': 'Nine activity ideas and resources for learning about birds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In many parts of the country, it’s the height of spring – the season when flowers push their stalks through the ground, buds burst into leaves, and insects, frogs and countless other species emerge from winter dormancy. But perhaps the most obvious sign of spring’s return is the arrival of migrating birds on their expedition north for the summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Fly: Studying Bird Migration and Behavior', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:21:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/26129572-25c7-5a1a-89b8-38e6c2150bff', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26129572-25c7-5a1a-89b8-38e6c2150bff'}, {'abstract': 'Reluctant to be called anything that makes them sound old, baby-boomer grandparents are naming themselves or accepting toddlers’ nicknames for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/fashion/noticed-who-are-you-calling-grandma.html', 'snippet': 'Reluctant to be called anything that makes them sound old, baby-boomer grandparents are naming themselves or accepting toddlers’ nicknames for them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAST month, Gwyneth Paltrow, promoting her new cookbook, “My Father’s Daughter” (Grand Central Life & Style), on the television show “Chelsea Lately,” revealed that her mother, the actress Blythe Danner, wanted to be called Woof by her grandchildren, Apple and Moses. “My mom’s hot and she didn’t want to be called Grandma,” Ms. Paltrow said. “So she kept trying to make the Woof thing stick. It’s even her e-mail address.” ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12NOTICED-1/Z-NOTICED-P1-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12NOTICED-1/Z-NOTICED-P1-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12NOTICED-1/Z-NOTICED-P1-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Are You Calling Grandma?', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Are You Calling Grandma?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Zissu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zissu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e3e8b8-6dfb-5d58-96ae-fc0b103bc9c5', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e3e8b8-6dfb-5d58-96ae-fc0b103bc9c5'}, {'abstract': 'A two-bedroom penthouse in a former textile factory in the Barracas neighborhood of Buenos Aires is on the market for $800,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/11/greathomesanddestinations/20110511buenos_ss.html', 'snippet': 'A two-bedroom penthouse in a former textile factory in the Barracas neighborhood of Buenos Aires is on the market for $800,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A two-bedroom penthouse in a former textile factory in the Barracas neighborhood of Buenos Aires is on the market for $800,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Buenos Aires, a Trilevel Penthouse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/67f23f60-b63a-5c93-98b4-edcb810e79f5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/67f23f60-b63a-5c93-98b4-edcb810e79f5'}, {'abstract': 'Hair coloring D.I.Y.-ers, take note: there are new foaming systems that are easy to apply and drip-free.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/a-homecoming-for-hair/', 'snippet': 'Hair coloring D.I.Y.-ers, take note: there are new foaming systems that are easy to apply and drip-free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'D.I.Y.-ers who are sick of the mess home hair coloring entails, brands like John Frieda, Clairol and L’Oréal now offer a foaming system that is easy to apply and drip-free. “Color Blend Foam is really the next big thing in hair color,” says the colorist Marie Robinson, Clairol’s color director, referring to the new Nice ’N Easy Foam ($10). “Women can easily cover their entire head with their hands and still won’t make a mess, since the formula doesn’t drip.” John Frieda’s Precision Foam Colour ($13) was seven years in the making, resulting in an innovative coloring system that is as easy to apply as shampoo. You’re even given your own gloves. And L’Oreal’s Sublime Mousse costs just under $10 and comes in 12 different shades. With this kind of easy expertise at your fingertips, you can take full creative control of your hair without the added (and endless) expense. Scared? Don’t be. Harry Josh, the celebrity stylist and creative consultant for John Frieda Hair Care, assures consumers that “with stylist-selected shades, there’s no way to tell that the at-home color isn’t straight out of the salon.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Homecoming for Hair', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T19:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERIN NOONAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NOONAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c347c64d-d6a0-59f7-9687-1cec0e1cd5b7', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c347c64d-d6a0-59f7-9687-1cec0e1cd5b7'}, {'abstract': 'Barracas, once an industrial area, is gaining ground as a desirable neighborhood, but still bears traces of its grittier past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/greathomesanddes