orme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a tricky business for a married couple to parade their personal lives on the musical stage, to convey intimacy while also protecting privacy. How do they decide what to reveal and what to withhold? Because even the most solid relationship has its sour moments, how do they factor in a bad day when togetherness through thick and thin is their message? The answer, of course, is a shared sense of humor. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/MAZZIE/MAZZIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 869, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/MAZZIE/MAZZIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/MAZZIE/MAZZIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cabaret Evening of Songs From a Marriage Made Off Broadway', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cabaret Evening of Songs From a Marriage Made Off Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzie, Marin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danieley, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T20:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0193f3bf-0311-50c0-92e4-c025c04dd902', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0193f3bf-0311-50c0-92e4-c025c04dd902'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn trio Vacation takes a few looks from Comme des Garçons to the streets.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/vacation-comme-des-garcons-video/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn trio Vacation takes a few looks from Comme des Garçons to the streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its skeletal, cut-out blazers, skull-printed skirts, and checkered shorts, Comme des Garçons was easily one of the season’s most ambitious (and hard-to-pull-off) men’s wear collections. To help make sense of it, we asked Brooklyn trio Vacation to take a few looks to the streets. Their experimental pop sound — an amalgamation of influences from the likes of J. Dilla, Brian Eno, and Pierre Schaeffer — lends itself well to the mismatched, layered nature of the clothes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vacation | Comme des Garçons Video', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T20:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Rider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc810197-e650-5caa-b94c-6be7fd4285f4', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc810197-e650-5caa-b94c-6be7fd4285f4'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya and Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/pictures-of-the-day-greece-and-elsewhere-2/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Greece, Libya and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs 