eLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/video-onlinejeans/video-onlinejeans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/video-onlinejeans/video-onlinejeans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to D.I.Y. Jeans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenbloom, Stephanie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T21:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'Matthew Orr|Samantha Stark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'Orr', 'lastname': 'Samantha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/42209012-d034-515b-b1e8-3ece8337ed8a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/42209012-d034-515b-b1e8-3ece8337ed8a'}, {'abstract': 'You can customize jeans, shoes, even underwear on the Web, but be prepared for a few hurdles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/fashion/on-the-web-design-your-own-clothes.html', 'snippet': 'You can customize jeans, shoes, even underwear on the Web, but be prepared for a few hurdles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN an age of style blogs and “Project Runway,” everyone’s an armchair Alexander Wang. And would-be couturiers who long to design their own wardrobes but can’t sketch or sew are in luck. Do-it-yourself Web sites are making it easy for fashion buffs to design and order custom outfits: all you need is an Internet connection and a credit card.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12Cover/12Cover-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 653, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12Cover/12Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/fashion/12Cover/12Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Designer: You. The Maker: Who?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Designed By You, Made By...Who?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T21:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88dddaf0-f7fe-57c8-809d-11c4cde199ab', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88dddaf0-f7fe-57c8-809d-11c4cde199ab'}, {'abstract': 'Video shows Libyan rebels taking control of an airport in Misurata, the country’s third-largest city, and seizing a cache of weapons and ammunition there too.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/video-of-libyan-rebels-at-misuratas-airport/', 'snippet': 'Video shows Libyan rebels taking control of an airport in Misurata, the country’s third-largest city, and seizing a cache of weapons and ammunition there too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague C. J. Chivers reports, Libyan rebels in Misurata, the country’s third-largest city, wrested control of the besieged town’s airport from forces loyal to Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Libyan Rebels at Misurata’s Airport', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Misurata (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T22:03:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/55db0afb-ad70-520b-9bdb-4e5d66645db2', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55db0afb-ad70-520b-9bdb-4e5d66645db2'}, {'abstract': 'Remembering the Palin that might have been.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/the-tragedy-of-sarah-palin/', 'snippet': 'Remembering the Palin that might have been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Green has a great piece in the latest Atlantic on the Sarah Palin who might have been — Palin the reformist governor of Alaska, that is, rather than Palin the spotlight-chasing, media-feuding avatar of right-wing identity politics that we’ve come to know since the 2008 election. The Alaskan Palin fought corruption within her own party, attacked the nexus of government and big business, avoided polarizing feuds and cut successful bipartisan deals; in the process, Green notes, “she succeeded to a remarkable extent in settling, at least for a time, what had seemed insoluble problems, in the process putting Alaska on a trajectory to financial well-being.” This was the Palin that I liked from afar, before John McCain elevated her to national prominence: The charismatic pro-life working mom who was also a good-government reformer capable of thinking outside the ideological box. (Imagine Mitch Daniels crossed with Michelle Bachmann — in a good way.) And it’s a Palin who was swallowed up, almost immediately, by the national culture war, which made her both a right-wing icon and a left-wing hate figure almost instantaneously, and effectively erased her more interesting and complicated past.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Palin Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-11T22:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2702fb98-7442-584f-8eed-ab82f6586c6d', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2702fb98-7442-584f-8eed-ab82f6586c6d'}, {'abstract': 'The paper has hired Erik Wemple, a longtime critic of The Post, and has moved the Style editor, Ned Martel, to a reporting job.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/11/two-staffing-moves-at-the-washington-post/', 'snippet': 'The paper has hired Erik Wemple, a longtime 