1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/books/infamous-players-a-memoir-by-peter-bart.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Bart’s new memoir recalls his years as a vice president at Paramount under Robert Evans in the late 1960s and 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Bart’s latest Hollywood book includes a 1976 picture of its author as a bare-chested, longish-haired guy in jeans, taken at a Hawaiian location for the Hemingway adaptation “Islands in the Stream.” Despite this extremely business-casual look, Mr. Bart’s “Infamous Players” is about his stint at Paramount Pictures as what was then known, and is still known, as “a suit.” He was a Paramount vice president from 1967 to 1975. And he served as a kind of literary aide to the studio’s larger- and noisier-than-life head of production, Robert Evans.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/arts/JPBOOK1/JPBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Near the Top at Paramount, Handling Players and Egos', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Near the Top at Paramount, Handling Players and Egos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bart, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'valu