nippet': 'The New York Schools chief announced appointments to fill gaps left by a string of recent high-level departures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dennis M. Walcott, the new city schools chancellor, made his first senior appointments on Wednesday, selecting a Philadelphia school official to oversee labor issues, and promoting a local superintendent supervisor to lead efforts to teach at-risk students and reduce the achievement gap between students of different races and economic classes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schools Chief Appoints Two Deputies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Schools Chief Appoints Two As Deputies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T00:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46a30660-fd6d-5f41-a597-c1714b257a1f', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46a30660-fd6d-5f41-a597-c1714b257a1f'}, {'abstract': '“La Conquête,” or “The Conquest,” is a semifictional film about the rise of Nicolas Sarkozy, the president of France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/world/europe/12sarkozy.html', 'snippet': '“La Conquête,” or “The Conquest,” is a semifictional film about the rise of Nicolas Sarkozy, the president of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — As if the life of Nicolas Sarkozy has not produced enough melodrama — especially with rumors now that his third wife, Carla Bruni-Sarkozy, may be pregnant — French moviemakers have produced a semifictional drama, called “La Conquête,” or “The Conquest,” that purports to take us behind the scenes of his rise to power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12sarkozy/12sarkozy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12sarkozy/12sarkozy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12sarkozy/12sarkozy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12sarkozy/12sarkozy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/world/12sarkozy/12sarkozy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A President Loves Movies, but Perhaps Not This One', 'kicker': 'Memo From Paris', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A President Loves Movies, But Perhaps Not This One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Carla', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Cecilia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T00:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/150a4c89-3e50-5496-9b3d-aca72b78594f', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/150a4c89-3e50-5496-9b3d-aca72b78594f'}, {'abstract': 'In Burlington, Vt., the city’s partnership with a military contractor to work on clean-energy projects has rankled community and peace activists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/us/12burlington.html', 'snippet': 'In Burlington, Vt., the city’s partnership with a military contractor to work on clean-energy projects has rankled community and peace activists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURLINGTON, Vt. — Car sharing is beloved in this laid-back college town, as are solar panels, rain gardens and most anything designed to fight global warming from the ground up. A bicycle service will pick up your kitchen scraps for composting, and farmers will deliver your vegetables in a biodiesel-fueled truck. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/us/BURLINGTON-3/BURLINGTON-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/us/BURLINGTON-3/BURLINGTON-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name