can cars and was offered a job at a Mercedes repair shop when he was 20. He opened Rheinland Motors, now in Sunnyside, Queens, in 1981. He lives in Chelsea. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/EXPERIENCE2/EXPERIENCE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/EXPERIENCE2/EXPERIENCE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/nyregion/EXPERIENCE2/EXPERIENCE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Car Doctor Who Caters to the Classics', 'kicker': 'Experience Necessary', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Car Doctor Who Caters to the Classics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T00:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d538aba0-ce1a-538c-8d7a-782d82f6f8b6', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d538aba0-ce1a-538c-8d7a-782d82f6f8b6'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s bid for the Republican presidential nomination is built on divisiveness and name-calling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/opinion/12thu2.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s bid for the Republican presidential nomination is built on divisiveness and name-calling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker and latest entrant in the Republican presidential field, has money, experience and name recognition. His introductory video is all serenity and hope, a deceptively calm way for many voters to meet a splenetic politician with a long history of slashing divisiveness and intolerance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Gingrich’s Intolerant History', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Gingrich’s Intolerant History: A presidential bid built on divisiveness and name-calling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T01:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/28403dc4-00a1-5ec6-a7fe-ce20ad5a8eb4', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28403dc4-00a1-5ec6-a7fe-ce20ad5a8eb4'}, {'abstract': 'After watching the party contort its policies and its principles, voters concluded it was not such a good idea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/opinion/12thu4.html', 'snippet': 'After watching the party contort its policies and its principles, voters concluded it was not such a good idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The remarkable political story in Britain is the dizzying decline of the third party, the Liberal Democrats, from kingmakers to helpless dependents on a Conservative coalition partner whose core beliefs could not be more different from their own. The result has been an economic disaster for Britain and an electoral disaster for the Liberal Democrats in this month’s local elections.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Decline of the ‘Lib-Dems’ in Britain', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Decline of the &#8216;Lib-Dems&#8217; in Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberal Democrats (Great Britain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clegg, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T01:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dbcdde6-e8c3-5cd9-b935-82be5f81c5d8', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dbcdde6-e8c3-5cd9-b935-82be5f81c5d8'}, {'abstract': 'Two Tibetan monks from a restive monastery have been sentenced to three years in prison during a two-month crackdown in Sichuan Province.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/world/asia/12briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'Two Tibetan monks from a restive monastery have been sentenced to three years in prison during a two-month crackdown in Sichuan Province.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two Tibetan monks from a restive monastery have been sentenced to three years in prison during a two-month crackdown in Sichuan Province, and about 300 monks taken away in April from the same monastery are still in detention, according to a report by the International Campaign for Tibet, an advocacy group based outside China. The two monks, both from the Kirti Monastery, are Losang Dargye, 31, and Konchok Tsultrim, 33; they were arrested separately in the last two months, the group said. Chinese security forces began surrounding Kirti Monastery in March, when a young monk, Phuntsog, died after setting himself on fire to protest Chinese policies. Local officers have declined to comment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: 2 Tibetan Monks Sentenced to Prison', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: 2 Tibetan Monks Sentenced to Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sichuan Province (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T01:10:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/12705723-71be-5c43-8496-1f7f9875a9d5', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12705723-71be-5c43-8496-1f7f9875a9d5'}, {'abstract': 'If golf trends continue as they have for the first five months of the year, the Players Championship could produce a winner whose name did not come up in the week before the event.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/sports/golf/stalking-big-names-at-players-championship-young-pros-full-of-confidence.html', 'snippet': 'If golf trends continue as they have for the first five months of the year, the Players Championship could produce a winner whose name did not come up in the week before the event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — If golf trends continue as they have for the first five months of the year, the Players Championship, which starts Thursday at the Stadium Course at T.P.C. Sawgrass, could produce a winner whose name did not come up in the weeklong frenzy of prognostication that always accompanies a big event. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/Y-GOLF1/Y-GOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/Y-GOLF1/Y-GOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/Y-GOLF1/Y-GOLF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/Y-GOLF1/Y-GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/sports/Y-GOLF1/Y-GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stalking Big Names, Young Pros Are Full of Confidence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stalking Big Names, Young Pros Are Full of Confidence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major':