07', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65aec7d5-ad8f-5b50-9c83-106d59f54d07'}, {'abstract': 'Vintage Italian sports cars that participate in the annual rally sometimes require a very good wrench.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/for-california-mille-drivers-a-mobile-triage-unit/', 'snippet': 'Vintage Italian sports cars that participate in the annual rally sometimes require a very good wrench.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last April, while gathering notes for a recent article which appeared in the Automobiles section, I spent a day riding shotgun in a trio of vintage Alfa Romeos participating in the 20th annual California Mille, a rally that pays tribute to Italy’s historic road race, the Mille Miglia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For California Mille Drivers, a Mobile Triage Unit', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alfa Romeo Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Czap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Czap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/28d8bc88-a675-5959-9dd0-31baf80f8d1e', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28d8bc88-a675-5959-9dd0-31baf80f8d1e'}, {'abstract': 'We like to think of medicine as a rational science, and that our attention to our lives and our bodies pays off in reasonably predictable ways. But our health and well-being is much more bound to random chance than we’d like to think.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/when-health-is-the-luck-of-the-draw/', 'snippet': 'We like to think of medicine as a rational science, and that our attention to our lives and our bodies pays off in reasonably predictable ways. But our health and well-being is much more bound to random chance than we’d like to think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes you hear stories from your patients that leave you staggered by the caprice of life. A young West African patient told me how his extended family had trudged through the forest on foot to escape rebels. He was 10 years old at the time. At one point in the journey, he had to urinate. He excused himself and retreated several feet into the bush. Moments later shots rang out. When he finally had the courage to crawl back out onto the path, he saw that his entire family had been killed in an ambush.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Health and the Luck of the Draw', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Ofri, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ofri', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/43fdc256-9cfb-53ef-8efb-2914112574a9', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43fdc256-9cfb-53ef-8efb-2914112574a9'}, {'abstract': 'Great design transcends borders and, in the case of “Destination: Istanbul,’’ a joint project from the Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts and the Museum of Modern Art in New York, it literally crosses them.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/turkish-designs-for-sale-in-istanbul-and-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Great design transcends borders and, in the case of “Destination: Istanbul,’’ a joint project from the Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts and the Museum of Modern Art in New York, it literally crosses them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great design transcends borders and, in the case of “Destination: Istanbul,’’ it literally crosses them. In the project, a joint effort by the Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts and the Museum of Modern Art in New York, cleverly rendered items by Turkish designers will be for sale at the MoMA Design Store starting this month and at the IKSV Design Store (Sadi Konuralp Caddesi No: 5; 90-212-334-0830; www.iksvtasarim.com/giris.asp) in the Sishane neighborhood of Istanbul. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkish Designs for Sale in Istanbul and New York', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA Design Store', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Fowler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fowler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e83d623-e07e-5815-a300-7831967605c5', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e83d623-e07e-5815-a300-7831967605c5'}, {'abstract': 'The  limitations of Vince Young – including arm strength, ball security and simple quarterbacking awareness – allowed opponents to focus their  approach on stopping Chris Johnson.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/2010-titans-what-the-film-revealed/', 'snippet': 'The  limitations of Vince Young – including arm strength, ball security and simple quarterbacking awareness – allowed opponents to focus their  approach on stopping Chris Johnson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we wonder whether there will be a 2011 season, this is part of a series looking back at the 2010 season, with the benefit of film analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2010 Titans: What the Film Revealed', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Titans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T10:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8cf2bcc-37f5-5fa5-9311-4ba8d8fadd8b', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8cf2bcc-37f5-5fa5-9311-4ba8d8fadd8b'}, {'abstract': 'How to get Windows Media Player to stream Internet audio.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/qa-a-quick-fix-for-windows-media-player/', 'snippet': 'How to get Windows Media Player to stream Internet audio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: A Quick Fix for Windows Media Player', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'C