0b06250e', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6d0875-76e9-57f1-9ccc-45650b06250e'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists estimate that more than 10,000 bowhead whales are passing from the Bering Sea to the Canadian Beaufort.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/watching-whales-around-the-clock/', 'snippet': 'Scientists estimate that more than 10,000 bowhead whales are passing from the Bering Sea to the Canadian Beaufort.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Kate Stafford, an oceanographer at the Applied Physics Laboratory at the University of Washington, writes from Alaska, where she is participating in a visual census of bowhead whales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching Whales Around the Clock', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T11:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Stafford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stafford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d54efb1d-dddf-5074-9f11-6af691d59d45', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d54efb1d-dddf-5074-9f11-6af691d59d45'}, {'abstract': 'Two seemingly moribund staples, the musical and the comic drama, have come throbbing back to life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/theater/theaterspecial/book-of-mormon-and-new-plays-rejuvenate-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Two seemingly moribund staples, the musical and the comic drama, have come throbbing back to life.', 'lead_paragraph': '“WHAT’S new?” is not, as a general rule, a tactful way to begin a conversation about Broadway. It’s sort of like asking an agoraphobic shut-in, “And where have you been lately?” Still, go ahead. Ask me what’s new this season on Broadway, the one that’s being celebrated by the presentation of the 65th annual Tony Awards on June 12. For once, I can provide some encouraging answers.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/BRANTLEY-SUB/BRANTLEY-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/BRANTLEY-SUB/BRANTLEY-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/BRANTLEY-SUB/BRANTLEY-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/BRANTLEY-SUB/BRANTLEY-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/BRANTLEY-SUB/BRANTLEY-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Broadway, Old Friends Walking on Air', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Broadway, Old Friends Walking on Air', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2