, 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62343133-4f40-58d3-86df-169369d16d7e', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62343133-4f40-58d3-86df-169369d16d7e'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: In an interview on Rolling Stone magazine’s Web site, Donald Trump talks about his implausible hair and how he gets it to look that way; also, a lightning roundup of news from other sources.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/wash-let-it-dry-comb-it-thats-trumps-deal/', 'snippet': 'The Day: In an interview on Rolling Stone magazine’s Web site, Donald Trump talks about his implausible hair and how he gets it to look that way; also, a lightning roundup of news from other sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many of you, maybe most, this is going to fall squarely under the heading of T.M.I., but the New Yorker who defies parody more than any other admits to using a comb but not a hair dryer. That would be Donald Trump. Before you start groaning, remember: You were told going in that this might qualify as too much information. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wash, Let It Dry, Comb It. That’s Trump’s Deal.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T12:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/322cd97c-1e78-5640-8e64-3acbcfd9661c', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/322cd97c-1e78-5640-8e64-3acbcfd9661c'}, {'abstract': 'Web sites let you design your own clothes, a proposal to tax parents of obese children, Google’s Chrome laptops and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/thursday-reading-the-mixed-results-of-designing-clothes-online/', 'snippet': 'Web sites let you design your own clothes, a proposal to tax parents of obese children, Google’s Chrome laptops and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: The Mixed Results of Designing Clothes Online', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T12:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/155a4cc7-87ff-517e-8c6c-7ce5944946f0', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/155a4cc7-87ff-517e-8c6c-7ce5944946f0'}, {'abstract': 'Turning a historic house — whether designed for laborers or lords — into a hotel is never easy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/this-old-hotel/', 'snippet': 'Turning a historic house — whether designed for laborers or lords — into a hotel is never easy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning a historic house — whether designed for laborers or lords — into a hotel is never easy. When Fred Krehbiel, a Chicago industrialist, decided to buy Ballyfin, a Georgian manor on 600 acres in Ireland’s County Laois, the property was being used as a school, he says, “and we had to give them six years to build a new building.” During that time, Krehbiel’s team of more than 100 workers began transforming the 1812 mansion into a hotel with 15 rooms, all while working around 500 teenagers. Krehbiel and crew restored ornate plasterwork, bought back some of the previous owner’s paintings, rebuilt the conservatory (which had to be disassembled and shipped to England for repairs) and even uncovered a Roman sarcophagus bathtub, now installed in one of the guest rooms. (Appropriately, a family motto of Ballyfin’s original owner, Sir Charles Coote, was “coûte que coûte” — “cost what it may.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Old Hotel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7b23ee6-bb4a-5c7e-a200-9de72fcf08ec', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7b23ee6-bb4a-5c7e-a200-9de72fcf08ec'}, {'abstract': 'A study in Italy shows the effect on the local economy when public spending is frozen in response to public corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/insights-on-stimulus-thanks-to-the-mafia/', 'snippet': 'A study in Italy shows the effect on the local economy when public spending is frozen in response to public corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is hard to prove that a burst of public spending can stimulate economic activity. Governments generally try the experiment in response to a downturn, and who is to say how quickly an economy would have recovered?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insights on Stimulus, Thanks to the Mafia', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T13:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/955a2a3b-3b20-58da-805e-847663d1bb0f', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/955a2a3b-3b20-58da-805e-847663d1bb0f'}, {'abstract': 'Will Ferrell, the “Anchorman” and “Talledega Nights” star, is one of several “Saturday Night Live” figures to receive the Mark Twain Prize, including Tina Fey, Lorne Michaels and Steve Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/will-ferrell-to-receive-mark-twain-prize-for-humor/', 'snippet': 'Will Ferrell, the “Anchorman” and “Talledega Nights” star, is one of several “Saturday Night Live” figures to receive the Mark Twain Prize, including Tina Fey, Lorne Michaels and Steve Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mark Twain Prize for American Humor is named for one of history’s most distinguished satirists and has, since 1998, been awarded to noteworthy comedians and writers\xa0 like Whoopi Goldberg, Bob Newhart, Neil Simon and Bill Cosby. But somehow, it just got a little classier: Will Ferrell, the “Saturday Night Live” alumnus turned star of hit films like “Talladega Nights: The Ballad of Ricky Bobby” and “Anchorman: The Legend of Ron Burgundy,” will be the 14th recipient of the Mark Twain Prize, the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts said on Thursday morning. Mr. Ferrell said in a statement that he was “truly honored to receive this distinction,” adding: “I will now begin cultivating a Mark Twain-esque mustache in anticipation of the event.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Ferrell to Receive Mark Twain Prize for Humor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrell, Will', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T13:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3373a57f-ad00-5751-89ce-1f31a4873dc5', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3373a57f-ad00-5751-89ce-1f31a4873dc5'}, {'abstract': 'The moment that Scotty McCreery won season 10 of “American Idol” came midway through his first performance on Wednesday night’s show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/american-idol-the-top-4/', 'snippet': 'The moment that Scotty McCreery won season 10 of “American Idol” came midway through his first performance on Wednesday night’s show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Durbin > Scotty McCreery > Lauren Alaina > Haley Reinhart', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Idol: The Top 4', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name':