d technical support until Dec. 31, 2013, but that videos will expire 30 days after posting.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/new-for-flip-videos-an-expiration-date/', 'snippet': 'Cisco, maker of the Flip video camera, said it would provide its FlipShare service and technical support until Dec. 31, 2013, but that videos will expire 30 days after posting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Cisco said it would stop making its popular Flip video cameras, consumers have wondered what will happen to their videos stored on FlipShare’s Web service. Now the company is telling us. It has announced two important deadlines for Flip video camera owners if they want to keep and share their movies. One is coming up fast, and the other is a little further out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New For Flip Videos: An Expiration Date', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camcorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T14:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dba1f01a-8d95-5c36-9ee4-ca591bc3e334', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dba1f01a-8d95-5c36-9ee4-ca591bc3e334'}, {'abstract': 'People working for the anti-secrecy group had to agree to keep secret not just the contents of documents obtained by the organization, but also any “newsworthy information related to the workings of WikiLeaks.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/wikileaks-confidentiality-agreement-leaked/', 'snippet': 'People working for the anti-secrecy group had to agree to keep secret not just the contents of documents obtained by the organization, but also any “newsworthy information related to the workings of WikiLeaks.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 7:09 p.m. According to a leaked copy of a confidentiality agreement that WikiLeaks asked members of its staff to sign, people working for the anti-secrecy group were obliged to agree to keep secret not only the contents of documents obtained by the organization, but also any “newsworthy information related to the workings of WikiLeaks.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'WikiLeaks Confidentiality Agreement Leaked', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T14:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c37851eb-bf96-534e-ae55-7beb68779faa', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c37851eb-bf96-534e-ae55-7beb68779faa'}, {'abstract': 'The designer and international dandy pushed Fiat, his grandfather Gianni Agnelli’s company, to bring back its iconic Cinquecento.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/styled-to-a-t-lapo-elkann/', 'snippet': 'The designer and international dandy pushed Fiat, his grandfather Gianni Agnelli’s company, to bring back its iconic Cinquecento.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guy', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Styled to a T | Lapo Elkann', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, '