 the margins of public life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — In a country where the power blinks out several times a day, where filling up a gas tank can take hours and motorists stew in seemingly endless traffic jams, smoking is one thing that seems blissfully easy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13iraqspan/13iraqspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13iraqspan/13iraqspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13iraqspan/13iraqspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13iraqspan/13iraqspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13iraqspan/13iraqspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bogged Down on Big Issues, Iraq Takes Aim at Smoking', 'kicker': 'Baghdad Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bogged Down on Big Issues, Iraq Takes Aim at Smoking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T15:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9815d6fd-5406-586c-9451-23fc0fc70e0a', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9815d6fd-5406-586c-9451-23fc0fc70e0a'}, {'abstract': 'A TimesTalk at Cannes, to be streamed live on Thursday, will tackle the issue in a year where a record (though still low) number of female filmmakers are competing for top prizes.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/a-cannes-conversation-about-women-in-film/', 'snippet': 'A TimesTalk at Cannes, to be streamed live on Thursday, will tackle the issue in a year where a record (though still low) number of female filmmakers are competing for top prizes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — There are a record number of female filmmakers competing for the biggest prizes in competition for the Palme d’Or at the Cannes Film Festival this year: four. That’s 4 out of 20 (last year, there were zero women in the competition). As lopsided as that 20 percent figure may still be, some of the buzzed-about films around the Croissette this year are directed by women, including Lynne Ramsay’s “We Need to Talk About Kevin” and Julia Leigh’s “Sleeping Beauty.” An entry far out of the competition, “Kung Fu Panda 2,” the animated sequel starring Angelina Jolie, Jack Black and Dustin Hoffman, was directed by Jennifer Yuh, who was a story artist on the first film; at a press conference on Thursday, a journalist asked Ms. Jolie if her character was more developed because of Ms. Yuh’s involvement. (Ms. Jolie, who plays a tigress, hedged an answer. “I do feel if we had a male director, I would have had a bigger part,” Mr. Hoffman – red panda – said jokingly.) Other films have notable female performances, like “The Beloved,” in which Catherine Deneuve stars, and sings, with her daughter, Chiara Mastroianni. It is scheduled to be the festival’s closing film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cannes Conversation About Women in Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leigh, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramsay, Lynne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T15:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ea940d-a6c9-51e4-b7d6-e979cec6d8ff', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ea940d-a6c9-51e4-b7d6-e979cec6d8ff'}, {'abstract': 'At the Chihuahua Races, a Chandler, Ariz., tradition now in its ninth year, tutus and frilly outfits overshadow speed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/us/13outhere.html', 'snippet': 'At the Chihuahua Races, a Chandler, Ariz., tradition now in its ninth year, tutus and frilly outfits overshadow speed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no starting gun at a Chihuahua race. The loud noise might unduly alarm the competitors, who are high-strung even when not running for $1,000 in prize money.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/us/13outhere-illo/13outhere-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 249, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/us/13outhere-illo/13outhere-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7