nyt://article/63afc6a1-b3e8-5009-8bcf-e3c6ebcbf3e9', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63afc6a1-b3e8-5009-8bcf-e3c6ebcbf3e9'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said that the United States would pursue “additional steps to hold Syria responsible for its gross human rights abuses.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/middleeast/13clinton.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton said that the United States would pursue “additional steps to hold Syria responsible for its gross human rights abuses.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NUUK, Greenland — Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton moved the United States a step closer to calling for the ouster of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria on Thursday as she denounced his government’s intensifying crackdown on protesters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Toughens Tone Toward Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Toughens Tone Toward Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:11:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/deeba3d6-00c3-5327-91cd-5b20ef7e71f0', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deeba3d6-00c3-5327-91cd-5b20ef7e71f0'}, {'abstract': 'Inflammation, and not necessarily infection, is the common theme in chronic sinusitis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sinusitis-ess.html', 'snippet': 'Inflammation, and not necessarily infection, is the common theme in chronic sinusitis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The humble sinuses, those hollow cavities hidden in the bones around the nose, usually draw little appreciation. But nothing makes one yearn for clear sinuses like sinusitis, a condition that can make the head feel as if it were filled with cement and can render every breath a struggle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/health/12Sinus/12Sinus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Sinus Problems Won’t Go Away', 'kicker': "Reporter's File", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinusitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nose', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': 'By INGFEI CHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingfei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CHEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db36ae08-00b5-5b1b-9cbd-05e860b88db8', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db36ae08-00b5-5b1b-9cbd-05e860b88db8'}, {'abstract': 'Yale University is opening its digital image archive online to the public for free.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/yale-opens-its-vault-online-for-free/', 'snippet': 'Yale University is opening its digital image archive online to the public for free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yale\xa0is going first. The university, in New Haven, announced that it is opening its entire digital image collection to the public for free – the first Ivy League institution to take this step toward open access. Yale houses millions of images in its archives, museum and libraries, including a sonata written by the hand of Mozart and a watercolor by William Blake. “The open access policy allows us to more fully harness the potential of digital and networked technologies in service to scholarship as well as to creative use and reuse of our rich cultural heritage,” said Meg Bellinger, director of the Yale Office of Digital Assets and Infrastructure. “It frees us to concentrate on our core mission to create, preserve and disseminate knowledge in digital form.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yale Opens Its Image Vault Online for Free', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Haven (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6febc59-671c-5019-aece-43b553fae0d7', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6febc59-671c-5019-aece-43b553fae0d7'}, {'abstract': 'The Miami Heat’s season followed a perfect narrative for the N.B.A.’s new villain franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/sports/heat-arrives-on-cue-in-nba-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'The Miami Heat’s season followed a perfect narrative for the N.B.A.’s new villain franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If we didn’t know better — and didn’t mind being lumped in with the black helicopter crowd — we would be certain the script for these N.B.A. playoffs was being written in some studio somewhere, perhaps by out-of-work soap opera writers under the watchful eye of the N.B.A. marketing department. The Miami Heat’s whole season followed the perfect narrative for the league’s new villain franchise: the players stumbled early, really stunk for a while, blamed their clueless coach, bounced back, humbled the mighty Lakers a few times, then overcame the sage elder statesmen of the Celtics in the second round of the playoffs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heat Arrives on Cue', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heat Arrives on Cue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thornton, Joe (1979- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 