s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/asia/13china.html', 'snippet': 'Nineteen pastors signed a petition calling for an investigation into the crackdown on Shouwang, a so-called house church, as well as legal protections for similar churches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — More than a dozen Christian leaders in China have thrown their support behind an embattled underground church, calling for the government to end its persecution and for broader religious freedoms as well. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13china/13china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13china/13china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13china/13china-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Christians Rally Around Underground Church', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Support for a Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:20:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78cbcf26-a542-50e9-b36f-87d9e48b8d2a', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78cbcf26-a542-50e9-b36f-87d9e48b8d2a'}, {'abstract': 'Talking points for patients and physicians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sinusitis-questions.html', 'snippet': 'Talking points for patients and physicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Confronting a new diagnosis can be frightening and, because research changes so often, confusing. Here are some questions you may not think to ask your doctor, along with notes on why they’re important.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Ask About Sinusitis', 'kicker': 'Questions for Your Doctor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinusitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': 'By INGFEI CHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingfei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CHEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ec135c1-d0d8-5d5c-b89e-835a64cf61bf', 'word_count': 1495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ec135c1-d0d8-5d5c-b89e-835a64cf61bf'}, {'abstract': 'Research studies on sinusitis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sinusitis-trials.html', 'snippet': 'Research studies on sinusitis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Government agencies, universities and corporations frequently enroll patients in studies developed to test the effectiveness of new drugs, procedures and medical devices. Participants may benefit by gaining access to experimental therapies, and they make an important contribution to scientific research. For more information, visit ClinicalTrials.gov, a service of the National Institutes of Health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selected Studies: Sinusitis', 'kicker': 'Clinical Trials', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinusitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ad162d-7afa-50c0-9b5f-2344b51430ec', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ad162d-7afa-50c0-9b5f-2344b51430ec'}, {'abstract': 'On the flight home, “with a shirt from each university stowed safely beneath the seat in front of me,” the author, a high school senior from Colorado, “couldn’t help but love both schools even more.” So how to decide?', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/cherry-creek-campbell/', 'snippet': 'On the flight home, “with a shirt from each university stowed safely beneath the seat in front of me,” the author, a high school senior from Colorado, “couldn’t help but love both schools even more.” So how to decide?', 'lead_paragraph': '“I think I know where I’m going,” I say as I walk into the living room, checking my phone for anticlimactic effect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Red-Eyes, 36 Sleepless Hours and Still a Choice', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Campbell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Campbell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/15dcca0a-f453-5c82-9051-02c752dd0c00', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15dcca0a-f453-5c82-9051-02c752dd0c00'}, {'abstract': 'Wearing’s unnerving photographs and videos, as seen at the Tanya Bonakdar Gallery, wrest the dark side of being human from a deceptive public image.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/artifacts-gillian-wearings-true-stories/', 'snippet': 'Wearing’s unnerving photographs and videos, as seen at the Tanya Bonakdar Gallery, wrest the dark side of being human from a deceptive public image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of us don’t actually wear our hearts on our sleeves. Not unless we are the subjects of Gillian Wearing’s unnerving photographs and videos, documents that wrest the dark side of being human from a deceptive public image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artifacts | Gillian Wearing’s True Stories', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Yablonsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yablonsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/54456f97-fa7d-5295-ab67-69be780da62b', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54456f97-fa7d-5295-ab67-69be780da62b'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Richard M. Rosenfeld on interpreting sinus infections and when you need antibiotics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/ref/health/healthguide/esn-sinusitis-know.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Richard M. Rosenfeld on interpreting sinus infections and when you need antibiotics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Richard M. Rosenfeld, an otolaryngologist at SUNY Downstate Medical Center in Brooklyn, was chairman of a panel of the American Academy of Otolaryngology — Head and Neck Surgery that wrote clinical practice guidelines on adult sinusitis in 2007. The guidelines clarified how to distinguish when an acute sinus infection is caused by a virus versus by bacteria. Antibiotics don’t work against viruses but are nonetheless frequently prescribed for sinusitis. The drugs’ overuse can foster resistant bacteria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2008/08/21/health/fivethings_190/fivethings_190-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What You Need to Know About Sinusitis', 'kicker': '5 Things to Know', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinusitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Health Guide', 'byline': {'original': 'By INGFEI CHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingfei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CHEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6dd456c-1949-553c-84b2-e5419d3730e7', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6dd456c-1949-553c-84b2-e5419d3730e7'}, {'abstract': 'Experts discuss biofilms and the underlying causes of chronic sinusitis.', 'web_url': 'https://consults.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/exploring-the-roots-of-sinus-trouble/', 'snippet': 'Experts discuss biofilms and the underlying causes of chronic sinusitis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ingfei Chen, health reporter, writes about chronic sinus problems, which affect up to 14 percent of adults, in The Times Health Guide: Sinusitis. Here she interviews Dr. Noam A. Cohen and Dr. James N. Palmer, sinus surgery specialists at the rhinology lab at the University of Pennsylvania in Philadelphia, about the underlying causes of chronic sinus complaints. See, too, Ms. Chen’s stories, “When Sinus Problems Won’t Go Away,” “5 Things to Know About Sinusitis,”  and “Questions for Your Doctor.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring the Roots of Sinus Trouble', 'kicker': 'Consults', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nose', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinusitis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:36:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ingfei Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingfei', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d311d810-7c32-5c64-8de5-bac5bc162b53', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d311d810-7c32-5c64-8de5-bac5bc162b53'}, {'abstract': 'In his forthcoming ninth studio album, Brad Paisley offers a more expansive definition of country music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/arts/music/brad-paisleys-new-album-this-is-country-music.html', 'snippet': 'In his forthcoming ninth studio album, Brad Paisley offers a more expansive definition of country music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT is country music? Is it a sound: an acoustic guitar, a pedal steel, a fiddle, a high lonesome croon? Is it regional art — and if so, what region, exactly? (Nashville? Appalachia? Bakersfield, Calif.?) Is it a grand tradition, stretching from the Carter Family and Jimmie Rodgers, to Roy Acuff and Hank Williams, to Johnny Cash and Dolly Parton and George Jones, down to the present day? Is country a way of life? A worldview? The best answer might be that country is music that can’t stop defining itself — the genre that can’t stop asking “What is country music?”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PAISLEY/PAISLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 631, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PAISLEY/PAISLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PAISLEY/PAISLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brad Paisley’s Country Underground', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brad Paisley’s Country Underground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paisley, Brad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jody Rosen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jody', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0934f90a-ddb8-55c4-8260-b3dc143f30a9', 'word_count': 1397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0934f90a-ddb8-55c4-8260-b3dc143f30a9'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign, initially featuring a Chrysler 200, Eminem and Detroit, now includes a Chrysler 300, the fashion designer John Varvatos and Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/chrysler-exports-imported-from-detroit-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The campaign, initially featuring a Chrysler 200, Eminem and Detroit, now includes a Chrysler 300, the fashion designer John Varvatos and Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After viewing Chrysler‘s two-minute Super Bowl XLV advertisement, during which the rapper Eminem emerged not from the all-new Chrysler 300, but from a 200 sedan, some Monday-morning quarterbacks felt that the brand missed an opportunity to showcase a superior product, one deserving of the spot’s emotional impact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chrysler Exports ‘Imported From Detroit’ to New York', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varvatos, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/068ef5f6-29da-5317-9de9-33290b09263d', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068ef5f6-29da-5317-9de9-33290b09263d'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is asking Congress to extend the 10-year term of F.B.I. Director Robert S. Mueller III by two years.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/obama-seeks-extension-of-muellers-term-as-fbi-director/', 'snippet': 'President Obama is asking Congress to extend the 10-year term of F.B.I. Director Robert S. Mueller III by two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is asking Congress to pass legislation that would extend the 10-year term of Robert S. Mueller III, the director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, by two years, the White House said in a statement Thursday. Mr. Mueller’s tenure is scheduled to end on Sept. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Seeks to Extend Mueller’s Term as F.B.I. Director', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:43:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/379f064d-8e3f-5c83-8501-17782d22516f', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/379f064d-8e3f-5c83-8501-17782d22516f'}, {'abstract': 'A shop in the Prospect-Lefferts Gardens neighborhood in Brooklyn has gained a large following with its offerings of ital food and vegetarian ice cream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/15/nyregion/20110515JOINTss.html', 'snippet': 'A shop in the Prospect-Lefferts Gardens neighborhood in Brooklyn has gained a large following with its offerings of ital food and vegetarian ice cream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A shop in the Prospect-Lefferts Gardens neighborhood in Brooklyn has gained a large following with its offerings of ital food and vegetarian ice cream.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG/20110515JOINTss-slide-T1RG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighborhood Joint | Scoops', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rastafarianism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Lefferts Gardens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d7053113-ec8b-599c-9999-8135a5d2d1ab', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d7053113-ec8b-599c-9999-8135a5d2d1ab'}, {'abstract': 'Nondairy ice cream and hot meals share space in Scoops, a Brooklyn shop that conforms to the dietary traditions of Rastafarians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/at-scoops-in-brooklyn-ital-food-even-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'Nondairy ice cream and hot meals share space in Scoops, a Brooklyn shop that conforms to the dietary traditions of Rastafarians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A YOUNG man stepped in from a wet and howling Friday afternoon, letting the door swing shut behind him. Inside the shop, the air was thick with incense and spice. A European soccer match on a small television set competed with the reggae playing on the stereo and the crackle of mock salmon steaks frying on the stove. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JOINT2/15JOINT2-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JOINT2/15JOINT2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JOINT2/15JOINT2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Haven for Rastafarian Food', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Meat, No Dairy, No Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rastafarianism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Lefferts Gardens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'sect