 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c096c3-2b02-5db5-b6fd-925538a19590', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c096c3-2b02-5db5-b6fd-925538a19590'}, {'abstract': 'The war between Google and Facebook escalated a bit with news that Facebook hired a public-relations firm known for its political work to push for articles critical of a new Google social service.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/facebook-seeks-to-downplay-campaign-against-google/', 'snippet': 'The war between Google and Facebook escalated a bit with news that Facebook hired a public-relations firm known for its political work to push for articles critical of a new Google social service.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:17 p.m. | Updated Added comment from Burson-Marsteller and public relations experts, and more details on Social Circle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Seeks to Downplay Campaign Against Google', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft and Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fbf6c86-97c9-5ccd-a13b-be681158ea3c', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fbf6c86-97c9-5ccd-a13b-be681158ea3c'}, {'abstract': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, I write about Shawn Ryan and Cathy Wood, who are leading a new gold rush in the Yukon.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/tracks-in-the-yukon/', 'snippet': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, I write about Shawn Ryan and Cathy Wood, who are leading a new gold rush in the Yukon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this Sunday’s magazine, I write about Shawn Ryan and Cathy Wood, who are leading a new gold rush in the Yukon. I first met Ryan and Wood while reporting a story for T magazine about a commercial boom in wild morels near Dawson City in 2005. As soon as I had the assignment, I called my friend David Arora and asked if he wanted to go along. Arora is famous among mushroom pickers; nearly all of them own a copy of his giant field guide, “Mushrooms Demystified.” Arora seems to know everybody, but the two people he recommended as most important to talk to in the Yukon were Ryan and Wood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tracks in the Yukon', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RYAN, SHAWN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yukon Territory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T16:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Wolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/40623da1-7ec5-50ea-b71e-7a4078e2396f', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40623da1-7ec5-50ea-b71e-7a4078e2396f'}, {'abstract': 'NBC has picked up the musical comedy “Smash,” about the making of a Broadway show, for the 2011-12 television season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/curtain-up-broadway-set-smash-gets-a-spot-on-nbcs-roster/', 'snippet': 'NBC has picked up the musical comedy “Smash,” about the making of a Broadway show, for the 2011-12 television season.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:26 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Curtain Up: Broadway-Set ‘Smash’ Gets a Spot on NBC’s Roster', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T17:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy and Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41b0a0d0-5550-5e89-a963-6515329b1ce9', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41b0a0d0-5550-5e89-a963-6515329b1ce9'}, {'abstract': 'White rappers have become preservationists of past hip-hop sounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/arts/music/white-rappers-like-the-beastie-boys-pay-homage.html', 'snippet': 'White rappers have become preservationists of past hip-hop sounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT 30 seconds into “Dr. Lecter,” the debut full-length album by’ Action Bronson, and the hi