imes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: Remembering Michael Baze', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/94be19bb-f7b5-520c-9a6f-4559ce75151c', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94be19bb-f7b5-520c-9a6f-4559ce75151c'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Popcast, Jody Rosen talks about Brad Paisley and Jon Caramanica discusses white rappers-as-preservationists.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/popcast-brad-paisley-proudly-preaches-to-the-choir/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Popcast, Jody Rosen talks about Brad Paisley and Jon Caramanica discusses white rappers-as-preservationists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad Paisley is openly wooing his old audience with his new album, “This Is Country Music,” his ninth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Popcast: Brad Paisley Proudly Preaches to the Choir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9877f2a-5554-518f-8d98-39339ec1777e', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9877f2a-5554-518f-8d98-39339ec1777e'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of lesson plans and New York Times articles to use alongside the reading and viewing of Arthur Miller’s play.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/teaching-the-crucible-with-the-new-york-times/', 'snippet': 'A collection of lesson plans and New York Times articles to use alongside the reading and viewing of Arthur Miller’s play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though often considered second best to his “Death of a Salesman” and opening to lukewarm, if not downright hostile, reviews, Arthur Miller’s play “The Crucible” continues to be mounted and taught worldwide because it speaks to universal fears of social isolation and the unknown – fears especially present in a rapidly changing world, not to mention in the topsy-turvy social order of school.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching ‘The Crucible’ With The New York Times', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Arthur', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Christy Brown and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': 'Christy', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6105fa7-31b4-5d9a-8849-03e837abf66d', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6105fa7-31b4-5d9a-8849-03e837abf66d'}, {'abstract': 'The body of the contractor who was in the country to discuss business opportunities with the rebel authorities in Libya was discovered in Benghazi. Two of his colleagues were also reported missing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/africa/13benghazi.html', 'snippet': 'The body of the contractor who was in the country to discuss business opportunities with the rebel authorities in Libya was discovered in Benghazi. Two of his colleagues were also reported missing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BENGHAZI, Libya — The president of a French private security company who had scheduled a meeting on Thursday to discuss business opportunities with opponents of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi died in a hospital here on Wednesday, apparently after he was shot in the stomach, the French Foreign Ministry and rebel officials here in Benghazi said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13bengazi/13bengazi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13bengazi/13bengazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13bengazi/13bengazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Head of French Company Is Killed in Libyan City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Head of French Company Is Killed in Libyan City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and Maïa de la Baume', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca24ac7-a2e2-5ee4-9e28-5fac889737da', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca24ac7-a2e2-5ee4-9e28-5fac889737da'}, {'abstract': 'Foreign reporters were given rare access to a base south of Tel Aviv, including a system designed to identify, locate and destroy missiles from farther afield.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/middleeast/13israel.html', 'snippet': 'Foreign reporters were given rare access to a base south of Tel Aviv, including a system designed to identify, locate and destroy missiles from farther afield.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALMACHIM AIR FORCE BASE, Israel — The Israeli military allowed foreign reporters rare access to this heavily guarded Mediterranean base south of Tel Aviv on Thursday in what military officials described as an effort to showcase Israel’s technological advancements in the field of air defense and to underscore the array of threats from rockets and missiles. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13israel/13israel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Allows a Glimpse of Its Array of Defenses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Allows A Glimpse Of Its Array Of Defenses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub