/hawks-grizzlies-demonstrates-value-of-depth/', 'snippet': 'Roster depth is typically disregarded as a legitimate playoff advantage for N.B.A. teams, but the Hawks and Grizzlies each lost Game 5 in their respective series because of the heavy minutes their starters are forced to play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.B.A. teams have reached the point in the playoffs when they are hindered by the most basic of human limitations: physical fatigue. Like it or not, basketball players are not conceptual beings nor robots, and as such they’re limited by what their bodies are able to do. Obvious though that may be, it’s a factor of performance sometimes lost in the “one game at a time” playoff mentality, an inescapable component of teams failing or succeeding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawks, Grizzlies Demonstrates Value of Depth', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Grizzlies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc7015a-b23a-5e6b-bc90-245d3cfa05f4', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc7015a-b23a-5e6b-bc90-245d3cfa05f4'}, {'abstract': 'Big donors may now owe gift taxes on their contributions to nonprofit advocacy groups that are playing an increasing role in American politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/business/13gift.html', 'snippet': 'Big donors may now owe gift taxes on their contributions to nonprofit advocacy groups that are playing an increasing role in American politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big donors like David H. Koch and George Soros could owe taxes on their millions of dollars in contributions to nonprofit advocacy groups that are playing an increasing role in American politics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/business/Gift2/Gift2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I.R.S. Moves to Tax Gifts to Groups Active in Politics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.R.S. Sets Sights On Donors’ Gifts That Push Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soros, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA Action', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads GPS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T18:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname'