n into members of an Iranian dissident group eight years after charging that the group was planning attacks in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The French authorities are dropping a terrorism investigation into 24 members of an Iranian dissident group for lack of evidence, court documents show, nearly eight years after a sensational raid on the organization’s headquarters amid charges that the group was planning attacks on targets in Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Will Drop Charges Against Iranian Dissidents', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Terrorism Charges Dropped Against Iranian Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dab96175-2364-5112-abc9-dcbf47835ab4', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dab96175-2364-5112-abc9-dcbf47835ab4'}, {'abstract': 'A film’s depiction of child rape has resulted in charges of exhibiting child pornography for the director of a film festival in Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/movies/in-spain-serbian-film-raises-questions-of-artistic-license.html', 'snippet': 'A film’s depiction of child rape has resulted in charges of exhibiting child pornography for the director of a film festival in Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/SERBIAN-2/SERBIAN-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/SERBIAN-2/SERBIAN-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/SERBIAN-2/SERBIAN-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/SERBIAN-2/SERBIAN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/SERBIAN-2/SERBIAN-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Scandalous a Prosecutor Took Notice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Scandalous A Prosecutor Took Notice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc815c4a-3776-53f7-a7db-9421739d30e3', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc815c4a-3776-53f7-a7db-9421739d30e3'}, {'abstract': 'A survey finds 39 of consumers have had a bad customer-service experience and most of them complained about it.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/consumers-want-fast-friendly-service/', 'snippet': 'A survey finds 39 of consumers have had a bad customer-service experience and most of them complained about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a third of consumers report having had a bad experience with a service provider, and the vast majority of them took time to complain about it, a recent survey finds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumers Want Fast, Friendly Service', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Accenture Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0affadaf-ec99-5e2a-8d1d-3827f48e1604', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0affadaf-ec99-5e2a-8d1d-3827f48e1604'}, {'abstract': 'A trip to Immokalee, Fla., the source of almost all the winter tomatoes grown in the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/immokalee-americas-tomato-capital/', 'snippet': 'A trip to Immokalee, Fla., the source of almost all the winter tomatoes grown in the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This morning I left Immokalee, Fla., the source of almost all the winter tomatoes grown in the United States. Its inspiring tomato workers have gone from enduring slavery, beatings, wage theft (and sub-minimum wage pay) and 12-hour days in the blazing heat with no shade, to a victory that, that, while not quite complete, is possibly the most successful labor action in the United States in 20 years, the details of which will have to wait for a column or even a story. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immokalee, America’s Tomato Capital', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coalition of Immokalee Workers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd657f0-39f7-56de-9693-1fa0dd1dd564', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd657f0-39f7-56de-9693-1fa0dd1dd564'}, {'abstract': 'A new sign that detects drivers’ speeds, will flash a skeleton to those who are going faster than the limit — 30 m.p.h. Also, the city will experiment with a slower speed limit in some areas.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/a-spooky-reminder-to-obey-the-speed-limit/', 'snippet': 'A new sign that detects drivers’ speeds, will flash a skeleton to those who are going faster than the limit — 30 m.p.h. Also, the city will experiment with a slower speed limit in some areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City, it should be noted, has a speed limit: 30 miles per hour unless otherwise noted. The Transportation Department is hoping a pixelated image of a skeleton won’t let you forget it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spooky Reminder to Obey the Speed Limit', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speed Limits and Speeding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadik-Khan, Janette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Alternatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9047daa-e45b-5cbf-8df7-ccbc9c699e4f', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9047daa-e45b-5cbf-8df7-ccbc9c699e4f'}, {'abstract': "The potential presidential candidate Mitt Romney confronts health care questions; NATO planes strike Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi's compound; and crime sweeps Cairo.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000816572/timescast--may-12-2011.html', 'snippet': "The potential presidential candidate Mitt Romney confronts health care questions; NATO planes strike Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi's c