out a 10-year-old girl possessed by the devil and the Catholic priest who tries to save her, is set to open there at the Geffen Playhouse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nail Down the Seats – ‘The Exorcist’ Is Coming to the Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d98584-6440-50db-a8dc-5dc0eed182d5', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d98584-6440-50db-a8dc-5dc0eed182d5'}, {'abstract': 'A reporter who covered neo-Nazis in California describes his impressions of the world of Jeff Hall, a neo-Nazi leader who the police say was killed by his 10-year-old son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/us/13hall.html', 'snippet': 'A reporter who covered neo-Nazis in California describes his impressions of the world of Jeff Hall, a neo-Nazi leader who the police say was killed by his 10-year-old son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jesse McKinley spent two months looking into the activities of the Southern California chapter of the National Socialist Movement, the nation’s largest neo-Nazi group, and the chapter’s leader, Jeff Hall. On May 1, midway through his reporting on the project, Mr. McKinley received word that Mr. Hall’s 10-year-old son had been charged with murdering him with a handgun as he lay on the living room sofa, just a day after Mr. McKinley had spent much of the afternoon at the family home for a meeting of the group. His subsequent article on Mr. Hall and the murder, and the unusual circumstances of the case, have aroused so much reader interest that Mr. McKinley was asked to describe his impressions of Mr. Hall, his family and his world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/us/NAZI1_span/WHITE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/11/us/NAZI1_span/WHITE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/us/NAZI1_span/WHITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/11/us/NAZI1_span/WHITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/11/us/NAZI1_span/WHITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Domesticity and Radicalism Clash in a Neo-Nazi Home', 'kicker': 'Reporter’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Domesticity and Radicalism Clash in a Neo-Nazi Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Socialist Movement (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:47:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b247712c-e085-51db-bbcb-4d64f1808bbd', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b247712c-e085-51db-bbcb-4d64f1808bbd'}, {'abstract': 'A new filling station in Torrance, Calif., dispenses hydrogen from a pipeline instead of from on-site tanks.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/wheelies-the-pipeline-edition/', 'snippet': 'A new filling station in Torrance, Calif., dispenses hydrogen from a pipeline instead of from on-site tanks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Pipeline Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydrogen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:47:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cf2b073-3491-50f9-b95e-01c631b52719', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cf2b073-3491-50f9-b95e-01c631b52719'}, {'abstract': 'The Indian prime minister’s visit to Kabul was a reminder of how much Pakistan and India are competing for the geopolitical advantage in Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/asia/13kabul.html', 'snippet': 'The Indian prime minister’s visit to Kabul was a reminder of how much Pakistan and India are competing for the geopolitical advantage in Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Afghanistan and India agreed to move ahead on a strategic partnership framework during a visit to the Afghan capital by India’s prime minister on Thursday, just weeks after a visit from the prime minister of Pakistan, India’s archrival. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13kabul/13kabul-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13kabul/13kabul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/world/13kabul/13kabul-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian and Afghan Leaders Forge Deeper Ties in Meeting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian and Afghan Leaders Forge Deeper Ties in Meeting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilani, Yousaf Raza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and Sangar Rahimi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sangar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rahimi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef3981c4-bb52-5cf3-87eb-004f5f52d262', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef3981c4-bb52-5cf3-87eb-004f5f52d262'}, {'abstract': 'Rob Young’s new book explores folk music during the 1960s and early ’70s in Britain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/books/electric-eden-by-rob-young-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Rob Young’s new book explores folk music during the 1960s and early ’70s in Britain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brilliant and largely forgotten critic Seymour Krim (1922-1989) grew up, as have so many American readers, worshiping those writers who captured what he called “the unofficial seamy side of American life.” The excitable Krim put it this way: “I dreamed Southern accents, Okies, bourbon-and-branchwater, Gloria Wandrous, jukejoints, Studs Lonigan, big trucks and speeding highways, Bigger Thomas, U.S.A.!, U.S.A.!”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK---AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK---AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK---AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Primordial Soup, a Musical Brew', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Primordial Soup, A Musical Brew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8f9cfc6-01bc-5f91-8d80-5acb298ef31f', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8f9cfc6-01bc-5f91-8d80-5acb298ef31f'}, {'abstract': '“A Serbian Film,” directed by Srdjan Spasojevic, doesn’t just push the envelope of the extreme-cinema niche, it shreds it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/a-serbian-film-directed-by-srdjan-spasojevic-review.html', 'snippet': '“A Serbian Film,” directed by Srdjan Spasojevic, doesn’t just push the envelope of the extreme-cinema niche, it shreds it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In spite of its generic title, “A Serbian Film,” directed by Srdjan Spasojevic, has already provoked scandal on the festival circuit and fascination from devotees of extreme cinema. At first glance — and few are likely to dare a second — it belongs in the high-concept shock-horror tradition whose most recent and notorious specimen is probably “The Human Centipede.” As is often the case with movies like this, “A Serbian Film” revels in its sheer inventive awfulness and dares the viewer to find a more serious layer of meaning.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/movies/13serbian-span/13serbian-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/movies/13serbian-span/13serbian-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/movies/13serbian-span/13serbian-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/movies/13serbian-span/13serbian-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/movies/13serbian-span/13serbian-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Torture or Porn? No Need to Choose', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'A Serbian Film'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Torture or Porn? No Need to Choose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T20:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_