he campaign’s home. It is only a few blocks from the 2008 headquarters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Campaign Moves Into Chicago Headquarters', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T21:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aef48fdb-8d2d-54c5-937b-6c5665cb3d3b', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aef48fdb-8d2d-54c5-937b-6c5665cb3d3b'}, {'abstract': 'In her show at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, Nnenna Freelon is much jazzier and more experimental, but you could hear the influence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/arts/music/nnenna-freelon-tribute-to-lena-horne-at-feinsteins-review.html', 'snippet': 'In her show at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, Nnenna Freelon is much jazzier and more experimental, but you could hear the influence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the jazz singer Nnenna Freelon was a little girl, she recalled in her show, “Lena: A Lovesome Thing,” on Wednesday evening at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, Lena Horne was “held up as the standard of beauty and pride.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13freelon-span/freelon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13freelon-span/freelon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13freelon-span/freelon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13freelon-span/freelon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13freelon-span/freelon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Singer’s Tribute to Lena Horne, Her Regal and Daunting Role Model', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Singer’s Tribute to Lena Horne, Her Regal and Daunting Role Model', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Feinstein's at the Regency", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horne, Lena', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freelon, Nnenna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T21:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4d4595c-64ec-50f2-8d73-892d38c43288', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4d4595c-64ec-50f2-8d73-892d38c43288'}, {'abstract': 'Videos of cirrate octopuses filmed swimming in the deep ocean and set to classical music seem well on their way to becoming a YouTube genre.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/dancing-octopuses/', 'snippet': 'Videos of cirrate octopuses filmed swimming in the deep ocean and set to classical music seem well on their way to becoming a YouTube genre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have ever felt guilty about eating octopus because of its relatively large brain size, prepare to feel doubly so. As Boing Boing reports: “videos of cirrate octopuses filmed swimming in the deep ocean and set to classical ballet music seem well on their way to becoming a YouTube genre.” Boing Boing links to a recent Guardian article that describes what has made this glimpse into the balletic life of our favorite cephalopod possible. Thanks to improvements in digital technology — a high-definition underwater video camera that can film at 6,600 feet where “less than 1 percent of the sun’s rays ever penetrate” — we can now take\xa0a “rare look at a mysterious benthopelagic sea animal: Grimpoteuthis bathynectes, one in a group of 14 recognized species that are often referred to as ‘Dumbo octopus’ because their fins resemble the large ears that the fictional character, Dumbo the elephant, used to fly.” (O.K., maybe these aren’t exactly the ones you eat, but still.) \xa0The video below, filmed 200 miles off the Oregon coast, shows you what you’ve been missing:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dancing Octopuses', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T21:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte