l reasons” and that Olga Borodina would not sing the role of Eboli on the Metropolitan Opera’s two-week tour of Japan in June.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/met-opera-singers-pull-out-of-japan-tour/', 'snippet': 'Jonas Kaufmann withdrew from the title role of “Don Carlo” for “personal reasons” and that Olga Borodina would not sing the role of Eboli on the Metropolitan Opera’s two-week tour of Japan in June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two star singers have backed out of the Metropolitan Opera’s tour to Japan, the Met said on Thursday. The news is sure to stir dissatisfaction among some members of the company who have expressed worry over safety risks following the nuclear emergency in Japan caused by the March earthquake and resulting tsunami. The Met, citing reassurances from the State Department and experts, has said it was going ahead with the two-week tour in June, and that all company employees — chorus and orchestra members and others — would be required to go. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Opera Singers Pull Out of Japan Tour', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borodina, Olga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gubanova, Ekaterina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufmann, Jonas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T22:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qu