cker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:06:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/83500742-e51a-5875-8a4d-13b6c6d1f244', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83500742-e51a-5875-8a4d-13b6c6d1f244'}, {'abstract': 'Kimani Ng’ang’a Maruge, a member of the Kikuyu tribe in Kenya who enrolled in a primary school in 2003, at age 84, became an inspiration and a lightning rod.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/the-first-grader-justin-chadwicks-tale-of-kenyan-culture-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kimani Ng’ang’a Maruge, a member of the Kikuyu tribe in Kenya who enrolled in a primary school in 2003, at age 84, became an inspiration and a lightning rod.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The First Grader,” directed by Justin Chadwick and written by Ann Peacock, tells the remarkable true story of Kimani Ng’ang’a Maruge, an illiterate member of the Kikuyu tribe in Kenya who enrolled in a rural primary school in 2003, when he was 84. The Kenyan government had recently established universal free education, and in claiming his right to it Mr. Maruge became both an inspiration and a lightning rod. He was invited to New York to address the United Nations, but in his own country his embodiment of the concept of lifelong learning was decidedly controversial.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13first-span/13first-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13first-span/13first-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13first-span/13first-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13first-span/13first-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13first-span/13first-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Simple Quest for Literacy Hits a Wall of Politics', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The First Grader'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Simple Quest for Literacy Hits a Wall of Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illiteracy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chadwick, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bacc458-f7e3-516e-a4dd-12e7a33deb3e', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bacc458-f7e3-516e-a4dd-12e7a33deb3e'}, {'abstract': 'It remains to be seen whether Glencore can make the transition from a commodities dealer that thrives on secrecy to a transparent public company that must report its finances.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/glencore-to-emerge-from-shadows-with-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'It remains to be seen whether Glencore can make the transition from a commodities dealer that thrives on secrecy to a transparent public company that must report its finances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Tucked away in a small village about 30 minutes from Zurich, Glencore International has grown from a small, secretive trading firm into one of the biggest buyers, sellers and producers of commodities in the last three decades. Behind the scenes, Glencore touches most basic resources, like sugar in coffee and the wires in cellphones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore to Emerge From Shadows With I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glasenberg, Ivan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Marc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5233e6c-081d-57b0-b576-65d90d70993c', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5233e6c-081d-57b0-b576-65d90d70993c'}, {'abstract': '“The Big Bang” carries film noir parody into particle physics territory to try to solve the mystery to end all mysteries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/the-big-bang-with-antonio-banderas-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Big Bang” carries film noir parody into particle physics territory to try to solve the mystery to end all mysteries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smirking at its own putative cleverness, “The Big Bang” carries film noir parody into previously unexplored territory — particle physics — to address, if not to solve, the mystery to end all mysteries. Its resident madman, Simon Kestral (Sam Elliott), who with the help of a kinky physicist has built a particle collider under the New Mexico desert, is a multibillionaire with below-the-shoulders silver tresses, a death-rattle voice and a taste for psychedelics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BIG-span/BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BIG-span/BIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BIG-span/BIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BIG-span/BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13BIG-span/BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Taste for Psychedelics and the God Particle', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Big Bang'", 'c