ect', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c56b73-b169-58f3-af74-7d74b8756c02', 'word_count': 25, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c56b73-b169-58f3-af74-7d74b8756c02'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: Restaurant employees must wear plastic gloves when handling food. But shouldn’t they change them to clean up, smoke and wipe their noses?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/complaint-box-gloves-that-go-everywhere/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s Complaint Box: Restaurant employees must wear plastic gloves when handling food. But shouldn’t they change them to clean up, smoke and wipe their noses?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York City health code mandates that all fast food restaurant employees must wear plastic gloves when handling or serving food. I think we can all agree that this is a good rule.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaint Box | Gloves That Go Everywhere', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marlow, Russell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:3