 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27416a56-8ff9-587e-9a72-1e28b5cfd1b2', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27416a56-8ff9-587e-9a72-1e28b5cfd1b2'}, {'abstract': 'Leanne Pooley’s film looks at the phenomenon of the Topps, country-singing lesbian twins from New Zealand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/the-topp-twins-untouchable-girls-review.html', 'snippet': 'Leanne Pooley’s film looks at the phenomenon of the Topps, country-singing lesbian twins from New Zealand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may never have heard of Jools and Lynda Topp, country-singing lesbian twins from New Zealand, but it’s not because of their retiring personalities. Boisterous, big-voiced and built to last, these musical sisters have carved successful careers by doing what most people only dream of: that is, exactly as they please.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13topp-span/ROUNDUP-7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13topp-span/ROUNDUP-7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13topp-span/ROUNDUP-7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13topp-span/ROUNDUP-7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13topp-span/ROUNDUP-7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boisterous, Big-Voiced and Built to Last', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'The Topp Twins: Untouchable Girls'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-12T23:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/de2b7ae7-9187-54ea-a438-121a1fba8f94', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2b7ae7-9187-54ea-a438-121a1fba8f94'}, {'abstract': 'The father of a kindergartner at Sidwell Friends School in Washington filed a lawsuit claiming that the school’s psychologist had an affair with his wife while treating his daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/education/13sidwell.html', 'snippet': 'The father of a kindergartner at Sidwell Friends School in Washington filed a lawsuit claiming that the school’s psychologist had an affair with his wife while treating his daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The father of a kindergartner at Sidwell Friends, one of the most prestigious private schools in Washington, filed a lawsuit on Thursday against the school and its former psychologist, claiming that the psychologist had an affair with his wife while treating his daughter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Father Sues Elite Washington School, Saying Psychologist Had Affair With His Wife', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Father Sues Elite Washington School, Saying Psychologist Had Affair With His Wife', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sidwell Friends School', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists',