://video/e4058ac5-564e-5249-b013-20b12bf86f72', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e4058ac5-564e-5249-b013-20b12bf86f72'}, {'abstract': 'An entire floor at 1 Prudential Plaza, which looks out on the city’s prized Millennium Park downtown, will be the home President Obama’s re-election effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/us/politics/13campaign.html', 'snippet': 'An entire floor at 1 Prudential Plaza, which looks out on the city’s prized Millennium Park downtown, will be the home President Obama’s re-election effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — A clump of reporters and photographers on Thursday got a glimpse of the new Chicago headquarters for President Obama’s re-election effort. An entire floor at 1 Prudential Plaza, which looks out on the city’s prized Millennium Park downtown, will be the campaign’s home — only a few blocks from the 2008 headquarters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Chicago, a Peek at Home Base for a Re-Election Bid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Chicago, a Peek at Home Base for a Re-Election Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T00:12:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f2f801c-492d-57e2-a225-69416f0696e6', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f2f801c-492d-57e2-a225-69416f0696e6'}, {'abstract': 'The Oscar-winning career of Jack Cardiff, a cinematographer for the Archers and others, covered almost a century of the movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/cameraman-the-life-and-work-of-jack-cardiff-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Oscar-winning career of Jack Cardiff, a cinematographer for the Archers and others, covered almost a century of the movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Obsessive fans of the exuberant and enchanting British filmmaking team the Archers — Michael Powell (1905-90), who largely directed, and Emeric Pressburger (1902-88), who largely wrote the screenplays — will not want to miss “Cameraman,” a documentary about Jack Cardiff, the cinematographer behind some of their most indelible images. A specialist in Technicolor from its early days, Cardiff was best known for the lush, painterly compositions in Archer films like the fantastical “Matter of Life and Death,” his first feature as cinematographer; “Black Narcissus,” for which a mountaintop Indian monastery was vividly created at Pinewood Studios, and for which he won an Oscar; and “The Red Shoes,” widely regarded as the definitive film about ballet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13camera/ROUNDUP-6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 801, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13camera/ROUNDUP-6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/13camera/ROUNDUP-6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting for the Stars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Movie Review | 'Cameraman: The Life and Work of Jack Cardiff'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardiff, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T00:15:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/23941de7-11bb-53bc-97f7-6956c7e38f67', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23941de7-11bb-53bc-97f7-6956c7e38f67'}, {'abstract': 'Rescuers will try to capture a mother hawk and treat her injured leg.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/hawk-cam-rescue-on-the-ledge/', 'snippet': 'Rescuers will try to capture a mother hawk and treat her injured leg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 8:15 p.m. |  A medical rescue team, which spent Thursday observing Violet, the red-tailed hawk and new mother with an injured leg, decided not to try to take her from her nest high above Washington Square Park in order to treat her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Rescue on the Ledge', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl