kly learning that even the most well-intentioned plans can get swept up by politics and the sometimes divisive preferences of the taxi and livery cab industries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steps to Help Taxi Service Outside Manhattan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steps to Help Taxi Service Outside Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mateo, Fernando', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York State Federation of Taxi Drivers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vacca, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T00:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1c35fac-fbff-5251-8162-7fe698ee58da', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1c35fac-fbff-5251-8162-7fe698ee58da'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for May 12, 2011, from New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for May 12, 2011, from New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 12, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T00:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a930e70-fd50-5141-a638-937a1dbb61ef', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a930e70-fd50-5141-a638-937a1dbb61ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Libyan opposition needs financial support and diplomatic recognition to defeat Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/opinion/13elwarfally.html', 'snippet': 'The Libyan opposition needs financial support and diplomatic recognition to defeat Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN late February, as the Libyan opposition gained strength, the regime of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi predicted there would be “rivers of blood” and “hundreds of thousands of dead” because of the uprising. At the time, little stood between him and this chilling threat. But thanks to decisive action from the United States and the international community, the pulse of freedom still beats strong in opposition-controlled areas of Libya. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Libyan Resistance Needs', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What the Libyan Resistance Needs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T00:55:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mahmoud Gebril Elwarfally', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mahmoud', 'middlename': 'Gebril', 'lastname': 'Elwarfally', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b16e4c75-c040-51e9-b0b5-881dc5c704b1', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b16e4c75-c040-51e9-b0b5-881dc5c704b1'}, {'abstract': '“Make Believe” follows teenagers competing at an international magic contest in Las Vegas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/movies/make-believe-documentary-review.html', 'snippet': '“Make Believe” follows teenagers competing at an international magic contest in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With teenagers so camera-conscious today, it’s almost impossible to capture them looking genuine in a documentary or reality show; every smart remark or screaming meltdown feels staged for the lens. But not in “Make Believe,” J. Clay Tweel’s charming look at a very small subset of teenagers: those who are interested in becoming magicians. The young people seen here never seem artificial; you feel their passion for doing magic, as well as their nagging loneliness, devoted as they are to practicing card tricks and such for hours on end, while their peers are off doing what most teenagers do.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ