ugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f119399-65b8-5408-9412-c42034f324fe', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f119399-65b8-5408-9412-c42034f324fe'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kahn found success with supermarkets, and then helped create Staples, the office supply retailer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/business/13kahn.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kahn found success with supermarkets, and then helped create Staples, the office supply retailer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leo Kahn, whose success in pioneering big-box, warehouse-style supermarkets led him to join with another entrepreneur in 1986 to start Staples, the retail chain that calls itself the “office superstore,” died on Wednesday in Boston. He was 94. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/business/KAHN-obit/KAHN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/business/KAHN-obit/KAHN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leo Kahn, Trailblazer in Big-Box Retailing, Dies at 94', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leo Kahn, Trailblazer in Big-Box Retailing, Dies at 94', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staples Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6afa0eab-c162-55b5-8b46-fe4cda3fdad2', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6afa0eab-c162-55b5-8b46-fe4cda3fdad2'}, {'abstract': 'Barry Irwin, the loquacious chief of Team Valor, criticized trainers after Animal Kingdom’s victory and has since increased security for the colt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/sports/tough-talk-after-winning-the-derby.html', 'snippet': 'Barry Irwin, the loquacious chief of Team Valor, criticized trainers after Animal Kingdom’s victory and has since increased security for the colt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes, Barry Irwin admits, he is his own worst enemy and says things before thinking about them. He did it last Saturday on national television moments after his colt Animal Kingdom won the Kentucky Derby. Irwin openly questioned the honesty of the trainers who send horses out to race every week at tracks around the United States.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/sports/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/sports/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/sports/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN/SUB-Y-JP-IRWIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',