ss action, the court provided other corporations with a model of how they can avoid class actions. It gave companies even more power when it also ruled out class-based arbitrations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gutting Class Action', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gutting Class Action: The five conservatives of the Supreme Court chose corporations over everyone else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breyer, Stephen G', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7660aa6-1c05-5276-9774-5d4122cbb04a', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7660aa6-1c05-5276-9774-5d4122cbb04a'}, {'abstract': 'A day after rebels reclaimed the airport in Misurata, reporters were shown three huge water-filled NATO bomb craters in Tripoli at the site of the Bab al-Aziziya government compound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/12/world/africa/20110513_LIBYA.html', 'snippet': 'A day after rebels reclaimed the airport in Misurata, reporters were shown three huge water-filled NATO bomb craters in Tripoli at the site of the Bab al-Aziziya government compound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A day after rebels reclaimed the airport in Misurata, reporters were shown three huge water-filled NATO bomb craters in Tripoli at the site of the Bab al-Aziziya government compound.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/world/africa/20110513_LIBYA-slide-5J48/20110513_LIBYA-slide-5J48-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle for Libya | May 12', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2b233404-8c51-55bd-8818-2e7a48b3148b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2b233404-8c51-55bd-8818-2e7a48b3148b'}, {'abstract': 'The Gators’ second-year team, which has become an improbable contender for the national championship, plays Stanford on Saturday in a first-round game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/sports/at-florida-womens-lacrosse-fast-becomes-familiar.html', 'snippet': 'The Gators’ second-year team, which has become an improbable contender for the national championship, plays Stanford on Saturday in a first-round game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Janine Hillier arrived at Florida as a freshman last school year, she proudly told some math classmates that she played for the Gators’ new women’s lacrosse team. Then they looked at her as if she were speaking in differential equations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed