erial': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed8ce75e-473c-5e51-b637-925d1d382ab6', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed8ce75e-473c-5e51-b637-925d1d382ab6'}, {'abstract': 'The warm weather in New York City brought men’s chests out into the open, as well as pollen that causes sneezing, itchy eyes and runny noses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/nyregion/great-day-to-be-outdoors-in-new-york-if-not-for-allergies.html', 'snippet': 'The warm weather in New York City brought men’s chests out into the open, as well as pollen that causes sneezing, itchy eyes and runny noses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noon, Thursday, in the sun-soaked spring lushness of Bryant Park. A chain reaction of male shirtlessness begins with a young man in sneakers stripping down to his summer shorts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/Y-WEATHER1/Y-WEATHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/Y-WEATHER1/Y-WEATHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/Y-WEATHER1/Y-WEATHER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/Y-WEATHER1/Y-WEATHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/Y-WEATHER1/Y-WEATHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Great Day to Be Outside, If It Weren’t for Allergies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Great Day to Be Outside, If It Weren’t for Allergies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70144403-4b91-5bdc-b240-91fff0ab8242', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70144403-4b91-5bdc-b240-91fff0ab8242'}, {'abstract': 'Players are seeking a minimum of $707 million in damages, and an injunction to prevent the N.F.L. from using television revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/sports/football/in-court-players-push-nfl-in-tv-case.html', 'snippet': 'Players are seeking a minimum of $707 million in damages, and an injunction to prevent the N.F.L. from using television revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — More than two months after a federal judge ruled that the N.F.L. failed to maximize revenue in its renegotiated television deals, lawyers for the locked-out players returned to United States District Court on Thursday seeking a minimum of $707 million in damages, as well as an injunction to prevent the league from accepting more than $4 billion in television revenue during the lockout.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Players Push N.F.L. for Money in TV Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Players Push N.F.L. For Money In TV Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doty, David S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:27:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e35c88ef-876f-51a5-9d92-aae1da248c0d', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e35c88ef-876f-51a5-9d92-aae1da248c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should set tight caps on what former officials can earn from lobbying before they must register as lobbyists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/opinion/13fri3.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should set tight caps on what former officials can earn from lobbying before they must register as lobbyists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meredith Attwell Baker, one of two Republicans on the Federal Communications Commission, was not on Comcast’s payroll when she voted to approve its controversial acquisition of NBC Universal, the television powerhouse. But she soon will be. Four months after she endorsed the deal — chastising the F.C.C. for delaying its approval and imposing too many conditions on the merger — she has been hired to be NBC’s top Washington lobbyist. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Didn’t Take Long', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Didn&#8217;t Take Long', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Meredith Attwell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1166f1cd-9fd0-52ca-a8d3-7829b01c6a04', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1166f1cd-9fd0-52ca-a8d3-7829b01c6a04'}, {'abstract': 'The conflict in Libya has been, by almost any human measure, a sorrow, with thousands of people killed, but, among the many emotions are moments of relief, like that in the airport hangar on Thursday, as the siege of Misurata appeared to be nearing an end.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/for-libyan-rebels-a-light-moment-in-a-doleful-war/', 'snippet': 'The conflict in Libya has been, by almost any human measure, a sorrow, with thousands of people killed, but, among the many emotions are moments of relief, like that in the airport hangar on Thursday, as the siege of Misurata appeared to be nearin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MISURATA, Libya — If the official statements by the government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi about the battle for this city were true, then much that was visible around the airport on Thursday did not actually happen or exist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Libyan Rebels, a Light Moment in a Doleful War', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Misurata (Libya)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T01:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C.J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49cd14d-e96d-5b02-952b-da7a7a84edc8', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49cd14d-e96d-5b02-952b-da7a7a84edc8'}, {'abstract': 'Bartolo Colon underwent a novel procedure involving injection of stem cells in the spring of 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/sports/baseball/yankees-to-look-at-colons-disclosure-of-his-medical-past.html', 'snippet': 'Bartolo Colon underwent a novel procedure involving injection of stem cells in the spring of 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a standard bit of protocol for players joining a major league baseball team: providing a full medical history, including operations, injections and other treatments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/sports/Y-COLON/Y-COLON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, '