eads: “Every length of answer from 3 to 15 letters – except one – appears in this puzzle. Some people might have a 1-Across about that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday: Hard to Nail Down', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb82f083-e834-55d0-829d-3bab2d25eb31', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb82f083-e834-55d0-829d-3bab2d25eb31'}, {'abstract': 'Next week is the deadline for terminating combat operations that have not been authorized by Congress and it seems there is no intention of pulling out of NATO’s bombing campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/africa/13powers.html', 'snippet': 'Next week is the deadline for terminating combat operations that have not been authorized by Congress and it seems there is no intention of pulling out of NATO’s bombing campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama and his legal advisers are deliberating about how the United States military may lawfully continue participating in NATO’s bombing campaign in Libya after next week, when the air war will reach a legal deadline for terminating combat operations that have not been authorized by Congress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Deadline, U.S. Seeks to Continue War in Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Deadline, U.S. Seeks To Continue War in Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Powers Act (1973)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7126b363-c5f8-5c5a-80fd-5355ed9f909d', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7126b363-c5f8-5c5a-80fd-5355ed9f909d'}, {'abstract': 'The panel was set up last year by the Department of Energy after President Obama canceled a longstanding plan to bury waste at Yucca Mountain, a site in the Nevada desert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/science/earth/13waste.html', 'snippet': 'The panel was set up last year by the Department of Energy after President Obama canceled a longstanding plan to bury waste at Yucca Mountain, a site in the Nevada desert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A commission created to help resolve the impasse over the disposal of the nation’s nuclear waste will propose establishing one or more sites where used reactor fuel could be stored in steel and concrete structures on the earth’s surface for decades, members of the commission said this week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panel on Nuclear Waste Disposal to Propose Above-Ground Storage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panel on Nuclear Waste Disposal to Propose Above-Ground Storage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yucca Mountain (Nev)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5312c823-0797-5bf1-a563-7960ddf2d02c', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5312c823-0797-5bf1-a563-7960ddf2d02c'}, {'abstract': 'After the Miami Heat eliminated the Boston Celtics in five games, LeBron James said he was sorry for the way he left Cleveland.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/12/in-his-triumph-james-apologizes/', 'snippet': 'After the Miami Heat eliminated the Boston Celtics in five games, LeBron James said he was sorry for the way he left Cleveland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — On the night he finally vanquished the Boston Celtics, LeBron James was consumed by an odd blend of emotions: elation and contrition, satisfaction and vindication. In the moment, it all made sense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In His Triumph, James Apologizes', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3cd488-0f59-5d59-98fe-1896fcb476b3', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3cd488-0f59-5d59-98fe-1896fcb476b3'}, {'abstract': 'Security forces have detained a woman believed to be involved in a riot last weekend that left at least 12 dead and two churches in flames, officials said on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/africa/13briefs-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Security forces have detained a woman believed to be involved in a riot last weekend that left at least 12 dead and two churches in flames, officials said on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Security forces have detained a woman believed to be at the center of a riot between Muslim and Christian mobs last weekend that left at least 12 dead and two churches in flames, Interior Ministry officials said on Thursday. Officials said the woman, who identified herself as Abeer Fakhri, 25, was a Coptic Christian who had left her Christian husband for a Muslim man and sought to convert to Islam. When the Muslim man and about 20 other men arrived at the church where he believed she was being held, sectarian street battles erupted. Ms. Fakhri, who has done television interviews, said church authorities had detained her while they encouraged her not to convert. She said she called her Muslim boyfriend, who called the police, but when an officer called she was afraid to speak to him. Her account could not be confirmed. The Coptic Church forbids divorce, and reports of Coptic women converting to end a marriage are common. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Woman Held Over Riot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Woman Held Over Riot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coptic Orthodox Church of Alexandria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/73b10a38-3936-521b-b851-3c48118c0fb9', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73b10a38-3936-521b-b851-3c48118c0fb9'}, {'abstract': 'The French authorities are dropping terrorism charges against 24 members of an Iranian dissident group for lack of evidence, court documents show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/world/europe/13briefs-France.html', 'snippet': 'The French authorities are dropping terrorism charges against 24 members of an Iranian dissident group for lack of evidence, court documents show.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The French authorities are dropping terrorism charges against 24 members of an Iranian dissident group for lack of evidence, \xa0court documents show, nearly eight years after a sensational raid on the organization’s headquarters amid charges that the group was planning attacks in Europe. The police arrested 120 people in the raid on the offices of the group, the People’s Mujahedeen Organization of Iran, which wants to overthrow the Iranian government, in a Paris suburb in 2003. Most were released, but 24 people were held on terrorism or terrorism-financing charges. The authorities said the organization had been plotting to attack Iranian embassies and assassinate former members working with Iranian intelligence services in Europe. In a ruling dated Wednesday, the investigating judges found that there were no grounds for proceeding with indictments for terrorism or terrorism financing. The group’s lawyer, William Bourdon, said the judges based their decision partly on “a legitimate right to resist tyranny,” as well as the fact that there was no evidence that the group had ever been responsible for attacks on civilians. Nine members of the group remain under investigation for financial wrongdoing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Terrorism Charges Dropped Against Iranian Group', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Terrorism Charges Dropped Against Iranian Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Mujahedeen of Iran", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:14:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c507bc2-d03a-570f-8066-40d69cc8981e', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c507bc2-d03a-570f-8066-40d69cc8981e'}, {'abstract': 'The schools will be in a federal program in which nonprofit agencies try to manage them better than the city did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/nyregion/9-low-scoring-new-york-high-schools-to-stay-open.html', 'snippet': 'The schools will be in a federal program in which nonprofit agencies try to manage them better than the city did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a sense of relief at nine low-performing city high schools on Thursday as the city’s Department of Education announced they would not be closed next year. The decisions came after months of uncertainty about the schools’ future.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine City High Schools to Stay Open, With Private Management', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine City High Schools to Stay Open, With Private Management', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T02:16:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1abee70-d832-53eb-b2f5-9dacdd57e1d0', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1abee70-d832-53eb-b2f5-9dacdd57e1d0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hoffman’s life seemed to be lifted straight from the tabloids. Divorced from the woman known as the Mayflower Madam, he was a lawyer for the man known as the Subway Vigilante.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/nyregion/darnay-hoffman-dies-at-63-lawyer-with-notorious-clients.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hoffman’s life seemed to be lifted straight from the tabloids. Divorced from the woman known as the Mayflower Madam, he was a lawyer for the man known as the Subway Vigilante.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Darnay Hoffman’s life seemed to be lifted straight from the tabloids. Divorced from the woman known as the Mayflower Madam, he was a lawyer for the man known as the Subway Vigilante, as well as for a notorious child killer. He also played a minor role in the case of JonBenet Ramsey, the 6-year-old beauty pageant winner who was killed in 1996.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/HOFFMAN-obit/HOFFMAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/HOFFMAN-obit/HOFFMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/nyregion/HOFFMAN-obit/HOFFMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Darnay Hoffman Dies at 6