mmy of the spring auction previews from the Christie’s auction house and the Hong Kong International Art Fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art fairs and auctions are usually seen as playgrounds for high-flying insiders, like dealers and collectors. What most travelers don’t know is that they are often also open to the public. And in Hong Kong, a city with tepid museum options, they are often a better bet than the places written about in travel guides. The trick is being in town at the right time and finding events that are not widely advertised.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hong Kong, Art Fair and Auction Share Spotlight', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Hor-Chung Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': 'Hor-chung', 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7feac09-8f7d-5502-a5d7-daca0d8f6e45', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7feac09-8f7d-5502-a5d7-daca0d8f6e45'}, {'abstract': 'The former Cowboy had a remarkable friendship with Everson Walls, who saved him by donating a kidney.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/ron-springss-death-and-revisiting-a-gift-of-life/', 'snippet': 'The former Cowboy had a remarkable friendship with Everson Walls, who saved him by donating a kidney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Cowboys running back Ron Springs died on Thursday at 54, having never awoken from a coma after a mishap during a minor operation in 2007. Eight months before, Everson Walls, a former teammate on the Cowboys, donated a kidney to help keep Springs alive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ron Springs’s Death, and Revisiting a Gift of Life', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springs, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walls, Everson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T10:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a3912b0-4458-5079-b2de-70f0d303c97d', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a3912b0-4458-5079-b2de-70f0d303c97d'}, {'abstract': 'A Firefox extension lets you organize all your downloads in a separate tab in your browser.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/tip-of-the-week-cleaning-up-firefox-downloads/', 'snippet': 'A Firefox extension lets you organize all your downloads in a separate tab in your browser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you use the Mozilla Firefox browser and do not like the program’s Downloads window cluttering your screen when you are snagging files off the Web, you can tidy things up with the Downloads in Tab add-on. As its name suggests, Downloads in Tab gives you the option to display the Downloads window as a separate tab within your existing browser — instead of as a free-floating window that can get lost in the shuffle. The add-on is available on Mozilla’s site here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Cleaning Up Firefox Downloads', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mozilla Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T10:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/09e18ee4-379c-5ac1-ab1b-becb304985aa', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09e18ee4-379c-5ac1-ab1b-becb304985aa'}, {'abstract': 'The dancer from the Girl Walk//All Day video tries some moves at Yankee Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/an-illegal-act-and-an-invitation-to-dance/', 'snippet': 'The dancer from the Girl Walk//All Day video tries some moves at Yankee Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday night, a free-spirited, freestyle dancer named Anne Marsen was booted out of Yankee Stadium. Her crime? Making a really great dance video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Illegal Act and an Invitation to Dance', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tough, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yankee Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T10:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b63211-133f-542f-a51b-4e0ab63d5708', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b63211-133f-542f-a51b-4e0ab63d5708'}, {'abstract': 'The smash Broadway musical “The Book of Mormon” took a tortuous route to the stage, including the departure of a director, before earning 14 Tony nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/theater/theaterspecial/the-path-of-the-book-of-mormon-to-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'The smash Broadway musical “The Book of Mormon” took a tortuous route to the stage, including the departure of a director, before earning 14 Tony nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was February 2010, and Scott Rudin, the prolific theater and film producer, felt something was wrong with “The Book of Mormon,” the new musical he was developing. A weeks-long workshop had just ended, he recalled, and the show’s main character was an unlikable prig, the tone was muddled, and some of the humor wasn’t worthy of his two star creators, Trey Parker and Matt Stone of the animated series “South Park.” Mr. Parker, usually the engine of ideas, felt stalled, and the musical just seemed to be drifting toward an Off Broadway run set for that summer, all three men said recently.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/MORMON-4/MORMON-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/MORMON-4/MORMON-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/MORMON-4/MORMON-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/MORMON-4/MORMON-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/MORMON-4/MORMON-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Twisty Road to Uganda and Broadway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Twisty Road To Uganda And Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Theater Workshop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Trey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T11:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fe2b95-0047-5de3-8d3b-d7e176ef1aa4', 'word_count': 1844, 'uri