: 'Sometimes a paycheck is about more than money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15Lives-t.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a paycheck is about more than money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were a couple of dozen costumes to choose from — Superman and spaceman and muscleman and Popeye and, inexplicably, Baby Huey — but unless the customer had something specific in mind, I went with the gorilla suit every time. I delivered cakes and flowers and balloons. I sang songs upon request. I was just old enough for it to be a horrible job. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15lives/15lives-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 617, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15lives/15lives-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15lives/15lives-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Monkey Suit', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Monkey Suit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T12:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb1be583-5b76-5aa8-ac43-7d52279bd36a', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb1be583-5b76-5aa8-ac43-7d52279bd36a'}, {'abstract': 'Dealing straight; getting even.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15Ethicist-t.html', 'snippet': 'Dealing straight; getting even.', 'lead_paragraph': ' My supermarket has a card that must be swiped to get the “on sale” price on many items. I know that the supermarket is amassing and perhaps even selling information that I would rather it not have. What if, for example, my insurance company raises my rates because I buy butter? I have an idea of swapping cards among others at my church who share my values about Big Brother. That way we can enjoy the discounts while preserving something of our privacy. What is my ethical obligation? PAUL DAVID WADLER, PH.D. CHICAGO ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Card Games', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CARD GAMES', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T12:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6f29d92-4152-5f30-95e0-195d9d0a94c5', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6f29d92-4152-5f30-95e0-195d9d0a94c5'}, {'abstract': '“I’ll never forget the first time I read Sam Anderson’s article about reading Luca Spaghetti’s memoir.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/my-thoughts-on-reading-sam-andersons-essay.html', 'snippet': '“I’ll never forget the first time I read Sam Anderson’s article about reading Luca Spaghetti’s memoir.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ll never forget the first time I read Sam Anderson’s article about reading Luca Spaghetti’s memoir. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '65', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Thoughts on Reading Sam Anderson’s Essay', 'kicker': 'Bonus Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Thoughts on Reading Sam Anderson’s Essay About Reading Luca Spaghetti’s Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Sam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T12:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3cefc3-8ff7-5dcd-a888-5e9bdc99529a', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3cefc3-8ff7-5dcd-a888-5e9bdc99529a'}, {'abstract': 'The entrepreneurs who want to restore America’s ability to make stuff — one homemade, molten-plastic iPad stand at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/the-kitchen-table-industrialists.html', 'snippet': 'The entrepreneurs who want to restore America’s ability to make stuff — one homemade, molten-plastic iPad stand at a time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in 2007, Ayah Bdeir was working in a plush office in Midtown Manhattan, making a lot of money and feeling miserable. She was a financial-software consultant for a technology company. One of her specialties was peddling software for credit-default swaps — among the many complex financial instruments that would soon wreak havoc on the planet. Somewhere there was a thing from which these derivatives were derived, but Bdeir, atop countless layers of transacting, was too far away to see it, much less touch it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15meetthemakers_span/mag-15DIY-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15meetthemakers_span/mag-15DIY-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15meetthemakers_span/mag-15DIY-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15meetthemakers_span/15meetthemakers_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15meetthemakers_span/15meetthemakers_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kitchen-Table Industrialists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MEET THE MAKERS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T12:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anand Giridharadas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anand', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giridharadas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f12825b1-e66a-562c-a729-a25784bbf749', 'word_count': 2867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f12825b1-e66a-562c-a729-a25784bbf749'}, {'abstract': 'Gratitude, mysticism and the banality two weeks after everything was ripped apart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/recovering-from-twisters-in-rural-north-carolina.html', 'snippet': 'Gratitude, mysticism and the banality two weeks after everything was ripped apart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the middle of a field, among the possessions strewn there by the tornado, all of them somehow embarrassing in their blown-open intimacy, the guts of obscure rooms — plastic organizers from inside closets, Kmart-level guitar gear somebody wailed on deep in the night — there lay an old LP of Handel’s “Water Music” suites, performed by the Philadelphia Orchestra. Repeated soakings left it unplayable-looking, but the indigo of its Columbia Masterworks label remained iridescent in the twilight.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15here_span/mag-15Here-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15here_span/mag-15Here-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15here_span/mag-15Here-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15here_span/mag-15Here-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/15here_span/mag-15Here-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recovering From Twisters in Rural North Carolina', 'kicker': 'You Are Here', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘THAT’S LUCKY.’ ‘THAT’S GOD.’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T12:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN JEREMIAH SULLIVAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Jeremiah', 'lastname': 'SULLIVAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4655a57-cb5b-5863-baac-614c4dfa3890', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4655a57-cb5b-5863-baac-614c4dfa3890'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, the country is recovering — by forgetting about banking and rediscovering its essential weirdness. Ever try cod sperm?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/magazine/icelands-big-economic-thaw.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, the country is recovering — by forgetting about banking and rediscovering its essential weirdness. Ever try cod sperm?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to understand what happened in Iceland — the whole story of the crash, the banks failing, the recent signs of recovery — start at the prime minister’s office in downtown Reykjavik and continue east for a bit until you ascend a steep bluff overlooking the icy waters of Faxafloi Bay. There you will arrive at a used-car lot. Ask for the owner of this establishment, who is a short, 61-year-old man with extremely thick glasses named Gudfinnur S. Halldorsson — he goes by the name Guffi (pronounced Goofy) — and have him to tell you the story of the Porsche that kept on giving. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15iceland-t_CA0/mag-15iceland-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15iceland-t_CA0/mag-15iceland-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15iceland-t_CA0/mag-15iceland-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15iceland-t_CA0/mag-15iceland-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/magazine/mag-15iceland-t_CA0/mag-15iceland-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iceland’s Big Thaw', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE BIG THAW', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'},