 Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ddf101-3bcd-5900-8619-a45088829892', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ddf101-3bcd-5900-8619-a45088829892'}, {'abstract': 'At Danziger Projects in Manhattan,  a show of Kate Moss photographs: a favorite image selected by each of 11 leading photographers, working with Ms. Moss.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/gathering-photos-of-kate-moss/', 'snippet': 'At Danziger Projects in Manhattan,  a show of Kate Moss photographs: a favorite image selected by each of 11 leading photographers, working with Ms. Moss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those of us who follow fashion and photography tend to have a favorite image of Kate Moss. I have two: Corinne Day’s portrait (styled by Melanie Ward) of a laughing and feather-headdressed Kate for a 1990 cover of The Face; and Mario Sorrenti’s 1993 image of her, with its deep shadow and her eyes looking at once tender and wary. The early ’90s announced a more stripped-down view of fashion — call it grunge, if you like — and the waif Kate fit the bill as she inspired an industry. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gathering Photos of Kate Moss', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Kate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/86abcf32-ab02-52d6-bdfc-79b4a02a4207', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86abcf32-ab02-52d6-bdfc-79b4a02a4207'}, {'abstract': 'On our hardcover list this week, “S.H.I.E.L.D.: Architects of Forever” (no. 10), uncovers some big secrets about the Marvel Universe.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/graphic-books-best-sellers-long-lost-heroes/', 'snippet': 'On our hardcover list this week, “S.H.I.E.L.D.: Architects of Forever” (no. 10), uncovers some big secrets about the Marvel Universe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Undiscovered truths are a big part of comic-book stories. On our hardcover list this week, “S.H.I.E.L.D.: Architects of Forever” (No. 10) shares some big secrets about the Marvel Universe. The story, by Jonathan Hickman and Dustin Weaver, collects the first six issues of an adventure that reveals how some luminaries of the past – including Leonardo Da Vinci, Michelangelo and Isaac Newton – protected the Marvel Universe long before heroes like Captain America, Iron Man and Spider-Man were born.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Long-Lost Heroes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Entertainment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a57a5e92-3af6-5886-a537-9704218e09d3', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a57a5e92-3af6-5886-a537-9704218e09d3'}, {'abstract': 'While much of Europe has been struggling to bounce back from the financial crisis, German unemployment has declined to a level lower than it was in September 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/business/economy/14charts.html', 'snippet': 'While much of Europe has been struggling to bounce back from the financial crisis, German unemployment has declined to a level lower than it was in September 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE financial crisis and the severe recession that followed destroyed jobs in every industrialized country. While many countries have started to recover, in only one major one, Germany, has unemployment declined to a level lower than it was in September 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jobs Recovery Is Happening Faster for Some Countries Than Others', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jobs Recovery Is Happening Faster for Some Countries Than Others', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:34:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c253954c-3774-5f2a-bca4-1e4feaa0d973', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c253954c-3774-5f2a-bca4-1e4feaa0d973'}, {'abstract': 'Input from New Old Age readers reinforces a research team’s inclination to offer greater public access to a new online tool.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/a-lifespan-predictor-the-readers-have-spoken/', 'snippet': 'Input from New Old Age readers reinforces a research team’s inclination to offer greater public access to a new online tool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s virtually unanimous: About 70 readers (including several who weighed in by e-mail) commented on the plan by palliative care specialists at the University of California, San Francisco, to build a Web site containing tested geriatric calculators that can predict older people’s odds of dying in the coming six months, or four years, or nine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life Span Predictor? The Readers Have Spoken', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc166aa4-e8c2-59a0-bfca-1c0ec3015657', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc166aa4-e8c2-59a0-bfca-1c0ec3015657'}, {'abstract': 'An interactive map from the Census Bureau showing how political and economic forces have moved the center of the United States population from Kent County, Md. in 1790 to Plato, Mo., in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/the-population-shifts-westward/', 'snippet': 'An interactive map from the Census Bureau showing how political and economic forces have moved the center of the United States population from Kent County, Md. in 1790 to Plato, Mo., in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:28 p.m. | Updated The Census Bureau has put together a neat interactive map showing the shifting center of the population, defined as “the place where an imaginary, flat, weightless and rigid map of the United States would balance perfectly if all residents were of identical weight.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Population Shifts Westward', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b2a386d-36ca-5d8e-abc8-0d850f8096d0', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b2a386d-36ca-5d8e-abc8-0d850f8096d0'}, {'abstract': 'Chicago and Miami offer N.B.A. fans a morality play, while Vancouver and San Jose’s biggest N.H.L. opponents have often been themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/sports/nba-and-nhl-conference-finals-charged-with-psychodrama.html', 'snippet': 'Chicago and Miami offer N.B.A. fans a morality play, while Vancouver and San Jose’s biggest N.H.L. opponents have often been themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to hand it to the N.B.A. and the N.H.L. for producing conference finals with great psychodramatic subplots. Now, you don’t have to credit the actual leagues — especially the N.H.L., which was too busy trying to figure out what to do with the Green Men to concoct any actual strategy — but feel free to enjoy the results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Psyched for the Semifinals', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Psyched for the Semifinals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doty, David S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Derrick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f8dc05e-181f-58c3-a29d-c94c00cc8498', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f8dc05e-181f-58c3-a29d-c94c00cc8498'}, {'abstract': 'Killebrew, who announced last year that he was being treated for esophageal cancer, announced his decision in a statement Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/harmon-killebrew-ends-cancer-treatment-and-looks-to-hospice-care/', 'snippet': 'Killebrew, who announced last year that he was being treated for esophageal cancer, announced his decision in a statement Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harmon Killebrew, the brawny slugger who announced last year that he was being treated for esophageal cancer, said in a statement Friday: “With the continued love and support of my wife, Nita, I have exhausted all options with respect to controlling this awful disease. My illness has progressed beyond my doctors’ expectation of cure.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Killebrew Ends Treatment and Looks to Hospice Care', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Killebrew, Harmon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d54f28e4-7753-5a47-beb8-015f4fafa49c', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d54f28e4-7753-5a47-beb8-015f4fafa49c'}, {'abstract': 'With the early hour, conference fatigue and late-night partying, attendance at the morning session of the SkyBridge Alternatives Conference at the Bellagio was as sparse as the dusty landscape surrounding Las Vegas.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/debts-deficits-and-defaults-in-sin-city/', 'snippet': 'With the early hour, conference fatigue and late-night partying, attendance at the morning session of the SkyBridge Alternatives Conference at the Bellagio was as sparse as the dusty landscape surrounding Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Nothing much happens on the Las Vegas Strip at 8 a.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debts, Deficits and Defaults in Sin City', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:44:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e61fad03-7a06-55ea-9ab8-03941b22b160', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e61fad03-7a06-55ea-9ab8-03941b22b160'}, {'abstract': 'The three widows had been held and questioned for days by Pakistani officials before the C.I.A. interrogators spoke to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/world/asia/14widows.html', 'snippet': 'The three widows had been held and questioned for days by Pakistani officials before the C.I.A. interrogators spoke to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — C.I.A. interrogators questioned three wives of Osama bin Laden for the first time on Thursday, 10 days after they were taken by Pakistani security forces from the compound where the Al Qaeda leader was killed, an American official confirmed on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bin Laden Widows in Pakistan Questioned by C.I.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bin Laden Widows in Pakistan Questioned by C.I.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1877ba6-868a-557a-bef1-350853013e48', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1877ba6-868a-557a-bef1-350853013e48'}, {'abstract': 'An effort to come to terms with the unknown consequences that synthetic chemicals may hold for consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/book-review-whats-gotten-into-us-by-mckay-jenkins.html', 'snippet': 'An effort to come to terms with the unknown consequences that synthetic chemicals may hold for consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We all know by now — don’t we? — that many of the synthetic chemicals in our food, personal-\xadcare and cleaning products, toys and household goods are harming not just the environment but ourselves. Body-burden tests, for measuring exposure to chemicals, reveal flame retardants, plasticizers, pesticides and perfluorinated chemicals in the blood of almost every person studied. We see rising rates of some cancers, autoimmune disorders, reproductive illnesses, autism and learning disabilities. Meanwhile, our consumption of synthetic chemicals, a majority of which haven’t been tested for human health impacts, has skyrocketed. A growing number of books make the case that these phenomena are linked.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Royte/Royte-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Royte/Royte-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Royte/Royte-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Sense of a Toxic World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Everyday Perils', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, McKay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Royte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Royte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e29cdd9d-4213-5670-a138-b5b2b70f2b9b', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e29cdd9d-4213-5670-a138-b5b2b70f2b9b'}, {'abstract': '“Crafting Genre: Kathryn Bigelow,” running at the Museum of Modern Art from June 1 through Aug. 13, will highlight movies like “The Hurt Locker” as well as the director’s artistic career.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/moma-calls-action-on-kathryn-bigelow-retrospective/', 'snippet': '“Crafting Genre: Kathryn Bigelow,” running at the Museum of Modern Art from June 1 through Aug. 13, will highlight movies like “The Hurt Locker” as well as the director’s artistic career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could this be the first event at the Museum of Modern Art where a full-body blast suit, a parachute and a rubber Richard M. Nixon mask might be appropriate attire? The museum said on Friday that it would host a retrospective of the works of Kathryn Bigelow, the Academy Award-winning director of films including “The Hurt Locker” and “Point Break.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MoMA Calls ‘Action!’ on Kathryn Bigelow Retrospective', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bigelow, Kathryn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dafoe, Willem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Art Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e9be9e-00ab-568c-995b-3e589c7f7b1f', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e9be9e-00ab-568c-995b-3e589c7f7b1f'}, {'abstract': 'The University of Arizona? University of Colorado, Boulder? The University of Oregon? Kori Hazel, a high school senior from Denver, makes his choice after realizing it is not “the most important” decision in his life, only “the next phase.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/cherry-creek-kori-hazel-3/', 'snippet': 'The University of Arizona? University of Colorado, Boulder? The University of Oregon? Kori Hazel, a high school senior from Denver, makes his choice after realizing it is not “the most important” decision in his life, only “the next phase.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was in an airport restaurant, talking with a complete stranger, that I found myself making the most important decision of my life thus far. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Stranger in an Airport, a Decision Becomes Clear', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:47:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kori C. Hazel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kori', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hazel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbcd8cc6-982e-5061-a0ea-9efa6c9bc386', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbcd8cc6-982e-5061-a0ea-9efa6c9bc386'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the restless, searching people in Edna O’Brien’s stories confront political violence, others reflect on disappointing loves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/book-review-saints-and-sinners-by-edna-obrien.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the restless, searching people in Edna O’Brien’s stories confront political violence, others reflect on disappointing loves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fraughans, bostoons, coolth, coatee, turloughs, chambering, doyleys, billio. These words are all plucked from Edna O’Brien’s sublime new collection of stories, “Saints and Sinners.” To read O’Brien is not only to succumb to her sibyl’s vision of other people’s fates, it’s to fall under the spell of her singular, potent language, which clings to the tactile realities of another century’s earthier, guiltier sensibility — to bogs and turf fires, to poverty and proud airs, lust and furtive \xadpassions.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Schillinger/Schillinger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 866, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Schillinger/Schillinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Schillinger/Schillinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Edna O’Brien’s Elemental Fiction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pint of Virtue, Pint of Vice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Edna", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:51:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview'