hose merger she had recently voted to approve.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/f-c-c-commissioner-defends-taking-comcast-job/', 'snippet': 'Meredith Attwell Baker said she didn’t break any ethical laws by taking a job with the company whose merger she had recently voted to approve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A Federal Communications commissioner who announced this week that she planned to join the lobbying office of Comcast defended her actions on Friday, saying she had no contact with Comcast about a potential job while the company’s takeover of NBC Universal was pending before the commission this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Commissioner Defends Taking Comcast Job', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Meredith Attwell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T16:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/56756714-13b2-5bcd-b85d-db66436269e7', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56756714-13b2-5bcd-b85d-db66436269e7'}, {'abstract': 'Two soldiers say they were swept into a tide of suspicion as the Army investigated unfounded accusations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/us/14muslim.html', 'snippet': 'Two soldiers say they were swept into a tide of suspicion as the Army investigated unfounded accusations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, Khalid Lyaacoubi and Yassine Bahammou, immigrants from Morocco, enlisted in the Army National Guard, recruited for a program that promised higher rank, bonuses and quick citizenship to Arabic speakers who could help fill the military’s need for interpreters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/us/14muslim_337_span/14muslim_337_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/14/us/14muslim_337_span/14muslim_337_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/us/14muslim_337_span/14muslim_337_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/us/14muslim_337_span/14muslim_337_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/us/14muslim_337_span/14muslim_337_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Allegations Upend Lives of 2 Muslims in Army', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unfounded Suspicions Wreak Havoc on Lives Of Two Muslim Soldiers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Guard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:01:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c27326-cd11-536f-90fd-075ec1701d4c', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c27326-cd11-536f-90fd-075ec1701d4c'}, {'abstract': 'Induced pluripotent stem cells appear to have the healing potential of embryonic stem cells without the controversy, but when given to mice, they didn’t survive the immune response.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/science/14stem.html', 'snippet': 'Induced pluripotent stem cells appear to have the healing potential of embryonic stem cells without the controversy, but when given to mice, they didn’t survive the immune response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an unexpected setback to efforts to harness a promising new type of stem cell to treat diseases, researchers reported on Friday that tissues made from those stem cells might be rejected by a patient’s immune system — even though the tissues would be derived from the same patient. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Setback for New Stem Cell Treatment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Noncontroversial Type of Stem Cells Failed a Key Test, Researchers Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells (Embryonic)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:01:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/062b9d91-9dcd-5a93-9a21-c7c51abbc609', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/062b9d91-9dcd-5a93-9a21-c7c51abbc609'}, {'abstract': 'This biography of Lincoln Steffens traces the convictions and delusions of one of the original “muckrakers.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/lincoln-steffens-muckrakers-progress.html', 'snippet': 'This biography of Lincoln Steffens traces the convictions and delusions of one of the original “muckrakers.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'He knew everyone and he went \xadeverywhere. He was a confidant to presidents, a mentor to two of the most influential journalists in American history, a friend to industrialists, artists, ward heelers, Communists and bohemians. He claimed to have spent the rest of his life after college “unlearning” everything he had been taught. He saw through all pretenses, circumventions and lies — even the ones he told himself — until in the end he was hornswoggled by the biggest lie of all.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/BAKER/BAKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/BAKER/BAKER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/BAKER/BAKER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Steffens: Muckraker’s Progress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Muckraker’s Progress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steffens, Lincoln', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c71d6d-773b-5589-a394-34e46bc684fc', 'word_count': 1395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c71d6d-773b-5589-a394-34e46bc684fc'}, {'abstract': 'The MakerBot, a new consumer-grade, desktop-size 3-D printer, makes, or “prints,” three-dimensional objects from molten plastic based on its users designs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/13/arts/design/MakerBot.html', 'snippet': 'The MakerBot, a new consumer-grade, desktop-size 3-D printer, makes, or “prints,” three-dimensional objects from molten plastic based on its users designs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The MakerBot, a new consumer-grade, desktop-size 3-D printer, makes, or “prints,” three-dimensional objects from molten plastic based on its users designs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/design/MakerBot-slide-V67O/MakerBot-slide-V67O-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/design/MakerBot-slide-V67O/MakerBot-slide-V67O-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/13/arts/design/MakerBot-slide-V67O/MakerBot-slide-V67O-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '3-D Art, Ready to Print', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9c44a432-ad12-5627-986a-75bed49cceb0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9c44a432-ad12-5627-986a-75bed49cceb0'}, {'abstract': 'At Lincoln Center this spring, balletgoers will get a crash course in 19th-century ballet, with its overriding themes of adultery and redemption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/arts/dance/onstage-this-spring-crash-course-in-19th-century-ballet-history.html', 'snippet': 'At Lincoln Center this spring, balletgoers will get a crash course in 19th-century ballet, with its overriding themes of adultery and redemption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF the world of Ballet Ever After employed Match.com, a good many entries would run along the following lines: “Handsome prince seeks the ideal beloved. Enjoys hunting, adores the big beyond, and will travel. Is already affianced to a woman he knows well, but seeks to forget this and other minor inconveniences with perfect and irresistible female.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/CLASSICAL-3/CLASSICAL-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/CLASSICAL-3/CLASSICAL-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/CLASSICAL-3/CLASSICAL-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 993, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classic Tales of Temptation in the Woods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classic Tales Of Temptation In the Woods', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Danish Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwest Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7454b609-e48e-5d4e-8869-4565099fb8b4', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7454b609-e48e-5d4e-8869-4565099fb8b4'}, {'abstract': 'A new book delves into the history of the voiture minimum, which was sketched but never built by the Swiss architect.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/architect-as-auto-designer-le-corbusiers-minimum-car/', 'snippet': 'A new book delves into the history of the voiture minimum, which was sketched but never built by the Swiss architect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A “machine for living” was how Le Corbusier famously described his vision for the home. Le Corbusier, the Swiss architect, however, was transfixed by machines of less metaphorical form, like airplanes, ocean liners and locomotives. He called steam shovels and fountain pens the “fauna of the new age.” And he was particularly fascinated with the car, or so argues the author of a new book.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Architect as Auto Designer: Le Corbusier’s Minimum Car', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Corbusier', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citroen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b6b382-e2c6-58d1-a521-ab6140eb23f3', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b6b382-e2c6-58d1-a521-ab6140eb23f3'}, {'abstract': 'The composer Peter Lieberson, who died last month, never let a crisis go to waste. His difficult experiences enriched his imagination, bringing him closer to the music he wanted to write.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/arts/music/peter-liebersons-path-as-a-composer.html', 'snippet': 'The composer Peter Lieberson, who died last month, never let a crisis go to waste. His difficult experiences enriched his imagination, bringing him closer to the music he wanted to write.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PETER LIEBERSON, who wrote music of such visceral intensity that it seemed to startle even him, died last month at 64. If he dealt with his final illness the way he handled previous misfortunes, I suspect he saw it as an opportunity for growth. Peter never let a crisis go to waste. He took a tortuous road toward maturity, and every difficulty enriched his imagination, bringing him closer to the music he was meant to write. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PETER-1/PETER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PETER-1/PETER-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PETER-1/PETER-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PETER-1/PETER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/arts/PETER-1/PETER-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Accessing a Place Of Shaggy Wildness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accessing a Place Of Shaggy Wildness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberson, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca34dbbe-c73d-5b4d-92fb-c2a1c8b48a74', 'word_count': 1460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca34dbbe-c73d-5b4d-92fb-c2a1c8b48a74'}, {'abstract': 'A Times journalist explains how Bernard Madoff pulled off history’s greatest Ponzi scheme, and how he got away with it for so long.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/book-review-the-wizard-of-lies-bernie-madoff-and-the-death-of-trust-by-diana-b-henriques.html', 'snippet': 'A Times journalist explains how Bernard Madoff pulled off history’s greatest Ponzi scheme, and how he got away with it for so long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the Madoff scandal broke in December 2008, the public has been morbidly fascinated by the affair. How had so ordinary a man pulled off the largest swindle in history? How had he gotten away with it for so long? Then there were the casualties. In contrast to so many other financial scandals of the last 20 years, those who lost money this time were not just impersonal institutions — they were real people. And what a spectrum of the world: Jewish philanthropists from the Upper East Side; almost half the membership of the Palm Beach Country Club; rich South Americans; retired accountants living in Florida; the demimonde of Monaco; even, it was whispered, figures from the Russian mafia and the Colombian drug cartels. Some of us could imagine ourselves among the victims; others found a certain voyeuristic pleasure in the financial travails of the rich and famous.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Ahamed/Ahamed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Ahamed/Ahamed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Ahamed/Ahamed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Ahamed/Ahamed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/books/review/Ahamed/Ahamed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Bernard Madoff Did It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leading the Blind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':