b_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/charting-julianna-barwick/', 'snippet': 'Julianna Barwick is an experimental singer/songwriter from Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julianna Barwick is an experimental singer/songwriter from Brooklyn who makes ethereal music with vocal loops and other electronic effects. Her latest album is called “The Magic Place” and she recently performed at Glasslands in Brooklyn. The artist Andrew Kuo charts the show. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting Julianna Barwick', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8538ecfc-cca5-5c74-9a0e-174c0f5c5fdd', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8538ecfc-cca5-5c74-9a0e-174c0f5c5fdd'}, {'abstract': 'A cardiac surgeon who knew little about restaurants found himself taken with a proprietor of Manhattan restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/donatella-arpaia-and-allan-stewart-vows.html', 'snippet': 'A cardiac surgeon who knew little about restaurants found himself taken with a proprietor of Manhattan restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN early 2010, Dr. Allan Stewart, a cardiac surgeon, was challenged by a patient on whom he had operated the previous year, to sign up for the New York City Triathlon. The doctor broke two ribs while training, but soldiered on, knowing his patient had overcome a much bigger obstacle. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/VOWS-2/VOWS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/VOWS-2/VOWS-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/VOWS-2/VOWS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/VOWS-2/VOWS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/fashion/weddings/VOWS-2/VOWS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donatella Arpaia and Allan Stewart', 'kicker': 'Vows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Donatella Arpaia and Allan Stewart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA JANE GROSSMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': 'Jane', 'lastname': 'GROSSMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cfdceea-801a-5df0-876d-3b5e451942c0', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cfdceea-801a-5df0-876d-3b5e451942c0'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/EdChoice-t.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE BOY IN THE MOON: A Father’s Journey to Understand His Extraordinary Son,  by Ian Brown (St. Martin’s, $24.99.) The truth Brown learns from his severely disabled child is a rare one: The life that seems to destroy you is the one you long to embrace.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Editors' Choice | Recent books of particular interest", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:36:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2e3c6a1-7b24-5a5e-9303-1e9422edf77d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2e3c6a1-7b24-5a5e-9303-1e9422edf77d'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/books/review/PaperRow-t.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE SABBATH WORLD: Glimpses of a Different Order of Time,  by Judith Shulevitz (Random House, $15.) Dissatisfied with the frenzied quality of modern life, Shulevitz explores the history and philosophical foundations of the Sabbath, the day of rest. Part spiritual memoir, part religious history, part literary exegesis, this is “a book of richness and depth,” Rebecca Newberger Goldstein wrote here.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/209d5e1d-e38c-5249-913d-f2176944b17b', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/209d5e1d-e38c-5249-913d-f2176944b17b'}, {'abstract': 'The Al Gore problem isn’t about Al Gore.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/algorithms/', 'snippet': 'The Al Gore problem isn’t about Al Gore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Chait gets angry, rightly over Dana Milbank asserting that Mitt Romney has an “Al Gore problem”, seeming insincere whatever he does. As Chait says,', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Algorithms', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6392e0db-291f-5bf8-9421-d6ffc45623fb', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6392e0db-291f-5bf8-9421-d6ffc45623fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Detroit Red Wings won three games in a row to come back from a 0-3 series deficit to the San Jose Sharks. But taking Game 7 was another matter.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/red-wings-comeback-falls-just-short/', 'snippet': 'The Detroit Red Wings won three games in a row to come back from a 0-3 series deficit to the San Jose Sharks. But taking Game 7 was another matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were only two ways Thursday night could end for the Detroit Red Wings: either with the joy of accomplishing one of the greatest playoff comebacks in N.H.L. history, or crushed by falling just short to the San Jose Sharks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Wings Comeback Falls Just Short', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babcock, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holland, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/500472f3-094f-5c79-b9d9-4fe725e77f73', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/500472f3-094f-5c79-b9d9-4fe725e77f73'}, {'abstract': 'The House of Representatives approved a 2011 intelligence authorization bill that increases spending for 16 intelligence agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/houses-passes-intelligence-authorization-bill/', 'snippet': 'The House of Representatives approved a 2011 intelligence authorization bill that increases spending for 16 intelligence agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House of Representatives departed from its usually partisan caviling on Friday and approved a 2011 intelligence authorization bill that increases spending for 16 intelligence agencies, but at a lower level than requested by President Obama. The amount of the increase is classified but is reported to be substantial. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Houses Passes Intelligence Authorization Bill', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b871a450-db08-58f1-babe-89efe4534942', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b871a450-db08-58f1-babe-89efe4534942'}, {'abstract': 'Ric Pipino’s sprawling new beauty destination is more like a really cool apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/salon-glam/', 'snippet': 'Ric Pipino’s sprawling new beauty destination is more like a really cool apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This is going to be the sexiest salon uptown,” said Ric Pipino, whose sprawling new beauty destination, Ric Pipino-Wella Professional Flagship, is more like a really cool apartment. Conceived by Rawlins Calderone Design, the space is superglam, with black and white walls that serve as graphic foil to a colorful mix of vintage and custom furniture and accessories. The front desk is an homage to the ’70s designer Paul Evans, while the slick red “color bar” is pure Donald Judd. Besides a full menu of services, there’s a boutique selling art books and chocolate, and a bar stocked with Scotch and tequila for clients needing something stiffer than Elnett. 115 East 57th Street; (212) 355-5544.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salon Glam', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:45:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/88ad6e69-03c7-52f2-a55c-66f184d4703d', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88ad6e69-03c7-52f2-a55c-66f184d4703d'}, {'abstract': 'The composer and lyricist Adam Gwon and the book writer and lyricist Michelle Elliott are the 2011 recipients of the 2011 Kleban Prize.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/adam-gwon-michelle-elliott-win-lucrative-musical-theater-writing-prizes/', 'snippet': 'The composer and lyricist Adam Gwon and the book writer and lyricist Michelle Elliott are the 2011 recipients of the 2011 Kleban Prize.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The composer and lyricist Adam Gwon and the book writer and lyricist Michelle Elliott are the recipients of the 2011 Kleban Prize, which recognizes talent and promise in musical theater, the sponsors of the prize said this week. Each award comes with a cash prize of $100,000, payable over two years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adam Gwon and Michelle Elliott Win Musical-Theater Writing Prizes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a6c5473-335e-5c3a-816b-ae06707ff910', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a6c5473-335e-5c3a-816b-ae06707ff910'}, {'abstract': 'Navy Seals like Eric Greitens, author of “The Heart and the List,” may have nabbed Osama bin Laden. But can they stop the celebrity invasion of the best-seller list?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/books/review/InsideList-t.html', 'snippet': 'Navy Seals like Eric Greitens, author of “The Heart and the List,” may have nabbed Osama bin Laden. But can they stop the celebrity invasion of the best-seller list?', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIN LADEN BUMP: President Obama isn’t the only one to get a numbers boost from the recent kill operation against Osama bin Laden. Books by and about Navy Seals have also been flying off the shelves. “The Heart and the Fist,” a memoir of derring-do in Iraq, Afghanistan and beyond by Eric Greitens, a Rhodes scholar turned Navy Seal officer turned humanitarian volunteer, lands at No. 9 on the hardcover nonfiction list. Meanwhile over on the paperback list, Marcus Luttrell and Patrick Robinson’s “Lone Survivor: The Eyewitness Account of Operation Redwing and the Lost Heroes of Seal Team 10,” jumps to No. 3, up from No. 18 two weeks ago. (The book, first published in 2007, has spent 61 weeks on the printed paperback list so far, on top of a 38-week run in hardcover.) There’s no sign yet of “Seal Team Six” — a memoir by a former member of the supersecret unit that brought down Bin Laden, which was rushed into stores a few weeks early following the raid — but stay tuned.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/books/review/22insidelist/22insidelist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/books/review/22insidelist/22insidelist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': 'TBR', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/60e9ba3d-d424-5b98-8ca4-5f26087d124c', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60e9ba3d-d424-5b98-8ca4-5f26087d124c'}, {'abstract': 'Michael D. Shear gets reader feedback on which candidate has the best Web video so far. Also, Megan Liberman and Jim Rutenberg discuss the Republican field taking shape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000000818107/caucus--the-youtube-primary.html', 'snippet': 'Michael D. Shear gets reader feedback on which candidate has the best Web video so far. Also, Megan Liberman and Jim Rutenberg discuss the Republican field taking shape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael D. Shear gets reader feedback on which candidate has the best Web video so far. Also, Megan Liberman and Jim Rutenberg discuss the Republican field taking shape.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/us/politics/video-caucus-051311-campaign/video-caucus-051311-campaign-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/12/us/politics/video-caucus-051311-campaign/video-caucus-051311-campaign-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/12/us/politics/video-caucus-051311-campaign/video-caucus-051311-campaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/12/us/politics/video-caucus-051311-campaign/video-caucus-051311-campaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Caucus | The YouTube Primary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:53:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Werschkul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werschkul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0268560a-1c55-5ac9-828e-1f0cf5d03390', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0268560a-1c55-5ac9-828e-1f0cf5d03390'}, {'abstract': 'Dave Ramsey has helped thousands get out of debt, but his investment advice is sometimes questionable.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/dave-ramseys-12-solution/', 'snippet': 'Dave Ramsey has helped thousands get out of debt, but his investment advice is sometimes questionable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of people swear by the philosophy of Dave Ramsey, an up-by-the-bootstraps kind of guy who doles out tough financial advice about getting out of debt and living within your means. His legions of fans call his nationally syndicated radio show to seek his advice, attend his self-help seminars in both big arenas and small church classrooms and buy his best-selling books and DVDs. He’s part entertainer, part financial coach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dave Ramsey’s 12% Solution', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramsey, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/50350706-932b-5939-80da-db953c909596', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50350706-932b-5939-80da-db953c909596'}, {'abstract': 'The once-exotic bird is becoming a notorious pest as it enjoys a population explosion in many London suburbs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/science/earth/14parakeet.html', 'snippet': 'The once-exotic bird is becoming a notorious pest as it enjoys a population explosion in many London suburbs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STANWELL, England — The evening started peacefully enough at Long Lane Recreation Park in the western suburbs of London, disturbed only by the occasional rumble of a distant jet landing at Heathrow Airport. But just before sunset, five bright green missiles streaked through the air toward a row of poplars at the park’s edge. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/europe/14parakeets/14parakeets-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'British Parakeet Boom Is a Mystery, and a Mess', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Latest London Blitz, Pets Turn Into Pests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parakeets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T17:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd377cd-a6a8-52ff-a192-5fb62b370dc6', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd377cd-a6a8-52ff-a192-5fb62b370dc6'}, {'abstract': 'Aboard the yacht Clara One, a Norwegian actor turned producer touts his latest acquisition, a decades-old serial about a gunslinger turned U.S. Marshal-turned rancher-turned bodyguard to Teddy Roosevelt in the 19th-century American southwest. Yes, aboard a yacht.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/film-announcements-always-more-fun-aboard-a-yacht/', 'snippet': 'Aboard the yacht Clara One, a Norwegian actor turned producer touts his latest acquisition, a decades-old serial about a gunslinger turned U.S. Marshal-turned rancher-turned bodyguard to Teddy Roosevelt in the 19th-century American southwest. Yes,...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France— We’ve traversed the red carpets and the publicity stunts. But there is another side to the film festival here: the maritime side. We’re talking, of course, about yachts. Big ones and bigger ones, they crowd the harbor, drawing gawkers and aspirants (and Diddy). Really, no trip to the French Riviera is complete without a yacht party. And though the festival may be the pinnacle of the “glamour racket,” as Manohla Dargis noted in The New York Times, but that doesn’t mean it’s without its share of left-field come-ons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Announcements Are Always More Fun Aboard a Yacht', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T18:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5118e6a7-354a-54e2-ac45-fcbb44d463ca', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5118e6a7-354a-54e2-ac45-fcbb44d463ca'}, {'abstract': 'Denmark was told by the European Commission that its plans to restart checks at its frontiers could be against European Union law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/world/europe/14border.html', 'snippet': 'Denmark was told by the European Commission that its plans to restart checks at its frontiers could be against European Union law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Controversy over the future of Europe’s passport-free travel zone grew Friday when Denmark was warned that its plans to restart checks at its frontiers could be against European Union law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Denmark Warned Over Border Plans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Denmark’s Border Plan Angers Its E.U. Partners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European 