 treetops of the Alakai wilderness — a cloud forest atop the mountain hinterlands of Kauai — when my guide spotted something yellowish flitting among the boughs of an ohia tree.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15explorerspan/15explorerspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15explorerspan/15explorerspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15explorerspan/15explorerspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15explorerspan/15explorerspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15explorerspan/15explorerspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eden for Rare Birds in Hawaii', 'kicker': 'The U.S. Issue:\u2002Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Precarious Eden for Rare Birds on Kauai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kauai (Hawaii)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T20:14:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gustave Axelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gustave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Axelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952fbdbb-35d8-5327-942a-33e0d9a5280c', 'word_count': 1873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952fbdbb-35d8-5327-942a-33e0d9a5280c'}, {'abstract': 'There are many ways to see bears in Alaska. On Kodiak Island, you can live among them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/travel/its-a-bears-world-in-kodiak-alaska.html', 'snippet': 'There are many ways to see bears in Alaska. On Kodiak Island, you can live among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHE gave a chuff and pulled up short, as surprised to see us as we were to see her. Her dense, fluffy fur was blond. I watched her square, expressive face very closely because this bear — maybe 300 pounds and 10 yards away — would be the one deciding how the encounter played out. An adrenaline-driven voice in my head said, “This could go badly.” But it was also telling me how incredibly thrilling it was to be so near this animal. Not being on top of the food chain certainly heightens one’s awareness.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15coverspan/15coverspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15coverspan/15coverspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15coverspan/15coverspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/