e becoming increasingly uncommon. Invasive buffelgrass is crowding out saguaros and other native cactuses throughout the Southwest, while melting sea ice is threatening the Pacific walrus and polar bear in Alaska. Mosquito-borne diseases are threatening Hawaii’s songbirds, and white-nose syndrome is wiping out bats in the East.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15endangeredspan/15endangeredspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15endangeredspan/15endangeredspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15endangeredspan/15endangeredspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/travel/15endangeredspan/15endangeredspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Coast-to-Coast Guide to Endangered Species', 'kicker': 'The U.S. Issue: Endangered Species', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Coast-to-Coast Guide to the Precious Few', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T20:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryn Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2741973f-d579-50cc-8ee9-4350285e1283', 'word_count': 3352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2741973f-d579-50cc-8ee9-4350285e1283'}, {'abstract': 'Google is bracing for a settlement over concerns that it displayed ads from online pharmacies that sell counterfeit drugs or do not require a prescription.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/technology/14google.html', 'snippet': 'Google is bracing for a settlement over concerns that it displayed ads from online pharmacies that sell counterfeit drugs or do not require a prescription.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Google allowed rogue online pharmacies to advertise on its site in violation of its own advertising policies, according to one of the companies subpoenaed in the federal investigation of Google’s drug ad sales. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Is Said to Have Broken Internal Rules on Drug Ads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Firm Says Google Accepted Ads From Rogue Pharmacies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T20:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67314db0-f279-54a7-9a67-aa33d4abc397', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67314db0-f279