, 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a40637d-d9d8-5608-9980-13e7cc20de01', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a40637d-d9d8-5608-9980-13e7cc20de01'}, {'abstract': 'They’re down.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/inflation-expectations/', 'snippet': 'They’re down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just to follow up on something I’ve mentioned before: after the commodity correction, plus the fairly tame inflation report, market expectations of future inflation have fallen. Here’s the spread between 10-year Treasuries and inflation-protected versions of the same:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation Expectations', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T21:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c1bfb93-94f9-5f0a-bb4c-807715f1fe05', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c1bfb93-94f9-5f0a-bb4c-807715f1fe05'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at some of the movies from the director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/15/movies/rob-marshall-movies.html', 'snippet': 'A look back at some of the movies from the director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look back at some of the movies from the director.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/movies/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/movies/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/movies/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ/rob-marshall-movies-slide-7JGJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Films of Rob Marshall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T21:59:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/335fd56c-6c03-5847-9561-37229f5951f1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/335fd56c-6c03-5847-9561-37229f5951f1'}, {'abstract': 'The Kitchen, the 40-year-old performance and exhibition space on West 19th Street in New York, said that its board of directors had appointed Tim Griffin as its new executive director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/arts/footnote.html', 'snippet': 'The Kitchen, the 40-year-old performance and exhibition space on West 19th Street in New York, said that its board of directors had appointed Tim Griffin as its new executive director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kitchen, the 40-year-old performance and exhibition space on West 19th Street in New York, said that its board of directors had appointed Tim Griffin as its new executive director and chief curator. Mr. Griffin, a former editor of Artforum magazine, will replace Debra Singer, who has held the job since 2004 and who announced plans in January to resign.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnote', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T21:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf33cc3-2a25-52dd-b212-73c182e7d815', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf33cc3-2a25-52dd-b212-73c182e7d815'}, {'abstract': 'Fox finished atop the Thursday-night ratings as 21.6 million viewers tuned in for the “American Idol” elimination episode at 8, according to Nielsen’s estimates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/arts/television/american-idol-delivers-yet-again.html', 'snippet': 'Fox finished atop the Thursday-night ratings as 21.6 million viewers tuned in for the “American Idol” elimination episode at 8, according to Nielsen’s estimates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fox finished atop the Thursday-night ratings as 21.6 million viewers tuned in for the “American Idol” elimination episode at 8, according to Nielsen’s estimates. The “Idol” finalist James Durbin failed to advance to next week’s round, earning fewest votes of the nearly 72 million cast, leaving Lauren Alaina, Scotty McCreery and Haley Reinhart in the finale. Fox’s “Bones” (11 million) trailed slightly behind CBS’s “CSI” (11.5 million) in the 9 p.m. hour. CBS delivered a second-place finish over all, attracting 13.8 million at 10 for “The Mentalist” and broadcasting the sitcoms “The Big Bang Theory” (10.5 million) and “Rules of Engagement” (8 million) at 8 and 8:30. ABC was third with “Wipeout” (5.5 million), “Grey’s Anatomy” (9.4 million) and “Private Practice” (7.2 million). In a distant fourth place, NBC’s comedy lineup struggled, led by “The Office” at 9 (6.2 million) and back-to-back episodes of “Parks and Recreation” at 9:30 (4.5 million) and 10 (3.6 million).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Idol’ Delivers Yet Again', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘American Idol’ Delivers Yet Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T22:06:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1891605c-6d37-541c-b6e4-f0fac42ec9b1', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1891605c-6d37-541c-b6e4-f0fac42ec9b1'}, {'abstract': 'In an unusual and apparently heated closed-door session, Pakistan’s spy chief denied that Pakistan maintained any links with militant groups, according to lawmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/world/asia/14pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'In an unusual and apparently heated closed-door session, Pakistan’s spy chief denied that Pakistan maintained any links with militant groups, according to lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — In an unusual, and apparently heated, closed-door session of Parliament, Pakistan’s spy chief issued a rousing denunciation of the United States on Friday for its raid that killed Osama bin Laden and denied that Pakistan maintained any links with militant groups, according to lawmakers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Denying Links to Militants, Pakistan’s Spy Chief Denounces U.S. Before Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Denying Links to Militants, Pakistan’s Spy Chief Denounces U.S. Before Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasha, Ahmed Shuja', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T22:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fabb16e9-d64b-5b53-89a5-84f5d5afcfd1', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fabb16e9-d64b-5b53-89a5-84f5d5afcfd1'}, {'abstract': 'The Queens duo, Havoc and Prodigy, headed back to the stage after Prodigy’s release from prison. If they were thrilled, they didn’t let on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/arts/music/havoc-and-prodigy-of-mobb-deep-at-best-buy-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Queens duo, Havoc and Prodigy, headed back to the stage after Prodigy’s release from prison. If they were thrilled, they didn’t let on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No rap group — maybe no act in any genre — has gotten more mileage from straight talk than Mobb Deep. This Queens duo, Havoc and Prodigy, have specialized in plainspoken menace for almost two decades: almost every song is in the aggressive, threatening second person. Havoc and Prodigy can go long stretches — whole albums, it can feel like — without so much as one metaphor. Metaphors are indirect. Mobb Deep doesn’t want to confuse you.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/sub-depp-1/sub-depp-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/sub-depp-1/sub-depp-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/sub-depp-1/sub-depp-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/sub-depp-1/sub-depp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/sub-depp-1/sub-depp-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rap Duo Heads Back to the Stage, Granting No Compromises (or Smiles)', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rap Duo Heads Back to the Stage, Granting No Compromises (or Smiles)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T22:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/361f4292-68f7-514d-8172-111bbcf9ad29', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361f4292-68f7-514d-8172-111bbcf9ad29'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s ethics commission says John J. O’Connor, a senior vice chancellor for research and innovation, hired the daughter of Joseph Bruno to a position where she “did virtually no work.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/13/a-top-suny-official-is-accused-of-giving-a-no-show-job/', 'snippet': 'The state’s ethics commission says John J. O’Connor, a senior vice chancellor for research and innovation, hired the daughter of Joseph Bruno to a position where she “did virtually no work.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state’s ethics commission on Friday charged the president of the research foundation of the State University of New York, John J. O’Connor, with giving a no-show job to the daughter of the former Senate Majority Leader Joseph L. Bruno.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Top SUNY Official Is Accused of Giving a No-Show Job', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruno, Joseph L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commission on Public Integrity (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-13T22:20:48+0000', 'document_type'