merican-gala-at-temple-of-dendur-nocturnalist.html', 'snippet': 'A gala at the Metropolitan Museum of Art celebrated links between China and the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a pagoda in the Egyptian wing of the Metropolitan Museum of Art on Thursday night, at least at first glance. The sandstone Temple of Dendur was bathed in red light, as several hundred people — mostly Chinese-Americans — gathered to celebrate connections between China and the United States. At times, the shadows cast on the temple’s lintel conjured the up-ticked eaves of Asian architecture.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/nyregion/NOCTURNALIST1/NOCTURNALIST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taste of China Not as Far East: Egyptian Wing at the Met', 'kicker': 'Nocturnalist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taste of China Not as Far East: Egyptian Wing At the Met', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, Henry M Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T00:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_