king in Libya sought refuge in Lampedusa, Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/world/europe/14refugees.html', 'snippet': 'More than 1,000 sub-Saharan Africans and South Asians who had been working in Libya sought refuge in Lampedusa, Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAMPEDUSA, Italy — The fishing boats from Tripoli began arriving in the clear light of morning and continued well into the day on Friday, unloading more than 1,000 immigrants to this tiny Sicilian island. Most who made the rough crossing were men in their 20s and 30s, but there were also dozens of women, some pregnant, and several babies, whose sharp cries pierced the fresh sea air. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/14refugees1/14refugees1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/14/world/14refugees1/14refugees1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/14refugees1/14refugees1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/world/14refugees1/14refugees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/world/14refugees1/14refugees1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libyan Immigrants Becoming Italian Immigrants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libyan Immigrants Becoming Italian Immigrants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tripoli (Libya)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lampedusa (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:11:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63121dc5-b195-561b-907e-828d2698b7d3', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63121dc5-b195-561b-907e-828d2698b7d3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Greenhouse was a founder of the Beaux Arts Trio and a member for 32 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/arts/music/bernard-greenhouse-cellist-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Greenhouse was a founder of the Beaux Arts Trio and a member for 32 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernard Greenhouse, an internationally acclaimed cellist and a founding member of the Beaux Arts Trio, died on Friday at his home in Wellfleet, Mass., on Cape Cod. He was 95. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/GREENHOUSE-obit/GREENHOUSE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/GREENHOUSE-obit/GREENHOUSE-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/GREENHOUSE-obit/GREENHOUSE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/GREENHOUSE-obit/GREENHOUSE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/arts/GREENHOUSE-obit/GREENHOUSE-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bernard Greenhouse, Acclaimed Cellist, Dies at 95', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bernard Greenhouse, Cellist, Is Dead at 95', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beaux Arts Trio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca694e8-435a-54fe-b07e-2570ba0036bf', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca694e8-435a-54fe-b07e-2570ba0036bf'}, {'abstract': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden shows why the U.S. can’t trust Pakistan, and why it can’t just walk away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/opinion/14sat1.html', 'snippet': 'The killing of Osama bin Laden shows why the U.S. can’t trust Pakistan, and why it can’t just walk away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like most Americans, we have long despaired at the cynicism of Pakistan’s leaders, who accept American “counterterrorist” aid while also sheltering and enabling some of the worst anti-American extremists. But we never imagined that Osama bin Laden would be found hiding in plain sight, a stone’s throw from Pakistan’s leading military academy and an hour’s drive from Islamabad. Pakistan’s behavior since then has only added to the outrage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan After Bin Laden', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan After Bin Laden: The killing shows why the U.S. can’t trust Pakistan, and why it can’t just walk away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/93fe4976-66ef-5e9d-9e22-f7c13e2220fa', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93fe4976-66ef-5e9d-9e22-f7c13e2220fa'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gralnick was an executive producer for the evening news shows at CBS and ABC and helped revamp NBC’s “Nightly News” in the mid-1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/business/14gralnick.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gralnick was an executive producer for the evening news shows at CBS and ABC and helped revamp NBC’s “Nightly News” in the mid-1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Gralnick, a blunt, gravel-voiced television news executive who got his start in the days of the 15-minute, black-and-white evening newscast and went on to play leading roles in the news divisions of three major broadcast networks, died on Monday at his home in Weston, Conn. He was 72.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/business/GRALNICK-obit/GRALNICK-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 597, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/business/GRALNICK-obit/GRALNICK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/14/business/GRALNICK-obit/GRALNICK-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeff Gralnick, Power in News at 3 TV Networks, Dies at 72', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeff Gralnick, 72, a Power In News at 3 TV Networks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gralnick, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:16:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis Hevesi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hevesi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f21f9e5e-5d26-5afa-b333-4d5e8cffdfa0', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f21f9e5e-5d26-5afa-b333-4d5e8cffdfa0'}, {'abstract': 'Companies continue to press for higher premiums, saying they need protection against any sudden uptick in demand once people have more money to spend on their health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/business/14health.html', 'snippet': 'Companies continue to press for higher premiums, saying they need protection against any sudden uptick in demand once people have more money to spend on their health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s major health insurers are barreling into a third year of record profits, enriched in recent months by a lingering recessionary mind-set among Americans who are postponing or\xa0forgoing medical care. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/business/Health/Health-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Insurers Making Record Profits as Many Postpone Care', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Insurers Profit as Many Postpone Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UnitedHealth Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cigna Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ced3102c-c48b-5530-8f08-8bdca6106429', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ced3102c-c48b-5530-8f08-8bdca6106429'}, {'abstract': 'The Armory Foundation said it would change the location of the meet, which has been held for nearly a century at Madison Square Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/sports/millrose-games-to-move-from-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'The Armory Foundation said it would change the location of the meet, which has been held for nearly a century at Madison Square Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Millrose Games will be broken into two sessions and held on a Saturday when the meet moves next year to the Armory Track and Field Center in Upper Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/14/sports/millrose/millrose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Millrose Games Will Move Uptown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Millrose Games Will Move Uptown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millrose Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T01:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': '