war crimes trial, was released from prison on Friday pending the outcome of his appeals.', 'lead_paragraph': ' John Demjanjuk, a former concentration camp guard who was convicted Thursday in what may have been one of the last Nazi war crimes trials, was released from a Munich prison on Friday pending the outcome of his appeals. Mr. Demjanjuk, 91, who is ill and stateless, was not considered a flight risk, but the authorities had trouble finding a nursing home to accept him. He will remain free while he appeals his conviction and five-year sentence for taking part in the killing of 28,000 Jews as a guard at the Sobibor concentration camp in Nazi-occupied Poland. A court spokeswoman said the appeals could take 18 months to two years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Ex-Nazi Guard Released Pending Appeals', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Ex-Nazi Guard Released Pending Appeals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demjanjuk, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concentration Camps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T03:34:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://a