n steep terrain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOES inventiveness run in families? Is there a gene that awakens the entrepreneurial urge? A look at the Smith family offers at least anecdotal evidence that the answer is yes.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/business/PROTO-1/PROTO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/business/PROTO-1/PROTO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/business/PROTO-1/PROTO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Innovation, Gliding Across the Generations', 'kicker': 'Prototype', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Innovation, Gliding Across the Generations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SKATEBOARDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T17:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b0bbaa-f601-5df2-9c9c-06e612937c7d', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b0bbaa-f601-5df2-9c9c-06e612937c7d'}, {'abstract': 'In a change from its previous text-only policy, Google is about to allow images — though not animation — on some advertising that accompanies Gmail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/business/15digi.html', 'snippet': 'In a change from its previous text-only policy, Google is about to allow images — though not animation — on some advertising that accompanies Gmail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Google introduced Gmail seven years ago, it didn’t copy Yahoo Mail or Microsoft’s Hotmail. Gmail was built for distraction-free speed. The ads were text-only, and so unobtrusive that you could forget they were even there.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/business/SUB-DIGI/SUB-DIGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/business/SUB-DIGI/SUB-DIGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/business/SUB-DIGI/SUB-DIGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When It Comes to Inbox Advertising, Less Is Still More', 'kicker': 'Digital Domain', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When It Comes to Inbox Advertising, Less Is Still More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T17:46:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randall Stross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randall', 'mid