': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fcf0ceb-8b89-5cad-afa5-f9eece91e39f', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fcf0ceb-8b89-5cad-afa5-f9eece91e39f'}, {'abstract': 'Video tales from Tunica, Miss., whose casino-dependent economy has ground to a halt because of the Mississippi flooding.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/14/in-flooded-tunica-casinos-are-idle-but-concerns-are-nonstop/', 'snippet': 'Video tales from Tunica, Miss., whose casino-dependent economy has ground to a halt because of the Mississippi flooding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUNICA, Miss. — Like countless communities up and down the Mississippi River, life these days in this town of 1100, and its surrounding countryside, depends on which side of the levee you’re on. The town center, shielded from the river, looks nothing more than a bit bedraggled, while on the other side, flood waters have invaded homes, displaced hundreds and submerged crop fields.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Flooded Tunica, the Casinos Are Idle but Concerns Are Nonstop', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T19:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catrin Einhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Einhorn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f361e0d8-c3b6-5c1d-a9ab-e35786cfa1d8', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f361e0d8-c3b6-5c1d-a9ab-e35786cfa1d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Oxford, Conn., brewery makes four ales and offers tours in which samples are provided and half-gallon growlers are for sale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/cavalry-brewing-uses-imported-british-ingredients.html', 'snippet': 'The Oxford, Conn., brewery makes four ales and offers tours in which samples are provided and half-gallon growlers are for sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To an out-of-towner, Oxford’s narrow, winding Hurley Road holds a couple of surprises. The first is its proximity to an airport. The second, just off the slightly overgrown country lane in a modern industrial park, is Cavalry Brewing, which began producing beer last July. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brewery With a British Flavor', 'kicker': 'Quick Sip | Oxford', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brewery With a British Flavor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T19:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b73a827d-1c6f-53a5-8d30-05a840fbcbf7', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b73a827d-1c6f-53a5-8d30-05a840fbcbf7'}, {'abstract': 'Brushmill by the Waterfall, housed in a 19th-century factory, serves sturdy cuisine in a historic, elegant setting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/at-brushmill-by-the-waterfall-the-food-comes-with-a-view.html', 'snippet': 'Brushmill by the Waterfall, housed in a 19th-century factory, serves sturdy cuisine in a historic, elegant setting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE will always be a place for a traditional New England-style steakhouse serving plain, sturdy cuisine. Particularly if it sits on an exquisite piece of Connecticut real estate. Brushmill by the Waterfall in Chester is such a destination.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15DINECT1/15DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15DINECT1/15DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15DINECT1/15DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Steakhouse With Quite a View', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Chester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Steakhouse With Quite a View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T19:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lyness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '