ng system became so dominant that government trust-busters took it to court. They spent four years and millions of dollars making the case that Microsoft was unduly using its power to wipe out rivals in the Web browser business and other domains.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Did the Microsoft Case Change the World?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Did the Microsoft Case Change the World? A decade later, in the age of Google and Facebook, the antitrust settlement is a dim memory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T21:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/45462348-4d47-5b16-8034-17cef8d784ab', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45462348-4d47-5b16-8034-17cef8d784ab'}, {'abstract': 'The I.R.S. has put fat-cat political donors on notice that it is enforcing existing law on campaign fund-raising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/opinion/15sun3.html', 'snippet': 'The I.R.S. has put fat-cat political donors on notice that it is enforcing existing law on campaign fund-raising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who are the fat-cat five? Political money bundlers are wondering now that the Internal Revenue Service has put five unnamed donors on notice that it is looking at the checks they write to nonprofit groups that are increasingly funneling money directly to political campaign troughs.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secrecy Tax', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Secrecy Tax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T21:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/80935b7c-ce5e-523f-bcd2-d0f6d581ea7c', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80935b7c-ce5e-523f-bcd2-d0f6d581ea7c'}, {'abstract': 'City officials proposed to replace worn-out boardwalk stretches with concrete causeway slabs. Purists complain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/opinion/15sun4.html', 'snippet': 'City officials proposed to replace worn-out boardwalk stretches with concrete causeway slabs. Purists complain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not since Charles Feltman was credited with inventing the hot dog 140 years ago has Coney Island had to adjust to such ra