itan Opera itself) twiddling their thumbs while waiting for the start of a live high-definition broadcast of “D...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The massive set for Wagner’s “Ring” being staged at the Metropolitan Opera picked a fine time to misbehave. A technical problem left an estimated 175,000 people sitting in movie theaters around the world (and nearly 4,000 people at the Met itself) twiddling their thumbs while waiting for the start of a live high-definition broadcast of “Die Walküre,” the cycle’s second installment. Finally, after about 45 minutes, the performance started.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadcast of ‘Die Walküre’ Performance at the Met Is Delayed', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-14T22:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea83225-2d39-5ae8-914f-71aa40a4c175', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea83225-2d39-5ae8-914f-71aa40a4c175'}, {'abstract': 'Why are college grads irrationally optimistic about the future?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/opinion/15Sharot.html', 'snippet': 'Why are college grads irrationally optimistic about the future?', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/opinion/15sharotimgsf/15sharotimgsf-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'le