}, {'abstract': 'Nick Watney birdied his first two holes and Graeme McDowell joined him atop the leader board Saturday at the Players Championship on a short day of work at the T.P.C. Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/sports/golf/mcdowell-joins-lead-before-play-is-stopped.html', 'snippet': 'Nick Watney birdied his first two holes and Graeme McDowell joined him atop the leader board Saturday at the Players Championship on a short day of work at the T.P.C. Sawgrass in Ponte Vedra Beach, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PONTE VEDRA BEACH, Fla. — A four-and-a-half-hour rain delay during Saturday’s third round of the Players Championship defanged T.P.C. Sawgrass, and golfers filled with pent-up energy attacked the softened course like a swarm of children at an Easter egg hunt.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 641, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McDowell and Watney Lead, but Storms Leave Much of Two Rounds to Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'McDowell and Watney Lead, but Storms Leave Much of Two Rounds to Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDowell, Graeme', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watney, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PGA Championship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T00:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa1dee9-c42c-5689-87f9-dad4c9b966ff', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa1dee9-c42c-5689-87f9-dad4c9b966ff'}, {'abstract': 'Beijing has tried to stop the release of a report that North Korea and Iran may have shared ballistic missile technology in violation of United Nations sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/world/asia/15nations.html', 'snippet': 'Beijing has tried to stop the release of a report that North Korea and Iran may have shared ballistic missile technology in violation of United Nations sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China has tried to suppress a report at the United Nations suggesting that North Korea and Iran have been routinely sharing ballistic missile technology, United Nations diplomats said Saturday, expressing concern that Beijing was again working to shield the North. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Delays Report Suggesting North Korea Violated Sanctions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Delays Report Suggesting North Korea Violated Sanctions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/114aeee0-fbba-518c-ac7b-df7dbfeb372d', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/114aeee0-fbba-518c-ac7b-df7dbfeb372d'}, {'abstract': 'A decade ago, 24 children from P.S. 86 in the Bronx went on an unlikely chorus trip to Finland. The journey seemed to show that anything was possible in New York City. Was it?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/at-a-10-year-reunion-old-songs-but-new-voices.html', 'snippet': 'A decade ago, 24 children from P.S. 86 in the Bronx went on an unlikely chorus trip to Finland. The journey seemed to show that anything was possible in New York City. Was it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if guided by sense memory, they took their positions from their gospel chorus days, only they were standing on a sidewalk on the Upper West Side.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a 10-Year Reunion, Old Songs and New Voices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Songs, New Voices: A Reunion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Finland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810654f8-542d-5606-a0d3-2b7cebf40094', 'word_count': 1701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810654f8-542d-5606-a0d3-2b7cebf40094'}, {'abstract': 'Six dozen examples of Thomas Rowlandson’s works, some never before exhibited, are on view at Vassar, chronicling Georgian-era London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/rowlandson-art-rude-lewd-and-funny-at-vassar-review.html', 'snippet': 'Six dozen examples of Thomas Rowlandson’s works, some never before exhibited, are on view at Vassar, chronicling Georgian-era London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'America’s baby boomers savored the joyously irreverent cartoons of Mad Magazine and the leeringly carnal comix of R. Crumb. Gilded Age New Yorkers either cheered or fumed at the political savagery in the drawings of Thomas Nast. And Georgian-era Londoners got early versions of all three in the rude, lewd, devilishly funny prints of Thomas Rowlandson.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTWE3/15ARTWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTWE3/15ARTWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTWE3/15ARTWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Visual Narrative of Old England, Rude, Lewd and Colorful', 'kicker': 'Arts | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Visual Narrative of Old England, Rude, Lewd and Colorful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nast, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vassar College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loeb, Frances Lehman, Art Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crumb, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:24:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4e74651-b79d-5923-bce1-85afbae41017', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4e74651-b79d-5923-bce1-85afbae41017'}, {'abstract': 'A group of slightly graying, occasionally doughy volunteers keeps watch over in-line skaters in the park, armed with advice on stopping and keeping injuries to a minimum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/for-in-line-skaters-the-bruise-patrol-of-central-park.html', 'snippet': 'A group of slightly graying, occasionally doughy volunteers keeps watch over in-line skaters in the park, armed with advice on stopping and keeping injuries to a minimum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE three men wearing in-line skates stood quietly in the shade in Central Park, studying the passing crowd. Then a nearby skater, Jesse Madigan, 25, slammed into a curb, doubling over, and they pounced. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15SKATE2/15SKATE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'