tion': 'LI', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI4sub/15ARTSLI4sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI4sub/15ARTSLI4sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Southampton, Portraits From a Luxe Life', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Southampton, Portraits From a Luxe Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aileen Jacobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aileen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34b625e5-9870-5247-bfae-dbd191c14ba9', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34b625e5-9870-5247-bfae-dbd191c14ba9'}, {'abstract': '“Dancing With the Dark: Joan Snyder Prints 1963-2010” is at the Zimmerli Art Museum in New Brunswick through May 29.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/dancing-with-the-dark-prints-by-joan-snyder-review.html', 'snippet': '“Dancing With the Dark: Joan Snyder Prints 1963-2010” is at the Zimmerli Art Museum in New Brunswick through May 29.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many painters, prints serve as a place to try out new ideas, experiment in a different medium or circulate their images in a reproducible format, while earning some extra money. Sometimes, however, a print exhibition can feel like a vital key to an artist’s career. Such is the case with “Dancing With the Dark: Joan Snyder Prints 1963-2010” at the Jane Voorhees Zimmerli Art Museum in New Brunswick. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTNJ3/15ARTNJ3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTNJ3/15ARTNJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ARTNJ3/15ARTNJ3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Consciousness of a Feminist Expressionist', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Consciousness of a Feminist Expressionist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zimmerli Art Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Joan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/097dff72-d209-5af4-af35-2e59a3f5a541', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/097dff72-d209-5af4-af35-2e59a3f5a541'}, {'abstract': 'The president of the Staten Island Historical Society, who says Sunday is the day to give everybody else a break from him, begins with a blend of Guatemalan coffee and eases into decaf.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/for-john-gustafsson-sundays-are-for-church.html', 'snippet': 'The president of the Staten Island Historical Society, who says Sunday is the day to give everybody else a break from him, begins with a blend of Guatemalan coffee and eases into decaf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A connoisseur of and a cheerleader for all things Staten Island, John C. Gustafsson, president (until June 30) of the Staten Island Historical Society, was born there 49 years ago. Both he and the borough expect a busy summer as the celebration of Staten Island’s 350th anniversary hits its peak. Mr. Gustafsson retired in 2006 from a law career that began at Simpson Thacher & Bartlett and concluded at Sheppard Mullin Richter & Hampton, where he was administrative partner in the New York office. He and his wife, Mary Beth, general counsel of First Solar, live in a Stanford White house in West Brighton; Mr. Gustafsson’s son, Christopher, 13, visits every other weekend.  ROBIN FINN', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE-SPAN/15ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE-SPAN/15ROUTINE-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE-SPAN/15ROUTINE-SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE-SPAN/15ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE-SPAN/15ROUTINE-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pick a Car, Then Off to Church', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pick a Car, Then Off to Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staten Island Historical Society', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/223d9420-2c07-5115-8a30-c9a2d271f871', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/223d9420-2c07-5115-8a30-c9a2d271f871'}, {'abstract': 'Comcast, in Hartford, became the setting for Bombfest’s third Memorial Day weekend when Western Connecticut State University pulled out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/bombfest-music-festival-moves-to-comcast-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Comcast, in Hartford, became the setting for Bombfest’s third Memorial Day weekend when Western Connecticut State University pulled out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEMORIAL DAY weekend will bring the third installment of Bombfest — an acronym for Bring Our Music Back Festival. But instead of bringing the music back to Durham, where the multigenre festival was held last year, the event’s founders, Frank Bombaci and his son, also named Frank Bombaci, will be delivering headliners like Weezer, Wiz Khalifa and Snoop Dogg to Hartford. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15MUSICCT/15MUSICCT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As a Festival Expands, Its Needs Do, Too', 'kicker': 'Music | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As a Festival Expands, Its Needs Do, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tammy La Gorce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tammy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Gorce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ba46c98-004a-5b59-8bc6-7eceb8b4421c', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ba46c98-004a-5b59-8bc6-7eceb8b4421c'}, {'abstract': 'A visit to the Museum of Sex inspires a few new blue laws for an uninhibited city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/nyregion/new-blue-laws-for-new-york-inspired-by-the-museum-of-sex.html', 'snippet': 'A visit to the Museum of Sex inspires a few new blue laws for an uninhibited city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was Sunday morning, about 11 o’clock, and a casual glance might have suggested I was in church. There were a couple of bibles nearby; a depiction of the Garden of Eden was available for examination. But I wasn’t in church. I was in the Museum of Sex. New York’s blue laws, it appears, are not holding up so well.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JPCRITIC2/15JPCRITIC2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JPCRITIC2/15JPCRITIC2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JPCRITIC2/15JPCRITIC2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JPCRITIC2/15JPCRITIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/15/nyregion/15JPCRITIC2/15JPCRITIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Can Do That on a Sunday?', 'kicker': 'City Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Can Do That On a Sunday?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T01:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 