es', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When a Batting Order Becomes a Reflection of Disorder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T04:55:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a30bf54-c338-53a6-9fea-fc6595083e2b', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a30bf54-c338-53a6-9fea-fc6595083e2b'}, {'abstract': 'A transcript of Manager Joe Girardi’s postgame news conference Saturday night.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/posadas-mental-health-day/', 'snippet': 'A transcript of Manager Joe Girardi’s postgame news conference Saturday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jorge Posada’s late scratch from the Yankees’ lineup shortly before a 6-0 loss to the Boston Red Sox on Saturday at Yankee Stadium led to a night of speculation and disagreement over why he did not play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Posada’s Mental Health Day', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T05:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Plutnicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plutnicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a17bb2e7-79bb-5d31-81c0-c637d9ebae42', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17bb2e7-79bb-5d31-81c0-c637d9ebae42'}, {'abstract': 'Jorge Posada and Derek Jeter will have some more questions to answer on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/no-20-on-your-roster-no-9-in-the-order/', 'snippet': 'Jorge Posada and Derek Jeter will have some more questions to answer on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jorge Posada and Derek Jeter have been friends for nearly 20 years, since they were teammates at Class A Greensboro in 1992. Their daily interaction is part of the fabric of the Yankees’ clubhouse. Jeter, holding a cup from Starbucks, grabs a pair of sanitary socks and belts out, “Sado!” – his nickname for Posada. They have won together – five World Series championships – and they have lost together, and now they are, almost inevitably, declining together, a 36-year-old shortstop and a 39-year-old designated hitter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No. 20 on Your Roster, No. 9 in the Order', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T05:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0278603-d08c-5613-8457-665526b2b2d6', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0278603-d08c-5613-8457-665526b2b2d6'}, {'abstract': 'Works by the Young Japanese Calligraphers collective will be on display at Espace Japon in Paris from May 17 to 28.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/in-paris-the-striking-strokes-of-japanese-calligraphy/', 'snippet': 'Works by the Young Japanese Calligraphers collective will be on display at Espace Japon in Paris from May 17 to 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ritsuko Koga met Ayako Wakahara, the president of the Young Japanese Calligraphers collective, she was “moved by her ambition and her objective to make the value of Japanese calligraphy known to the world.” Ms. Koga, who oversees the gallery space at Espace Japon (12 rue de Nancy; 33-1-47-00-77-47; www.espacejapon.com), then invited the group to display their oeuvre in Paris. All of the artists studied calligraphy at Tokyo’s University of Taito-bunka, an institution that puts special emphasis on Eastern traditions and culture. By working as a collective, the Young Japanese Calligraphers’ communal nature fortifies the solitary aspects of this written art. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, the Striking Strokes of Japanese Calligraphy', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0db88a77-d1e7-58c6-acc8-19a457820101', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0db88a77-d1e7-58c6-acc8-19a457820101'}, {'abstract': 'Obviously, Houston had a pass defense that did very little to challenge opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/2010-texans-what-the-film-revealed/', 'snippet': 'Obviously, Houston had a pass defense that did very little to challenge opponents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we wonder whether there will be a 2011 season, this is part of a series looking back at the 2010 season, with the benefit of film analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2010 Texans: What the Film Revealed', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T10:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7aa3e7-9dc7-5db3-aaaf-811051239839', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7aa3e7-9dc7-5db3-aaaf-811051239839'}, {'abstract': 'Red Bulls defender Rafael Marquez spoke with Jack Bell of The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/qa-with-red-bulls-rafael-marquez/', 'snippet': 'Red Bulls defender Rafael Marquez spoke with Jack Bell of The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael Marquez, the captain of Mexico’s national team, is in his second season with the Red Bulls of M.L.S. The veteran, who has played in France and for Barcelona in Spain, is back at his natural center back position and has helped to steady the club’s defense as the Red Bulls prepare for Sunday’s game against visiting Chivas USA. Marquez, a superstar in Mexico, has often times seemed like that other guy as the club and league promote the exploits of Thierry Henry, who was also his teammate in Spain. Marquez spoke recently with Jack Bell of The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With the Red Bulls’ Rafael Marquez', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Backe, Hans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Thierry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marquez, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FC Barcelona', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T10:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/52515da4-dfa7-5446-9fc2-f3852fe08889', 'word_count': 2220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52515da4-dfa7-5446-9fc2-f3852fe08889'}, {'abstract': 'The lure and the promise of the Dutch tulip.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/going-dutch/', 'snippet': 'The lure and the promise of the Dutch tulip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those of us fortunate enough to regularly patronize New York City’s wondrous bodegas, the appearance of cut tulips ($7 a bunch, two for $12) in mid-February is our first inkling that spring is coming. Most of us don’t have access to real trees, after all. Besides, those other, more fluorescent flowers, the ones that require a certain level of patience to sift through, don’t appear to be tied to a particular season — or to Earth, even — as they sit huddled in green buckets, illuminated by fluorescent lights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Dutch', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convenience Stores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T10:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f0e8f51-de25-5e7e-8846-26c4b307e323', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f0e8f51-de25-5e7e-8846-26c4b307e323'}, {'abstract': 'The arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn comes at an especially sensitive time for the International Monetary Fund’s most high-profile project: saving Greece from default.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/business/16fund.html', 'snippet': 'The arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn comes at an especially sensitive time for the International Monetary Fund’s most high-profile project: saving Greece from default.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It’s hard to imagine a worse time for the International Monetary Fund to be without a forceful European leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Europe in Crisis, Fragile Time for I.M.F.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Europe in Crisis, Fragile Time for I.M.F.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T10:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d855eff3-bb06-5d90-ac84-af52185d6a3c', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d855eff3-bb06-5d90-ac84-af52185d6a3c'}, {'abstract': 'On Saturday, Alex Brown headed over to Fair Hill to watch Animal Kingdom train.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/a-morning-at-fair-hill/', 'snippet': 'On Saturday, Alex Brown headed over to Fair Hill to watch Animal Kingdom train.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday morning, I met three friends and headed over to Fair Hill to watch Animal Kingdom train. We met at the local deli, formerly named Prizzios, and drove to the clocker’s stand. There was light chatter among my friends, who had not yet seen the Derby champion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Morning at Fair Hill', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irwin, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANIMAL KINGDOM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T11:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c84aadc-9280-5d33-86f2-dc2ad420852f', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c84aadc-9280-5d33-86f2-dc2ad420852f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers report their efforts to fix credit report errors with Equifax, Experian and TransUnion.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/credit-report-errors-how-have-you-handled-them/', 'snippet': 'Readers report their efforts to fix credit report errors with Equifax, Experian and TransUnion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On today’s front page, Tara Siegel Bernard uncovers something you’ve probably suspected for a long time: Equifax, Experian and TransUnion has one system for solving important people’s credit report errors and another for everybody else.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Report Errors: How Have You Handled Them?', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equifax Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Experian Group Ltd