etition at Cannes so far is Jean-Pierre and Luc Dardenne’s “Kid With a Bike,” though critics have welcomed it with polite yawns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — There may not have been consensus by Day 4 of the Cannes Film Festival — no movie has yet been universally loved, loathed or violently debated — but the critics have staked out their positions and fired up their thumbs. The British are keen on the British film “We Need to Talk About Kevin,” Lynne Ramsay’s drama about an American mother and her psycho son, while the French are less impressed. The reviewer at Cahiers du Cinéma anointed it with an unsmiley face in a trade magazine, a perfect representation of what sometimes seems to be the default critical attitude here. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/arts/CANNES/CANNES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/16/arts/CANNES/CANNES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/arts/CANNES/CANNES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/arts/CANNES/CANNES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/arts/CANNES/CANNES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Cannes, Synergy but Not Consensus', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Cannes, Synergy But Not Consensus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'na