suchi faces the prospect of losing its younger residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTSUCHI, Japan — The crumpled cars have reddened with rust, and spring rains and a warming sun have left the ashes and mud hardened into an earthen plate of armor. But Satoshi Watanabe still comes every day to pick through the charred debris that was once his home, searching for the remains of his 2-month-old infant daughter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/world/RECOVERY-2/RECOVERY-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before It Can Rebuild, Japanese Town Must Survive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Rebuild, Stricken Japanese Town Must First Survive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-15T23:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff92d388-8cf9-5dcf-ad5c-f82a3ed590fb', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff92d388-8cf9-5dcf-ad5c-f82a3ed590fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Pew Research Center asks adults and college presidents for their perspective on higher education, and each group shares similar concerns.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/pew/', 'snippet': 'The Pew Research Center asks adults and college presidents for their pe