ame': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T01:44:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c341f4c-9672-502a-8071-5a57c4831625', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c341f4c-9672-502a-8071-5a57c4831625'}, {'abstract': 'A new documentary on PBS stations captures the political complexities and drama of a pivotal chapter in civil rights history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/opinion/16mon4.html', 'snippet': 'A new documentary on PBS stations captures the political complexities and drama of a pivotal chapter in civil rights history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago this month, a group of black and white volunteers boarded two public buses in the District of Columbia to travel into the Deep South, where segregated waiting rooms, restrooms, lunch counters and other indignities were a fact of life despite Supreme Court rulings striking down segregation in interstate travel. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Freedom Riders', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering the Freedom Riders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ku Klux Klan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T01:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffab1f4-503a-5c3b-935f-462e1b3a1251', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffab1f4-503a-5c3b-935f-462e1b3a1251'}, {'abstract': 'The New Jersey governor’s stance has led to higher transit fares and highway tolls, and could cause bridge and tunnel tolls to reach or exceed $10.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/nyregion/in-christies-policies-pain-for-commuters.html', 'snippet': 'The New Jersey governor’s stance has led to higher transit fares and highway tolls, and could cause bridge and tunnel tolls to reach or exceed $10.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a standard-bearer of fiscal conservatism, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey won over voters with his aggressive, no-excuses approach to taming budget problems and identifying the parties he held responsible for them. He has sparred with unions, cut spending and sworn off raising taxes, including the state’s low gasoline tax.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/JERSEY/JERSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/JERSEY/JERSEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/JERSEY/JERSEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/JERSEY/JERSEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/JERSEY/JER