 in Vicksburg during a 1927 flood, and waters were expected to keep rising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VICKSBURG, Miss. — Late Sunday morning, as the Mississippi River was rushing faster and higher past this town than it has in 183 years of record-keeping, Dontaye Buck was sitting perfectly still.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/FLOOD-2/FLOOD-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/16/us/FLOOD-2/FLOOD-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/FLOOD-2/FLOOD-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/FLOOD-2/FLOOD-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/us/FLOOD-2/FLOOD-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Water for a Mississippi River City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mississippi River City Gets an Unwelcome View of the Floodwaters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vicksburg (Miss)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T02:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'ori