, {'abstract': 'Raising the federal debt limit has become a familiar Washington ritual in which both parties jockey for the right to say no.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/15/frugality-is-a-virtue-but-politics-rule-the-debt-limit-fight/', 'snippet': 'Raising the federal debt limit has become a familiar Washington ritual in which both parties jockey for the right to say no.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president needed an increase in the federal debt limit. His partisan adversary, a powerful Ohio congressman, wanted something in return: deep spending cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frugality Is a Virtue, but Politics Rule the Debt-Limit Fight', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T03:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a973dd-74e5-5261-8a44-7e50edb2f80e', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a973dd-74e5-5261-8a44-7e50edb2f80e'}, {'abstract': 'The Gramm-Rudman-Hollings act of 1985, for all its flaws, created a fiscal climate compelling compromises that eventually made deficit reduction possible, or so it seems now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/us/politics/16fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'The Gramm-Rudman-Hollings act of 1985, for all its flaws, created a fiscal climate compelling compromises that eventually made deficit reduction possible, or so it seems now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Among the highest-profile laws of recent decades was a failed one: the 1985 deficit-reduction statute called Gramm-Rudman-Hollings for its Senate sponsors. Intended to force a balanced budget, it spawned budget gimmicks and did little to cut deficits, provoking one of its authors, Senator Ernest F. Hollings, to say, “I’m filing for divorce on grounds of infidelity and irreconcilable differences.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/ALT-FISCAL/ALT-FISCAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/ALT-FISCAL/ALT-FISCAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/us/ALT-FISCAL/ALT-FISCAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Idea Rebounds: Automatic Cuts to Curb Deficits', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Idea Rebounds: Automatic Cuts To Curb Deficits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lew, Jacob J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank':