the Henry Viscardi School, one of 11 schools of its kind in New York, paid its top executive $1.25 million over two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBERTSON, N.Y. — Kathleen Cervasio’s daughter, Gina, who is 12, has cerebral palsy, cannot speak and is quadriplegic. Without a doubt, Ms. Cervasio said, the best thing that ever happened to Gina was getting into the Henry Viscardi School, one of 11 state-supported public schools for the severely disabled in New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/WINERIP/WINERIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/WINERIP/WINERIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/WINERIP/WINERIP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/WINERIP/WINERIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/WINERIP/WINERIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At School for the Disabled, High Pay Leads to State Pressure and Now Layoffs', 'kicker': 'On Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At School for the Disabled, High Pay Leads to State Pressure and Now Layoffs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Viscardi, Henry, School', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T03:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74532181-5bdc-5371-98b4-459a86801f65', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74532181-5bdc-5371-98b4-459a86801f65'}, {'abstract': 'A proposed map of new county legislative districts is being closely watched as an indicator of how Republicans may approach state redistricting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/nyregion/in-nassau-many-eyes-on-fight-over-redistricting.html', 'snippet': 'A proposed map of new county legislative districts is being closely watched as an indicator of how Republicans may approach state redistricting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINEOLA, N.Y. — Even by the raucous standards of Nassau County politics, it was a wild day. Almost 200 residents, mostly minorities, trooped into the county office building for 10 hours last Monday to testify, shout, wave placards and threaten to sue over a redistricting plan being rushed through in record speed by the Legislature’s Republican majority.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/nyregion/NASSAU1/NASSAU1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images