ing health insurance to workers, many nursing homes are seeking an exemption from the new law, which is intended to ensure access to affordable coverage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/us/16nursing.html', 'snippet': 'Alarmed at the cost of providing health insurance to workers, many nursing homes are seeking an exemption from the new law, which is intended to ensure access to affordable coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It is an oddity of American health care: Many nursing homes and home care agencies do not provide health insurance to their workers, or they pay wages so low that employees cannot afford the coverage that is offered.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/us/JP-NURSES-2/JP-NURSES-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nursing Homes Seek Exemptions From Health Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nursing Homes Seek Exemptions From Health Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T03:38:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f463e1-d6d5-5c5b-abb4-772fef9be778', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f463e1-d6d5-5c5b-abb4-772f