097e4b13-f226-5e50-afc8-9dedd3fa6285'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, it’s National Small Business Week!', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/this-week-in-small-business-get-your-party-hats-on/', 'snippet': 'Yes, it’s National Small Business Week!', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week in Small Business: Get Your Party Hats On!', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T11:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/86828bab-2076-53ca-8ea3-b9c315dbe0ce', 'word_count': 1489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86828bab-2076-53ca-8ea3-b9c315dbe0ce'}, {'abstract': 'In their new memoirs, Shirley MacLaine and Rob Lowe treat the reader like a friend while making it clear that noncelebrities can never really understand the strangeness of celebrity life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/books/review/book-review-memoirs-by-shirley-maclaine-and-rob-lowe.html', 'snippet': 'In their new memoirs, Shirley MacLaine and Rob Lowe treat the reader like a friend while making it clear that noncelebrities can never really understand the strangeness of celebrity life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someday, someone will write a definitive phenomenological study of what it’s like now to be famous, although a simple infographic would probably just about cover it. “This Is Your Consciousness on Fame” would be the heading, just above arrows representing a positive feedback loop and captions reading: “Noncelebrities become convinced that celebrity dwells on a different plane of existence .\u2008.\u2008. which increases the magnitude of unreality, solipsism and alienation already being experienced by celebrity; celebrity succumbs to exponentially alienated and surreal view of reality and with behavior to match .\u2008.\u2008. which further increases the fascination exerted on noncelebrities; celebrity builds permanent residence on a different plane of existence, applies for passport.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unreality of Being a Celebrity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacLaine, Shirley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowe, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T11:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carina Chocano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chocano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a564c77-9578-5924-9cc3-5f842a51870d', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a564c77-9578-5924-9cc3-5f842a51870d'}, {'abstract': 'The decision comes after antitrust regulators made it clear they would not approve the joint takeover bid for the operator of the Big Board.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/nasdaq-and-ice-pull-offer-for-nyse-euronext/', 'snippet': 'The decision comes after antitrust regulators made it clear they would not approve the joint takeover bid for the operator of the Big Board.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:05 a.m. | Updated The Nasdaq OMX Group and IntercontinentalExchange announced on Monday they were withdrawing their bid for NYSE Euronext, after antitrust regulators said the deal would not gain the necessary approvals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nasdaq and ICE Drop Offer for NYSE Euronext', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nasdaq Stock Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYSE Euronext', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T11:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a9e92c6-2bbb-5c31-aa7e-0372b6630d48', 'word_count': 561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a9e92c6-2bbb-5c31-aa7e-0372b6630d48'}, {'abstract': 'A prosecutor said he had ample evidence to charge three top Libyan officials for crimes against humanity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/africa/17hague.html', 'snippet': 'A prosecutor said he had ample evidence to charge three top Libyan officials for crimes against humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The prosecutor of the International Criminal Court in The Hague on Monday sought arrest warrants for Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi of Libya, a son and the colonel’s brother-in-law on charges of orchestrating systematic attacks against civilians that amount to crimes against humanity. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime