S — French accident investigators said Monday that they had succeeded in downloading all of the flight data and cockpit conversations from the so-called black boxes of an Air France jet that crashed two years ago in the Atlantic Ocean — a critical breakthrough that could finally resolve the mystery behind why the plane went down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/world/17airfrance-cnd-inline1/17airfrance-cnd-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/world/17airfrance-cnd-inline1/17airfrance-cnd-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/world/17airfrance-cnd-inline1/17airfrance-cnd-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Data Recovered From Air France Flight Recorders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Data Recovered From Air France Flight Recorders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airplane Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T11:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03984673-cc9b-58ba-a181-689d49742c49', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03984673-cc9b-58ba-a181-689d49742c49'}, {'abstract': 'DuPont said on Monday that its $6.3 billion tender offer for the Danish food ingredient maker had been accepted by enough shareholders to be completed. \xa0', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/dupont-offer-for-danisco-succeeds/', 'snippet': 'DuPont said on Monday that its $6.3 billion tender offer for the Danish food ingredient maker had been accepted by enough shareholders to be completed. \xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'DuPont has won a five-month takeover fight for the Danish food ingredient maker Danisco, after more than 92 percent of shareholders approved its $6.3 billion tender offer, the company announced on Monday. \xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DuPont Offer for Danisco Succeeds', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danisco A/S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Advisors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T11:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4355ccd9-61dd-5339-a2a1-284a1df8ba27', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4355ccd9-61dd-5339-a2a1-284a1df8ba27'}, {'abstract': 'There were conflicting reports about why Sammy Wanjiru of Kenya, the Olympic champion, jumped from a balcony on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/marathon-champion-dies-in-fall-from-balcony.html', 'snippet': 'There were conflicting reports about why Sammy Wanjiru of Kenya, the Olympic champion, jumped from a balcony on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he won the Chicago Marathon in October after a frustrating year of injury and illness, Sammy Wanjiru of Kenya seemed relieved and upbeat. Finally, he said, he could think about chasing the world record held by Haile Gebrselassie of Ethiopia.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/cty-runner-2/cty-runner-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 728, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/cty-runner-2/cty-runner-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/cty-runner-2/cty-runner-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mystery Remains in Death of Marathon Champion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mystery Remains in Death of Olympic Marathon Champion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wanjiru, Sammy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T12:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/048483d3-0b43-5d9e-96f4-55ae83dfcde1', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/048483d3-0b43-5d9e-96f4-55ae83dfcde1'}, {'abstract': 'A lot of work has gone into keeping the feel of the old place.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/empire-diner-is-reborn-as-the-highliner/', 'snippet': 'A lot of work has gone into keeping the feel of the old place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people see the Highliner, in what was the iconic Empire Diner and remark that “nothing has changed,” it’s music to Charles Milite’s ears.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Empire Diner Is Reborn as the Highliner', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T12:15:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d5c4e8e-bb39-5880-95e5-dcc9177a5735', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d5c4e8e-bb39-5880-95e5-dcc9177a5735'}, {'abstract': 'The Portuguese restaurant left the West Village two years ago in the face of a rent increase.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/alfama-returns-in-midtown/', 'snippet': 'The Portuguese restaurant left the West Village two years ago in the face of a rent increase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tarcisio Costa and Miguel Jerónimo are reopening Alfama, one of the city’s rare Portuguese restaurants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alfama Returns, in Midtown', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T12:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cd4fc5e-26e8-5cda-82ec-f9dcea676df1', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cd4fc5e-26e8-5cda-82ec-f9dcea676df1'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican told bishops to make fighting sexual abuse of minors by clerics a priority, but the recommendations are not binding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/europe/17vatican.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican told bishops to make fighting sexual abuse of minors by clerics a priority, but the recommendations are not binding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VATICAN CITY — The Vatican told bishops worldwide on Monday to make fighting sexual abuse of minors by clerics a priority, telling them to create “clear and coordinated” procedures by next year and cooperate with law enforcement authorities when required.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vatican Tells Bishops to Set Clear Strategy Against Abuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vatican Tells Bishops to Set Clear Strategy Against Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-0