': 'Koninklijke Philips Electronics NV', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T12:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric A. Taub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Taub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb5a1ba1-e2f2-5ac0-8399-3a80cd409a85', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb5a1ba1-e2f2-5ac0-8399-3a80cd409a85'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: If a civilian trial downtown is O.K. for the two men accused of plotting to blow up a synagogue, why not for Khalid Shaikh Mohammed? Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/civilian-courts-are-getting-job-done-in-terror-trials/', 'snippet': 'The Day: If a civilian trial downtown is O.K. for the two men accused of plotting to blow up a synagogue, why not for Khalid Shaikh Mohammed? Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Security seemed more intense than usual on Saturday for worshipers attending Sabbath services at some prominent synagogues in Manhattan. Two police officers and a patrol car planted themselves outside the Lexington Avenue entrance of Central Synagogue. On Fifth Avenue, officers stood on the front steps of Temple Emanu-El, while around the corner an enormous police van commanded a stretch of East 65th Street. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Civilian Courts Are Getting Job Done in Terror Trials', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 