': 'American Airlines Tests In-Flight Streaming Video', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T17:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3645334-866f-525c-968a-716822b49339', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3645334-866f-525c-968a-716822b49339'}, {'abstract': 'Louise Fili’s identity for L’Arte del Gelato.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/who-made-that-gelato-look-so-good/', 'snippet': 'Louise Fili’s identity for L’Arte del Gelato.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was delighted to discover recently that the legendary graphic designer Louise Fili created the current identity and packaging for L’Arte del Gelato, a small gelateria in New York that I’ve visited countless times. Although there can be many downsides to spending the hottest months in the city (such as this, that, and this other thing), eating gelato while lazily walking the streets is not one of them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Gelato Look So Good?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gelato', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ICE CREAM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T17:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8a2d91b-9605-5daa-ac5b-e4007a0dca65', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8a2d91b-9605-5daa-ac5b-e4007a0dca65'}, {'abstract': 'Video posted on YouTube showed Sunday’s protests by Palestinians from several angles.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/the-palestinian-nakba-protests-from-several-angles-on-youtube/', 'snippet': 'Video posted on YouTube showed Sunday’s protests by Palestinians from several angles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Tuesday | 8:44 p.m. As my colleague Ethan Bronner reported, more than a dozen people were killed on Sunday when Israeli troops fired at Palestinian protesters who marched from Syria, Lebanon, Gaza and the West Bank to commemorate what they call the “catastrophe,” or “nakba,” of Israel’s creation in 1948, during which hundreds of thousands of Palestinians lost their homes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Palestinian ‘Nakba’ Protests From Several Angles on YouTube', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T17:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/34cbd0a3-a543-54e1-8957-11cf352faf56', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34cbd0a3-a543-54e1-8957-11cf352faf56'}, {'abstract': 'Look who’s lecturing us.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/wisdom-from-the-enema-man/', 'snippet': 'Look who’s lecturing us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So I see that Alan Simpson is still giving us wise advice. What does it take for someone to stop being regarded in Washington as a wise man?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisdom From the Enema Man', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T17:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/da08a5d6-a5be-532c-869a-131c97780450', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da08a5d6-a5be-532c-869a-131c97780450'}, {'abstract': 'A trip to Iowa includes dairy farms, funicular railways and an unlikely feast from Wal-Mart.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/live-from-the-baymont-inn-pella-iowa/', 'snippet': 'A trip to Iowa includes dairy farms, funicular railways and an unlikely feast from Wal-Mart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You last heard from me, I think, leaving Immokalee en route to Detroit. The Motor City, as we used to call it, is the subject of this week’s column, so you’re getting nothing on that now, though I will say it was one of the most memorable and inspiring couple of days I’ve had, ever. (“Honey? Pack your bags. We’re moving to Detroit.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live From the Baymont Inn, Pella, Iowa', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farmers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T17:07:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4efd3edd-0576-5322-88f8-f4aeae7446ea', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4efd3edd-0576-5322-88f8-f4aeae7446ea'}, {'abstract': 'A seminar at the Manhattan Cocktail Classic discussed the the pleasures and pitfalls of cocktail historicism.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/do-you-need-to-think-when-you-drink/', 'snippet': 'A seminar at the Manhattan Cocktail Classic discussed the the pleasures and pitfalls of cocktail historicism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pick up a drink menu these days and it’s not unusual to find a citation for each cocktail detailing its inventor, its place of origin and year of creation. There might even be a few lines of colorful back story. This can charm and inform, or in the wrong hands, it can be very annoying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Need to Think When You Drink?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k