hour season finale, according to Nielsen’s estimates. After three previous tries, Rob Mariano, a k a Boston Rob, was finally victorious, winning this season’s $1 million prize. CBS ranked No. 1 for the night, leading at 7 p.m. with “60 Minutes” (12 million) as well as at 10, following the “Survivor” finale with a reunion special (11.3 million). ABC placed second for the night, garnering 10 million viewers from 9 to 11 for the season finale of “Desperate Housewives.” NBC was third with “Dateline” at 7 (5.2 million), “Minute to Win It” at 8 (3.5 million) and “The Celebrity Apprentice” from 9 to 11 (6.6 million). Fox and its animated comedy lineup finished fourth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS and ‘Boston Rob’ Win on Sunday Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/55d5159b-3136-5a5d-b23d-2ecb6d96c2b5', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55d5159b-3136-5a5d-b23d-2ecb6d96c2b5'}, {'abstract': 'While a failed bid for NYSE Euronext cost it some money, there are several reasons why Nasdaq may have considered the exercise worthwhile.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/the-logic-behind-nasdaqs-longshot-bid-for-nyse/', 'snippet': 'While a failed bid for NYSE Euronext cost it some money, there are several reasons why Nasdaq may have considered the exercise worthwhile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There 