', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c4edb0d-93ca-55c8-8da1-efd8ee20a09c', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c4edb0d-93ca-55c8-8da1-efd8ee20a09c'}, {'abstract': 'The former model, who now runs two successful cosmetics lines, discusses her success with the Metabolic Balance Diet.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/vain-glorious-jemma-kidds-secrets-to-a-brilliant-body/', 'snippet': 'The former model, who now runs two successful cosmetics lines, discusses her success with the Metabolic Balance Diet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jemma Kidd has been busy: the 36-year-old former model runs the Jemma Kidd Makeup School in London, looks after two successful cosmetics lines — JK for Target, available at the mass retailer, and her makeup “academy,” for which she makes the QVC rounds — and last year, had twins with Arthur Wellesley, the Earl of Mornington (when she married him in 2005, it made her an official countess). All of this left her feeling, understandably, sluggish, until she adopted the Metabolic Balance Diet. “It’s this German diet. They take your blood and they analyze your hormone levels, vitamin levels, what’s right for you, your body type, your height, your weight. They analyze everything and give you this big list of what you can and cannot eat,” Kidd explained while previewing her summer and fall collections. “But the main rules are one type of protein for each meal, you’ve got to wait five hours between each meal, no snacking, an apple a day. The first thing you eat should be protein — it’s all about leveling your blood sugar and your hormones. Weight loss is the third thing. It’s detox for the first two weeks — you’re not allowed any fat. I’ve lost 23 pounds since January, 15 of them in the first 10 days.” The svelte Kidd was in New York a couple of weeks ago for the Metropolitan Museum of Art Costume Institute Gala (she wore McQueen), where she was privy to some testimonials to one of her Target products, Show Stopper Year-Round Body Glow. “It’s organically grown into quite a successful little product,” she said. “I had five people at the Met ball come up to me and say, ‘My makeup artist put it on me. It’s fabulous!’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Jemma Kidd’s Secrets to a Brilliant Body', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd19810-b859-5d5a-b9da-270ca541aeec', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd19810-b859-5d5a-b9da-270ca541aeec'}, {'abstract': 'An animation focuses on Bukit Tigapuluh, a hilly region that provides habitat to endangered tigers, elephants, orangutans and other rare species.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/on-our-radar-a-satellite-tour-of-a-threatened-rain-forest/', 'snippet': 'An animation focuses on Bukit Tigapuluh, a hilly region that provides habitat to endangered tigers, elephants, orangutans and other rare species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A computer illustration created by the wildlife activist group WWF-Indonesia using Google Earth provides a tour of Sumatran rain forest areas at risk of destruction by logging companies and palm oil producers. The animation focuses on Bukit Tigapuluh, a hilly region that provides habitat to endangered tigers, elephants, orangutans and other rare species. Camera trap footage from this area released by WWF this month showed a dozen tigers living in a logging concession. [Yale Environment 360]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Satellite Tour of a Threatened Rain Forest', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:23:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f275fc-e8af-5a3a-b39d-23bc6b98bd65', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f275fc-e8af-5a3a-b39d-23bc6b98bd65'}, {'abstract': 'Global Entertainment sold several cities on building arenas. But many have been a bust, and the cities are stuck with the losses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/a-companys-small-town-arenas-leave-cities-with-big-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Global Entertainment sold several cities on building arenas. But many have been a bust, and the cities are stuck with the losses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO RANCHO, N.M. — The plan sounded great during the real estate boom: build a midsize arena, stuff it with sports, music acts and monster trucks and create a centerpiece for the new city center being developed on a dusty mesa here, 20 miles north of downtown Albuquerque.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/17ranchopix/17ranchopix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/17ranchopix/17ranchopix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/17ranchopix/17ranchopix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/17ranchopix/17ranchopix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/17ranchopix/17ranchopix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Company’s Arenas Leave Cities With Big Problems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Small-Town Arenas, Big Financial Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Entertainment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name':