lle, N.Y., just across the border from Greenwich. On Sunday, he opened up those garages for a fund-raiser.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/16/automobiles/wheels/16wheels-pray.html', 'snippet': 'Malcom Pray was a car dealer in Greenwich, Conn., for about 25 years and started collecting cars in the early 1960s. Now he has more than 50 and keeps most of them in two garages in Banksville, N.Y., just across the border from Greenwich. On Sunda...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Malcom Pray was a car dealer in Greenwich, Conn., for about 25 years and started collecting cars in the early 1960s. Now he has more than 50 and keeps most of them in two garages in Banksville, N.Y., just across the border from Greenwich. On Sunday, he opened up those garages for a fund-raiser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/16/automobiles/wheels/16wheels-pray-slide-MLR5/16wheels-pray-slide-MLR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Car Collection Gets a Rare Showing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T18:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Wheels', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/73b70d95-2a2e-5a8d-bb75-9f18546e9935', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/73b70d95-2a2e-5a8d-bb75-9f18546e9935'}, {'abstract': 'The actor Rob Lowe recently visited The Times to talk about his memoir, “Stories I Only Tell My Friends.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/video-rob-lowe-on-writing-his-memoir/', 'snippet': 'The actor Rob Lowe recently visited The Times to talk about his memoir, “Stories I Only Tell My Friends.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actor Rob Lowe recently visited The Times to talk about his memoir, “Stories I Only Tell My Friends.” A video of his conversation with Sam Tanenhaus, the editor of the Book Review, is embedded above. Carina Chocano’s review of Mr. Lowe’s book — and Shirley MacLaine’s “I’m Over All That” —\xa0is online today. Also, Janet Maslin’s review of “Stories.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Rob Lowe on Writing His Memoir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T19:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc63450-0e5f-56ea-8ee7-fb83482bdae8', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc63450-0e5f-56ea-8ee7-fb83482bdae8'}, {'abstract': 'A Democratic consultant will help write a film about how candidates often use “the lowest means to achieve the greatest ends.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/politics-on-film-have-knife-will-use-it/', 'snippet': 'A Democratic consultant will help write a film about how candidates often use “the lowest means to achieve the greatest ends.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' In Washington, Chris Lehane, a Democratic consultant, is known – and this is a compliment in that world – as a fervent advocate of the dark arts of politics: the cutthroat, destroy-your-enemies, do-what-it-takes-to win approach to political campaigns. “In the last five days, it always comes down to a knife fight in a telephone booth,” Mr. Lehane said, commenting on the final days of the 2008 presidential campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics on Film: Have Knife, Will Use It', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehane, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T19:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/07c07ad5-e177-5f59-91ed-c0df1f47a89f', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07c07ad5-e177-5f59-91ed-c0df1f47a89f'}, {'abstract': 'Three view of the legacy of a departed expert on the intersection of energy, pollution, health and public welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/lester-lave-an-appreciation/', 'snippet': 'Three view of the legacy of a departed expert on the intersection of energy, pollution, health and public welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Keith, a University of Calgary researcher focused on carbon, climate and energy technology and policy, sent a note last week alerting me to the death of Lester B. Lave, an environmental economist at Carnegie Mellon University who had been a mentor, colleague and friend of his.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lester Lave – An Appreciation', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemicals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Apt, Jay', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lave, Lester', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Mellon University', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Calgary', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T19:05:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a02647-ea97-52f5-9dbf-ff7ba18a6ab4', 'word_count': 1545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a02647-ea97-52f5-9dbf-ff7ba18a6ab4'}, {'abstract': 'Now that Costa Rica’s best breaks have been overrun, Nicaragua is luring wave riders with low-key surf camps and undiscovered beaches.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/southern-swell/', 'snippet': 'Now that Costa Rica’s best breaks have been overrun, Nicaragua is luring wave riders with low-key surf camps and undiscovered beaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Costa Rica’s best breaks have been overrun, Nicaragua is luring wave riders with low-key surf camps and undiscovered beaches. Popoyo, on the southern Pacific coast, has the most consistent barrel, along with hotels like the Popoyo Beach Lodge (popoyobeachlodge.com; doubles from $55 ). But two and a half hours north of Managua and just west of the town of Chinandega lies the country’s undeveloped northern Pacific coast — and dozens of breaks so new that many don’t have names. This is where the pro surfer and model Holly Beck set up her camp, Suave Dulce (surfwithhollybeck.com) after she stopped competing in 2008. Nicaragua, says Beck, a California native, is the ideal place to “help people experience the joy of getting pushed by the ocean.” Many of Beck’s students stay at El Coco Loco (011-505-8999-8662; elcocolocoresort.com; doubles from $100), a rustic resort near the town of Santa Maria del Mar with five palm-thatch cabanas near several surf spots. La Bahia Beach Hodel (011-505-8958-5075; labahiabeachhotel.com; doubles from $150) is a more luxurious option: four stone-and-teak casitas with outdoor showers, private pathways to one of Nicaragua’s most beautiful beaches and three breaks in front of the hotel (with more nearby). Both resorts serve seafood delivered daily by local fishermen, and there’s also plenty of the local catch at Al Cielo (011-505-8993-4840), a popular open-air palapa run by two French guys, with 360-degree views.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Southern Swell', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T19:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, '