, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6a5b96a-26fe-5627-b63e-fb0f5442abfd'}, {'abstract': 'Now $40,000 in debt, Annie is miserably working in retail, living with two revolting roommates and driving a car that’s ready for the junkyard. And she can’t bear the thought of baking.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/what-bridesmaids-says-about-losing-a-business/', 'snippet': 'Now $40,000 in debt, Annie is miserably working in retail, living with two revolting roommates and driving a car that’s ready for the junkyard. And she can’t bear the thought of baking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend, I saw “Bridesmaids.” The movie, with its female-driven plot, is a welcome departure from the sappy fare typically marketed to women and the comedies that put them on the sidelines. But it’s also an exploration of the emotions that follow the failure of a small business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bridesmaids’ Looks at Losing a Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T19:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf19860f-ae26-5154-9a26-59384fb3da93', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf19860f-ae26-5154-9a26-59384fb3da93'}, {'abstract': 'TPG Capital has agreed to acquire Primedia in a deal valued at $525 million including debt, finally unwinding K.K.R.’s investment in the comp