11-12 television network upfronts continue in New York. Walking into the Beacon Theater this afternoon, where Fox is presenting its new prime-time schedule, attendees passed life-size visages of Simon Cowell. Fox is betting that Mr. Cowell’s “X Factor” will improve its performance in the fall just like “American Idol” has in the winter and spring. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Blogging the Upfronts: Fox', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ab4198f-805d-5a54-a4c7-693cad9821ee', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ab4198f-805d-5a54-a4c7-693cad9821ee'}, {'abstract': 'Derek Jeter has a conference call over his comments on Jorge Posada with Yankees officials.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/jeter-explains-posada-comments-to-yankees-officials/', 'snippet': 'Derek Jeter has a conference call over his comments on Jorge Posada with Yankees officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derek Jeter had a conference call with high-ranking Yankees officials Monday afternoon to clarify comments he made Sunday in support of Jorge Posada. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Explains Posada Comments to Yankees Officials', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8decdf4-6bc3-5f7d-814f-d903481534ff', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8decdf4-6bc3-5f7d-814f-d903481534ff'}, {'abstract': 'Biarritz, Europe’s surf capital since the 1950s, has managed to retain its scruffy coolness.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/basque-boogie/', 'snippet': 'Biarritz, Europe’s surf capital since the 1950s, has managed to retain its scruffy coolness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The laid-back Basque town of Biarritz has been Europe’s surf capital since the 1950s. Yet despite the crowds and the casinos, it has retained its scruffy coolness. The Bay of Biscay provides the town with two main waves: the Plage de la Côte des Basques, a popular and consistent sandbar break; and the Grande Plage, an unpredictable, high-performance beach break up the coast. At least a dozen groups give surfing lessons, among them Jo Moraiz (011-33-6-62-76-17-24; jomoraiz.com), France’s first surf school. Biarritz’s plushest beach hotel is the Hôtel Du Palais (011-33-5-59-41-64-00; hotel-du-palais.com; doubles from about $665), a palace-turned-hotel where Alain Ducasse worked one of his first kitchen jobs. You’re less likely to see surfers there than at one of the campgrounds on Biarritz’s outskirts. A happy medium between opulence and outdoors is Hôtel Le Caritz (011-33-5-59-24-41-84; hotel-lecaritz-biarritz.com; doubles from $210), a handsome inn with a terrace restaurant. For the closest surf proximity, try the basic but comfortable Carlina Lodge (011-33-5-59-24-42-14; carlina.com; doubles from $190), which has direct access to the Côte des Basques. For post-surf refueling, the lovely covered market Les Halles (halles-biarritz.fr) offers outdoor fish and tapas restaurants, palpable reminders of the city’s vicinity to Spain. And Le Surfing (011-33-5-59-24-78-72; lesurfingbiarritz.fr), an inviting bar and restaurant where vintage surf memorabilia serves as décor, might be the only brasserie in town that allows sandy feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Basque Boogie', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a66f40f6-0308-5e0f-a991-504d28ed840a', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a66f40f6-0308-5e0f-a991-504d28ed840a'}, {'abstract': 'The I.M.F. chief is denied bail in a sexual assault case; some in France see a setup; French journalists’ unspoken rule to protect politicians’ privacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000821438/timescast--may-16-2011.html', 'snippet': 'The I.M.F. chief is denied bail in a sexual assault case; some in France see a setup; French journalists’ unspoken rule to protect politicians’ privacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The I.M.F. chief is denied bail in a sexual assault case; some in France see a setup; French journalists’ unspoken rule to protect politicians’ privacy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm