Update, May 17, 4:08 p.m. | Read about the baby hawk’s newly bestowed name. » ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vote to Name the Baby Hawk', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:37:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7de815-8501-5368-ac2a-c547326ed853', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7de815-8501-5368-ac2a-c547326ed853'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets said David Wright, their third baseman, does not face surgery, but could miss several weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/baseball/mets-david-wright-has-stress-fracture-in-back.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets said David Wright, their third baseman, does not face surgery, but could miss several weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Wright pulled on a maroon Virginia Tech T-shirt, jeans and running shoes, then strolled out of the Mets’ clubhouse at 4:40 p.m. Monday, done for the day and who knows how much longer. A half-hour earlier, the club disclosed that he had a stress fracture in his lower back.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/baseball/17metspix/17metspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/baseball/17metspix/17metspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':