ox office from “The Lion King.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/earning-power-of-spider-man-undiminished/', 'snippet': 'With all the changes to the plot of “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark,” the Broadway musical’s creative team didn’t fiddle with its super-power earning potential, raking in almost $810,000 for just five preview performances last week.  “Wicked” regai...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Returning to Broadway after a brief hiatus to accommodate a creative overhaul, the musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark” earned $809,941 for five preview performances last week before mostly full audiences at the Foxwoods Theater, according to the weekly box office data released on Monday by the Broadway League.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earning Power of ‘Spider-Man’ Undiminished', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadway League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foxwoods Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1355e9af-1989-5d57-89ae-7cfb18f2722f', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1355e9af-1989-5d57-89ae-7cfb18f2722f'}, {'abstract': 'Malcolm Pray, whose cars are a fixture at the Greenwich Concours d’Élégance, held a charity viewing of his collection on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/for-two-hours-a-vintage-car-collector-throws-open-his-garage-doors/', 'snippet': 'Malcolm Pray, whose cars are a fixture at the Greenwich Concours d’Élégance, held a charity viewing of his collection on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he was growing up, Malcolm Pray went to the 1939 New York World’s Fair, where he saw a 1937 Delahaye. He promptly fell in love, and 25 years later, when he found that very car for sale, he bought it. That was the first purchase in a vintage-car collection that today consists of more than 50 vehicles.\u2028\u2028 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Two Hours, a Vintage Car Collector Throws Open His Garage Doors', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boys and Girls Clubs of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "World's Fair", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:48:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d9b5ee9-5e08-58a5-8166-3a8b25977688', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d9b5ee9-5e08-58a5-8166-3a8b25977688'}, {'abstract': 'In flood-ravaged Memphis, a high school hears from a bold-face-name commencement speaker.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/obama-and-graduates-cheer-for-each-other/', 'snippet': 'In flood-ravaged Memphis, a high school hears from a bold-face-name commencement speaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The graduating class of Booker T. Washington High School in Memphis was getting a last-minute pep talk from its principal, Alisha Kiner, on Monday, just before the ceremony began, when an out-of-town visitor dropped by to offer his own words of encouragement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Graduates Cheer for Each Other', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T20:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/65b3ebd4-21ed-5e50-a8b8-fbd520137cb9', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65b3ebd4-21ed-5e50-a8b8-fbd520137cb9'}, {'abstract': 'After Julio Garcia’s widow agreed to donate his organs, five recipients gathered in New York to thank the family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/health/17organ.html', 'snippet': 'After Julio Garcia’s widow agreed to donate his organs, five recipients gathered in New York to thank the family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mirtala Garcia laid a hand on Sebastiao Lourenco’s chest, then pressed her ear there for a moment.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17donorspan/17donorspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17donorspan/17donorspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '