hey will have a bar, a library lounge and two a la carte dining rooms will be installed in the ground floor and there will also be a seasonal outdoor dining room on the roof.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/humm-and-guidara-of-eleven-madison-park-will-run-restaurants-in-the-nomad-hotel/', 'snippet': 'They will have a bar, a library lounge and two a la carte dining rooms will be installed in the ground floor and there will also be a seasonal outdoor dining room on the roof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Humm and Will Guidara, the executive chef and manager of Eleven Madison Park, will be running the lounges and restaurants in the NoMad hotel, which is being developed on Broadway and 28th Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humm and Guidara of Eleven Madison Park Will Run Restaurants in the NoMad Hotel', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6dd8eff-ed08-5dc6-bbef-f51581c1f8f5', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6dd8eff-ed08-5dc6-bbef-f51581c1f8f5'}, {'abstract': 'Images of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, a French politician, being paraded in handcuffs before cameras in New York caused some observers in France to complain about the “violence” of the American justice system.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/french-shocked-by-i-m-f-chiefs-perp-walk/', 'snippet': 'Images of Dominique Strauss-Kahn, a French politician, being paraded in handcuffs before cameras in New York caused some observers in France to complain about the “violence” of the American justice system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As our colleagues Steven Erlanger and Katrin Bennhold report, “The arrest in New York of one of France’s leading global figures and a possible next president, Dominique Strauss-Kahn, on charges of attempted rape produced an earthquake of shock, outrage, disbelief and embarrassment throughout France on Sunday.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Shocked by I.M.F. Chief’s ‘Perp Walk’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare, Maïa de la Baume and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Maïa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Baume', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2501b6-deb1-521f-8baf-a9c9f6591f15', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2501b6-deb1-521f-8baf-a9c9f6591f15'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Olympia Snowe, the chief architect of legislation to set aside 2.5 percent of federal agency grants to outside researchers for small companies,  blocked a bill to extend the program.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/senate-posturing-kills-s-b-i-r-renewal-for-now/', 'snippet': 'Senator Olympia Snowe, the chief architect of legislation to set aside 2.5 percent of federal agency grants to outside researchers for small companies,  blocked a bill to extend the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Efforts to renew — and overhaul — the well-regarded Small Business Investment Research and Small Business Technology Transfer programs, which expire at the end of this month, may be in jeopardy now that the Senate appears unlikely to vote on its reauthorization bill anytime soon. And the person behind that bill’s demise, according to Democrats, at least, happens to be one of its chief architects — Senator Olympia Snowe, the Maine Republican on the Senate Small Business Committee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Posturing Kills Small Business Investment Research Renewal', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:06:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e683af2-c651-59b0-89d8-679efcf34b03', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e683af2-c651-59b0-89d8-679efcf34b03'}, {'abstract': '“You’re Fired” is apparently too good to resist in stories about Mr. Trump himself.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/in-trump-coverage-catchphrase-becomes-cliche/', 'snippet': '“You’re Fired” is apparently too good to resist in stories about Mr. Trump himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was as common as the lack of surprise that greeted Donald Trump’s announcement that he would not run for president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Trump Coverage, Catchphrase Becomes Cliché', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Science Monitor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politico, The', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/02e54fe1-e0c6-594f-8ac6-c4df5f4d4d29', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02e54fe1-e0c6-594f-8ac6-c4df5f4d4d29'}, {'abstract': 'Jason Moran and Meshell Ndegeocello led a band through tunes with fragments of Fats Waller songs at the Harlem Stage Gatehouse in the “Fats Waller Dance Party: Small’s Paradise.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/arts/music/jason-moran-and-meshell-ndegeocello-play-fats-waller-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jason Moran and Meshell Ndegeocello led a band through tunes with fragments of Fats Waller songs at the Harlem Stage Gatehouse in the “Fats Waller Dance Party: Small’s Paradise.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once, a special event in jazz meant something warm and secretive and spontaneous: two guys who hadn’t seen each other in a while, improvising several choruses together. But lately — since the early 1990s, when jazz became fixed in the world of arts grants and cultural institutions — it has often meant something more structured, official and imposing: heady written music, presented before a theater audience, sometimes elaborated with text or image or drama, program-noted and documented and ready to be reproduced elsewhere.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/WALLER/WALLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/WALLER/WALLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/WALLER/WALLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feet’s Too Big? No Problem; Everyone Dances Here', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feet’s Too Big? No Problem; Everyone Dances Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ndegeocello, Meshell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harlem Stage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moran, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcc0ea48-9420-5461-be1e-949f319ed6e4', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcc0ea48-9420-5461-be1e-949f319ed6e4'}, {'abstract': 'At the Wall to Wall Sonidos marathons at Symphony Space, the program explored Latino culture, with performers and composers from Spain and Central and South America representing myriad styles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/arts/music/wall-to-wall-sonidos-at-symphony-space-review.html', 'snippet': 'At the Wall to Wall Sonidos marathons at Symphony Space, the program explored Latino culture, with performers and composers from Spain and Central and South America representing myriad styles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since their founding in 1978, the annual Wall to Wall 12-hour marathons at Symphony Space have focused on a single composer; a genre, like opera; or a region, as did last year’s survey of music from behind the Iron Curtain. On Saturday the Wall to Wall Sonidos program explored Latino culture, with performers and composers from Spain and Central and South America representing myriad styles, including 16th-century vocal polyphony, tango, contemporary string quartets and Latin jazz. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/SONIDOS/SONIDOS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/SONIDOS/SONIDOS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTy