e artistic director of Shiseido Makeup, Page traverses the usual New York-Paris-London-Milan-Tokyo circuit. When it comes to his coveted downtime, however, he gets off fashion’s beaten track, heading for rugged destinations like Iceland and the Arctic. The Long Island country ‘‘shack’’ he shares with his husband, James Gibbs, serves as the starting point for his favorite way to explore: camping. ‘‘Our Teardrop trailer is always ready to go,’’ he says. As is his Olympus digital camera: ‘‘I photograph everything.’’ Naturally, Page’s photos don’t merely serve as souvenirs — they also become makeup colors. View slide show >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style | Dick Page', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c0b38f9-ea06-5761-804b-db37fd23d06b', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c0b38f9-ea06-5761-804b-db37fd23d06b'}, {'abstract': 'Julio Garcia died unexpectedly in 2010. His widow decided to donate his organs to seven different people. And they recently had the opportunity to thank her in person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/health/100000000821483/donating-lives.html', 'snippet': 'Julio Garcia died unexpectedly in 2010. His widow decided to donate his organs to seven different people. And they recently had the opportunity to thank her in person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julio Garcia died unexpectedly in 2010. His widow decided to donate his organs to seven different people. And they recently had the opportunity to thank her in person.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/video-transplant/video-transplant-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/science/video-transplant/video-transplant-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/video-transplant/video-transplant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/science/video-transplant/video-transplant-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donating Lives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellick, Adam B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'Adam B. Ellick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/617f1e45-2e6e-53ec-a0da-d56823bdb0bf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/617f1e45-2e6e-53ec-a0da-d56823bdb0bf'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found that great desert skinks build and maintain elaborate tunneled homes, where they live in cooperative multigenerational family groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/science/17oblizard.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found that great desert skinks build and maintain elaborate tunneled homes, where they live in cooperative multigenerational family groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many animals build houses for their offspring, but no one thought lizards were among them. Now researchers have found that great desert skinks, lizards that live only in northern Australia, build and maintain elaborate tunneled homes, where they live in cooperative multigenerational family groups.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17oblizardspan/17oblizardspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17oblizardspan/17oblizardspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17oblizardspan/17lizardspan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17oblizardspan/17oblizardspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/science/17oblizardspan/17oblizardspan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lizard That Builds With the Family in Mind', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lizard That Builds With the Family in Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'va