7/arts/music/hearing-10-new-works-at-the-vox-festival-of-city-opera.html', 'snippet': 'As City Opera’s board ponders a next season, the company’s Vox festival previewed 10 mostly safe works in progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The board of New York City Opera is to meet on Thursday and consider that beleaguered company’s plans for next season. As it happened, the discussion about City Opera’s uncertain future coincided with Vox, the company’s annual festival of contemporary American opera, which was held over the weekend at New York University’s Skirball Center and at Le Poisson Rouge. Since its start in 1999, Vox has been the centerpiece of City Opera’s vision of itself as a “lab” for new work; the festival’s tag line has long been “Preview the Future of Opera.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/vox/vox-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/vox/vox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/vox/vox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Vox Festival, Future of City Opera Sounds All Too Familiar', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Vox Festival, Future Of City Opera Sounds All Too Familiar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zorn, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60e0bc2e-0575-5d83-b211-d0a69fbb8f21', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60e0bc2e-0575-5d83-b211-d0a69fbb8f21'}, {'abstract': 'A business leaders’ committee has spent millions on advertising in support of a pared-down New York State budget.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/group-spent-nearly-5-million-backing-cuomo-budget/', 'snippet': 'A business leaders’ committee has spent millions on advertising in support of a pared-down New York State budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY – A coalition of business leaders supportive of Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo spent nearly $5 million in the past two months lobbying in favor of the governor’s budget and his proposal to limit local property taxes, according to a new filing with the state ethics commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Spent Nearly $5 Million Backing Cuomo Budget', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d0d3149-af53-5a35-a4f8-cebbf38d5634', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d0d3149-af53-5a35-a4f8-cebbf38d5634'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Tree of Life” Terrence Malick takes a direct approach in asking some big questions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/movies/terrence-malick-asks-big-questions-in-the-tree-of-life.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Tree of Life” Terrence Malick takes a direct approach in asking some big questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — In “The Tree of Life,” a cosmic head movie of the most ambitious order, Terrence Malick reaches high, his ecstatic camera and thoughts soaring. Shown on Monday morning at a press screening at the 64th Cannes Film Festival, where it was met with pre-emptive, harshly insistent boos and a vigorous rejoinder of equally determined applause, the film directly addresses the larger questions of existence that are woven throughout Mr. Malick’s work. It seeks to affirm the beauty of a world in which God is present in all things. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/JPMALICK/JPMALICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/JPMALICK/JPMALICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/JPMALICK/JPMALICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/JPMALICK/JPMALICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/JPMALICK/JPMALICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Malick’s Film Adds a Dose of Sincerity to the Festivities', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Cirque de Cannes, Party Love and Movie Love: Throwing In a Dose of Sincerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malick, Terrence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/854ed8bf-a833-5579-acaf-b04b8f290855', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/854ed8bf-a833-5579-acaf-b04b8f290855'}, {'abstract': 'The Salzburg Easter Festival is scrambling to find a substitute for the Berlin Philharmonic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/arts/music/salzburg-must-replace-berlin-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'The Salzburg Easter Festival is scrambling to find a substitute for the Berlin Philharmonic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Salzburg Easter Festival is scrambling to find a substitute for the Berlin Philharmonic, which said last week that after next year it would move to Baden-Baden’s Festspielhaus, or festival hall. “This has to be a reinvention, a restart of the whole thing, or we have to quit it,” Martin Riegler, the festival’s spokesman, said on Monday. Officials were trying to “find a future for the festival,” including a new orchestra, he said. The festival was founded in 1967 by the Philharmonic’s conductor, Herbert von Karajan, as a place for it to play opera. The decision to move to Baden-Baden follows a financial scandal that led to allegations of fraud against two former officials. In explaining the move, a Philharmonic spokesman, Olaf Maninger, said, “We need the kind of long-term security that the Baden-Baden Festspielhaus has to offer,” according to Bloomberg News. Mr. Riegler said the orchestra wanted to expand its offerings beyond the two opera performances, six concerts and handful of chamber music performances it has been giving in Salzburg. “We don’t have the money for it, and Baden-Baden seems to have,” he said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salzburg Must Replace Berlin Philharmonic', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salzburg Must Replace Berlin Philharmonic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a62771b-1241-5c77-b782-2aa0069798e7', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a62771b-1241-5c77-b782-2aa0069798e7'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Israel, Lebanon, Libya and Turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/pictures-of-the-day-israel-and-elsewhere-4/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Israel, Lebanon, Libya and Turkey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Israel, Lebanon, Libya and Turkey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Israel and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times'