'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ea96d9-6417-57ab-bbd3-9f42f10265b0'}, {'abstract': 'Kristen Wiig’s comedy “Bridesmaids” sold $26.2 million in tickets over the weekend, more than was estimated at the end of the weekend, but for Mr. Apatow, a producer of the film, the gender debate it initiated isn’t over yet.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/hold-on-for-one-more-day-judd-apatow-talks-about-the-aftermath-of-bridesmaids/', 'snippet': 'Kristen Wiig’s comedy “Bridesmaids” sold $26.2 million in tickets over the weekend, more than was estimated at the end of the weekend, but for Mr. Apatow, a producer of the film, the gender debate it initiated isn’t over yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looks like moviegoers tossed Kristen Wiig a bigger bouquet than was originally expected this weekend: her new Universal comedy “Bridesmaids” sold $26.2 million through Sunday, according to box-office numbers released on Monday, up from the $24.4 million in ticket sales estimated on Sunday. That’s good news for Ms. Wiig and her co-screenwriter, Annie Mumolo; the film’s director, Paul Feig; its prolific producer, Judd Apatow (of “Knocked Up” and “Funny People” renown), fans of funny women and anyone who likes to laugh at moving images displayed on a screen, all of whom had pretty much concluded that “Bridesmaids” was a crucial standard-bearer for studio comedies with female leads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hold On for One More Day: Judd Apatow Talks About the Aftermath of ‘Bridesmaids’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T21:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstna