ity-review.html', 'snippet': 'A revival of “Winter Wedding” at Theater for the New City spotlights the mad satire of Hanoch Levin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Israeli playwright Hanoch Levin (1943-99) ticked off many of his countrymen with his blowtorch satires on human venality, often with a political dimension. With “Winter Wedding,” now in a revival ably directed by David Willinger at Theater for the New City, he pillories the familial calamities of matrimony with cynicism, absurdist flair and relish for whoopee-cushion humor. (The play, translated by the director and Laurel Hessing, has been retitled from its original, “Winter Funeral.”)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/winter/winter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Funeral Party Ran Off; Now Go Chase It Down', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Winter Wedding' ", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Funeral Party Ran Off; Now Go Chase It Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Hanoch', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zane, Debra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater for the New City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T22:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/38222727-48bd-56de-8588-b4204ded5f