tery-could-create-more-problems-than-solutions.html', 'snippet': 'The Minnesota Timberwolves have the best chance of winning the No. 1 pick Tuesday, but doing so could limit their options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A. draft lottery, an event that hinges on bouncing Ping-Pong balls, can give a team hope of claiming direction and focus out of years of misfortune.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Draft Lottery Could Create More Problems Than Solutions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Draft Lottery Could Create More Problems Than Solutions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:35:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dc2929b-eac0-585c-893c-1ae68d88acd2', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dc2929b-eac0-585c-893c-1ae68d88acd2'}, {'abstract': 'While promising more efficiency than a traditional hot-water tank, tankless heaters come with their own set of dos and don’ts.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/home-tech-tankless-water-heaters-explained/', 'snippet': 'While promising more efficiency than a traditional hot-water tank, tankless heaters come with their own set of dos and don’ts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months ago my husband and I moved into a house outfitted with a “demand” or “tankless” water heater. Having lived only in rentals that were tapped into giant hot-water tanks, I was intrigued by the device’s claims of energy efficiency. But after a few weeks of turning on the faucet as I normally do, I began to wonder if I was using my newfangled appliance the way it was meant to be. I decided to find out exactly how these new warmers work, and how to best to take advantage of their efficiency claims. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Tech: Tankless Water Heaters Explained', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Heaters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:36:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonia Zjawinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zjawinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8245143-b16b-59fe-a8d7-2742d7322922', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8245143-b16b-59fe-a8d7-2742d7322922'}, {'abstract': 'A more disciplined Tampa Bay team, which refused to retaliate against Boston at the end of their series opener, could be tested again Tuesday in Game 2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/hockey/nhl-playoffs-lightning-leads-with-its-focus-not-with-its-fists.html', 'snippet': 'A more disciplined Tampa Bay team, which refused to retaliate against Boston at the end of their series opener, could be tested again Tuesday in Game 2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Last season, the Tampa Bay Lightning was the most penalized team in the N.H.L. This season, under its first-year coach, Guy Boucher, 21 teams took more penalties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lightning Leads With Its Focus, Not With Its Fists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lecavalier, Vincent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c7c9d16-fba4-56bc-a9a7-7dcf417c0c82', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c7c9d16-fba4-56bc-a9a7-7dcf417c0c82'}, {'abstract': 'Bing announces new social features that tap in Facebook data to improve search results.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/bing-taps-facebook-data-for-fight-with-google/', 'snippet': 'Bing announces new social features that tap in Facebook data to improve search results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Microsoft is hoping that its alliance with Facebook will get more people to choose Bing over Google.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bing Taps Facebook Data for Fight With Google', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f84f9673-4855-561f-b71c-71d8a44b3b26', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f84f9673-4855-561f-b71c-71d8a44b3b26'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Nuclear Regulatory Commission said its 24-hour operations center had stopped monitoring the nuclear reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi plant because the situation there had improved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/asia/17briefs-Fukushima.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Nuclear Regulatory Commission said its 24-hour operations center had stopped monitoring the nuclear reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi plant because the situation there had improved.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Nuclear Regulatory Commission said on Monday that its 24-hour operations center had stopped monitoring the nuclear reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi plant because the situation there had improved. “The conditions at the Japanese reactors are slowly stabilizing,” said William Borchardt, the agency’s chief staff official. “As conditions have continued to improve and the Japanese continue to implement their recovery plan, the N.R.C. has determined that it is time to adjust our response,” he said. The agency still has a team of engineers in Tokyo, he said. Mr. Borchardt said last week that the condition of the reactors was “static but not stable.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: U.S. Agency to Stop Monitoring Nuclear Plant', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: U.S. Agency to Stop Monitoring Nuclear Plant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:44:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd62db3d-3c74-5012-a4ff-b53b3c1e9312', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd62db3d-3c74-5012-a4ff-b53b3c1e9312'}, {'abstract': 'After Derek Jeter had a conference call with Yankees officials to discuss his comments about Jorge Posada, the team blew a four-run lead against Tampa Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/baseball/call-with-derek-jeter-cant-put-end-to-yankees-problems.html', 'snippet': 'After Derek Jeter had a conference call with Yankees officials to discuss his comments about Jorge Posada, the team blew a four-run lead against Tampa Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — A new workweek dawned Monday, and with it came the opportunity for the Yankees to purge themselves of one of the uglier stretches in Joe Girardi’s tenure. Off the field, a messy dispute engulfed the front office, the manager and two of the club’s iconic players. On it, ragged performances had dropped them out of first place in the American League East, sending them backsliding toward mediocrity.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Tension, Yanks’ Slump Hits 6', 'kicker': 'Rays 6, Yankees 5', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Tension, Yanks’ Slump Reaches 6', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, Hal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:51:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73bb2059-be81-513a-a76f-d7633a2966ed', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73bb2059-be81-513a-a76f-d7633a2966ed'}, {'abstract': 'A Belarussian court convicted a journalist and critic of the nation’s authoritarian president on Monday of helping to organize a large antigovernment protest in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/europe/17briefs-Belarus.html', 'snippet': 'A Belarussian court convicted a journalist and critic of the nation’s authoritarian president on Monday of helping to organize a large antigovernment protest in December.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Belarussian court convicted a journalist and critic of the nation’s authoritarian president on Monday of helping to organize a large antigovernment protest in December. The journalist, Irina Khalip, received a two-year suspended sentence. Her husband, Andrei Sannikov, a former presidential candidate, was sentenced to five years in prison on Saturday for a similar offense, and the authorities had previously threatened to take custody of their young son. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus: Government Critic Sentenced Over Protest', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus: Government Critic Sentenced Over Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sannikov, Andrei', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khalip, Irina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b732c818-4222-5bc1-bffd-6398e91195a3', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b732c818-4222-5bc1-bffd-6398e91195a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Forbidden City’s management group handed out registration forms last month for a luxury private club to be located in the compound’s Jianfu Pavilion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/asia/17briefs-forbidden.html', 'snippet': 'The Forbidden City’s management group handed out registration forms last month for a luxury private club to be located in the compound’s Jianfu Pavilion.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Forbidden City’s management group handed out registration forms last month for a luxury private club to be located in the compound’s Jianfu Pavilion, which was restored with money from a fund in Hong Kong, according to a report in The Beijing News on Sunday and in the English-language edition of Global Times on Monday. Rumors about the club surfaced last week, when Rui Chenggang, an anchor for China Central Television, said on his microblog that the entry fee was one million renminbi, or about $154,000. Officials sent a statement to Global Times saying there were no plans to open any club. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Rumors of a Private Club in the Forbidden City', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Rumors of a Private Club in the Forbidden City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rui Chenggang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-16T23:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World'