her way to the airport to fly to the United States when her car was stopped by security forces and towed to a police station. She was soon released. Mr. Besigye has staged twice-weekly street demonstrations over the last month and has been arrested repeatedly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uganda: Opposition Leader’s Wife Is Briefly Held', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | AFRICA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uganda: Opposition Leader’s Wife Is Briefly Held', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Development Program', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Besigye, Kizza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:33:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/006652ed-2bc4-57e8-a0c1-249fbe605e0d', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006652ed-2bc4-57e8-a0c1-249fbe605e0d'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent article about the arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/l17kahn.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent article about the arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The I.M.F. Chief’s Arrest', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The I.M.F. Chief&#8217;s Arrest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1676758-5496-5715-bede-6da933ce90a1', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1676758-5496-5715-bede-6da933ce90a1'}, {'abstract': 'The game plan of Chicago Coach Tom Thibodeau was a key to limiting LeBron James to 15 points in a runaway Game 1 victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sports/basketball/discipline-on-defense-helps-bulls-stop-heat.html', 'snippet': 'The game plan of Chicago Coach Tom Thibodeau was a key to limiting LeBron James to 15 points in a runaway Game 1 victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — LeBron James’s nemesis stands about 6 feet tall, with thinning hair, a thickish torso and a reputation for rarely leaving the office. In his starched white shirt and crisp suit, Tom Thibodeau looks more likely to sell James a life insurance policy than he is to thwart his title hopes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 847, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/yBULLS/yBULLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulls’ Defense Is Devilishly Familiar to the Heat’s James', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bulls’ Defense Is Devilishly Familiar to the Heat’s James', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thibodeau, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04170131-6e65-572f-986e-4887b2f041f1', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04170131-6e65-572f-986e-4887b2f041f1'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent Week in Review article about the flooding of the Mississippi River.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/l17warming.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent Week in Review article about the flooding of the Mississippi River.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Global Warming', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Global Warming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e41e87f-b63f-5ddf-b823-7bd5d783e272', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e41e87f-b63f-5ddf-b823-7bd5d783e272'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy was dealt a resounding blow on Monday when Mayor Letizia Moratti of Milan failed to avoid a run-off in her bid for re-election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/europe/17briefs-milan.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy was dealt a resounding blow on Monday when Mayor Letizia Moratti of Milan failed to avoid a run-off in her bid for re-election.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi of Italy was dealt a resounding blow on Monday when Mayor Letizia Moratti, left, of Milan failed to avoid a runoff in her bid for re-election. Mr. Berlusconi had staked his reputation in support of Ms. Moratti and had campaigned strenuously for her. But with two-thirds of the votes counted, the center-left candidate Giuliano Pisapia was well out in front, but was short of a majority. The runoff election will be in two weeks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Berlusconi Candidate Trails in Milan Race', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Berlusconi Candidate Trails in Milan Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moratti, Letizia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:37:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/41eb8580-f6c9-5958-9b93-87e6704137d8', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41eb8580-f6c9-5958-9b93-87e6704137d8'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent column about female genital mutilation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/l17kristof.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent column about female genital mutilation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ending Genital Mutilation', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ending Genital Mutilation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Female Genital Mutilation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T00:45:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f74d0e5-1048-5447-91a9-16bee1addac9', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f74d0e5-1048-5447-91a9-16bee1addac