bstract': 'Hair used for extensions has become so valuable that thieves sometimes bypass the cash register and go right for the hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/us/17hair.html', 'snippet': 'Hair used for extensions has become so valuable that thieves sometimes bypass the cash register and go right for the hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thieves pulled the iron bars out of the windows, outsmarted the motion detector that would have triggered a burglar alarm and did not give the safe or cash register a second look.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/HAIR/HAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/us/HAIR/HAIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/HAIR/HAIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/HAIR/HAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/us/HAIR/HAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Costly Hairstyle Is a Beauty Trend That Draws Thieves’ Notice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Costly Hairstyle Is a Beauty Trend That Draws Thieves’ Notice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd8b38fa-a142-5772-9cb7-2ef882146d3a', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8b38fa-a142-5772-9cb7-2ef882146d3a'}, {'abstract': 'Medicare can’t push doctors to use a cheaper drug, even if it is as effective as a far costlier one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/17tue2.html', 'snippet': 'Medicare can’t push doctors to use a cheaper drug, even if it is as effective as a far costlier one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before you take a drug or undergo a medical procedure, wouldn’t you want to be sure it is the most effective and, if possible, the least costly available? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Value of Comparison', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Value of Comparison: Medicare can’t push doctors to use a cheaper drug, even if it is as effective as a far costlier one', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avastin (Drug)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Macular Degeneration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genentech Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb0d36e-ce6f-5027-a8fb-00966feaeb5b', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb0d36e-ce6f-5027-a8fb-00966feaeb5b'}, {'abstract': 'Congress should reject the N.R.A.’s latest proposed legislation, and the federal government should ban the use of lead in hunting and fishing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/17tue3.html', 'snippet': 'Congress should reject the N.R.A.’s latest proposed legislation, and the federal government should ban the use of lead in hunting and fishing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Environmental Protection Agency declined to block the use of lead in hunting and fishing last year. It was the wrong call. To ensure that the agency doesn’t come to its senses, the National Rifle Association — assisted, as usual, by Congress — is pushing legislation that would bar the E.P.A. from restricting the sale of lead shot and bullets or lead sinkers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Misguided Idea From the Gun Lobby', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Misguided Idea From the Gun Lobby', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lead', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f84d0ce-b728-5915-b1e8-f14739d0c5c8', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f84d0ce-b728-5915-b1e8-f14739d0c5c8'}, {'abstract': 'As a cast of top Washington figures looked on, Rahm Emanuel was sworn in Monday as mayor of Chicago, promising sweeping change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/us/politics/17rahm.html', 'snippet': 'As a cast of top Washington figures looked on, Rahm Emanuel was sworn in Monday as mayor of Chicago, promising sweeping change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — As a cast of top Washington figures looked on, Rahm Emanuel was sworn in Monday as mayor of Chicago, offering praise to the longtime mayor he succeeds but mainly promising sweeping change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/rahm/rahm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/rahm/rahm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/us/rahm/rahm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Washington Flavor as Chicago Swears in a Mayor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Washington Flavor as Chicago Swears In a Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23278247-f687-5cd1-a819-46410baf20e7', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23278247-f687-5cd1-a819-46410baf20e7'}, {'abstract': 'A law giving a special statewide commission the power to authorize charter schools is struck down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/education/17georgia.html', 'snippet': 'A law giving a special statewide commission the power to authorize charter schools is struck down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ruling by the Georgia Supreme Court on Monday cast doubt on the future of 17 charter schools there, leaving thousands of families uncertain about whether classes will continue through the end of the academic year and how students will continue in the fall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Georgia, Court Ruling Could Close Some Charter Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Georgia, Court Ruling Could Close Some Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dillon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/732ff8a3-2975-5078-9fb8-f636799055cc', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732ff8a3-2975-5078-9fb8-f636799055cc'}, {'abstract': 'A painting at the National Portrait Gallery of Bill and Melinda Gates is one of the first to be commissioned and completed of someone not a president who is still alive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/opinion/17tue4.html', 'snippet': 'A painting at the National Portrait Gallery of Bill and Melinda Gates is one of the first to be commissioned and completed of someone not a president who is still alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new portrait of Bill and Melinda Gates commissioned by the National Portrait Gallery in Washington depicts the leaders of the giant foundation bearing their name, and its work, with a respectful familiarity. Sitting on the arm of a chair with his arms crossed, Bill Gates appears supremely self-assured. Sitting slightly in front, Melinda looks confident. Over her shoulder is a video monitor showing two African girls and displaying “ALL LIVES HAVE EQUAL VALUE.” That is the credo of their foundation that addresses huge problems in American education, global health and other areas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gateses as ‘Living Sitters’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Gateses as &#8216;Living Sitters&#8217;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Portrait Gallery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Melinda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba99dabe-8ac1-55e8-9ab2-19ad022a31bb', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba99dabe-8ac1-55e8-9ab2-19ad022a31bb'}, {'abstract': 'John J. O’Connor, the president of the State University’s research foundation, is accused of giving a no-show job to the daughter of former Senate Majority Leader Joseph L. Bruno.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/nyregion/suny-official-in-bruno-case-takes-leave-of-absence.html', 'snippet': 'John J. O’Connor, the president of the State University’s research foundation, is accused of giving a no-show job to the daughter of former Senate Majority Leader Joseph L. Bruno.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — A top official at the State University of New York accused of giving a no-show job to the daughter of former Senate Majority Leader Joseph L. Bruno agreed on Monday to take a leave of absence until his case is resolved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SUNY Official in Bruno Case Takes Leave of Absence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SUNY Official in Bruno Case Takes Leave of Absence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBANY (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruno, Joseph L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, John J", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T02:49:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8ef11b3-a81a-5a18-b4b5-41b01596325a', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8ef11b3-a81a-5a18-b4b5-41b01596325a'}, {'abstract': 'A display of Hollywood excess brought crowds to Disneyland for the premiere of “Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/us/17outhere.html', 'snippet': 'A display of Hollywood excess brought crowds to Disneyland for the premiere of “Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was the 3,000-foot red carpet (though in this case it was black) that rolled up Main Street in Disneyland, right to Frontierland. The street was lined with television cameras, correspondents and photographers. Nearly 20,000 fans, many wearing mouse ears, screamed at people they recognized, or thought they recognized. It all led to a full-blown outdoor theater, with a 3-D screen and stadium seating for 2,000 guests, built — for this night only— over a lake in the center of Disneyland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/17outhere1_span/17outhere1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/us/17outhere1_span/17outhere1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/17outhere1_span/17outhere1_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/us/17outhere1_span/17outhere1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 't