given to him earlier in the day from the Yankees’ executive vice president, Felix Lopez.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/16/soriano-to-have-elbow-examined/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Soriano said he expected to miss another week or two based on advice given to him earlier in the day from the Yankees’ executive vice president, Felix Lopez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — Rafael Soriano has been with the Yankees for an eventful four months, and his tenure took another fascinating turn Monday night after their 6-5 loss to the Tampa Bay Rays.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soriano to Have Elbow Examined', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T03:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc9fe99c-066d-5f84-8d81-0db191fccfbd', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc9fe99c-066d-5f84-8d81-0db191fccfbd'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Flanigan had sung, managed and advised the singing group since its founding in 1948.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/arts/music/bob-flanigan-84-four-freshmen-founder.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Flanigan had sung, managed and advised the singing group since its founding in 1948.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bob Flanigan, a founding member of the Four Freshmen, the well-scrubbed tight-harmony group begun more than 60 years ago, when all of its members really were undergraduates, died on Sunday at his home in Las Vegas. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/FLANIGAN-obit/FLANIGAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/FLANIGAN-obit/FLANIGAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/arts/FLANIGAN-obit/FLANIGAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Flanigan, Four Freshmen Founder, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bob Flanigan, 84, Four Freshmen Founder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flanigan, Bob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T03:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b91ad98-9a05-5026-abc5-68a3673b64e2', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b91ad98-9a05-5026-abc5-68a3673b64e2'}, {'abstract': 'A judge sentenced two American pilots to community service for their role in a collision over the Amazon rain forest that killed 154 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/world/americas/17brazil.html', 'snippet': 'A judge sentenced two American pilots to community service for their role in a collision over the Amazon rain forest that killed 154 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — A Brazilian federal judge on Monday sentenced two American pilots involved in a fatal air crash over the Amazon rain forest in 2006 to community service. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pilots Avoid Jail in Brazil Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pilots Avoid Jail In Brazil Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepore, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airplane Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paladino, Jan Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T03:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c851db05-e207-50b8-a903-43a53b64ce53', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c851db05-e207-50b8-a903-43a53b64ce53'}, {'abstract': 'David Rosenthal’s new imprint at Penguin Group USA will be called Blue Rider Press and will publish its first book in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/penguins-new-imprint-blue-rider-press/', 'snippet': 'David Rosenthal’s new imprint at Penguin Group USA will be called Blue Rider Press and will publish its first book in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For six months, the new imprint at Penguin Group USA headed by David Rosenthal has remained stubbornly nameless. No longer, Mr. Rosenthal said on Monday: it will be called Blue Rider Press, a name inspired by the group of painters in early 20th-century Germany who bucked convention and promoted individual expression. “The Blue Rider name historically represents individuality and quality in the arts,” Mr. Rosenthal said in an e-mail. “And that same intent will be reflected in the eclectic fiction and nonfiction books Blue Rider Press will publish.” Mr. Rosenthal’s imprint will release its first titles in the fall, including “The New New Rules” by Bill Maher and a bedtime story parody, “Goodnight iPad.” It has also acquired books by Valerie Plame Wilson, Delia Ephron and R. A. Dickey. Mr. Rosenthal was offered his own imprint at Penguin after losing his job as publisher of the flagship imprint of Simon & Schuster last summer, and joins other Penguin imprints like Riverhead Books, Portfolio and the Penguin Press. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Penguin’s New Imprint: Blue Rider Press', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T04:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d16b62d6-7867-5ae8-ae3c-d0daa1fae072', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d16b62d6-7867-5ae8-ae3c-d0daa1fae072'}, {'abstrac