e-to-give-up-post-op-photo-ops/', 'snippet': 'Every president in memory has obliged the still photographers by allowing them a few minutes of post-speech face time. Until now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday morning, May 2, readers of The New York Times — and newspapers around the country — could pick up the latest editions to see the face of President Obama staring back at them from Page 1 with that quiet but steely resolve that had been evident the night before. It seemed a fitting record of his announcement that Osama bin Laden had been killed by American forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Stops Post-Speech Photo Ops', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin and David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ed85580-afc6-51b3-8a9e-914db45ce830', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ed85580-afc6-51b3-8a9e-914db45ce830'}, {'abstract': 'Manchester City has a shiny new silver trophy, paid for largely with Middle Eastern gold, but can money really buy happiness?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/was-manchester-citys-trophy-worth-what-it-cost/', 'snippet': 'Manchester City has a shiny new silver trophy, paid for largely with Middle Eastern gold, but can money really buy happiness?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manchester City has a shiny new silver trophy, paid for largely with Middle Eastern gold, and a reason to beat its chest in the streets of a city long dominated by its crosstown rival. It will surely take more than an F.A. Cup triumph for Manchester City to close the gap on mighty Manchester United, but after hundreds of millions of dollars spent to build a Premier League contender, it’s something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Manchester City’s Trophy Worth What It Cost?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T09:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a0e6b9-3860-5b95-a9a2-0d86f37ae14d', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a0e6b9-3860-5b95-a9a2-0d86f37ae14d'}, {'abstract': 'What would you want to be able to do with your money to consider yourself well-off as opposed to middle class?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/how-do-you-define-wealthy/', 'snippet': 'What would you want to be able to do with your money to consider yourself well-off as opposed to middle class?', 'lead_paragraph': 'To separate the middle class from the wealthy, federal income tax policy sets the dividing line at $250,000 for family income. But some people have disputed that policy, arguing that there’s a big difference between earning a quarter of a million dollars a year – especially in a high-cost-of-living area – and earning millions or even billions. What do you think? How do you define “wealthy”? How much do you think a family needs to earn to be considered wealthy by the government? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Define Wealthy?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T09:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/af8840ae-9280-5585-bf7c-c1afc664b058', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af8840ae-9280-5585-bf7c-c1afc664b058'}, {'abstract': 'Hours before Queen Elizabeth II was to arrive in Dublin on Tuesday, the army there defused a pipe bomb discovered on a bus heading for the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/europe/18queen.html', 'snippet': 'Hours before Queen Elizabeth II was to arrive in Dublin on Tuesday, the army there defused a pipe bomb discovered on a bus heading for the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Brushing aside bomb threats, Queen Elizabeth II embarked on the first visit by a reigning British monarch to the Irish Republic on Tuesday — a visit heavy on symbolism after decades of hostility and mistrust, and protected by some of the tightest security Dubliners could recall. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/world/europe/QUEEN/QUEEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Found in Bus in Ireland Hours Before Queen Arrives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bomb Found in Bus in Ireland Hours Before Queen Arrives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T09:36:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell and Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc410a9d-44c0-5a20-a48b-5c90bc4537be', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc410a9d-44c0-5a20-a48b-5c90bc4537be'}, {'abstract': 'After a competitive bidding process, Toshiba has emerged as the sole potential buyer for Landis & Gyr, a Swiss smart-metering company, in a deal that could be worth more than $2 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/toshiba-in-advanced-talks-to-buy-landis-gyr/', 'snippet': 'After a competitive bidding process, Toshiba ha