blic Library has created a new iPad app that bring the library’s research collections to users’ tablet computers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/new-york-public-library-launches-ipad-app/', 'snippet': 'the New York Public Library has created a new iPad app that bring the library’s research collections to users’ tablet computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here an app, there an app, everywhere an apt app. Now, the New York Public Library has created a new iPad app that bring the library’s research collections into “the palms of the public’s hand,” as library officials put it in a statement released Tuesday. “Biblion: The Boundless Library” is the name for a series of apps available on Apple’s tablet computer that highlight different elements in the library’s collection. It was developed by the library and the design firm Potion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Public Library Launches iPad App', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGonigal, Jane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ca6bc6-dfe0-550e-aac5-2f90fcf935be', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ca6bc6-dfe0-550e-aac5-2f90fcf935be'}, {'abstract': 