Bank report sees China and five emerging economies as the leading engines of growth, and the dollar sharing primacy with the European and Chinese currencies.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/the-world-economic-order-circa-2025/', 'snippet': 'A World Bank report sees China and five emerging economies as the leading engines of growth, and the dollar sharing primacy with the European and Chinese currencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With China overtaking Japan as the world’s second-largest economy last year, there can be no doubt that emerging markets are becoming increasingly powerful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The World Economic Order, Circa 2025', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cea166b4-53d9-5587-a385-3c3feede056b', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cea166b4-53d9-5587-a385-3c3feede056b'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: As Dominique Strauss-Kahn appeared before a judge in Criminal Court in Manhattan, the trial of Offi