te symbol of power, the inner sanctum from which authority emanated across a vast land.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/world/BEIJING/BEIJING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/world/BEIJING/BEIJING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/world/BEIJING/BEIJING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Call for Revolution? Probably a Typo', 'kicker': 'Beijing Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Call for Revolution? Probably a Typo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rui Chenggang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a619d4e-d90a-58a0-9b68-d89600825622', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a619d4e-d90a-58a0-9b68-d89600825622'}, {'abstract': 'The best credit cards for travelers, comparing weight-loss plans and other consumer news from Tuesday’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/tuesday-reading-taking-measure-of-weight-loss-plans/', 'snippet': 'The best credit cards for travelers, comparing weight-loss plans and other consumer news from Tuesday’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Taking Measure of Weight-Loss Plans', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cd2df5f-f127-511a-80fa-70fa38a055eb', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cd2df5f-f127-511a-80fa-70fa38a055eb'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan, same as he ever was.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/do-do-that-voodoo/', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan, same as he ever was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So Paul Ryan gave his big speech defending his plan — and demonstrated, in case you were wondering, that there’s no there there (and there never was).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Do That Voodoo', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e34587-a389-539e-b8fe-52e2ab5ef0de', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e34587-a389-539e-b8fe-52e2ab5ef0de'}, {'abstract': 'Memory holes don’t work like they used to.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/apparatchiks-2/', 'snippet': 'Memory holes don’t work like they used to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Mark Thoma, Brendan Nyhan catches the Tax Foundation trying to disappear some apparently accidental honesty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apparatchiks', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/aff8c42b-a1b0-5989-a7f5-31cabfe675ed', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aff8c42b-a1b0-5989-a7f5-31cabfe675ed'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Jacques Demy’s musical.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/critics-picks-video-the-umbrellas-of-cherbourg/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott looks back at Jacques Demy’s musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Critics’ Picks, A. O. Scott looks back at Jacques Demy‘s 1964 musical “The Umbrellas of Cherbourg.” The film stars Catherine Deneuve and Nino Castelnuovo as a couple in love who are separated by war. Mr. Scott calls it “one of the most romantic films ever made.” With every line of dialogue sung, the film plays more like an opera than a musical. “This is singing as conversation,” Mr. Scott says, “a way for the actors to express their emotions, simply, sincerely and with a minimum of artifice.” Yet the film itself uses the artifice of cinema to its advantage, with bright colors and an attractive cast. Have you seen “The Umbrellas of Cherbourg?” Please share your thoughts in the comments area below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics’ Picks Video: ‘The Umbrellas of Cherbourg’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/45649619-7cfe-5b3b-bf0d-c646764e317f', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45649619-7cfe-5b3b-bf0d-c646764e317f'}, {'abstract': 'The minister’s departure appeared to be another high-level defection from the increasingly isolated government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/africa/18libya.html', 'snippet': 'The minister’s departure appeared to be another high-level defection from the increasingly isolated government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — The oil minister of Libya fled to neighboring Tunisia over the weekend, the Tunisian Interior Ministry said Tuesday, in what appeared to be another high-level defection from the increasingly isolated government of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. Officials in Tripoli said the oil minister was on official business outside the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/world/LIBYA-1/LIBYA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libyan Oil Minister Said to Defect to Tunisia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defection Hinted in Libyan Oil Minister’s Trip to Tunisia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns and Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f249c1d-83c3-583c-b5c2-38e0706f7bd6', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f249c1d-83c3-583c-b5c2-38e0706f7bd6'}, {'abstract': 'Three years, and 3.11%.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/the-invisible-attack-intensifies/', 'snippet': 'Three years, and 3.11%.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those wily invisible bond vigilantes are at it again: as part of their cunning plan, they have driven the 10-year bond rate down to 3.11 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Invisible Attack Intensifies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T13:49:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugma