riple-crown/', 'snippet': 'Five years after Barbaro’s injury, the controversy about catastrophic breakdowns in thoroughbreds continues. Is it right to ask 3-year-old horses to run their hearts out before they are fully mature?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Deitz is a psychiatrist and psychoanalyst in Connecticut and New York. He teaches at the Beth Israel Medical Center. He learned to read the Daily Racing Form at Pimlico Race Course in Maryland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Horses Too Young for the Triple Crown?', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbaro (Race Horse)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T14:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Deitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ba08d84-e552-5d62-96d8-82d6c95b71a7', 'word_count': 1528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ba08d84-e552-5d62-96d8-82d6c95b71a7'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Feist, CNN’s longtime political director, becomes the network’s Washington bureau chief.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sam-feist-to-lead-cnn-washington-bureau/', 'snippet': 'Sam Feist, CNN’s longtime political director, becomes the network’s Washington bureau chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Feist, CNN’s longtime political director, is becoming the Washington bureau chief for the cable news network.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi