arger project, which is ongoing.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/a-conversation-with-photographer-ashley-gilbertson/', 'snippet': 'This week, Ashley Gilbertson won a National Magazine Award for his photo essay “A Shrine Down the Hall.” The photographs published in this magazine were a selection from a larger project, which is ongoing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Ashley Gilbertson won a National Magazine Award for his photo essay “The Shrine Down the Hall.” The photographs show the perfectly preserved bedrooms of young men and women killed in Iraq or Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Photographer Ashley Gilbertson', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T15:03:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/02b5de6a-f7cb-5adc-86ab-ab8db3429f60', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02b5de6a-f7cb-5adc-86ab-ab8db3429f60'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/morning-take-out-245/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Once-Tight Flock at Goldman, Now Scattered | When Goldman Sachs went public 12 years ago this month, an elite group of 221 executives controlled the strategy and shares of the investment bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T15:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ac3564-8ef9-57b0-8cdd-f3ac435a29b8', 'word_count': 2157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ac3564-8ef9-57b0-8cdd-f3ac435a29b8'}, {'abstract': 'The venerable saloon/salon/hotspot couldn’t survive the death of its former owner, Elaine Kaufman.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/elaines-is-closing/', 'snippet': 'The venerable saloon/salon/hotspot couldn’t survive the death of its former owner, Elaine Kaufman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'City Room reports that Elaine’s, the venerable Upper East Side literary saloon, will close on May 26. Elaine Kaufman, the proprietor whose name had been on the yellow marquee since 1963, died last year. Her longtime manager, Diane Becker, who inherited the restaurant, said that things weren’t the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elaine’s Is Closing', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T15:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c0559e9-96ae-5d07-8eb2-7546f415614e', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'n