, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82b47607-756d-5ea6-88c6-d690598ad9f7'}, {'abstract': 'If you live in shale-gas country, there’s a new tool for getting information on materials used in developing nearby wells.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/new-tool-and-tune-for-tracking-fracking/', 'snippet': 'If you live in shale-gas country, there’s a new tool for getting information on materials used in developing nearby wells.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:27 p.m. | Updated In the final session of an environmental-science communication course that I co-taught at Pace University this spring, Thad Cook, a graduate student, gave a thorough overview of the issues raised by extracting natural gas from shale using hydraulic fracturing, the method now widely called fracking. He mentioned a useful new source of information, FracFocus.org.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Tool, and Tune, for Tracking Fracking', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T16:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizatio