ion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bc5f1fb-871b-5ad5-95c0-c732edead094', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bc5f1fb-871b-5ad5-95c0-c732edead094'}, {'abstract': 'The Collegium Vocale Gent will forgo a visit to China.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/citing-safety-concerns-vocal-group-cancels-visit-to-japan/', 'snippet': 'The Collegium Vocale Gent will forgo a visit to China.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Not all musical groups are following the Metropolitan Opera’s lead in forging ahead with tours to post-earthquake Japan. The Collegium Vocale Gent, a highly regarded ensemble that helped open the newly renovated Alice Tully Hall two years ago, has canceled a June tour that was to have included three performances in and near Tokyo because of concerns over nuclear safety brought on by the March quake and tsunami that crippled a nuclear power plant, resulting in releases of radiation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citing Safety Concerns, Vocal Group Cancels Visit to Japan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Johann Sebastian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'COLLEGIUM VOCALE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T16:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/035a2a57-b66d-5d7c-b84a-fe02dbc25fb6', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/035a2a57-b66d-5d7c-b84a-fe02dbc25fb6'}, {'abstract': 'Animal Kingdom galloped by us the first time at Fair Hill and looked good. He galloped by us the second time and he looked fantastic.  He was striding out nicely, and moving right along.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/animal-kingdom-gallops-at-fair-hill/', 'snippet': 'Animal Kingdom galloped by us the first time at Fair Hill and looked good. He galloped by us the second time and he looked fantastic.  He was striding out nicely, and moving right along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a damp morning on Tuesday at Fair Hill. A lot of rain had fallen through the night, but we were fortunate that the rain had eased off a little for training hours. Animal Kingdom was scheduled to train at his usual time, 9 a.m., on the Tapeta track. More news media were in attendance, but the weather had scared off any fans who might have considered coming out to see the Kentucky Derby winner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Animal Kingdom Gallops at Fair Hill', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T16:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ec7dd98-9057-5e35-b214-7fdd4b23b755', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ec7dd98-9057-5e35-b214-7fdd4b23b755'}, {'abstract': 'ESPN executives see a strong advertising market as they present their plans for the 2011-12 fall television season.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/upfronts-espn-shows-its-upfront-game-face/', 'snippet': 'ESPN executives see a strong advertising market as they present their plans for the 2011-12 fall television season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As one of the first cable channels to insinuate its way into the annual skein of presentations by broadcast networks known as upfront week, ESPN has always seemed determined to prove it belonged in their company by offering advertisers a busy series of announcements. And the ESPN upfront presentation for 2011-12, held on Tuesday morning in Times Square, was no exception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upfronts: ESPN Shows Its (Upfront) Game Face', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T16:37:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c5bceb-b85b-530e-834f-419d2f0e431c', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c5bceb-b85b-530e-834f-419d2f0e431c'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Stringer, Sony’s chief executive, argued that Sony had responded to the attack in a timely manner and  regularly shared information with customers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/sony-chief-defends-response-to-playstation-data-breach/', 'snippet': 'Howard Stringer, Sony’s chief executive, argued that Sony had responded to the attack in a timely manner and  regularly shared information with customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend Sony finally brought its PlayStation Network back online after attackers forced it to shut down for almost a month. Now the company’s top managers are defending their response to the attack, which some say was too slow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Chief Defends Response to PlayStation Data Breach', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T16:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c83f4c1f-6b70-5fb5-b560-dec5f8656251', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c83f4c1f-6b70-5fb5-b560-dec5f8656251'}, {'abstract': 'In the Schools: A mural in a Brooklyn school has become a recurring part of the academic year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/classes-come-and-go-but-the-mural-grows-and-grows/', 'snippet': 'In the Schools: A mural in a Brooklyn school has become a recurring part of the academic year.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Classes Come and Go, but the Mural Grows and Grows', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'ran