, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb5654f7-4a87-5043-bfb7-767a699a30cc', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb5654f7-4a87-5043-bfb7-767a699a30cc'}, {'abstract': 'For the better part of the past decade, and particularly in the past few months, the dollar has been the weakling of the foreign exchange world. That may be starting to change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/business/global/18dollar.html', 'snippet': 'For the better part of the past decade, and particularly in the past few months, the dollar has been the weakling of the foreign exchange world. That may be starting to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Could the long dollar slide be over?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/business/DOLLAR/DOLLAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/business/DOLLAR/DOLLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/business/DOLLAR/DOLLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some See Rise Ahead for Dollar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some See Rise Ahead For Dollar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff59a146-c1d5-50fc-a323-a5ee0aac3bcf', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff59a146-c1d5-50fc-a323-a5ee0aac3bcf'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone warned me. Managers and owners of other restaurants told me about the impossibility of hiring a staff in the off season. Even my wife warned me.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/the-hardest-part-of-running-a-restaurant/', 'snippet': 'Everyone warned me. Managers and owners of other restaurants told me about the impossibility of hiring a staff in the off season. Even my wife warned me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael thanked me for offering him a dream job. A fisherman since childhood, a painter of fish by day and a server at night, he had been waiting for a sustainable seafood place in which to work. He was well-spoken and mannerly, a good listener. We talked for an hour, going over his experience, his ambitions, how he stretched his canvases. He wanted to start work immediately. We agreed he would start the next day, at noon, train and taste and get familiar with our steps of service. That was a month ago. We have not heard from Rafael since. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hardest Part of Running a Restaurant', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waiters and Waitresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Buschel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buschel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/51ec0870-231b-5a6a-be5b-c1fe18b279c6', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51ec0870-231b-5a6a-be5b-c1fe18b279c6'}, {'abstract': 'More than 21 million people watch the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/dancing-with-the-stars-leaves-rivals-in-the-dust/', 'snippet': 'More than 21 million people watch the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A two-hour installment of semifinal performances on “Dancing With the Stars” topped the ratings on Monday night as 21.4 million viewers tuned in to the ABC reality show from 8 to 10 p.m., according to Nielsen’s estimates. No other network came close to matching ABC’s ratings, including during the 10 p.m. hour when ABC’s “Castle” (13.2 million) outperformed CBS’s “Hawaii Five-0” (9.8 million) and NBC’s “Law & Order: LA” (4.3 million). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dancing With the Stars’ Leaves Rivals in the Dust', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings and Rating Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Toff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e9194fb-eecd-5198-b3e6-ad977c651a02', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e9194fb-eecd-5198-b3e6-ad977c651a02'}, {'abstract': 'The Socialist Party is trying to reassure its troops after the arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/europe/18france.html', 'snippet': 'The Socialist Party is trying to reassure its troops after the arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — With its presumptive presidential candidate in a New York jail awaiting resolution of sexual assault charges, including attempted rape, the Socialist Party moved on Tuesday to try to reassure its troops, while President Nicolas Sarkozy was reported to have told his party’s legislators that the arrest of Dominique Strauss-Kahn was a disaster for the Socialists, who had lost “the moral part of the battle for the presidency.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/world/FRANCE-1/FRANCE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 