surfer Ryan Burch shapes from scratch a five-foot, two-inch asymmetrical board he calls the Sledgehammer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The California-based surfer and shaper Ryan Burch is fast gaining recognition for his iconoclastic D.I.Y. board designs and ability to ride almost any shape and size with spontaneity and grace. Here, Burch shapes from scratch a five-foot, two-inch asymmetrical board he calls the Sledgehammer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Land to Sea | Ryan Burch Video', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/76cdd4ec-f482-5f0a-b5a7-96f4df391a89', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76cdd4ec-f482-5f0a-b5a7-96f4df391a89'}, {'abstract': 'D.I.Y. surfboards are on the rise. Here, a list of some of the California-based gear guys who are leading the way.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/gear-gurus/', 'snippet': 'D.I.Y. surfboards are on the rise. Here, a list of some of the California-based gear guys who are leading the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the late ’80s through the early 2000s, much of surf culture was marked by homogeneity. The gear companies became behemoths, and the most popular boards (many shaped by computers) looked largely the same. In recent years, though, surfing’s zeitgeist has begun to celebrate individuality — a shift back to the homespun ethos of the sport’s early days. A surfer now is more likely to be riding a board he made himself, often a radically new shape. Even high-ranked pros are working collaboratively with their preferred shaper to come up with original, untested designs. Here, from left to right, some of the California-based gear guys who are leading the way.Mitch Abshere The owner of the Captain Fin Company produces surfboard fins and wet suits from Japanese rubber, which is especially soft, allowing for more agility (captainfincompany.com).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gear Gurus', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:34:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/383fcbfc-02cc-5778-aacf-5d8505f8d9b9', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/383fcbfc-02cc-5778-aacf-5d8505f8d9b9'}, {'abstract': 'Iran said Tuesday it was pursuing the case of a missing Al Jazeera reporter, saying she had committed “several offenses,” including traveling without a valid passport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/middleeast/18journalist.html', 'snippet': 'Iran said Tuesday it was pursuing the case of a missing Al Jazeera reporter, saying she had committed “several offenses,” including traveling without a valid passport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran said Tuesday that it was pursuing information about a missing Al Jazeera reporter sent to Tehran by the Syrian government in early May, saying she had committed “several offenses,” including traveling without a valid passport.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Says Missing Al Jazeera Reporter Committed Offenses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Says Missing Al Jazeera Reporter Committed Offenses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parvaz, Dorothy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2b1bd40-820f-5da5-9e3f-83e77babc76a', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2b1bd40-820f-5da5-9e3f-83e77babc76a'}, {'abstract': 'The Egyptian military could bring charges against 136 people arrested during a protest outside the Israeli Embassy in Cairo on Sunday, including two prominent bloggers.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/egypt-holds-136-for-israeli-embassy-protest/', 'snippet': 'The Egyptian military could bring charges against 136 people arrested during a protest outside the Israeli Embassy in Cairo on Sunday, including two prominent bloggers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Egyptian military could bring charges against 136 people arrested during a protest outside the Israeli Embassy in Cairo on Sunday, including two prominent bloggers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Holds 136 for Israeli Embassy Protest', 'kic