still-dead/', 'snippet': 'Home construction is at a new low, and for good reasons. But wouldn’t it be nice to put all those unemployed people to work building something we need?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may not be anything to be done about the sad state of the home-building industry. They built too many homes before; now they are building very few. But the numbers released on Tuesday are still a stark reminder of the weakness of a large section of the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Housing Starts: Still Dead', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing Starts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b479ae4-3bb4-5cb5-8659-e56579aea317', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b479ae4-3bb4-5cb5-8659-e56579aea317'}, {'abstract': 'Home construction is at a new low, and for good reasons. But wouldn’t it be nice to put all those unemployed people to work building something we need?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/housing-starts-still-dead/', 'snippet': 'Home construction is at a new low, and for good reasons. But wouldn’t it be nice to put all those unemployed people to work building something we need?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may not be anything to be done about the sad state of the home-building industry. They built too many homes before; now they are building very few. But the numbers released on Tuesday are still a stark reminder of the weakness of a large section of the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Housing Starts: Still Dead', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing Starts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T18:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814aba06-c8f1-518c-946a-89fd0017ef7f', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814aba06-c8f1-518c-946a-89fd0017ef7f'}, {'abstract': 'The shooting came after an armed suspect confronted members of the Emergency Service Unit who had been summoned by uniformed colleagues, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/police-kill-man-in-confrontation-on-staten-island/', 'snippet': 'The shooting came after an armed suspect confronted members of the Emergency Service Unit who had been summoned by uniformed colleagues, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 7:28 p.m. |  A man who shot and killed a business associate and wounded the victim’s wife in their home on Staten Island on Tuesday was fatally shot by the police after he pointed a gun at responding officers and refused orders to drop his weapon, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police K