by-woody-allen-elaine-may-ethan-coen-heading-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Allen described his play, “Honeymoon Motel,” as “a broad comedy, for laughs, no redeeming social value.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six months ago Woody Allen heard from the theater producer Julian Schlossberg that he was thinking of staging a new one-act play by Elaine May. Did Mr. Allen have anything in the drawer?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Triple Bill by Woody Allen, Elaine May, Ethan Coen Heading to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa3fd463-b7ed-583f-b19e-86d7967e5ceb', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa3fd463-b7ed-583f-b19e-86d7967e5ceb'}, {'abstract': 'Cooked in wine, leeks develop a rich, tangy flavor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/health/nutrition/20recipehealth.html', 'snippet': 'Cooked in wine, leeks develop a rich, tangy flavor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you cook leeks in wine, they develop great depth of flavor. This is my favorite way to prepare leeks on their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/science/20recipehealth/20recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/s