tion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34f8a53-bb86-5cae-8a9f-89e6f3bac011', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34f8a53-bb86-5cae-8a9f-89e6f3bac011'}, {'abstract': 'In his forthcoming autobiography, Sugar Ray Leonard says he was sexually abused by “a prominent Olympic boxing coach” as a young boxer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/sports/in-book-sugar-ray-leonard-says-coach-sexually-abused-him.html', 'snippet': 'In his forthcoming autobiography, Sugar Ray Leonard says he was sexually abused by “a prominent Olympic boxing coach” as a young boxer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening segment of a forthcoming autobiography by Sugar Ray Leonard runs counter to the cunning style he used in winning boxing championships in five weight divisions more than a quarter-century ago. It is more like hearing the bell, rushing to the center of the ring and being hit with a straight right hand.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/sports/LEONARD1/LEONARD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/sports/LEONARD1/LEONARD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/sports/LEONARD1/LEONARD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/sports/LEONARD1/LEONARD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/sports/LEONARD1/LEONARD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Book, Sugar Ray Leonard Says Coach Sexually Abused Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Baring His Secret Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonard, Sugar Ray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/560c4a2f-0285-5949-87ab-fcd0a523e759', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/560c4a2f-0285-5949-87ab-fcd0a523e759'}, {'abstract': 'The open-air food court in Williamsburg will be open on Saturdays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/dining/the-vendors-a-list-of-the-smorgasburg-participants.html', 'snippet': 'The open-air food court in Williamsburg will be open on Saturdays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are descriptions from Eric Demby, the organizer of Smorgasburg, of vendors that will be at this new open-air food court in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Most are new, but some have been at Brooklyn Flea before. Smorgasburg will be open on Saturdays from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m., at 27 North Sixth Street, between Kent Avenue and the East River (near East River State Park).',