': 'Model T Embarks on Historic Climb in Scotland', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c85a5532-b4cc-5333-b541-01353a7c8687', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c85a5532-b4cc-5333-b541-01353a7c8687'}, {'abstract': 'Researching historical eras in which major events happened with respect to the Mississippi River and reflecting on the larger meaning of those events and of the river itself in American culture and identity.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/body-of-a-nation-examining-the-role-of-the-mississippi-river-in-american-history/', 'snippet': 'Researching historical eras in which major events happened with respect to the Mississippi River and reflecting on the larger meaning of those events and of the river itself in American culture and identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What roles has the Mississippi River played throughout United States history? How has the river been central to struggles to define “America” and “American”? In this lesson, students examine what life was like on the banks of the Mississippi River during pivotal moments in American history. They will then write diary entries from the perspective of riverbank residents during different historical eras. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Body of a Nation: Examining the Role of the Mississippi River in American History', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kavanagh, Holly Epstein Ojalvo and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f121d262-5070-5b50-90b6-cfeaa3500e38', 'word_count': 1618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f121d262-5070-5b50-90b6-cfeaa3500e38'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Beaty’s musical “Tearing Down the Walls” waxes nostaligic for Harlem and a Cro-Magnon view of the female of the species.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/theater/reviews/tearing-down-the-walls-by-daniel-beaty-review.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Beaty’s musical “Tearing Down the Walls” waxes nostaligic for Harlem and a Cro-Magnon view of the female of the species.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Beaty has shown promise as a theatrical form-bender with works like “Emergence-See!,” a one-man show in which he played about 40 characters. But he takes a step backward into the land of shopworn plots and easy button pushing with “Tearing Down the Walls,” his new, overly long musical at the Riverside Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/tear/tear-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/tear/tear-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/tear/tear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/tear/tear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/tear/tear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Men Are From Mars, It Appears That Some Women Can Be, Too', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Tearing Down the Walls'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Men Are From Mars, It Appears That Some Women Can Be, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaty, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5a75ebb-3dfa-58cf-b094-eff381ac2309', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5a75ebb-3dfa-58cf-b094-eff381ac2309'}, {'abstract': 'The Chicago Bulls’ reserves don’t show well in the “bench points” statistic, but they’re among the most successful bench collectives in entire league.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/impact-of-chicagos-reserves-transcends-scoring/', 'snippet': 'The Chicago Bulls’ reserves don’t show well in the “bench points” statistic, but they’re among the most successful bench collectives in entire league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bench success in the N.B.A. is typically measured in terms of the lowest possible denominator; the Sixth Man of the Year award typically honors the highest scoring reserve (this season’s winner, Lamar Odom, provides a rare exception), and the oft-used bench points measure inherently trumpets scoring above all else. It is telling that bench rebounds and bench assists” are nonexistent as a talking point, as reserves seem to warrant public praise only when they score sufficiently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Impact of Bulls’ Reserves Transcends Scoring', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bogans, Keith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng, Luol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Derrick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T19:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id'