Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/87d7aba7-a1f0-5b28-a18f-7aa1c840b832', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87d7aba7-a1f0-5b28-a18f-7aa1c840b832'}, {'abstract': 'Condé Nast is to lease one million square feet in the lead tower at ground zero in a deal worth an estimated $2 billion over 25 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/nyregion/conde-nast-to-anchor-1-world-trade-center.html', 'snippet': 'Condé Nast is to lease one million square feet in the lead tower at ground zero in a deal worth an estimated $2 billion over 25 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Condé Nast Publications, whose stable of magazines chronicles the American zeitgeist as meticulously as any anthropologist, has reached an agreement to lease one million square feet at 1 World Trade Center, giving ground zero a much-needed corporate anchor with a proven ability to attract other businesses. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/nyregion/WTC/WTC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/nyregion/WTC/WTC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/nyregion/WTC/WTC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Condé Nast Will Be Anchor of 1 World Trade Center', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stylish Anchor for 1 World Trade Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom Tower (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Office Buildings and Commercial Properties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05d737c8-4c6e-5f3c-8833-171f40f9c355', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05d737c8-4c6e-5f3c-8833-171f40f9c355'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Scooter Club held its annual night run from the Meatpacking District to Times Square on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/scooter-enthusiasts-descend-on-times-square/', 'snippet': 'The New York Scooter Club held its annual night run from the Meatpacking District to Times Square on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Scooter Club held its sixth annual Block Party last weekend, and despite various barbecues and concerts packing the calendar, the unofficial highlight for the club is a nighttime cruise through Times Square.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scooter Enthusiasts Descend on Times Square', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Kurczewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurczewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5c23f1a-483d-58e7-ac5b-d8f279d4199c', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5c23f1a-483d-58e7-ac5b-d8f279d4199c'}, {'abstract': 'For my trip around the Mediterranean, I’m asking readers to plan a fun-filled, smartly-themed, low-budget five-day trip to somewhere on the Italian coast.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/plan-a-week-in-italy-for-the-frugal-traveler-the-rules/', 'snippet': 'For my trip around the Mediterranean, I’m asking readers to plan a fun-filled, smartly-themed, low-budget five-day trip to somewhere on the Italian coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For my trip around the Mediterranean, I’m asking readers to plan a fun-filled, smartly-themed, low-budget five-day trip to somewhere on the Italian coast. It’s up to you to come up with a destination and associated theme. A multiday hike through gorgeous countryside and small towns? A lesser-known side of a much-visited tourist destination? Sampling the seafood specialties along a string of coastal villages? Anything goes, as long as you can get me there from Naples (where I’ll be the week before) and keep the budget light.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan a Week in Italy for the Frugal Traveler: The Rules', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e792eb3-51bd-5862-827c-6e9099935ff7', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e792eb3-51bd-5862-827c-6e9099935ff7'}, {'abstract': 'Thursday’s the beginning of what sounds like a foolhardy adventure: high season in the Mediterranean on a budget.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/the-mediterranean-on-a-budget-the-voyage-begins/', 'snippet': 'Thursday’s the beginning of what sounds like a foolhardy adventure: high season in the Mediterranean on a budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, I head to Spain to begin what sounds like a foolhardy adventure: high season in the Mediterranean on a budget. For 10 weeks, I’ll be just one soul among the gobs of tourists descending on its azure waters from around the world. Why would someone with a schedule as flexible and a wallet as light as mine want to fight the hordes of Italian and British and Norwegian and Chinese and Pennsylvanian vacationers and their affiliated bathing suit styles?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mediterranean on a Budget: The Voyage Begins', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfa099a7-97f9-5a40-840c-23515ecd254b', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfa099a7-97f9-5a40-840c-23515ecd254b'}, {'abstract': 'Lisa Edelstein, who has played Dr. Lisa Cuddy for seven years on the Fox drama “House,” announced on Tuesday that she will not return to wrap up the popular series.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/a-final-season-of-house-but-without-dr-cuddy/', 'snippet': 'Lisa Edelstein, who has played Dr. Lisa Cuddy for seven years on the Fox drama “House,” announced on Tuesday that she will not return to wrap up the popular series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whatever final-season plans the creators of the Fox drama “House” may have had for sending the curmudgeonly and lovelorn title character off into the sunset with his boss, Dr. Lisa Cuddy, were dashed Tuesday when the actress Lisa Edelstein announced she would not return to wrap up the popular series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Final Season of ‘House,’ but Without Dr. Cuddy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edelstein, Lisa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:46:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7650ce7e-83ab-5402-a991-2eddcb68552c', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7650ce7e-83ab-5402-a991-2eddcb68552c'}, {'abstract': 'Museums overseen by the Regents are barred from selling artworks to raise money for operating expenses.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/new-york-board-of-regents-approves-restrictions-on-museum-sales/', 'snippet': 'Museums overseen by the Regents are barred from selling artworks to raise money for operating expenses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Board of Regents on Tuesday made permanent a set of emergency regulations regarding the deaccessioning of artworks. In September the Regents approved the expiration of the regulations, which enjoined museums from selling artworks for operating costs and had been in effect since 2008. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Board of Regents Approves Restrictions on Museum Sales', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brodsky, Richard L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Regents (NYS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T20:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/14155869-6724-5f5a-b488-f6ab768147c1', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14155869-6724-5f5a-b488-f6ab768147c1'}, {'abstract': 'The three myths that have for too long propped up climate diplomacy.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/exploring-roots-of-climate-stasis-and-next-steps/', 'snippet': 'The three myths that have for too long propped up climate diplomacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Roberts, the Grist blogger, has written a double-barreled book review for the American Prospect that’s well worth reading. It explores “The Climate War,” Eric Pooley’s deconstruction of the long, and ultimately failed, effort to pass a comprehensive climate bill in the United States. But Roberts focuses most on David Victor‘s new book “Global Warming Gridlock,” which I’m way overdue to read. Victor, from the University of California, San Diego, has been a frequent and welcome voice on Dot Earth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Roots of Climate Stasis, and Next Steps', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pooley, Eric', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T21:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e3f5ead-4a9d-589d-9bbf-ba82654e755a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e3f5ead-4a9d-589d-9bbf-ba82654e755a'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Communications Commission and the Federal Trade Commission will conduct a “public education forum” about location-based mobile services next month.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/u-s-agencies-plan-a-public-forum-on-location-services/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Communications Commission and the Federal Trade Commission will conduct a “public education forum” about location-based mobile services next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Location-based services, the mobile-phone applications that make use of a person’s geographic location, are attracting growing attention in Washington following reports that phone and software companies might have been sharing location information with third parties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Agencies Plan a Public Forum on Location Services', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T21:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e711756-9aac-505d-9699-6c49b60be672', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e711756-9aac-505d-9699-6c49b60be672'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor, one of the biggest contributor to State Senate Republicans, said he would offer campaign support to any Republican who backed a bill to allow gay couples to marry.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/bloomberg-visits-albany-to-lobby-for-same-sex-marriage/', 'snippet': 'The mayor, one of the biggest contributor to State Senate Republicans, said he would offer campaign support to any Republican who backed a bill to allow gay couples to marry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — Calling same-sex marriage the single most important issue facing New York State, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg on Tuesday visited the Capitol and pledged to support the campaign of any Republican senator who votes in favor of allowing gay couples to wed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Visits Albany to Lobby for Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T21:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e1d05bc-ce81-5bc8-8b40-3d96dc3025ac', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e1d05bc-ce81-5bc8-8b40-3d96dc3025ac'}, {'abstract': 'Tavarua, the small, heart-shaped island in the Fijian archipelago, has two of the world’s most sought-after waves.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/fiji-for-all/', 'snippet': 'Tavarua, the small, heart-shaped island in the Fijian archipelago, has two of the world’s most sought-after waves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tavarua, the small, heart-shaped island in the Fijian archipelago, has two of the world’s most sought-after waves, Cloudbreak and Restaurants. Since 1984, access to them had been controlled by the Tavarua Island Resort (tavarua.com). But last year, Fiji’s military dictatorship put an end to the hotel’s exclusive rights, to the delight of local Fijians and international surfers, who have begun boating to the breaks from neighboring islands. Look for other resorts to spring up nearby and take advantage of the new access.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiji for All', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T21:02:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/865979ca-a218-5b9a-8683-049a5048c798', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/865979ca-a218-5b9a-8683-049a5048c798'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln Center Theater on Tuesday started a program to provide $30 seats to its performances for people ages 21 to 35.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/lincoln-center-theater-entices-a-younger-crowd/', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Center Theater on Tuesday started a program to provide $30 seats to its performances for people ages 21 to 35.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Center Theater on Tuesday started a program to provide $30 seats to its performances for people ages 21 to 35, theater officials announced. The program, called LincTix, allows members to buy tickets for productions at the Vivian Beaumont and Mitzi E. Newhouse Theaters at Lincoln Center, as well as to Lincoln Center Theater productions on Broadway. A limited number of LincTix will be available for every performance and available in advance. Once registered online, LincTix members (memberships are available at LincTix.org) can buy tickets for coming productions and to “War Horse,” now at the Vivian Beaumont Theater (regular tickets cost $75 to $125), and to “A Minister’s Wife,” now at the Mitzi E. Newhouse Theater (regular tickets are $85). LincTix members will also have a chance to purchase seats together with other LincTix members and will get invitations to free LincTix parties and other special events. Mem Membership includes advance notice of the $20 tickets for all LCT3 productions, which showcase the work of new playwrights, directors and designers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Center Theater  Entices a Younger Crowd', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T21:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf81548-7f20-5b9f-9b61-18beb9ae7f61', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf81548-7f20-5b9f-9b61-18beb9ae7f61'}, {'abstract': 'Okkervil River’s refreshing promotional video for its new album, “I Am Very Far.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/interesting-rock-talk-no-really/', 'snippet': 'Okkervil River’s refreshing promotional video for its new album, “I Am Very Far.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Promotional band videos — virtually without exception — are joy vacuums. No one wants to see 