ent a second letter to Sony asking the company to answer questions about a data breach.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/congress-asks-sony-to-address-unanswered-questions/', 'snippet': 'A House subcommittee sent a second letter to Sony asking the company to answer questions about a data breach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A House subcommittee sent a followup letter to Sony on Tuesday after the company failed to answer a number of questions regarding an attack on its PlayStation Network last month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Asks Sony to Address Unanswered Questions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3672d6d-51b4-5eb7-a595-7204ebe759b2', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3672d6d-51b4-5eb7-a595-7204ebe759b2'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview at Cannes, Dan Talbot, who created New Yorker Films in 1965, said he was optimistic about the art-film world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/movies/dan-talbot-at-the-cannes-film-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview at Cannes, Dan Talbot, who created New Yorker Films in 1965, said he was optimistic about the art-film world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CANNES, France — As he sat on his balcony overlooking the Mediterranean, Dan Talbot, the celebrated founder of New Yorker Films, could have lighted every screen here with his optimism. Up close, this town can sometimes look a little grubby, the business somewhat desperate, the movies too. But on the fifth floor of the Hotel Splendid on Tuesday, as he sat taking in the bright blues of the sky and sea, the rushing festivalgoers and languidly moving rest, and even said hello to a dove perched on a railing, life looked pretty grand and so did the 64th Cannes Film Festival. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/cannes-1/cannes-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/cannes-1/cannes-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/cannes-1/cannes-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/cannes-1/cannes-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/cannes-1/cannes-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Cannes, an Upbeat View of the Film World', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Cannes, an Upbeat View of the Film World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:26:54+0000', 'do