elissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artichokes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'David Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0b195ea1-19f3-561a-b9d4-ea69d11d9071', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0b195ea1-19f3-561a-b9d4-ea69d11d9071'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Louder Than a Bomb” follows four teams of teenagers as they prepare for a high school poetry slam in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/movies/teenage-poets-in-louder-than-a-bomb-review.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Louder Than a Bomb” follows four teams of teenagers as they prepare for a high school poetry slam in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gather a bunch of teenagers together in a room, and usually what you sense is an abundance of hormones. But in “Louder Than a Bomb,” a documentary about a high school poetry slam of that name in Chicago, it is earnestness that is thick in the air as these young writers convene and try to shape their emotions and observations into competition-worthy poetry.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/LOUD1/LOUD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/LOUD1/LOUD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/LOUD1/LOUD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/LOUD1/LOUD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/LOUD1/LOUD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stream of Words, Painting a Picture', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Louder Than a Bomb'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stream Of Words, Painting A Picture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a84a101-bbae-5126-8118-a24c1b3b7c69', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a84a101-bbae-5126-8118-a24c1b3b7c69'}, {'abstract': 'More than 600 fungi are described and illustrated in “The Book of Fungi,” a scholarly and beautiful book.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/dining/the-book-of-fungi-mushrooms-from-dazzling-to-deadly.html', 'snippet': 'More than 600 fungi are described and illustrated in “The Book of Fungi,” a scholarly and beautiful book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How dazzling is the world of mushrooms? The fan-shaped cinnabar oysterling looks like something you would find undersea. The violet webcap is vibrant. These are among the more than 600 fungi described and illustrated in this scholarly and beautiful book. It gives examples of cultivated mushrooms like shiitake, explains why porcini cannot be cultivated (no spores), has an interesting section on truffles and describes dozens of edible wild mushrooms. It also covers hundreds of mushrooms that are inedible or deadly poisonous.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18stuff-book/18stuff-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18stuff-book/18stuff-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18stuff-book/18stuff-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mushrooms, From Dazzling to Deadly', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Case You Think a Mushroom Can’t Dazzle You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fungi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mushrooms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62e727b5-057f-5ad5-9ddb-7f98d9613e54', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62e727b5-057f-5ad5-9ddb-7f98d9613e54'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities in Kazakhstan were trying to determine whether a man who blew himself up inside a government office building in a provincial town had links to Islamic radicals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/asia/18briefs-Kazakhstan.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities in Kazakhstan were trying to determine whether a man who blew himself up inside a government office building in a provincial town had links to Islamic radicals.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Authorities in Kazakhstan were trying to determine whether a man who blew himself up on Tuesday inside a government office building in a provincial town had links to Islamic radicals. If so, it would be the first known terrorist suicide bombing in oil-rich Kazakhastan. Governments in the region, including Russia, have expressed concern that violence from the Afghan war is spreading to formerly Soviet Central Asia. The attack wounded two bystanders at a local police headquarters in the city of Aktobe. Kazakh prosecutors said it appeared that the bomber had ties to organized crime but not to radical Islamic groups. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kazakhstan: Suicide Bomber Strikes', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kazakhstan: Suicide Bomber Strikes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kazakhstan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad34256d-1d09-5450-8826-25e943c23840', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad34256d-1d09-5450-8826-25e943c23840'}, {'abstract': 'Japan vowed Tuesday to stick to its goal of stabilizing the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant in as soon as six months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/asia/18tepco.html', 'snippet': 'Japan vowed Tuesday to stick to its goal of stabilizing the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant in as soon as six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan vowed Tuesday to stick to its goal of stabilizing a stricken nuclear power plant in as soon as six months, despite recently acknowledging that damage to the plant’s reactors might be worse than initially estimated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Reactor Damage Thought to Be Worse, Tokyo Utility Sticks to Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Reactor Damage Thought to Be Worse, Tokyo Utility Sticks to Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2648daab-227e-5e99-b9bd-80bda17cc60d', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2648daab-227e-5e99-b9bd-80bda17cc60d'}, {'abstract': 'The year has brought a rush of new recipe search engines designed to solve dining challenges. But will they evaluate the recipes the way a good cook would?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/dining/can-recipe-search-engines-make-you-a-better-cook.html', 'snippet': 'The year has brought a rush of new recipe search engines designed to solve dining challenges. But will they evaluate the recipes the way a good cook would?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LET’S say you have invited four people for dinner on Saturday. It’s now Wednesday morning, and reality is setting in. On the guest list: two pescatarians, a “Top Chef” fanboy and a gluten avoider. Also, spring is in the air; local asparagus, arriving now. The challenge, as always: how to find dishes that are reliable, delicious and gastronomically correct?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18search2/18search2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18search2/18search2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/dining/18search2/18search2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Recipe Search Engines Make You a Better Cook?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Too Many Search Engines Spoil The Chili', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T22:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a85b0d13-02d9-5ac0-985e-5b9edfb1d93f', 'word_count': 1744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a85b0d13-02d9-5ac0-985e-5b9edfb1d93f'}, {'abstract': 'Google provided The Times with a snapshot of the most popular searches in one week in late March.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/googles-most-wanted-recipes/', 'snippet': 'Google provided The Times with a snapshot of the most popular searches in one week in late March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julia Moskin’s article on recipe search engines discusses some the major players in that world, including the newest member of that group: Google’s Recipe View tool. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google’s Most Wanted Recipes', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T23:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Weinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/24f0c9a4-bac0-50a9-ba78-3f140d10ec33', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24f0c9a4-bac0-50a9-ba78-3f140d10ec33'}, {'abstract': 'Gretchen Morgenson discusses the investigation into three major Wall Street banks by the New York attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000000823478/timescast--wall-streets-new-enforcer.html', 'snippet': 'Gretchen Morgenson discusses the investigation into three major Wall Street banks by the New York attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gretchen Morgenson discusses the investigation into three major Wall Street banks by the New York attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/multimedia/video-tc-110517-morgenson/video-tc-110517-morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/17/multimedia/video-tc-110517-morgenson/video-tc-110517-morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/multimedia/video-tc-110517-morgenson/video-tc-110517-morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/17/multimedia/video-tc-110517-morgenson/video-tc-110517-mor