s to Medicare. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/us/COBURN/COBURN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/us/COBURN/COBURN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/us/COBURN/COBURN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Group on Debt Loses a Key Republican', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Group on Debt Loses a Key Republican', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coburn, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T23:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb04062b-738d-5533-bea2-46860b2ea395', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb04062b-738d-5533-bea2-46860b2ea395'}, {'abstract': 'Vents that American officials said would prevent devastating explosions at nuclear plants in the United States were put to the test in Japan and failed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/asia/18japan.html', 'snippet': 'Vents that American officials said would prevent devastating explosions at nuclear plants in the United States were put to the test in Japan and failed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Emergency vents that American officials have said would prevent devastating hydrogen explosions at nuclear plants in the United States were put to the test in Japan — and failed to work, according to experts and officials with the company that operates the crippled Fukushima Daiichi plant.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Japan Reactor Failings, Danger Signs for the U.S.', 'kicker': 'Hidden Dangers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Japan Reactor Failings, Danger Signs for the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydrogen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T23:35:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi, Keith Bradsher and Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84084bb8-2f52-5025-9f2a-5e69b5f86124', 'word_count': 1579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84084bb8-2f52-5025-9f2a-5e69b5f86124'}, {'abstract': 'If you’d like to use your iPad as a cookbook, there are ways to keep it clean and dry while cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/how-to-protect-the-ipad-in-the-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'If you’d like to use your iPad as a cookbook, there are ways to keep it clean and dry while cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tablet computer, with those wonderful apps that display recipes and color pictures, is one of the best new kitchen tools. But if you cook like Julia Child did — splashing the bouillabaisse and tossing the flour all over the counter— there is no way you’d bring it into the kitchen. An iPad, after all, doesn’t rinse off like a cutting board. Moisture is its chief enemy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Protect the iPad in the Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kitchens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-17T23:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Darlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb6e2580-388c-53e1-8d05-8b19642ef1f0', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb6e2580-388c-53e1-8d05-8b19642ef1f0'}, {'a