earlier this year. He said the university wanted to “underscore the fundamental unfairness of our denying a path to citizenship to some of the most motivated college students in the country.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Honor for Immigrant Activist', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Honor for Immigrant Activist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of San Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Development, Relief, and Education for Alien Minors Act', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T00:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aab95d3-da99-564e-b3f4-b3557cf9a8bb', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aab95d3-da99-564e-b3f4-b3557cf9a8bb'}, {'abstract': 'The emergency vent system designed to help prevent hydrogen explosions failed to work in at least two of the three reactors in operation. Venting would have reduced the amount of hydrogen gas that accumulated in the buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/17/world/asia/venting-failure-in-the-nuclear-reactors-at-fukushima-daiichi.html', 'snippet': 'The emergency vent system designed to help prevent hydrogen explosions failed to work in at least two of the three reactors in operation. Venting would have reduced the amount of hydrogen gas that accumulated in the buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The emergency vent system designed to help prevent hydrogen explosions failed to work in at least two of the three reactors in operation. Venting would have reduced the amount of hydrogen gas that accumulated in the buildings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venting Failure in the Nuclear Reactors at Fukushima Daiichi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T00:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a6dd3ae9-a104-5e5f-af83-c1de62ec8a5d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a6dd3ae9-a104-5e5f-af83-c1de62ec8a5d'}, {'abstract': 'The Palestinian Authority said Tuesday that it was delaying local elections scheduled for July until late October in order to organize the voting in Gaza, which is controlled by Hamas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/world/middleeast/18briefs-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'The Palestinian Authority said Tuesday that it was delaying local elections scheduled for July until late October in order to organize the voting in Gaza, which is controlled by Hamas.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Palestinian Authority said Tuesday that it was delaying local elections scheduled for July until late October in order to organize the voting in Gaza, which is controlled by Hamas. Last month, Hamas and its rival, Fatah, which dominates the Palestinian Authority, announced a surprise unity agreement. Palestinians have not held an election in five years because of a bitter split between the groups. The October poll will indicate how each party is faring as it prepares for legislative and presidential elections within a year, as called for in the unity accord. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Authority Delays Elections', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinian Authority Delays Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fatah, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T00:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f9ba45-9899-5b38-936a-a71aa024ce57', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f9ba45-9899-5b38-936a-a71aa024ce57'}, {'abstract': 'The soldier faces multiple charges in what the Army has described as the sport killings of three Afghan civilians last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/us/18soldier.html', 'snippet': 'The soldier faces multiple charges in what the Army has described as the sport killings of three Afghan civilians last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — A sixth soldier was charged Tuesday in connection with what Army prosecutors have described as the sport killings of three Afghan civilians last year, officials at Joint Base Lewis-McChord near here said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source':