an', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a454c87-8836-5fe7-b281-2166b07ab445', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a454c87-8836-5fe7-b281-2166b07ab445'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Stelter discusses Fox’s announcement that “America’s Most Wanted,” a mainstay on the network for 23 years, will no longer be a weekly show.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/americas-most-wanted-unwanted-by-fox/', 'snippet': 'Brian Stelter discusses Fox’s announcement that “America’s Most Wanted,” a mainstay on the network for 23 years, will no longer be a weekly show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Stelter discusses Fox’s announcement that “America’s Most Wanted,” a mainstay on the network for 23 years, will no longer be a weekly show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: ‘America’s Most Wanted’ Unwanted by Fox', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T00:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f98ef912-b70b-5c0e-8939-d60f7f7181f2', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f98ef912-b70b-5c0e-8939-d60f7f7181f2'}, {'abstract': 'Tracing the roots of Lincoln’s problems with the military to the Mexican War.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/a-legacy-of-insubordination/', 'snippet': 'Tracing the roots of Lincoln’s problems with the military to the Mexican War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he took office, Abraham Lincoln faced the greatest strategic challenge of any American president before or since: that of holding the country together as political and moral tensions that had risen steadily over the course of nearly 100 years strained mightily to tear it apart. But he also confronted a standard of civil-military relations that internalized domestic political intrigue and countenanced soldierly insubordination. Epitomized by Gen. George B. McClellan, this organizational problem was a crippling impediment for Lincoln early in the Civil War that required all of his political and psychological acumen to overcome. It was substantially a product of the Mexican War of 1846-48. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Legacy of Insubordination', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican-American War (1846-48)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClellan, George B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polk, James Knox', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T01:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cda95ed-85d9-5b93-82e0-6f23487430d8', 'word_count': 1529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cda95ed-85d9-5b93-82e0-6f23487430d8'}, {'abstract': 'The nature of any potential physical problem with the Yankees’ slugger was unclear, though it is possible that his surgically repaired right hip could be a factor.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/day-after-contentious-remarks-soriano-heads-to-disabled-list/', 'snippet': 'The nature of any potential physical problem with the Yankees’ slugger was unclear, though it is possible that his surgically repaired right hip could be a factor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees put reliever Rafael Soriano on the disabled list Tuesday, but, befitting their fortunes recently, they also dealt with a matter unrelated to his ailing right elbow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day After Contentious Remarks, Soriano Heads to Disabled List', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T01:03:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed25fc0b-1562-57c5-a4c3-57701674a4f7', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed25fc0b-1562-57c5-a4c3-57701674a4f7'}, {'abstract': 'The agent, an indictment says, lied to have a woman designated an informer, lied to help her in a criminal case and had a relationship with her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/nyregion/fbi-agent-charged-with-making-false-statements.html', 'snippet': 'The agent, an indictment says, lied to have a woman designated an informer, lied to help her in a criminal case and had a relationship with her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An agent with the Federal Bureau of Investigation got too close to a confidential informer in a criminal investigation and is now in trouble with the law, an indictment made clear on Tue