icle/28d63cd3-a354-5931-bf27-1f77bfded45a'}, {'abstract': 'A video takes a look at some of the Spanish-language shows pitched to advertisers at upfront week. Executives also discuss the goals and spirit of their programs.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/17/video-from-the-upfronts-spanish-language-programming-on-the-rise/', 'snippet': 'A video takes a look at some of the Spanish-language shows pitched to advertisers at upfront week. Executives also discuss the goals and spirit of their programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Stuart Elliott and Tanzina Vega reported, the continuing growth of the Spanish-speaking population shown by the 2010 census is not going unnoticed by media and marketers. This year’s upfront week features presentations from as many Spanish-language programmers as there are from English-language broadcasters. This video takes a look at some of the shows pitched to advertisers. Executives also discuss the goals and spirit of their programs. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video From the Upfronts: Spanish-Language Programming on the Rise', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T03:47:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3a0ee73-d5fe-509f-bb35-3716878880e4', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3a0ee73-d5fe-509f-bb35-3716878880e4'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate blocked a Democratic proposal to strip the five leading oil companies of tax breaks that backers of the measure said were unfairly padding industry profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/us/politics/18congress.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate blocked a Democratic proposal to strip the five leading oil companies of tax breaks that backers of the measure said were unfairly padding industry profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate on Tuesday blocked a Democratic proposal to strip the five leading oil companies of tax breaks that backers of the measure said were unfairly padding industry profits while consumers were struggling with high gas prices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/us/CONGRESS/CONGRESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Refuses to End Tax Breaks for Big Oil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Refuses to End Tax Breaks for Big Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ConocoPhillips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T03:55:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538e8e52-9981-5dae-b134-1e3d6eec2a4f', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538e8e52-9981-5dae-b134-1e3d6eec2a4f'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker is experimenting with diagnostic health apps, which would operate on its Sync entertainment and information system.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/diabetic-ford-may-have-an-app-for-that/', 'snippet': 'The automaker is experimenting with diagnostic health apps, which would operate on its Sync entertainment and information system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While driving recently along the Ventura Freeway in Los Angeles, I watched a driver drift across traffic and settle at the shoulder of the road. Other drivers pulled over, exited their vehicles and began slapping the car’s windows in an effort to arouse the motorist, who was slumped over the wheel. I do not know the driver’s fate, as I was traveling in the leftmost lane.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diabetic? Ford May Have an App for That', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T04:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric A. Taub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Taub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/218c2deb-e279-5e58-9157-92d2f02c3bd6', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/218c2deb-e279-5e58-9157-92d2f02c3bd6'}, {'abstract': 'Two economists from The Hamilton Project argue that we spend much more on energy that we think.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/the-true-cost-of-carbon/', 'snippet': 'Two economists from The Hamilton Project argue that we spend much more on energy that we think.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Greenstone and Adam Looney, economists at The Hamilton Project, are releasing a new paper Wednesday on the costs of American energy policy. They argue:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The True Cost of Carbon', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T04:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e50537c-87e7-5ea3-bd7f-1921edd9c3f6', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e50537c-87e7-5ea3-bd7f-1921edd9c3f6'}, {'abstract': 'People who are overweight complain that moving is difficult. It’s possible that their muscular strength is not keeping pace with their growing body size.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/the-body-weight-muscle-mismatch/', 'snippet': 'People who are overweight complain that moving is difficult. It’s possible that their muscular strength is not keeping pace with their growing body size.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently scientists at Penn State sewed tiny weighted vests and slipped them around the middles of healthy laboratory rats, hoping to discover how animals’ muscles respond to changes in body size. The vests increased the animals’ weight by as much as 36 percent. After five days, the scientists found that the rats’ muscles contained increased amounts of certain proteins involved in the generation of muscle force. The muscles were redesigning themselves to be stronger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Body Weight-Muscle Mismatch', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Proteins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rats', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T04:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/174ab4b0-0c75-5b9f-b227-57c44c618e6c', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/174ab4b0-0c75-5b9f-b227-57c44c618e6c'}, {'abstract': 'Can you figure out what is going on with this patient with a toothache, slurred speech and a descending paralysis?', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/think-like-a-doctor-a-toothache-and-slurred-speech/', 'snippet': 'Can you figure out what is going on with this patient with a toothache, slurred speech and a descending paralysis?', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 19 9:39 a.m. | Thanks for all your submissions! You can find the correct diagnosis in “Think Like a Doctor: A Toothache and Slurred Speech Solved!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Like a Doctor: A Toothache and Slurred Speech', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guillain-Barre Syndrome', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T04:02:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bec5c403-fe33-5d20-ab87-f7ae9cee4ac0', 'word_count': 1961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bec5c403-fe33-5d20-ab87-f7ae9cee4ac0'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports, from the waters of Brazil to baseball fields in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/17/sports/SPTSREPLAY0517.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports, from the waters of Brazil to baseball fields in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports, from the waters of Brazil to baseball fields in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/17/sports/SPTSREPLAY0517-slide-A2VJ/SPTSREPLAY0517-slide-A2VJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 