y The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/814d31c4-395a-5b65-83ba-ee7439c05cd0', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814d31c4-395a-5b65-83ba-ee7439c05cd0'}, {'abstract': 'Dallas, the oldest team in the N.B.A. playoffs, got a game-high 48 points from Dirk Nowitzki to overshadow a 40-point performance by the Thunder’s Kevin Durant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/sports/basketball/nowitzki-scores-48-as-mavericks-show-experience-not-their-age.html', 'snippet': 'Dallas, the oldest team in the N.B.A. playoffs, got a game-high 48 points from Dirk Nowitzki to overshadow a 40-point performance by the Thunder’s Kevin Durant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — As the oldest team in the N.B.A. playoffs, the Dallas Mavericks have embarked on a farewell tour of sorts, as if they were aging rock stars refusing to stop the music. Tuesday night, they hit virtually every note and rolled the Oklahoma City Thunder, 121-112, to take a 1-0 lead in the Western Conference finals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/18mavericks-1/18mavericks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/18mavericks-1/18mavericks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/18mavericks-1/18mavericks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nowitzki Scores 48 as Mavericks Show Experience, Not Their Age', 'kicker': 'Playoffs | Mavericks 121, Thunder 112', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nowitzki Scores 48 as Mavericks S