yt://article/02dcf3be-c10e-59a6-9d28-1af18139c86f'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Greatness and Goodness: Barbaro and His Legacy” by Alex Brown.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/barbaro-getting-ready-for-the-derby/', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Greatness and Goodness: Barbaro and His Legacy” by Alex Brown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Brown, a regular contributor to The Rail, is author of the newly published “Greatness and Goodness: Barbaro and His Legacy.” In this excerpt, he describes Barbaro’s preparations before his dazzling performance in the Kentucky Derby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barbaro: Getting Ready for the Derby', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbaro (Race Horse)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kentucky Derby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T13:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f126cd7-aba7-5717-9f03-0c02d51eb854', 'word_count': 1873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f126cd7-aba7-5717-9f03-0c02d51eb854'}, {'abstract': 'Two months after an atomic bomb destroyed Hiroshima, President Harry S. Truman commissioned a study of the damage done to the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/22/magazine/22look-hiroshima.html', 'snippet': 'Two months after an atomic bomb destroyed Hiroshima, President Harry S. Truman commissioned a study of the damage done to the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two months after an atomic bomb destroyed Hiroshima, President Harry S. Truman commissioned a study of the damage done to the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hiroshima Files', 'kicker': 'Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hiroshima (Japan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T13:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/7c0b0b84-94b7-5dc7-9715-63e8e426e52f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/7c0b0b84-94b7-5dc7-9715-63e8e426e52f'}, {'abstract': 'The insurance company will acquire Esurance, an online provider of auto insurance quotes, and Answer Financial, which gives quote comparisons, from White Mountains Insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/allstate-buys-insurance-businesses-for-1-billion/', 'snippet': 'The insurance company will acquire Esurance, an online provider of auto insurance quotes, and Answer Financial, which gives quote comparisons, from White Mountains Insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:58 p.m. | Updated The Allstate Corporation said on Wednesday that it had agreed to acquire two insurance businesses from the White Mountains Insurance Group for about $1 billion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allstate Buys Insurance Businesses for $1 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLSTATE CORP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T13:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': '