5-bb778da44f22', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60aec7e-3628-5995-8505-bb778da44f22'}, {'abstract': 'Two granddaughters of Jacques Cousteau are in the inspiration business, invoking his name to prompt others to take interest in a variety of environmental issues.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/cousteau-cousins-come-to-town/', 'snippet': 'Two granddaughters of Jacques Cousteau are in the inspiration business, invoking his name to prompt others to take interest in a variety of environmental issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few environmental legends rival Jacques Cousteau, who died in 1997, for his energy, charisma, popularity and skills as an educator. This week, two of his granddaughters stopped by The New York Times. Alexandra and Céline Cousteau, cousins, did not seem to know each other’s schedule but were on the same wavelength in some other respects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cousteau Cousins Pitch Water Issues', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cousteau, Jacques', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Resources Institute', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T14:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4869ecb6-ad46-5c04-889a-f5861d1ce718', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4869ecb6-ad46-5c04-889a-f5861d1ce718'}, {'abstract': 'Will the United States keep its troops in Iraq after 2011? The answers, sought by Iraqis, reporters and American soldiers, are as redundant as they are critical to Iraq’s future.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/for-iraqis-and-u-s-troops-a-question-is-still-unanswered/', 'snippet': 'Will the United States keep its troops in Iraq after 2011? The answers, sought by Iraqis, reporters and American soldiers, are as redundant as they are critical to Iraq’s future.', 'lead_paragraph': ' UMM QASR, Iraq — Wherever American military leaders turn in Iraq, they are peppered with a question they don’t seem to be able to answer: Will the United States keep its troops in Iraq after 2011?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Iraqis and U.S. Troops, a Question Is Still Unanswered', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Status of Forces Agreements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T14:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8da9e533-6409