8-5765-886d-0e243e52cbdd', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8887bd2-5538-5765-886d-0e243e52cbdd'}, {'abstract': 'The stretch of coastline from Acapulco to Puerto Vallarta offers a range of surf towns, from established to emerging. Pick your paradise.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/mex-it-up/', 'snippet': 'The stretch of coastline from Acapulco to Puerto Vallarta offers a range of surf towns, from established to emerging. Pick your paradise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The globe-trotting surferati have been quietly colonizing Mexico’s Pacific coast for years. Alongside cheap and cheery beach shacks, you now find famous artists hanging out in French bistros. But not all is spoiled; the stretch of coastline from Acapulco to Puerto Vallarta offers a range of surf towns, from established to emerging. Pick your paradise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mex It Up', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T15:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f94355-ab32-5ede-ae8c-91adcedfc1c8', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f94355-ab32-5ede-ae8c-91adcedfc1c8'}, {'abstract': 'What thinking in 140 characters does to our brains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/magazine/the-twitter-trap.html', 'snippet': 'What thinking in 140 characters does to our brains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week my wife and I told our 13-year-old daughter she could join Facebook. Within a few hours she had accumulated 171 friends, and I felt a little as if I had passed my child a pipe 