y of a little bear’s day told backwards.', 'lead_paragraph': "Bedtime stories are charged with the mighty, sometimes seemingly insurmountable task of quieting and perhaps even inducing an audience to slumber. At the very least, they’re meant to compel the intended listener, say, a 4-year old boy, to stop somersaulting off the bunk bed and to please, please sit down. (That this process is often fraught with irritation has recently been showcased by a forthcoming children's-book parody, “Go the — to Sleep,” by Adam Mansbach and Ricardo Cortés, whose appearance online ricocheted among parental Twitterers like the answer key to next week’s S.A.T. exam.)", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/books/review/childrens-review-1/childrens-review-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/18/books/review/childrens-review-1/childrens-review-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/books/review/childrens-review-1/childrens-review-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/books/review/childrens-review-1/childrens-review-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/18/books/review/childrens-review-1/childrens-review-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bedtime Books for Boys', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', '