ream cable channels.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/upfronts-discovery-ups-the-stakes-in-hispanic-media/', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of Discovery Communications told advertisers on Wednesday that the Hispanic market promises significant growth when compared to mainstream cable channels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To underscore the priority that Discovery Communications says it is placing on Hispanic viewers, the president and chief executive, David Zaslav, made a herculean effort to attend the Discovery U.S. Hispanic upfront presentation at the Four Seasons restaurant in Midtown Manhattan on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upfronts: Discovery Ups the Stakes in Hispanic Media', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zaslav, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a162dc13-5056-57be-b894-1e8fc63998ed', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a162dc13-5056-57be-b894-1e8fc63998ed'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of demonstrators clashed with security forces in Takhar Province after a NATO night raid that local officials say killed four civilians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/world/asia/19afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of demonstrators clashed with security forces in Takhar Province after a NATO night raid that local officials say killed four civilians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A normally peaceful northern city erupted in violence on Wednesday, as thousands of protesters clashed with security forces after a NATO night raid that local officials claim killed four civilians. NATO defended the night operation and said the four people who were killed, two of them women, were armed insurgents who fired on its troops. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/world/19afghanistan2_337_span/19afghanistan2_337_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/19/world/19afghanistan2_337_span/19afghanistan2_337_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/world/19afghanistan2_337_span/19afghanistan2_337_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/world/19afghanistan2_337_span/19afghanistan2_337_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/19/world/19afghanistan2_337_span/19afghanistan2_337_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A NATO Raid Sets Off a Deadly Afghan Protest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A NATO Raid Sets Off A Deadly Afghan Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Rivera and Sangar Rahimi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rivera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sangar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rahimi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb695536-d98d-5ef9-9289-2b6ede3c178c', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb695536-d98d-5ef9-9289-2b6ede3c178c'}, {'abstract': 'Multiple relocations are surprisingly common and often harmful to the elderly. Poor communication regarding medical needs is often to blame, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/another-month-another-home/', 'snippet': 'Multiple relocations are surprisingly common and often harmful to the elderly. Poor communication regarding medical needs is often to blame, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For five years, Jim Casparie pleaded with his parents, Robert and Virginia Casparie, to accept more help. His father, then 91, had Alzheimer’s disease, and his mother, 84, had diabetes and poor balance, falling frequently. When they finally agreed to move to an independent living apartment in 2008, Mr. Casparie, 61, an investment banker, thought at last he could stop worrying about their safety.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Month, Another Home', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:10:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Plummer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Plummer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1018c5-2f41-52e9-ad9a-643fff0f4ba8', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1018c5-2f41-52e9-ad9a-643fff0f4ba8'}, {'abstract': 'Air Force One had a missed approach before landing safely at Bradley International Airport near Hartford on Wednesday morning, White House officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/air-force-one-lands-safely-after-circling/', 'snippet': 'Air Force One had a missed approach before landing safely at Bradley International Airport near Hartford on Wednesday morning, White House officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid poor visibility and a light rain, Air Force One had a missed approach before landing safely at Bradley International Airport near Hartford on Wednesday morning, White House officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Air Force One Lands Safely After Circling', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',