facebook-devalues-birthday-greetings-noticed.html', 'snippet': 'Facebook makes it easy to remember birthdays, but does it count as much now?', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORGETTING a friend’s birthday used to be uncomplicated. The excuse would be made, the gaffe forgiven. But among the many changes wrought by Facebook, the site’s ritual birthday reminders — those jolly alerts on the edge of that blue-and-white screen — have rendered old rules moot.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/fashion/Z-NOTICED/Z-NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/19/fashion/Z-NOTICED/Z-NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Wishes Turn Middling', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Wishes Turn Middling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birthdays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Lee Ball', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Ball', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29716d99-9a71-5ac4-9754-ee0a072bf6e8', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29716d99-9a71-5ac4-9754-ee0a072bf6e8'}, {'abstract': 'The Pew Charitable Trusts advise extending credit card protections to small business accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/extending-credit-card-protections-to-small-business-users/', 'snippet': 'The Pew Charitable Trusts advise extending credit card protections to small business accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each month, Americans get more than 10 million business credit card pitches in their home mailboxes. The cards are aimed at small businesses and sole proprietors, but they generally lack the new protections that apply to consumer cards, a new report from the Pew Charitable Trusts says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Extending Credit Card Protections to Small Business Users', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capital One Financial Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T16:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf60d4f-473a-57fa-a971-82a2faa19c66', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf60d4f-473a-57fa-a971-82a2faa19c66'}, {'abstract': 'Time to let go of your baggy board shorts: the trend is toward leaner, shorter cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/fashion/swim-trunks-whats-new.html', 'snippet': 'Time to let go of your baggy board shorts: the trend is toward leaner, shorter cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OUR guarantee: 10 seconds after putting on a pair of Orlebar Brown swim trunks, you will immediately lose your muffin top, develop a six-pack and instantly bear an uncanny resem