ring for last Sunday’s magazine article, “The Kitchen-Table Industrialists,” I found myself itching to make something myself. Like many urban professionals, I spend a lot of time producing things on a screen and very little time making anything tangible — besides lunch. As I describe in my article, I tried, on a trip to Detroit, to make an iPad stand, based on a design I downloaded from the Web. But the 3-D printer — yes, this exists — kept botching it. So I scaled back my ambitions and 3-D printed this lovely hexagonal nut. It’s not much, and it’s not much use without a bolt, but it’s something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Personal Hardware', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giridharadas, Anand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T18:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anand Giridharadas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anand', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giridharadas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e0ad2f-ed22-5588-81d9-13486bdaaa84', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e0ad2f-ed22-5588-81d9-13486bdaaa84'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Schwab will begin marketing 401(k) plans that offer only index funds as investment options.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/charles-schwab-to-offer-index-only-401k-plans/', 'snippet': 'Charles Schwab will begin marketing 401(k) plans that offer only index funds as investment options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Lieber’s Your Money column last weekend urged investors to ask their employers for more index-fund choices in their 401(k) r