mes is with Animal Kingdom at the Fair Hill Training Center as he prepares for the Preakness Stakes on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steeplechase Times is with Animal Kingdom at the Fair Hill Training Center as he prepares for the Preakness Stakes on Saturday. On Wednesday, Joe Clancy captured the scene:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Long Gallop for Animal Kingdom', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T19:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/47b67c3a-132b-5fb7-9336-202caac704ad', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47b67c3a-132b-5fb7-9336-202caac704ad'}, {'abstract': 'India spends more on programs for the poor than most developing countries, but it has failed to eradicate poverty because of widespread corruption, the World Bank said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/world/asia/19india.html', 'snippet': 'India spends more on programs for the poor than most developing countries, but it has failed to eradicate poverty because of widespread corruption, the World Bank said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — India spends more on programs for the poor than most developing countries, but it has failed to eradicate poverty because of widespread corruption and faulty government administration, the World Bank said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Anti-Poverty Programs Are Big but Troubled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Bank Reports on India Poverty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T19:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5614559c-25ac-553d-9931-8e472dc1f42f', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5614559c-25ac-553d-9931-8e472dc1f42f'}, {'abstract': 'With Lady Gaga on deck, Adele’s reign at the top of the Billboard charts may soon end.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/18/adele-is-at-no-1-for-8th-week-but-lady-gaga-is-on-deck/', 'snippet': 'With Lady Gaga on deck, Adele’s reign at the top of the Billboard charts may soon end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adele still dominates the Billboard charts, but with Lady Gaga on deck her reign probably won’t last much longer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adele Is at No. 1 for 8th Week, but Lady Gaga Is On Deck', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samberg, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaffer, Akiva', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taccone, Jor