, 'snippet': 'The second United States team for this year’s Bermuda Bowl world championship will be Kevin Bathurst, Daniel Zagorin, Joe Grue, Justin Lall, John Hurd and Joel Wooldridge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second United States team for this year’s Bermuda Bowl world championship will be Kevin Bathurst, Daniel Zagorin, Joe Grue, Justin Lall, John Hurd and Joel Wooldridge. Originally seeded ninth, they won the 120-board trial final in Henderson, Nev., on Tuesday against the Rosenblum Cup world champions and top seeds, John Diamond, Brian Platnick, Fred Gitelman, Brad Moss, Eric Greco and Geoff Hampson, by 288 international match points to 257. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/18/arts/card1/card1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weighing a Tough Choice With a 5-3 Major Fit', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weighing a Tough Choice With a 5-3 Major Fit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-18T22:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b1f72ff-2f2e-56ef-8998-44182660d72f', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b1f72ff-2f2e-56ef-8998-44182660d72f'}, {'abstract': 'The Times\'s television critic Ginia Bellafonte on the end of secon