bol of a brilliant effort by a short-handed bullpen. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Yankees, Start and Finish Make Up for What’s Between', 'kicker': 'Yankees 4, Orioles 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Yankees, Start and Finish Make Up for What’s Between', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T04:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a09c0555-ba94-5ebb-9698-bcc279930cc1', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a09c0555-ba94-5ebb-9698-bcc279930cc1'}, {'abstract': 'Cole Hamels allowed one run and five hits as the Phillies beat the Colorado Rockies 2-1 on a sacrifice fly be Jimmy Rollins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/sports/baseball/baseball-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'Cole Hamels allowed one run and five hits as the Phillies beat the Colorado Rockies 2-1 on a sacrifice fly be Jimmy Rollins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A post-trial hearing in San Francisco for Barry Bonds’s federal perjury case was postponed from Friday to June 17, giving prosecutors more time to decide if they will retry any of the three counts in which the jury deadlocked. The delay also will allow defense lawyers to hone their arguments for the judge to overrule the jury and throw out Bonds’s lone conviction.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/sports/BATS/BATS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 789, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Phillies Snap Losing Streak With Win Over Rockies', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecution Gets More Time To Decide on Retrying Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamels, Cole', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonds, Barry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perjury', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T04:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc441ee7-a964-5c50-9636-1e0058e9525d', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc441ee7-a964-5c50-9636-1e0058e9525d'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors will consider upgrading charges against a woman who left her baby in a trash can at a Queens hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/newborn-left-in-restroom-trash-can-dies/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors will consider upgrading charges against a woman who left her baby in a trash can at a Queens hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A newborn girl abandoned last week in a hospital trash can in Queens died on Wednesday, officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newborn Left in Restroom Trash Can Dies', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elmhurst Hospital Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T04:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7c2ce75-58fc-5689-bccf-e1342be02946', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c2ce75-58fc-5689-bccf-e1342be02946'}, {'abstract': 'Young singers audition for the Metropolitan Opera’s annual contest, a kind of American Idol for serious vocalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/22/magazine/opera-stars.html', 'snippet': 'Young singers audition for the Metropolitan Opera’s annual contest, a kind of American Idol for serious vocalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young singers audition for the Metropolitan Opera’s annual contest, a kind of American Idol for serious vocalists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/opera-slide-BGTD/opera-slide-BGTD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Longing To Perform Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T05:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/83f3ec54-1281-5f2f-ad26-ada04e768175', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/83f3ec54-1281-5f2f-ad26-ada04e768175'}, {'abstract': 'Imagine if there were an “American Idol” just for opera. Actually, there is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/magazine/an-american-idol-just-for-opera.html', 'snippet': 'Imagine if there were an “American Idol” just for opera. Actually, there is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Speedo Green stands almost six-foot-five and weighs 300 pounds and wears size 17 shoes, and on a Sunday afternoon in March he was running in place and doing jumping jacks as he waited in the wings of the Metropolitan Opera for his turn to sing. It was the semifinals of the most important operatic voice competition in America, and Ryan was seized by such anxiety that he felt his massive body vanishing. Seventeen of the 22 singers left in the contest had gone before him; to his ears their performances were spectacular. He was fighting off the feeling that he didn’t belong here. Ryan, who is African-American, grew up in low-income housing and a trailer park in southeastern Virginia. When he was 12, he spent time in juvenile detention for threatening his brother and mother. During high school he moved to a street of shacklike homes, with a drug dealer’s headquarters across from his family’s front door and with bullet holes from stray gunfire just above his mother’s bedroom window. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/22opera_span/22opera_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/22opera_span/22opera_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/22opera_span/22opera_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/22opera_span/22opera_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/magazine/22opera_span/22opera_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sing for Your Life', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'SING FOR YOUR LIFE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T05:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Bergner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c71b60dd-dcb4-57b0-be2e-3d61dd352555', 'word_count': 5690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c71b60dd-dcb4-57b0-be2e-3d61dd352555'}, {'abstract': 'The scary part of Wednesday’s marathon was the beaning of Chris Dickerson. The puzzling part was the rash ejection of the pitcher, Mike Gonzalez.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/scary-moment-puzzling-ejection/', 'snippet': 'The scary part of Wednesday’s marathon was the beaning of Chris Dickerson. The puzzling part was the rash ejection of the pitcher, Mike Gonzalez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE – Of all the bizarre moments in 296 minutes of baseball at Camden Yards on Wednesday, nothing was weirder than the plate umpire, Dan Bellino, ejecting Orioles pitcher Mike Gonzalez in the 15th inning. Gonzalez had just drilled the Yankees’ Chris Dickerson in the head, cracking his helmet and forcing Dickerson from the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scary Moment, Puzzling Ejection', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T05:03:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e959ed9a-561d-5fb2-92bc-5934486566fa', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e959ed9a-561d-5fb2-92bc-5934486566fa'}, {'abstract': 'Emerging-market nations like Brazil hope to brake the stranglehold Europe has had on the top job at the International Monetary Fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/business/20imf.html', 'snippet': 'Emerging-market nations like Brazil hope to brake the stranglehold Europe has had on the top job at the International Monetary Fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'European officials moved quickly to assert their claim over the leadership of the International Monetary Fund on Thursday, suggesting a serious challenge is being mounted by emerging economic powers like China and India that believe the time has come to break Europe’s historic grip on the post.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/IMF_span/IMF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 221, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/20/business/IMF_span/IMF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 221}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/IMF_span/IMF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/IMF_span/IMF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/business/IMF_span/IMF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '