 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/85c2bc48-2d7c-5211-b529-5fbdef5af275', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85c2bc48-2d7c-5211-b529-5fbdef5af275'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook will become the first service to use Microsoft’s PhotoDNA, a new technology that can quickly comb through millions of photos to identify illegal images.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/facebook-to-combat-child-porn-using-microsofts-technology/', 'snippet': 'Facebook will become the first service to use Microsoft’s PhotoDNA, a new technology that can quickly comb through millions of photos to identify illegal images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As online photo sharing has exploded so has, tragically, the distribution of child pornography. But while the rise of the Internet and digital cameras have revived a scourge that had nearly been eliminated in the late 1980s, new technology may also help to beat it back again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook’s New Way to Combat Child Pornography', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Pornography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Riva Richmond', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Riva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richmond', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8d7918f-d991-5d62-81e4-7976dd126c9b', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8d7918f-d991-5d62-81e4-7976dd126c9b'}, {'abstract': 'from May 26 through 29, Spreepark, Berlin’s only theme park, which has laid dormant for years, will come alive with the arrival of a multimedia festival.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/a-festival-brings-dormant-berlin-park-to-life/', 'snippet': 'from May 26 through 29, Spreepark, Berlin’s only theme park, which has laid dormant for years, will come alive with the arrival of a multimedia festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A borderline apocalyptic scene awaits when you enter Spreepark, Berlin’s only theme park, in the Treptow-Köpenick district in the former East Berlin. Life-size replicas of dinosaurs lie toppled on the ground. A pirate ship sits disintegrating in an algae-covered pond. A rusty Ferris wheel stands askew. Spreepark has been dormant since its insolvency in 2002. But from May 26 through 29, the fairground will come alive with the arrival of a multimedia festival called Lunapark Berlin. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Festival Brings Dormant Berlin Park to Life', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chaney Kwak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chaney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kwak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d633f22-d7ed-530b-a9fe-08cbc3475de0', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d633f22-d7ed-530b-a9fe-08cbc3475de0'}, {'abstract': 'Are social networks like Facebook and Twitter enhancing our real-world relationships? Or causing them to decay?', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/does-facebook-help-or-hinder-offline-friendships/', 'snippet': 'Are social networks like Facebook and Twitter enhancing our real-world relationships? Or causing them to decay?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two recent articles in the New York Times have raised the question of whether or not the daily interactions on Twitter and Facebook are trivializing our real world friendships by making it easier to do things like wish our friends a happy birthday online and send a tweet instead of picking up the phone, effectively diminishing our desire to have actual, face-to-face conversations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Facebook Help or Hinder Offline Friendships?', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T10:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b740e154-d6bc-5f3b-833b-c4ad8b593e49', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b740e154-d6bc-5f3b-833b-c4ad8b593e49'}, {'abstract': 'The suit claims that Trump misled buyers about his role in developing three luxury towers.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/judge-allows-florida-case-against-trump-to-proceed/', 'snippet': 'The suit claims that Trump misled buyers about his role in developing three luxury towers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Donald J. Trump tries to fend off lawsuits from angry home buyers, who claim he misled them about his role in developing luxury towers, his lawyers have repeatedly put forth a simple argument. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Allows Florida Case Against Trump to Proceed', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'JORDAN, ADALBERTO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trump International Hotel and Tower', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Lauderdale (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T10:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3533f575-b978-5033-88b3-7518783b5ce7', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3533f575-b978-5033-88b3-7518783b5ce7'}, {'abstract': 'If you go big-box, you may face backlash from consumers who will accuse you of making a deal with “the man.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/should-green-companies-work-with-giant-companies/', 'snippet': 'If you go big-box, you may face backlash from consumers who will accuse you of making a deal with “the man.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I started TerraCycle, we quickly came to a defining crossroads: Did we want to sell our made-from-waste products to independent retailers or to big-box retailers? Basically, we were told that if we sold to the big-box chains we would be blackballed by the independents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Green Companies Work With Giant Companies?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8295157-73e1-535f-838e-c6fb074a3884', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8295157-73e1-535f-838e-c6fb074a3884'}, {'abstract': 'Early in the crazy, culture-shifting 1960s, a little brown horse named Carry Back and John Sellers, a lanky, photogenic, 23-year-old rider from Oklahoma, were the stars of the Run for the Roses in Kentucky and, soon thereafter, the black-eyed Susans in Maryland.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/remembering-carry-back/', 'snippet': 'Early in the crazy, culture-shifting 1960s, a little brown horse named Carry Back and John Sellers, a lanky, photogenic, 23-year-old rider from Oklahoma, were the stars of the Run for the Roses in Kentucky and, soon thereafter, the black-eyed Susa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leslie Knauf is a writer, editor, marketer and horsewoman in upstate New York who has been attending the races at Saratoga for 50 years. She began riding horses at 9 and owned several thoroughbreds over the years that she rode for pleasure. She’s confident they taught her far more than she ever could teach them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Carry Back', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T11:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Knauf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knauf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ede737-0962-52d2-acc3-0c7b498ea064', 'word_count': 2004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ede737-0962-52d2-acc3-0c7b498ea064'}, {'abstract': 'Takeda Pharmaceutical, the Japanese drug maker, agreed to buy Nycomed of Switzerland for 9.6 billion euros on Thursday, bolstering its presence in Europe and emerging markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/takeda-to-buy-nycomed-for-13-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'Takeda Pharmaceutical, the Japanese drug maker, agreed to buy Nycomed of Switzerland for 9.6 billion euros on Thursday, bolstering its presence in Europe and emerging markets.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:09 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Takeda to Buy Nycomed for $13.7 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Millennium Pharmaceuticals Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nycomed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takeda Pharmaceuti