ame': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Policy (Magazine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T11:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/efdabe60-304f-5a2e-9f22-c65cfda905dd', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efdabe60-304f-5a2e-9f22-c65cfda905dd'}, {'abstract': 'The parks department has said that it will be bringing in higher quality food vendors around the city.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/rouge-tomate-says-it-will-have-a-food-cart-by-central-park/', 'snippet': 'The parks department has said that it will be bringing in higher quality food vendors around the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, some cutting-edge Brooklyn restaurateurs said that the parks department has agreed to let them run food stands on the Rockaway Boardwalk. Now, the owners of the more refined Rouge Tomatesay that the department had given them permission to open a food cart at the 64th street entrance to Central Park along Fifth Avenue, starting in mid-June. The cart’s menu, by the restaurant’s executive chef, Jeremy Bearman, will use seasonal and local ingredients in sandwiches — like BLTs made with local bacon and lettuce, heirloom tomatoes and whole wheat bread from Amy’s Bread — soups, snacks, juices and house-made ice cream and sorbets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rouge Tomate Says It Will Have a Food Cart by Central Park', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T11:58:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e50791fd-a279-5894-9b0d-19ed6fe61ef0', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e50791fd-a279-5894-9b0d-19ed6fe61ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Woody Allen, with the help of Paris and the ghosts of its famous dead, has found a credible blend of whimsy and wisdom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/movies/midnight-in-paris-by-woody-allen-with-owen-wilson-review.html', 'snippet': 'Woody Allen, with the help of Paris and the ghosts of its famous dead, has found a credible blend of whimsy and wisdom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The definitive poem in English on the subject of cultural nostalgia may be a short verse by Robert Browning called “Memorabilia.” It begins with a gasp of astonishment — “Ah, did you once see Shelley plain?” — and ends with a shrug: “Well I forget the rest.” Isn’t that always how it goes? The past seems so much more vivid, more substantial, than the present, and then it evaporates with the cold touch of reality. The good old days are so alluring because we were not around, however much we wish we were.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/movies/20midnight-span/20midnight-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/20/movies/20midnight-span/20midnight-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/movies/20midnight-span/20midnight-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/movies/20midnight-span/20midnight-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/movies/20midnight-span/20midnight-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Ennui and the Lost Generation', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Midnight in Paris'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Old Ennui and the Lost Generation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Owen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAdams, Rachel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T12:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fde4384-d1d0-578b-a341-1bbb153674c5', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fde4384-d1d0-578b-a341-1bbb153674c5'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant is part of a 10-year renovation of the building owned by the Czech Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/with-hospoda-czech-food-returns-to-the-upper-east-side/', 'snippet': 'The restaurant is part of a 10-year renovation of the building owned by the Czech Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beer is a big part of the vibe at Hospoda, the restaurant set to open on Monday in the landmark Bohemian National Hall on the Upper East Side, once a bastion of Czech food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Hospoda, Czech Food Returns to the Upper East Side', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T12:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/80aa7f44-5611-5be2-9258-d4d4cca68496', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80aa7f44-5611-5be2-9258-d4d4cca68496'}, {'abstract': 'Toshiba is buying Landis & Gyr for $2.3 billion to bolster its presence in energy and infrastructure technology solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/toshiba-to-acquire-swiss-electronics-maker-for-2-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'Toshiba is buying Landis & Gyr for $2.3 billion to bolster its presence in energy and infrastructure technology solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:04 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toshiba to Acquire Swiss Electronics Maker', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, 