e_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9edabbe-c2dc-5718-9db9-ba5ad96aeeda', 'word_count': 1798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9edabbe-c2dc-5718-9db9-ba5ad96aeeda'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Colbert, the host of the “Colbert Report,” talks about his admiration for Paddy Chayefsky’s dark satire of television broadcasting and how it influenced his the modern-day media personalities he satirizes.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/stephen-colbert-on-network-great-film-or-the-greatest-film/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Colbert, the host of the “Colbert Report,” talks about his admiration for Paddy Chayefsky’s dark satire of television broadcasting and how it influenced his the modern-day media personalities he satirizes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article in Arts & Leisure looks at the notes, drafts and correspondence kept by the screenwriter Paddy Chayefsky during the years he wrote “Network,” his dark 1976 comedy about the corruption of the news media, the degradation of the truth and the downfall of Howard Beale, a television news anchor with a messiah complex. So who’s better qualified to speak about the contemporary relevance of “Network” than Stephen Colbert, who holds a mocking mirror up to the Howard Beales of the present day while playing one himself on his Comedy Central program, “The Colbert Report”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Stephen Colbert on ‘Network': Great Film or the Greatest Film?", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chayefsky, Paddy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Steph