230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54400747-f5f0-58dc-b87a-464e85dedea2'}, {'abstract': 'A 21-year-old Parisian personality and Galliano-sympathizer continues to turn heads with his  “enhanced” Louboutins.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/taking-a-stand-igor-dewe/', 'snippet': 'A 21-year-old Parisian personality and Galliano-sympathizer continues to turn heads with his  “enhanced” Louboutins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what fashion week you attend around the world, part of the fun is checking out the cuckoo creatures who prance around outside in seriously thought-out get-ups. One who flies his freak flag high is Igor Dewe, a 21-year-old Parisian personality and performer, who made headlines in March when he paraded outside the Dior show carrying a placard offering sympathy for John Galliano. Dewe, who said he was shocked by the designer’s ethnic slurs but felt that his body of work deserved more respect, is best known for his “enhanced” Louboutins and other pricey footwear which he customizes with the help of his father, a welder. As to how he affords them, he says: “You don’t need money for clothes when you are fabulous, but for food, that is another story.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking a Stand | Igor Dewe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T17:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cator Sparks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cator', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sparks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/43e0fe42-6e02-579e-aefd-9be7a80c61d4', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43e0fe42-6e02-579e-aefd-9be7a80c61d4'}, {'abstract': 'A hike down Herkimer Street.', 'web_url': 'h