: '“Do we really live in a society that is still stuck in the lie that black men cannot be fathers?”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/a-minority-father-at-the-playground/', 'snippet': '“Do we really live in a society that is still stuck in the lie that black men cannot be fathers?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Which barrier looms larger — racism or sexism? Minority women raise that topic often when discussing how to navigate the workplace, and pundits ask the question periodically when discussing politics, from my informal mental scan of those writings, they are divided on the answer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Minority Father at the Playground', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T17:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0b186f9-ce9e-5769-9a42-b877ab906f7d', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0b186f9-ce9e-5769-9a42-b877ab906f7d'}, {'abstract': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention promoted its achievements, but its primer on preparing for the undead got the attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/health/20cdc.html', 'snippet': 'The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention promoted its achievements, but its primer on preparing for the undead got the attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity poor Tom Skinner, a top spokesman for the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention who has been valiantly trying to interest reporters in a new study in the agency’s Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report trumpeting “10 Great Public Health Achievements.” Unfortunately for Mr. Skinner, over at his agency’s public health blog, his colleagues were posting something that really got to the beating heart of morbidity and mortality: the first official C.D.C. instructions on coping with a zombie apocalypse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/CDC/CDC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/20/us/CDC/CDC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/CDC/CDC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/CDC/CDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/us/CDC/CDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zombies Upstage a Routine Public Health Bulletin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zombies Upstage a Routine Public Health Bulletin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and E