 Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T18:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bethany Lyttle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bethany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyttle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95b4516d-2f95-589e-82e3-bb672691d3a6', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95b4516d-2f95-589e-82e3-bb672691d3a6'}, {'abstract': 'The unlikely story of the Shaggs, whose fans included Kurt Cobain and Frank Zappa, hits the stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/theater/the-shaggs-stage-musical-is-about-to-return.html', 'snippet': 'The unlikely story of the Shaggs, whose fans included Kurt Cobain and Frank Zappa, hits the stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THEY may be the most defensive album liner notes in rock history: “The Shaggs love you and love to perform for you,” begins one paragraph on the back of the 1969 LP “The Shaggs: Philosophy of the World,” a cult classic for its guilelessly awful music and otherworldly lyrics. “You may love their music or you may not, but whatever you feel, at last you know you can listen to artists who are real.” The three members of this young sister act, we read, “are happy people and love what they are doing.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/SHAGGS-1/SHAGGS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/SHAGGS-1/SHAGGS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/SHAGGS-1/SHAGGS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 929, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/SHAGGS-1/SHAGGS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/SHAGGS-1/SHAGGS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sad and Haunted Girls Who Couldn’t Play Worth a Lick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sad and Haunted Girls Who Couldn’t Play Worth a Lick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shaggs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T18:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Weinert-Kendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weinert-Kendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8f195ad-7f10-5d7b-8689-a88f355f47b2', 'word_count': 1308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8f195ad-7f10-5d7b-8689-a88f355f47b2'}, {'abstract': 'Cory Arcangel specializes in modifying old videogames and other electronic detritus into statements about our relationship with technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/arts/design/cory-arcangels-video-games-at-the-whitney-art.html', 'snippet': 'Cory Arcangel specializes in modifying old videogames and other electronic detritus into statements about our relationship with technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a rainy April morning in what looked more like a makeshift office than an art studio, Cory Arcangel was deciding what drawings to produce for his survey show “Cory Arcangel: Pro Tools,” which opens Thursday at the Whitney Museum of American Art. Of two possible contenders, one would present the lyrics of the Miley Cyrus song “Party in the U.S.A.” in playful, loopy lettering; the other would be an intricately rendered tree. Both images would feature delicate lines laid down by a steady hand, though not Mr. Arcangel’s: the drawings would in fact be the product of a 1990s pen plotter machine, until recently defunct, which Mr. Arcangel had rerigged and reprogrammed. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/ARCANGEL-1/ARCANGEL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/ARCANGEL-1/ARCANGEL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/ARCANGEL-1/ARCANGEL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Sing the Gadget Electronic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Sing The Gadget Electronic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T18:53:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy Spears', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spears', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c391248-adae-558f-85c2-7e04518155c5', 'word_count': 1422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c391248-adae-558f-85c2-7e04518155c5'}, {'abstract': 'On view this month at the Harold Golen Gallery in Miami is a showcase of Ms. Yeager’s self-portraits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/19/fashion/Bunny-Yeager.html', 'snippet': 'On view this month at the Harold Golen Gallery in Miami is a showcase of Ms. Yeager’s self-portraits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On view this month at the Harold Golen Gallery in Miami is a showcase of Ms. Yeager’s self-portraits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/fashion/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 996, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/19/fashion/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/19/fashion/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO/Bunny-Yeager-slide-IHCO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bunny Yeager, Shy Beyond the Lens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeager, Bunny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T18:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/297ed821-2c0e-5a5b-99d9-96fc89a56115', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/297ed821-2c0e-5a5b-99d9-96fc89a56115'}, {'abstract': 'The Morning Line for Thursday, May 19', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/morning-line-is-the-outside-the-right-side-for-animal-kingdom/', 'snippet': 'The Morning Line for Thursday, May 19', 'lead_paragraph': 'The draw for the Preakness took place Wednesday. A full field of 14 was entered. The Kentucky Derby winner Animal Kingdom drew the No. 11 post, and was denominated the morning line favorite for the race at odds of 2-1. Second choice in the race is  Dialed In at odds of 9-2. There are differences of opinion on whether Animal Kingdom will be hurt by the outside draw.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: Is the Outside the Right Side for Animal Kingdom?', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/59291940-4268-533f-a905-0bc16cfc0b6f', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59291940-4268-533f-a905-0bc16cfc0b6f'}, {'abstract': 'The stage version will largely re-tell the movie plot about a Seattle widower, his son, and a woman who becomes obsessed with their heartbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/sleepless-in-seattle-musical-to-awaken-at-pasadena-playhouse/', 'snippet': 'The stage version will largely re-tell the movie plot about a Seattle widower, his son, and a woman who becomes obsessed with their heartbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sleepless in Seattle,” the 1993 Tom Hanks-Meg Ryan film that set its climax on the top of the Empire State Building, may yet find its own path to New York as part of the trend of turning hit movies into Broadway musicals. But the stage version of “Seattle” will start in Southern California: the Pasadena Playhouse announced on Thursday that it would mount the world premiere of “Sleepless in Seattle — The Musical” beginning June 12, 2012, with performances set to run through July 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sleepless in Seattle’ Musical to Awaken at Pasadena Playhouse', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a01b2c4e-ad20-5601-beff-18e9c9085ca8', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a01b2c4e-ad20-5601-beff-18e9c9085ca8'}, {'abstract': 'A judge’s decision came as a grand jury indicted Dominique Strauss-Kahn, who is accused of sexually assaulting a hotel housekeeper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/nyregion/grand-jury-indicts-former-imf-chief.html', 'snippet': 'A judge’s decision came as a grand jury indicted Dominique Strauss-Kahn, who is accused of sexually assaulting a hotel housekeeper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge granted bail on Thursday to Dominique Strauss-Kahn, the former managing director of the International Monetary Fund, allowing him to be freed from Rikers Island to stay in a Manhattan apartment while his sexual assault case is pending.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/20crime2_inline/20crime2_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/20crime2_inline/20crime2_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/business/20crime2_inline/20crime2_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strauss-Kahn Is Indicted and Will Soon Leave Jail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strauss-Kahn Is Indicted And Will Soon Leave Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss-Kahn, Dominique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee0c90c0-0066-54ad-a576-79b452ebfd3d', 'word_