 York City, horse-drawn carriages are required to travel in the same direction as horseless carriages. But on one Midtown block, the horses may get a chance to trot against the flow this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trotting Against Traffic', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ebf35a9-0009-5505-af66-cbdef4ac9593', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ebf35a9-0009-5505-af66-cbdef4ac9593'}, {'abstract': 'The deficit is smaller.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/u-s-manufacturing-trade-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'The deficit is smaller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been doing some number-crunching on trade issues, and thought I’d put something up for those who are interested: a picture of the recent improvement in the US manufacturing trade position.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Manufacturing Trade (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f340da45-bd76-5b48-8e72-c78a20f01a41', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f340da45-bd76-5b48-8e72-c78a20f01a41'}, {'abstract': 'Surfer-artists Alex Kopps and Tin Ojeda give an urban edge to what is usually a beachy domain.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/the-new-wave-2/', 'snippet': 'Surfer-artists Alex Kopps and Tin Ojeda give an urban edge to what is usually a beachy domain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Surf culture has long produced its own aesthetic, along with a tradition of surfer-artists. On the visual vanguard at the moment are Alex Kopps and Tin Ojeda. Kopps’s films, graffiti and collage-like prints (alexkopps.com) give an urban edge to what is usually a beachy domain. “The content and events that have influenced my artwork were not discovered at the beach,” says Kopps, who lives in the Bay Area and sells some of his T-shirts and posters (right) at Mollusk Surf Shop. His film “Displacement,” about “displacement hull” surfboards, uses 1970s Super-8 footage with abstract effects. Ojeda, the Argentinian-born painter and surfer behind the Drug Money Art clothing line (drugmoneyart.com), is bringing the beach to the city. His tees, on which he hand-prints phrases (“Beauty Is Boring,” says one), first gained a following in his home base of Montauk, N.Y. Now they’re at Barneys and in stores in Tokyo, Berlin and London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Wave', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c14b978e-f8a3-5f49-a57b-d9e83bd17edc', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c14b978e-f8a3-5f49-a57b-d9e83bd17edc'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian government condemned on Wednesday United States sanctions against President Bashar al-Assad and six of his top officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/world/middleeast/20syria.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian government condemned on Wednesday United States sanctions against President Bashar al-Assad and six of his top officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The Syrian government condemned on Thursday American sanctions against President Bashar al-Assad and six of his top officials over the ferocious crackdown on antigovernment protesters that human rights activists say has killed at least 850 people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Condemns U.S. Sanctions on Assad', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Sanctions Are Condemned; Town Is Shelled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0454c76c-2d0c-58ed-89f6-4631aeaa6808', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0454c76c-2d0c-58ed-89f6-4631aeaa6808'}, {'abstract': 'The speech prompted Israel’s prime minister to push back testily and the Palestinians to call an urgent meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/world/middleeast/20mideast.html', 'snippet': 'The speech prompted Israel’s prime minister to push back testily and the Palestinians to call an urgent meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — President Obama’s endorsement on Thursday of using the 1967 boundaries as the baseline for a solution to the Israeli-Palestinian dispute — the first by an American president — prompted Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel to push back testily and the Palestinian leadership to call an urgent meeting.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20mideast/20mideast-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20mideast/20mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20mideast/20mideast-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Netanyahu Responds Icily to Obama Remarks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Icily Greets Call By Obama for ’67 Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank