ents don’t work hard enough, leaving them unprepared for the working world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve received a lot of passionate (and angry) e-mails in response to my article today on the employment fate of recent college graduates. While the messages from young people almost uniformly expressed frustration at the job market they’d been thrust into, some of the e-mails from older readers argued that today’s college graduates were having trouble finding jobs because they hadn’t worked hard enough. For example, a reader named Norman Berger asks why graduates wonder why they prove worthless to a potential employer when they follow this approach:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Young College Grads Too Lazy to Work?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:53:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4979791-54f0-56cf-9984-8728ef1384b8', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4979791-54f0-56cf-9984-8728ef1384b8'}, {'abstract': 'Emergency venting systems in Japan and the United States variously require button-pushing in the control room, electricity or compressed gas to operate the valves, and/or muscle power on a crank. After the quake in Japan, operators there couldn’t make the valves work through any of these methods.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/the-importance-of-venting-when-a-reactor-threatens-to-blow-its-stack/', 'snippet': 'Emergency venting systems in Japan and the United States variously require button-pushing in the control room, electricity or compressed gas to operate the valves, and/or muscle power on a crank. After the quake in Japan, operators there couldn’t ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wrote in Thursday’s paper, the Fukushima Daiichi accident is renewing a debate over whether the emergency venting systems that were added to boiling water reactors 20 years ago should be opened only directly by operators or function automatically. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Importance of Venting, When a Reactor Threatens to Blow Its Stack', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T19:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d071935-6a9b-52c6-a1c5-e3f4ca3da629', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d071935-6a9b-52c6-a1c5-e3f4ca3da629'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Drape’s picks for the Preakness.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/joe-drapes-preakness-picks-3/', 'snippet': 'Joe Drape’s picks for the Preakness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pimlico oddsmaker Frank Carulli set the morning line for Saturday’s Preakness Stakes, and Joe Drape has listed the horses in order of preference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe Drape’s Preakness Picks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 