ne explosion in West Virginia put the blame squarely on Massey Energy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/20/us/20110520_MINE_REPORT_DOC.html', 'snippet': 'An independent team investigating 2010 coal mine explosion in West Virginia put the blame squarely on Massey Energy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An independent team investigating 2010 coal mine explosion in West Virginia put the blame squarely on Massey Energy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report on the Upper Big Branch Mine Explosion \ufeff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massey Energy Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T20:10:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/016ebf20-2ea8-5718-a2bc-e2dd0be22e3c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/016ebf20-2ea8-5718-a2bc-e2dd0be22e3c'}, {'abstract': 'A Berlin post in the 1930s was no plum, but William E. Dodd accepted the role of ambassador to Germany, and he and his family offer a glimpse into life as Hitler rose to power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/books/in-the-garden-of-beasts-by-erik-larson-review.html', 'snippet': 'A Berlin post in the 1930s was no plum, but William E. Dodd accepted the role of ambassador to Germany, and he and his family offer a glimpse into life as Hitler rose to power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the malicious nicknames given to William E. Dodd by his fellow American diplomats in the 1930s was “Telephone Book Dodd.” The joke was that Franklin D. Roosevelt, who appointed Dodd ambassador to Germany in 1933, had supposedly meant to offer the post to a Yale law professor named Walter F. Dodd but made a mistake in looking up the name. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20BOOK-AUTHOR/BOOK-AUTHOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perched in Berlin With Hitler Rising', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perched in Berlin With Hitler Rising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larson, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T20:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/efee1f7e-79c0-5d5e-9707-fe3f9135a0fd', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efee1f7e-79c0-5d5e-9707-fe3f9135a0fd'}, {'abstract': 'Dillon Gee made the game a little more exciting than usual, throwing five and two-thirds innings of no-hit ball as the Mets edged the Washington Nationals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/sports/baseball/gees-no-hit-bid-ends-in-sixth.html', 'snippet': 'Dillon Gee made the game a little more exciting than usual, throwing five and two-thirds innings of no-hit ball as the Mets edged the Washington Nationals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first batter Mets starter Dillon Gee faced Thursday, Roger Bernadina, fouled off one two-strike pitch after another, eight in all. Twelve pitches into the at-bat, Bernadina still stood in the batter’s box, as determined as Gee.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/baseball/2metspix/2metspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/baseball/2metspix/2metspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/baseball/2metspix/2metspix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/baseball/2metspix/2metspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/02/sports/baseball/2metspix/2metspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nothing New as No-Hit Bid Again Teases Mets', 'kicker': 'Mets 1, Nationals 0', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nothing New as No-Hit Bid Again Teases Mets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Nationals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gee, Dillon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Livan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T20:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59187d6c-1d38-542a-9f04-288cdb545163', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59187d6c-1d38-542a-9f04-288cdb545163'}, {'abstract': 'Inspiring bouts of irrational fear may be among the ancillary ambitions of Sleep No More,” an immersive production from the London-based Punchdrunk company.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/theater-talkback-the-skittish-play/', 'snippet': 'Inspiring bouts of irrational fear may be among the ancillary ambitions of Sleep No More,” an immersive production from the London-based Punchdrunk company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My patience with “Sleep No More,” the elaborate haunted house masquerading as theater in Chelsea, began to wear thin at about the time the pointy plastic mask I was wearing started pinching at the bridge of my nose. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: The Skittish Play', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T20:14:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa8d1fb-c9ca-5291-9335-3652e3571fc8', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa8d1fb-c9ca-5291-9335-3652e3571fc8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s major speech on Middle East policy did not appear to make a deep impression in Arab capitals on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/world/middleeast/20egypt.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s major speech on Middle East policy did not appear to make a deep impression in Arab capitals on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — President Obama may have hoped that his embrace of the democracy movement sweeping the Arab world might revive the warmth his name evoked after his speech to the Muslim world two years ago. But across the region, many said his soaring words and financial pledges did little to undo their disappointment at his apparent equivocation during the early days of the Arab revolt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaction in Arab Capitals Is Muted and Mixed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Many in Arab World Say Obama’s Speech Doesn’t Dispel Grievances Against U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T20:16:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1d1493c-1e1e-54fe-b1ee-e25f1043094f', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1d1493c-1e1e-54fe-b1ee-e25f1043094f'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama left open how far the U.S. could go in matching its enthusiasm with concrete steps to support a transformation in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/world/middleeast/20assess.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama left open how far the U.S. could go in matching its enthusiasm with concrete steps to support a transformation in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — After six months of struggle inside the White House to reconcile American interests in the Arab uprisings with American values, President Obama on Thursday sought to portray the region’s revolt in the historical tradition of the American Revolution and the civil rights movement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20assess/20assess-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20assess/20assess-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20assess/20assess-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20assess/20assess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/world/20assess/20assess-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {