s, the city’s unemployment rate dipped again in April to its lowest level in more than two years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Unemployment Rate Dips to 8.6%', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T21:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/113db2e8-3f09-5020-b939-e0ef1e7978d4', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/113db2e8-3f09-5020-b939-e0ef1e7978d4'}, {'abstract': 'Cool gear for wave-riding dudes — on and off the long board.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/hit-the-breakers/', 'snippet': 'Cool gear for wave-riding dudes — on and off the long board.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#124", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hit the Breakers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T21:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/f341147e-01a6-5fa2-afcc-a79d9367cafc', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f341147e-01a6-5fa2-afcc-a79d9367cafc'}, {'abstract': '“Access to Tools,” a modest but stirring time capsule of an exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art, considers the Whole Earth Catalog, from the 1960s and ’70s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/arts/design/access-to-tools-and-whole-earth-catalog-at-moma-review.html', 'snippet': '“Access to Tools,” a modest but stirring time capsule of an exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art, considers the Whole Earth Catalog, from the 1960s and ’70s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a generation that came of age in the late 1960s and early ’70s, three unusual reference books were catalytic consciousness raisers. “The Joy of Sex” and “Our Bodies, Ourselves” are still in print; the third and possibly most influential of all is less familiar to people born after 1980: the Whole Earth Catalog. Brainchild of the visionary techno-hippie artist Steward Brand, this compendium of resources for the New Age is the subject of “Access to Tools: Publications From the Whole Earth Catalog, 1968-1974,” a modest but stirring time capsule of an exhibition at the Museum of Modern Art. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20TOOLS/TOOLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 758, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20TOOLS/TOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/arts/20TOOLS/TOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Empowering People of Spaceship Earth', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kic