in perspective about his career and appreciate the player he once was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Paine is an analyst at Baseball-Reference.com, an online baseball encyclopedia of players, teams and box scores in the major and minor leagues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Posada Put Off Decline for Years', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T22:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEIL PAINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PAINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa00ef3a-5344-5c29-9ecf-8c43fdc53928', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa00ef3a-5344-5c29-9ecf-8c43fdc53928'}, {'abstract': 'Tune into The Caucus podcast to hear Times editors and reporters discuss President Obama’s Middle East speech and the reaction of some Republican presidential candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/the-caucus-podcast-obamas-speech-and-republican-reaction/', 'snippet': 'Tune into The Caucus podcast to hear Times editors and reporters discuss President Obama’s Middle East speech and the reaction of some Republican presidential candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tune into The Caucus podcast to hear a discussion of President Obama’s Middle East speech and the reaction of some of the Republican presidential candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Podcast: Obama’s Speech and Republican Reaction', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T22:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc7fc4b1-3038-5670-9544-6f3ef26b1a41', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc7fc4b1-3038-5670-9544-6f3ef26b1a41'}, {'abstract': 'Sculpture is enjoying a high-profile moment in New York, thanks to a head-spinning assortment of solo shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/arts/design/sculpture-exhibitions-in-high-relief-review.html', 'snippet': 'Sculpture is enjoying a high-profile moment in New York, thanks to a head-spinning assortment of solo shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a while since sculpture could be dismissed as “something you bump into when you back up to look at a painting,” as Ad Reinhardt, the Abstract Expressionist painter, once said. Even before Reinhardt died, in 1967, the medium was going supernova, expanding and diversifying at an astounding pace. First it began incorporating all manner of found objects and nontraditional materials; then it lifted brilliant color from painting and achieved new levels of abstraction. Since then it has come to include installations, environments, land art, performance and all manner of spectacle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'