e days, but the next generation of mobile devices will make today’s gadgets look dumb, due in part to sensor technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you own a smartphone, you probably know just how smart those little gadgets are. They know where you’re standing, the direction you’re moving in and if you’re holding the phone vertically or horizontally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sensors Are Coming!', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handheld Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sensors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-19T23:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/97137d90-543f-51a6-a945-aadf919f8577', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97137d90-543f-51a6-a945-aadf919f8577'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Thiel is an entrepreneur turned venture capitalist and investor whose macroperspective defines his investments in start-ups and securities.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/19/contrarian-investor-shuns-hot-idea-for-bigger-picture/', 'snippet': 'Peter Thiel is an entrepreneur turned venture capitalist and investor whose macroperspective defines his investments in start-ups and securities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As investors clamor for shares of social media darlings, Peter Thiel is avoiding the frenzy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contrarian Investor Shuns Hot Idea for Bigger Picture', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker'