n of the promises and challenges of the upheaval in the Arab world. His speech on Thursday did not go far enough — there was no game-changing proposal on the Israeli-Palestinian conflict — but he did promise strong support to those yearning for freedom and goaded American allies, including Israel, to take the political risks that are essential for peaceful change and the only way to build a lasting peace.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peace and Change', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peace and Change: President Obama said many right things about the Arab Spring, but he can’t stop there', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T01:20:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d69cd48-9021-5f2a-a60c-ae50d1109ca2', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d69cd48-9021-5f2a-a60c-ae50d1109ca2'}, {'abstract': 'Having appointed himself temporary oil minister, Iran’s leader is likely to add drama to what is usually a staid proceeding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/world/middleeast/20iran.html', 'snippet': 'Having appointed himself temporary oil minister, Iran’s leader is likely to add drama to what 