harging untreated sewage into the Chicago River during storms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent days, the federal government and environmental groups have increased the pressure on Chicago’s wastewater treatment agency to stop discharging untreated sewage into the Chicago River during storms and to disinfect the treated sewage that makes up 70 percent of the river’s flow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/20CNCRIVER/20CNCRIVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressure to Improve Water Quality in Chicago River', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressure to Improve Water Quality in Chicago River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T02:07:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Lydersen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lydersen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fcd0085-675e-5688-b97b-856bfefec455', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fcd0085-675e-5688-b97b-856bfefec455'}, {'abstract': 'In a grueling daylong meeting of board members, union officials appealed for more mainstream programming and criticized the company’s marketing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/arts/music/nyc-opera-budgeters-seek-to-save-next-season.html', 'snippet': 'In a grueling daylong meeting of board members, union officials appealed for more mainstream programming and criticized the company’s marketing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Board members of the New York City Opera hashed through the company’s budget and programming options for next season in a grueling daylong meeting on Thursday, a watershed moment for what was once one of the country’s major opera companies. Adding to the pressure, union officials appealed for more mainstream programming and denounced the way the company has been marketing itself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Budgeters Try to Save Season for the New York City Opera', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budgeters Try to Save Season For the New York City Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GUILD OF MUSICAL ARTISTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T02:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a6271c9-ce58-5920-9a6f-48982b0950de', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a6271c9-ce58-5920-9a6f-48982b0950de'}, {'abstract': "Ann Althouse, left, of the University of Wisconsin Law School and Matt Welch of Reason deb