nd harking back to the dot-com boom of the late 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It looks as if even LinkedIn’s bankers underestimated the hype. The shares more than doubled on the day of their debut, meaning underwriters left more money on the table than they harvested for LinkedIn and its selling shareholders. But if the hype doesn’t wear off soon, the scarcity value of social network investments surely will.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/business/Views/Views-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exuberant Days for LinkedIn', 'kicker': 'Reuters Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exuberant Days For LinkedIn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackRock Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T02:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales and Agnes T. Crane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Agnes', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Crane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b847002-0711-5be8-8358-fc25d67fa448', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b847002-0711-5be8-8358-fc25d67fa448'}, {'abstract': 'Our quirky, discerning picks for the 