 how far the capital city has come in embracing cuisines from around the world, not to mention its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long gone are the days when the primary dining options in Prague revolved around meat, dumplings and cabbage. Come the weekend of May 27 to 29, visitors to the Prague Food Festival can see — and taste — exactly how far the capital city has come in embracing cuisines from around the world, not to mention its own. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Festival to Feed Prague ‘Gastronauts’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fiona Gaze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fiona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9217b586-a948-5bf8-8ef4-e3d215099431', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9217b586-a948-5bf8-8ef4-e3d215099431'}, {'abstract': 'More students are taking longer to earn a bachelor’s degree, and colleges have no incentive to speed them up, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/the-rise-of-the-five-year-four-year-degree/', 'snippet': 'More students are taking longer to earn a bachelor’s degree, and colleges have no incentive to speed them up, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judith Scott-Clayton is an assistant professor at Teachers College, Columbia University.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rise of the Five-