e, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T10:54:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61f9ab73-6486-53d3-9f88-a4162b354ccf', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61f9ab73-6486-53d3-9f88-a4162b354ccf'}, {'abstract': 'The large majority of owners and breeders may well go ignored and uncounted as the industry, facing the threat of federal government involvement to outlaw race-day medications, attempts to deal with the most debilitating of all its current problems — a drug culture image among fans and bettors alike.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/at-racings-poker-table-owners-and-breeders-are-the-marks/', 'snippet': 'The large majority of owners and breeders may well go ignored and uncounted as the industry, facing the threat of federal government involvement to outlaw race-day medications, attempts to deal with the most debilitating of all its current problem...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Billy Walters, one of the world’s most successful professional gamblers, warns that no matter what game you are playing, if you look around the room and can’t find the mark, you are it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Racing’s Poker Table, Owners and Breeders Are the Marks', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T11:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim