, '_id': 'nyt://article/83514c96-69cf-5502-96ea-b8e5aa3c1daa', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83514c96-69cf-5502-96ea-b8e5aa3c1daa'}, {'abstract': 'My father, Mr. Rationality, has decided it’s time to move to an independent living facility.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/moving-murray/', 'snippet': 'My father, Mr. Rationality, has decided it’s time to move to an independent living facility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I spent a recent weekend in southern New Jersey with my father, carefully labeling his entire wardrobe — every sock, pajama top and handkerchief — with a black Sharpie. The continuing care retirement community he’s moving to will do his laundry weekly, and it wants his name on each garment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Murray', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T12:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a68f72d1-9664-52e2-94ec-d56783beb4c5', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a68f72d1-9664-52e2-94ec-d56783beb4c5'}, {'abstract': 'Jon Pareles, the New York Times’s pop music critic, talked to Lady Gaga before the release of her new album, “Born This Way.” Here are excerpts from their conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/q-and-a-with-lady-gaga-on-her-freedom-ride/', 'snippet': 'Jon Pareles, the New York Times’s pop music critic, talked to Lady Gaga before the release of her new album, “Born This Way.” Here are excerpts from their conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a profile in Arts & Leisure, Jon Pareles sat down with Lady Gaga as she prepares for the release of “Born This Way,” her second studio album. “The album is as catchy and euphorically overblown as the music that made her a sensation,” Mr. Pareles writes about the pop superstar. “It also adds an additional dimension to her songs: her cherished relationship with a mass audience — fans who call themselves Little Monsters and dress up with a gender-bending zeal — to whom she is a goddess, a big sister, a mouthpiece, a counselor and a cheerleader.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. With Lady Gaga on Her ‘Freedom Ride’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemons, Clarence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penthouse', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vogue', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T12:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cde3d732-f9c3-5343-936b-7f376d9517fd', 'word_count': 1963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cde3d732-f9c3-5343-936b-7f376d9517fd'}, {'abstract': 'Are the Yankees nothing more than barely a .500 team? When will the Mets truly be relevant again? And what do we make of all those crazy new statistics?', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/answers-to-readers-baseball-questions-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Are the Yankees nothing more than barely a .500 team? When will the Mets truly be relevant again? And what do we make of all those crazy new statistics?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following are responses from Tyler Kepner, David Waldstein and Ben Shpigel, the Times’s baseball writers, who took questions from readers this week about the Mets, Yankees and the game overall through the first quarter of the 2011 season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Readers’ Baseball Questions, Part 2', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Cliff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pujols, Albert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T12:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/e17610e8-b592-574b-925f-8bbe96d2f823', 'word_count': 2413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e17610e8-b592-574b-925f-8bbe96d2f823'}, {'abstract': 'Soon a rooftop cafe there will have beer and wine.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/bark-hot-dogs-will-open-at-pier-6-in-brooklyn-bridge-park/', 'snippet': 'Soon a rooftop cafe there will have beer and wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The eating options in Brooklyn Bridge Park will spread south to Pier 6 on May 28 when Bark, the haute dog spot in Park Slope, Brooklyn, opens a stand there serving franks and burgers, along with ice cream from Blue Marble and Uncle Louie G’s, and sandwiches from Milk Truck Grilled Cheese. Later next month it will move to a terrace cafe on the pier with 200 seats and will start serving beers from Sixpoint Craft Ales and wine. The stand will be open Saturdays and Sundays, then the terrace will be open Friday nights, Saturdays and Sundays through Labor Day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bark Hot Dogs Will Open at Pier 6 in Brooklyn Bridge Park', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T12:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/368eae8a-9103-51d4-ab36-94ebb82d124a', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/368eae8a-9103-51d4-ab36-94ebb82d124a'}, {'abstract': 'Greece’s financial problems led to a call for the European Union to develop a more comprehensive plan to deal with the region’s debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/business/global/21iht-euro21.html', 'snippet': 'Greece’s financial problems led to a call for the European Union to develop a more comprehensive plan to deal with the region’s debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greek bonds led declines among euro area nations on Friday on concern a restructuring of its debt would reignite Europe’s sovereign debt crisi