etition-rules-for-life/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists are invited to share their rules for life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, co-vocabularists are invited to share their rules for life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Competition: Rules for Life', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T16:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b857b535-a9e7-5e23-b8d6-de876a486472', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b857b535-a9e7-5e23-b8d6-de876a486472'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Canetti, the president of the Houston Dynamo, talks about retooling his team’s roster under the restrictive salary budget of Major League Soccer.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/in-houston-retooling-not-rebuilding/', 'snippet': 'Chris Canetti, the president of the Houston Dynamo, talks about retooling his team’s roster under the restrictive salary budget of Major League Soccer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has become a rite of spring (at least since 2007) in Major League Soccer: the union that represents the league’s more than 500 players publishes their salaries on its Web site. (It is a useful look, but it would be even more valuable if the union, instead of listing the players alphabetically or by club in the static PDF format, presented the material in an Excel spreadsheet for easy manipulation. But why quibble?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Houston, Retooling, Not Rebuilding', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '