 basement, nearly destroyed i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “Little Boy” that devastated Hiroshima in 1945 altered the Earth’s axis, while also (albeit briefly) changing the way war would be waged. It virtually leveled an entire city — the scope of which is only hinted at in these dramatic photographs — and, followed three days later by a second, smaller detonation on Nagasaki, did what determined American military bombing was unable to do: it forced a Japanese surrender.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hiroshima Exhibit That Almost Wasn’t', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Center for Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hiroshima (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c0966dc-4fd3-5e46-8b4e-10be7e0ca254', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c0966dc-4fd3-5e46-8b4e-10be7e0ca254'}, {'abstract': 'David Strasser, an analyst with Janney Capital Markets, weighs in on Liberty Media’s $1 billion offer for Barnes & Noble. Has the growth of e-book sales made the bookseller more attractive to potential buyers?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/barnes-noble-looking-better-as-it-ages/', 'snippet': 'David Strasser, an analyst with Janney Capital Markets, weighs in on Liberty Media’s $1 billion offer for Barnes & Noble. Has the growth of e-book sales made the bookseller more attractive to potential buyers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the growth of e-book sales, Barnes & Noble may now be more valuable to potential buyers than it was when it put itself on the market in August. In an interview with CNBC, David Strasser, an analyst with Janney Capital Markets, weighs in on Liberty Media’s $1 billion offer for the giant bookseller.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barnes & Noble Looking Better as It Ages', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberty Media Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/411c4df5-52ff-56f8-b1dc-daba3ffcff8d', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/411c4df5-52ff-56f8-b1dc-daba3ffcff8d'}, {'abstract': 'A statement by the medical examiner in Hennepin County, Minn., said the Rangers player’s death was accidental.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/sports/hockey/boogaard-died-from-mix-of-alcohol-and-oxycodone.html', 'snippet': 'A statement by the medical examiner in Hennepin County, Minn., said the Rangers player’s death was accidental.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Derek Boogaard of the Rangers died from an accidental overdose of the drug oxycodone mixed with alcohol, the office of the medical examiner in Minnesota’s Hennepin County announced Friday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/BOOGAARD/BOOGAARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 938, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boogaard Died From Alcohol and Drug Mix', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boogaard Died From Alcohol and Drug Mix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'OxyContin (Drug)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boogaard, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11b79da3-17d9-5d60-9c60-5ae4958d85a3', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11b79da3-17d9-5d60-9c60-5ae4958d85a3'}, {'abstract': 'Norman Jewison, who has directed films like “Moonstruck” and “In the Heat of the Night,” will be the subject of a retrospective at the Film Society of Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/movies/a-norman-jewison-retrospective-at-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'Norman Jewison, who has directed films like “Moonstruck” and “In the Heat of the Night,” will be the subject of a retrospective at the Film Society of Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': '“FOR me, films are about ideas,” said Norman Jewison, looking out over Central Park on a fine New York day not long ago. “Every director should ask himself, ‘Why am I making this picture?’ And if you can’t answer that, you shouldn’t make it.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/JEWISON-2/JEWISON-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/JEWISON-2/JEWISON-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/JEWISON-2/JEWISON-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/JEWISON-2/JEWISON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/arts/JEWISON-2/JEWISON-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Director of Ideas With Decades of Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Director of Ideas With Decades of Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jewison, Norman', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terrence Rafferty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafferty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4cee13a-bfda-5b12-b681-462704ec03aa', 'word_count': 1436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4cee13a-bfda-5b12-b681-462704ec03aa'}, {'abstract': 'Hong Kong’s private kitchens have taken a turn for the upscale and inventive, becoming hubs for young chefs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/inside-hong-kongs-private-kitchens.html', 'snippet': 'Hong Kong’s private kitchens have taken a turn for the upscale and inventive, becoming hubs for young chefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON little Star Street, a sliver of a lane in Hong Kong’s Wan Chai neighborhood, a group of hungry friends and I walked up and down the same block, iPhone maps in hand, a handful of times before pausing before a quiet apartment building. “Is this it?” I asked, triple-checking the address before pressing the buzzer.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/18choice-span/18choice-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/18choice-span/18choice-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/18choice-span/Choice-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/18choice-span/18choice-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/18choice-span/18choice-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Hong Kong’s Private Kitchens', 'kicker': 'Choice Tables', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside Private Kitchens, Adventures Await', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Lu-Lien Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': 'Lu-lien', 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7128c721-9598-5824-a433-9761dc87b02b', 'word_count': 1662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7128c721-9598-5824-a433-9761dc87b02b'}, {'abstract': 'Saving gas money at the car rental counter and more tips on group travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/hello-tour-operator.html', 'snippet': 'Saving gas money at the car rental counter and more tips on group travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding the May 8 Practical Traveler column, “How to Save on Group Travel”: The article provides some useful information, but omits the single easiest solution: using a tour operator.\xa0Someone planning a group tour needn’t negotiate with the cruise line, the airline, the hotel or the visitor/convention bureau separately. Tour operators have special group departments that make all the arrangements, saving not only money but time, one of today’s most precious commodities. Terry Dale New York City', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Hello, Tour Operator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hello, Tour Operator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/78e9e5a3-e8c0-5db3-b863-84c5208b8ed1', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78e9e5a3-e8c0-5db3-b863-84c5208b8ed1'}, {'abstract': 'Saving gas money at the car rental counter and more tips on group travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/passing-on-upgrades.html', 'snippet': 'Saving gas money at the car rental counter and more tips on group travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding the May 15 Practical Traveler column, “13 Ways to Save on Gas This Summer”: An other important tip when renting cars: think twice before accepting the “upgrade” offer they often throw at you while at the counter — bigger, fancier or sportier cars often burn more gas. Many rental companies will now tell you what are the most fuel-efficient models available, and many now have hybrids. If you plan on driving your rental far, this kind of thinking can save a small fortune. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: Passing on Upgrades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Passing On Upgrades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0cdeab0-1430-5b0a-b57f-8190ba3e7773', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0cdeab0-1430-5b0a-b57f-8190ba3e7773'}, {'abstract': 'An hour and a half from the Chilean capital, Viña del Mar, on the Pacific coast, gives visitors reasons to stay and relax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/the-charms-of-vina-del-mar-along-chiles-coast.html', 'snippet': 'An hour and a half from the Chilean capital, Viña del Mar, on the Pacific coast, gives visitors reasons to stay and relax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DANNY DIAZ stared out into the Pacific, scanning the water, ready to dash at the right moment. “We are here to catch a sider,” Mr. Diaz, 24, said, referring to what he considers the perfect wave, as he stood on the sandy embankment where the inlet Estero Marga Marga meets the ocean in Viña del Mar, Chile. He was with a group of friends, all skimboarders, a sport Mr. Diaz described as “a mix between skateboarding and surfing.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22overnighter-span/22overnighter-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22overnighter-span/22overnighter-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22overnighter-span/Overnighter-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22overnighter-span/22overnighter-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22overnighter-span/22overnighter-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Charms of Viña del Mar, Along Chile’s Coast', 'kicker': 'Overnighter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Santiago Goes to Relax by the Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vina del Mar (Chile)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:55:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael T. Luongo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Luongo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e78bfe4-05d6-5cce-861c-63761d403bed', 'word_count': 1687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e78bfe4-05d6-5cce-861c-63761d403bed'}, {'abstract': 'Through the farmland, pastures and one-light towns along Virginia’s Crooked Road, there is a single, unifying sound: old-time, foot-tapping homegrown music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/on-virginias-crooked-road-music-lights-the-way.html', 'snippet': 'Through the farmland, pastures and one-light towns along Virginia’s Crooked Road, there is a single, unifying sound: old-time, foot-tapping homegrown music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT starts with a well-worn fiddle, held in equally well-worn hands above a tapping black cowboy boot. Then in comes the banjo, plucked with steel finger picks, followed by the autoharp, the mandolin, the percussive beat of an upright bass. Another banjo grabs the melody, and suddenly the room is bursting with knee-slapping, country-porch music. A man in a crisp checked shirt gets up and starts to dance, bouncing out a complicated bumbumBAM bumbumBAM with his feet, moving as smoothly as a Martha Graham dancer, hitting the floor on the downbeat.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22cover-span/22cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22cover-span/22cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22cover-span/22cover-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22cover-span/22cover-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22cover-span/22cover-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Virginia’s Crooked Road, Mountain Music Lights the Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mountain Music by the Mile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T18:55:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wildman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wildman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c249701-9b56-5059-bc89-40d486a0f74d', 'word_count': 2887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c249701-9b56-5059-bc89-40d486a0f74d'}, {'abstract': 'As more Americans discover the affordable living of old East Berlin, they bring with them a fresh angle on the restaurant scene. Take Little Otik in the Kreuzberg district.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/travel/restaurant-report-little-otik-in-berlin.html', 'snippet': 'As more Americans discover the affordable living of old East Berlin, they bring with them a fresh angle on the restaurant scene. Take Little Otik in the Kreuzberg district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American cuisine in Berlin is something of an anomaly. Food in the German capital is about Turkish kebabs, Greek shawarma, Thai green curry and the ubiquitous German trinity of bockwurst, currywurst and schnitzel.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22bites-span/22bites-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22bites-span/22bites-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22bites-span/22-BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22bites-span/22bites-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/travel/22bites-span/22bites-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: Little Oti