les Patrick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T20:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac04d657-2f7d-5889-8114-42ed1434960c', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac04d657-2f7d-5889-8114-42ed1434960c'}, {'abstract': 'The first volume of “Ai Ore-Love Me!” hits the manga list at No. 10 this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/graphic-book-best-sellers-star-crossed-romance/', 'snippet': 'The first volume of “Ai Ore-Love Me!” hits the manga list at No. 10 this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first volume of “Ai Ore-Love Me!” hits the manga list at No. 10 this week. The book is about what happens when Mizuki, the lead guitarist at an all-girl school, is approached by Akira, a student at an all-boys school, who wants to join her band. Seems like a reasonable enough premise, but things get more confusing, according to the description on the web site of VIZ Media, which publishes the book: “Love may be on his mind, but romance is difficult when everyone keeps mistaking Mizuki for a boy and Akira for a girl!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Book Best Sellers: Star-Crossed Romance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T20:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d831f4d-265d-5772-bd16-ae2e1d5b0c7c', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d831f4d-265d-5772-bd16-ae2e1d5b0c7c'}, {'abstract': 'A science meeting tests new ways to capture hearts, minds, guts and more.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/can-scientists-arouse-and-fulfill/', 'snippet': 'A science meeting tests new ways to capture hearts, minds, guts and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a Dot Earth Postcard from Randy Olson, the marine biologist turned filmmaker and science-communication evangelist, who recently attended a conference on neglected diseases, complex systems, learning and more organized by Larry Gold, a biotechnology entrepreneur and microbiologist at the University of Colorado:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Scientists Arouse and Fulfill?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biotechnology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gold, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Randy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TED (Technology, Entertainment, Design)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T20:50:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4832a3b9-afdb-5f5a-8dad-57a120eca612', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4832a3b9-afdb-5f5a-8dad-57a120eca612'}, {'abstract': 'Goldikova, the grande dame of worldwide thoroughbred racing, is set to make her seasonal reappearance on Sunday in the Group 1 Prix d’Ispahan at Longchamp.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/goldikova-racings-grande-dame-returns-on-sunday/', 'snippet': 'Goldikova, the grande dame of worldwide thoroughbred racing, is set to make her seasonal reappearance on Sunday in the Group 1 Prix d’Ispahan at Longchamp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She was around when Curlin won the Preakness in 2007. She saw Big Brown come and go in 2008, too. She had already staked her turf in the history books when Rachel Alexandra won her Preakness in 2009, and she saw Lookin at Lucky’s short burst of fame last year, too. All those champions flowered and faded in the blink of an eye next to her glittering career, which is still far from over. Goldikova, the grande dame of worldwide thoroughbred racing, is set to make her seasonal reappearance on Sunday in the Group 1 Prix d’Ispahan at Longchamp.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldikova, Racing’s Grande Dame, Returns on Sunday', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T21:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Rarick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rarick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4f4b5ea-9471-501b-b689-094e660d6a59', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4f4b5ea-9471-501b-b689-094e660d6a59'}, {'abstract': 'The women who would be president in 2012 are still sitting on the sidelines. But that coul