': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T23:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/824ed93f-5637-5122-ad85-aefa0069d18a', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/824ed93f-5637-5122-ad85-aefa0069d18a'}, {'abstract': 'Curious to see the adaptive abilities of liberals in action, the City Critic gave five stand-up comics a secret phrase to see how seamlessly they could work it into their acts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/nyregion/can-liberal-comics-tickle-the-right-funny-bone.html', 'snippet': 'Curious to see the adaptive abilities of liberals in action, the City Critic gave five stand-up comics a secret phrase to see how seamlessly they could work it into their acts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps you, like City Critic, thought that liberals had been eradicated through some kind of spraying program or mass inoculation. No elected official has admitted to being one since the Carter administration, and the very word “liberal” ranks right up there with “care to respond to the rumors about your love child?” as guaranteed to make Sunday morning talk-show guests change the subject.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22jpCRITIC5/22jpCRITIC5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22jpCRITIC5/22jpCRITIC5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22jpCRITIC5/22jpCRITIC5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enter Laughing, From the Liberal Wing', 'kicker': 'City Critic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enter Laughing, From the Liberal Wing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drinking Liberally', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T23:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06c90844-2180-538a-bbe0-97cae830ebeb', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06c90844-2180-538a-bbe0-97cae830ebeb'}, {'abstract': 'An American journalist’s observational documentary on Sunday’s protest by Palestinians in Lebanon to mark the anniversary of what they call the “nakba” or the “catastrophe” of Israel’s founding.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/20/video-of-the-nakba-day-protest-in-lebanon/', 'snippet': 'An American journalist’s observational documentary on Sunday’s protest by Palestinians in Lebanon to mark the anniversary of what they call the “nakba” or the “catastrophe” of Israel’s founding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, a senior official who traveled to Washington with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel told Yediot Aharonot, an Israeli newspaper, that it was important for the White House to understand the seriousness of last Sunday’s protests along Israel’s frontiers with Lebanon and Syria. “People are waging war along the fences,” the official said, “and it’s not an exaggeration.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of the ‘Nakba Day’ Protest in Lebanon', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-20T23:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2deea5f3-ab88-5eae-a4b7-712b0b95eafd', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2deea5f3-ab88-5eae-a4b7-712b0b95eafd'}, {'abstract': 'With the average price for a new car in the United States edging toward $30,000, some executives fear that sticker shock could stall the industry’s recent comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/business/21auto.html', 'snippet': 'With the average price for a new car in the United States edging toward $30,000, some executives fear that sticker shock could stall the industry’s recent comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The average price for a new car in the United States is edging toward $30,000, as automakers remain stingy with discounts and ther