t': 'May 20, 2011- President Obama meets with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 20, 2011- President Obama meets with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/politics/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/20/us/politics/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/20/us/politics/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/20/us/politics/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu/video-tc-052011-obamanetanyahu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | Distrustful Allies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T00:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/bd5b5094-6798-564c-826e-96d3f3cf8802', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/bd5b5094-6798-564c-826e-96d3f3cf8802'}, {'abstract': 'The owners of Massa’ describe their menu as classic Italian cuisine influenced by their native Puglia, but there was little on it that strayed from the standard Italian-American script.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/nyregion/an-italian-newcomer-that-sticks-to-the-script.html', 'snippet': 'The owners of Massa’ describe their menu as classic Italian cuisine influenced by their native Puglia, but there was little on it that strayed from the standard Italian-American script.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAVE never seen a wait staff burn more calories than I did on a recent night at Massa’, a vigorous new Italian restaurant in Scarsdale (Massa’ is short for “masseria,” a fortified southern Italian farmhouse). Seated at the base of a broad staircase leading from the main dining room up to a spacious bar and ancillary dining area, where a private party for 30 was in full swing, my guests and I had the equivalent of front-row seats as we watched waiters dash from the kitchen and sprint up the stairs, then trot back down again, taking two steps at a time.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22DINEWE2/22DINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22DINEWE2/22DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/nyregion/22DINEWE2/22DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Italian Newcomer That Sticks to the Script', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Scarsdale', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Italian Newcomer That Sticks to the Script', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T00:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/001d45f6-f955-5746-8fb8-9c42d11f0bbe', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/001d45f6-f955-5746-8fb8-9c42d11f0bbe'}, {'abstract': 'Jolo Moise, a native of Haiti, offers takeout and eat-in food without meat or dairy, and smoothies, seven days a week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/nyregion/vegan-dishes-at-jolos-kitchen-in-new-rochelle.html', 'snippet': 'Jolo Moise, a native of Haiti, offers takeout and eat-in food without meat or dairy, and smoothies, seven days a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many restaurants offer vegetarian dishes these days, but diners who want to avoid any kind of animal products, including fish and dairy, will find the pickings slim — unless they visit Jolo’s Kitchen in New Rochelle. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Sausage, but Soysage', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | New Rochelle', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Sausage, but Soysage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations'