/2011/05/21/sports/for-trainers-the-preakness-legitimizes-a-horse.html', 'snippet': 'Horsemen say that more often than not, the winner of the Preakness is the best horse of its generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — When it comes to myth-making, the Preakness Stakes has had trouble competing with the Kentucky Derby and its reputation as the Greatest Two Minutes in Sports and the Belmont Stakes, known as the Test of the Champion. Instead, it is merely the second jewel in horse racing’s Triple Crown.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/yPREAKNESS/yPREAKNESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/yPREAKNESS/yPREAKNESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/yPREAKNESS/yPREAKNESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/yPREAKNESS/yPREAKNESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/21/sports/yPREAKNESS/yPREAKNESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Trainers, the Preakness ‘Legitimizes’ a Horse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Trainers, the Preakness ‘Legitimizes’ a Horse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj