d_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — Indonesia on Friday released the details of a $1 billion program to curb forest destruction and reduce greenhouse gas emissions, but environmentalists said the plan gave industry too much leeway to continue clearing vital ecosystems. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/world/21jakarta/21jakarta-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/21/world/21jakarta/21jakarta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/21/world/21jakarta/21jakarta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Environmentalists Criticize Indonesia’s Plan to Save Forests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Environmentalists Criticize Indonesia’s Plan to Save Forests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jakarta (Indonesia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T01:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aubrey Belford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aubrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d9ea407-8532-53fc-9a68-39bf7a5fb6d4', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d9ea407-8532-53fc-9a68-39bf7a5fb6d4'}, {'abstract': 'Apple has entered the final stages of negotiations with major record labels and music publishers for a service that will allow people to listen to their music stored on the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/technology/21apple.html', 'snippet': 'Apple has entered the final stages of negotiations with major record labels and music publishers for a service that will allow people to listen to their music stored on the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For tens of millions of iTunes users, listening to music may soon get a lot easier. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Is Called Poised to Offer ‘Cloud’ Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple Is Called Poised to Offer ‘Cloud’ Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Audio)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T01:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario and Miguel Helft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Helft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/887db0c8-ce96-5863-aca0-47db317b9216', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/887db0c8-ce96-5863-aca0-47db317b9216'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal for a retirement plan for the sport’s horses has not been embraced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/sports/racing-industry-should-care-for-its-own.html', 'snippet': 'A proposal for a retirement plan for the sport’s horses has not been embraced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I covered my last Triple Crown race, the Kentucky Derby, three years ago. Eight Belles, only the 39th filly to run the race, nearly beat the heavily favored Big Brown. Shortly after crossing the finish line, Eight Belles collapsed and was euthanized, marking one of the saddest days in Triple Crown history.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing Should Care for Its Own', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Racing Industry Should Care For Its Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T01:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f90cc019-5d19-52b7-89c2-779e7cbb0293', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f90cc019-5d19-52b7-89c2-779e7cbb0293'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the Mets’ off-field turbulence and a raft of injuries, Terry Collins is leading a young group that is walking and talking like a winner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/sports/baseball/mets-manager-collins-having-a-surprisingly-good-time.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the Mets’ off-field turbulence and a raft of injuries, Terry Collins is leading a young group that is walking and talking like a winner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terry Collins doesn’t kid himself, or anyone else within 60 feet 6 inches of him. He would rather have a healthy team than the Mets’ M*A*S*H unit. He would prefer to be working with a Steinbrenner payroll as opposed to an organization burdened with Wilpon legal expenditures. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Description of Managing Mets Adds an Unlikely Word: Fun', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Job Description of Managing Mets Adds an Unlikely Word: Fun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T01:25:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b112d4-09b8-5316-815f-380fe02fe467', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b112d4-09b8-5316-815f-380fe02fe467'}, {'abstract': 'China’s management of grants and its hostility toward grass-roots organizations in public health issues has drawn a rebuke from a global fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/world/asia/21china.html', 