None, 'print_headline': 'Gas Prices and Political Pandering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T02:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a8a18c-b77b-557d-8e49-bcf163d6ca32', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a8a18c-b77b-557d-8e49-bcf163d6ca32'}, {'abstract': 'The Guardian Council has ruled that President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad overstepped his authority by assuming control of the Oil Ministry when he fired the oil minister a week ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/world/middleeast/21briefs-Iran.html', 'snippet': 'The Guardian Council has ruled that President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad overstepped his authority by assuming control of the Oil Ministry when he fired the oil minister a week ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Guardian Council, Iran’s top legal panel, has ruled that President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad overstepped his authority by assuming control of the Oil Ministry when he fired the oil minister a week ago, the state-run Fars news agency reported Friday. The report casts doubt on whether Mr. Ahmadinejad will be able to lead the OPEC meeting in Vienna next month, and suggests a further deterioration of his relationship with Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, the country’s supreme leader. The Guardian Council is partly appointed by the ayatollah. The council has not confirmed the report, which said that the president’s appointment of himself as acting oil minister was unconstitutional. Last month, Mr. Ahmadinejad tried to dismiss the intelligence chief, but was reversed by Ayatollah Khamenei. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Panel Rules President Overreached, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | MIDDLE EAST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Panel Rules President Overreached, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guardian Council (Iran)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T02:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/138b8352-800a-5614-8c2c-47fe677faeae', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/138b8352-800a-5614-8c2c-47fe677faeae'}, {'abstract': 'Nonohitters.com chronicles nearly 50 years of Mets baseball in which none of the team’s pitchers has thrown a no-hitter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/sports/baseball/a-mets-web-site-about-nothing.html', 'snippet': 'Nonohitters.com chronicles nearly 50 years of Mets baseball in which none of the team’s pitchers has thrown a no-hitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dirk Lammers was in Paris 