D, Pakistan — At least 15 people were killed when a damaged oil tanker carrying fuel for NATO forces in Afghanistan exploded Saturday in the northwestern tribal region, government officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/sub-22pakistan/sub-22pakistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/world/sub-22pakistan/sub-22pakistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/sub-22pakistan/sub-22pakistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/sub-22pakistan/sub-22pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/world/sub-22pakistan/sub-22pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Truck Explosion Kills at Least 15 in Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oil Truck Explosion Kills at Least 15 in Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T11:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea3f4d8d-cf44-5bac-8c46-6257a3f57755', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea3f4d8d-cf44-5bac-8c46-6257a3f57755'}, {'abstract': 'Halfway through the final season of “Friday Night Lights” on NBC, and questions abound. When will we see Tim Riggins again, and where will Julie Taylor end up?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/friday-night-lights-watch-turns-of-fortune/', 'snippet': 'Halfway through the final season of “Friday Night Lights” on NBC, and questions abound. When will we see Tim Riggins again, and where will Julie Taylor end up?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The episode up for discussion is called “Swerve,” alluding both to Julie’s self-imposed car accident and various other instances of changes of heart and turns of fortune. Unable to muster the stamina to return to college after her run-in with Derek’s wife last, week Julie decides that the way to bide more time at home is to ram her car into a mailbox near her parents’ house. Maybe I’d be a really weak and bad parent to a teenager, but I don’t think I would have tried to force Julie to go back to Burleson, which is after all, a fictitious college and one at a significant psychic remove from her dreams of a Northeastern educational experience. Coach Taylor being Coach Taylor, he wanted Julie to man up and face the mess. The whole point of the affair now seems to have been to stack the deck so in favor of Julie’s return home that the show could easily situate her back in Dillon. Perhaps it was too implausible that Julie would just go to Dillon Tech in the first place, so the writers dispatched her to a place where she implausibly made no friends and experienced not a second’s worth of intellectual fulfillment or genuine freshman pleasure.It was interesting to see Coach having the correct perception of Julie’s motives rather than Tami. It is coach who realizes that Julie must have crashed on purpose. Tami is a disbeliever. It was interesting to see the show cast Coach’s impotence — he can’t get Julie in the car and back to school because she refuses with every fiber of her being to go — against Vince’s father’s assertion of paternal authority. Vince is in trouble with his thug lender, and his father steps in and solves problems by beating the daylights out of the guy, hoping to make sure the guy never gets within a yard of Vince again. Will this work? It sure felt as if it would. I’d hate to see this come back to haunt Vince’s father, or worse, for Vince to take the moral high ground against his dad in response.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Friday Night Lights’ Watch: Turns of Fortune', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T12:26:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd832642-f0b5-52f1-8679-8664072d7fa2', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd832642-f0b5-52f1-8679-8664072d7fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Royal Delta rolled to a two-and-a-half-length victory in the $250,000 Black-Eyed Susan Stakes on Friday afternoon at Pimlico Race Course.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/black-eyed-susan-winner-pointed-toward-mother-goose/', 'snippet': 'Royal Delta rolled to a two-and-a-half-length victory in the $250,000 Black-Eyed Susan Stakes on Friday afternoon at Pimlico Race Course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Royal Delta rolled to a two-and-a-half-length victory in the $250,000 Black-Eyed Susan Stakes on Friday afternoon at Pimlico Race Course. Trained by the Hall of Famer Bill Mott, Royal Delta completed the one and one-eighth miles in 1:49 3/5 over a fast track. Buster’s Ready was second, followed by Hot Summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Black-Eyed Susan Winner Pointed Toward Mother Goose', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T12:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7822c3-b4ac-5b2c-8a87-b50a62687060', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7822c3-b4ac-5b2c-8a87-b50a62687060'}, {'abstract': 'Answers about the Twins’ fall; small-market payrolls versus big-market payrolls; Jason Bay; and the Yankees’ lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/answers-to-readers-baseball-questions-part-3/', 'snippet': 'Answers about the Twins’ fall; small-market payrolls versus big-market payrolls; Jason Bay; and the Yankees’ lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following are responses from Tyler Kepner, David Waldstein and Ben Shpigel, The Times’s baseball writers, who took questions from readers this week about the Mets, the Yankees and the game over all through the first quarter of the 2011 season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Readers’ Baseball Questions, Part 3', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota Twins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T13:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e92bde4-606b-5ac4-b55b-b2b0ecfce8e9', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e92bde4-606b-5ac4-b55b-b2b0ecfce8e9'}, {'abstract': 'Red Bulls defender Tim Ream is waiting anxiously for the release of the U.S. roster for next month’s Concacaf Gold Cup. The roster will be announced on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/dreaming-of-the-gold-cup/', 'snippet': 'Red Bulls defender Tim Ream is waiting anxiously for the release of the U.S. roster for next month’s Concacaf Gold Cup. The roster will be announced on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Gold Cup roster set to be announced on Monday, I thought now would be a good to write about the pending roster and my experience with the national team, so far. Here goes it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreaming of the Gold Cup', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T13:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Ream', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ream', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aa88a80-c9b6-5e3f-8d84-5daef199a863', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aa88a80-c9b6-5e3f-8d84-5daef199a863'}, {'abstract': 'On the final day of the English Premier League season, two of the five struggling teams at the bottom of the standings will be relegated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/sports/soccer/as-manchester-united-raises-trophy-scramble-to-avoid-relegation-is-on.html', 'snippet': 'On the final day of the English Premier League season, two of the five struggling teams at the bottom of the standings will be relegated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before collecting the Premier League trophy on Sunday, Manchester United can end Blackpool’s brief stay in the top flight of English soccer.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Manchester United Savors Trophy, a Scramble to Avoid Relegation', 'kicker': 'Soccer Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Manchester United Savors Its Trophy, Scramble to Avoid Relegation Is On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T13:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c3e4bd5-15e7-5ac1-9143-555787a74a7f', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c3e4bd5-15e7-5ac1-9143-555787a74a7f'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Thompson has written eight books on youth sports, including the recent “Elevating Your Game: Becoming a Triple-Impact Competitor.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/sports/30-seconds-with-jim-thompson-youth-sports-expert.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Thompson has written eight books on youth sports, including the recent “Elevating Your Game: Becoming a Triple-Impact Competitor.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jim Thompson is founder of Positive Coaching Alliance, a national nonprofit formed to transform youth sports so sports can transform youth. He has written eight books on youth sports, including the recent “Elevating Your Game: Becoming a Triple-Impact Competitor,” one who commits to making oneself, one’s teammates and the game better by how one compete and lives. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/sports/seconds/seconds-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/sports/seconds/seconds-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/sports/seconds/seconds-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Jim Thompson', 'kicker': '30 Seconds With Jim Thompson', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Youth Sports, A Bigger Picture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T14:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/62505cd4-65fb-58aa-bc81-aade3b455d1b', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62505cd4-65fb-58aa-bc81-aade3b455d1b'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Webber scored pole position for the Spanish Grand Prix, his first pole of the year at his Red Bull team, while Sebastian Vettel finished second.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/webber-beats-vettel-to-pole-in-spain-but-kills-show-too/', 'snippet': 'Mark Webber scored pole position for the Spanish Grand Prix, his first pole of the year at his Red Bull team, while Sebastian Vettel finished second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be that qualifying sessions would be nail-biting competitions to the end. This season, the Red Bull cars are so much stronger than the other cars, and the new tires have to be preserved so much that qualifying suspense is starting to end several minutes before the session itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Webber Beats Vettel to Pole in Spain, but Kills Show Too', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T14:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c6ae02a-5389-5221-aa88-06579bf0a05f', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c6ae02a-5389-5221-aa88-06579bf0a05f'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Webber scored pole position for the Spanish Grand Prix, his first pole of the year at his Red Bull team, while Sebastian Vettel finished second.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/webber-beats-vettel-to-pole-in-spain-but-kills-show-too/', 'snippet': 'Mark Webber scored pole position for the Spanish Grand Prix, his first pole of the year at his Red Bull team, while Sebastian Vettel finished second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be that qualifying sessions would be nail-biting competitions to the end. This season, the Red Bull cars are so much stronger than the other cars, and the new tires have to be preserved so much that qualifying suspense is starting to end several minutes before the session itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Webber Beats Vettel to Pole in Spain, but Kills Show Too', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T14:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a618f6-617b-5939-8cb6-2af8f46ad31d', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a618f6-617b-5939-8cb6-2af8f46ad31d'}, {'abstract': 'Florida’s center fielder missed much of last season, hurting his knee while making a shaving-cream pie attack on a teammate. The Marlins no longer celebrate that way, but Coghlan tries to maintain the joy of playing.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/a-moment-of-celebration-and-months-of-recovery-for-coghlan/', 'snippet': 'Florida’s center fielder missed much of last season, hurting his knee while making a shaving-cream pie attack on a teammate. The Marlins no longer celebrate that way, but Coghlan tries to maintain the joy of playing.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:05 p.m. | Updated When the Florida Marlins have reason to celebrate, which happens often these days, center fielder Chris Coghlan knows his place: on the fringes of the throng, being careful, without a pie in his hands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Moment of Celebration, and Months of Recovery for Coghlan', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coghlan, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Marlins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T14:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d15f7c8-0947-58f3-8b9f-9e7381be1334', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d15f7c8-0947-58f3-8b9f-9e7381be1334'}, {'abstract': 'Fueling the demonstrators’ anger is the perceived failure by politicians to alleviate the hardships imposed on a struggling population by a jobless rate of 21 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/world/europe/22spain.html', 'snippet': 'Fueling the demonstrators’ anger is the perceived failure by politicians to alleviate the hardships imposed on a struggling population by a jobless rate of 21 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Tens of thousands of demonstrators across Spain continued sit-ins and other protests against the established political parties on Saturday. They did so in defiance of a ban against such protests and ahead of regional and municipal elections on Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/22spain/22spain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/world/22spain/22spain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/22spain/22spain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/22spain/22spain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/world/22spain/22spain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Ban, Protests Continue Before Spanish Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Ban, Protests Continue Before Spanish Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'P