own to Pimlico Race Course.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/animal-kingdoms-arrival-standard-procedure/', 'snippet': 'Animal Kingdom left his barn at the Fair Hill Training Center at 5:20 this morning for his 70-minute ride down to Pimlico Race Course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Animal Kingdom left his barn at the Fair Hill Training Center at 5:20 this morning for his 70-minute ride down to Pimlico Race Course. He was the only horse in his van, although his trainer, Graham Motion, has a number of other horses in the races at Pimlico this afternoon. They were in a second Cooper Transportation horse van. The vans were joined by a one-car police escort, and a truck behind that in which I was a passenger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Animal Kingdom’s Arrival: Standard Procedure', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T18:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3714cd19-40fe-56a8-8ec7-c911e369fd5b', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3714cd19-40fe-56a8-8ec7-c911e369fd5b'}, {'abstract': 'May 21 brings the trifecta of the Preakness Stakes, Kegasus and the rapture.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/21/the-morning-line-musings-on-the-preakness/', 'snippet': 'May 21 brings the trifecta of the Preakness Stakes, Kegasus and the rapture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'May 21 brings the trifecta of the Preakness Stakes, Kegasus and the rapture. Using the numbers of Harold Camping, the head of the Family Radio network, Rob Kasper at The Baltimore Sun forecasts the 10 horse Dialed In to win with the No. 5 horse Shackleford to place.This 5-10 box exacta (known as the Woolworth to longtime racing fans), Kasper said, “is a bit of a long shot — but then again, so it seems is our continued existence.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: Musings on the Preakness', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T18:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a65115c2-1a94-5fb1-84ef-8fdb2f7f2074', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a65115c2-1a94-5fb1-84ef-8fdb2f7f2074'}, {'abstract': 'For the roughly 20,000 Arabs of the Druze religious sect who live in the Israeli-controlled Golan Heights, this is Syrian territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/world/middleeast/22golan.html', 'snippet': 'For the roughly 20,000 Arabs of the Druze religious sect who live in the Israeli-controlled Golan Heights, this is Syrian territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAJDAL SHAMS, Golan Heights — Until the Internet came to this Druze village in the Israeli-controlled Golan Heights in late 1990s, residents used to go to an area known as the shouting hill and use megaphones to communicate with relatives across the fence in the motherland, Syria. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2