ting plan of a fellow Republican, Representative Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/weekinreview/22fighting.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich, a presidential aspirant, spent much of last week explaining his comments on the deficit-cutting plan of a fellow Republican, Representative Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich, a newly announced presidential aspirant, spent much of last week explaining comments widely interpreted as an attack on the long-term deficit-cutting plan of a fellow Republican, Representative Paul Ryan of Wisconsin, to whom Mr. Gingrich later apologized.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/weekinreview/22fightingimg/22fightingimg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/weekinreview/22fightingimg/22fightingimg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fighting Words', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-21T21:26:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'WeekInReview', 'section_name': 'Week in Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f088c704-ffa7-5a67-9978-399b4963ea3a', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f088c704-ffa7-5a67-9978-399b4963ea3a'}, {'abstract': 'The fates of eight American men are a haunting piece of unfinished business that the military will leave behind when it withdraws by the end of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/22/world/middleeast/22missing.html', 'snippet': 'The fates of eight American men are a haunting piece of unfinished business that the military will leave behind when it withdraws by the end of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — The last Americans missing in Iraq followed disparate paths to an uncertain fate. They arrived from Indiana and North Carolina, Chicago and Denver. They came out of a sense of duty, in search of a paycheck, or hoping to reclaim a homeland they had fled decades earlier. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/MISSING/MISSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/22/world/MISSING/MISSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/MISSING/MISSING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/22/world/MISSING/MISSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/22/world/MISSING/MISSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Withdrawal Looming, Trails Grow Cold for Americans Missing in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Withdrawal Looming, Trails Grow Cold for Americans Missing in Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'