 Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/07990814-6aa4-5fd7-9e83-7bc7e9c69bd4', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07990814-6aa4-5fd7-9e83-7bc7e9c69bd4'}, {'abstract': 'The attack comes a day after a bomber infiltrated a Kabul hospital and killed at least six medical students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan.html', 'snippet': 'The attack comes a day after a bomber infiltrated a Kabul hospital and killed at least six medical students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Insurgents wearing police uniforms and vests laced with explosives stormed a police compound in eastern Afghanistan early Sunday morning, engaging in a firefight that lasted several hours before Afghan and NATO forces regained control of the complex, government officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan/23afghan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan/23afghan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan/23afghan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan/23afghan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/23/world/asia/23afghan/2