er golfers and told them I had a ball that wouldn’t slice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Tread on Golfers’ Right to Hit Ball Poorly', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Polara Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T00:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/07922b84-536d-52b0-a490-5d0bbd32557a', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07922b84-536d-52b0-a490-5d0bbd32557a'}, {'abstract': 'After a trial in absentia, the harshest sentence to date as Egypt’s new government seeks to punish wrongdoing by the previous one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/world/middleeast/23egypt.html', 'snippet': 'After a trial in absentia, the harshest sentence to date as Egypt’s new government seeks to punish wrongdoing by the previous one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A Cairo court sentenced a rank-and-file police officer to death after trying him in absentia for the killings of unarmed protesters during the Egyptian revolution, the harshest sentence given to date as the military-led interim government grapples with calls for retribution against members of the former government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Egypt, Police Officer Is Sentenced to Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Egypt, Police Officer Is Sentenced To Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'su