r.html', 'snippet': 'Personalized information filters pose a threat to democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONCE upon a time, the story goes, we lived in a broadcast society. In that dusty pre-Internet age, the tools for sharing information weren’t widely available. If you wanted to share your thoughts with the masses, you had to own a printing press or a chunk of the airwaves, or have access to someone who did. Controlling the flow of information was an elite class of editors, producers and media moguls who decided what people would see and hear about the world. They were the Gatekeepers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Internet Thinks It Knows You', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Internet Thinks It Knows You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T01:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eli Pariser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eli', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pariser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/749c1b12-8111-5702-87a9-b79c85ec9dba', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/749c1b12-8111-5702-87a9-b79c85ec9dba'}, {'abstract': 'The suit, filed by a rights group, was based on Cisco sales materials. Cisco said there was “no basis” for the claims and that it would “vigorously” defend itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/technology/23cisco.html', 'snippet': 'The suit, filed by a rights group, was based on Cisco sales materials. Cisco said there was “no basis” for the claims and that it would “vigorously” defend itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Cisco, the maker of Internet routing gear, customized its technology to help China track members of the Falun Gong spiritual movement, according to a federal lawsuit filed last week by members of the movement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suit Claims Cisco Helped China Pursue Falun Gong', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suit Claims Cisco Helped China Pursue Falun Gong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Falun Gong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T01:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1afcfe7c-4290-5158-a132-d8654a39d91c', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1afcfe7c-4290-5158-a132-d8654a39d91c'}, {'abstract': 'A politically driven filibuster of a sound judicial nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/opinion/23mon2.html', 'snippet': 'A politically driven filibuster of a sound judicial nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I will not vote to deny a vote to a Democratic president’s judicial nominee just because the nominee may have views more liberal than mine.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Faith', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaking Faith: A politically driven filibuster of a sound judicial nominee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, Goodwin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T01:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/afba9a3b-ab55-54e9-95b5-f812b14e8310', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afba9a3b-ab55-54e9-95b5-f812b14e8310'}, {'abstract': 'A study shows that early treatment of H.I.V. curbs the risk of transmitting it to the uninfected partner by 96 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/opinion/23mon3.html', 'snippet': 'A study shows that early treatment of H.I.V. curbs the risk of transmitting it to the uninfected partner by 96 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The discovery of a near-perfect way to halt sexual transmission of the AIDS virus has the potential to change the way international agencies and nations cope with the epidemic. But that can only happen if troubling issues of cost and practicality can be surmounted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Treatment Is Also Prevention', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Treatment Is Also Prevention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T01:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab8a8a24-b823-5469-93b2-717ae7a14ec9', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab8a8a24-b823-5469-93b2-717ae7a14ec9'}, {'abstract': 'The budget debate belies belief in a common American purpose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/opinion/23mon4.html', 'snippet': 'The budget debate belies belief in a common American purpose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama trusts America’s generous and compassionate nature, that our rugged individualism is tempered by a belief that we’re all connected. In his speech on budget reform on April 13, he celebrated “our belief that those who benefited most from our way of life can afford to give back a little bit more.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Budget Without Core Purposes, Taxation Without Compassion', 'kicker': 'Editorial Observer ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Budget Without Core Purposes, Taxation Without Compassion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject