n', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirshbaum, Laurence J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T12:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/92ec2ae7-1da5-56ca-aac2-059095ab65e2', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92ec2ae7-1da5-56ca-aac2-059095ab65e2'}, {'abstract': 'Major indexes fell sharply, following declines in Asia and Europe, after a ratings agency lowered its outlook on Italy’s debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/business/24markets.html', 'snippet': 'Major indexes fell sharply, following declines in Asia and Europe, after a ratings agency lowered its outlook on Italy’s debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sovereign debt concerns and the prospects for slower growth in Europe and Asia took their toll on global markets on Monday, with stocks on Wall Street spiraling more than 1 percent lower on all three major indexes. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Stocks Tumble as Concern Over Europe’s Debt Crisis Heightens', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Shares Tumble on Worries Over European Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T12:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96769e26-a66d-52b9-80b2-47ce1ca995a5', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96769e26-a66d-52b9-80b2-47ce1ca995a5'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the New York City Ballet test out the Swiss luxury-house’s new shoes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/on-pointe-bally-rina-flats/', 'snippet': 'Members of the New York City Ballet test out the Swiss luxury-house’s new shoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who better to judge Bally’s new Bally-Rina collection than the real ballerinas of the New York City Ballet? The differences between the Swiss luxury-house’s flats and your run-of-the-mill ballet ones are vast according to the company’s senior corps de ballet dancers, Gretchen Smith and Marika Anderson. The women work in nude leather Bloch dance shoes both in the classroom and throughout rehearsals. And when they’re not dancing they still prefer to slip into flats. “I’m really picky when it comes to flats because I wear them to the bone,” says Anderson, who previously wore Cole Haan because of the Nike-Air instep. “We really like the Bally-Rina’s in blue,” says Smith pointing out the shoe’s ultra low vamp. Smith also likes that the sole of the shoe is comfortable and how the inside looks like an actual pointe shoe. This summer, the company heads for a slew of performances in Saratoga and both women see themselves wearing Bally-Rina flats, Smith with a flowy high-waisted skirt; Anderson with fitted jeans and a T-shirt. They’ll pair them with matching Bally-Rina bags stuffed with the tools of the trade: several pairs of pointe shoes, flat shoes, tape, scissors, glue, needles and thread, water and vitamin B. The cute but functional special Bally-Rina collection comes in shades of navy, grass green and yellow – that should be more than enough to keep more than New York City ballerinas dancing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballerinas, Meet Bally-Rina', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb46afa6-f181-5537-bcf2-9ac5d1ec6839', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb46afa6-f181-5537-bcf2-9ac5d1ec6839'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/morning-take-out-249/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grassley Investigates SAC Trades \xa0|\xa0 Senator Charles Grassley is taking a look at 20 trades by SAC Capital, DealBook reported over the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T13:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd88cfed-f400-501f-abae-d257c4a5130b', 'word_count': 2009, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd88cfed-f400-501f-abae-d257c4a5130b'}, {'abstract': 'Melanie Oudin is finally comfortable. Since the 2009 United State Open, where she was a spunky 17-year-old beating back a series of high-ranked Russians on the way to the quarterfinals, Oudin has carried the weight of follow-up expectations on her 5-foot-6 frame.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/oudin-19-is-taking-her-time/', 'snippet': 'Melanie Oudin is finally comfortable. Since the 2009 United State Open, where she was a spunky 17-year-old beating back a series of high-ranked Russians on the way to the quarterfinals, Oudin has carried the weight of follow-up expectations on her...', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Melanie Oudin is finally comfortable. Since the 2009 United States Open, where she was a spunky 17-year-old beating back a series of high-ranked Russians on the way to the quarterfinals, Oudin has carried the weight of follow-up expectations on her 5-foot-6 frame. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oudin, 19, Is Taking Her Time', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T13:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0cd93e-552e-5987-904b-f923b7bd29ea', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0cd93e-552e-5987-904b-f923b7bd29ea'}, {'abstract': 'Video from news crews and residents of Joplin, Mo. shows the impact of a deadly tornado that struck the city on Sunday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/video-shows-missouri-tornado-damage/', 'snippet': 'Video from news crews and residents of Joplin, Mo. shows the impact of a deadly tornado that struck the city on Sunday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 11:49 a.m. As my colleague A.G. Sulzberger reports, a swath of Joplin, Mo., “lay in ruins on Monday morning after a massive tornado, the latest storm to ravage the Midwest and South this spring, tore through the area, killing at least 90 people. Officials say they expect the death toll to climb.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Shows Missouri Tornado Damage', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T13:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/708ae06e-4315-56d7-b0c0-732d07f185b3', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708ae06e-4315-56d7-b0c0-732d07f185b3'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview from 1966, Mr. Dylan, then 24, talks about overcoming a heroin habit and shares some grim thoughts on death and what he calls “this suicidal thing.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/another-darker-side-of-bob-dylan-in-vintage-interview-tape/', 'snippet': 'In an interview from 1966, Mr. Dylan, then 24, talks about overcoming a heroin habit and shares some grim thoughts on death and what he calls “this suicidal thing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s hoping that the approach of his 70th birthday finds Bob Dylan in a better mood than the weeks preceding his 25th. In an interview from 1966, conducted by the critic and journalist Robert Shelton and recently posted by BBC News, Mr. Dylan, then 24, talks about having overcome a heroin habit and shares some grim thoughts on death and what he calls “this suicidal thing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another, Darker Side of Bob Dylan in Vintage Interview Tape', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T13:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa296f6-ea58-56b3-a19c-c4a1a0b6103f', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa296f6-ea58-56b3-a19c-c4a1a0b6103f'}, {'abstract': 'Photo: A young hawk touches its toes, or something like that.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/hawk-cam-rise-and-shine/', 'snippet': 'Photo: A young hawk touches its toes, or something like that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pip, stretching, Sunday, 1:55 p.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawk Cam | Rise and Shine', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '',