elers with \xa0a dose of extreme adventure starting this summer. The CN Tower is home to a new attraction called EdgeWalk, which will allow visitors to walk around the observation deck, 1,168 feet, or 116 stories, above ground. Guided groups of six to eight walkers (who must be 13 or older) will be attached by harness to an overhead safety rail that encircles the deck, absent of any hand rails.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the CN Tower in Toronto, Leaning Over a 116-Story Deck', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T17:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/0882c90f-7de6-543e-ac5a-640629db5c8a', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0882c90f-7de6-543e-ac5a-640629db5c8a'}, {'abstract': 'Fox News Channel executives are disputing a quotation made by an unnamed Republican in New York magazine saying that the network’s chairman, Roger Ailes, thinks former Gov. Sarah Palin of Alaska is “an idiot.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/fox-news-executives-say-ailes-not-critical-of-palin/', 'snippet': 'Fox News Channel executives are disputing a quotation made by an unnamed Republican in New York magazine saying that the network’s chairman, Roger Ailes, thinks former Gov. Sarah Palin of Alaska is “an idiot.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fox News Channel executives are disputing a quotation made by an unnamed Republican in the latest issue of New York magazine saying that the network’s chairman, Roger Ailes, 