wards season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEVERLY HILLS, Calif.— Very soon, the annual mailing of the official Oscar ballots — one of the goofier rituals in the annual Academy Awards cycle — will be a thing of the past. On Thursday, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, which presents the Oscars, sent a letter advising its 6,000 or so voting members that an electronic system for Oscar voting will be implemented “as early as this year, and will certainly be in effect by next year.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Electronic Voting Comes to The Oscars (Finally)', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T18:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dad7764-c764-5323-8e0c-b5a8aa8f6f1f', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dad7764-c764-5323-8e0c-b5a8aa8f6f1f'}, {'abstract': 'Vines are proliferating in tropical forests, threatening forests’ capacity as carbon sinks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/science/24vine.html', 'snippet': 'Vines are proliferating in tropical forests, threatening forests’ capacity as carbon sinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARRO COLORADO ISLAND, Panama — Stefan Schnitzer paused along one of the trails that crisscross this forested island in the Panama Canal waterway. Around him were trees, their high canopies muting the light from the tropical sun, the occasional woody vine, or liana, climbing up their thick trunks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/science/24vine2/24vine2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/science/24vine2/24vine2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/science/24vine2/24vine2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tree Hugger, With a Twist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tree Hugger, With a Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAZON JUNGLE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T18:55:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5db13f7-2a03-5ca2-b98b-491af01bb727', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5db13f7-2a03-5ca2-b98b-491af01bb727'}, {'abstract': '(Male) enthusiasm for television’s portrayal of su