y years before the museum opened in 1997. And despite the fact that, in garden years, 15 is relatively young, it feels very sure of itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Culturialist | Robert Irwin’s Garden Path', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T19:19:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc636186-2417-5431-be93-ec9478c281ab', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc636186-2417-5431-be93-ec9478c281ab'}, {'abstract': 'Since the earliest days of commercial aviation, airlines have depended on doctors who board planes as passengers to deal with in-flight medical emergencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/health/24doctors.html', 'snippet': 'Since the earliest days of commercial aviation, airlines have depended on doctors who board planes as passengers to deal with in-flight medical emergencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Matthew Rhoa is still haunted by one of his lowest moments as a physician. Several years ago, on the first leg of an international flight, he was just settling in for a nap when a flight attendant came on the public address system to ask, “Is there a doctor on the plane?”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/health/24doctors/24doctors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/health/24doctors/24doctors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/health/24doctors/24doctors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Doctors Are Called to the Rescue in Midflight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dr. Anyone, Summoned To Duty at 30,000 Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T19:24:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Hafner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hafner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa7703c-9830-57c6-afdb-647d58dd0eb1', 'word_count': 1473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa7703c-9830-57c6-afdb-647d58dd0eb1'}, {'abstract': 'People speak from a variety of perspectives about the impact of childhood cancer on their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/health/views/24voices.html', 'snippet': 'People speak from a variety of perspectives about the impact of childhood cancer on their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the advances that have been made against childhood cancer, it remains the leading cause of disease-related death among children younger than 15, with 1,500 fatalities a year. And while the five-year survival rate has improved in recent decades — to 80 percent, up from less than half 40 years ago — the number of cases is rising, too; it now stands at 10,000, up from 8,000 in 1975.', '