4205f8c176'}, {'abstract': 'Out with the Manhattan Cup fishing tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/fish-tales/', 'snippet': 'Out with the Manhattan Cup fishing tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Crescitelli, chairman of the Fishermen’s Conservation Association, is a garrulous Staten Islander with a booming voice and a sure hand on the wheel of his enormous fishing boat, which on Friday was bobbing peacefully on an ebb tide off the Breezy Point jetty, Midtown Manhattan rising in front of him in the mist. It was late morning, a few rainy hours into the Manhattan Cup, a catch-and-release fishing tournament that has been an annual competition in New York Harbor since at least 1999. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish Tales', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T19:51:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d66c4201-7407-59d7-8148-d7e8ac7419e6', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d66c4201-7407-59d7-8148-d7e8ac7419e6'}, {'abstract': 'A panel cites a tendency to dismiss customer complaints and a lack of a clear procedure for handling safety problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/business/global/24toyota.html', 'snippet': 'A panel cites a tendency to dismiss customer complaints and a lack of a clear procedure for handling safet