ill-lesson-2-agencies-team-up/', 'snippet': 'From now on, the Bureau of Ocean Energy Management will draw on NOAA’s expertise when making decisions on drilling permits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the lessons painfully learned from the Deepwater Horizon blowout and spill was that the federal officials responsible for regulating offshore drilling lacked adequate input from government agencies with expertise in shorelines, ocean science and toxic spills. One of the key recommendations of the presidential commission that studied the disaster was that federal agencies talk to each other about potential environmental hazards before granting permits to drill offshore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heeding an Oil-Spill Lesson, 2 Agencies Team Up', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bromwich, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lubchenco, Jane', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Commission on the BP Deepwater Horizon Oil Spill and Offshore Drilling', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T20:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d260900-2437-531e-8b1f-7d4c1730d06c', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d260900-2437-531e-8b1f-7d4c1730d06c'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Missouri, Iceland, Pakistan and Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/23/blogs/20110523POD.html', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Missouri, Iceland, Pakistan and Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Missouri, Iceland, Pakistan and Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/blogs/20110523POD-slide-KT0V/20110523POD-slide-KT0V-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/blogs/20110523POD-slide-KT0V/20110523POD-slide-KT0V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/23/blogs/20110523POD-slide-KT0V/20110523POD-slide-KT0V-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Missouri and Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T20:38:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/48afec32-1e33-5720-a5cd-f03e4487d2da', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/48afec32-1e33-5720-a5cd-f03e4487d2da'}, {'abstract': 'A suite of puzzles exploring tinkered variations on classic number and word ladders.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/numberplay-tinkering-with-ladders/', 'snippet': 'A suite of puzzles exploring tinkered variations on classic number and word ladders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s Numberplay puzzle, presented by Gary Antonick and suggested and masterfully moderated by Joshua Zucker, had all the hallmarks of a classic. This puzzle, known as the Ducci game or 4-number game, is easy to state and understand, uses a procedure a child can carry out, and yet it unlocks the door to fabulous mathematical riches. For those who missed it I would urge you to go back and take a look at it. Here is a brief restatement, given a slightly different visual model from last week. Given any four arbitrary positive integers a, b, c and d, representing the top rung of a ladder, you construct another step below it, consisting of the positive differences between them taken cyclically: |a-b|, |b-c|, |c-d| and |d-a|. An example 2-step ladder is:1 2 5 91 3 4 8It turns out that all such ladders eventually end as all the numbers become zeroes. One challenge was to find what initial numbers gave rise to the longest ladders, and it turned out that the champion quartets had a fascinating mathematical property.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Tinkering with Ladders', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ladders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T20:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c731c5b-134f-5ae6-83c9-b0d549728643', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c731c5b-134f-5ae6-83c9-b0d549728643'}, {'abstract': 'Two groups of researchers have come to different conclusions on how serotonin levels affect bone density and production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/health/research/24bone.html', 'snippet': 'Two groups of researchers have come to different conclusions on how serotonin levels affect bone density and production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, researchers at Columbia came to an astonishing conclusion. The amount of bone people make — and their risk of osteoporosis — seems to depend on levels of serotonin, a chemical known mainly for its effects on the brain. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Studies in Conflict on Growth of Bone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Studies In Conflict On Growth Of Bone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Osteoporosis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T20:44:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e372632e-ee56-562c-9135-6f3b3c1e759f', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e372632e-ee56-562c-9135-6f3b3c1e759f'}, {'abstract': 'Reader responses from the author’s recent piece on enlightened cafeteria cuisine.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.c