f_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f2d7a58-6f9d-5dc5-b111-0bf946342c28', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f2d7a58-6f9d-5dc5-b111-0bf946342c28'}, {'abstract': 'Karol Wight had replaced Marion True, the Getty curator who was put on trial by the Italian government.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/getty-curator-of-antiquities-is-leaving-for-corning-museum-of-glass/', 'snippet': 'Karol Wight had replaced Marion True, the Getty curator who was put on trial by the Italian government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The curator of antiquities at the J. Paul Getty Museum in Los Angeles announced on Monday that she was stepping down to take a job as the director of the Corning Museum of Glass in Corning, N.Y.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getty Curator of Antiquities Is Leaving for Corning Museum of Glass', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuno, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'True, Marion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corning Museum of Glass', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ceff2e5-8cb7-53d3-b785-6b39d8072a5f', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ceff2e5-8cb7-53d3-b785-6b39d8072a5f'}, {'abstract': 'In his recital at the Frick Collection, the violinist Thomas Zehetmair delivered highly personalized, philosophical readings of hefty works by Bach and Karl Amadeus Hartmann.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/arts/music/thomas-zehetmair-in-recital-at-frick-collection-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his recital at the Frick Collection, the violinist Thomas Zehetmair delivered highly personalized, philosophical readings of hefty works by Bach and Karl Amadeus Hartmann.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Austrian violinist Thomas Zehetmair has always been a deeply thoughtful player, and if he was sometimes an erratic interpreter in his early days, his highly personalized readings now sound philosophical rather than wayward. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/THOMAS/THOMAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/THOMAS/THOMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/THOMAS/THOMAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emotional Essays and a Soliloquy for the Violin', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emotional Essays and a Soliloquy for the Violin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frick Collection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zehetmair, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:02:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c1bb23a-bb96-522a-8c33-e0056ed0af43', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c1bb23a-bb96-522a-8c33-e0056ed0af43'}, {'abstract': 'Call for medical assistance on flights pose a singular challenge for physicians, who find themselves suddenly caring for a stranger whose history they don’t know, often with a problem well outside their specialty, in a setting with limited equipment but no shortage of onlookers scrutinizing their every move.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/is-there-a-doctor-on-the-plane/', 'snippet': 'Call for medical assistance on flights pose a singular challenge for physicians, who find themselves suddenly caring for a stranger whose history they don’t know, often with a problem well outside their specialty, in a setting with limited equipme...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In-flight emergencies are on the rise, but airlines still rely on the goodwill of doctors who happen to be passengers. As Katie Hafner writes in this week’s Science Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There a Doctor on the Plane?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9aa3a9e-e5be-5299-8c14-3ddc314978ca', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9aa3a9e-e5be-5299-8c14-3ddc314978ca'}, {'abstract': '“Sleeping Beauty Wakes,” a musical that sets the fairy tale in modern times, finds the heroine enamored of a hospital orderly with his own sleep problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/theater/reviews/sleeping-beauty-wakes-at-the-mccarter-theater-review.html', 'snippet': '“Sleeping Beauty Wakes,” a musical that sets the fairy tale in modern times, finds the heroine enamored of a hospital orderly with his own sleep problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRINCETON, N.J. — Chronic insomniacs may well view the heroine of “Sleeping Beauty Wakes,” a new musical at the McCarter Theater Center here, with a ravenous envy. She’s been dozing peacefully for almost a millennium, without so much as a milligram of pharmaceutical assistance. As in the original fairy tale, tweaked in this modern update, when she emerges from that long slumber she finds herself staring into the eyes of a love-struck swain, not groping for coffee to dispel the dim haze of an Ambien hangover.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/Sleeping/Sleeping-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/Sleeping/Sleeping-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/Sleeping/Sleeping-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/Sleeping/Sleeping-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/Sleeping/Sleeping-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fairy Tale, Updated Without Ambien', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Sleeping Beauty Wakes'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fairy Tale, Updated Without Ambien', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GrooveLily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheinkin, Rachel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McCarter Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taichman, Rebecca Bayla', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sleeping Beauty Wakes (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e43a6234-2a79-5f29-a127-b65346e6ad04', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e43a6234-2a79-5f29-a127-b65346e6ad04'}, {'abstract': 'Brian F. Madigan, who played a leading role in the Fed’s emergency lending programs during the financial crisis, will be a senior policy adviser at Barclays Capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/barclays-capital-hires-former-fed-official/', 'snippet': 'Brian F. Madigan, who played a leading role in the Fed’s emergency lending programs during the financial crisis, will be a senior policy adviser at Barclays Capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian F. Madigan, a former top official at the Federal Reserve who played a leading role in the emergency lending programs during the financial crisis, has joined Barclays Capital as a senior policy adviser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barclays Capital Hires Former Fed Official', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:13:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c6a9bf1-e00a-54e1-8ee5-9089a597df2c', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c6a9bf1-e00a-54e1-8ee5-9089a597df2c'}, {'abstract': 'Rakotondrabe performed recently at an intimate, invitational salon at the Brooklyn loft of Bianca Casady in an evening entitled “So Long Sorrow.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/notes-from-the-underground-gael-rakotondrabe/', 'snippet': 'Rakotondrabe performed recently at an intimate, invitational salon at the Brooklyn loft of Bianca Casady in an evening entitled “So Long Sorrow.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Best known as the pianist for the sister act CocoRosie, Gaël Rakotondrabe is also a renowned musician in his own right. And deservedly so. Rakondtrabe and Yasmine Hamdan performed recently at an intimate, invitational salon at the Brooklyn loft of Bianca Casady (one half of CocoRosie), in an evening entitled “So Long Sorrow.” Hamdan, dressed in strategically ripped acid wash jeans, and yellow wedge espadrilles, sang powerfully in Arabic, accompanied by Rakotondrabe’s remarkable keystrokes. The lights of the Manhattan skyline illuminated them from behind as Sierra Casady crouched on the floor beside the stage area, nodding her head in unison with the performers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes from the Underground | Gaël Rakotondrabe', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T21:19:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/49dbf048-f306-550a-9aea-72bd2155b50f', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49dbf048-f306-550a-9aea-72bd2155b50f'}, {'abstract': 'Two studies show that a person’s fitness level at midlife is a strong predictor of long-term heart health.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/on-your-marks-get-set-measure-heart-health/', 'snippet': 'Two studies show that a person’s fitness level at midlife is a strong predictor of long-term heart health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How fast can you run a mile?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Your Marks, Get Set, Measure Heart Health', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Your Marks, Get Set, Measure Heart Health', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exe