to be in communion with other worlds. Though she well may be the weakest technician among New York City Ballet’s female principals, she brings spiritual intensity to everything she does. On Friday night she made her debut as the Sleepwalker, the title role in “La Sonnambula,” George Balanchine’s ballet. The luminous, eerie, compulsive quality she brought to the role refreshed the whole drama. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/sub-nycb-1/sub-nycb-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/sub-nycb-1/sub-nycb-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/arts/sub-nycb-1/sub-nycb-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Season Brings New Faces and Insights to Classic Roles', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Season Brings New Faces and Insights to Classic Roles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Jerome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Janie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fairchild, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balanchine, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T22:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7ddfe21-408e-57de-8cb1-2bc2f55c3004', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7ddfe21-408e-57de-8cb1-2bc2f55c3004'}, {'abstract': 'The retailer’s employees are unhappy about low wages and short workweeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/business/economy/24target.html', 'snippet': 'The retailer’s employees are unhappy about low wages and short workweeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of big-box discounters, Target enjoys a reputation as a model corporate citizen that sells the latest in cheap chic. That’s a sharp contrast to the image of Wal-Mart, the world’s largest retailer, which labor unions have pilloried for years, accusing it of providing skimpy wages and benefits and skirting various labor laws.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/business/TARGET/TARGET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/business/TARGET/TARGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/business/TARGET/TARGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Effort Turns Its Focus to Target', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Union Struggle at Target', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target C