n.html', 'snippet': 'Irving H. Picard has asserted that most of the documents that were turned over were routine financial statements, almost all of which were peripheral to the substance of the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the points that the owners of the Mets have been most insistent about in their legal fight with the trustee for the victims of Bernard L. Madoff’s fraud has been their claim to have been completely forthcoming during the trustee’s investigation of their finances.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madoff Trustee and Mets Owners Differ on Issue of Cooperation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trustee and Mets Owners Differ on Cooperation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sterling Equities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi Schemes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Saul B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-23T23:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e298e22e-69f8-552f-954f-61abf64b05bb', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e298e22e-69f8-552f-954f-61abf64b05bb'}, {'abstract': 'The police made the first of what they said would be several arrests in connection with the attack outside Dodgers Stadium that left Bryan Stow, a San Francisco Giants fan in a coma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/sports/baseball/arrest-is-first-break-in-dodger-stadium-beating-case.html', 'snippet': 'The police made the first of what they said would be several arrests in connection with the attack outside Dodgers Stadium that left Bryan Stow, a San Francisco Giants fan in a coma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — For seven weeks after the opening day attack on a San Francisco Giants fan outside Dodger Stadium, as the victim languished in a coma, the police struggled to find a suspect. The brutal beating had been witnessed by dozens. Billboards displaying composite sketches of the two assailants offered a grim reminder of problems at the stadium. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/us/BEATING/BEATING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Arrest Signals a Break in a Stadium Beating Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Arrest Signals a Break In a Stadium Beating Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizat