ause-of-financial-problems.html', 'snippet': 'The board of directors voted to close Rice, a Roman Catholic boys’ high school, after it became clear that it could not attract enough students to make ends meet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rice High School, a Roman Catholic boys’ school in Harlem known equally for serious academics and excellent basketball players, announced on Monday that it would shut down at the end of the school year, after 73 years, because of financial difficulties. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catholic School in Harlem Is Closing Over Financial Woes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Catholic School in Harlem Is Closing Over Financial Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Brothers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RICE HIGH SCHOOL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T02:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0120276a-8cb4-5ca7-8dd8-ebfc6c0440e2', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0120276a-8cb4-5ca7-8dd8-ebfc6c0440e2'}, {'abstract': 'The United States attorney’s office in Manhattan has opened an investigation into whether the lack of wheelchair-accessible taxicabs in New York City violates the Americans with Disabilities Act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/nyregion/us-inquiry-into-wheelchair-access-in-new-york-taxis.html'