y.html', 'snippet': 'A police officer testifying in an unrelated drunken-driving trial offered a glimpse into a Bronx scandal, saying she once fixed tickets for her mother and boyfriend’s relative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Details of a ticket-fixing scandal involving Bronx police officers were spelled out for a jury on Monday, though they were revealed as part of an old, unrelated drunken-driving case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Testimony, an Officer Admits She Fixed Tickets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Testimony, an Officer Admits She Fixed Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Harrington', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T02:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2403cf94-045f-5d43-a795-71868cbd368d', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2403cf94-045f-5d43-a795-71868cbd368d'}, {'abstract': 'In a potentially disastrous decision, Chile approved construction of dams in a largely unspoiled natural haven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/opinion/24tue3.html', 'snippet': 'In a potentially disastrous decision, Chile approved construction of dams in a largely unspoiled natural haven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An environmental review commission in the Aysén region of southern Chile has made a potentially disastrous decision, voting to approve the construction of five hydroelectric dams, two on the Baker River and three on the Pascua. The damage these dams would do to the environment is tremendous, and their construction — in a largely unspoiled natural haven — would open the way for further development, including more dams. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep Chilean Patagonia Wild', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keep Chilean Patagonia Wild', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydroelectric Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T02:16:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4a5a045-a30a-5bbf-99c8-47388a4526c2', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4a5a045-a30a-5bbf-99c8-47388a4526c2'}, {'abstract': 'The Bulls, with their offense built around the scoring of Derrick Rose, will have trouble challenging the Heat without Rose at his best.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/23/bulls-plot-ways-to-turn-rose-loose/', 'snippet': 'The Bulls, with their offense built around the scoring of Derrick Rose, will have trouble challenging the Heat without Rose at his best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — To free himself of the Miami Heat’s swarming defense, Derrick Rose wants to be less crowded by his Chicago Bulls teammates. After poring over game film, Rose is hoping for more isolation plays that offer Miami less chance to double-team him Tuesday in Game 4 of the Eastern Conference finals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulls Plot Ways To Turn Rose Loose', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Derrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T02:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f79179c-9643-5187-8f26-9730702b220b', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f79179c-9643-5187-8f26-9730702b220b'}, {'abstract': 'In a bid to hold on to its majority in Nassau County, the Republican Party tried to hack away at the legislative map.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/opinion/24tue4.html', 'snippet': 'In a bid to hold on to its majority in Nassau County, the Republican Party tried to hack away at the legislative map.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Albany isn’t the only place where lawmakers are fighting to save a protected species, the ludicrous gerrymander. In Nassau County, the Republican Party has hacked away at the legislative map in a bid to keep its 11-to-8 majority by whatever squiggly lines necessary. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nassau’s Extremely Cynical Makeover', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nassau’s Extremely Cynical Makeover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n