uri': 'nyt://article/c879d008-2690-5e5f-8d7e-ebd389477f9e'}, {'abstract': 'In documenting refugees and displaced people worldwide, Espen Rasmussen found that the problem extended to his homeland, Norway.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/in-transit-to-a-home-that-isnt-there/', 'snippet': 'In documenting refugees and displaced people worldwide, Espen Rasmussen found that the problem extended to his homeland, Norway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rootless. Stateless. Homeless. Millions of people worldwide are in transit, a condition that has nothing to do with the morning commute and everything to do with intolerable conditions that drove them from their own homes and into perennial limbo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Transit to a Home That Isn’t There', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6ca19c-ae47-51fa-b942-ab560977d135', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6ca19c-ae47-51fa-b942-ab560977d135'}, {'abstract': 'Airlines canceled about 500 European flights as the ash cloud from the Grimsvotn volcano in Iceland drifted into northern Britain and Ireland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/world/europe/25volcano.html', 'snippet': 'Airlines canceled about 500 European flights as the ash cloud from the Grimsvotn volcano in Iceland drifted into northern Britain and Ireland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Airlines canceled about 500 European flights on Tuesday as the ash cloud from the Grimsvotn volcano in Iceland drifted into northern Britain and Ireland, but a senior European official predicted that the disruption would not reach the scale of a year ago, when millions of travelers were inconvenienced. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/25volcano_cnd/25volcano_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/world/25volcano_cnd/25volcano_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/25volcano_cnd/25volcano_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/25volcano_cnd/25volcano_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/world/25volcano_cnd/25volcano_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Volcanic Ash Forces Flight Cancellations in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Volcanic Ash Forces Flight Cancellations in Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T09:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbca3ecc-0c2f-533a-8e81-c407cd857875', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbca3ecc-0c2f-533a-8e81-c407cd857875'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, the Raiders had one of the best run games in the N.F.L. Problem is, they were handcuffed in the passing game.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/2010-raiders-what-the-film-revealed/', 'snippet': 'Yes, the Raiders had one of the best run games in the N.F.L. Problem is, they were handcuffed in the passing game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While we wonder whether there will be a 2011 season, this is part of a series looking back at the 2010 season, with the benefit of film analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2010 Raiders: What the Film Revealed', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c95cee8-37f1-5bde-af65-34565a42a09e', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c95cee8-37f1-5bde-af65-34565a42a09e'}, {'abstract': 'This past weekend marked the unofficial start of the Woodward Avenue cruising season in Detroit, when enthusiasts rouse their classic cars from hibernation.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/pollen-and-exhaust-fumes-return-to-woodward-avenue/', 'snippet': 'This past weekend marked the unofficial start of the Woodward Avenue cruising season in Detroit, when enthusiasts rouse their classic cars from hibernation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 1955 Chevrolet Bel Air convertible was purchased a dozen years ago in California. It sleeps in the garage all winter, but when the weather turns, I wake it up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pollen and Exhaust Fumes Return to Woodward Avenue', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T10:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0232d4-e9f6-5d3f-bac4-147f32b7441d', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0232d4-e9f6-5d3f-bac4-147f32b7441d'}, {'abstract': 'The Democrat in a hotly contested congressional race can’t vote for herself, or anyone on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/as-contested-district-votes-a-candidate-cant/', 'snippet': 'The Democrat in a hotly contested congressional race can’t vote for herself, or anyone on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is the closing ritual of campaigns: a candidate emerging from behind a polling booth curtain and giving the thumbs-up sign to photographers as they snap away. But there will be no such moment Tuesday for Kathy Hochul, the Democratic candidate in a nationally watched election in a Congressional district in western New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Contested District Votes, a Candidate Can’t', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corwin, Jane L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eddaf35-f4b0-5a9b-8a6a-51cd5b3b6558', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eddaf35-f4b0-5a9b-8a6a-51cd5b3b6558'}, {'abstract': 'Offering a wide assortment of stage acts, from physical theater, comedy and cabaret to spoken word and puppetry, the Prague Fringe Festival takes over the city’s tony Little Quarter for a nine-day run, starting May 27.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/prague-fringe-festival-celebrates-10-years/', 'snippet': 'Offering a wide assortment of stage acts, from physical theater, comedy and cabaret to spoken word and puppetry, the Prague Fringe Festival takes over the city’s tony Little Quarter for a nine-day run, starting May 27.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last decade, the Prague Fringe Festival has evolved into one of Central Europe’s hottest tickets. Offering a wide assortment of stage acts, from physical theater, comedy and cabaret to spoken word and puppetry, the festival takes over the city’s tony Little Quarter for a nine-day run, starting May 27. Celebrating its 10th anniversary, the Prague Fringe is one of the few annual city events dedicated solely to English-language performing arts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prague Fringe Festival Celebrates 10 Years', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T10:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By Julie O'Shea", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shea", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7411fe1-358e-56c7-8ead-dab2d06848bb', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7411fe1-358e-56c7-8ead-dab2d06848bb'}, {'abstract': 'Those who would like to institute a national sales tax, eliminate all existing federal taxes and shut down the Internal Revenue Service have a kindred spirit in the Republican presidential field, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/is-the-fair-tax-herman-cains-ace-in-the-hole/', 'snippet': 'Those who would like to institute a national sales tax, eliminate all existing federal taxes and shut down the Internal Revenue Service have a kindred spirit in the Republican presidential field, an economist writes.', 'lead_pa