t': 'A local New Zealand fire department said two people working on the film had been treated at the scene and taken in an ambulance to a hospital, but a publicist for the film said it was a “slight overstatement” to say an explosion had occurred.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/two-people-are-hospitalized-after-explosion-on-hobbit-film/', 'snippet': 'A local New Zealand fire department said two people working on the film had been treated at the scene and taken in an ambulance to a hospital, but a publicist for the film said it was a “slight overstatement” to say an explosion had occurred.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An explosion on the set of Peter Jackson‘s film version of “The Hobbit” is the latest bout of bad luck to befall the project, though a publicist for the movie said no one had been seriously injured in the incident. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 People Are Hospitalized After ‘Explosion’ on ‘Hobbit’ Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Toro, Guillermo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sydney Morning Herald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wellington (New Zealand)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T13:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2be8369-7e56-5e22-9ce5-6408be700bcb', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2be8369-7e56-5e22-