aragraph': 'Pink is back. Reversing the food safety dictates of decades, the United States Department of Agriculture has announced it is no longer necessary to cook meat (except ground meat) to an internal temperature of 160 degrees. The new magic number for pork chops and other cuts is a much juicier 145 degrees, plus a three minute resting time. This allows the internal temperature to rise slightly, but also has the culinary benefit of thickening the juices so they don’t run out when the meat is cut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pink Pork Safe to Eat, Government Says', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T16:46:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d2d6f4-f6e0-5847-88c6-d1149e7a1c81', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d2d6f4-f6e0-5847-88c6-d1149e7a1c81'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors are trying to force James Risen to testify at a trial about who leaked information to him about a C.I.A. effort to sabotage Iran’s nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/us/25subpoena.html', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors are trying to force James Risen to testify at a trial about who leaked information to him about a C.I.A. effort to sabotage Iran’s nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the approval of Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., federal prosecutors are trying to force the author of a book on the C.I.A. to testify at a criminal trial about who leaked information to him about the agency’s effort to sabotage the Iranian nuclear program at the end of the Clinton administration. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subpoena Issued to Writer in C.I.A.-Iran Leak Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subpoena Issued to Writer In C.I.A.-Iran Leak Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subpoenas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News Sources, Confidential Status of', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T16:53:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9574a7c0-71e7-5e78-a989-6464ac2e9259', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9574a7c0-71e7-5e78-a989-6464ac2e9259'}, {'abstract': 'One of our clients, the Austin Humane Society, recently agreed to a campaign that tries a different approach.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/finding-the-nerve-to-take-an-advertising-risk/', 'snippet': 'One of our clients, the Austin Humane Society, recently agreed to a campaign that tries a different approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the hardest things to do in business is to take a risk with your advertising. I’ve made ad campaign presentations to fiercely competitive, Type A owners and here’s what happens:', 'source':