xes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T17:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a02455b-fde6-5619-9156-b7007d4c92dd', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a02455b-fde6-5619-9156-b7007d4c92dd'}, {'abstract': 'Many voters in the 26th Congressional district race mentioned the overhaul of Medicare passed by House Republicans last month as an important campaign issue.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/medicare-is-on-voters-minds-in-congressional-election/', 'snippet': 'Many voters in the 26th Congressional district race mentioned the overhaul of Medicare passed by House Republicans last month as an important campaign issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The special election in western New York State’s 26th Congressional District has focused on Medicare for weeks now, and as voters emerged from polling places on Tuesday, it remained the dominant topic of conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Is on Voters’ Minds in Congressional Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corwin, Jane L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T17:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9436b6b-2060-5517-a388-1059ff8b65af', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9436b6b-2060-5517-a388-1059ff8b65af'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Bob Bradley announced his United States roster for next month’s Gold Cup, but the promising defender Timmy Chandler was not on it.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/chandlers-gold-cup-absence-raises-concerns/', 'snippet': 'Coach Bob Bradley announced his United States roster for next month’s Gold Cup, but the promising defender Timmy Chandler was not on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one has sought Timmy Chandler’s long-form birth certificate (yet). Nürnberg’s swift young defender, the son of an American serviceman and a German woman, has spent his entire life and professional soccer career in Germany. In March, he pulled on the jersey of the United States national team for matches against Argentina and Paraguay. He was nothing short of impressive, the apparent heir apparent to right back Steve Cherundolo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chandler’s Gold Cup Absence Raises Concerns', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United State Soccer Federation', 'rank'