mer Financial Protection Bureau will be too powerful a regulator. But Elizabeth Warren argues that there are unprecedented checks on the bureau.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/warren-and-g-o-p-lawmakers-spar-over-bureaus-power/', 'snippet': 'G.O.P. lawmakers contend the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau will be too powerful a regulator. But Elizabeth Warren argues that there are unprecedented checks on the bureau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican lawmakers contend the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau will be able to exert too much power over Wall Street. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warren and Republicans Spar Over Bureau’s Power', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T19:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aa1f0a7-8cfb-55ad-8035-7d5808ee1d88', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aa1f0a7-8cfb-55ad-8035-7d5808ee1d88'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater has announced a replacement for the injured principal dancer Herman Cornejo.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/ivan-vasiliev-to-appear-with-american-ballet-theater/', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater has announced a replacement for the injured principal dancer Herman Cornejo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater has announced a replacement for the injured principal dancer Herman Cornejo. Ivan Vasiliev, a principal dancer with the Bolshoi Ballet, will appear with Ballet Theater as a guest artist for three performances during the company’s spring season, said Kevin McKenzie, the artistic director. Mr. Vasiliev will replace Mr. Cornejo, who withdrew from scheduled performances in “The Bright Stream” for the June 11 matinee and the evening of June 14. He will also replace Mr. Cornejo in the leading role of Franz in “Coppélia” on June 16.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivan Vasiliev to Appear With American Ballet Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornejo, Herman', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vasiliev, Ivan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T19:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebe4dddc-d324-5d79-8f8a-d48c0b5a8307', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebe4dddc-d324-5d79-8f8a-d48c0b5a8307'}, {'abstract': 'Ways to use the multimedia feature “Coming Out,” in which gay, lesbian, bisexual and transgender teenagers share their personal stories, for teaching and learning.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/on-coming-out-exploring-the-stories-of-gay-teenagers/', 'snippet': 'Ways to use the multimedia feature “Coming Out,” in which gay, lesbian, bisexual and transgender teenagers share their personal stories, for teaching and learning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month we’re experimenting with a new format in which we feature a multimedia project on NYTimes.com and provide questions and activity ideas for teaching and learning with it. Today, our third such experiment, uses an audio slide show feature. Please also check out the other two, on an interactive map and a photo slide show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Coming Out: Exploring the Stories of Gay Teenagers', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T19:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kavanagh and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/967ae0f4-053b-522b-b14b-cdb4abeb43bb', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/967ae0f4-053b-522b-b14b-cdb4abeb43bb'}, {'abstract': 'Under a settlement negotiated by the United States Attorney for the Eastern District of New York and announced on Monday, the Speed Art Museum in Louisville, Ky., will soon turn over the painting to the United States government, which will transfer it to Italian cultural authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/an-italian-painting-in-kentucky-headed-home/', 'snippet': 'Under a settlement negotiated by the United States Attorney for the Eastern District of New York and announced on Monday, the Speed Art Museum in Louisville, Ky., will soon turn over the painting to the United States government, which will transfe...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Small museums don’t often find themselves at the center of international investigations, but last year the Speed Art Museum in Louisville, Ky., did, when agents from the Department of Homeland Security tracked an altarpiece stolen in Italy in 1971 to the Speed’s store rooms. The piece, a triptych featuring a Madonna and child that may date from as long ago as the 14th century, was stolen from a villa in Goito, southwest of Verona; two years later, the museum bought it from Newhouse Galleries in New York for $38,000. Under a settlement negotiated by the United States Attorney for the Eastern District of New York and announced on Monday, the Speed will soon turn over the work to Homeland Security, which will transfer it to Italian cultural authorities. (The collector who had owned it in 1971 has since died, and the authorities will be responsible for determining who is now entitled to the work.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Italian Painting in Kentucky, Headed Home', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisville (Ky)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T19:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77aab9fd-c7b4-5c20-b416-51e2b1cf079f', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77aab9fd-c7b4-5c20-b416-51e2b1cf079f'}, {'abstract': 'Oprah Winfrey taped the final hour of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” in Chicago on Tuesday, 18 months after she decided to end her 25-year-old talk show and concentrate on OWN, her new cable channel.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/with-a-final-taping-a-daytime-talk-era-ends/', 'snippet': 'Oprah Winfrey taped the final hour of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” in Chicago on Tuesday, 18 months after she decided to end her 25-year-old talk show and concentrate on OWN, her new cable channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before a hand-picked audience of boisterous fans, Oprah Winfrey taped the final hour of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” in Chicago on Tuesday afternoon, effectively lowering the curtain on the nation’s most popular daytime talk program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With a Final Taping, a Daytime Talk Era Ends', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oprah Winfrey Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T19:31:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti