Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b2d3096-bf7d-52a0-8ac4-5625b351099c', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b2d3096-bf7d-52a0-8ac4-5625b351099c'}, {'abstract': 'Americans, even without Andy Roddick and the Williams sisters playing, are making a few waves at the French Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/there-are-americans-in-paris-still-playing-too/', 'snippet': 'Americans, even without Andy Roddick and the Williams sisters playing, are making a few waves at the French Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — For the American contingent, it was sure to be a little different at the French Open without Andy Roddick, and Serena and Venus Williams, all not playing because of with injuries. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There are Americans in Paris, Still Playing, Too', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:14:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d481a7bb-af23-58ed-9864-a1c1874f5269', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d481a7bb-af