imilar to Rickey Henderson, Don Mattingly and Dave Winfield of the 1980s Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As once-heralded New York baseball trios go, Carlos Beltran, Jose Reyes and David Wright were not the first to invoke their owner’s ire for their team’s failures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Wilpon’s Scapegoats vs. Steinbrenner’s', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delgado, Carlos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Rickey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattingly, Don', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinbrenner, George M 3d', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfield, Dave', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, David', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa9938ab-08ab-53a6-a5e0-7cfed7aefe52', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa9938ab-08ab-53a6-a5e0-7cfed7aefe52'}, {'abstract': '“Tuesday, After Christmas,” a Romanian film directed by Radu Muntean, tells the story of a married regular guy who is having an affair with his daughter’s dentist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/movies/tuesday-after-christmas-by-radu-muntean-from-romania.html', 'snippet': '“Tuesday, After Christmas,” a Romanian film directed by Radu Muntean, tells the story of a married regular guy who is having an affair with his daughter’s dentist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around 40, with a soft gut, rounded shoulders and graying hair, Paul (Mimi Branescu), the middle-class Romanian who appears in virtually every frame of Radu Muntean’s “Tuesday, After Christmas,” is probably 10 years past the peak of his handsomeness. But he still has some attractive qualities, among them a low-key sense of humor, a decent work ethic and an obliging, if sometimes brusque, demeanor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/jp-tuesday/jp-tuesday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 283, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/jp-tuesday/jp-tuesday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 283}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/jp-tuesday/jp-tuesday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/jp-tuesday/jp-tuesday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/jp-tuesday/jp-tuesday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Case of Romanian Realism: Regular Guy, With Wife and Girlfriend', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Tuesday, After Christmas'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Case of Romanian Realism: Regular Guy, With Wife and Girlfriend', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:25:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5706aa98-bc78-5424-8752-3b963966c1da', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5706aa98-bc78-5424-8752-3b963966c1da'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s two-day state visit includes some ceremony, and some serious business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/25/us/20110525_OBAMA_BIG.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s two-day state visit includes some ceremony, and some serious business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president’s two-day state visit includes some ceremony, and some serious business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/a60fc0f7-1502-5a6d-93af-1e2f754c7f7b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/a60fc0f7-1502-5a6d-93af-1e2f754c7f7b'}, {'abstract': 'Although an Iraqi Christian almost lost his life to gunmen apparently targeting Christians, he and his family have refused to leave Baghdad.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/an-iraqi-christian-stands-firm-with-his-muslim-neighbors/', 'snippet': 'Although an Iraqi Christian almost lost his life to gunmen apparently targeting Christians, he and his family have refused to leave Baghdad.', 'lead_paragraph': ' BAGHDAD — Over the past several months, Iraq’s dwindling Christian population has gotten even smaller.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Iraqi Christian Stands Firm With His Muslim Neighbors', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Omar Al-Jawoshy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Omar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Al-Jawoshy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/918c21e1-30de-5b41-b0d6-e278c86a7ddd', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/918c21e1-30de-5b41-b0d6-e278c86a7ddd'}, {'abstract': 'Alexander Melamid’s Art Healing Ministry opens on Wednesday in SoHo. Drop by, and let fine art ease your afflictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/arts/design/alexander-melamids-art-healing-ministry-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'Alexander Melamid’s Art Healing Ministry opens on Wednesday in SoHo. Drop by, and let fine art ease your afflictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian-born artist Alexander Melamid is by nature an ironist, so adept at serving as his own straight man that it’s hard to tell how seriously he means to be taken. He may not know himself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/JPMELAMID1/JPMELAMID1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/JPMELAMID1/JPMELAMID1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/JPMELAMID1/JPMELAMID1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/JPMELAMID1/JPMELAMID1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/JPMELAMID1/JPMELAMID1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Picasso Cure You?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can a Picasso Cure You?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melamid, Alexander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc466dec-029c-5c1e-979f-266c2618e8c9', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc466dec-029c-5c1e-979f-266c2618e8c9'}, {'abstract': 'Mickey Mouse beats Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg to the punch, tourism-wise, according to the mayor of Orlando.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/orlando-beats-n-y-c-to-50-million-visitor-mark/', 'snippet': 'Mickey Mouse beats Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg to the punch, tourism-wise, according to the mayor of Orlando.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as the stage appeared set for Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg to take bows for the achievement of one of his more audacious goals, he was upstaged on Tuesday by the mayor of the city that Mickey Mouse built.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orlando Beats N.Y.C. to 50 Million Visitors, Officials Say', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dyer, Buddy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orlando (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32a853f6-befa-5e3f-93cc-15c7281b76c0', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32a853f6-befa-5e3f-93cc-15c7281b76c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Whitney Museum of American Art held a groundbreaking ceremony Tuesday for its new building on Gansevoort Street that is scheduled to open in 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/whitney-breaks-ground-for-new-building/', 'snippet': 'The Whitney Museum of American Art held a groundbreaking ceremony Tuesday for its new building on Gansevoort Street that is scheduled to open in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whitney Breaks Ground for New Building', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onassis, Jacqueline Kennedy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piano, Renzo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinberg, Adam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitney, Gertrude Vanderbilt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Streb Extreme Action', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e76369a-5c42-5f23-8320-7dc61c47041f', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e76369a-5c42-5f23-8320-7dc61c47041f'}, {'abstract': 'T caught up with the director to talk about his latest project: a film about his father.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/mike-mills-o-beginners/', 'snippet': 'T caught up with the director to talk about his latest project: a film about his father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director Mike Mills is considered a jack-of-all-trades in the indie world (he’s directed music videos and designed album covers for bands like Sonic Youth, Air and the Beastie Boys). So it’s no surprise that his soon-to-be-released dramedy, “Beginners,” about a young man who learns that his father is gay and has terminal cancer, is more than just a film. “I seem to need to make a lot of stuff,” he jokingly says. Collateral material includes a book of sketches, aptly titled “Mike Mills: Drawings From the Film ‘Beginners,’ ” and some animated shorts to accompany them. T caught up with Mills to talk about “Beginners” and its never-ending possibilities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mike Mills on ‘Beginners’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yuri Chong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yuri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc489df2-3488-58ff-b71e-2b27d1b0370d', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc489df2-3488-58ff-b71e-2b27d1b0370d'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from England, Missouri, Afghanistan and Yemen.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/pictures-of-the-day-england-and-elsewhere-3/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from England, Missouri, Afghanistan and Yemen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from England, Missouri, Afghanistan and Yemen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: England and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T20:59:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38e27d08-2683-530a-b8ca-cba3fda9bd6e', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38e27d08-2683-530a-b8ca-cba3fda9bd6e'}, {'abstract': 'A panel chairman accused Elizabeth Warren, who is directing the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, of lying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/business/25consume.html', 'snippet': 'A panel chairman accused Elizabeth Warren, who is directing the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, of lying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A House committee hearing on Tuesday about the new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau disintegrated into heated accusations of lying, with the panel’s chairman accusing Elizabeth Warren of giving misleading testimony at a hearing in March and of making up facts about her agreement to testify this week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/business/25CONSUME/25CONSUME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/business/25CONSUME/25CONSUME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/business/25CONSUME/25CONSUME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/business/25CONSUME/25CONSUME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/business/25CONSUME/25CONSUME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Decorum Breaks Down at House Hearing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hearing Over a Consumer Bureau Descends Into Sharp Accusations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51f509b-818d-59ae-9d63-9682f163eed1', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51f509b-818d-59ae-9d63-9682f163eed1'}, {'abstract': 'Like other companies before it, Barnes & Noble is being pushed to complete a deal, even if it means losing potential value by selling itself now to a sole bidder.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/barnes-noble-caught-in-a-wall-st-whirlwind/', 'snippet': 'Like other companies before it, Barnes & Noble is being pushed to complete a deal, even if it means losing potential value by selling itself now to a sole bidder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Campbell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barnes & Noble Caught in a Wall St. Whirlwind', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Nook', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkle, Ronald W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malone, John C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riggio, Leonard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberty Media Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yucaipa Cos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83456584-c522-5460-b916-e3520e551a52', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83456584-c522-5460-b916-e3520e551a52'}, {'abstract': 'The string quartet Ethel performed at Merkin Concert Hall as part of the Tribeca New Music Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/arts/music/tribeca-new-music-festival-at-merkin-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The string quartet Ethel performed at Merkin Concert Hall as part of the Tribeca New Music Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New music is hardly scarce during the main part of the New York concert season, and spaces like Issue Project Room, Galapagos and the Tank specialize in it year round. But spring and summer are a virtually nonstop parade of festivals celebrating the experimental. Recent weeks have featured the MATA, Look & Listen and Keys to the Future festivals in rapid succession, and on Monday evening the Tribeca New Music Festival opened its 10th season with a tightly packed program performed by Ethel, the string quartet, and devoted almost entirely to premieres. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/SUB-FESTIVAL/SUB-FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 294, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/SUB-FESTIVAL/SUB-FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 294}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/SUB-FESTIVAL/SUB-FESTIVAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/SUB-FESTIVAL/SUB-FESTIVAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/SUB-FESTIVAL/SUB-FESTIVAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Electronics And Energy', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating Electronics And Energy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ethel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merkin Concert Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/64389ccf-015c-5479-afd7-ff9c29d0abc0', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64389ccf-015c-5479-afd7-ff9c29d0abc0'}, {'abstract': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/24/us/20110525_TORNADO.html', 'snippet': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/us/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/24/us/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/24/us/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3/20110525_TORNADO-slide-D3S3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding Out Hope in Missouri', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Joplin (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:09:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/cc8860b0-f0ea-582e-a781-ebe44870a66e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/cc8860b0-f0ea-582e-a781-ebe44870a66e'}, {'abstract': 'The Ottawa Bach Choir made its debut at the Weill Recital Hall on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/arts/music/ottawa-bach-choir-has-debut-at-weill-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Ottawa Bach Choir made its debut at the Weill Recital Hall on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not every musician’s Carnegie Hall debut takes place during a concert produced by Carnegie Hall. The institution’s in-house artistic administration is responsible for only a fraction of the events that take place there, admittedly including most of its starriest affairs. Still, an artistically successful debut not produced by Carnegie is no less remarkable or noteworthy an achievement — a point made by the Ottawa Bach Choir at Weill Recital Hall on Monday night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Visitors Lift Up Their Voices to Bach and More', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Visitors Lift Up Their Voices to Bach and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c76166-7170-5dd3-a079-31afaed242b3', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c76166-7170-5dd3-a079-31afaed242b3'}, {'abstract': 'Shanghai Stainless Product & Design Company in Brooklyn is among New York’s new breed of haute food-truck entrepreneurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/dining/fashioning-artistry-on-wheels-shanghai-stainless-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Shanghai Stainless Product & Design Company in Brooklyn is among New York’s new breed of haute food-truck entrepreneurs.', 'lead_paragraph': '“ALWAYS crazy here,” Ernie Wong was saying. It’s not just the constant ring-ring of the land lines. There’s the smash-bash of stainless steel resisting ball-peen hammers. The wheeeen of the polishers smoothing steel burrs. The shoooosss of the welding sparks. Not to mention Mr. Wong’s mother, Sylvia, schmoozing on the cellphone in Shanghainese while his father, Jimmy, issues production orders in Mandarin.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,