/2011/05/25/dining/recently-reviewed.html', 'snippet': 'Capsules of restaurants recently reviewed.', 'lead_paragraph': ' CHEF’S TABLE AT BROOKLYN FARE', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recently Reviewed', 'kicker': 'Recently Reviewed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CHEF’S TABLE AT BROOKLYN FARE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton, Julia Moskin and Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0add2ba-ee22-55e6-9e5b-d2279f84f47b', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0add2ba-ee22-55e6-9e5b-d2279f84f47b'}, {'abstract': 'The chef will run an al fresco taproom in a temporary park under the girders of the northern terminus of the High Line.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/tom-colicchio-to-open-the-lot-on-tap-and-curate-high-line-food-trucks/', 'snippet': 'The chef will run an al fresco taproom in a temporary park under the girders of the northern terminus of the High Line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a pop-up plaza in a vacant parking lot. It’s a food truck food court. It’s an al fresco taproom. It’s an art installation. It’s a community event space. And oh, yes — it’s a destination for hordes of future visitors to the High Line whose strolls northward on the elevated public promenade would otherwise have deposited them pretty much nowhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Colicchio to Open the Lot on Tap, and Curate High Line Food Trucks', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Line (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colicchio, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colicchio & Sons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a82149e-1d36-5da5-bf63-9a32b067066c', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a82149e-1d36-5da5-bf63-9a32b067066c'}, {'abstract': 'Elvis Costello is playing three shows at the Beacon Theater, inviting audience members to pick the songs by twirling a wheel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/arts/music/elvis-costello-at-the-beacon-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'Elvis Costello is playing three shows at the Beacon Theater, inviting audience members to pick the songs by twirling a wheel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elvis Costello came on as all jovial show business — carny barker, M.C. and musical attraction — on Monday at the Beacon Theater. It was part of a three-night stand there for his Spectacular Spinning Songbook tour with his longtime band, the Imposters. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/ELVIS/ELVIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/ELVIS/ELVIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/ELVIS/ELVIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Spin of the Musical Wheel', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Spin of the Musical Wheel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beacon Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costello, Elvis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3f4c1a-0a62-56fb-afca-8171e220f147', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3f4c1a-0a62-56fb-afca-8171e220f147'}, {'abstract': 'In “Paying for It,” Chester Brown, a Toronto cartoonist, delivers a comic-strip memoir of his life with prostitutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/books/paying-for-it-is-chester-browns-memoir-of-prostitutes.html', 'snippet': 'In “Paying for It,” Chester Brown, a Toronto cartoonist, delivers a comic-strip memoir of his life with prostitutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Book titles are a touchy subject for writers. It’s not rare to hear an author complain in private about one of his or hers, and ache to reach back in time to swap it for something else. A different title for a fizzled book might have meant a different life for it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/book-2/book-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/book-2/book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/arts/book-2/book-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Graphic Memoir That Earns the Designation', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Graphic Memoir That Earns the Designation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:25:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2291b66-e0f3-53ee-ab55-0e97e2c62255', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2291b66-e0f3-53ee-ab55-0e97e2c62255'}, {'abstract': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/24/us/20110525_TORNADO_GOBIG.html', 'snippet': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Joplin, Mo., rescue workers searched for survivors and victims in buildings leveled by the United States’ deadliest tornado in more than 60 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding Out Hope in Missouri', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tornadoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Joplin (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:26:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e959297d-7eb0-56ed-b39e-b16c4805c1d9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e959297d-7eb0-56ed-b39e-b16c4805c1d9'}, {'abstract': 'Premium increase for individual health-insurance plans will get greater scrutiny starting in September.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/wrestling-with-health-insurance-costs/', 'snippet': 'Premium increase for individual health-insurance plans will get greater scrutiny starting in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting Sept. 1, double-digit increases in health insurance premiums for individuals and small businesses will be subject to a review and possible rejection by state and federal officials. The change is part of the new Affordable Care Act, and is meant to make sure that premium increases are justified.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wrestling With Health Insurance Costs', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f67b3b46-264d-5171-8d8c-2de28c522bc7', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f67b3b46-264d-5171-8d8c-2de28c522bc7'}, {'abstract': 'As protesters filled Tahrir Square in Cairo this spring, one of them turned to  Alaa Al-Aswany and asked him to write a novel about the revolution. Moments later the protester was dead, killed by a sniper.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/egypts-literary-revolutionary/', 'snippet': 'As protesters filled Tahrir Square in Cairo this spring, one of them turned to  Alaa Al-Aswany and asked him to write a novel about the revolution. Moments later the protester was dead, killed by a sniper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As protesters filled Tahrir Square in Cairo this spring, one of them turned to Alaa Al Aswany and asked him to write a novel about the revolution. Moments later the protester was dead, killed by a sniper. This would be enough to throw any writer into the spotlight, except that Al Aswany didn’t need any help getting there. What made him a household name in Egypt was his first novel, “The Yacoubian Building.” It portrayed Egypt as a corrupt society, whose public mores were belied by private sins. Considered somewhat scandalous, it nonetheless became a bestseller in the Arab world and\xa0was even made into a feature film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Literary Revolutionary', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aswany, Alaa Al', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b364526f-cb5a-5fc2-ba58-388e5ba07b23', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b364526f-cb5a-5fc2-ba58-388e5ba07b23'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s campaign manager meets with Democratic donors who aligned with Hillary Rodham Clinton in 2008, a step toward merging two formidable fund-raising machines.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/obama-campaign-cultivates-clinton-donors/', 'snippet': 'The president’s campaign manager meets with Democratic donors who aligned with Hillary Rodham Clinton in 2008, a step toward merging two formidable fund-raising machines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s campaign manager, Jim Messina, met privately on Monday night with donors close to his erstwhile rival, Hillary Rodham Clinton, as the campaign sought to knit together and mobilize the Democratic fund-raising elite in advance of the 2012 election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'ma