 of Stuff We Like That Maybe You Won’t, I’d originally intended to recommend the poetry of Frederick Seidel, which I turn to habitually for a rush of dread and pleasure, until I realized it’s quite possible you will like it, or that you already do. Which is not to say Seidel is impossible to not-love: He has been called “crass, disturbing, a name-dropping, upmarket sinner”; he has also been called “America’s greatest living poet.” In fact, he was called both in the same article (specifically, the display text to the article), when Wyatt Mason profiled him for the Times magazine back in 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Frederick Seidel, Radiohead, the End of the World, Pink Floyd and Weeping Sugar', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1507d1c-989a-5a5b-811f-fc63b30ecd84', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1507d1c-989a-5a5b-811f-fc63b30ecd84'}, {'abstract': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad’s decision appeared to show a retreat in his struggle with Iran’s supreme leader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/world/middleeast/25opec.html', 'snippet': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad’s decision appeared to show a retreat in his struggle with Iran’s supreme leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad of Iran will not preside over — or even attend — next month’s OPEC meeting in Vienna as previously planned, Iran’s Foreign Ministry said Tuesday. The change in plan, reported late Monday in Iran’s state-run press, appeared to signify a retreat by the president in his power struggle with the nation’s supreme leader. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/OPEC/OPEC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/OPEC/OPEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/world/OPEC/OPEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ahmadinejad Backs Out of Key Role at OPEC', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ahmadinejad Backs Out Of Key Role at OPEC; Hand of Rival Is Seen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T21:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec4ce3bf-9c17-52dd-93f2-16b50b90f2fb', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec4ce3bf-9c17-52dd-93f2-16b50b90f2fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Agriculture on Tuesday dropped the safe cooking tem