 fresh to New York, when he set out for the Public Theater one snowy night in 1985 to see “The Normal Heart,” Larry Kramer’s play about the first years of AIDS. Watching the protagonist Ned Weeks — a blunt, opinionated gay man not unlike himself — Mr. Mantello understood his need to take action in the face of death and denial, he recalled recently. If others found “The Normal Heart” a statistics-laden screed, Mr. Mantello felt a visceral recognition that Molière and Sophocles had never triggered.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/MANTELLO-1/MANTELLO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/MANTELLO-1/MANTELLO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/MANTELLO-1/MANTELLO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Return to Acting That’s From the Heart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Return to Acting That’s From the Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantello, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:46:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Tony Awards', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05c61deb-2c25-566c-8b8c-869b47c732c0', 'word_count': 1627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05c61deb-2c25-566c-8b8c-869b47c732c0'}, {'abstract': 'The reliever, who has gotten off to a poor start in his first year in the Bronx, felt soreness after a throwing session.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/yankees-shut-down-soriano/', 'snippet': 'The reliever, who has gotten off to a poor start in his first year in the Bronx, felt soreness after a throwing session.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest of a series of disappointments in his first season with the Yankees, Rafael Soriano has been shut down after a throwing session in which he felt soreness in his arm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Shut Down Soriano', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soriano, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:46:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/679df6cd-0f23-53b4-a38c-0ec2305b09c8', 'word_count': 766, 'uri': 'nyt://article/679df6cd-0f23-53b4-a38c-0ec2305b09c8'}, {'abstract': 'The new rule is intended to encourage coaches to teach the proper technique to avoid the kind of hits to the head and neck area that the N.F.L. cracked down on last season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/sports/football/nfl-will-fine-teams-over-dangerous-hits.html', 'snippet': 'The new rule is intended to encourage coaches to teach the proper technique to avoid the kind of hits to the head and neck area that the N.F.L. cracked down on last season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — The N.F.L. will begin fining teams if their players are repeatedly disciplined by the league for improper hits. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Will Fine Teams Whose Players Are Punished Repeatedly for Improper Hits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teams Face Fines for Players Punished Repeatedly for Hits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3bb4c45-1b78-5c28-b385-893a2f6e5868', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3bb4c45-1b78-5c28-b385-893a2f6e5868'}, {'abstract': 'The admissions policies of elite colleges don’t matter just to high school seniors; they’re a matter of national interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/business/economy/25leonhardt.html', 'snippet': 'The admissions policies of elite colleges don’t matter just to high school seniors; they’re a matter of national interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last four presidents of the United States each attended a highly selective college. All nine Supreme Court justices did, too, as did the chief executives of General Electric (Dartmouth), Goldman Sachs (Harvard), Wal-Mart (Georgia Tech), Exxon Mobil (Texas) and Google (Michigan).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/leonhardt-75/leonhardt-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/leonhardt-75/leonhardt-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Colleges, Largely for the Elite', 'kicker': 'Economic Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Colleges, Largely For the Elite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marx, Anthony W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMHERST COLLEGE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:49:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a4b1c8f-e934-528a-8ca4-d8508ebdefa5', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a4b1c8f-e934-528a-8ca4-d8508ebdefa5'}, {'abstract': 'One reason that many colleges are admitting more low- and middle-income students is a big expansion of the Pell Grant program over the last four years.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/behind-the-rise-in-pell-grants/', 'snippet': 'One reason that many colleges are admitting more low- and middle-income students is a big expansion of the Pell Grant program over the last four years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column this week looks at Amherst College’s impressive recent track record of recruiting low- and middle-income students. Amherst now has a much higher share of Pell Grant recipients — who tend to come from the lower-half of the income distribution — than most other elite colleges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Rise in Pell Grants', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMHERST COLLEGE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8de8d16-3899-5bd4-9cf6-948fbc0ce05c', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8de8d16-3899-5bd4-9cf6-948fbc0ce05c'}, {'abstract': 'The first lady pleases both sides of the Atlantic with her fashion choices during the state visit to England.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/mrs-obamas-american-british-day/', 'snippet': 'The first lady pleases both sides of the Atlantic with her fashion choices during the state visit to England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michelle Obama seems to be pleasing both sides of the Atlantic with her fashion choices during the state visit to England. She arrived in the country on Tuesday morning dressed in a royal blue outfit by Preen, a British label. Later, at Buckingham Palace, she wore a dress by the American Barbara Tfank. She then changed into a purple dress by the London designer Roksanda Ilincic for a visit to 10 Downing Street. For a white-tie dinner at the palace on Tuesday night, the first lady chose a ruched ivory georgette gown by Tom Ford, an American who has his design offices in London, where he lives part of the year. The Ford number looks super on her — flattering neckline, perfect fit, just right for all the pomp.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mrs. Obama’s American-British Day', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:56:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2b6a035-3cc5-5ca0-b7db-21f306ca4459', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2b6a035-3cc5-5ca0-b7db-21f306ca4459'}, {'abstract': 'The defense secretary, who will retire next month, said he was making his “last major policy speech in Washington.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/world/middleeast/25military.html', 'snippet': 'The defense secretary, who will retire next month, said he was making his “last major policy speech in Washington.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Defense Secretary Robert M. Gates said on Tuesday that if some American troops remained in Iraq beyond the scheduled withdrawal of all United States forces by the end of the year, it would be reassuring to Persian Gulf countries, but not to Iran. “And that’s a good thing,” Mr. Gates said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gates Sees Iran as a Consideration for U.S. Troops in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gates Sees Iran as a Consideration for U.S. Troops in Iraq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadr, Moktada Al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T22:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c372de40-01da-58c2-adb5-3c3eafb70fa9', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c372de40-01da-58c2-adb5-3c3eafb70fa9'}, {'abstract': 'The team’s principal owner had made disparaging remarks about his star players and the team in general in the latest New Yorker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/sports/baseball/wilpon-apologizes-to-mets-for-comments.html', 'snippet': 'The team’s principal owner had made disparaging remarks about his star players and the team in general in the latest New Yorker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — With his public-relations campaign backfiring, Fred Wilpon, the Mets’ principal owner, apologized to Jose Reyes and Carlos Beltran via speaker phone in a cramped office in the clubhouse at Wrigley Field on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilpon Says He Is Sorry for Remarks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wilpon Says He Is Sorry For Remarks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltran, Carlos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T23:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e8d9af-99c8-50b0-8005-5216c7be260f', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94e8d9af-99c8-50b0-8005-5216c7be260f'}, {'abstract': 'A surprise appearance on Syrian state television by a man whose beating by government security forces was captured on video last month.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/24/syrian-abused-by-security-forces-appears-on-state-television/', 'snippet': 'A surprise appearance on Syrian state television by a man whose beating by government security forces was captured on video last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the hundreds of video clips posted online by Syrian activists in recent weeks, documenting protests and a brutal security crackdown, few are as arresting as this 75 seconds, apparently filmed last month in the village of Bayda, while members of the security forces hit and kicked a group of prisoners forced to lie face down on the pavement:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Beaten on Camera Appears on State Television', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL ARABIYA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T23:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b9c1c4a-ed70-52f4-a3fe-8e1916cfd903', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b9c1c4a-ed70-52f4-a3fe-8e1916cfd903'}, {'abstract': 'Some people who claim to be investigating whether the Jan. 8 shootings in Tucson were a government conspiracy have been confronting those injured in the attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/us/25tucson.html', 'snippet': 'Some people who claim to be investigating whether the Jan. 8 shootings in Tucson were a government conspiracy have been confronting those injured in the attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — Television images of the chaotic scene after the Jan. 8 shootings here do not convince them. Neither do the funerals for the deceased, the scars of the wounded or the federal prosecution of the man accused of being the gunman.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoax Site Distressing for Victims of Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoax Site Distressing For Victims Of Shooting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoaxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T23:23:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/902731ba-f590-5307-9506-2c755528fa2f', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/902731ba-f590-5307-9506-2c755528fa2f'}, {'abstract': 'People are grappling with what comes next in Puttaparthi after the death last month of Sri Sathya Sai Baba, who transformed this village into a small city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/world/asia/25guru.html', 'snippet': 'People are grappling with what comes next in Puttaparthi after the death last month of Sri Sathya Sai Baba, who transformed this village into a small city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PUTTAPARTHI, India — His face adorns the yellow motorized rickshaws zipping down the streets. Billboards bear his simple motto, “Love All, Serve All.” His portrait hangs in almost every shop: a tiny man with a gravity-defying crown of curly hair regarded by millions of worldwide devotees as a god.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/GURU/GURU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/world/GURU/GURU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/GURU/GURU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/world/GURU/GURU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/world/GURU/GURU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A God Is Dead, but It’s Business That May Suffer Most', 'kicker': 'Puttaparthi Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A God Is Dead, but It’s Business That May Suffer Most', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baba, Sai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-24T23:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'l