t', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T00:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6678bb07-e4c7-5e58-9b1c-ef8c3cab5d5e', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6678bb07-e4c7-5e58-9b1c-ef8c3cab5d5e'}, {'abstract': 'If Jo-Jo Reyes does not beat the Yankees on Wednesday, he will join Matt Keough of the 1978-79 Oakland Athletics as the only pitchers since 1923 to make 28 consecutive starts without a victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/sports/baseball/hapless-but-not-hopeless-blue-jays-jo-jo-reyes-carries-on.html', 'snippet': 'If Jo-Jo Reyes does not beat the Yankees on Wednesday, he will join Matt Keough of the 1978-79 Oakland Athletics as the only pitchers since 1923 to make 28 consecutive starts without a victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jo-Jo Reyes did everything he could. For seven innings last Sunday in Toronto, he shut out the Houston Astros and gave a 2-0 lead to the Blue Jays’ bullpen. At that point, the outcome was out of his control, and he could live with the result: a blown lead and another winless day.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/sports/baseball/losers/losers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/25/sports/