am Palace by their hostess, Queen Elizabeth herself. They got to meet and have an actual conversation with one of the few couples in the world even more famous than they are: Prince William and his wife, the Duchess of Cambridge (formerly known as Kate Middleton).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking in Some London Sights, the Obamas Display Skill at Official Travel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking In Some London Sights, the Obamas Display Skill at Official Travel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Gordon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T00:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db08d2b8-0ddb-5ec9-9dfd-b6da7c17c7a8', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db08d2b8-0ddb-5ec9-9dfd-b6da7c17c7a8'}, {'abstract': 'Born in Belarus three years after the Chernobyl nuclear disaster, Yan Leyfman is preparing to graduate from Stony Brook University and working toward curing cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/nyregion/chernobyl-radiation-victim-at-stony-brook-sets-cancer-cure-as-goal.html', 'snippet': 'Born in Belarus three years after the Chernobyl nuclear disaster, Yan Leyfman is preparing to graduate from Stony Brook University and working toward curing cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STONY BROOK, N.Y. — Yan Leyfman was born in Belarus in 1989, three years after the Chernobyl nuclear disaster. His family lived only about 75 miles from the nuclear plant, and as a toddler, Mr. Leyfman had a constellation of mysterious symptoms: cysts that covered his entire body, fingernails that fell out, limbs that were swollen and skin that itched torturously.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/nyregion/CHERNOBYL/CHERNOBYL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/nyregion/CHERNOBYL/CHERNOBYL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/nyregion/CHERNOBYL/CHERNOBYL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chernobyl Behind Him, Student Takes on Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chernobyl Behind Him, a Student Takes On Cancer Cells', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chernobyl (Ukraine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York at Stony Brook', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Re