, NASA Gives Up on Spirit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T06:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3344689-455d-5f5a-8762-1335e88c4c70', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3344689-455d-5f5a-8762-1335e88c4c70'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will visit Puerto Rico on June 14, the first official visit by a sitting president since John F. Kennedy stopped there, in 1961.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/us/politics/25brfs-OBAMAWILLVIS_BRF.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama will visit Puerto Rico on June 14, the first official visit by a sitting president since John F. Kennedy stopped there, in 1961.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama will visit Puerto Rico on June 14, the first official visit by a sitting president since John F. Kennedy stopped there, in 1961. “Since the beginning of my administration, we have been working in close collaboration with the president and his administration to make this historic visit a reality,” Gov. Luis Fortuno, of Puerto Rico, a Republican, said in announcing the trip. President Gerald R. Ford visited in 1976, but he was there as a member of the Group of Seven economic summit, not on an official presidential visit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Will Visit Puerto Ric