agining and revamping, even if it means turning Little Red Riding Hood into a very grown-up-looking Amanda Seyfried. Two new picture book retellings, “Rapunzel,” by Sarah Gibb (“The Tiara Club”), and “Twelve Dancing Princesses” by Brigette Barrager, take a gentler approach, bringing lovely, distinctive illustrations to highly sweetened variations on two Grimm’s classics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/books/review/25childrens-review-2/25childrens-review-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/25/books/review/25childrens-review-2/25childrens-review-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/25/books/review/25childrens-review-2/25childrens-review-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pretty Princesses, Not So Grimm', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T13:25:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/daab47d8-8b3d-5d58-95b2-756d11a29ae6', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daab47d8-8b3d-5d58-95b2-756d11a29ae6'}, {'abstract': 'The as-yet untitled film by Kathryn Bigelow and Mark Boal, to be released in the fourth quarter of 2012 by Columbia Pictures, will focus “on the black ops mission to capture or kill Osama bin Laden, which culminated in his death earlier this month during a high-stakes raid on his compound in Pakistan.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/bigelows-film-on-bin-laden-mission-is-planned-for-next-year/', 'snippet': 'The as-yet untitled film by Kathryn Bigelow and Mark Boal, to be released in the fourth quarter of 2012 by Columbia Pictures, will focus “on the black ops mission to capture or kill Osama bin Laden, which culminated in his death earlier this month...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Weeks after the United States operation that resulted in the killing of Osama bin Laden, the Columbia Pictures division of Sony Pictures Entertainment said it had acquired a new film project by Kathryn Bigelow, the Academy Award-winning director of “The Hurt Locker,” about that mission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bigelow’s Film on Bin Laden Mission Is Planned for Next Year', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T13:31:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b181dcf7-b29a-5b89-8e9b-67ab583da731', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b181dcf7-b29a-5b89-8e9b-67ab583da731'}, {'abstract': 'Stocks were helped by news of somewhat tighter fuel supplies, and Fitch said German banks had “manageable” risk on Greece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/business/26markets.html', 'snippet': 'Stocks were helped by news of somewhat tighter fuel suppl