 '_id': 'nyt://article/b89f1ae0-4707-5ec0-998d-0535cc94b2ac', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b89f1ae0-4707-5ec0-998d-0535cc94b2ac'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Will and her work.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/who-made-that-purple-heart/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Will and her work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1782, George Washington created the Badge of Military Merit to honor any enlisted American for, in Washington’s words, “any singularly meritorious action … not only instances of unusual gallantry, but also of extraordinary fidelity and essential service in any way.” Washington described the form of the honor as “the figure of a heart in purple cloth or silk, edged with narrow lace or binding.” Only a handful of people have been known to receive that high standing, all of which were awarded in 1783.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Purple Heart?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Purple Heart (Military Decoration)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T15:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Greenbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70dc24d2-add1-519b-a18e-368bc8ed7ade', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70dc24d2-add1-519b-a18e-368bc8ed7ade'}, {'abstract': 'The move heralds possible links between the institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/washington-national-opera-names-glimmerglass-chief-as-artistic-adviser/', 'snippet': 'The move heralds possible links between the institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francesca Zambello, a busy director of opera and theater and the artistic and executive director of the Glimmerglass Festival, has been appointed artistic adviser of the Washington National Opera – heralding a possible link between the institutions, officials said on Wednesday. The appointment is part of the Washington company’s reorganization as it merges with the Kennedy Center, which was a response to the Washington opera’s financial troubles. Plácido Domingo, the company’s general manager, is departing next month. Washington National Opera also announced that its chief operating officer, Michael L. Mael, had been named executive director. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington National Opera Names Glimmerglass Chief as Artistic Adviser', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domingo, Placido', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zambello, Francesca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glimmerglass Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Opera', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington National Opera', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cooperstown (NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T15:43:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77098c15-b15a-5098-89ae-d83db5c9a4d3', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77098c15-b15a-5098-89ae-d83db5c9a4d3'}, {'abstract': 'The Tony-nominated play, which stars Mark Rylance as the manly, mangy, quasi-magical trailer denizen Johnny “Rooster” Byron, will run at the Music Box Theater through Aug. 21.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/jerusalem-gets-four-week-extension-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'The Tony-nominated play, which stars Mark Rylance as the manly, mangy, quasi-magical trailer denizen Johnny “Rooster” Byron, will run at the Music Box Theater through Aug. 21.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Rylance had better have a healthy appetite for the concoction of milk and a raw egg that he consumes at the opening of “Jerusalem” eight shows a week, because he’s going to be swigging it down for an additional month: that Jez Butterworth play, in which Mr. Rylance stars as the manly, mangy, quasi-magical trailer denizen Johnny “Rooster” Byron, will extend its run at Broadway’s Music Box Theater by four weeks, press representatives for the production said on Wednesday. Its limited run will now end on Aug. 21, having previously been scheduled to conclude on July 24. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Jerusalem’ Gets Four-Week Extension on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T15:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By