, 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7fbc740-d6ee-5176-9b75-c3b6b2e3c720', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7fbc740-d6ee-5176-9b75-c3b6b2e3c720'}, {'abstract': 'News from upstate.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/buffalo-buffalo-buffalo-buffalo-buffalo-buffalo-buffalo-buffalo/', 'snippet': 'News from upstate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Steven Pinker points out, the above is a grammatical sentence. You have to posit that there’s a kind of buffalo called a Buffalo buffalo; what the sentence then asserts is that beast of this kind, if buffaloed – that is, intimidated – by fellow members of their species, go on to do the same to other co-speciesists. Buffalo buffalo that are buffaloed by Buffalo buffalo go on to buffalo Buffalo buffalo themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo Buffalo.', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T16:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5ae115d-3e47-5a50-afc2-7e06386ff863', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5ae115d-3e47-5a50-afc2-7e06386ff863'}, {'abstract': 'Experts answer questions on treating sinusitis.', 'web_url': 'https://consults.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/the-best-treatment-for-sinus-complaints/', 'snippet': 'Ex