 have been “that nerdy Jewish kid in high school who ran the A.V. club.” The columnist called me for a reaction, and I had to correct Ms. O’Donnell. Actually, I was the president of the Herpetology Society.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26GEEKS-1/z-JP-GEEKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26GEEKS-1/z-JP-GEEKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26GEEKS-1/z-JP-GEEKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Former Geek Offers Hope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Former Geek Offers Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Alexandra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f05d2dc-c8bb-527d-b751-00379f866d08', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f05d2dc-c8bb-527d-b751-00379f866d08'}, {'abstract': 'The crossover is one of the most lethal offensive moves in the N.B.A. Miami’s Dwyane Wade found inspiration for his version from players like Allen Iverson and Tim Hardaway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/basketball/100000000831937/the-crossover-on-display.html', 'snippet': 'The crossover is one of the most lethal offensive moves in the N.B.A. Miami’s Dwyane Wade found inspiration for his version from players like Allen Iverson and Tim Hardaway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The crossover is one of the most lethal offensive moves in the N.B.A. Miami’s Dwyane Wade found inspiration for his version from players like Allen Iverson and Tim Hardaway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/23/sports/video-crossover-nba/video-crossover-nba-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Crossover on Display', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iverson, Allen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hardaway, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'Bedel Saget|Xaquín G.V', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bedel', 'middlename': 'Saget', 'lastname': 'Xaquín', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f4423105-e3e6-5909-bed9-f9b2460b8c8d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f4423105-e3e6-5909-bed9-f9b2460b8c8d'}, {'abstract': 'Miami Coach Erik Spoelstra’s flexibility in using his lineup has been crucial to the Heat’s playoff success.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/miamis-fluid-rotation-pays-off/', 'snippet': 'Miami Coach Erik Spoelstra’s flexibility in using his lineup has been crucial to the Heat’s playoff success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a night, Mike Miller was a star. He converted from inside and out, initiated the fast break and racked up rebounds in Game 4. His influence on the court was just as significant as that of any player on the floor; despite sharing the court with the likes of LeBron James, Derrick Rose and Dwyane Wade, Miller posted the game’s highest plus-minus rating (plus-36), a testament to his impact. He did the little things and hit the big shots, and in a game with a razor-thin margin for error, it’s not hyperbolic to say that Miller’s 12 points and team-high nine rebounds made all the difference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami’s Fluid Rotation Pays Off', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spoelstra, Erik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7289f43a-4161-53fa-9b10-613a690791f3', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7289f43a-4161-53fa-9b10-613a690791f3'}, {'abstract': 'The Detroit Symphony Orchestra, struggling to find its feet after a bitter six-month strike, has suffered another loss.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/detroit-symphony-orchestra-concertmaster-is-leaving/', 'snippet': 'The Detroit Symphony Orchestra, struggling to find its feet after a bitter six-month strike, has suffered another loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Detroit Symphony Orchestra, struggling to find its feet after a bitter six-month strike, has suffered another loss. Its concertmaster of 23 years, Emmanuelle Boisvert, is moving to the Dallas Symphony Orchestra as an associate concertmaster. The announcement, which came on Wednesday, was made not by the Detroit Symphony but by a committee of orchestra members that was set up during the strike and sponsored their own concerts. The orchestra’s spokeswoman, Elizabeth Weigandt, confirmed the move and said Ms. Boisvert had told the players but not yet formally informed orchestra management. “Management has the news release, and that’s what we’ve got,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Symphony Orchestra Concertmaster Is Leaving', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b0e1b41-a750-5552-b557-e6bc1c0d45ec', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b0e1b41-a750-5552-b557-e6bc1c0d45ec'}, {'abstract': 'Veteran defenseman Brian Rafalski retired Wednesday, walking away from $6 million of guaranteed contract money. In the end, having fun and feeling healthy proved more important.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/rafalski-retires-pain-trumping-money/', 'snippet': 'Veteran defenseman Brian Rafalski retired Wednesday, walking away from $6 million of guaranteed contract money. In the end, having fun and feeling healthy proved more important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, Red Wings defenseman Brian Rafalski couldn’t deny the painful truth his body had been telling him all season. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rafalski Retires, Pain Trumping Money', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rafalski, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97270fd3-424f-5ccb-bffc-34bd699049eb', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97270fd3-424f-5ccb-bffc-34bd699049eb'}, {'abstract': 'Though his shots for the luxury brand’s Spirit of Ecstasy centennial celebration are not represented, a retrospective by the English fashion photographer Rankin is now on view in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/rolls-royce-photographer-channels-ecstasy-but-not-in-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'Though his shots for the luxury brand’s Spirit of Ecstasy centennial celebration are not represented, a retrospective by the English fashion photographer Rankin is now on view in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Milk Gallery in Manhattan’s meatpacking district on Tuesday night, hundreds of guests wandered among the photographs of a new show by Rankin, the British photographer of fashion, celebrities and titillating nudes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rolls-Royce Photographer Channels Ecstasy, but Not in Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34dec9e9-3370-5920-a74c-4c0c3a4e9a85', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34dec9e9-3370-5920-a74c-4c0c3a4e9a85'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: At a demonstration near the mayor’s house, protesters against marijuana arrests included a city councilwoman.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/east-79th-street-1026-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: At a demonstration near the mayor’s house, protesters against marijuana arrests included a city councilwoman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'City Councilwoman Melissa Mark-Viverito, left, joined protesters against the city’s marijuana arrest policies at demonstration half a block from the mayor’s house. More people were arrested in New York City on marijuana possession charges last year than in the entire period from 1978 to 1996. The arrests cost $75 million and disproportionately involve blacks and Hispanics, advocates say. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'East 79th Street, 10:26 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T18:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c6ec6a-cbd6-52f6-9c28-5bad831a6834', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c6ec6a-cbd6-52f6-9c28-5bad831a6834'}, {'abstract': 'While some classical orchestras have folded or declared bankruptcy, others are coming up with alternative approaches to ensure their continued existence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/arts/music/survival-strategies-for-orchestras.html', 'snippet': 'While some classical orchestras have folded or declared bankruptcy, others are coming up with alternative approaches to ensure their continued existence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FROM the recent string of crises at symphony orchestras you might conclude that orchestral business models are as outdated as the musicians’ Victorian attire. The Philadelphia Orchestra filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy in April; the Honolulu Symphony and the Syracuse Symphony Orchestra recently folded; and musicians of the Detroit Symphony had their pay cut after a six-month strike. In a turbulent economy that has carried a wide range of organizations, including arts groups, banks and newspapers, to the brink, orchestras are being forced to re-examine their missions and structures to accommodate a changing fiscal and social landscape.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/CITY-1/CITY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/CITY-1/CITY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': No