snippet': 'Keeping logs to record sleep patterns and analyzing those patterns to discover opportunities for improving sleep habits, then writing proposals to the school district about related policies like school start times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | How much sleep does the average teenager need? How do the natural sleep rhythms of most adolescents sometimes conflict with the typical high school schedule? In this lesson, students explore their own sleep habits by keeping sleep logs. They look for patterns in the data they collect, explore current research on adolescent sleep needs and make suggestions to their local school boards regarding sleep and school schedules. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Rest for the Weary? Analyzing Sleep Habits', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T19:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4568d384-605d-5c1e-b76c-bd2b525b8b6e', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4568d384-605d-5c1e-b76c-bd2b525b8b6e'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Haines, an anchor at CNBC who for years narrated the vicissitudes of the markets, died on Tuesday evening, the network said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/20