ts will try to address the fiscal problems without touching the elderly or the middle class, while the Republicans will focus on tax revenue. No matter how you slice the issue, it’s voodoo policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David, this is going to be our last conversation until after Labor Day. I’m already nostalgic — we’ve been doing this for almost three years to the day, and this will be our first real break. I’ve been remembering all our fun times — like how plucky you were about finding ways to communicate during severe power outages — which, I must point out, seem to follow you around the country. And the night the Republicans won the Ted Kennedy Senate seat and I carried on my half of the conversation by e-mail while curled up in a fetal position under a hotel bed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does It All Come Down to Medicare?', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T19:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article