5d5fd5-51cc-5972-8b05-e871a564a9ba', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/975d5fd5-51cc-5972-8b05-e871a564a9ba'}, {'abstract': 'In addition to $200 million in new Race to the Top grants, all states can compete for an $500 million for early learning initiatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/education/26early.html', 'snippet': 'In addition to $200 million in new Race to the Top grants, all states can compete for an $500 million for early learning initiatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nine states that were also-rans in last year’s Race to the Top school improvement competition will get another chance, the Obama administration announced on Wednesday, though this time $200 million will be up for grabs, compared with $4 billion awarded last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '9 States Get New Chance at Federal Education Aid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '9 States Get New Chance At Federal Education Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T19:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dillon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e6f0beb-95f7-57e8-9b5a-31a52492d3b8', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e6f0beb-95f7-57e8-9b5a-31a52492d3b8'}, {'abstract': 'Two of the company’s top executives spoke about the criticism levied against them and the challenges of doing business during the economic crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/business/smallbusiness/26sbiz.html', 'snippet': 'Two of the company’s top executives spoke about the criticism levied against them and the challenges of doing business during the economic crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in the darkest days of the economic crisis, few people had anything good to say about the nation’s biggest banks, least of all small-business owners. The big banks took federal bailout money, if in some cases reluctantly, and then faced accusations of being stingy with all of that capital. Even some business owners with longstanding banking relationships reported difficulty getting new loans. Others claimed their banks had dropped them altogether.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/26sbiz/26sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/26sbiz/26sbiz-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/business/26sbiz/26sbiz-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wells Fargo Bankers Answer Criticism of Lending Practices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wells Fargo Bankers Answer Criticism Of Lending Practices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T19:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fe9662a-13a7-59aa-9388-ef38d2f30499', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fe9662a-13a7-59aa-9388-ef38d2f30499'}, {'abstract': 'A filmmaker who loves food finds the right character.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/jon-shook-in-fish-a-new-short-film-by-r-j-cutler/', 'snippet': 'A filmmaker who loves food finds the right character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'R. J. Cutler is a documentary film director who on another blog would be introduced as the guy who made “The September Issue,” about Anna Wintour and Vogue. Here at Diner’s Journal, however, Mr. Cutler is known as a food maniac — a restaurant enthusiast and scratch cook who is always game for a late dinner reservation in whatever city he visits, and who has a wood-burning pizza oven in his outdoor kitchen at his home high in the hills of Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Shook in ‘Fish,’ a Film By R. J. Cutler', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T19:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2d5825d-38eb-5941-8ba5-a23852c23ebe', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2d5825d-38eb-5941-8ba5-a23852c23ebe'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Sharapova’s competitive nature goes beyond the tennis court as she fights for turf among athletes who aspire to be brands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/fashion/maria-sharapovas-campaign-to-establish-herself-as-a-brand.html', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova’s competitive nature goes beyond the tennis court as she fights for turf among athletes who aspire to be brands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Maria Sharapova won her first grand slam title in 2004, at age 17, she made the cover of Sports Illustrated. The issue showed Ms. Sharapova at the moment she became a household name, proudly beaming on court at Wimbledon in a body-skimming white tank dress from Nike. “Star Power,” the headline read.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26maria-span/26maria-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26maria-span/26maria-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 6