nsumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Kathleen L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khuzami, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paredes, Troy A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T20:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c03cbc17-57b1-58b1-bacd-1cdf1261c999', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c03cbc17-57b1-58b1-bacd-1cdf1261c999'}, {'abstract': 'A hearing is planned Thursday to ‘examine what actions (or inactions)’ led to the findings.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/house-bookkeeping-criticized-in-audit/', 'snippet': 'A hearing is planned Thursday to ‘examine what actions (or inactions)’ led to the findings.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The House had trouble keeping its own financial house in order in 2009, according to a memo sent Wednesday to members of the oversight subcommittee. The memo said an extensive audit had found deficiencies for the first time in 12 years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Bookkeeping Criticized in Audit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T20:04:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e507780-eb07-58c2-b7d2-ea34e8848f8e', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e507780-eb07-58c2-b7d2-ea34e8848f8e'}, {'abstract': 'The associate creative director of Dossier Journal provides his short list of exceptional photographers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/the-lowdown-alec-friedman/', 'snippet': 'The associate creative director of Dossier Journal provides his short list of exceptional photographers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alec Friedman has the hustler mentality of the native New Yorker that he is. He is most often contextualized by the work he does as the associate creative director of the uber-hip, twice-a-year glossy Dossier Journal. Friedman, who is constantly on the move, can be found at the chicest parties world round, including the photographer Tim Barber’s late night bash during Miami Basel (see above). The ultimate consultant, he is also one of the nicest guys in fashion and publishing, a soft-spoken example of how far a smile can go in a generally cutthroat universe. Brands have begun to tap him for his creative insight, not to mention his casting skills, asking him to nominate cool kids and artists for modeling gigs and video spots. Friedman himself is something of a style icon in the downtown creative scene, and appears regularly in the pages of magazines, and lately in subway entrances via the most recent Cole Haan campaign, along with the rest of the stylish Dossier staff. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lowdown | Alec Friedman', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name'