, the country’s authoritarian president, Aleksandr G. Lukashenko, indicated on Wednesday that he might free his imprisoned political rivals, a signal that he could be ready to strike a deal with Western governments in exchange for financial support.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus Leader May Trade Rivals’ Freedom for Aid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus Leader May Trade Rivals’ Freedom for Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T20:55:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2683217e-b6c7-5cbe-bddf-eacd5d18f359', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2683217e-b6c7-5cbe-bddf-eacd5d18f359'}, {'abstract': 'Yahoo’s chief executive stuck to a script when discussing negotiations over Alibaba’s transfer of Alipay, a Chinese online payment service.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/yahoos-bartz-holds-her-tongue-on-alibaba/', 'snippet': 'Yahoo’s chief executive stuck to a script when discussing negotiations over Alibaba’s transfer of Alipay, a Chinese online payment service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carol A. Bartz, Yahoo’s outspoken chief executive, was anything but on Wednesday while being questioned about her company’s dispute with Alibaba Group, the Chinese Internet giant that it partly owns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yahoo’s Bartz Holds Her Tongue on Alibaba', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartz, Carol A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALIBABA.COM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T20:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verne G. Kopytoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verne', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Kopytoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d24e810b-1a32-5e94-882f-da3895262bf2', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d24e810b-1a32-5e94-882f-da3895262bf2'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter announced Wednesday that it purchased TweetDeck, a popular third-party Twitter client available for mobile phones and desktop computers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/twitter-officially-acquires-tweetdeck-software/', 'snippet': 'Twitter announced Wednesday that it purchased TweetDeck, a popular third-party Twitter client available for mobile phones and desktop computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After days of speculation on technology blogs, Twitter officially announced Wednesday that it had agreed to acquire TweetDeck, a service that organizes Twitter feeds to make them more useful. According to people who had been briefed on the deal who were not authorized to speak publicly, Twitter agreed to pay about $40 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter Acquires TweetDeck Software', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline