...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s magazine, Susan Dominus writes about Tatiana and Krista Hogan, 4-year-old conjoined twins whose brains are linked by a neural bridge. It’s an incredible story that leads to all kinds of fascinating questions about empathy, consciousness and the nature of the self: If the girls share sensation, could they also share higher thoughts? Do they experience some kind of cross-talk in their brains that they are constantly having to filter out? Will their identities merge together over time or become more differentiated?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tatiana and Krista’s Special Connection', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dominus, Susan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Kern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1c7584a-61a3-5cd0-9599-401c524fb555', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1c7584a-61a3-5cd0-9599-401c524fb555'}, {'abstract': 'The program tries to get 38,000 system employees, from physicians to clerks, to ask more open ended, less judgmental questions of patients.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/for-public-hospital-employees-new-training-on-gay-patients/', 'snippet': 'The program tries to get 38,000 system employees, from physicians to clerks, to ask more open ended, less judgmental questions of patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A doctor asks a girl if she is using condoms, and a boy if he has a girlfriend. A woman has to fill out the usual medical forms, asking whether she needs birth control, and if she is married, single, divorced or widowed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Public Hospital Employees, New Training on Gay Patients', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Hospitals Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dd3734a-d8af-5400-886a-11fac17bde64', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dd3734a-d8af-5400-886a-11fac17bde64'}, {'abstract': 'A judge has approved a new home for Mr. Strauss-Kahn, whose temporary stay at 71 Broadway was not welcomed by neighbors.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/strauss-kahn-finds-new-home/', 'snippet': 'A judge has approved a new home for Mr. Strauss-Kahn, whose temporary stay at 71 Broadway was not welcomed by neighbors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 7:50 p.m. | Dominique Strauss-Kahn is about to be on the move again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strauss-Kahn Finds a New Home', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55b10665-1e55-5b73-b90b-0f4deb2ea804', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b10665-1e55-5b73-b90b-0f4deb2ea804'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Missouri, Libya, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/pictures-of-the-day-missouri-and-elsewhere-2/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Missouri, Libya, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Missouri, Libya, Afghanistan and Spain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Missouri and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b231f5-5078-56fc-92c3-0e12e4f2da1e', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b231f5-5078-56fc-92c3-0e12e4f2da1e'}, {'abstract': 'Apple computer users were targeted by fake antivirus software that hopes to gain access to users’ credit cards. Apple said Wednesday that it plans to issue a software update to remove the malware.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/apple-operating-system-targeted-by-malware/', 'snippet': 'Apple computer users were targeted by fake antivirus software that hopes to gain access to users’ credit cards. Apple said Wednesday that it plans to issue a software update to remove the malware.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years Apple Mac users have boasted about the lack of malware on their computers. In comparison, Microsoft Windows owners have\xa0regularly felt the brunt of viruses and malware that can easily debilitate an entire computer system in minutes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Operating System Affected by Malware', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Malware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e86a283-9407-5723-8caa-99cf2fe133f0', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e86a283-9407-5723-8caa-99cf2fe133f0'}, {'abstract': 'Before his death this month, Arthur Laurents gave his blessing to a new film version of “Gypsy,” possibly starring Barbra Streisand, and finished a full-length play and his third memoir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/theater/before-death-laurentss-was-working-on-new-gypsy-film.html', 'snippet': 'Before his death this month, Arthur Laurents gave his blessing to a new film version of “Gypsy,” possibly starring Barbra Streisand, and finished a full-length play and his third memoir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the month before his death, on May 5, the Tony Award-winning writer and director Arthur Laurents gave his blessing to a plan for a new film version of “Gypsy,” starring Barbra Streisand, and also finished a full-length play as well as his third memoir, Laurents’s agent and several associates said this week.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/LAURENTS/LAURENTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/LAURENTS/LAURENTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/07/arts/LAURENTS/LAURENTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laurents Left Book, Play and Plan for ‘Gypsy’ Film', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laurents Left Book, Play And Plan for ‘Gypsy’ Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laurents, Arthur', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T21:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c91faf9c-64c7-5e98-b2c4-ad5b3f8f1089', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c91faf9c-64c7-5e98-b2c4-ad5b3f8f1089'}, {'abstract': 'As workers moved from farms and factories to desks over the last half-century, calories hav