organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/139397c5-4817-5bda-b58e-a30ce3ee2646', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/139397c5-4817-5bda-b58e-a30ce3ee2646'}, {'abstract': 'One of the many revelations in Alfred Kazin’s journals, published now for the first time, is the sense they impart of how ill at ease, how easily wounded, he was behind his bluff cosmopolitan mien.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/books/alfred-kazins-journals-review.html', 'snippet': 'One of the many revelations in Alfred Kazin’s journals, published now for the first time, is the sense they impart of how ill at ease, how easily wounded, he was behind his bluff cosmopolitan mien.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love my worldliness, my snobbery, my ease,” the great literary critic Alfred Kazin confided to his journal in 1959, when he was 43. He was at the apex of his powers as a writer and as a man. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/3dSUBBOOK/3dSUBBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/3dSUBBOOK/3dSUBBOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/3dSUBBOOK/3dSUBBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/3dSUBBOOK/3dSUBBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/3dSUBBOOK/3dSUBBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lifetime of Anxiety and Lust', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "In His Own Words, an Intellectual's Life of Anxiety and Lust", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Richard M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kazin, Alfred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:17:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e7f2635-5d69-5f7e-885f-ef2fc54fa0bc', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e7f2635-5d69-5f7e-885f-ef2fc54fa0bc'}, {'abstract': 'The soul singer Bettye LaVette puts her own heartfelt spin on songs by Ringo Starr, the Who, Elton John and others during her cabaret show at the Café Carlyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/arts/music/bettye-lavette-astounds-at-cafe-carlyle-review.html', 'snippet': 'The soul singer Bettye LaVette puts her own heartfelt spin on songs by Ringo Starr, the Who, Elton John and others during her cabaret show at the Café Carlyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To choose a song at random from the soul singer Bettye LaVette’s astounding two-hour show at the Café Carlyle on Tuesday evening, how about that jolly 1971 Ringo Starr singalong, “It Don’t Come Easy”? If you are like me, you probably never paid much attention to the lyrics of a number that’s catchy enough but no great shakes as a piece of songwriting. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/Lavette/Lavette-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 811, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/Lavette/Lavette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/Lavette/Lavette-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rock Songs Turned Testaments of Triumphant Soul', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rock Songs Turned Testaments of Triumphant Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaVette, Bettye', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:18:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d173c92-aefe-5463-a2d5-cc69303ae848', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d173c92-aefe-5463-a2d5-cc69303ae848'}, {'abstract': 'A modernist architect and designer who worked for Richard Meier and Peter Marino applies his approach to design to the cutlery he collects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/garden/modernist-flatware-shopping-with-s-russell-groves.html', 'snippet': 'A modernist architect and designer who worked for Richard Meier and Peter Marino applies his approach to design to the cutlery he collects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERYTHING about S. Russell Groves is just so, from his style of dress to his choice of words; nothing is superfluous. A modernist who worked for Richard Meier and Peter Marino before starting his own architecture and design firm in 1995, Mr. Groves does not seem like the sort of person who would amass anything in quantity.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26shop-span/26shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26shop-span/26shop-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26shop-span/Shop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26shop-span/26shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26shop-span/26shop-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spoons for Thinkers', 'kicker': 'Shopping With S. Russell Groves', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spoons for Thinkers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69e0c823-f85d-5703-bc4d-54189c567b59', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69e0c823-f85d-5703-bc4d-54189c567b59'}, {'abstract': '“4th and Forever” on Current TV looks at the football program at Long Beach Polytechnic High School in California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/arts/television/4th-and-forever-high-school-football-players-review.html', 'snippet': '“4th and Forever” on Current TV looks at the football program at Long Beach Polytechnic High School in California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long Beach Polytechnic High School in California is not much like the fictional East Dillon High of “Friday Night Lights” or even, for that matter, the wealthier rival Panthers across town with their championship victories. Poly, as the locals call it, exists in a realm unto its own: Sports Illustrated called it “sports school of the century.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/FOREVER/FOREVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/FOREVER/FOREVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/FOREVER/FOREVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/FOREVER/FOREVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/FOREVER/FOREVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard Times at a Factory of Legends', 'kicker': "Television Review | '4th and Forever'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard Times at a Factory of Legends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/26af859a-103a-5710-9101-35fe4e8d75bd', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26af859a-103a-5710-9101-35fe4e8d75bd'}, {'abstract': 'Our guide to where to eat, drink, shop and sweat in the Hamptons this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/fashion/the-hamptons-whats-new-this-season.html', 'snippet': 'Our guide to where to eat, drink, shop and sweat in the Hamptons this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IS it summer already? It certainly feels that way in the Hamptons, where a post-recession lift brings new places to dine, shop and, of course, party. Mercifully, the mood has shifted from the go-go 2000s. Instead of magnums of Cristal, it’s now about communal seaplanes, hipster charities, hippie festivals, Montauk and more Montauk. Our guide:', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26HAMPTONS-span/Z-HAMPTONS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26HAMPTONS-span/Z-HAMPTONS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26HAMPTONS-span/Z-HAMPTONS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26HAMPTONS-span/26HAMPTONS-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/fashion/26HAMPTONS-span/26HAMPTONS-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clouds Have Lifted, and the Hamptons Beckon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clouds Have Lifted, and the Hamptons Beckon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:21:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Chaplin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chaplin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e069ca6-7fee-5a61-a27b-c79256e0fe97', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e069ca6-7fee-5a61-a27b-c79256e0fe97'}, {'abstract': 'Teatro Grattacielo performed the verismo operas “I Compagnacci” and “Il Re” at the Rose Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/arts/music/teatro-grattacielo-brings-two-verismos-to-the-rose-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Teatro Grattacielo performed the verismo operas “I Compagnacci” and “Il Re” at the Rose Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Verismo operas were the reality television of their time. Dispensing with the typical operatic kings and gods, they featured recognizably ordinary characters experiencing way-larger-than-life emotions. Capped by generous helpings of sex and violence, these operas made it hard to look away.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/teatro/teatro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/teatro/teatro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/teatro/teatro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Melodramatic Sounds of Young Love', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Melodramatic Sounds of Young Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teatro Grattacielo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d59b45fa-1dca-5fd2-817e-e66eca355841', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d59b45fa-1dca-5fd2-817e-e66eca355841'}, {'abstract': 'The company, which previously disclosed that its initial public offering could raise more than $1 billion, raised just $783 million on Wednesday, reflecting weak demand from investors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/freescale-prices-its-i-p-o-at-18-a-share/', 'snippet': 'The company, which previously disclosed that its initial public offering could raise more than $1 billion, raised just $783 million on Wednesday, reflecting weak demand from investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It hardly seems possible in the current environment where investors are clamoring for newly public companies like LinkedIn and Yandex. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freescale Prices Its I.P.O. at $18 a Share', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackstone Group, The', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Freescale Semiconductor Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Permira Advisers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4758402-1c66-5473-880d-c52b51a7f661', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4758402-1c66-5473-880d-c52b51a7f661'}, {'abstract': 'Uprooting the bushes to take to a new home can be a difficult move.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/garden/moving-the-plants-to-your-next-home-in-the-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Uprooting the bushes to take to a new home can be a difficult move.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A BERRY bush may be nature’s answer to the gumball machine. There the thing stands, dispensing bits of cheer by the palmful. And a berry bush needs no coins; the currency is grab and go. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26garden-span/26garden-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26garden-span/26garden-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26garden-span/Garden-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26garden-span/26garden-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/garden/26garden-span/26garden-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m Moving. And the Plants?', 'kicker': 'In the Garden', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’m Moving. And the Plants?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moving and Moving Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tortorello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tortorello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83e61b12-1979-5145-83ad-37fe6bd18776', 'word_count': 1505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83e61b12-1979-5145-83ad-37fe6bd18776'}, {'abstract': 'Lady Gaga’s new album is likely to sell even better than expected.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/yet-again-adele-tops-the-charts/', 'snippet': 'Lady Gaga’s new album is likely to sell even better than expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The old news about the latest music sales: Adele is No. 1, yet again. The new news: Thanks to an aggressive marketing campaign and some apparently unsolicited promotion by Amazon, Lady Gaga is selling even better than expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yet Again, Adele Tops the Charts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:29:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22929211-dff7-5304-937e-4f376eab2a4a', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22929211-dff7-5304-937e-4f376eab2a4a'}, {'abstract': 'The revival, originally been aiming to open on Broadway in the summer of 2008, will be staged at Circle in the Square, with previews to begin on Oct. 13 and an opening night scheduled for Nov. 7.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/prepare-ye-the-way-of-the-lord-godspell-revival-coming-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'The revival, originally been aiming to open on Broadway in the summer of 2008, will be staged at Circle in the Square, with previews to begin on Oct. 13 and an opening night scheduled for Nov. 7.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Godspell,” the parable-driven musical based on the Gospel of Matthew that ran on various New York stages from 1971 to 1977, will be revived on Broadway for the first time this fall, the producers announced on Wednesday. The revival had originally been aiming to open on Broadway in the summer of 2008, but its financing plans did not come together, largely due to the approaching economic recession. The lead producer of the upcoming production, Ken Davenport, said on Wednesday that the musical would be staged at Broadway’s only in-the-round theater, Circle in the Square. Preview performances of the open-ended run are scheduled to begin on Oct. 13, with an opening night of Nov. 7.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "‘Prepare Ye the Way of the Lord': ‘Godspell’ Revival Coming to Broadway", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-25T22:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/204bee0a-760a-5589-81b4-892834b7251e', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/204bee0a-760a-5589-81b4-892834b7251e'}, {'abstract': 'In a team event, when one side gains a sizable swing, it is usually because one pair did something especially meritorious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/crosswords/bridge/two-overcalls-one-worked-one-didnt.html', 'snippet': 'In a team event, when one side gains a sizable 