ield.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scotty McCreery Wins ‘American Idol’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, MARC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennett, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarkson, Kelly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Simon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeWyze, Lee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edge, The', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Simon', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Randy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strait, George', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyler, Steven', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Underwood, Carrie', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'U2', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T00:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f73e2a1-75f1-5065-934a-808a3d8ae221', 'word_count': 1735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f73e2a1-75f1-5065-934a-808a3d8ae221'}, {'abstract': 'A fully renovated Victorian house on the Hudson sits atop a gentle slope in a hamlet that dates to the 1700s.;', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/25/realestate/20110527tour.html', 'snippet': 'A fully renovated Victorian house on the Hudson sits atop a gentle slope in a hamlet that dates to the 1700s.;', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fully renovated Victorian house on the Hudson sits atop a gentle slope in a hamlet that dates to the 1700s.;', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Tour: Cheviot, N.Y.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dutchess County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T00:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/455cd2a2-e9be-5e59-86ae-6d00af3767f1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/455cd2a2-e9be-5e59-86ae-6d00af3767f1'}, {'abstract': 'In a case that has galvanized a protest movement against the government’s campaign against drug traffickers, the authorities arrested a man believed to have ordered the murder of seven people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/world/americas/26briefs-Mexico.html', 'snippet': 'In a case that has galvanized a protest movement against the government’s campaign against drug traffickers, the authorities arrested a man believed to have ordered the murder of seven people.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In a case that has galvanized a protest movement against the government’s conduct of the campaign against drug traffickers, the authorities said that they had arrested a man believed to have ordered the murder of seven people. Among the victims was Juan Francisco Sicilia, 24, the son of the poet and journalist Javier Sicilia, left, who has since led marches demanding a change in the government’s strategy. The suspect, Julio de Jesús Radilla, who was arrested Tuesday, is the leader of the South Pacific cartel in the central state of Morelos, said Luis Cárdenas Palomino, chief of regional security for the federal police. Mr. Radilla is accused of ordering the killings after two of the younger Mr. Sicilia’s friends got into an argument with members of the cartel. Juan Francisco Sicilia was found bound and fatally shot along with six friends in the city of Cuernavaca in March. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Man Arrested in Murder Tied to Drug Cartel', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | THE AMERICAS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Man Arrested in Murder Tied to Drug Cartel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T00:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0930e53d-db92-5c61-ae21-e63db6d885c9', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0930e53d-db92-5c61-ae21-e63db6d885c9'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly 2,000 Mongolian students marched on a government building in the city of Xilinhot in Inner Mongolia Province to demand that Chinese officials respect the rights of Mongolian herders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/world/asia/26briefs-China.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly 2,000 Mongolian students marched on a government building in the city of Xilinhot in Inner Mongolia Province to demand that Chinese officials respect the rights of Mongolian herders.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Nearly 2,000 Mongolian students on Wednesday marched on a government building in the city of Xilinhot in Inner Mongolia Province to demand that Chinese officials respect the rights of Mongolian herders, according to the Southern Mongolia Human Rights Information Center. The center, an advocacy group based in New York, posted on its Web site photographs of the protesters, the vast majority of whom were dressed in yellow or blue athletic jackets. The protest was over the way Chinese officials handled the death on May 10 of a Mongolian herder named Mergen, who was run over during a dispute by a coal truck driven by an ethnic Han, according to Mongolians in the area. The Han are the dominant ethnicity in China and make up the majority of the population in Inner Mongolia. The protest on Tuesday ended after government officials made several promises, including addressing the case of Mergen. Though many Mongolians resent the Han, the Mongolians in Inner Mongolia have rarely held large protests. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Mongolian Students Protest Handling of Death', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | ASIA', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Mongolian Students Protest Handling of Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mongolia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Han Chinese (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T00:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'or