'Thursday Reading: Sedentary Jobs Contribute to Obesity', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T12:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df3375e9-1986-5b2e-82aa-b2dcb323a2c8', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df3375e9-1986-5b2e-82aa-b2dcb323a2c8'}, {'abstract': 'Before its debut, Simon Cowell shook up the cast of ‘X-Factor’ after determining that a judge on the show, the singer Cheryl Cole, was not adequately comfortable alongside the other judges, Paula Abdul and Antonio “L.A.” Reid.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/reports-of-a-shake-up-in-the-x-factor-cast/', 'snippet': 'Before its debut, Simon Cowell shook up the cast of ‘X-Factor’ after determining that a judge on the show, the singer Cheryl Cole, was not adequately comfortable alongside the other judges, Paula Abdul and Antonio “L.A.” Reid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night that one Fox reality show, “American Idol,” was ending its season, another Fox reality show, “The X Factor,” was aswirl in tabloid-ready developments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reports of a Shake-Up in the ‘X Factor’ Cast', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDUL, PAULA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Simon', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Steve', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T12:40:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/758494bc-e742-5dee-b612-6813a48443a2', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/758494bc-e742-5dee-b612-6813a48443a2'}, {'abstract': 'After Amazon stumbled on Monday when it offered Lady Gaga’s new album on MP3 at 99 cents — a surprise one-day promotion that proved so popular it stalled the company’s servers — it is trying the promotion again on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/amazon-to-try-again-on-lady-gaga-album-special/', 'snippet': 'After Amazon stumbled on Monday when it offered Lady Gaga’s new album on MP3 at 99 cents — a surprise one-day promotion that proved so popular it stalled the company’s servers — it is trying the promotion again on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon stumbled on Monday when it offered Lady Gaga’s new album in the MP3 format at 99 cents, a surprise one-day promotion that proved so popular it stalled the company’s servers. But on Thursday it is trying the promotion again, and promises that it will be prepared.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon to Try Again on Lady Gaga Album Special', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Audio)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T12:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e252d08-ccdf-542e-937b-b58b6f16ffb6', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e252d08-ccdf-542e-937b-b58b6f16ffb6'}, {'abstract': 'Delphi, the auto parts maker, filed on Wednesday evening for an initial public offering after emerging from bankruptcy nearly two years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/delphi-automotive-files-for-an-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Delphi, the auto parts maker, filed on Wednesday evening for an initial public offering after emerging from bankruptcy nearly two years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Delphi Automotive, the auto parts maker that languished in bankruptcy for years, filed late on Wednesday for an initial public offering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delphi Automotive Files for an I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T12:55:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c35f1896-29c5-55d5-8bee-4a078fcfa94c', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c35f1896-29c5-55d5-8bee-4a078fcfa94c'}, {'abstract': 'New York meets L.A. in “Superba,” an exhibition at J.F. Chen’s megaspace in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/seeing-things-cest-superba/', 'snippet': 'New York meets L.A. in “Superba,” an exhibition at J.F. Chen’s megaspace in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York meets L.A. in “Superba,” an exhibition at J.F. Chen’s megaspace in Los Angeles. To mark their new collaboration, Joel Chen, the driving force behind one of the largest antique and vintage furniture stores in the city, and Paul Johnson of the Johnson Trading Gallery in Manhattan, which has an outpost in Chen’s space, have brought together an eclectic roster of 14 designers to show works that range from the primitive to the futuristic. Designers from Johnson’s stable, including Max Lamb, Simon Hasan and Kwangho Lee, joined Chen’s invitees, who include the architects Greg Lynn, Eddy Sykes (who was first featured in Seeing Things in 2008) and Aranda/Lasch, and the artists Yassi Mazandi and Mary Brogger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Things | C’est Superba', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/882a8b35-d158-579b-b096-171d2873d291', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/882a8b35-d158-579b-b096-171d2873d291'}, {'abstract': 'Raptr, a social network for gamers, thinks it can relieve the clutter of information that overwhelms gamers. The approach could be useful to nongamers too.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/raptr-wants-to-kill-information-overload/', 'snippet': 'Raptr, a social network for gamers, thinks it can relieve the clutter of information that overwhelms gamers. The approach could be useful to nongamers too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When an idea gets hot in Silicon Valley, scores of entrepreneurs come up with me-too ideas to try to get some of the money sloshing around. Why else are there so many photo-sharing apps, geolocation services and social networks?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raptr Wants to Kill Information Overload', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Darlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2c1d889-79f6-5822-bef2-2056568e022d', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2c1d889-79f6-5822-bef2-2056568e022d'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: In New York, decisions about the death penalty are usually not about the killer, but rather the victim, and the case of Vincent Basciano may be no exception. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/to-avoid-the-death-penalty-kill-another-killer/', 'snippet': 'The Day: In New York, decisions about the death penalty are usually not about the killer, but rather the victim, and the case of Vincent Basciano may be no exception. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s how the death penalty works — or, to be more accurate, doesn’t work — in New York. It’s usually not about the killer, but rather the victim. The case against one Vincent Basciano in Federal District Court in Brooklyn may be no exception. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Avoid the Death Penalty, Kill Another Killer', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basciano, Vincent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bonanno Crime Family', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Massino, Joseph C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0cf1e3c-7021-5c1d-be74-9332776333c6', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0cf1e3c-7021-5c1d-be74-9332776333c6'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Clijsters was eliminated by Arantxa Rus of the Netherlands, leaving the women’s draw dim in star power but brimming with possibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/sports/tennis/2011-french-open-clijsters-makes-an-early-exit.html', 'snippet': 'Kim Clijsters was eliminated by Arantxa Rus of the Netherlands, leaving the women’s draw dim in star power but brimming with possibility.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0PARIS — After her shocking loss Thursday at the French Open, Kim Clijsters did not blame the ankle that she injured while dancing at an April wedding. She did not use her five-year absence from Roland Garros as an excuse.\xa0Instead, she surprisingly cited a sudden lack of confidence midway through a second-round match that she was controlling against the world’s 114th-ranked player. \xa0', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/sports/MATCHES/MATCHES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/27/sports/MATCHES/MATCHES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/sports/MATCHES/MATCHES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/sports/MATCHES/MATCHES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/sports/MATCHES/MATCHES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clijsters Exits in Second Round', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clijsters Exits in Second Round', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rus, Arantxa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a94039-fb73-5c24-b183-88e28bdaa2ba', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a94039-fb73-5c24-b183-88e28bdaa2ba'}, {'abstract': 'Mahesh Bhupathi and Leander Paes of India got off to a slow start on a gray and windy afternoon, then kicked the accelerator, coasting away from Tommy Haas and Philipp Petzschner of Germany, 2-6, 6-3, 6-2.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/bhupathi-and-paes-advance/', 'snippet': 'Mahesh Bhupathi and Leander Paes of India got off to a slow start on a gray and windy afternoon, then kicked the accelerator, coasting away from Tommy Haas and Philipp Petzschner of Germany, 2-6, 6-3, 6-2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Mahesh Bhupathi and Leander Paes of India got off to a slow start on a gray and windy afternoon, then kicked the accelerator, coasting away from Tommy Haas and Philipp Petzschner of Germany, 2-6, 6-3, 6-2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bhupathi and Paes Advance in Doubles', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qual