'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85edc5cd-1d52-5e48-8fa7-f6576c4cbc13', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85edc5cd-1d52-5e48-8fa7-f6576c4cbc13'}, {'abstract': 'Reprising his dead-on impersonation of Neil Young on “Late Night,” Mr. Fallon was joined by the ornery folk-rocker’s sometime collaborators David Crosby and Graham Nash.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/deja-vu-on-jimmy-fallon-a-fake-neil-young-gets-some-familiar-support/', 'snippet': 'Reprising his dead-on impersonation of Neil Young on “Late Night,” Mr. Fallon was joined by the ornery folk-rocker’s sometime collaborators David Crosby and Graham Nash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what the “Late Night With Jimmy Fallon” announcer, Steve Higgins, says at the start of this clip, that is not — we repeat, Internet, not — Neil Young covering Miley Cyrus’s “Party in the U.S.A.” on the NBC program Thursday night: that’s Mr. Fallon himself, reprising his dead-on impersonation of that ornery folk-rocker. But be sure to stick around past the one-minute mark, when Mr. Fallon receives some harmonic support from a couple of Mr. Young’s real-life collaborators, Graham Nash and David Crosby. (And if that’s not the actual Mr. Crosby, we’re very much in favor of Wilford Brimley‘s new longhair look.) Catch you next time, Stephen Stills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Déjà Vu: On ‘Jimmy Fallon,’ a Fake Neil Young Gets Some Familiar Support', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impersonations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crosby, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cyrus, Miley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallon, Jimmy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nash, Graham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stills, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Neil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b01acb55-f350-5b31-9615-45aa14514244', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b01acb55-f350-5b31-9615-45aa14514244'}, {'abstract': 'He constructs his movies like magical boxes, full of intriguing mysteries. Of course, eventually he has to let everyone see what’s in there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/filmmaker-j-j-abrams-is-a-crowd-teaser.html', 'snippet': 'He constructs his movies like magical boxes, full of intriguing mysteries. Of course, eventually he has to let everyone see what’s in there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after taking the stage at the TED conference, where specially anointed trailblazers and titans are asked to explain their inspiration, J. J. Abrams made a crack about the television sensation that branded him one of the entertainment industry’s most tenacious keepers of secrets, a purveyor of sustained ambiguity above all else.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29abrams_span/mag-29Abrams-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 60