facebook-taps-joel-kaplan-to-head-washington-office/', 'snippet': 'The move is a coup for Facebook, which is trying to increase its influence in the capital, and a setback for the private-equity-owned Energy Future Holdings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an effort to expand its power base in the nation’s capital, Facebook has hired Joel Kaplan, an executive vice president at the Texas utility giant Energy Future Holdings, to head the company’s office in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Taps Joel Kaplan to Head Washington Office', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burr, Richard M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Joel D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luttig, J Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandberg, Sheryl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ullyot, Ted', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T13:43:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli and Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4a74b6e-0e97-5703-ae82-5b80f9c004b7', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4a74b6e-0e97-5703-ae82-5b80f9c004b7'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government, foundations and private donors can all play a role in persuading top colleges to become more economically diverse and meritocratic.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/pushing-colleges-to-become-more-diverse/', 'snippet': 'The federal government, foundations and private donors can all play a role in persuading top colleges to become more economically diverse and meritocratic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How can top colleges be persuaded to admit more talented low- and middle-income students? My column this week laid out a strategy for making colleges more economically diverse and meritocratic, based on policies at Amherst College and the University of California. But I didn’t spent much time on the politics of getting colleges to make changes. Fortunately, several other writers have done so — some today, in response to the column, and some long before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pushing Colleges to Become More Diverse', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T14:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a22253b5-f944-564c-8310-f7f6cec9f75d', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a22253b5-f944-564c-8310-f7f6cec9f75d'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links by the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/