omehow echoes, extends or challenges the poem’s themes. Each poem is introduced briefly by Ted Kooser, a former United States poet laureate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | May 26, 2011', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T14:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb9bb842-e20f-5f96-9c44-508ece9a525e', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb9bb842-e20f-5f96-9c44-508ece9a525e'}, {'abstract': 'A 22-year-old Marine was killed by a car on the West Side Highway as he returned to a ship that was docked as part of the Fleet Week celebration.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/marine-celebrating-fleet-week-killed-by-car/', 'snippet': 'A 22-year-old Marine was killed by a car on the West Side Highway as he returned to a ship that was docked as part of the Fleet Week celebration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The young Marine served in Afghanistan, surviving months of perils like sniper fire, mortar rounds and improvised explosive devices before returning to the United States and taking up quarters in the comparatively tranquil precincts of Camp Lejeune, on the North Carolina coast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marine Celebrating Fleet Week Is Killed by Car', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fleet Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T14:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5efcf4e0-1c2d-546f-acf2-89a27b075274', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5efcf4e0-1c2d-546f-acf2-89a27b075274'}, {'abstract': 'Bennet Gartside, a first soloist for the Royal Ballet, has created a series of Web videos.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/new-video-for-royal-ballet-blends-rock-and-shakespeare/', 'snippet': 'Bennet Gartside, a first soloist for the Royal Ballet, has created a series of Web videos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ballet companies are trying ever harder to promote themselves through blogs and social media, but they often struggle to strike just the right note with that much-coveted younger, hipper audience. That’s exactly what Bennet Gartside, a first soloist for the Royal Ballet, is trying to do in the first of a series of promotional videos he is creating for the company’s Web site about the troupe’s coming performances of “Romeo and Juliet” June 17-19 at the O2 Arena — an enormous dome in southeast London that can hold up to 20,000 people. (Imagine American Ballet Theater briefly relocating to Madison Square Garden. Hmmm.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Video for Royal Ballet Blends Rock and Shakespeare', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'