 of data on a veteran’s health from enlistment through death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many years, service members who were leaving the military had to worry about whether their medical records would be properly transferred from one vast computer network in the Defense Department to another, in the Department of Veterans Affairs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Plans to Consolidate Military Health Records', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Plans to Consolidate Military Health Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T16:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c06ce53d-fa95-5301-960f-9d109308a990', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c06ce53d-fa95-5301-960f-9d109308a990'}, {'abstract': 'I am proposing a little list that matches stars in search of redemption with stage roles tailor-made to their particular skills and images.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/theater-talkback-stage-resuscitation-for-career-challenged-celebrities/', 'snippet': 'I am proposing a little list that matches stars in search of redemption with stage roles tailor-made to their particular skills and images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While you theatergoing butterflies out there keep nattering on about the Tonys — who will win, who should win, and so on — I have been focused on an issue of far greater momentousness and urgency. That’s the shameful squandering on Broadway of what our country would seem to believe is our most valued (and infinitely exploitable) natural resource: our celebrities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Stage Resuscitation for Career-Challenged Celebrities', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T16:16:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c746d558-5dbc-5c34-bfaf-1f5a4a4d6014', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c746d558-5dbc-5c34-bfaf-1f5a4a4d6014'}, {'abstract': 'Senior officials at the White House want to make sure President Obama is associated with one word: tough.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/white-house-looks-to-cast-obama-as-tough/', 'snippet': 'Senior officials at the White House want to make sure President Obama is associated with one word: tough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As they gear up for a tough re-election battle, senior officials at the Whi