iled hawk hatchling, and its mother, Violet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Elizabeth Bunting, a wildlife veterinarian at the Animal Health Diagnostic Center at Cornell College of Veterinary Medicine, and other experts responded to readers’ questions about Pip, the red-tailed hawk hatchling, or eyas, who emerged from the egg on May 6 in a nest on a 12th-floor ledge at New York University — and about Pip’s mother, Violet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers About Pip and Violet, Part 2', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hawks (Birds)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T18:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76103234-7378-5416-99bb-aa8ea950bb1c', 'word_count': 1867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76103234-7378-5416-99bb-aa8ea950bb1c'}, {'abstract': 'Lillias White sings "The Oldest Profession" from the musical "The Life" as part of "The Best is Yet to Come: The Music of Cy Coleman" at 59E59 Theaters. (Video courtesy of the production.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000000833871/excerpt-the-best-is-yet-to-come.html', 'snippet': 'Lillias White sings "The Oldest Profession" from the musical "The Life" as part of "The Best is Yet to Come: The Music of Cy Coleman" at 59E59 Theaters. (Video courtesy of the production.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lillias White sings "The Oldest Profession" from the musical "The Life" as part of "The Best is Yet to Come: The Music of Cy Coleman" at 5