n drivers’ test today, nearly one in five licensed drivers would not pass, according to results of the 2011 GMAC Insurance National Driver’s Test. This translates to 36.9 million American drivers, or 18 percent of the country’s total licensed motorists, who lack knowledge of some basic rules of the road — a conclusion that probably won’t surprise many drivers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Do at a Yellow Light? And Other Things American Drivers Don’t Know', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Motor Vehicles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GMAC LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T18:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c03efcd-2e31-5f36-ba55-4ed35a58294d', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c03efcd-2e31-5f36-ba55-4ed35a58294d'}, {'abstract': 'The “Hangover” star Justin Bartha will portray a heartbroken man whose solitude is interrupted by misfit characters played by Krysten Ritter, Anna Camp and David Wilson Barnes in the Second Stage Theater production.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/zach-braff-finds-people-for-his-play-all-new-people/', 'snippet': 'The “Hangover” star Justin Bartha will portray a heartbroken man whose solitude is interrupted by misfit characters played by Krysten Ritter, Anna Camp and David Wilson Barnes in the Second Stage Theater production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having been successfully located on a hotel rooftop in “The Hangover” — and had the good sense to stay out of trouble in its sequel, “The Hangover Part II” — Justin Bartha will next turn up in Second Stage Theater’s production of the Zach Braff play “All New People,” as part of a cast that also features Anna Camp, Krysten Ritter and David Wilson Barnes, the theater company said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zach Braff Finds People for His Play ‘All New People’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartha, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braff, Zach', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DuBois, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T18:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e05b032-00d4-5126-a2b7-e6e6ffa94a1e', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e05b032-00d4-5126-a2b7-e6e6ffa94a1e'}, {'abstract': 'It’s best to go back and forth between Canada and New York to get the best of both Niagaras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS.html', 'snippet': 'It’s best to go back and forth between Canada and New York to get the best of both Niagaras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s best to go back and forth between Canada and New York to get the best of both Niagaras.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE/20110529-HOURS-slide-D8ZE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours Niagara Falls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niagara Falls (Ontario)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niagara Falls (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T18:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/16d531cc-cc5c-5801-b825-b004d22d6175', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/16d531cc-cc5c-5801-b825-b004d22d6175'}, {'abstract': 'In Canada you get views and hooplah; in New York, quiet exploration. To get the best of both Niagaras, hop back and forth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/travel/36-hours-in-niagara-falls.html', 'snippet': 'In Canada you get views and hooplah; in New York, quiet exploration. To get the best of both Niagaras, hop back and forth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT Niagara Falls, the United States is the poor relation and Canada is king. Nature gave Canada the wide-angle view of the majestic waterfall that straddles the border between the two countries, and the Canadians’ commercial bet on tourism landed most of the visitor comforts on their side of the Niagara River. American reliance on industry, however, ended in Rust Belt ruin. Yet the story isn’t so simple. Casinos, high-rise hotels and hucksterish come-ons have so proliferated in Niagara Falls, Ontario, that it risks feeling like a tired amusement park. Meanwhile, in Niagara Falls, New York, the visitor who ventures inside the shabby, underfinanced state park is surprised to discover vestiges of something like a natural landscape. The party is in Canada. The real feel of the river, in all its awesome power, is more accessible in the United States. Hop back and forth to get the best of both Niagaras and see for yourself.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY/20110529-HOURS-slide-H0TY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Niagara Falls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 HOURS: Niagara Falls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and 