nal': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17862353-ba47-54e5-8be2-5432f6ee91e6', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17862353-ba47-54e5-8be2-5432f6ee91e6'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld an Arizona law that imposes harsh penalties on businesses that hire illegal immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2011/05/27/us/27scotus-text.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld an Arizona law that imposes harsh penalties on businesses that hire illegal immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld an Arizona law that imposes harsh penalties on businesses that hire illegal immigrants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Opinion: Chamber of Commerce v. Whiting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T19:54:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/991d4096-e84d-5bcc-a5ac-5117d1842a26', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/991d4096-e84d-5bcc-a5ac-5117d1842a26'}, {'abstract': 'Bing Gordon is a well-known venture capitalist rooted in the tech world. He spoke to DealBook about whether investor interest in internet giants like Facebook and LinkedIn left room for smaller firms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000000837264/a-conversation-with-bing-gordon.html', 'snippet': 'Bing Gordon is a well-known venture capitalist rooted in the tech world. He spoke to DealBook about whether investor interest in internet giants like Facebook and LinkedIn left room for smaller firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bing Gordon is a well-known venture capitalist rooted in the tech world. He spoke to DealBook about whether investor interest in internet giants like Facebook and LinkedIn left room for smaller firms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-db-disrupt-gordon/video-db-disrupt-gordon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-db-disrupt-gordon/video-db-disrupt-gordon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-db-disrupt-gordon/video-db-disrupt-gordon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-db-disrupt-gordon/video-db-disrupt-gordon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With Bing Gordon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T19:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/abcc5a80-6162-579f-ac12-b00a2d628f35', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/abcc5a80-6162-579f-ac12-b00a2d628f35'}, {'abstract': 'Practicing safe sun just got a whole lot sexier, thanks to the young designers Anne Botica and Monique Moore.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/here-comes-the-sun/', 'snippet': 'Practicing safe sun just got a whole lot sexier, thanks to the young designers Anne Botica and Monique Moore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Practicing safe sun just got a whole lot sexier. Thanks to the young designers Anne Botica and Monique Moore, whose recently launched clothing line, Mott 50, contains brightly colored basics with UPF (ultraviolet protection factor) 50 — which is 10 times the protection of a typical white tee. “It really started because we noticed a shift in trends amongst our friends,” says Moore, 28, who quit her day job at Condé Nast Digital a few short months after starting the line in the pink-walled apartment she shares with Botica (fittingly located on Manhattan’s Mott Street). “Girls were finally starting to cover up with hats, sun block and tunics rather than trying to get as tan — and burned to a crisp — as possible.” For the 27-year-old Botica, fashion is really a family affair. “There’s a history of skin cancer in my family,” she says. (An olive-green cotton poplin shirtdress with gold accents is named after Botica’s younger sibling, Faith, $125.) “Our clothes block both UVB, which causes burning and tanning, and UVA rays, which cause aging, wrinkles, sunspots, and skin cancer.” This summer, a portion of Mott 50’s proceeds will go towards cancer research. Go to mott50.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Here Comes the Sun', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T19:56:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6fc9350-a66a-5119-97cf-65b6c002d552', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6fc9350-a66a-5119-97cf-65b6c002d552'}, {'abstract': 'The political maneuvering behind the capture of Ratko Mladic; the history of his war crimes; and the Op-Ed columnist Roger Cohen describes meeting Mr. Mladic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000000837319/timescast--may-26-2011.html', 'snippet': 'The political maneuvering behind the capture of Ratko Mladic; the history of his war crimes; and the Op-Ed columnist Roger Cohen describes meeting Mr. Mladic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The political maneuvering behind the capture of Ratko Mladic; the history of his war crimes; and the Op-Ed columnist Roger Cohen describes meeting Mr. Mladic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/multimedia/video-tc-110526/video-tc-110526-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/26/multimedia/video-tc-110526/video-tc-110526-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | May 26, 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosnia and Herzegovina'