riginal': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/700a808b-89ac-5b3a-b0dd-8166e23ddef5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/700a808b-89ac-5b3a-b0dd-8166e23ddef5'}, {'abstract': '“The Best Is Yet to Come” is a revue tribute to Cy Coleman, whose songwriting career does not make for easy anthologizing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/theater/reviews/the-best-is-yet-to-come-at-59e59-theater-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Best Is Yet to Come” is a revue tribute to Cy Coleman, whose songwriting career does not make for easy anthologizing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little bit of Las Vegas in the 1960s has splashed down Off Broadway. “The Best Is Yet to Come: The Music of Cy Coleman,” a finger-snapping, hard-charging, small-scale but still shiny-looking revue, has taken up residence at the 59E59 Theaters, becoming the latest cultural artifact seemingly spawned by the influential “Mad Men” television series. A Broadway composer whose glory years began in the heyday of the Rat Pack, Coleman can be seen on the cover of the program in a sleek suit, posing coolly like an honorary member of that informal fraternity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27Best-span/Best-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27Best-span/Best-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27Best-span/Best-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27Best-span/Best-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27Best-span/Best-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brassy and Bawdy, With Fingers Snapping', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Best Is Yet to Come'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brassy and Bawdy, With Fingers Snapping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, Cy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T21:34:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a2800c2-a7a9-5aa7-9167-e186984399ce', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a2800c2-a7a9-5aa7-9167-e186984399ce'}, {'abstract': 'Polls in Florida and New Jersey show significant improvements in President Obama’s job-approval ratings over the last month.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/obama-approval-ratings-up-in-two-states/', 'snippet': 'Polls in Florida and New Jersey show significant improvements in President Obama’s job-approval ratings over the last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two state polls out Thursday offer some good news for President Obama, showing significant improvements in his approval rating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Approval Ratings Up in Two States', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name