'pub_date': '2011-05-26T21:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f668dc40-9f1b-5755-8387-50347d952c5b', 'word_count': 1404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f668dc40-9f1b-5755-8387-50347d952c5b'}, {'abstract': 'A couple live in an apartment with an unusual provenance: Frank Gehry designed the interior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/realestate/space-light-and-bragging-rights-habitatswashington-heights.html', 'snippet': 'A couple live in an apartment with an unusual provenance: Frank Gehry designed the interior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE real estate ad promised a space renovated by a “well-known architect,” or words to that effect. But Mindy Fox, a food writer who was apartment hunting with her husband, Steve Hoffman, was dubious. “If he’s so well known,” Ms. Fox muttered to Mr. Hoffman as they headed up to Washington Heights back in 2005 to check out the place, “how come they don’t say who he is?”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/realestate/Habitats-1/Habitats-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/realestate/Habitats-1/Habitats-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/realestate/Habitats-1/Habitats-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Space, Light, Bragging Rights', 'kicker': 'Habitats | Washington Heights', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Space, Light, Bragging Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'WASHINGTON HEIGHTS (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T21:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b8c90c-ff05-5ad3-bea3-1db96aff5bb5', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b8c90c-ff05-5ad3-bea3-1db96aff5bb5'}, {'abstract': 'The finale of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” evidently brought back some fans who had not watched for quite some time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/arts/television/oprah-finale-generates-best-ratings-since-1994.html', 'snippet': 'The finale of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” evidently brought back some fans who had not watched for quite some time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The finale of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” evidently brought back some fans who had not watched for quite some time. It was the highest-rated episode in almost 18 years. The show recorded a 13.3 household rating in major cities on Wednesday, meaning that 13.3 percent of all households with television sets tuned in. That’s more than twice the normal household rating for her show this season, and its highest since 1994, when its ratings were generally higher and there were fewer competing shows on the air. The ratings are subject to change when the Nielsen Company releases total viewer ratings later, according to CBS Television Distribution, which syndicates the show. Expecting high ratings, CBS charged a premium for advertisers who wanted to be a part of the finale.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Oprah’ Finale Generates Best Ratings Since 1994', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Oprah’ Finale Generates Best Ratings Since 1994', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T21:38:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c12cb09-e2d6-5fbc-b33f-7554d7fd1a55', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c12cb09-e2d6-5fbc-b33f-7554d7fd1a55'}, {'abstract': 'The Complexions program at the Joyce Theater on Tuesday night included the New York premiere of “Testament.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/arts/dance/complexions-contemporary-ballet-at-joyce-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Complexions program at the Joyce Theater on Tuesday night included the New York premiere of “Testament.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Complexions Contemporary Ballet is one of the great mysteries of the dance world. Formed in 1994 by the artistic directors Dwight Rhoden and Desmond Richardson, the troupe continues on despite its dire level of choreography, which used to be soulless but is now sappy too.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/27complexions-span/complexions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/20