gainst it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/fashion/dominique-brownings-argument-for-natural-aging.html', 'snippet': 'Over time, friends don’t look the way they used to. It’s not aging so much as the fight they’ve put up against it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THANK goodness it was drilled into me to greet people with the words, “How do you do?” Because these days, the question that springs more frequently to mind is, “Who are you?” Not because my memory is going, but because many of my acquaintances are erasing the traces of identity, if not life, from their faces.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/MIRROR/MIRROR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/MIRROR/MIRROR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/MIRROR/MIRROR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for Laugh Lines', 'kicker': 'Mirror', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Case For Laugh Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Botox (Drug)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Face', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Surgery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-26T22:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominique Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d772409a-463c-51ad-bb00-67b0042a9ef6', 'word_count': 1553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d772409a-463c-51ad-bb00-67b0042a9ef6'}, {'abstract': 'The alto saxophonist Tim Berne performed with Matt Mitchell and Ches Smith at Korzo in Brooklyn on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/arts/music/tim-berne-matt-mitchell-and-ches-smith-at-korzo-review.html', 'snippet': 'The alto saxophonist Tim Berne performed with Matt Mitchell and Ches Smith at Korzo in Brooklyn on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The alto saxophonist Tim Berne, who often acts as if he’s making a joke out of a disappointment, stood at the back of Korzo, a Hungarian restaurant in Brooklyn between the Prospect Expressway and Greenwood Cemetery. He announced that his trio would perform 13 new songs for the very first time — and that the last 10 would be joined together in one piece. “Didn’t you come up with a name for it?” he asked his pianist, Matt Mitchell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/BEEFEATER/BEEFEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/BEEFEATER/BEEFEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/BEEFEATER/BEEFEATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/arts/BEEFEATER/BEEFEATER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu