e-af3fc33af731', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d362c44-d600-54ac-b87e-af3fc33af731'}, {'abstract': 'Social businesses require a delicate balance of the humanitarian and the financial to succeed.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/26/the-path-from-charity-to-profit/', 'snippet': 'Social businesses require a delicate balance of the humanitarian and the financial to succeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday I wrote about Kedai Balitaku, a for-profit company started last year by the development group Mercy Corps in Indonesia.\xa0 Mercy Corps took this unusual step because it realized that its programs to educate mothers about nutrition were not changing what mothers fed their children.\xa0 Healthy food is expensive, and the crowded conditions in the Jakarta slums mean that many families have no place to cook or eat.\xa0 So they buy their children the cheapest street food, which is usually either sweet or deep fried.\xa0 Kedai Balitaku, which usually goes by the name KeBal, aims to become a chain of street carts selling low-priced healthy food to children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Path From Charity to Profit', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vendors, Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercy Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ACEH PROVINCE (INDONESIA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jakarta (Indonesia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T00:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original':