': 'nyt://article/53c5ba9d-5ce3-5f8e-8600-14dab800ac3a'}, {'abstract': 'American-born children of illegal immigrants are pushed into the shadows alongside their parents and suffer steep consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/opinion/27fri3.html', 'snippet': 'American-born children of illegal immigrants are pushed into the shadows alongside their parents and suffer steep consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Lower East Side Tenement Museum in Manhattan, visitors can view meticulously recreated moments in the lives of the immigrant families who lived there, like the Moores of Ireland. Their dark, stifling apartment sits ready for the wake of a baby girl, dead of malnutrition. This was in the 1870s, when America’s newcomers struggled mightily against poverty and isolation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Other Half Lives, Still', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Other Half Lives, Still', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Youth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T01:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f516588-18a3-5e0f-9d33-902a9eebfa61', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f516588-18a3-5e0f-9d33-902a9eebfa61'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery Numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery