ide-meghan-mccains-bachelorette-pad.html', 'snippet': 'The famous daughter of the famous senator shows off her 1,100-square-foot home in West Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The famous daughter of the famous senator shows off her 1,100-square-foot bachelorette home in West Hollywood.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29domains_span/29domains_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 365, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29domains_span/29domains_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 365}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29domains_span/mag-29domains-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29domains_span/29domains_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29domains_span/29domains_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Meghan McCain’s Bachelorette Pad', 'kicker': 'Domains', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE SKULL PALACE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, Meghan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Lewine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8c0d617-416f-5122-978d-86b94db6bc6e', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8c0d617-416f-5122-978d-86b94db6bc6e'}, {'abstract': 'Alberto Contador, the three-time Tour de France winner, may be clear to race in this summer’s Tour after the appeal regarding his doping case was postponed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/sports/cycling/contador-appeal-is-postponed.html', 'snippet': 'Alberto Contador, the three-time Tour de France winner, may be clear to race in this summer’s Tour after the appeal regarding his doping case was postponed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alberto Contador, the three-time Tour de France winner and current leader of the Giro d’Italia, may be clear to race in this summer’s Tour after the appeal regarding his doping case was postponed Thursday from early June to a yet-to-be-set date. That appeal, in which the Court of Arbitration for Sport would decide Contador’s fate after he tested positive for the banned drug clenbuterol last July, was supposed to be resolved before the Tour began July 2. If he were to lose the appeal, he could receive up to a two-year ban from the sport. His Tour title could also be stripped. In February, the Spanish cycling federation cleared Contador of any wrongdoing, but the International Cycling Union and the World Anti-Doping Agency appealed. The appeal was postponed because both sides needed more time to prepare for the hearing, the court said on its Web site. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contador Appeal Is Postponed', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Cycling', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contador Appeal Is Postponed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contador, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Giro d'Italia (Bicycle Race)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c491f18d-3dd5-52c4-95b8-9fb1437f3f78', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c491f18d-3dd5-52c4-95b8-9fb1437f3f78'}, {'abstract': 'DAR, a new internet service, is essentially "Tivo for the radio." It may be just what the doctor ordered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/personaltech/100000000837654/a-cure-for-the-radio-industry.html', 'snippet': 'DAR, a new internet service, is essentially "Tivo for the radio." It may be just what the doctor ordered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAR, a new internet service, is essentially "Tivo for the radio." It may be just what the doctor ordered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-pogue-radio/video-pogue-radio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-pogue-radio/video-pogue-radio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/26/business/video-pogue-radio/video-pogue-radio-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSta