ar sunscreen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/us/27scottsdale2_337/27scottsdale2_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/27/us/27scottsdale2_337/27scottsdale2_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/us/27scottsdale2_337/27scottsdale2_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/us/27scottsdale2_337/27scottsdale2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/us/27scottsdale2_337/27scottsdale2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Neighborly Advice to the Palins: In Arizona, the Sun Burns', 'kicker': 'Scottsdale Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Neighborly Advice to the Palins: In Arizona, the Sun Burns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scottsdale (Ariz)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Lacey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lacey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a42ae3e3-c1a6-55f0-bdd5-e1d2f6d567fd', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a42ae3e3-c1a6-55f0-bdd5-e1d2f6d567fd'}, {'abstract': 'Belarus sentenced two former presidential candidates to lengthy prison terms for organizing a large protest against elections held in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/world/europe/27briefs-Belarus.html', 'snippet': 'Belarus sentenced two former presidential candidates to lengthy prison terms for organizing a large protest against elections held in December.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Belarus sentenced two former presidential candidates to lengthy prison terms on Thursday for organizing a large protest against elections held in December that independent observers said were tainted by widespread fraud. The former Soviet republic’s authoritarian president won the election. The two former candidates, Nikolai Statkevich and Dmitri Uss, received six and five-and-a-half year sentences, respectively. The convictions came a day after President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko suggested that he might free his political opponents, remarks broadly interpreted as a signal to the West that he might be willing to negotiate to secure a badly needed loan. But the convictions seemed to indicate the president’s hard line would not soon soften. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus: Ex-Presidential Candidates Are Sentenced', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | EUROPE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus: Ex-Presidential Candidates Are Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f2d0f9c-55b3-554c-b7c9-e5bbfb01bf9f', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f2d0f9c-55b3-554c-b7c9-e5bbfb01bf9f'}, {'abstract': 'The acquittal of two police officers was a blow to Cyrus R. Vance, Jr., the Manhattan prosecutor, at a time when he is taking on the high-profile case of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/nyregion/verdict-in-rape-case-may-have-an-impact-on-cyrus-vance.html', 'snippet': 'The acquittal of two police officers was a blow to Cyrus R. Vance, Jr., the Manhattan prosecutor, at a time when he is taking on the high-profile case of Dominique Strauss-Kahn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final days of the trial against two police officers charged with rape, the Manhattan district attorney, Cyrus R. Vance Jr., made a move that his legendary predecessor, Robert M. Morgenthau, would not have contemplated:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/nyregion/Y-VANCE/Y-VANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/nyregion/Y-VANCE/Y-VANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/nyregion/Y-VANCE/Y-VANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Se