ing of a radical Muslim cleric from privately sharing classified information about the case with a Federal District Court judge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Seeks to Withhold Secret Data From Judge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Seeks to Withhold Secret Data From Judge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zaid, Mark S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a235f2c1-b3c0-5c5b-8070-493b56c463f2', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a235f2c1-b3c0-5c5b-8070-493b56c463f2'}, {'abstract': 'Anibal Sanchez threw a five-hitter for another complete game in San Francisco as Florida completed a three-game sweep.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/sports/baseball/sanchez-leads-way-as-marlins-sweep.html', 'snippet': 'Anibal Sanchez threw a five-hitter for another complete game in San Francisco as Florida completed a three-game sweep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARLINS 1, GIANTS 0 Anibal Sanchez threw a five-hitter as Florida completed a three-game sweep in San Francisco. Sanchez (4-1) struck out eight and walked two for his fifth career complete game. (AP)', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanchez Leads Way as Marlins Sweep', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ROUNDUP', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Marlins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/182f3f05-6fee-5393-8f31-4dde25cac239', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/182f3f05-6fee-5393-8f31-4dde25cac239'}, {'abstract': 'South Carolina’s education superintendent faced criticism the day after announcing that the state would not compete for federal money in the Race to the Top school improvement competition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/education/27brfs-Southcarolina.html', 'snippet': 'South Carolina’s education superintendent faced criticism the day after announcing that the state would not compete for federal money in the Race to the Top school improvement competition.', 'lead_paragraph': ' South Carolina’s education superintendent, Mick Zais, faced criticism on Thursday, the day after announcing that the state would not compete for federal money in the Obama administration’s Race to the Top school improvement competition. The chairman of the Charleston Education Network, a nonprofit advocacy group, told The Charleston Post and Courier that children would pay the price. Mr. Zais, a Republican, said this year’s $200 million grant competition amounted to “pieces of silver in exchange for strings attached to Washington.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: Stance on School Aid Is Criticized', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stance on School Aid Is Criticized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Race to the Top Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dillon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dillon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a9b320-38a6-5ecc-a24f-7236fa91e98e', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a9b320-38a6-5ecc-a24f-7236fa91e98e'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Peter Shumlin signed a bill on Thursday that sets Vermont on a path to creating the nation’s first publicly financed health care system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/us/27brfs-Vermont.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Peter Shumlin signed a bill on Thursday that sets Vermont on a path to creating the nation’s first publicly financed health care system.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Gov. Peter Shumlin signed a bill on Thursday that sets Vermont on a path to creating the nation’s first publicly financed health care system. The law calls for something close to a single-payer system, with doctors and hospitals billing one entity, the state government, for their services. All 620,000 of the state’s residents would be eligible for coverage under the system, which proponents say would be cheaper than the current patchwork of insurers. A board appointed by the governor will determine payment rates for doctors, benefits and other details. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vermont: Governor Signs Health Care Law', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vermont: Governor Signs Health Care Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shumlin, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e44e645-aedc-5454-96ac-80279c7bd7af', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e44e645-aedc-5454-96ac-80279c7bd7af'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Carrington was a British-born Surrealist and onetime romantic partner of Max Ernst whose paintings depicted women and half-human beasts floating in a dreamscape of images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/arts/design/leonora-carrington-surrealist-dies-at-94.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Carrington was a British-born Surrealist and onetime romantic partner of Max Ernst whose paintings depicted women and half-human beasts floating in a dreamscape of images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leonora Carrington, a British-born Surrealist and onetime romantic partner of Max Ernst whose paintings depicted women and half-human beasts floating in a dreamscape of images drawn from myth, folklore, religious ritual and the occult, died on Wednesday in Mexico City, where she lived. She was 94.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/CARRINGTON2-obit/CARRINGTON2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/CARRINGTON2-obit/CARRINGTON2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/CARRINGTON2-obit/CARRINGTON2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leonora Carrington Is Dead at 94; Artist and Author of Surrealist Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leonora Carrington Is Dead at 94; Artist and Author of Surrealist Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ernst, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrington, Leonora', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:48:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/cceb2281-8b07-5309-adc7-be006031d2c7', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cceb2281-8b07-5309-adc7-be006031d2c7'}, {'abstract': 'A hearing ended after three days of testimony in the trial of Eugenio Vides Casanova, a retired general from El Salvador accused of participating in torture there during the civil war in the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/us/27brfs-Deport.html', 'snippet': 'A hearing ended after three days of testimony in the trial of Eugenio Vides Casanova, a retired general from El Salvador accused of participating in torture there during the civil war in the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After three days of testimony in immigration court in Orlando, a hearing ended in the deportation trial of Eugenio Vides Casanova, a retired general from El Salvador accused of participating in torture there during the civil war in the 1980s. General Vides, who as defense minister was a close American ally, testified on Thursday. Judge James Grim said he would decide whether to order General Vides deported in January. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: General’s Deportation Hearing Ends', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: General&#8217;s Deportation Hearing Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vides Casanova, Carlos Eugenio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T02:51:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dd12686-5f1f-51ba-968d-c51eae5bb8bd', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dd12686-5f1f-51ba-968d-c51eae5bb8bd'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant on Second Avenue, one of the most famous night spots in America, shut its doors on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/nyregion/elaines-restaurant-jammed-on-it