in-london/', 'snippet': 'A London gallery is hosting the first ever retrospective of the work of the controversial British artist Tracey Emin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of British art, only Damien Hirst has raised as much controversy as the 48-year-old artist Tracey Emin, who became an overnight sensation with her work “Everyone I Have Ever Slept With 1963–1995.” The tent, appliquéd with names and decorated with graphic mementos from her love life, was shown at the Charles Saatchi exhibition at the Royal Academy in London in 1997.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Controversy and Fabric at Emin Show in London', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emin, Tracey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hayward Gallery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb02bd17-75bf-5585-a6e3-6f3e4d1b3163', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb02bd17-75bf-5585-a6e3-6f3e4d1b3163'}, {'abstract': 'Eventually voters will have to choose between tax increases or steep cuts to spending programs that they embrace, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/the-case-for-higher-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Eventually voters will have to choose between tax increases or steep cuts to spending programs that they embrace, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for Higher Taxes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30954865-f5fb-5f93-af69-e6612317a91d', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30954865-f5fb-5f93-af69-e6612317a91d'}, {'abstract': 'Arizona may impose harsh penalties on employers of illegal immigrants, the Supreme Court ruled Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/the-early-word-setting-a-precedent/', 'snippet': 'Arizona may impose harsh penalties on employers of illegal immigrants, the Supreme Court ruled Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Setting a Precedent', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': N