to expand the availability of subtitles in its film and TV library.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/tip-of-the-week-netflix-streaming-in-other-languages/', 'snippet': 'The company’s video-streaming service continues to expand the availability of subtitles in its film and TV library.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Netflix continues to make progress on its project to add subtitles to its streaming video library. The company recently announced an update to its iOS app that brings subtitles to selected movies and TV shows on the iPad, iPod Touch and iPhone. If subtitles are available for the video that is playing, a caption icon appears on screen. Tap the caption icon to see the list of available subtitle languages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Netflix Streaming in Other Languages', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00352be5-eb07-5587-a4d2-c7bac9d26444', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00352be5-eb07-5587-a4d2-c7bac9d26444'}, {'abstract': 'The world’s leading industrialized nations said they would help revive the economies of Egypt and Tunisia to help anchor stability in the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/europe/28g8.html', 'snippet': 'The world’s leading industrialized nations said they would help revive the economies of Egypt and Tunisia to help anchor stability in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEAUVILLE, France — Leaders of the Group of 8 wealthiest industrialized nations pledged on Friday to send billions of dollars in aid to Egypt and Tunisia, hoping to reduce the threat that economic stagnation could undermine the transition to democracy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28g8-obama/28g8-obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28g8-obama/28g8-obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28g8-obama/28g8-obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28g8-obama/28g8-obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28g8-obama/28g8-obama-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aid Pledge by Group of 8 Seeks to Bolster Arab Democracy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'WEALTHY NATIONS MOVE TO BOLSTER ARAB DEMOCRACY', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Eight', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11e94773-f0b6-5424-9c44-1bf8f7a3f35c', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11e94773-f0b6-5424-9c44-1bf8f7a3f35c'}, {'abstract': 'Saudi Arabia is flexing its financial and diplomatic might in a bid to avert the overthrow of any more leaders in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28saudi.html', 'snippet': 'Saudi Arabia is flexing its financial and diplomatic might in a bid to avert the overthrow of any more leaders in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIYADH, Saudi Arabia — Saudi Arabia is flexing its financial and diplomatic might across the Middle East in a wide-ranging bid to contain the tide of change, shield other monarchies from popular discontent and avert the overthrow of any more leaders struggling to calm turbulent nations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/SAUDI/SAUDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/SAUDI/SAUDI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/SAUDI/SAUDI-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnai