{'abstract': 'The nation’s news service said that Jun Young-su, of Southern California, would be released because a visiting American official had apologized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/asia/28korea.html', 'snippet': 'The nation’s news service said that Jun Young-su, of Southern California, would be released because a visiting American official had apologized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — An American who had been detained for six months in North Korea arrived in Beijing on Saturday following his release a day earlier, a U.S. Embassy spokesman said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28korea/28korea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 371, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28korea/28korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28korea/28korea-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Frees American Held Since November, Reports Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Frees American Held Since November, Reports Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T10:34:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By SU-HYUN LEE and KEVIN DREW', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su-hyun', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LEE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DREW', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ccda730-0464-5c67-af7f-f95fba551f3e', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ccda730-0464-5c67-af7f-f95fba551f3e'}, {'abstract': 'Yemen degenerated further into bloody conflict as clashes beyond the capital drew in more tribal factions and threatened to widen the fighting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28yemen.html', 'snippet': 'Yemen degenerated further into bloody conflict as clashes beyond the capital drew in more tribal factions and threatened to widen the fighting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — More than 100 tribal fighters overran a military checkpoint northeast of the Yemeni capital on Friday, killing several soldiers and taking control of a strategic gateway to the city, according to tribesmen and witnesses. Five tribesmen were also killed, they said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28yemen1/28yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28yemen1/28yemen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28yemen1/28yemen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28yemen1/28yemen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28yemen1/28yemen1-thumbSt