,” I asked you to compare two sites, Continental.com and JetBlue.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JetBlue vs. Continental: Battle of the Airline Web Sites', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Continental Airlines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabriel Shaoolian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabriel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaoolian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e80b4853-6b9c-5dc7-b5f0-7ae1b66a6c2e', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e80b4853-6b9c-5dc7-b5f0-7ae1b66a6c2e'}, {'abstract': 'Land of fried-clam-cold-beer-live-music-and-raw-oyster gloriousness, Claudio’s Clam Bar is nestled on a wharf that juts 400 feet into Peconic Bay, in quaint Greenport.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/claudios-clam-bar/', 'snippet': 'Land of fried-clam-cold-beer-live-music-and-raw-oyster gloriousness, Claudio’s Clam Bar is nestled on a wharf that juts 400 feet into Peconic Bay, in quaint Greenport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hamptons-bound traffic in the summer is a sweaty, hectic, BMW-infested mess. But that’s not your problem. As you soar down the Long Island Expressway, past the long line of frustrated New Yorkers waiting to debark at Exit 70, grin and wave, because you’re not going to the Hamptons, pal. You’re headed for the North Fork — and straight to Claudio’s Clam Bar. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And Now, Fresh Clams and Salty Air', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T11:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd180abe-b5a1-57e6-a70f-02d71fc8afd5', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd180abe-b5a1-57e6-a70f-02d71fc8afd5'}, {'abstract': 'In a possible bid to keep down a rising death toll, security forces appeared to show restraint by not firing on demonstrations in some areas of the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28syria.html', 'snippet': 'In a possible bid to keep down a rising death toll, security forces appeared to show restraint by not firing on demonstrations in some areas of the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Thousands of Syrians took to the streets again on Friday in virtually every region of the country, but in some locales, Syrian security forces showed restraint in not firing on the demonstrations in a possible bid to keep down a death toll that has brought growing international pressure and strained relations with Syria’s few allies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28syria/28syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28syria/28syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28syria/28syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Forces Restrained as Syrian Protests Spread', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Forces Restrained As Syrian Protests Spread', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T11:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23be9189-5dc0-5eef-adcc-6e919c97f557', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23be9189-5dc0-5eef-adcc-6e919c97f557'}, {'abstract': 'Interior designers who use LED lighting don’t have to worry about returning regularly to replace incandescent bulbs that have burned out.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/a-bright-side-to-the-bulb-changeover/', 'snippet': 'Interior designers who use LED lighting don’t have to worry about returning regularly to replace incandescent bulbs that have burned out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted in an article in Thursday’s Home section, some interior designers whose results depend on precisely the right lighting are hoarding incandescent light bulbs before they are phased out under congressional legislation. But not all decorators are wedded to the incandescent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bright Side to the Bulb Changeover', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light Bulbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koninklijke Philips Electronics NV', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T11:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1797f84-bcb0-546d-8941-ff589f186732', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1797f84-bcb0-546d-8941-ff589f186732'}, {'abstract': 'Time-saving tip: All the popular web browsers will let you save a group of tabs so that your browser will open them all whenever it starts.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/setting-browser-tabs-to-open-at-launch/', 'snippet': 'Time-saving tip: All the popular web browsers will let you save a group of tabs so that your browser will open them all whenever it starts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you find yourself hitting the same group of Web sites every time you sit down at your computer? For me, it’s Facebook, The Times, Instapundit, Techmeme, my bank, and my Google Docs spreadsheet of freelance assignments. In fact, I open three separate Facebook tabs –- one for my messages, and two for groups in which I’m active. Most people have a similar set of pages they open over and over, several times a day. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Setting Browser Tabs to Open at Start-Up', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chrome (Browser)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Techmeme', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T11:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Boutin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boutin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3fd848f-bc94-5bbc-8783-7a6746a8aaaa', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3fd848f-bc94-5bbc-8783-7a6746a8aaaa'}, {'abstract': 'Australian researchers find that elderly drivers commonly commit serious errors.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/elderly-drivers-fail-a-test/', 'snippet': 'Australian researchers find that elderly drivers commonly commit serious errors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'True or false? Most older drivers drive as safely as anyone else. It’s just that a few bad apples, particularly those behind the wheel despite poor vision or dementia, make mistakes and produce the statistics showing that per mile driven, drivers over age 75 are almost as dangerous as teenagers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elderly Drivers Fail a Test', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/776c823a-f458-58b7-8750-0a16323e1c91', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/776c823a-f458-58b7-8750-0a16323e1c91'}, {'abstract': 'As new restrictions proliferate, does the abortion rights movement have what it takes to fight back?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/the-reincarnation-of-pro-life.html', 'snippet': 'As new restrictions proliferate, does the abortion rights movement have what it takes to fight back?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since Republicans took control of half the country’s statehouses this year, the anti-abortion movement has won one victory after another. At least 64 new anti-abortion laws have passed, with more than 30 of them in April alone. The campaign is the largest in history and also the most creative. Virginia started regulating abortion clinics as if they were hospitals. Utah, Nebraska and several other states have stopped private health insurers from covering abortions, with rare exceptions. South Dakota will soon tell women that before they go to an abortion clinic, they must first visit a crisis pregnancy center whose mission is to talk them out of it. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lede/29lede-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lede/29lede-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lede/29lede-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reincarnation of Pro-Life', 'kicker': 'First', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'THE REINCARNATION OF PRO-LIFE', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9157c591-fc2d-5585-886f-72e88fef5d91', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9157c591-fc2d-5585-886f-72e88fef5d91'}, {'abstract': '“I’ve been alienating my public since I was 20 years old.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/david-mamet-talks-about-his-shift-to-the-right.html', 'snippet': '“I’ve been alienating my public since I was 20 years old.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' While reading your new book, “The Secret Knowledge,” I thought, My God, in crucifying liberals, this guy is going to infuriate a huge chunk of the people who pay money to see plays. Are you concerned that you’re alienating your public?  I’ve been alienating my public since I was 20 years old. When “American Buffalo” came out on Broadway, people would storm out and say, “How dare he use that kind of language!” Of course I’m alienating the public! That’s what they pay me for. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 446, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29talk/29talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Mamet Explains His Shift to the Right', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ALWAYS BE CHANGING', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a8dc9f-dde0-53a2-bbed-a980ab4467f8', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a8dc9f-dde0-53a2-bbed-a980ab4467f8'}, {'abstract': 'Peace of mind; peace and quiet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/the-ethicist-vital-information.html', 'snippet': 'Peace of mind; peace and quiet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am an H.I.V.-positive man who, thanks to antiretroviral therapy, has had an undetectable viral load for the past three years. I have no sexually transmitted infections. Though I always practice safe sex, I feel an obligation to disclose my status to any potential partner well before engaging in any sexual contact. My doctors disagree, citing evidence that people in my condition are sexually noninfectious. Others make a buyer-beware type of argument. Am I right, or are they? NAME WITHHELD, ENGLEWOOD CLIFFS, N.J.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 610, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/28/magazine/ethicist-image/ethicist-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vital Information?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'VITAL INFORMATION?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a587f72-7b7a-564e-9d9f-585ec0c346db', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a587f72-7b7a-564e-9d9f-585ec0c346db'}, {'abstract': 'Jason McBride on “Feel It Break,” by Austra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/bonus-feature-the-enthusiast.html', 'snippet': 'Jason McBride on “Feel It Break,” by Austra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s enthusiast: Jason McBride, senior editor at www.torontostandard.com', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '49', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonus Feature: The Enthusiast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BONUS FEATURE | The Enthusiast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4d03d14-3f6d-588a-8ea6-82e4365ba5f2', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4d03d14-3f6d-588a-8ea6-82e4365ba5f2'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s exhilarating, terrifying brush with freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/egypts-next-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s exhilarating, terrifying brush with freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Wednesday morning, Zakaria Moh\xadyeldin steered his father’s black Skoda sedan through a thick belt of Cairo traffic and drove northward into the sleepy farmland of the Nile Delta. Mohyeldin, a tall, broad-shouldered 27-year-old with a jutting chin and a thicket of jet-black hair, had just quit his job as a stockbroker trainee. The revolution was almost three months old, and the hard work was just beginning, he told me. Mohyeldin had seen his life transformed during those amazing 18 days: battling police in clouds of tear gas, ferrying food to the protesters in Tahrir Square and cheering in awe as Hosni Mubarak, Egypt’s modern-day pharaoh, was cast out in a youth-led revolt. Now he wanted to see what he could do to spread the revolution’s high ideals in Egypt’s agricultural heartland. And he was vaguely contemplating a political career, starting in the village of Kafr Shukr, where his grandfather, a former prime minister, was born.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29egypt2/mag-29Egypt-t_CA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29egypt2/29egypt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29egypt2/29egypt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Next Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘THE REVOLUTION CAME, THE REVOLUTION ENDED. NOW I WANT TO KNOW, WHO DO I BELONG TO?’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fd8570f-dfed-5514-85f8-0e0f863a35ea', 'word_count': 5652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fd8570f-dfed-5514-85f8-0e0f863a35ea'}, {'abstract': 'Crawling around in the dark, searching for a link to the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/magazine/lives-underground-in-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'Crawling around in the dark, searching for a link to the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As tourists in Vietnam, my friend Vince and I ate coconut candy and rode bicycles around the Mekong Delta. We lunched on a fish that looked like Harry Dean Stanton and joked uneasily about Agent Orange. Now, as part of the same package tour, our no-name bus took us to the Cu Chi Tunnels, the infamous Viet Cong network that snakes below the jungle northwest of Ho Chi Minh City. We were going to slot our bodies into a hole in the ground and try not to entomb ourselves. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lives/mag-29lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lives/29lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/magazine/29lives/29lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Underground in Vietnam', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Underground in Vietnam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Russell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef576f8b-37e7-502b-843e-320a593c5b76', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef576f8b-37e7-502b-843e-320a593c5b76'}, {'abstract': 'An initial chronology confirmed that a loss of consistent speed readings triggered the events that led to the 2009 crash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/europe/28flight.html', 'snippet': 'An initial chronology confirmed that a loss of consistent speed readings triggered the events that led to the 2009 crash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The captain of the Air France jet that crashed in the Atlantic two years ago was in the cockpit, though not at the controls, as the crew struggled to recover from a high-altitude stall, according to an initial chronology of the flight’s final moments published Friday by French investigators.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28flight/28flight-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28flight/28flight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'