 not been kind to Ratko Mladic, a fugitive in his own land from war crimes charges. His mouth droops sideways and his skin is bluish and mottled red, the pallor of poor hygiene, bad nutrition and self-imposed prison, according to his longtime friend and defense lawyer, Milos Saljic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28mladic/28mladic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28mladic/28mladic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28mladic/28mladic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28mladic/28mladic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28mladic/28mladic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyer Seeks Medical Evaluation of Mladic, War Crimes Suspect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawyer Seeks Medical Evaluation Of Mladic, War Crimes Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T13:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcb22666-d6c6-54ca-8c9d-f96532c7d162', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcb22666-d6c6-54ca-8c9d-f96532c7d162'}, {'abstract': 'The restoration of the Brixton Windmill, a historic but derelict structure in London, affords the public a chance to see how flour is milled, and provides a rallying point for organic farming advocates.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/london-underground-an-old-mills-second-wind/', 'snippet': 'The restoration of the Brixton Windmill, a historic but derelict structure in London, affords the public a chance to see how flour is milled, and provides a rallying point for organic farming advocates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flour milling is not the first thing that comes to mind when you think of Brixton, a neighborhood in South London that is better known for jerk chicken and live music. Owned by the Lambeth Council, the Brixton Windmill has just reopened this month after a £580,000 (about $937,000) renovation. The effort was initiated by a local residents’ group, the Friends of Windmill Gardens, which was established in 2003 to restore the landmarked but derelict windmill and transform its surrounding park. The restoration and landscaping, which were overseen by Dannatt Johnson Architects, took seven months to complete, and the building now looks unpretentious yet elegant, with a tasteful color scheme.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Underground | An Old Mill’s Second Wind', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': No