 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Booking | St. Pancras Renaissance, London', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe06d5ac-62a7-5d9d-8e0d-a05e161a5669', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe06d5ac-62a7-5d9d-8e0d-a05e161a5669'}, {'abstract': 'It feels as if the teams in the N.B.A. finals, Dallas and Miami, were somehow magnetically drawn to each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/sports/heat-completes-a-stirring-run-to-the-nba-finals.html', 'snippet': 'It feels as if the teams in the N.B.A. finals, Dallas and Miami, were somehow magnetically drawn to each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may consider this headquarters for Miami Heat ennui. The headquarters for hating the Heat is elsewhere (hint: try Cleveland). Here, we give the necessary nod to the Heat for an inspired run to the N.B.A. finals, for its particularly inspired comeback from a 12-point deficit in the final three minutes against the Bulls on Thursday night, for its ability to jam all of those egos onto a team bus. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stirring Trip to the Finals', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stirring Trip to the Finals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tressel, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank':