loves when an item is selling. Well, naturally, every retailer does, but for Mr. Doroff the fact that something is moving — “flying out the door,” as they say — offers proof that desires and needs are being met, however mysterious the process actually is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blinded by Brights', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed91f373-810b-5478-b191-c7c8d8f6981b', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed91f373-810b-5478-b191-c7c8d8f6981b'}, {'abstract': 'Frogs, locusts, death of the firstborn, debt crises.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/pharaohs-of-europe/', 'snippet': 'Frogs, locusts, death of the firstborn, debt crises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even fewer posts for a while, because I’m busy meeting with a bunch of men and woman in suits — and yes, I mean woman, namely Laura Tyson — on matters economic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pharaohs of Europe', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00de2414-a3b7-5079-8da0-f3498fe7f0fd', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00de2414-a3b7-5079-8da0-f3498fe7f0fd'}, {'abstract': 'Memorial Day remembrances don’t change with time, but the passage of years have made it easier for an Iraq war vet to focus on the good times he had with his fallen friend.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/remembering-mark/', 'snippet': 'Memorial Day remembrances don’t change with time, but the passage of years have made it easier for an Iraq war vet to focus on the good times he had with his fallen friend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Memorial Day remembrances don’t change with time. Every year, it’s the same stories, the same fallen friends, the same whys and what-ifs. We change, at first slowly and barely discernible and then all in a rush, but they? They stay the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Mark', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:36:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Gallagher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gallagher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6a063d3-d157-5370-ae59-990880cfe922', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6a063d3-d157-5370-ae59-990880cfe922'}, {'abstract': 'A roadside bomb targeted a United Nations convoy near a southern Lebanese port Friday, wounding several Italian peacekeepers and a Lebanese passerby, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28lebanon.html', 'snippet': 'A roadside bomb targeted a United Nations convoy near a southern Lebanese port Friday, wounding several Italian peacekeepers and a Lebanese passerby, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — A roadside bomb struck a United Nations convoy near a southern Lebanese port on Friday, wounding six Italian peacekeepers and a Lebanese passer-by in the first attack on the force in more than three years, Lebanese and Italian officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28lebanon/28lebanon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28lebanon/28lebanon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28lebanon/28lebanon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombing Attack on Peacekeepers in Lebanon Adds Another Jolt to a Region in Upheaval', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombing Attack on Peacekeepers in Lebanon Adds Another Jolt to a Region in Upheaval', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:36:35+0000', '