imes.com/2011/05/27/health/27drug.html', 'snippet': 'Thyrogen, which is used to allay side effects of treatment like depression, fatigue and confusion, is expected to be in scarce supply until July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lisa Meidl’s thyroid cancer should be easily treatable with surgery and medication. But for her and as many as 30,000 other patients, the final steps to a cure are painfully out of reach. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thyroid Drug Shortage Presents Tough Choices for Cancer Patients', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thyroid Drug Shortage Presents Tough Choices for Cancer Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thyroid Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carolyn Sayre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00c7f1cb-f309-5bb3-bf39-1e14e8fdbccc', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00c7f1cb-f309-5bb3-bf39-1e14e8fdbccc'}, {'abstract': 'Should the cutoffs change to level the kindergarten playing field?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/to-redshirt-or-not/', 'snippet': 'Should the cutoffs change to level the kindergarten playing field?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So begins an article by my colleague Winnie Hu about the process of “redshirting” — holding a child back a year so that he or she is the oldest, rather than the youngest, in kindergarten. It is a question faced by many parents whose children have fall birthdays, and Hu’s article explores the ramifications — and the proposed changes to existing rules. She writes: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Redshirt or Not', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c849840-e4a6-5fec-85dd-8fe30a11fc30', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c849840-e4a6-5fec-85dd-8fe30a11fc30'}, {'abstract': 'A list of restaurants mentioned in this article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/25/dining/a-new-food-frontier.html', 'snippet': 'A list of restaurants mentioned in this article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE ASTOR ROOM 34-12 36th Street (35th Avenue), Astoria, Queens, (718) 255-1947, astorroom.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Food Frontier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Food Frontier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/51a06aa9-8e3b-5d65-ae54-d83bc85ec001', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51a06aa9-8e3b-5d65-ae54-d83bc85ec001'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli government did not issue a statement on Egypt’s plans to open its border with Gaza, but some officials said they worried about weapons and militants flowing into the strip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28gaza.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli government did not issue a statement on Egypt’s plans to open its border with Gaza, but some officials said they worried about weapons and militants flowing into the strip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — As Egypt prepared to open its border with Gaza on Saturday, Israeli officials said they were worried about weapons and militants flowing into the Hamas-controlled strip and about what the move indicated for Egypt’s future policies. The government did not issue a statement, saying it was in contact with the Egyptian authorities and wanted to see how the change played out in practice before reacting. Others did not wait. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28gaza/28gaza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28gaza/28gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28gaza/28gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Waits and Worries Before Gaza Border Opening', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Waits and Worries Before Egypt-Gaza Border Opening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T16:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/673c67a8-8abf-5c55-b4a5-21430c83600e', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/673c67a8-8abf-5c55-b4a5-21430c83600e'}, {'abstract': 'This year about 40 percent of the new hotels in New York are opening in the Bronx, Brooklyn, Queens and Staten Island, including the Four Points by Sheraton Long Island City/Queensboro Bridge in Queens and the Hotel Williamsburg in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/many-new-york-hotels-are-opening-beyond-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'This year about 40 percent of the new hotels in New York are opening in the Bronx, Brooklyn, Queens and Staten Island, including the Four Points by Sheraton Long Island City/Queensboro Bridge in Queens and the Hotel Williamsburg in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of hotel rooms in New York City has increased by almost 24 percent in the last three years, a growth that has been driven in part by hotels in boroughs beyond Manhattan, according to NYC & Company, the official marketing, tourism and partnership organization for New York City. This year the trend continues, with \xa0about 40 percent of the new hotels in New York opening in the Bronx, Brooklyn, Queens and Staten Island.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many New York Hotels Are Opening Beyond Manhattan', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf7f9fd-18e8-5a5d-9c2c-af9e75218254', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf7f9fd-18e8-5a5d-9c2c-af9e75218254'}, {'abstract': 'It’s been a tough week; tell us a joke…', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/weekend-competition-bring-the-funny/', 'snippet': 'It’s been a tough week; tell us a joke…', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a tough week; tell us a joke…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Competition: Bring the Funny', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T17:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben