York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Governors Island turns into one big picnic on Sunday and Monday from noon to 5 p.m. (V.I.P. entrance is at 11 a.m.) for the Brewers’ Pic-NYC event, part of this year’s Meatopia festivities. There will be street food — including vendors like Fette Sau, Luke’s Lobster and Asia Dog — and beer sold at Colonels’ Row. Plates of food will be $2 to $10 and beer is $6. Tickets are $15 and proceeds will benefit Added Value farms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T17:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c09f60e-0cc4-5a43-97fa-dda7f798a926', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c09f60e-0cc4-5a43-97fa-dda7f798a926'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for Father’s Day, Fox is releasing Blu-ray editions of two films that belong to John Wayne’s late-middle period: “The Horse Soldiers” and “The Comancheros.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/movies/homevideo/the-horse-soldiers-and-the-comancheros-on-blu-ray.html', 'snippet': 'Just in time for Father’s Day, Fox is releasing Blu-ray editions of two films that belong to John Wayne’s late-middle period: “The Horse Soldiers” and “The Comancheros.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS Father’s Day draws nigh, the studios traditionally shake out their libraries for films presumed to have paternal appeal — pipe-and-slippers movies, suitable for showing on big-screen TVs in wood-paneled dens.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank