 'On the biggest stage of the N.B.A. playoffs, the spotlight will shine bright on the finals’ most riveting, star-studded matchups. How the Dallas Mavericks contend with LeBron James and Dwyane Wade, and how the Miami Heat defend against Dirk Nowitzki will go under the microscope; the highly competitive games to come will lead to an insane amount of dissection and analysis, and the magnitude of talent focused in the stars of both teams will naturally draw all attention to them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sussing Out the Other Matchups of the N.B.A. Finals', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Tyson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Terry, Jason', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:13:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7631cfef-556e-5aa4-801a-67567941124a', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7631cfef-556e-5aa4-801a-67567941124a'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since the Jan. 25 protest that kicked off the revolution, a street demonstration in Cairo took place without the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/middleeast/28egypt.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time since the Jan. 25 protest that kicked off the revolution, a street demonstration in Cairo took place without the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Tens of thousands of mostly liberal protesters again filled Tahrir Square on Friday to press for an assortment of demands in a demonstration billed as “The Revolution Part II, ” but perhaps most notable for the absence of the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28egypt/28egypt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28egypt/28egypt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28egypt/28egypt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Protest In Cairo, One Group Is Missing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Protest In Cairo, One Group Is Missing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f625e3fc-3654-5705-b12f-bd5af5188603', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f625e3fc-3654-5705-b12f-bd5af5188603'}, {'abstract': 'The historian David McCullough talks about his new book “The Greater Journey: Americans in Paris.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/book-review-podcast-david-mccullough-and-gretchen-morgenson/', 'snippet': 'The historian David McCullough talks about his new book “The Greater Journey: Americans in Paris.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week the historian David McCullough talks about his new book, “The Greater Journey: Americans in Paris;” the business reporter Gretchen Morgenson, co-author of\xa0 “Reckless Endangerment,” describes the causes of the Wall Street implosion; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; and Jennifer Schuessler has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host. (Podcast Archive) // ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast:  David McCullough and Gretchen Morgenson', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCullough, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b755c8-5c21-515e-b447-9ab4b4ecaebd', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b755c8-5c21-515e-b447-9ab4b4ecaebd'}, {'abstract': 'Robin Rusch had a habit of making it up as she went along. So it wasn’t surprising that she fell for someone who makes a business of improvisation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/robin-rusch-and-thomas-heberer-vows.html', 'snippet': 'Robin Rusch had a habit of making it up as she went along. So it wasn’t surprising that she fell for someone who makes a business of improvisation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHETHER bartending, dishwashing or working at a foreign record label to support her world travels, Robin Dolphé Rusch had a habit of making it up as she went along. So it wasn’t surprising that she fell for someone who makes a business of improvisation.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/VOWS-1/VOWS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/VOWS-1/VOWS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/VOWS-1/VOWS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/VOWS-1/VOWS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/VOWS-1/VOWS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robin Rusch and Thomas Heberer', 'kicker': 'Vows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robin Rusch and Thomas Heberer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:18:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacey Stowe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stowe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2876dc9c-625e-5951-9f62-51e64e3c5f33', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2876dc9c-625e-5951-9f62-51e64e3c5f33'}, {'abstract': 'As baby boomers hit retirement age, the problem of when to step aside is becoming a hot-button issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/business/economy/28worker.html', 'snippet': 'As baby boomers hit retirement age, the problem of when to step aside is becoming a hot-button issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the managing partner of a top Los Angeles law firm, Norman H. Levine is no stranger to what might be called the Posada problem. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/business/28worker/28worker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/business/28worker/28worker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/business/28worker/28worker-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/business/28worker/28worker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/business/28worker/28worker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Easing Out the Gray-Haired. Or Not.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Easing Out the Gray-Haired. Or Not.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:21:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5867c8c6-bd3c-53b3-867f-a1b6c54bc0c8', 'word_count': 1560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5867c8c6-bd3c-53b3-867f-a1b6c54bc0c8'}, {'abstract': 'A tilt-shift lens does funky things to a picture’s focus and turns its subjects into miniature versions of themselves — into toy figurines, really.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/its-not-the-pictures-that-got-small/', 'snippet': 'A tilt-shift lens does funky things to a picture’s focus and turns its subjects into miniature versions of themselves — into toy figurines, really.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sports Illustrated featured this striking picture across two pages last week. It’s quite winning in a couple of senses. Not only does it capture the strike, ball in midflight, that would win Manchester City its first championship (England’s F.A. Cup) in more than three decades, it is also rather charming. This tends to happen when a photographer uses a tilt-shift lens. It does funky things to a picture’s focus and turns its subjects into miniature versions of themselves — into toy figurines, really.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not the Pictures That Got Small', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:26:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e11a827-a937-5038-a0f6-ca20f90a02ec', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e11a827-a937-5038-a0f6-ca20f90a02ec'}, {'abstract': 'Stanislas Wawrinka of Switzerland came from two sets down to beat Jo-Wilfried Tsonga of France, 4-6, 6-7 (3), 7-6 (5), 6-2, 6-3.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/wawrinka-comes-back-to-beat-tsonga/', 'snippet': 'Stanislas Wawrinka of Switzerland came from two sets down to beat Jo-Wilfried Tsonga of France, 4-6, 6-7 (3), 7-6 (5), 6-2, 6-3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – Stanislas Wawrinka of Switzerland hit two aces to reach two match points but Jo-Wilfried Tsonga of France refused to fold until Wawrinka slashed an inside-out forehand into a corner for a comeback five-set victory, 4-6, 6-7 (3), 7-6 (5), 6-2, 6-3, on Friday at the French Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wawrinka Comes Back to Beat Tsonga', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fr