': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29explorer-span/29explorer-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29explorer-span/Explorer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29explorer-span/29explorer-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29explorer-span/29explorer-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Collecting Wellfleet Oysters With the Best', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Collecting Wellfleet Oysters With the Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oysters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wellfleet (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Pergament', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pergament', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d0375c5-5e8e-5fe7-9b38-38dee69c2a02', 'word_count': 1595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d0375c5-5e8e-5fe7-9b38-38dee69c2a02'}, {'abstract': 'Lavish homegrown meals are just one aspect of a three-day stay with a family in the Georgian wine village of Tsinandali.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/travel/in-former-soviet-georgia-two-families-and-the-art-of-hospitality.html', 'snippet': 'Lavish homegrown meals are just one aspect of a three-day stay with a family in the Georgian wine village of Tsinandali.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FIRST the roasted eggplant arrived, topped with walnut paste and pomegranate seeds, followed by seared red peppers glistening with oil, and a salad of cucumbers and tomatoes, scattered with herbs. Then bread from a nearby kiln, a soul mate for the homemade cheese, which was akin to mozzarella with a sour kick. The two women of the house soon shuttled in with carafes of red and white wine, squeezed from grapes tended on the surrounding land and coaxed to life in cisterns out back. It was a fine finale — or so we thought — for our first lunch at a small farmstead in Georgia, the fertile backyard of the former Soviet Union.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29journeys/29journeys-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29journeys/29journeys-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29journeys/Journeys-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29journeys/29journeys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/travel/29journeys/29journeys-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Former Soviet Georgia, Two Families and the 