'snippet': 'Mr. Bloom will reprise his role from Mr. Jackson’s “Lord of the Rings” movies as the elf Legolas, even though that character doesn’t appear in J. R. R. Tolkien’s original “Hobbit” novel.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Would you cast someone to play Anna Karenina in a film version of “War and Peace”? Bring in Tom Joad to spruce up your “Of Mice and Men” movie? Or add Jack Pumpkinhead to the roster of “The Wizard of Oz”? Probably not if you know what’s good for you, but that hasn’t discouraged Peter Jackson from risking the wrath of the literary-adaptation gods by announcing that he has added his “Lord of the Rings” star Orlando Bloom to the cast of his “Hobbit” movies, even though Mr. Bloom’s character, the elf Legolas, doesn’t appear in J. R. R. Tolkien’s original “Hobbit” novel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tempting Fate and Tolkien Purists, Peter Jackson Adds Orlando Bloom to ‘The Hobbit’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Orlando', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolkien, J R R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T18:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/684073c4-1ad5-5f1e-9dc6-7d4dd2afe440', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/684073c4-1ad5-5f1e-9dc6-7d4dd2afe440'}, {'abstract': 'The Irish government still owns 25 percent of Aer Lingus, but the company’s chief executive, Christoph Mueller, says, “I believe we are ready to finally leave the parents behind.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/business/global/28air.html', 'snippet': 'The Irish government still owns 25 percent of Aer Lingus, but the company’s chief executive, Christoph Mueller, says, “I believe we are ready to finally leave the parents behind.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — Christoph Mueller, the chief executive of Aer Lingus, accompanied the Irish prime minister, Enda Kenny, and other officials on Friday on a flight aboard a restored 1936 De Havilland Dragon to observe the 75th anniversary of the airline’s first scheduled service. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/business/Air/Air-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stronger Aer Lingus Says It Is Ready to Fly Solo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stronger Aer Lingus Says It Is Ready for Irish Government to Sell Its Remaining Stake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Enda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ryanair Holdings PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AER LINGUS AIRLINES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-