san Dominus’s story about Krista and Tatiana Hogan said that they would be interested in seeing images of the girls’ unusual neural anatomy. Here is a brain image provided to The Times by the twins’ neurosurgeon, Douglas Cochrane of British Columbia Children’s Hospital. The attenuated line stretching between the two organs is what he refers to as the “thalamic bridge” that may allow them to share sensory perception.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conjoined Twins: Brain Imaging', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dominus, Susan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T19:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Kern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a78fb7c-54e1-5196-bd13-37cd85575c27', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a78fb7c-54e1-5196-bd13-37cd85575c27'}, {'abstract': 'We’ve got the one summer sandal style to last through Labor Day from day to night.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/summer-sandal-espadrille/', 'snippet': 'We’ve got the one summer sandal style to last through Labor Day from day to night.', 'lead_paragraph': ' NYTD.fullScreenSlideShowFactory.createSlideshow("#96", 592, 400, true, chameleonData);', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Sandal: Espadrille', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr