terial': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e2fcf065-2c10-5fc9-8b73-925638f26203', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e2fcf065-2c10-5fc9-8b73-925638f26203'}, {'abstract': 'Predictions are now that her album “Born This Way” will be the fastest-selling since 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/amazon-has-forecasters-rethinking-lady-gaga/', 'snippet': 'Predictions are now that her album “Born This Way” will be the fastest-selling since 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sales estimates for Lady Gaga’s new album keep going up and up. The latest projection: 1.15 million, according to the data-crunchers at Billboard magazine, which would make it the fastest-selling album in at least six years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Has Forecasters Rethinking Lady Gaga', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BILLBOARD', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interscope', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T19:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf42fa2b-4668-5657-998a-76ef7a98895f', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf42fa2b-4668-5657-998a-76ef7a98895f'}, {'abstract': 'Chastain was a ray of light in a Roland Mouret dress, at the “The Tree of Life” premiere in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/look-of-the-moment-jessica-chastain/', 'snippet': 'Chastain was a ray of light in a Roland Mouret dress, at the “The Tree of Life” premiere in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Ray of Light – muted green tones are enriched with a burst of neon chartreuse providing a bold, but balanced contrast.The Girl: Jessica Chastain, one of the stars of “The Tree of Life,” which won this year’s Cannes Film Festival’s Palme d’Or award, at the film’s premiere at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of the Moment | Jessica Chastain', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70835850-c8d6-5c1c-b275-11190dbb9ef0', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70835850-c8d6-5c1c-b275-11190dbb9ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Conaway, who earned praise as Kenickie, John Travolta’s bad-boy sidekick in the film version of “Grease,” was known to have an addiction to alcohol and drugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/arts/television/jeff-conaway-actor-in-taxi-and-grease-dies-at-60.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Conaway, who earned praise as Kenickie, John Travolta’s bad-boy sidekick in the film version of “Grease,” was known to have an addiction to alcohol and drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff Conaway, the personable actor who won television fame on the sitcom “Taxi” and movie success in the musical “Grease” three decades ago and who later publicly struggled with drug and alcohol abuse, died on Friday in Los Angeles. He was 60.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/obituaries/28conaway2_inline/28conaway2_inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/obituaries/28conaway2_inline/28conaway2_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/obituaries/28conaway2_inline/28conaway2_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeff Conaway, Actor In ‘Taxi,’ Is Dead at 60', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeff Conaway, Actor In ‘Taxi,’ Is Dead at 60', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conaway, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b11437b-0937-57c5-b40a-7955ddb353a2', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b11437b-0937-57c5-b40a-7955ddb353a2'}, {'abstract': 'Morning Line for Friday, May 27', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/morning-line-waiting-on-shackleford/', 'snippet': 'Morning Line for Friday, May 27', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Triple Crown news focuses on the fact that Shackleford, the winner of the Preakness, seems more likely than not to run in the Belmont Stakes on Saturday June 11. Shackleford is headed for the Big Apple with the Blood-Horse writing “Shackleford is expected to ship to New York in the next couple of days and will have a workout over the Belmont track before a final decision is made about running in the June 11 Belmont Stakes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: Waiting on Shackleford', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df36a969-7ddb-55a7-b439-2a42b6970e1d', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df36a969-7ddb-55a7-b439-2a42b6970e1d'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Ayoade, the director of "Submarine," discusses a scene from his film about an awkward teenager and his first love.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000000838902/anatomy-of-a-scene-submarine.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Ayoade, the director of "Submarine," discusses a scene from his film about an awkward teenager and his first love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Ayoade, the director of "Submarine," discusses a scene from his film about an awkward teenager and his first love.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/video-submarine-scene/video-submarine-scene-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/video-submarine-scene/video-submarine-scene-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/video-submarine-scene/video-submarine-scene-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/arts/video-submarine-scene/video-submarine-scene-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "Anatomy of a Scene: 'Submarine'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8044d5e7-5899-565a-9454-ac7ec68e34a7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8044d5e7-5899-565a-9454-ac7ec68e34a7'}, {'abstract': 'I don’t always highlight the magazine’s cover stories because, well, they’re on the cover.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/this-sunday-our-thing-for-twins/', 'snippet': 'I don’t always highlight the magazine’s cover stories because, well, they’re on the cover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t always highlight the magazine’s cover stories because, well, they’re on the cover. Of course, we think they’re brilliant and worth every minute of your Sunday morning (or whenever). But this week’s cover story, about conjoined twins Tatiana and Krista Hogan, deserves every extra little bit of attention I can bring to it. I expect that the cover picture will make some people squeamish. But I urge those of you who feel that way to get past it and read Susan Dominus’s powerful story. It won’t make you feel bad, I promise. It’s a story about the richness and complexity of human life. There really is something miraculous about these girls, and though the challenges they face are daunting, this is the life they have to live, and it is not without joy and love.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Sunday: Our Thing for Twins', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:10:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b103a50e-0a36-5b4b-9c8f-9fe18af44d91', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b103a50e-0a36-5b4b-9c8f-9fe18af44d91'}, {'abstract': 'What we can glean from Friday’s match is that Roger Federer will be looking to attack and come forward more in the second week.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/analysis-federer-goes-on-the-attack/', 'snippet': 'What we can glean from Friday’s match is that Roger Federer will be looking to attack and come forward more in the second week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roger Federer defeated Janko Tipsarevic in straight sets, mauling the feisty Serb with pinpoint serving and aggressive all-court tennis. Tipsarevic has a penchant for scoring upsets in Grand Slams, but Federer broke serve early in the first and played with great variety and imagination to run 