 be common, yet it’s slipping to extinction under our noses,” a conservationist says. [The Independent]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Habitat Loss and Climate Change Imperil Koala', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three Gorges Dam (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Provence (France)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Collins Rudolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Collins', 'lastname': 'Rudolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a96e1d6d-e8a3-5e13-9c69-f4db693d3e83', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a96e1d6d-e8a3-5e13-9c69-f4db693d3e83'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column lays out the common mistakes employers make in managing household staff.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/a-reminder-on-how-to-treat-the-household-staff/', 'snippet': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column lays out the common mistakes employers make in managing household staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, discusses the mistakes made by people who employ household help — anyone from housekeepers and nannies to chefs, butlers and estate managers. Nor is this an issue just for the wealthy anymore, Paul writes, because many two-income couples rely on an array of workers to keep their households going.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reminder on How to Treat the Household Staff', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-27T20:37:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43f737b3-435a-577b-a458-fe825a247115', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43f737b3-435a-577b-a458-fe825a247115'}, {'abstract': 'While fashion has evolved from its rigid dictates, it’s as true today as it ever was: after Memorial Day, white rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000000838728/on-the-street--snow-days.html', 'snippet': 'While fashion has evolved from its rigid dictates, it’s as true today as it ever was: after Memorial Day, white rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While fashion has evolved from its rigid dictates, it’s as true today as it ever was: after Memorial Day, white rules.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/fashion/video-onthestreet/video-onthestreet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail