rson': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ca67736-5463-5e70-a614-90d4f72096c3', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ca67736-5463-5e70-a614-90d4f72096c3'}, {'abstract': 'Students who went through a second round in New York City’s high school admission process have now been told where they’ll attend class next fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/belated-good-news-on-high-school-admissions-for-some-in-ny.html', 'snippet': 'Students who went through a second round in New York City’s high school admission process have now been told where they’ll attend class next fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This time when Radcliffe Saddler got his envelope at school on Friday afternoon, it was thin and feather-light, and he sensed it was good news. It also meant the end of a painful process that weighed on his family and occupied nearly his entire eighth-grade year. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29UPDATE/29UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29UPDATE/29UPDATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29UPDATE/29UPDATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29UPDATE/29UPDATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29UPDATE/29UPDATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Some Eighth Graders, Belated Good News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Some Eighth Graders, Belated Good News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/588f485a-0e44-54ad-a5cb-37dd0332b88d', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/588f485a-0e44-54ad-a5cb-37dd0332b88d'}, {'abstract': 'All sorts of little happenings here and there in the paddock in Monaco on the traditional down day of Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/a-day-off-at-the-monaco-grand-prix/', 'snippet': 'All sorts of little happenings here and there in the paddock in Monaco on the traditional down day of Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONACO – Friday is the down day in Monaco, with no track action and an almost empty paddock. Well, not quite. Today it has turned into a kind of Cannes festival Part II. Cannes ended last week, but I heard today that Leonardo DiCaprio is somewhere around here in Monaco. Kim Kardashian, the socialite and actress, and the New Jersey Nets forward Kris Humphries have also been around, and today we also had the Spanish model Esther Canadas completely sucking up the attention of all the TV cameras and photographers outside of the McLaren Mercedes motor home on the arm of Jenson Button.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day Off at the Monaco Grand Prix', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humphries, Kris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:08:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6459a07e-58df-51b8-bb31-0b0fc59328a1', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6459a07e-58df-51b8-bb31-0b0fc59328a1'}, {'abstract': 'All sorts of little happenings here and there in the paddock in Monaco on the traditional down day of Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/27/a-day-off-at-the-monaco-grand-prix/', 'snippet': 'All sorts of little happenings here and there in the paddock in Monaco on the traditional down day of Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONACO – Friday is the down day in Monaco, with no track action and an almost empty paddock. Well, not quite. Today it has turned into a kind of Cannes festival Part II. Cannes ended last week, but I heard today that Leonardo DiCaprio is somewhere around here in Monaco. Kim Kardashian, the socialite and actress, and the New Jersey Nets forward Kris Humphries have also been around, and today we also had the Spanish model Esther Canadas completely sucking up the attention of all the TV cameras and photographers outside of the McLaren Mercedes motor home on the arm of Jenson Button.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day Off at the Monaco Grand Prix', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humphries, Kris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:08:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99b1641d-1b26-5e5e-9a50-80ad830f132d', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99b1641d-1b26-5e5e-9a50-80ad830f132d'}, {'abstract': 'After Miami gained the title in 2006, the Heat’s point guard took winning for granted. Now Dwyane Wade knows better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/sports/basketball/a-wiser-dwyane-wade-returns-to-the-nba-finals.html', 'snippet': 'After Miami gained the title in 2006, the Heat’s point guard took winning for granted. Now Dwyane Wade knows better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June 2006, Dwyane Wade was a buoyant, boyish 24-year-old with an armful of shiny trophies and a perfectly naïve vision of the future. The Miami Heat had just claimed the N.B.A. championship, with Wade as the most valuable player. And Wade was certain — absolutely certain — that he was on the precipice of something great and enduring.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/beck-1/beck-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/beck-1/beck-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/beck-1/beck-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/beck-1/beck-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/beck-1/beck-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Time, Wade Knows How Hard It Is to Win a Title', 'kicker': 'On Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Time, Wade Knows How Hard It Is to Win a Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:12:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c9a445-6997-56f2-a18d-ec2c67c702c7', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c9a445-6997-56f2-a18d-ec2c67c702c7'}, {'abstract': 'The influence of religion on “The Oprah Winfrey Show” was easy to see, but the lessons Ms. Winfrey shared with her flock were sometimes questionable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/us/28beliefs.html', 'snippet': 'The influence of religion on “The Oprah Winfrey Show” was easy to see, but the lessons Ms. Winfrey shared with her flock were sometimes questionable.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Oprah Winfrey Show” ended Wednesday, bringing despair to booksellers who relied on her book club, television programmers who needed her ratings, and religion scholars who for a decade have tried explaining how this child of poverty became the leader of a worldwide cult. They have worked just as hard to define that cult, which is at once Christian and pantheistic, African-American in origin but global in reach.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/Y-BELIEFS/Y-BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 955, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/Y-BELIEFS/Y-BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/Y-BELIEFS/Y-BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Church of Oprah Winfrey and a Theology of Suffering', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Church of Oprah Winfrey and a Theology of Suffering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edward, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, Rhonda', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hay, Louise', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:12:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7df5b865-5a71-583c-8ac7-1742564eca3f', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7df5b865-5a71-583c-8ac7-1742564eca3f'}, {'abstract': 'With a few offhand words, Gov. Rick Perry joined a list of Republican leaders who are testing the waters for 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/us/politics/28perry.html', 'snippet': 'With a few offhand words, Gov. Rick Perry joined a list of Republican leaders who are testing the waters for 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — The ritual of reporters asking Gov. Rick Perry if he is running for president and getting a firm no has become so entrenched in Texas that jaws dropped Friday afternoon when Mr. Perry abruptly changed his tune — slightly — and hinted that he might run after all. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/us/PERRY/PERRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/us/PERRY/PERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/us/PERRY/PERRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Governor Hints at G.O.P. Run for White House', 'kicker