': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/27/opinion/video-bhisrael/video-bhisrael-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/27/opinion/video-bhisrael/video-bhisrael-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barack vs. Bibi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/45bef5f2-bd77-5d9f-99cb-b0d9febe156d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/45bef5f2-bd77-5d9f-99cb-b0d9febe156d'}, {'abstract': 'In Fort Greene and Clinton Hill in Brooklyn on Monday, a string of thefts left several homes without their heavy, metal gates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/nyregion/ignoring-homes-thieves-make-off-with-just-their-gates.html', 'snippet': 'In Fort Greene and Clinton Hill in Brooklyn on Monday, a string of thefts left several homes without their heavy, metal gates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hers was the hand of a little girl, smooth and quick, when she first learned to open that little iron gate. That was half a century ago, and while the hand aged — deeper wrinkles, better nails — the gate remained constant, its creak sounding the arrival of visitors like a doorbell and as much a part of the home on Vanderbilt Avenue as the brownstone walls themselves. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ignoring Homes, Thieves Make Off With Just the Gates Guarding Them', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ignoring Homes, Thieves Make Off With Just the Gates Guarding Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Clinton Hill (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Greene (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T00:22:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccabcba5-02da-549a-8b8f-22177231f3cd', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccabcba5-02da-549a-8b8f-22177231f3cd'}, {'abstract': 'The acquittal of Franklin L. Mata and Kenneth Morena, police officers charged with sexual assault, elicited emotions ranging from outrage to resignation among city residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/nyregion/reacting-to-police-rape-case-with-anger-but-little-surprise.html', 'snippet': 'The acquittal of Franklin L. Mata and Kenneth Morena, police officers charged with sexual assault, elicited emotions ranging from outrage to resignation among city residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a trial that bared some anxieties that run just below the city’s surface: the weakness of a drunken memory; the vulnerability of ordinary residents to abuse from the powerful, especially in a police uniform. For nearly two months, New Yorkers followed a courtroom drama that held all the fascination of a television crime series, with intimate sexual detail and a haunting void at its center into which they could project their own fears or anger. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/JP-RAPE/JP-RAPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/JP-RAPE/JP-RAPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/JP-RAPE/JP-RAPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reacting to Police Rape Case With Anger, but Little Surprise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Acquittals in Rape Case, New Yorkers Express Anger but Little Surprise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mata, Franklin L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':