ce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/AIRSHOW3/AIRSHOW3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/AIRSHOW3/AIRSHOW3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/nyregion/AIRSHOW3/AIRSHOW3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Adding Thrills When Flying Upside Down Just Isn’t Enough', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adding Thrills When Flying Upside Down Just Isn&#8217;t Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stunts and Stuntmen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR SHOWS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T01:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Negroni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Negroni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89f27b07-7f10-537d-88d4-b14d63540faf', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89f27b07-7f10-537d-88d4-b14d63540faf'}, {'abstract': 'An uncomfortable week that ended with a $200 million cash infusion does not seem that bad for Fred Wilpon, who still gets to control the Mets. So where has he been?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/sports/baseball/wilpons-sudden-silence-speaks-volumes-about-his-style.html', 'snippet': 'An uncomfortable week that ended with a $200 million cash infusion does not seem that bad for Fred Wilpon, who still gets to control the Mets. So where has he been?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fred Wilpon has called his team lousy and snakebitten. He has mocked Carlos Beltran, dismissed Jose Reyes’s earning power and said that his most marketable player, David Wright, is not a superstar. He has acknowledged that his Mets are bleeding cash. Yet his dreary portrait of the product was not enough to deter David Einhorn from giving Wilpon $200 million for a piece of it.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/jp-kepner/jp-kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/jp-kepner/jp-kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/jp-kepner/jp-kepner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/jp-kepner/jp-kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/sports/jp-kepner/jp-kepner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilpon’s Sudden Silence Speaks Volumes About His Style', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suddenly, Strikingly, Wilpon Is Silent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T01:08:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c831a0-c48f-53d2-9850-cc015863684e', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c831a0-c48f-53d2-9850-cc015863684e'}, {'abstract': 'For many Serbs, who are struggling with a very weak economy and high joblessness rates of some 20 percent, the arrest of Ratko Mladic is an ambivalent, even irrelevant moment for their near future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/world/europe/28serbia.html', 'snippet': 'For many Serbs, who are struggling with a very weak economy and high joblessness rates of some 20 percent, the arrest of Ratko Mladic is an ambivalent, even irrelevant moment for their near future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELGRADE, Serbia — The tall building that served as the headquarters for the late Slobodan Milosevic’s political party, bombed by an American cruise missile in the 1999 Kosovo war, has been privatized and rebuilt, covered now in blue-green glass. Before 1990, it was home to the Communist Party Central Committee; now it houses offices, including Western banks, and a modish shopping center.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28serbia/28serbia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28serbia/28serbia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28serbia/28serbia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28serbia/28serbia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/world/28serbia/28serbia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arrest Follows Serbia’s Uneven Path to Break With Its Past', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arrest Follows Serbia’s Uneven Path to Break With Its Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tadic, Boris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T01:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d71b9a02-c349-5e5b-b0de-ab55a847903d', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d71b9a02-c349-5e5b-b0de-ab55a847903d'}, {'abstract': 'The Mississippi tells us, again, to change the way we manage water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/opinion/28sat1.html', 'snippet': 'The Mississippi tells us, again, to change the way we manage water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The thousands of people forced to abandon their homes in recent weeks to floodwaters are victims not just of nature but of human error as well. Years of mismanagement of the vast Mississippi River ecosystem — the relentless and often inadvisable construction of levees and navigation channels, the paving over of wetlands, the commercial development of flood plains — have made the damage worse than it might otherwise have been.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Flood, Some Old Truths', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Flood, Some Old Truths: The Mississippi tells us, again, to change the way we manage water', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T01:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eaac9cb-1528-5b13-9384-3baccc4f71ef', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eaac9cb-1528-5b13-9384-3baccc4f71ef'}, {'abstract': 'Candidates with electoral resumes as thin as Herman Cain’s have very poor track records, but candidates with polling that looks like Mr. Cain’s despite low name recognition have an exceptionally good track record. We can’t really resolve this empirically.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/