ar’s special election for the late Senator Edward M. Kennedy’s seat, it seemed his tenure could be brief. Massachusetts is a left-leaning state, after all, where larger-than-life Democrats have run for president or become Washington power players. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/us/MASS-1/MASS-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/28/us/MASS-1/MASS-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/us/MASS-1/MASS-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/28/us/MASS-1/MASS-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/28/us/MASS-1/MASS-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Republican Stays Connected in Democratic Massachusetts', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Republican Stays Connected in Democratic Massachusetts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Deval L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Edward M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T03:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d6fbe1-7c16-5acc-a95d-c69d41cc4032', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d6fbe1-7c16-5acc-a95d-c69d41cc4032'}, {'abstract': 'Offerings in the Gold Coast International Film Festival include the documentary “Chasing Madoff” and Gérard Depardieu in “My Afternoons With Margueritte.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/new-li-festival-begins-offers-65-films-in-5-days.html', 'snippet': 'Offerings in the Gold Coast International Film Festival include the documentary “Chasing Madoff” and Gérard Depardieu in “My Afternoons With Margueritte.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Regina Keller Gil began to shape the Gold Coast International Film Festival — it opens Wednesday and runs for five days in five North Shore communities — she was already well aware of the power of movies to bring out a crowd. As the executive director of the Great Neck Arts Center, whose offerings include film, “I can fill an auditorium at a multiplex on a Thursday night, every week,” she said recently.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29FILM-LI/29FILM-LI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29FILM-LI/29FILM-LI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c