 Art in Huntington, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it too much to say that the history of 20th-century art can be read through its attitude toward toilets? Perhaps. But evidence that toilets played at least a cameo role is on view in “Edward Weston: Life Work” at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29ARTSLI2/29ARTSLI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29ARTSLI2/29ARTSLI2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29ARTSLI2/29ARTSLI2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beguiled by Humble Objects Like Peppers and Toilets', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beguiled by Humble Objects Like Peppers and Toilets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heckscher Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T03:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/00afb1c8-390d-5dc7-9b32-68021fc25f65', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://art