of Pakistan Restaurant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '8 Die in Bombing of Pakistan Restaurant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T11:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59fe6e47-d9e8-5f32-bbf4-023f0be32ed4', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59fe6e47-d9e8-5f32-bbf4-023f0be32ed4'}, {'abstract': 'It turns out Mr. Gingrich has operated at least five companies.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/newt-gingrich-small-business-owner/', 'snippet': 'It turns out Mr. Gingrich has operated at least five companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Sunday, Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker and current Republican presidential candidate, told America that he was a small-business owner. The revelation came on CBS’s “Face the Nation,” as the candidate tried to deflect questions (PDF) from Bob Schieffer, the host, about his recently revealed debts to Tiffany and Company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newt Gingrich, Small-Business Owner', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T12:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca80dea-16a4-52cb-91e6-b0452bf509e7', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca80dea-16a4-52cb-91e6-b0452bf509e7'}, {'abstract': 'Blue-collar conservatives and the backlash against Ryancare.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/medicare-and-the-disaffected-vote/', 'snippet': 'Blue-collar conservatives and the backlash against Ryancare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the NY-26 election, both Henry Olson and Jonathan Chait pointed out that the constituency most resistant to Paul Ryan’s Medicare reforms seems to be conservative-leaning blue collar voters — what the Pew Research Center, in a recent report, calls the “Disaffecteds.” (This is a cohort that I mentioned in my column on Mike Huckabee’s appeal, and it overlaps to some degree with the “Sam’s Club Republicans” that Reihan Salam and I spent a whole book talking about.) Chait calls this “the demographic group that should terrify Republicans,” because they’re a crucial constituency for the right-of-center coalition, but they’re also more resistant to cutting Medicare and Social Security than most Democratic-leaning groups.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare and the “Disaffected” Vote', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T12:25:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/657d2f35-d8e9-54ab-b32a-6632af55cab1', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/657d2f35-d8e9-54ab-b32a-6632af55cab1'}, {'abstract': 'Having Juan Martin Del Potro back in the mix in a Grand Slam adds excitement to the men’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/del-potro-returns-to-competitive-form/', 'snippet': 'Having Juan Martin Del Potro back in the mix in a Grand Slam adds excitement to the men’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I watched the first two sets of the Djokovic-Del Potro match searching for any sign of weakness in the tall Argentine’s game. I found none, and in fact felt that he had Djokovic on the defensive when the match was called in the waning light on Friday night. Despite a year’s absence from the tour, and a comeback interrupted by a slight tear high in the quadricep that put his return to Roland Garros in doubt, Del Potro served well, hit out with authority on his ground strokes, and competed fearlessly against the tour’s dominant player. Having Del Potro back in the mix in a Grand Slam adds excitement to the men’s game, and Saturday’s continuation of the match has tennis fans buzzing over the high quality of the first two sets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Del Potro Returns to Competitive Form', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T13:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f33621-5e8e-5943-a949-dfffc1f6be00', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f33621-5e8e-5943-a949-dfffc1f6be00'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal of Spain used his potent forehand and a strong-arm backhand service return to move easily into the fourth round of the French Open Saturday. He defeated Antonio Veic of Croatia, the world’s 227th ranked player,  6-1, 6-3, 6-0.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/28/nadal-advances-to-the-fourth-round/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal of Spain used his potent forehand and a strong-arm backhand service return to move easily into the fourth round of the French Open Saturday. He defeated Antonio Veic of Croatia, the world’s 227th ranked player,  6-1, 6-3, 6-0.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – Rafael Nadal of Spain used his potent forehand and a strong-arm backhand service return to move easily into the fourth round of the French Open Saturday. He defeated Antonio Veic of Croatia, the world’s 227th ranked player, 6-1, 6-3, 6-0.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nadal Advances to the Fourth Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T13:32:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88f7948f-065e-5563-aacd-bc25ee60ff2f', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88f7948f-065e-5563-aacd-bc25ee60ff2f'}, {'abstract': 'Visiting Warsaw, the president said Poland’s peaceful overthrow of Communism provided lessons for countries struggling with the chaotic aftermath of popular revolts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/world/europe/29prexy.html', 'snippet': 'Visiting Warsaw, the president said Poland’s peaceful overthrow of Communism provided lessons for countries struggling with the chaotic aftermath of popular revolts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW — President Obama held up Poland on Saturday as a model for Arab nations undergoing political change, saying its peaceful overthrow of Communism held lessons for Tunisia and other Arab countries grappling with the chaotic aftermath of popular revolts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/world/29obama-span/29obama-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/world/29obama-span/29obama-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/world/29obama-span/29obama-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/world/29obama-span/29obama-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/world/29obama-span/29obama-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Cites Poland as Model for Arab Shift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': N