r weapons materials because of problems between two arms of the Energy Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The United States is running out of a rare gas that is crucial for detecting smuggled nuclear weapons materials because one arm of the Energy Department was selling the gas six times as fast as another arm could accumulate it, and the two sides failed to communicate for years, according to a new Congressional audit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agencies’ Lack of Coordination Hindered Supply of Crucial Gas, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agencies’ Lack of Coordination Hindered Supply of Crucial Gas, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T16:45:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92e34c69-c8c9-5fbf-aade-2bd7cefdfc9d', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92e34c69-c8c9-5fbf-aade-2bd7cefdfc9d'}, {'abstract': 'Brand, a scholar of American literature who was chairman of the English department at Hofstra University, wrote of fans’ “delight and despair.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/sports/baseball/dana-brand-the-proust-of-mets-bloggers-dies-at-56.html', 'snippet': 'Brand, a scholar of American literature who was chairman of the English department at Hofstra University, wrote of fans’ “delight and despair.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'He was 7 ½ years old, sitting in his room, riveted to his family’s portable radio and wearing his little plastic baseball glove. It was 1962, and Dana Brand was listening to the Mets’ inaugural game, and so began a love affair that would last until his death on Wednesday at 56. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/dogBRAND-obit/dogBRAND-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/dogBRAND-obit/dogBRAND-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/dogBRAND-obit/dogBRAND-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dana Brand, Who Blogged of Mets Fans’ Delight and Despair, Dies at 56', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dana Brand, 56; Blogged of Mets Fans’ Delight and Despair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T16:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': No