44-be6b9bbeb655'}, {'abstract': 'Alba’s Italian restaurant in Port Chester is hardly hip, but it will probably continue to please long after trendier spots have faded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/albas-italian-restaurant-in-port-chester-review.html', 'snippet': 'Alba’s Italian restaurant in Port Chester is hardly hip, but it will probably continue to please long after trendier spots have faded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER almost a year of serious remodeling, Alba’s doors reopened last September onto a spiffy space with an upscale yet homey look. Done tastefully in muted tones with white architectural detailing, the large dining room is defined subtly by the varied shapes of large Oriental-style rugs that add softness and a touch of luxury.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINEWE1/29DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINEWE1/29DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINEWE1/29DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old-School Italian in a Spruced-Up Space', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Port Chester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old-School Italian In a Spruced-Up Space', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7517e8e-00bb-5bfc-8e0b-1264f23a4b30', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7517e8e-00bb-5bfc-8e0b-1264f23a4b30'}, {'abstract': 'The Freight House Cafe offers coffee, soup, sandwiches and a garage-sale eclectic décor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/freight-house-cafe-offers-food-coffee-and-charm.html', 'snippet': 'The Freight House Cafe offers coffee, soup, sandwiches and a garage-sale eclectic décor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you roll in from the Putnam County Trailway bike path or stroll in from the nearby Putnam Music Center, the laid-back Freight House Cafe is a nifty place to unwind or rewind — a charming piece of history set well back from the busy traffic of Route 6.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid a Bit of Railroad History', 'kicker': 'Quick Bite | Mahopac', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid a Bit of Railroad History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:12:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. H. Reed', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1da50db9-606e-5932-bc87-b2f5c9dbdba0', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1da50db9-606e-5932-bc87-b2f5c9dbdba0'}, {'abstract': 'A showcase in Brooklyn offered a chance to sample wines from more than two dozen producers who have kept a low profile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/boutique-long-island-wines-on-parade-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'A showcase in Brooklyn offered a chance to sample wines from more than two dozen producers who have kept a low profile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brooklyn Uncorked, a wine-and-food showcase at the Brooklyn Academy of Music this month, offered a chance to sample recent wines of Long Island boutique producers who have kept a low profile. Many of the wines\xa0were made by contract vintners from the vintners’ own or from bought grapes.\xa0', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boutique Wines on Parade', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boutique Wines on Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/60846cc0-618f-5d00-bff8-54f9b68811a2', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60846cc0-618f-5d00-bff8-54f9b68811a2'}, {'abstract': 'Lombardi’s on the Bay is a Long Island steak and seafood house offering large portions and panoramic views of Patchogue Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/lombardis-on-the-bay-review.html', 'snippet': 'Lombardi’s on the Bay is a Long Island steak and seafood house offering large portions and panoramic views of Patchogue Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORGET June 21. Summer starts this weekend, and on Long Island, summer is synonymous with water — including water views. One of the best places around to enjoy them while dining out is Lombardi’s on the Bay in Patchogue.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINELI1/29DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINELI1/29DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINELI1/29DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Steak and Seafood, and Views of a Bay', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Patchogue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steak and Seafood, And Views of a Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d1bfd08-0012-5bbc-b61b-90453360ef1c', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d1bfd08-0012-5bbc-b61b-90453360ef1c'}, {'abstract': 'If banks or credit card companies refused to settle payments with spammers’ banks, they could disrupt spam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/opinion/29sun3.html', 'snippet': 'If banks or credit card companies refused to settle payments with spammers’ banks, they could disrupt spam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early 2004 Bill Gates claimed that “two years from now, spam will be solved.” Today it amounts to 70 percent of all e-mail. Yet there may be a chance to cut it back. ', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spammers and Their Bankers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spammers and Their Bankers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spam (Electronic Mail)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:21:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6384674-f557-5a84-9a39-d45993777c3b', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6384674-f557-5a84-9a39-d45993777c3b'}, {'abstract': 'In a mission that lasted six years, the rover Spirit helped change the way we look at the red planet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/opinion/29sun4.html', 'snippet': 'In a mission that lasted six years, the rover Spirit helped change the way we look at the red planet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a final attempt last week, NASA has stopped trying to make contact with the Mars rover called Spirit, which was last heard from in March 2010 as the Martian winter was setting in. Hopes of hearing more from Spirit were slim even then, but there is a difference between not hearing and no longer listening. ', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Final Goodbye to a Mars Explorer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Final Goodbye to a Mars Explorer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f7abb83-9892-5e36-a97a-d451ea7df5a4', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f7abb83-9892-5e36-a97a-d451ea7df5a4'}, {'abstract': 'To address the looming shortage of primary care doctors, make medical school free but charge specialists for their training.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/opinion/29bach.html', 'snippet': 'To address the looming shortage of primary care doctors, make medical school free but charge specialists for their training.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOCTORS are among the most richly rewarded professionals in the country. The Bureau of Labor Statistics reports that of the 15 highest-paid professions in the United States, all but two are in medicine or dentistry.', 'print_section': 'WK', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Medical School Should Be Free', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Medical School Should Be Free', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter B. Bach and Robert Kocher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f2b75c4-76b5-5873-9487-302fee0fa174', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f2b75c4-76b5-5873-9487-302fee0fa174'}, {'abstract': 'At the Copper Canyon Restaurant in Atlantic Highlands, N.J., a welcoming atmosphere and generous portions of Southwestern cooking outweigh some steep prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/the-copper-canyon-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'At the Copper Canyon Restaurant in Atlantic Highlands, N.J., a welcoming atmosphere and generous portions of Southwestern cooking outweigh some steep prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLOSE by the beaches of Sandy Hook, Atlantic Highlands has a fairly lively eating scene, with fancy and family-style restaurants alike along the lower end of First Avenue, steps away from the town marina and Raritan Bay. If you’re not paying attention, though, you might walk right past one of the best: There is no sign outside the Copper Canyon Restaurant, just a rust-colored horseshoe logo above the door.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINENJ1/29DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINENJ1/29DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/nyregion/29DINENJ1/29DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Southwestern Fare, Inspired and Varied', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Atlantic Highlands', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Southwestern Fare, Inspired and Varied', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-28T22:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Veale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Veale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f711208d-afe4-5760-b050-ce5454094edf', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f711208d-afe4-5760-b050-ce5454094edf'}, {'abstract': 'Good Karma Cafe, a casual, cozy storefront restaurant and juice bar, tries to show “what vegan can be.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/nyregion/good-karma-cafe-in-red-bank-offers-vegan-fare.html', 'snippet': 'Good Karma Cafe, a casual, cozy storefront restaurant and juice bar, tries to show “what vegan can be.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Doherty believes in healthy eating, but she isn’t preachy about it. At Good Karma Cafe, the Red Bank restaurant and juice bar she owns with Tiffany Betts, vegan food is served with an easygoing air. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline