il', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/29FRANKLIN/29FRANKLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/fashion/weddings/29FRANKLIN/29FRANKLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christina Franklin, Steven Gersh', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christina Franklin, Steven Gersh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-29T02:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7301f865-57bd-55af-93b4-a5cc768435e6', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7301f865-57bd-55af-93b4-a5cc768435e6'}, {'abstract': '“Bridesmaids” has been hailed as a vindication of the rights and abilities of all women to make jokes, and thus a resounding rebuttal to what is supposedly a widespread assumption otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/movies/bridesmaids-allows-women-to-be-funny.html', 'snippet': '“Bridesmaids” has been hailed as a vindication of the rights and abilities of all women to make jokes, and thus a resounding rebuttal to what is supposedly a widespread assumption otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE stars of “Bridesmaids” — Kristen Wiig and Maya Rudolph, principally, with Ellie Kemper, Rose Byrne, Wendi McLendon-Covey and especially Melissa McCarthy in support — are very funny. This is not just my opinion, and it should not come as news, if the raucous laughter at a sold-out theater last weekend in Brooklyn is any indication. “Funny,” apart from being a subjective judgment, is also a commercial imperative, and it is one that “Bridesmaids” has fulfilled. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/SCOTT-3/SCOTT-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/SCOTT-3/SCOTT-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/SCOTT-3/SCOTT-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/SCOTT-3/SCOTT-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/arts/SCOTT-3/SCOTT-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Funnywoman, Alive and Well', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Funnywoman, Alive and Well', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudolph, Maya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-29T02:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstnam