g back at the 2010 season, with the benefit of film analysis. This is the final installment of the series. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2010 Chiefs: What the Film Revealed', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-29T10:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a47daa7-625a-5e4d-b966-93ce4617918e', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a47daa7-625a-5e4d-b966-93ce4617918e'}, {'abstract': 'The American painter Elizabeth Peyton is enjoying her first solo show in Paris at the Gagosian Gallery, spotlighting new paintings and drawings, through July 28.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/gagosian-hosts-peytons-first-solo-show-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'The American painter Elizabeth Peyton is enjoying her first solo show in Paris at the Gagosian Gallery, spotlighting new paintings and drawings, through July 28.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American painter Elizabeth Peyton is enjoying her first solo show in Paris at the Gagosian Gallery, spotlighting new paintings and drawings, through July 28. The gallery’s polished, high-ceilinged space (4 rue Ponthieu; 33-1-45-63-98-06; www.gagosian.com) may seem like an odd fit with Ms. Peyton’s small-scale, tightly framed portraits, but the power of her intimate style holds up in the gallery. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gagosian Hosts Peyton’s First Sol