orts', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2def645e-c633-5854-9626-3bf0a9a75fdc', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2def645e-c633-5854-9626-3bf0a9a75fdc'}, {'abstract': 'A game familiar to beachfront arcades and amusement parks is reborn as a competitive barroom pastime.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/skee-ball-played-for-fun-and-money/', 'snippet': 'A game familiar to beachfront arcades and amusement parks is reborn as a competitive barroom pastime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dressed in an orange Tony the Tiger vest and clashing red-on-black striped pants, and proudly sporting a mullet hairdo, Joe Mucha grasped ball after ball, achieving a score that reflected his years of training in the art of Skee-Ball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Skee-Ball, Played for Fun and Money', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-29T18:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfbea71c-5936-5aab-8c71-f11deb004c66', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfbea71c-5936-5aab-8c71-f11deb004c66'}, {'abstract': 'FIFA’s corruption scandal continued to widen but an ethics panel found no wrongdoing by FIFA president Sepp Blatter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/sports/soccer/two-fifa-officials-suspended-panel-clea