, after they were accused of corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/fifa-clears-blatter-and-suspends-two-others/', 'snippet': 'A FIFA ethics panel on Sunday suspended two of the organization’s most powerful figures, Mohamed bin Hammam of Qatar and Jack Warner of Trinidad and Tobago, after they were accused of corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FIFA ethics panel on Sunday suspended two of the organization’s most powerful figures, Mohamed bin Hammam of Qatar and Jack Warner of Trinidad and Tobago, after they were accused of corruption. But the panel found no wrongdoing by the FIFA president, Sepp Blatter, clearing him to run unopposed for a fourth term as president. The vote is scheduled for Wednesday. Read Jeré Longman’s article here, and a news analysis by Rob Hughes on what the ruling says about Blatter, then come back to comment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FIFA Clears Blatter and Suspends Two Others', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Hammam, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warner, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-29T23:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01a7ebb3-129e-5e19-9fff-504093d30d95', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01a7ebb3-129e-5e19-9fff-504093d30d95'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a recent article about school advocacy from the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation.', 'web_url': 'https:/