om a strain of Escherichia coli, has 400 reported cases but health officials have not determined the source.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/world/europe/30germany.html', 'snippet': 'The infection, from a strain of Escherichia coli, has 400 reported cases but health officials have not determined the source.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — With 10 people dead of infection and 400 cases reported, the European Center for Disease Prevention and Control said Sunday that a bacterial outbreak in northern Germany was one of the largest of its kind ever reported worldwide. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outbreak of Infections Kills 10 in Germany', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outbreak Of Infections In Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E Coli (Bacteria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T02:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Dempsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dempsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58261aed-72fc-5712-93eb-0efe37c67fd3', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58261aed-72fc-5712-93eb-0efe37c67fd3'}, {'abstract': 'At 61, Tom Watson became the second-oldest winner of the  Senior P.G.A. Championship when he sank a 4-foot putt on the first playoff hole to seal his victory.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/29/looking-like-his-old-self-watson-adds-another-major-title/', 'snippet': 'At 61, Tom Watson became the second-oldest winner of the  Senior P.G.A. Championship when he sank a 4-foot putt on the first playoff hole to seal his victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great players don’t forget how to do great things. When a defining moment comes, and a golfer like Tom Watson has an opportunity to win a major championship as he did on Sunday it’s just a matter of whether the body will do what the old head tells it to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Like His Old Self, Watson Adds Another Major Title', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T02:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad64895f-8592-56af-88e9-aaee8f106527', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad64895f-8592-56af-88e9-aaee8f106527'}, {'abstract': 'Troops and security forces backed by tanks stormed the locales, killing at least eight people and wounding many others, human rights groups and activists said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/world/middleeast/30syria.html', 'snippet': 'Troops and security forces backed by tanks stormed the locales, killing at least eight people and wounding many others, human rights groups and activists said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The Syrian government deployed the military and security forces to four villages and towns on Sunday, killing at least eight people and wounding many others, in the latest attempt to crush a two-month-old uprising against the leadership of President Bashar al-Assad, human rights groups and activists said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/middleeast/30syria_map/30syria_map-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 260, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Forces Struck Northern Villages, Activists Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Forces Struck Northern Villages, Activists Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T02:18:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65b4afe6-a69d-56f4-90aa-b760c68ebc76', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65b4afe6-a69d-56f4-90aa-b760c68ebc76'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Jhalanath Khanal agreed to step down as part of a deal that extended the deadline for a new constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/world/asia/30nepal.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Jhalanath Khanal agreed to step down as part of a deal that extended the deadline for a new constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATMANDU, Nepal — Nepal’s political parties averted a crisis on Sunday by reaching a last-minute deal that extended the deadline for a new constitution. Prime Minister Jhalanath Khanal agreed to step down as part of the deal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nepal Averts Crisis Over Constitution Deadline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nepal Averts Crisis Over Constitution Deadline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T02:23:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kiran Chapagain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kiran', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chapagain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef79f474-5dee-5f64-a177-02ae974c5889', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef79f474-5dee-5f64-a177-02ae974c5889'}, {'abstract': 'The president of Kazakhstan and his former son-in-law have enlisted government officials, lobbyists and others in the United States in what has been called a “blood feud.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/world/asia/30kazakhstan.html', 'snippet': 'The president of Kazakhstan and his former son-in-law have enlisted government officials, lobbyists and others in the United States in what has been called a “blood feud.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Four years ago, Kazakhstan’s foreign minister summoned the United States ambassador to a meeting in Astana, the capital of his oil-rich nation, to warn that a family squabble between the country’s president and his son-in-law — two of the country’s most powerful men — had boiled over.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/KAZAKH-1_span/KAZAKH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/30/world/KAZAKH-1_span/KAZAKH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/KAZAKH-1_span/KAZAKH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/KAZAKH-1_span/KAZAKH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/30/world/KAZAKH-1_span/KAZAKH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feud in Kazakh President’s Family Spills Into U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feud in Kazakh President’s Family Spills Into U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazarbayev, Nursultan A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kazakhstan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T02:26:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_nam