ion': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/bagapsh-obit/bagapsh-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/world/bagapsh-obit/bagapsh-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/30/world/bagapsh-obit/bagapsh-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sergei Bagapsh, Abkhazia’s Leader, Dies at 62', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sergei Bagapsh, 62, Abkhazia’s Leader, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ABKHAZIA (GEORGIAN REPUBLIC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bagapsh, Sergei V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T04:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/46104f98-c971-5271-b695-70b149fe1ab8', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46104f98-c971-5271-b695-70b149fe1ab8'}, {'abstract': 'A view of the day in sports, from the courts of Paris to the crashes in Indianapolis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/05/29/sports/SPTSREPLAY0529.html', 'snippet': 'A view of the day in sports, from the courts of Paris to the crashes in Indianapolis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A view of the day in sports, from the courts of Paris to the crashes in Indianapolis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/29/sports/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW/SPTSREPLAY0529-slide-W7ZW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: May 29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T04:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bcf70f6e-55c6-5190-b6f8-688095744e9b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bcf70f6e-55c6-5190-b6f8-688095744e9b'}, {'abstract': '“To a Restless Little Brother Calling for Mama in His Sleep,” by Victoria Ford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/us/30words.html', 'snippet': '“To a Restless Little Brother Calling for Mama in His Sleep,” by Victoria Ford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may not understand this now, but she isn’t coming back. Not tonight. Not tomorrow. Day after that. And no, she hasn’t left anything behind — a sticky note on the refrigerator door or a quick message for the answering machine, her voice a distant echo calling your name and mine. Nothing. I’m sorry because I know you get scared when the wind blows hard like this at night, when the shadows on your ceiling shuffle as if they’ve been alive all this time. But I’m right here. And the sun will not rise for another few hours and the birds outside are still sleeping —remember Johnjohn, your favorite cardinals nestled in the Sweet Gum tree down by the mailbox? The babies wrapped in small, ruby feathers. That’s how you should be right now. Dreaming and resting and not worrying.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘To a Restless Little Brother Calling for Mama in His Sleep’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘To a Restless Little Brother Calling for Mama in His Sleep’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T04:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3d23c72-6e66-5ac1-993d-79da1b842b0b', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3d23c72-6e66-5ac1-993d-79da1b842b0b'}, {'abstract': 'As more doctors abandon practice ownership and take salaried hospital jobs, their priorities are changing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/health/policy/30docs.html', 'snippet': 'As more doctors abandon practice ownership and take salaried hospital jobs, their priorities are changing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUGUSTA, Me. — With Republicans in complete control of Maine’s state government for the first time since 1962, State Senator Lois A. Snowe-Mello offered a bill in February to limit doctors’ liability that she was sure the powerful doctors’ lobby would cheer. Instead, it asked her to shelve the measure.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/us/DOCS/DOCS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/30/us/DOCS/DOCS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/30/us/DOCS/DOCS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Physicians’ Jobs Change, So Do Their Politics', 'kicker': 'Doctors Inc.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Physicians’ Jobs Change, So Do Their Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T04:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/526492d5-c43d-53b6-8d54-3b13b1494ead', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/526492d5-c43d-53b6-8d54-3b13b1494ead'}, {'abstract': 'A group of hackers took over the PBS Web site on Saturday night, posting PBS passwords and fake news stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/technology/31pbs.html', 'snippet': 'A group of hackers took over the PBS Web site on Saturday night, posting PBS passwords and fake news stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The PBS Web site briefly carried a fake article claiming that the famed rapper Tupac Shakur was alive and living in New Zealand after a group of hackers took over the organization’s computer systems on Saturday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Disrupt PBS Web Site and Post a Fake Report About a Rap Artist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hackers Disrupt PBS Web Site and Post a Fake Report About a Rap Artist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hackers (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T07:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aacb69ad-571f-5b4c-9d71-01c7d582c816', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aacb69ad-571f-5b4c-9d71-01c7d582c816'}, {'abstract': 'The German government said it would phase out its nine remaining operating facilities over the next decade, in a move that will likely be popular with the German public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/world/europe/31germany.html', 'snippet': 'The German government said it would phase out its nine remaining operating facilities over the next decade, in a move that will likely be popular with the German public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The German government on Monday announced plans to shut all of the nation’s nuclear power plants within the next 11 years, a sharp reversal for Chancellor Angela Merkel after the Japanese disaster at Fukushima caused an electoral backlash by voters opposed to reliance on nuclear energy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany, in Reversal, Will Close Nuclear Plants by 2022', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Reversal, Germany Announces Plans to Close All Nuclear Plants by 2022', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T09:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Dempsey and Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dempsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38