airlines because of delays in fulfilling membership conditions, an executive from Star Alliance said Monday, putting in jeopardy a key element of its turnaround plan. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Air India Faces Hurdles in Joining Alliance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Air India Struggles To Be Part Of Alliance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T11:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65df7241-9fdd-52f4-930e-3aea046835d8', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65df7241-9fdd-52f4-930e-3aea046835d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Ledge, a series of glass boxes that extend off the 103rd floor of the Willis Tower in Chicago, gives visitors a unique perspective on the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/arts/design/willis-tower-suspends-visitors-above-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The Ledge, a series of glass boxes that extend off the 103rd floor of the Willis Tower in Chicago, gives visitors a unique perspective on the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The view looking down through the glass floor toward South Wacker Drive is just what you’d expect if you were balanced on top of 6,960 boxes of this city’s deep-dish pizza — or, as the exhibition at the Willis Tower also tells us, standing atop 313 Oprah Winfreys or 283 Barack Obamas. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2