mf/', 'snippet': 'The case for Fischer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I suspect that an endorsement from me may be the kiss of death — but anyway, Stan Fischer really would be the best choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heading the IMF', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bce01a86-8916-5a83-8a47-c4965de98c01', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bce01a86-8916-5a83-8a47-c4965de98c01'}, {'abstract': 'Four percent, a million percent, what’s the difference?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/godwins-law-monetary-edition/', 'snippet': 'Four percent, a million percent, what’s the difference?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Any mention of the advantages of a higher inflation target will evoke, almost immediately, claims that you’re trying to turn America into the Weimar Republic and/or Zimbabwe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Godwin’s Law, Monetary Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b94302ff-50c5-5eb6-b944-5e3bbf5ec4ff', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b94302ff-50c5-5eb6-b944-5e3bbf5ec4ff'}, {'abstract': 'Oldies but baddies, recycled every few months.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/the-unkillable-yield-curve-fallacy-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Oldies but baddies, recycled every few months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bad ideas in economics never die; they just wait a few months, then resurface, once again touted as wisdom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unkillable Yield Curve Fallacy (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55b95905-5f05-55d6-850b-bf34eff9003b', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b95905-5f05-55d6-850b-bf34eff9003b'}, {'abstract': 'President Jacob Zuma of South Africa received a raucous red carpet greeting on Monday as he arrived in Libya for meetings with Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/world/africa/31libya.html', 'snippet': 'President Jacob Zuma of South Africa received a raucous red carpet greeting on Monday as he arrived in Libya for meetings with Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRIPOLI, Libya — Talks between President Jacob Zuma of South Africa and Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi ended Monday with no sign of the breakthrough Libyan officials had said they hoped for ahead of the visit. The outcome appeared to leave the Tripoli government and its rebel foes still mired in the stalemate that has settled over the conflict, and NATO with the prospect of an extended campaign of airstrikes in its bid to topple the Libyan leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/world/LIBYA/LIBYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaddafi and Zuma Meet but Reach No Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Qaddafi and Zuma Meet But Reach No Agreement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuma, Jacob G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0741aaf-9afb-5275-be40-2e5a57b5da00', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0741aaf-9afb-5275-be40-2e5a57b5da00'}, {'abstract': 'The Taliban launched a sophisticated attack on Monday against a NATO base in the western Afghan city of Herat, killing at least four people and wounding more than 30.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/world/asia/31afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Taliban launched a sophisticated attack on Monday against a NATO base in the western Afghan city of Herat, killing at least four people and wounding more than 30.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Taliban launched an unusual attack on targets in the western Afghan city of Herat on Monday, including a NATO base, and the police said at least 4 people had been killed and 38 wounded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Attack in Herat, Far From Their Usual Areas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Attack in Herat, Far From Their Usual Areas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:49:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73389217-8730-5a8b-ac0b-fc2b972d14d4', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73389217-8730-5a8b-ac0b-fc2b972d14d4'}, {'abstract': 'Bargain summer trips in the mountains or desert, Jeep Wranglers investigated for air-bag failures, retailers retool catalogs for the iPad and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/monday-reading-bargain-trips-in-the-mountains-or-the-desert/', 'snippet': 'Bargain summer trips in the mountains or desert, Jeep Wranglers investigated for air-bag failures, retailers retool catalogs for the iPad and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Bargain Trips in the Mountains or the Desert', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T12:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bb2f4d4-f327-5a93-86fd-ed7f2d575a2d', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bb2f4d4-f327-5a93-86fd-ed7f2d575a2d'}, {'abstract': 'A film that offers a depressing farewell to the apartments that used to be above Carnegie and the people who lived in them.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/carnegie-apartments-by-barron/', 'snippet': 'A film that offers a depressing farewell to the apartments that used to be above Carnegie and the people who lived in them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was not billed as a three-hankie movie — it was a documentary, after all. But Editta Sherman started sobbing a few minutes after the lights went down, and not because of the way she looked on the screen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carnegie’s Ousted Residents Agree: Film Has Sad Ending', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astor, Josef', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T13:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba597259-2113-52f5-868a-cc123bc543de', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba597259-2113-52f5-868a-cc123bc543de'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Palin and her family visited monuments Sunday night as part of their “One Nation Tour” by charter bus, but her aides continue to refuse to say where else they might show up.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/palin-family-tours-washington-incognito/', 'snippet': 'Sarah Palin and her family visited monuments Sunday night as part of their “One Nation Tour” by charter bus, but her aides continue to refuse to say where else they might show up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Palin and her family sneaked out in Washington on Sunday night for what she called an “incognito” tour of the national monuments, having successfully created a media frenzy and then ditched the press.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palin Family Tours Washington ‘Incognito’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Susteren, Greta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T13:10:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02a09e77-696d-51bb-a232-425ec44544da', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02a09e77-696d-51bb-a232-425ec44544da'}, {'abstract': 'Li Na, the No. 6 ranked player, fired her husband as coach and advanced to the French Open quarterfinals.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/li-fires-husband-as-coach-advances-to-quarterfinals/', 'snippet': 'Li Na, the No. 6 ranked player, fired her husband as coach and advanced to the French Open quarterfinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – At the Australian Open earlier this year, the surging Li Na reached her first Grand Slam final. She gave credit to her husband and coach, Jiang Shan, saying she would love her husband even if he were “fat and ugly.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Li Fires Husband as Coach, Advances to Quarterfinals', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kvitova, Petra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Na', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T13:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/731399af-24ac-5991-8f71-eaf1d4009f9b', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/731399af-24ac-5991-8f71-eaf1d4009f9b'}, {'abstract': 'The Navy has provided a vast trove of cruise books to ancestry.com, and some images from them have been granted shore leave to appear on City Room.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/capturing-moments-of-naval-history-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The Navy has provided a vast trove of cruise books to ancestry.com, and some images from them have been granted shore leave to appear on City Room.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source':