raph': 'On a day when the Kentucky Derby runner-up, Nehro, put in a smashing work at Churchill Downs (6 furlongs in 1:12.2), Animal Kingdom put in his first gallop since his second-place finish in the Preakness Stakes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Animal Kingdom Sharp in First Gallop Since Preakness', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T14:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff472fb7-aa64-580c-8c34-a10f961d0919', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff472fb7-aa64-580c-8c34-a10f961d0919'}, {'abstract': 'Fortis of Canada plans to buy Central Vermont Public Service, that state’s biggest electric utility, in an effort to further expand into the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/fortis-to-buy-vermont-utility-for-470-3-million/', 'snippet': 'Fortis of Canada plans to buy Central Vermont Public Service, that state’s biggest electric utility, in an effort to further expand into the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fortis Incorporated, a Canadian power company, said on Monday that it would expand its presence in the United States by buying Central Vermont Public Service for $470.3 million in cash. It will also assume the company’s $230 million in debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fortis to Buy Vermont Utility for $470.3 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures'