cic-into-quarters/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal of Spain advanced to the French Open quarterfinals with a straight-sets victory over Ivan Ljubicic of Croatia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS – Ivan Ljubicic wore a worried expression on his tanned face. It was only 1-1 in the first set against Rafael Nadal, the French Open’s top seed, but Ljubicic was already struggling with his serve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nadal Cruises Past Ljubicic into Quarters', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ljubicic, Ivan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T14:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26ec2b30-a985-5959-868e-526d876aad21', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ec2b30-a985-5959-868e-526d876aad21'}, {'abstract': 'The changing politics of the medical profession could have a profound effect on the healthcare debate.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/the-changing-politics-of-doctors/', 'snippet': 'The changing politics of the medical profession could have a profound effect on the healthcare debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doctors were once overwhelmingly male and conservative. But today the politics of the medical profession are changing, as more doctors abandon independent practice for salaried jobs and more women are graduating from medical school, reports Gardiner Harris in the latest installment of his Doctors, Inc. series. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Changing Politics of Doctors', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T14:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec1de25-a613-5567-b35d-979b5d6ff8c1', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec1de25-a613-5567-b35d-979b5d6ff8c1'}, {'abstract': 'Our puzzles this week are by 13-year-old Neil Bickford.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/numberplay-a-triplet-of-time-puzzles/', 'snippet': 'Our puzzles this week are by 13-year-old Neil Bickford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neil Bickford recently calculated the first 458 million terms for the continued fraction of pi. That’s a record. He cranked out the giant calculation several months ago to celebrate his 13th birthday. Holy cats! you might say: 458 million terms! It’s true. Here’s Mr. Bickford’s account of the adventure, including a link to a complete list of the terms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': 