am, the French Open, with a five-set victory over David Ferrer of Spain.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/monfils-delights-crowd-with-five-set-victory-over-ferrer/', 'snippet': 'Gael Monfils of France reached the quarterfinals of his home Grand Slam, the French Open, with a five-set victory over David Ferrer of Spain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS -– If Gael Monfils, the flamboyant French dynamo, picked a favorite shot from his 6-4, 2-6, 7-5, 1-6, 8-6 victory over David Ferrer of Spain, it might be an inside-out forehand that split Court Suzanne Lenghlen into two sharp angles and bounded onward for a winner. It was seven games into the fifth set and it put Monfils ahead, 5-2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monfils Delights Crowd With Five-Set Victory Over Ferrer', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrer, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T15:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24ad08b7-a3a6-5de6-aea8-ff0d63fa8f05', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24ad08b7-a3a6-5de6-aea8-ff0d63fa8f05'}, {'abstract': 'Sepp Blatter, the president of FIFA, held a news conference today that was streamed live on FIFA’s Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/blatters-news-conference-live/', 'snippet': 'Sepp Blatter, the president of FIFA, held a news conference today that was streamed live on FIFA’s Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:10 p.m. | Updated  Sepp Blatter’s news conference in Zurich, which was scheduled to begin at 12 p.m., Eastern, did not start until 12:35 p.m. What follows is a transcript of the news conference that was streamed live at FIFA.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blatter Defiant During News Conference', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zurich (Switzerland)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T15:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61fcd3fa-39c8-59dd-ae3a-554a3fe2c083', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61fcd3fa-39c8-59dd-ae3a-554a3fe2c083'}, {'abstract': 'Ethnic Mongolians seething over the killings of two Mongolians by Han Chinese drivers took their anger to the streets of the capital of Inner Mongolia on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/world/asia/31mongolia.html', 'snippet': 'Ethnic Mongolians seething over the killings of two Mongolians by Han Chinese drivers took their anger to the streets of the capital of Inner Mongolia on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOHHOT, China — Ethnic Mongolians seething over the killings of two