HANGSHA, China — China’s economy is starting to slow, after two years of torrid growth achieved following the global downturn. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Yuan/Yuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Yuan/Yuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Yuan/Yuan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Yuan/Yuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Yuan/Yuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Economy Slows, but Inflation Still Looms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Economy Is Starting to Slow, but Threat of Inflation Looms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T17:10:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e591eece-f281-5f62-a827-284d8353fce2', 'word_count': 1588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e591eece-f281-5f62-a827-284d8353fce2'}, {'abstract': 'The French hopes for two men in the French Open quarterfinals was squelched by Robin Soderling of Sweden, who beat Gilles Simon in straight sets Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/soderling-squashes-simons-french-dream/', 'snippet': 'The French hopes for two men in the French Open quarterfinals was squelched by Robin Soderling of Sweden, who beat Gilles Simon in straight sets Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS -– For the crowd at Roland Garros, the prize would have been two Frenchmen stepping into the final eight of their country’s international championship, the French Open. First, Gael Monfils made half of that prize come true. Then, Gilles Simon had a chance to join him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soderling Squashes Simon’s French Dream', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Gilles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soderling, Robin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T17:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e1b3d7e-96a6-5