ne': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3404d5a-d5f2-59bc-9752-315741742ed5', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3404d5a-d5f2-59bc-9752-315741742ed5'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s ruling center-right coalition was resoundingly beaten in run-off administrative elections on Monday, a defeat that further weakens Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/world/europe/31italy.html', 'snippet': 'Italy’s ruling center-right coalition was resoundingly beaten in run-off administrative elections on Monday, a defeat that further weakens Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Italy’s ruling center-right coalition was resoundingly beaten in runoff administrative elections on Monday, a defeat that further weakened Prime Minister Silvio Berlusconi, who has been besieged by growing dissent within his razor-thin majority and faces criminal charges in court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Blows to Berlusconi Coalition', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Berlusconi Coalition Set Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Di Pietro, Antonio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Northern League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlusconi, Silvio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T18:51:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26608e0c-09df-57c0-b244-77297a05e99e', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26608e0c-09df-57c0-b244-77297a05e99e'}, {'abstract': 'The Morning Line for Monday, May 30.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/the-morning-line-as-horses-arrive-at-belmont-alternation-is-out/', 'snippet': 'The Morning Line for Monday, May 30.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alternation, the winner of the Peter Pan Stakes at Belmont Park on May 12, will not race in the Belmont. According to the Daily Racing Form, Alternation will concentrate on major stakes events over the summer. Alternation’s trainer Donnie Van Hemel said, “We looked things over and decided to take a breather. … The horse is fine. We just decided to point for races like the Jim Dandy and the Travers. He’s had four or five races early in the year.\xa0We want to give him a little breather now, then make some noise later.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning Line: As Horses Arrive at Belmont, Alternation Is Out', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T18:56:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bennett Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bennett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liebman', 'qu