er 39 weeks of gestation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childbirth: Every Week in Utero Counts, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CHILDBIRTH: Every Week in Utero Counts, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infant Mortality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Obstetrics & Gynecology (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ab521a-9853-5d82-ac7d-507b05ec705d', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ab521a-9853-5d82-ac7d-507b05ec705d'}, {'abstract': 'Older people in areas with high concentrations of primary care doctors are hospitalized less often for conditions that can be treated outside hospitals and have lower death rates, researchers find.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/health/research/31patterns.html', 'snippet': 'Older people in areas with high concentrations of primary care doctors are hospitalized less often for conditions that can be treated outside hospitals and have lower death rates, researchers find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Older adults who live in areas with high concentrations of primary care doctors are less likely than those in areas with fewer such doctors to be hospitalized for illnesses that can be managed outside a hospital, like asthma and diabetes, a new study has found. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patterns: Seniors Fare Better Where Doctors Are', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PATTERNS: Seniors Fare Better Where Doctors Are', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66d8d587-f884-5bc5-82cb-d7da1c4d7282', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66d8d587-f884-5bc5-82cb-d7da1c4d7282'}, {'abstract': 'Earlier estimates from a much smaller study indicated that only 4 percent of adults 24 to 32 had hypertension.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/health/research/31risks.html', 'snippet': 'Earlier estimates from a much smaller study indicated that only 4 percent of adults 24 to 32 had hypertension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study finds that nearly one in five young adults has high blood pressure, a startling estimate much higher than any previously reported.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Risks: Hypertension Lurking in Young Adults', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'RISKS: Hypertension Lurking in Young Adults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17befbd5-b1a9-5dd3-a5a2-6441d5b3be43', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17befbd5-b1a9-5dd3-a5a2-6441d5b3be43'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Sharapova fell behind early against Agnieszka Radwanska, but advanced to the quarterfinals with a 7-6 (4), 7-5 victory.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/a-resolute-sharapova-holds-off-radwanska/', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova fell behind early against Agnieszka Radwanska, but advanced to the quarterfinals with a 7-6 (4), 7-5 victory.', 'lead_paragraph': ' PARIS — Agnieszka Radwanska of Poland, her left leg heavily bandaged, managed to jump ahead of Maria Sharapova of Russia, 3-0, in a fourth-round match Monday at the French Open. For awhile, she didn’t dare look back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Resolute Sharapova Holds Off Radwanska', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radwanska, Agnieszka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fc0b794-7ef3-5018-8146-933a6f18abbc', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fc0b794-7ef3-5018-8146-933a6f18abbc'}, {'abstract': 'There always seems to be something keeping us awake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/health/31brody.html', 'snippet': 'There always seems to be something keeping us awake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my younger years, I regarded sleep as a necessary evil, nature’s way of thwarting my desire to cram as many activities into a 24-hour day as possible. I frequently flew the red-eye from California, for instance, sailing (or so I thought) through the next day on less than four hours of uncomfortable sleep.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/science/BROD/BROD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/science/BROD/BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/science/BROD/BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Good Night’s Sleep Isn’t a Luxury; It’s a Necessity', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Good Night’s Sleep Isn’t a Luxury; It’s a Necessity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor