 a video link from Yangon to tell an audience in Hong Kong that she would seek to broaden her audience in her country since being released from house arrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, the most high-profile dissident in Myanmar, signaled on Monday that she would be seeking to broaden her audience in her country since being released from house arrest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissident Plans a More Active Role in Myanmar', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar: Dissident to Leave City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi, Daw', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:48:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0efda7cc-666e-5dd5-8c49-57a1e916b881', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0efda7cc-666e-5dd5-8c49-57a1e916b881'}, {'abstract': 'The Miami Heat and Dallas Mavericks did indeed meet in the 2006 Finals, but the changes within both franchises — and the league at large — since that time makes the thought of the 2011 Finals as a “rematch” a bit ridiculous.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/dispatching-the-worn-narrative-of-the-2006-finals/', 'snippet': 'The Miami Heat and Dallas Mavericks did indeed meet in the 2006 Finals, but the changes within both franchises — and the league at large — since that time makes the thought of the 2011 Finals as a “rematch” a bit ridiculous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Dallas Mavericks and Miami Heat crystallized their date to meet in the N.B.A. Finals, media dreams of rehashed narratives came true. Dirk Nowitzki will finally be given his shot at revenge and redemption, or so say the series taglines. Yet depicting these N.B.A. Finals as a rematch or even a re-imagining doesn’t do the matchup justice; these teams aren’t two shadows of their 2006 counterparts, but unique and successful basketball machines. Sport doesn’t pack the same punch without the underlying story, but is it really necessary to dig up ancient history?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dispatching the Worn Narrative of the 2006 Finals', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Terry, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a405a6-5374-5f38-a24a-f627fa3fbf00', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a405a6-5374-5f38-a24a-f627fa3fbf00'}, {'abstract': 'Haley Tanner’s “Vaclav & Lena” is a story of two Russian immigrants who first meet at age 6 in an English as a Second Language class at their Brooklyn school.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/books/vaclav-lena-by-haley-tanner-review.html', 'snippet': 'Haley Tanner’s “Vaclav & Lena” is a story of two Russian immigrants who first meet at age 6 in an English as a Second Language class at their Brooklyn school.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There comes a point in almost every relationship when you discuss the future. Where is this heading? Do you want to get married? Do you want to get married? Vaclav and Lena have had this talk. It has gone well. Vaclav and Lena are 10.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Russians in Brooklyn Find Love, the Wonder Wheel and Then Life', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Russians in Brooklyn Find Love, the Wonder Wheel and Then Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T19:56:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah Meadows', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meadows', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e1af625-54e1-525e-b595-afbfd053d726', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e1af625-54e1-525e-b595-afbfd053d726'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers used cameras and a doll to open a window on how people interpret the world around them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/science/31obbarbie.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers used cameras and a doll to open a window on how people interpret the world around them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the movie “Honey, I Shrunk the Kids,” an inventor accidently miniaturizes his children, making the world appear enormous to them. Now, scientists have simulated the sensation of feeling tiny using cameras and a doll. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/science/OBbarbie/OBOX-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/science/OBbarbie/OBOX-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/science/OBbarbie/OBOX-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaining Perspective, Small and Large, With Dolls', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaining Perspective, Small and Large, With Dolls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'