, 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/hockey/31bruinspix/31bruinspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/hockey/31bruinspix/31bruinspix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/hockey/31bruinspix/31bruinspix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/hockey/31bruinspix/31bruinspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/hockey/31bruinspix/31bruinspix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Their Fingers Crossed, Fans in Boston Embrace the Bruins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Their Fingers Crossed, Fans in Boston Embrace the Bruins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T21:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6733b623-5434-5654-b713-ba1d6cc33a5c', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6733b623-5434-5654-b713-ba1d6cc33a5c'}, {'abstract': 'In this tripartite story of brain, art and family life, the author aces the first part but comes up surprisingly short in the other two.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/health/31zuger.html', 'snippet': 'In this tripartite story of brain, art and family life, the author aces the first part but comes up surprisingly short in the other two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a fall afternoon in 1988, Jon Sarkin, a 35-year-old Massachusetts chiropractor, was happily playing the eighth hole on a local golf course when he felt something “twist” in his brain. Three days later he began to hear a high-pitched screech, a siren that only grew louder with the passing weeks. Doctors shrugged; a brain scan suggested a vague abnormality near a nerve at the base of the brain that controls hearing and balance.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/science/ZUGE-3/ZUGE-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Broad Brushstrokes Obscure a View of Brain Trauma', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broad Brushstrokes Obscure a View of Brain Trauma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nutt, Amy Ellis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T21:57:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/33e3421a-5132-5bc7-b9f3-bd7bdef21ab5', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e3421a-5132-5bc7-b9f3-bd7bdef21ab5'}, {'abstract': 'Jose Reyes may be gone for as long as a week after the death of his grandmother.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/reyes-placed-on-bereavement-list/', 'snippet': 'Jose Reyes may be gone for as long as a week after the death of his grandmother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jose Reyes left the Mets on Monday after the death of his grandmother and may be gone as long as a week on bereavement leave. That means a team already battered by injuries will now be without its best everyday player this season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reyes Placed on Bereavement List', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T22:03:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5658b6c-f535-5550-9ee0-b320d88fb978', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5658b6c-f535-5550-9ee0-b320d88fb978'}, {'abstract': 'The great unknowns are whether PBS viewers will welcome receiving programming in shorter bites, or rebel a