middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c782679-1340-52d2-abc6-52ee3eb5d0d2', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c782679-1340-52d2-abc6-52ee3eb5d0d2'}, {'abstract': 'Kentucky’s Joseph Holt was caught between his Southern roots and his loyalty to Lincoln.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/union-man/', 'snippet': 'Kentucky’s Joseph Holt was caught between his Southern roots and his loyalty to Lincoln.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 31, 1861, Joseph Holt spoke out on behalf of the Union. The man who had been Secretary of War in early 1861 (and who has a role played by Danny Huston in Robert Redford’s current film, “The Conspirator”) saw that his native state of Kentucky dangled precariously in the balance. Its leading men had just resolved upon “strict neutrality” between the Federal government and the Confederacy. Holt would have none of it. Neutrality, he insisted, was a delusion. He would as soon think “of being neutral in a contest between an officer of justice and an incendiary arrested in an attempt to fire the dwelling over my head.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Man', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T23:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By daniel w. crofts', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46c887cb-45cc-54b3-8a47-df071e224499', 'word_count': 1304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46c887cb-45cc-54b3-8a47-df071e224499'}, {'abstract': 'Bartolo Colon retired 23 of his first 26 hitters, allowing four hits, in the Yankees victory in Oakland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/sports/baseball/bartolo-colon-makes-quick-work-of-athletics-in-complete-game-shutout.html', 'snippet': 'Bartolo Colon retired 23 of his first 26 hitters, allowing four hits, in the Yankees victory in Oakland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAKLAND, Calif. — Since Bartolo Colon last pitched here in September 2007 — a time before elbow surgery, before retirement was considered, before a rejuvenating medical treatment — the stadium has changed names twice, but its features have remained the same. The roomy dimensions and acres of foul territory reward pitchers unafraid of contact, encouraging them to throw strikes. And one thing Colon can do, has done, is throw strikes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/31yankees-1/31yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/31yankees-1/31yankees-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/31yankees-1/31yankees-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/31yankees-1/31yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/sports/31yankees-1/31yankees-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With 