ing-score-which-team-has-the-right-stuff-to-win-the-cup/', 'snippet': 'Focusing on concepts of sports psychology like big-game experience, leadership on the ice and consistency can help determine who will win the Stanley Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After analyzing the championship games or series of the N.F.L., N.B.A., Major League Baseball and N.H.L., and the major finals in golf and tennis, we identified 50 championship characteristics in our book, “Who Will Win the Big Game? A Psychological and Mathematical Method.” Based on similar research, we focused on several championship characteristics that might predict the winner of the Stanley Cup finals, which start Wednesday in Vancouver. Focusing on concepts of sports psychology, we looked at factors such as big-game experience, leadership on the ice and consistency. So important are these concepts to winning championships that they have proven to be common themes across all sports we have studied.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Which Team Has the Right Stuff to Win the Cup?', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T23:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By CARLTON J. CHIN and JAY P. GRANAT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlton', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'CHIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'GRANAT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb9fbdd0-ff83-5f8d-bc54-abe3144663e9', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb9fbdd0-ff83-5f8d-bc54-abe3144663e9'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Health and Human Services is using existing rules to enforce medical privacy, but some wonder if stronger laws are needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/business/31privacy.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Health and Human Services is using existing rules to enforce medical privacy, but some wonder if stronger laws are needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal health officials call it the Wall of Shame. It’s a government Web page that lists nearly 300 hospitals, doctors and insurance companies that have reported significant breaches of medical privacy in the last couple of years. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Privacy1/Privacy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Privacy1/Privacy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 284}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/business/Privacy1/Privacy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaches Lead to Push to Protect Medical Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Push To Protect Health Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major'