by-line.html', 'snippet': 'In the competitive game of marketing New York homes, many real estate agencies are now enlisting independent draftsmen to draw floor plans from scratch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fiercely competitive game of marketing homes, brokers go to great lengths to cast a property in its most flattering light, sanding down rough edges, cleaning out clutter, loading in new furniture and hiring professional photographers to make the glossy images that lure salivating buyers to weekend open houses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/05/31/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/05/31/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/05/31/nyregion/APPRAISAL1/APPRAISAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of the Floor Plan: Capturing a Home, Line by Line', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Art of the Floor Plan: Capturing a Home, Line by Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Housing and Real Estate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30T23:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14dec801-bc36-59f7-b79b-761c5f39929b', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14dec801-bc36-59f7-b79b-761c5f39929b'}, {'abstract': 'The hedge fund mogul, who met reporters during batting practice Monday, said he hoped the deal being negotiating for him to purchase a stake in the Mets would be completed by the end of June.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/einhorn-says-deal-with-mets-is-a-win-win/', 'snippet': 'The hedge fund mogul, who met reporters during batting practice Monday, said he hoped the deal being negotiating for him to purchase a stake in the Mets would be completed by the end of June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Einhorn spoke formally in public for the first time since it was announced last Thursday that he is in talks to buy a minority stake in the team. The hedge fund mogul, who met reporters during batting practice before the Mets played the Pittsburgh Pirates at Citi Field on Monday, said that the deal being negotiating with the Wilpon family was a “win-win” agreement that he hopes will be completed by the end of June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Einhorn Says Deal With Mets Is a ‘Win-Win’', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einhorn, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-30