}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f4ed3b5-c7b8-534e-8bc8-3152d466fd1b', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f4ed3b5-c7b8-534e-8bc8-3152d466fd1b'}, {'abstract': 'The euro fell in currency trading as Greece’s prime minister tried to press ahead with a package of economic measures and keep bailout money flowing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/business/31markets.html', 'snippet': 'The euro fell in currency trading as Greece’s prime minister tried to press ahead with a package of economic measures and keep bailout money flowing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The euro weakened for the first time in three days versus the dollar, while oil and copper fell in New York on concern that European governments would struggle to resolve the region’s debt crisis amid a slowing global recovery.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro Weakens as Greece Struggles With Austerity', 'kicker': 'Stocks & Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Euro Weakens as Greece Struggles With Austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T01:22:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/841a4f56-43ab-52a6-a0a2-441f49775b12', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/841a4f56-43ab-52a6-a0a2-441f49775b12'}, {'abstract': 'Philip Duff, one of the founders of the FrontPoint hedge fund group, is starting a new firm, Massif Partners, to offer services to pension funds.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/30/a-frontpoint-founder-tries-again-with-a-new-firm/', 'snippet': 'Philip Duff, one of the founders of the FrontPoint hedge fund group, is starting a new firm, Massif Partners, to offer services to pension funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When FrontPoint Partners began in 2000, its founders envisioned the firm as a one-stop shop for multiple hedge funds, a distinctive strategy in an industry dominated at the time by single star managers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A FrontPoint Founder Tries Again With a New Firm', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T01:23:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cdb5fc0-9506-5f8e-89f4-56767b4cd3ad', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cdb5fc0-9506-5f8e-89f4-56767b4cd3ad'}, {'abstract': 'The state would like charge childless adults on Medicaid who smoke or are obese $50.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/us/31questions.html', 'snippet': 'The state would like charge childless adults on Medicaid who smoke or are obese $50.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arizona, like many other states, says it is no longer able to finance its Medicaid program adequately. As part of a plan to cut costs, the state has proposed imposing a $50 fee on childless adults on Medicaid who are either obese or who smoke. In Arizona, almost half of all Medicaid recipients smoke; while the number of obese people is unclear, about one in four Arizonans is overweight, according to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. The state’s plan must ultimately be approved by the federal government. Monica Coury, spokeswoman for Arizona’s Medicaid program, discusses. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under an Arizona Plan, Smokers and the Obese Would Pay Medicaid Fee', 'kicker': 'Asked and Answered | Monica Coury', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under an Arizona Plan, Smokers and the Obese Would Pay Medicaid Fee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T01:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ddd35f1-3691-5b3f-a637-a14535cf8b01', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ddd35f1-3691-5b3f-a637-a14535cf8b01'}, {'abstract': 'Fees imposed by airlines can add hundreds of dollars to a “free” frequent flier award ticket.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/business/31fees.html', 'snippet': 'Fees imposed by airlines can add hundreds of dollars to a “free” frequent flier award ticket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers who signed up for a British Airways Visa card issued by JP Morgan Chase got a sweet deal in a recent promotion: 100,000 frequent flier miles aft