an, Anna Nebtrebko, dropped out over concerns about radiation, as did a leading tenor, Met officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brightest star of the Metropolitan Opera’s tour to Japan, Anna Netrebko, has dropped out at the last minute over concerns about radiation, as did Joseph Calleja, a leading tenor, Met officials said in Tokyo on Tuesday. They joined Jonas Kaufmann, another tenor who pulled out over concerns after the March earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01mettour/01mettour-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01mettour/01mettour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01mettour/01mettour-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Stars Back Out of Tour to Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Stars Back Out Of Tour To Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netrebko, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calleja, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T07:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e8dd910-3948-5757-bfad-d408905e4d46', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e8dd910-3948-5757-bfad-d408905e4d46'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | How much progress has been made in the battle against H.I.V. and AIDS?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/30-years-of-fighting-aids/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | How much progress has been made in the battle against H.I.V. and AIDS?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHERE were the first AIDS cases reported?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Years of Fighting AIDS', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T07:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df005b75-aafb-5b87-be28-8453096788e4', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df005b75-aafb-5b87-be28-8453096788e4'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | How does being bilingual help in non-language aspects of life?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/do-you-speak-a-second-or-third-language/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | How does being bilingual help in non-language aspects of life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cognitive neuroscientist Ellen Bialystok has been studying how being able to speak two languages sharpens the mind. In her conversation with Claudia Dreifus, she states that kids who are bilingual have a way of thinking that helps them better distinguish important information from the less important. Are you or someone you are close to able to speak two (or more) languages fluently? Have you noticed any advantages other than being able to communicate with more people?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Speak a Second, or Third, Language?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T08:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88de94e0-08f3-5805-bb55-0ab8b5090556', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88de94e0-08f3-5805-bb55-0ab8b5090556'}, {'abstract': 'A rogue, scoundrel. A light woman; a strumpet.', 'web_url': 'https://schott.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/daily-lexeme-limmer/', 'snippet': 'A rogue, scoundrel. A light woman; a strumpet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s word, in association with the remarkable Oxford English Dictionary, is', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Lexeme: Limmer', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T08:24:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a5aaaf-b669-58f8-b111-d882abbb76e8', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a5aaaf-b669-58f8-b111-d882abbb76e8'}, {'abstract': 'The black photography collective Kamoinge grew out of the Harlem of the 1960s. It is still growing.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/intimate-moments-in-the-african-diaspora/', 'snippet': 'The black photography collective Kamoinge grew out of the Harlem of the 1960s. It is still growing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On an April Sunday in an artfully cluttered Harlem apartment, a group of photographers leaned over a coffee table, jazz playing softly in the background. Radcliffe Roye was about to present some work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intimate Moments in the African Diaspora', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barboza, Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cartier-Bresson, Henri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeCarava, Roy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Langston', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T09:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cebe3f78-6ce4-5567-87cd-b71eea4b7961', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cebe3f78-6ce4-5567-87cd-b71eea4b7961'}, {'abstract': 'Ratko Mladic’s transfer begins the final chapter in a nearly 16-year international effort to bring him to account after he was accused of crimes against humanity, war crimes and genocide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/europe/01serbia.html', 'snippet': 'Ratko Mladic’s transfer begins the final chapter in a nearly 16-year international effort to bring him to account after he was accused of crimes against humanity, war crimes and genocide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE HAGUE — Ratko Mladic, the long-fugitive international war crimes suspect captured last week, arrived here Tuesday to face trial after judges in Serbia ruled against the appeal of his extradition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/SERBIA/SERBIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/SERBIA/SERBIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/world/SERBIA/SERBIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mladic Arrives in The Hague', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Serbia Sends Mladic to War Crimes Tribunal in the Netherlands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mladic, Ratko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Tribunal for the former Yugoslavia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T09:35:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marlise Simons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marlise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a32f6f8-749e-5130-9058-94d2424ad6ca', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a32f6f8-749e-5130-9058-94d2424ad6ca'}, {'abstract': 'PAI Partners, the French buyout firm, has entered into a period of exclusivity with an investment group led by Clayton, Dubilier & Rice and AXA Private Equity to sell the engineering company SPIE for 2.1 billion euros.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/pai-partners-to-sell-engineering-firm-for-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'PAI Partners, the French buyout firm, has entered into a period of exclusivity with an investment group led by Clayton, Dubilier & Rice and AXA Private Equity to sell the engineering company SPIE for 2.1 billion euros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PAI Partners, the French buyout firm, said on Tuesday that it had entered into a period of exclusivity with an investment group led by Clayton, Dubilier & Rice and AXA Private Equity to sell its stake in the engineering company SPIE.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PAI Partners to Sell Engineering Firm for $3 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clayton Dubilier & Rice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T09:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris V. Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/582677f9-cc92-55dc-b9e8-15015fb34faf', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582677f9-cc92-55dc-b9e8-15015fb34faf'}, {'abstract': 'The former Russian oil tycoon failed to prove that his case was politically motivated, the human rights court ruled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/europe/01khodorkovsky.html', 'snippet': 'The former Russian oil tycoon failed to prove that his case was politically motivated, the human rights court ruled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, the former Russian oil tycoon who has been jailed since 2003, failed to prove that his prosecution was politically motivated, the European Court of Human Rights ruled Tuesday, while agreeing that the government had violated his rights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/01khodorkovsky_cnd/01khodorkovsky_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/01khodorkovsky_cnd/01khodorkovsky_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/world/01khodorkovsky_cnd/01khodorkovsky_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Court Partially Backs Kremlin in Khodorkovsky’s Prosecution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rejecting Political Motive, Court Says Russia Violated Tycoon’s Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T09:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d8101a6-b062-5cd8-9e54-d952a8f94852', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d8101a6-b062-5cd8-9e54-d952a8f94852'}, {'abstract': 'Rethinking the value of Ryan Braun, Jacoby Ellsbury, Jose Reyes and Cole Hamels.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/fantasy-focus-moving-the-needle-8/', 'snippet': 'Rethinking the value of Ryan Braun, Jacoby Ellsbury, Jose Reyes and Cole Hamels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard for a first-round pick to move up significantly, but aside from Jose Bautista, Ryan Braun is probably the top hitter in fantasy baseball this year. While Braun’s 12 home runs and .588 slugging percentage through Sunday are improvements over last year’s rates, the number that jumps out most is his 13 steals in 14 attempts. Milwaukee’s new manager, Ron Roenicke, is more aggressive on the basepaths than his predecessor, Ken Macha: the Brewers are 14th in the majors in stolen bases this year, as opposed to 21st last year, and Braun in particular is getting the green light. At this pace, a 35-35 season is within reach, and with Braun, you’re virtually assured a good batting average. Only Carlos Gonzalez and maybe Matt Kemp offer the same speed-power-average upside, and Gonzalez is struggling this year.Jacoby Ellsbury’s 2010 was a lost season because of rib injuries, but as he is 27, his value has never been higher. The 19 stolen bases through Sunday put him on pace for close to 60 steals, and that’s not accounting for chilly early-season conditions that often slow the running game. Ellsbury also has 6 home runs and 16 doubles and is posting a .298/.368/.462 line in 208 at-bats while hitting leadoff in one of the league’s best lineups. In short, he’s what the Red Sox hoped Carl Crawford would be when they gave him $142 million. Crawford was a late first-round pick in most leagues, and Ellsbury must be considered similarly at this point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Moving the Needle', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellsbury, Jacoby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamels, Cole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Liss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e53f258-69e2-5453-b385-2647ee37f9ca', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e53f258-69e2-5453-b385-2647ee37f9ca'}, {'abstract': 'Invited for the fourth edition of the Grand Palais’s annual Monumenta exhibition, the artist Anish Kapoor chose to take the title of the event literally.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/kapoors-leviathan-fills-grand-palais-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'Invited for the fourth edition of the Grand Palais’s annual Monumenta exhibition, the artist Anish Kapoor chose to take the title of the event literally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Invited for the fourth edition of the Grand Palais’s annual Monumenta exhibition, the artist Anish Kapoor chose to take the title of the event literally. His creation, titled “Leviathan,” fills the large-scale venue with a giant sculpture — measuring about 775,000 square feet — that seems to push the walls of the building and, within its interior, drenches the viewer with a blood-red hue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kapoor’s ‘Leviathan’ Fills Grand Palais in Paris', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kapoor, Anish', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Palais', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T10:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Houssin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Houssin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c8514b-8e22-569c-8636-49e1fbc92627', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c8514b-8e22-569c-8636-49e1fbc92627'}, {'abstract': 'Contrary to many Republican assertions, tax rates in the United States are low, both historically and in comparison with other developed nations, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/are-taxes-in-the-u-s-high-or-low/', 'snippet': 'Contrary to many Republican assertions, tax rates in the United States are low, both historically and in comparison with other developed nations, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett has served as an economic adviser in the White House, the Treasury Department and Congress. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed