avor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: So Old It’s New Again', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T11:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b57fe97a-079d-5699-85c4-34d729a4894a', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b57fe97a-079d-5699-85c4-34d729a4894a'}, {'abstract': 'Factors like leading scorer, points allowed and field-goal percentage are strong indicators of who will win the N.B.A. championship.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/keeping-score-championship-characteristics-in-the-n-b-a-finals/', 'snippet': 'Factors like leading scorer, points allowed and field-goal percentage are strong indicators of who will win the N.B.A. championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After analyzing the championship games or series of the N.F.L., N.B.A., Major League Baseball and N.H.L., and the major finals in golf and tennis, we identified 50 championships characteristics in our book, “Who Will Win the Big Game? A Psychological and Mathematical Method.” Based on this research, we focused on several championship characteristics that might help predict the winner of the N.B.A. finals, which start Tuesday night in Miami. Last year’s analysis highlighted leadership factors and correctly predicted that the Lakers would win the championship. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Championship Characteristics in the N.B.A. Finals', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nowitzki, Dirk', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T11:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By CARLTON J. CHIN and JAY P. GRANAT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlton', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'CHIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'GRANAT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bbe4838-5b20-569b-b377-448cf8fb084c', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bbe4838-5b20-569b-b377-448cf8fb084c'}, {'abstract': 'In one of his sternest warnings yet concerning civilian casualties, President Hamid Karzai said NATO must stop air attacks on Afghan homes or face “unilateral action” from the Afghan government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/asia/01afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'In one of his sternest warnings yet concerning civilian casualties, President Hamid Karzai said NATO must stop air attacks on Afghan homes or face “unilateral action” from the Afghan government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — In one of his sternest warnings yet concerning civilian casualties, President Hamid Karzai said Tuesday that NATO must stop air attacks on Afghan homes immediately, or face “unilateral action” from the Afghan government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': No