y Sports + Outdoors, a  Texas-based chain of 131 outdoors and sporting goods stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Company is going camping. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'K.K.R. to Buy Sporting Goods Chain', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sporting Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T12:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50798d8d-d114-5546-85fc-f49d9c66028f', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50798d8d-d114-5546-85fc-f49d9c66028f'}, {'abstract': 'The House overwhelmingly rejected a measure to increase the debt limit, a vote staged by Republicans to pressure President Obama to accept deep cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/us/politics/01fiscal.html', 'snippet': 'The House overwhelmingly rejected a measure to increase the debt limit, a vote staged by Republicans to pressure President Obama to accept deep cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The House on Tuesday overwhelmingly rejected a measure to increase the government’s debt limit, acting on a vote staged by Republican leaders to pressure President Obama to agree to deep spending cuts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/us/fiscal-1/fiscal-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressing Obama, House Bars Rise for Debt Ceiling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PRESSING OBAMA, HOUSE BARS RISE FOR DEBT CEILING', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T12:29:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b66f32e-8a90-511b-880e-9ba52c5cd1e9', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b66f32e-8a90-511b-880e-9ba52c5cd1e9'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The reputation of the military plummeted in tandem with Americans’ faith in the Vietnam War, but times and attitudes have changed. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/renewed-respect-for-the-military/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The reputation of the military plummeted in tandem with Americans’ faith in the Vietnam War, but times and attitudes have changed. Also, what City Room is reading in other papers and blogs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As usual, New Yorkers paused on Memorial Day to remember the terrible price paid by their compatriots in America’s many wars. As usual, one of the more solemn observances took place at the colonnaded Soldiers’ and Sailors’ Monument on the edge of Riverside Park. As usual, several hundred attended under a punishing sun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renewed Respect for the Military', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reserve Officers Training Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T12:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4635780-dec9-5290-a9f0-ab99e995daed', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4635780-dec9-5290-a9f0-ab99e995daed'}, {'abstract': 'Demag Cranes of Germany said on Tuesday that it had rejected a $1.3 billion bid from Terex, calling the offer from the United States heavy equipment manufacturer too low.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/demag-cranes-rejects-offer-from-terex/', 'snippet': 'Demag Cranes of Germany said on Tuesday that it had rejected a $1.3 billion bid from Terex, calling the offer from the United States heavy equipment manufacturer too low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demag Cranes of Germany said on Tuesday that it had rejected a $1.3 billion bid from Terex, calling the offer from the United States heavy equipment manufacturer too low.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demag Cranes Rejects Offer From Terex', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli