 clandestine release by the studio, roughed up to look like the work of a video pirate.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/sony-says-dragon-tattoo-trailer-was-probably-pirated-in-u-s-theater/', 'snippet': 'Some conspiratorially minded viewers wondered if a YouTube trailer for “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo” was a clandestine release by the studio, roughed up to look like the work of a video pirate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wouldn’t be another chapter in the story of Stieg Larsson without a little bit of mystery, would it?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Says ‘Dragon Tattoo’ Trailer Was Probably Pirated in U.S. Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recordings and Downloads (Video)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larsson, Stieg', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'O, Karen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reznor, Trent', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia Pictures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood Reporter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Led Zeppelin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T13:34:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/268cef75-d7bf-55db-8ab3-2e290b4ccd45', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/268cef75-d7bf-55db-8ab3-2e290b4ccd45'}, {'abstract': 'The summer will be filled with various treats in the way of classical music concerts, and the New York Philharmonic began the season with a Memorial Day concert.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/arts/music/new-york-philharmonics-memorial-day-concert-review.html', 'snippet': 'The summer will be filled with various treats in the way of classical music concerts, and the New York Philharmonic began the season with a Memorial Day concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is probably no piece of classical music written in the 20th century that is better known or more associated with grief than Barber’s Adagio for Strings — it was played at the funerals of John F. Kennedy and Franklin D. Roosevelt, popularized by Oliver Stone’s 1986 Vietnam War film, “Platoon,” and remixed by numerous D.J.s and pop singers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01cathedral/01cathedral-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01cathedral/01cathedral-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01cathedral/01cathedral-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01cathedral/01cathedral-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/01cathedral/01cathedral-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Echoes of Barber, Literally', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Echoes Of Barber, Literally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T13:52:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c9c68e9-1ccd-531b-9ae5-4bc76c75f6ee', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c9c68e9-1ccd-531b-9ae5-4bc76c75f6ee'}, {'abstract': 'New systems for answering hospital patients’ calls, hotels try to get in-room movies right, sleeping under the stars in Manhattan and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/tuesday-reading-new-ways-to-answer-hospital-patients-calls/', 'snippet': 'New systems for answering hospital patients’ calls, hotels try to get in-room movies right, sleeping under the stars in Manhattan and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: New Ways to Answer Hospital Patients’ Calls', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T13:54:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a27df2b8-9430-5a82-bf3e-6e40eea570d1', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a27df2b8-9430-5a82-bf3e-6e40eea570d1'}, {'abstract': 'A New York-bound bus was carrying 58 passengers when it rolled over on Interstate 95, about 30 miles north of Richmond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/us/01bus.html', 'snippet': 'A New York-bound bus was carrying 58 passengers when it rolled over on Interstate 95, about 30 miles north of Richmond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virginia authorities arrested the driver of a commercial bus that rolled over in Virginia on Tuesday, killing four people, and charged him with reckless driving. The accident was the latest of several for the bus operator, which has been cited for dozens of violations including driver fatigue, a factor the police believe caused this crash.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/us/01bus-cnd/01bus-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 262, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Driver Arrested After Fatal Bus Crash in Virginia; Carrier Has Record of Violations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Driver Arrested After Fatal Bus Crash in Virginia; Carrier Has Record of Violations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 1, 'maj