g Is Not for You…', 'kicker': 'Schott&#039;s Vocab', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fca5aea-24a6-5769-a795-8dfd123c277f', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fca5aea-24a6-5769-a795-8dfd123c277f'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s sentences were all over the place.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/sentence-of-the-week-neanderthal-edition/', 'snippet': 'This week’s sentences were all over the place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s sentences were all over the place. Witness:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentence of the Week, Neanderthal Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caves and Caverns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neanderthal Man', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37d365d-7fc5-51e5-ad4d-7bdcc61e4a4e', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37d365d-7fc5-51e5-ad4d-7bdcc61e4a4e'}, {'abstract': 'A group of mothers demanding justice for those who died during the Tiananmen Square massacre said Tuesday that police officials in Beijing had contacted one family in April to discuss compensation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/asia/01briefs-Chinasquare.html', 'snippet': 'A group of mothers demanding justice for those who died during the Tiananmen Square massacre said Tuesday that police officials in Beijing had contacted one family in April to discuss compensation.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A group of mothers demanding justice for the victims of the Tiananmen Square massacre of June 4, 1989, said Tuesday that police officials in Beijing had contacted one family in April to discuss giving compensation for the death in that family. It was a rare instance in which officials had mentioned compensation in relation to the killings. However, the group said in a letter circulated on the Internet that the police officials did not talk about revealing the truth of the killings, legal redress or the possibility of addressing each case. Instead, “they simply raised the issue of how much money should be given and stressed that this is for individuals, not the group as a whole,” said the letter, which had 127 signatures. The group said: “The bottom line is this: the souls of those killed during June 4 shall not be defiled; their families shall not be dishonored.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Tiananmen Payment Discussed, Activists Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Tiananmen Payment Discussed, Activists Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tiananmen Square (Beijing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c342f1bf-15a9-5f6d-987c-112d0f7ab169', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c342f1bf-15a9-5f6d-987c-112d0f7ab169'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Palin continued her bus tour of historic sites with a visit to a Gettysburg battlefield. She also continued her manipulation of the news media.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/palin-ditches-press-tours-battlefield/', 'snippet': 'Sarah Palin continued her bus tour of historic sites with a visit to a Gettysburg battlefield. She also continued her manipulation of the news media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GETTYSBURG, Pa. — Sarah Palin took a brief tour of the Gettysburg battlefield and cemetery Tuesday morning as she and her family continued their “One Nation” tour of historical sites.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palin Ditches Press and Tours Battlefield', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9117ccab-b71d-551c-bbb3-138b46c03682', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9117ccab-b71d-551c-bbb3-138b46c03682'}, {'abstract': 'A critique of grammar, style and usage in The Times. This week: riffing on a narrative.', 'web_url': 'https://topics.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/more-words-we-love-too-much/', 'snippet': 'A critique of grammar, style and usage in The Times. This week: riffing on a narrative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Words We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35352890-2172-515a-966b-9c6ec33776c0', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35352890-2172-515a-966b-9c6ec33776c0'}, {'abstract': 'A critique of grammar, style and usage in The Times. This week: riffing on a narrative.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/more-words-we-love-too-much/', 'snippet': 'A critique of grammar, style and usage in The Times. This week: riffing on a narrative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Words We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5f4b44f-7eec-53a8-b044-7622c05c2a3b', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f4b44f-7eec-53a8-b044-7622c05c2a3b'}, {'abstract': 'A reader’s view on why Barcelona dominates the midfield against opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/one-last-note-on-barcelonas-midfield-mastery/', 'snippet': 'A reader’s view on why Barcelona dominates the midfield against opponents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Kennedy is a Goal blog reader and a video producer whose credits include the Purple States series that ran on nytimes.com in 2008. He’s also a former college soccer player who wrote in with an interesting take on Barcelona’s success in the Champions League final.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Last Note on Barcelona’s Midfield Mastery', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FC Barcelona', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T14:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/771dd365-3310-5822-9cd7-80236e5d71fa', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/771dd365-3310-5822-9cd7-80236e5d71fa'}, {'abstract': 'A designer realized she needed a new branding and sales strategy when a chain’s buyer sent an e-mail saying the chain was dropping her Go GaGa’s bags.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/using-public-relations-to-drive-demand/', 'snippet': 'A designer realized she needed a new branding and sales strategy when a chain’s buyer sent an e-mail saying the chain was dropping her Go GaGa’s bags.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jill Cartwright hatched the idea for Go GaGa, an online retailer of bags used to tote everything from baby gear to camera equipment, while earning her M.B.A. at Babson. She graduated and started the company in 2007. That fall, she attended trade shows ABC Kids Expo, ENK Children’s Club, and New York International Gift Fair. She emerged with pre-orders and began producing her products, which she says are differentiated by an ergonomically safe strap, in January, 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Public Relations to Drive Demand', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b6edb98-160b-526b-9dfa-82fcdc33d39b', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b6edb98-160b-526b-9dfa-82fcdc33d39b'}, {'abstract': 'Men and women tend to have different responses to various emotional expressions in the opposite sex.', 'web_url': 'https://brooks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/expressive-attraction/', 'snippet': 'Men and women tend to have different responses to various emotional expressions in the opposite sex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day Kevin Lewis, who covers the social sciences for National Affairs and the Boston Globe, blasts out an email of wonky goodness—a collection of 10 to 20 study abstracts. Last Saturday’s was particularly rich. He sent out the abstract of a study by Jessica Tracy and Alex Beall from a forthcoming issue of Emotion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expressive Attraction', 'kicker': 'David Brooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Globe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:02:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5781e0a4-ca42-5495-b296-47d12343aac3', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5781e0a4-ca42-5495-b296-47d12343aac3'}, {'abstract': 'A former member of Saddam Hussein’s intelligence service was arrested in the assassination of Ali Faisal al-Lami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/middleeast/01briefs-Iraqarrest.html', 'snippet': 'A former member of Saddam Hussein’s intelligence service was arrested in the assassination of Ali Faisal al-Lami.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A former member of Saddam Hussein’s intelligence service was arrested in the assassination of Ali Faisal al-Lami, left, a politician who oversaw efforts to purge scores of candidates from national ballots because of ties to the former government, the Iraqi police announced Tuesday. They said the suspect was arrested in the Taji area north of Baghdad but did not release his name or provide any evidence tying him to the killing. Mr. Lami, a Shiite Muslim, was gunned down Thursday night as he drove through Baghdad, becoming one of the most prominent victims of an assassination campaign aimed at security forces and government officials. As the head of Iraq’s Accountability and Justice Commission, Mr. Lami played a central role in last year’s politically divisive attempt to bar a number of candidates, many of them Sunnis, from parliamentary elections. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Arrest in Killing of Anti-Baathist Politician', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Arrest in Killing of Anti-Baathist Politician', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lami, Ali Faisal al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36203a0-fcb5-5c86-b258-fa1930a894e5', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36203a0-fcb5-5c86-b258-fa1930a894e5'}, {'abstract': 'Fixing our health care system will be impossible without a larger pool of competent primary care doctors. One way to increase the number of primary care doctors is to make medical school free.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/should-medical-school-be-free/', 'snippet': 'Fixing our health care system will be impossible without a larger pool of competent primary care doctors. One way to increase the number of primary care doctors is to make medical school free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can free medical school help fix the American health care system? In this weekend’s opinion section, two physicians, Dr. Peter B. Bach and Dr. Robert Kocher, propose that it can.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Medical School Be Free?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:17:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/936e88b3-48a9-57c6-aed6-5a0e8013de9c', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/936e88b3-48a9-57c6-aed6-5a0e8013de9c'}, {'abstract': 'Francesca Schiavone, the defending French Open champion, pulled out a 1-6, 7-5, 7-5 victory over Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/schiavone-recovers-and-outlasts-pavlyuchenkova/', 'snippet': 'Francesca Schiavone, the defending French Open champion, pulled out a 1-6, 7-5, 7-5 victory over Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — It took Francesca Schiavone of Italy 21 minutes to get on the scoreboard at Roland Garros, almost enough time for Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova of Russia to run away with the match – but not quite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schiavone Recovers and Outlasts Pavlyuchenkova', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiavone, Francesca', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:22:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f345c3eb-e21d-5bc5-8837-531f75b3bba9', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f345c3eb-e21d-5bc5-8837-531f75b3bba9'}, {'abstract': 'Berlin investigators said a painting bought by Mr. Martin in 2004 and sold in 2006 and attributed to the modernist Heinrich Campendonk was probably the handiwork of a forgery ring that operated for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/forged-painting-was-once-in-collection-of-steve-martin-german-police-say/', 'snippet': 'Berlin investigators said a painting bought by Mr. Martin in 2004 and sold in 2006 and attributed to the modernist Heinrich Campendonk was probably the handiwork of a forgery ring that operated for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:28 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forged Painting Was Once in Collection of Steve Martin, German Police Say', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Der Spiegel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da