nal': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae10682e-7be7-56e0-8c48-447c7b2f2d0b', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae10682e-7be7-56e0-8c48-447c7b2f2d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Since the wedding season is upon us, I thought it would be a good time to chat wedding day beauty.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/face-time-lela-rose/', 'snippet': 'Since the wedding season is upon us, I thought it would be a good time to chat wedding day beauty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tina Turnbow is a professional makeup artist, who is known for lending her celebrity clients editorial polish. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Lela Rose', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e38f54b-1005-5047-9f2a-44092c87e30a', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e38f54b-1005-5047-9f2a-44092c87e30a'}, {'abstract': 'When did the end of the school year become a marathon of activity?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/the-end-of-school-year-scramble/', 'snippet': 'When did the end of the school year become a marathon of activity?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the conversation on Motherlode last week about how some parenting norms differ by neighborhood, many of you mentioned relationships with teachers. In some school districts, it is expected that parents will be present for all school activities; at others a parent who shows up too often is seen as pushy. In some places showering the teacher with end of year gifts is expected; elsewhere, is it frowned upon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The End-of-School-Year Scramble', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Belkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77a7483-4883-5bad-a7ac-bcdcdaf35a69', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77a7483-4883-5bad-a7ac-bcdcdaf35a69'}, {'abstract': 'Papaya King has landed in Los Angeles, a city that might be as crazy and competitive about food as New York is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/us/01papayaking.html', 'snippet': 'Papaya King has landed in Los Angeles, a city that might be as crazy and competitive about food as New York is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOLLYWOOD — It is tucked in a storefront a block from the Walk of Fame, walking distance from the annual Academy Awards ceremonies, and steps from the hubbub of tourists, hucksters and celebrity hunters that is Hollywood: a Papaya King hot dog stand, in all its garish yellow and orange glory, selling hot dogs imported straight from the Bronx.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0