ppointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Locke, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:41:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97afe4c7-4657-55ee-8b08-ffc649efb19f', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97afe4c7-4657-55ee-8b08-ffc649efb19f'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian police on Tuesday arrested Rustam Makhmudov, the man they suspect of shooting the journalist Anna Politkovskaya in 2006.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/europe/01russia.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian police on Tuesday arrested Rustam Makhmudov, the man they suspect of shooting the journalist Anna Politkovskaya in 2006.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Russian authorities on Tuesday arrested the man they suspect of shooting the journalist Anna Politkovskaya, whose apparent contract killing in 2006 sent a chilling message about the hazards of challenging the powerful in contemporary Russia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Held in ’06 Killing of Journalist in Moscow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect Held In ’06 Killing Of Journalist In Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Politkovskaya, Anna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:43:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bdf9782-623f-5952-bc50-d7b05c0560dd', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bdf9782-623f-5952-bc50-d7b05c0560dd'}, {'abstract': 'A group of mostly New York photographers are creating an archive of their work.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/kamoinge-photographers-convey-black-experience/', 'snippet': 'A group of mostly New York photographers are creating an archive of their work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kamoinge, a group of mostly New York photographers who strive to capture the black experience, are creating an archive of their work. The group first assembled in 1963 and now has 24 members, with some focusing on documentary work, others on fine art. They are all driven by a similar passion: honest portrayal. “What we’re documenting isn’t just black history,” said Russell Frederick, one of Kamoinge’s newer members. “It’s American history; it’s global history. It’s something that everybody needs to see.” Read and see more on the Lens blog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kamoinge Photographers Convey Black Experience', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T15:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2954a4ce-6805-511e-8924-a35d3191eb14', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2954a4ce-6805-511e-8924-a35d3191eb14'}, {'abstract': 'When Jean-Claude Trichet’s role as president of the European Central Bank ends, he will leave behind a more prominent institution and a difficult legacy for his successor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/business/global/01trichet.html', 'snippet': 'When Jean-Claude Trichet’s role as president of the European Central Bank ends, he will leave behind a more prominent institution and a difficult legacy for his successor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Since Europe’s debt crisis became acute last year, the European Central Bank has gone beyond its role as arbiter of monetary policy to become in effect the adult supervision for quarreling heads of government. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/global/01trichet-span/01trichet-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/business/global/01trichet-span/01trichet-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/business/global/01trichet-span/01trichet-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trichet to Leave a Difficult Legacy at Central Bank', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rescue Package for Greece Takes Shape: Trichet to Leave a Difficult Legacy at Central Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value':