a120045ce', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/521fde96-28bf-58ea-aef3-a5aa120045ce'}, {'abstract': 'The cellphone giant is battling to maintain its position in the face of competition from the iPhone and Android.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/technology/01nokia.html', 'snippet': 'The cellphone giant is battling to maintain its position in the face of competition from the iPhone and Android.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nokia, the cellphone giant battling to maintain its position in the face of competition from the iPhone and Android, said Tuesday that it was abandoning its 2011 profit targets after an unexpectedly poor second-quarter showing. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nokia Lowers Second-Quarter Forecast and Abandons 2011 Profit Goals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nokia Lowers Second-Quarter Forecast and Abandons 2011 Profit Goals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T17:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e02424-48e2-5e7f-a123-3c2de31308e4', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9e02424-48e2-5e7f-a123-3c2de31308e4'}, {'abstract': 'Part 1 of Peter Jackson’s fantasy epic, called “The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey,” will be released in 2012 on the birthday of Nostradamus, while Part 2, called “The Hobbit: There and Back Again,” will be released on Friday the 13th in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/what-hobbit-curse-jacksons-movies-get-star-crossed-release-dates/', 'snippet': 'Part 1 of Peter Jackson’s fantasy epic, called “The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey,” will be released in 2012 on the birthday of Nostradamus, while Part 2, called “The Hobbit: There and Back Again,” will be released on Friday the 13th in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As if to prove that there are no supernatural forces working against Peter Jackson’s “Hobbit” movies, for which that director has already contended with a labor dispute, the occasional explosion and emergency ulcer surgery, the studios have settled on some interesting release dates for the two-part fantasy epic. New Line Cinema, Warner Brothers and Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer said in a joint statement reported by The Associated Press that the first “Hobbit” movie would open on Dec. 14, 2012, when some scholars say is the 509th anniversary of the birth of Nostradamus, the French astrologer and soothsayer. (Historical spoilsports say he was born on Dec. 21.) And the concluding “Hobbit” film will be released on Dec. 13, 2013, a date that not only has two 13s but is also, wouldn’t you know it, Friday the 13th. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What ‘Hobbit’ Curse? Jackson’s Movies Get Star-Crossed Release Dates', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'v