glacier considered the world’s highest battlefield.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The slow, uncertain efforts to normalize relations between India and Pakistan apparently made little progress on Tuesday, after defense secretaries from both countries failed to deliver a breakthrough on demilitarizing a Himalayan glacier considered the world’s highest battlefield.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/INDIA/INDIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'India and Pakistan Fail to Resolve Glacier Dispute at Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India and Pakistan Fail to Resolve Glacier Dispute at Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T18:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76c6850a-7434-5ca1-b4bc-9bffe987291a', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76c6850a-7434-5ca1-b4bc-9bffe987291a'}, {'abstract': 'The sale of the franchise to True North Sports and Entertainment was announced Tuesday at a news conference in Winnipeg, Manitoba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/sports/hockey/atlanta-loses-thrashers-as-nhl-returns-to-winnipeg.html', 'snippet': 'The sale of the franchise to True North Sports and Entertainment was announced Tuesday at a news conference in Winnipeg, Manitoba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 15 years, the N.H.L. is returning to Winnipeg. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/hockey/01thrasherspic/01thrasherspic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/hockey/01thrasherspic/01thrasherspic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/sports/hockey/01thrasherspic/01thrasherspic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlanta Loses Thrashers as N.H.L. Returns to Winnipeg', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winnipeg Becomes Thrashers’ New Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Thrashers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winnipeg Jets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T18:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccd863a-6ef9-5568-ab85-1fec6ebfb0e7', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccd863a-6ef9-5568-ab85-1fec6ebfb0e7'}, {'abstract': 'There is a link between a woman’s menstrual cycle and her perception of sexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://brooks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/the-moons-tide/', 'snippet': 'There is a link between a woman’s menstrual cycle and her perception of sexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study by Jeffry Rudski, Lauren Bernstein and Joy Mitchell in the Archives of Sexual Behavior studied the link between the menstrual cycle and perception. Female research subjects were asked to react to various Georgia O’Keeffe paintings. Nearly a third of the women in the first half of their monthly cycle discerned sexual themes in her paintings, while only 6 percent of the women in the second half of their cycle did. Women who were taking oral contraceptives saw the paintings the same way throughout the month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moon’s Tide', 'kicker': 'David Brooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T18:37:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1cfaf2-b52c-51b6-919c-cc7574c3fe20', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1cfaf2-b52c-51b6-919c-cc7574c3fe20'}, {'abstract': 'The two sides have agreed to a preliminary arrangement on demilitarizing the border between them, though some officials from both sides immediately expressed skepticism of the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/world/africa/01sudan.html', 'snippet': 'The two sides have agreed to a preliminary arrangement on demilitarizing the border between them, though some officials from both sides immediately expressed skepticism of the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUBA, Sudan — Northern and southern Sudanese officials have agreed to a preliminary arrangement on demilitarizing the border between them, the African Union said Tuesday, though some officials from both sides immediately expressed skepticism of the deal, particularly its ability to resolve the dispute over the contested Abyei area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North and South Sudan Tentatively Agree to Demilitarize Disputed Border', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North and South Sudan Tentatively Agree to Demilitarize Disputed Border', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T18:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6fa9246-b754-5624-bf6c-8a563c2daf61', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6fa9246-b754-5624-bf6c-8a563c2daf61'}, {'abstract': 'Whites are least open to dating outside their racial group.', 'web_url': 'https://brooks.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/race-and-dating/', 'snippet': 'Whites are least open to dating outside their racial group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Internet dating is fertile territory for people who study social patterns. Belinda Robnett and Cynthia Feliciano studied racial exclusion patterns in the Journal Social Forces. They looked at over 6000 internet dating profiles and found that whites are least open to dating outside their group, with Asians and Latinos close behind. Asian males and black females are more highly excluded than their opposite sex counterparts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Race and Dating', 'kicker': 'David Brooks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T18:41:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eba608a-e1d4-5053-a1b6-336e64bb8194', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eba608a-e1d4-5053-a1b6-336e64bb8194'}, {'abstract': 'The deal being discussed would offer billions of euros in