ve effectively ended the long run of gag-heavy comedies like “Ace Ventura: Pet Detective” and “Zoolander” (to pick two at random). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There Is No Sheep at the Table: What Exactly Is a Jokeless Comedy?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'APATOW, JUDD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrell, Will', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKay, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudd, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samberg, Andy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Owen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T19:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92406b89-a01d-5483-b9e5-89071f6a812f', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92406b89-a01d-5483-b9e5-89071f6a812f'}, {'abstract': 'Our lessons are on summer vacation, but here’s a look back at social studies-related lessons from the 2010-11 school year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/year-end-round-up-social-studies-history-geography-and-civics-2/', 'snippet': 'Our lessons are on summer vacation, but here’s a look back at social studies-related lessons from the 2010-11 school year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The school year is drawing to a close, and our lesson plans have already gone on summer vacation. So this week we’re looking back at the 2010-11 school year and collecting the year’s teaching materials by subject matter, starting today with social studies, American history and civics, global history, economics and geography. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Year-End Roundup | Social Studies, History, Geography and Civics', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T19:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8ae2640-5223-5311-9636-d48c37048c8b', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8ae2640-5223-5311-9636-d48c37048c8b'}, {'abstract': 'A new ad screening on European television highlights the French automaker’s efforts to bring electric vehicles to market.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/a-day-in-the-unelectrified-life-by-renault/', 'snippet': 'A new ad screening on European television highlights the French automaker’s efforts to bring electric vehicles to market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlos Tavares, the former Nissan Americas head, recently was named the new chief operating officer at Renault. Along with Renault-Nissan chairman Carlos Ghosn, Mr. Tavares has been an outspoken proponent of electric vehicles, appearing at various conferences to tout the Nissan Leaf E.V. and sound the trumpet for strengthening private and public outlays for E.V. infrastructure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day in the Unelectrified Life, by Renault', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'na