n were tied with Rohan Bopanna of India and Aisam-Ul-Haq Qureshi of Pakistan, 5-5 in the third set, when the match was postponed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — French Open officials postponed a quarterfinal men’s doubles match because of darkness on Tuesday night with Bob and Mike Bryan of the United States tied at 5-5 in the third set with Rohan Bopanna of India and Aisam-Ul-Haq Qureshi of Pakistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Darkness Postpones Bryans’ Match in Final Set', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bopanna, Rohan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lipsky, Seth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Llodra, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirnyi, Max', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nestor, Daniel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qureshi, Aisam-Ul-Haq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ram, Rajeev', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimonjic, Nenad', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T20:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac4f42b-a380-5bef-bc33-7d4562de0147', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac4f42b-a380-5bef-bc33-7d4562de0147'}, {'abstract': 'Courts in West Virginia and Delaware refused to block a vote on Massey Energy’s $7.1 billion sale to Alpha Natural Resources, one day ahead of the shareholder meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/court-allows-vote-on-massey-sale-to-proceed/', 'snippet': 'Courts in West Virginia and Delaware refused to block a vote on Massey Energy’s $7.1 billion sale to Alpha Natural Resources, one day ahead of the shareholder meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:25 p.m. | Updated Delaware’s court of chancery also declined to bar the Massey energy shareholder vote scheduled for Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Allows Vote on Massey Sale to Proceed', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alpha Natural Resources Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massey Energy Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Upper Big Branch Mine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T20:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/052c518f-f6a1-5d9d-a222-e1e89fac3828', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/052c518f-f6a1-5d9d-a222-e1e89fac3828'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater seems to be experiencing an unusual rush of real romance.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/at-ballet-theater-popping-the-question-after-the-plie/', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater seems to be experiencing an unusual rush of real romance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it’s the influence of all those story ballets, where love mostly triumphs (at least when no-one is dying young and becoming a Wili). American Ballet Theater seems to be experiencing an unusual rush of real romance, with three engagements over the last two weeks. On the opening night of the season, Ethan Stiefel proposed to his longtime girlfriend Gillian Murphy on the stage of the Metropolitan Opera House, moments after she and her partner David Hallberg had taken their curtain calls for the “Tchaikovsky Pas de Deux.” A few days later, the about-to-retire Cuban star Jose Manuel Carreño and corps de ballet dancer Melanie Hamrick announced their engagement. And on Friday, which happened to be the 30th birthday of the Royal Ballet guest artist Alina Cojocaru, her longtime on-and-offstage partner Johan Kobborg (who had arrived unexpectedly to fill in for the injured Maxim Beloserkovsky at the Saturday matinee of “Giselle”) popped the question. \xa0Perhaps Alexei Ratmansky will choreograph a wedding dance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Ballet Theater, Popping the Question After the Plié', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cojocaru, Alina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Gillian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiefel, Ethan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T20:52:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bb22bc3-0525-597d-9579-3843d10d4dea', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bb22bc3-0525-597d-9579-3843d10d4dea'}, {'abstract': 'Is Representative Paul Ryan’s budget plan unpopular?', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/republicans-may-need-exit-strategy-from-medicare-plan/', 'snippet': 'Is Representative Paul Ryan’s budget plan unpopular?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is Representative Paul Ryan’s budget plan unpopular?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans May Need ‘Exit Strategy’ From Medicare Plan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T20:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cada0ef5-cabd-558c-8d03-1c80319d5eda', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cada0ef5-cabd-558c-8d03-1c80319d5eda'}, {'abstract': 'In the span of 20 minutes, Francesca Schiavone transformed herself from inconsistent and tentative to confident and bold against Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/analysis-schiavones-comeback/', 'snippet': 'In the span of 20 minutes, Francesca Schiavone transformed herself from inconsistent and tentative to confident and bold against Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I watched Francesca Schiavone claw her way back into the second set against Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova, I remembered a story I’d heard about Allen Fox, the legendary coach and tennis guru who helped develop Brad Gilbert at Pepperdine. Fox would tell his players to persevere when they were struggling in a match, and to believe that if they just kept battling, their level of play would almost certainly rise. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis: Schiavone’s Comeback', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f77d9c9-1537-54f8-868d-712132cf9139', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f77d9c9-1537-54f8-868d-712132cf9139'}, {'abstract': 'Can a Broadway flop be resurrected Off Broadway?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/a-date-for-the-prom-carrie-sets-key-casting-and-first-performance-off-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Can a Broadway flop be resurrected Off Broadway?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a year of work, MCC Theater’s stab at salvaging the musical “Carrie” from the Broadway flop hall of shame is far enough along that the company announced on Tuesday that it will produce the show next season, with preview performances set to begin Off Broadway on Jan. 31, 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Date for the Prom: ‘Carrie’ Sets Key Casting and First Performance Off Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1a02228-1f66-5c81-89af-42393cdd0e90', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1a02228-1f66-5c81-89af-42393cdd0e90'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the comptroller’s office says there was poor follow-through on reports that apartments with young children were missing the guards.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/city-is-faulted-on-enforcement-of-window-guards/', 'snippet': 'A report from the comptroller’s office says there was poor follow-through on reports that apartments with young children were missing the guards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An audit by the New York City comptroller’s office has found deficiencies in the city’s window-guard enforcement program, which prevents children from falling through open windows. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Is Faulted on Enforcement of Window Guards', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Windows', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Housing Preservation and Development (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8aa5687-e4e2-5867-85c6-533355d748c5', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8aa5687-e4e2-5867-85c6-533355d748c5'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary makes the case that the feminist art movement has been more influential than is generally acknowledged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/movies/women-art-revolution-by-lynn-hershman-leeson-review.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary makes the case that the feminist art movement has been more influential than is generally acknowledged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can you name three female artists? The people asked that question outside the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art and the Whitney Museum of American Art can’t get much beyond Frida You-Know-Who-I-Mean. That’s old, sad news to Lynn Hershman Leeson, the director of “!Women Art Revolution” — “!W.A.R.” — a documentary history of the feminist art movement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/WOMEN1/WOMEN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enhancing the Image of Feminist Art', 'kicker': "Movie Review | '!Women Art Revolution'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enhancing the Image of Feminist Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Feminist Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leeson, Lynn Hershman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saar, Betye', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spero, Nancy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosler, Martha', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneemann, Carolee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chicago, Judy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb9f14ab-fe6a-540b-93c6-09f755705b25', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb9f14ab-fe6a-540b-93c6-09f755705b25'}, {'abstract': 'The Verde Island Passage in the Philippines lives up to its reputation: the ocean vibrates with the cycles of living things inhabiting every nook and cranny.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/life-at-the-edge-of-the-verde-island-passage/', 'snippet': 'The Verde Island Passage in the Philippines lives up to its reputation: the ocean vibrates with the cycles of living things inhabiting every nook and cranny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rich Mooi, curator of invertebrate zoology and geology at the California Academy of Sciences, writes from the Philippines, where he is surveying echinoderms off the coast of Luzon Island.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life at the Edge of the Verde Island Passage', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rich Mooi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rich', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mooi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79b0fa00-331a-55c6-ae0d-b79e8381d47a', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79b0fa00-331a-55c6-ae0d-b79e8381d47a'}, {'abstract': 'Intact Financial, which is already Canada’s largest property and casualty insurer, said the acquisition of the AXA business would increase its total premiums by 2 billion Canadian dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/intact-financial-to-buy-axas-canadian-unit/', 'snippet': 'Intact Financial, which is already Canada’s largest property and casualty insurer, said the acquisition of the AXA business would increase its total premiums by 2 billion Canadian dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Intact Financial Corporation, the big Toronto-based insurer, said Tuesday that it had agreed to buy the Canadian insurance operation of the AXA Group of Paris for 2.6 billion Canadian dollars in cash ($2.68 billion).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intact Financial to Buy AXA’s Canadian Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AXA GROUP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:05:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2002cf52-925d-53d3-92ca-dca35b3a57c1', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2002cf52-925d-53d3-92ca-dca35b3a57c1'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art said Tuesday that its Alexander McQueen show, which it recently extended by a week to accommodate the overflow crowds, would be opened during special viewing hours on Mondays, when the Met is usually closed, for patrons willing to buy $50 tickets.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/met-museum-to-add-hours-charge-50-to-accommodate-mcqueen-show-crowds/', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Museum of Art said Tuesday that its Alexander McQueen show, which it recently extended by a week to accommodate the overflow crowds, would be opened during special viewing hours on Mondays, when the Met is usually closed, for patr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'High fashion and money have always gone together, and for the next few weeks, they will do so in the museum world as well as on the racks. The Metropolitan Museum of Art said Tuesday that its Alexander McQueen show, which it recently extended by a week to accommodate the overflow crowds, will be opened during special viewing hours on Mondays, when the Met is usually closed, for patrons willing to buy $50 tickets.', 'so