t': 'In a statement full of emotion, the woman who accused two police officers of rape said of the jury’s decision to acquit: “Hearing that verdict brought me to my knees.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The woman who accused two New York City police officers of rape released a statement on Tuesday expressing her disappointment in the jury’s verdict. The officers were acquitted of rape, but were convicted of three counts of official misconduct for entering her apartment. What follows is the statement from the woman, who requested that her name not be used:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman in Rape Case Says Verdict Left Her ‘Devastated’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balbert, Coleen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:38:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd05760-e223-5f08-92cb-7f674853810f', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd05760-e223-5f08-92cb-7f674853810f'}, {'abstract': 'Ike Davis, the Mets’ first baseman, must wear a protective boot on his injured ankle for another three weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/daviss-return-from-injury-delayed/', 'snippet': 'Ike Davis, the Mets’ first baseman, must wear a protective boot on his injured ankle for another three weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First baseman Ike Davis had a setback in his recovery from a bone bruise in his left ankle when a foot specialist told him Tuesday to wear a protective boot for another three weeks, meaning his return to the Mets is at least a month away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Davis’s Return From Injury Delayed', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T21:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b58e4f-fd78-5258-ba28-b97bf224b662', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b58e4f-fd78-5258-ba28-b97bf224b662'}, {'abstract': 'Broadway had another billion-dollar season between late May 2010 and Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/how-to-succeed-in-show-business-broadway-season-box-office-up-nearly-6-percent/', 'snippet': 'Broadway had another billion-dollar season between late May 2010 and Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway had another billion-dollar season between late May 2010 and Sunday, with shows grossing $1.08 billion — 5.9 percent more than the total for the 2009-10 season — and playing to more than 12.5 million people, according to the Broadway League, the trade group for theater owners and producers. That 2010-11 season attendance figure also reflects an increase of 5.4 percent over the previous season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Succeed in (Show) Business: Broadway Season Box Office Up Nearly 6 Percent', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name