': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78f17c88-62cd-5ce7-ab3f-174de0080574', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78f17c88-62cd-5ce7-ab3f-174de0080574'}, {'abstract': 'For his fall collection, the designer Jeremy Laing collaborated with the artist Scott Treleaven to create a pagan, slightly macabre spirit in his clothes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/lunar-expedition/', 'snippet': 'For his fall collection, the designer Jeremy Laing collaborated with the artist Scott Treleaven to create a pagan, slightly macabre spirit in his clothes.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We first met in Toronto, friends of friends, met on the scene, you know?” says the designer Jeremy Laing, referring to the artist Scott Treleaven. Laing is no stranger to the artist collaboration — in past seasons he worked with Karen Azoulay and also the band Grizzly Bear. For his fall collection (hitting stores this month), he and Trevleavan generated two different prints — a flaming hand and a moon — that will come in the form of silk jersey T-shirt and a slinky silk crepe dress. “Jeremy was in a mood of luminance and transformation, which coincided perfectly,” says Treleaven. “We were both seeing these circle patterns and lunar imagery.” The rest of the collection is a more subtle riff on the theme with crater-etched sweaters, voluminous wide-leg trousers and a black velvet sheath dress – albeit in the same pagan, slightly macabre spirit. “I really appreciate the collaborative process; it’s a great way to keep engaged and grasp onto someone else’s creativity,” Laing says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lunar Expedition', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T22:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person':