ent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who derive pleasure from meticulously organizing things — in this case, an iTunes music collection — will be pleased to know that TuneUp, a provider of add-ons for Apple’s music-management software, has added “DeDuper” to its suite of wares.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TuneUp’s DeDuper Finds Duplicate Tracks in iTunes', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T22:40:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/442a4126-b074-5b9e-b923-d5f559890cc1', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/442a4126-b074-5b9e-b923-d5f559890cc1'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the restaurant at the Gotham Hotel in Midtown, which Sam Sifton reviews this week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/reviewing-tenpenny/', 'snippet': 'A look at the restaurant at the Gotham Hotel in Midtown, which Sam Sifton reviews this week.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing Tenpenny', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gotham Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}]