 2008 suggests that other states take politics seriously, too.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2011/05/31/new-hampshire-is-not-unique/', 'snippet': 'Vastly increased voter turnout in 2008 suggests that other states take politics seriously, too.', 'lead_paragraph': ' I imagine that I may hear from a few people in New Hampshire and Iowa, in response to my column arguing for a different primary schedule. Someone may point out, accurately, that New Hampshire had the highest primary-voter turnout of any state in 2008 — 53.6 percent, according to the United States Elections Project at George Mason University. (Iowa, a caucus state, had a turnout of only 16.1 percent.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire Is Not Unique', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T22:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6b998e3-058a-5de9-bff9-a8633bb40657', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6b998e3-058a-5de9-bff9-a8633bb40657'}, {'abstract': 'Vancouver, seeking its first championship in its 40th season, and Boston, chasing its first title since 1972, begin the Stanley Cup finals on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/sports/hockey/for-either-canucks-or-bruins-four-decades-of-waiting-is-about-to-end.html', 'snippet': 'Vancouver, seeking its first championship in its 40th season, and Boston, chasing its first title since 1972, begin the Stanley Cup finals on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Stanley Cup finals get under way Wednesday, and two great hockey cities on opposite ends of the continent — Boston and Vancouver, British Columbia — are going full throttle in support of their teams. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Either Canucks or Bruins, Four Decades of Waiting Is About to End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Either Canucks or Bruins, Four Decades of Waiting Is About to End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T23:34:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c34926-b1e5-5124-91f7-a6b69ffc9ae2', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c34926-b1e5-5124-91f7-a6b69ffc9ae2'}, {'abstract': 'From the standpoint of presence and productivity, Todd English is one of the most successful chefs in the country. But in the media, he is one of the most mocked and hounded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/dining/todd-english-the-chef-in-motion.html', 'snippet': 'From the standpoint of presence and productivity, Todd English is one of the most successful chefs in the country. But in the media, he is one of the most mocked and hounded.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A GUY like Todd’s got 60 things going on his head,” Richard Henriksen said. “So a workout clears the mind a bit.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/11english-span/11english-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/11english-span/11english-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/11english-span/COVERENGLISH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/11english-span/11english-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/11english-span/11english-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Todd English, the Chef in Motion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Chef in Motion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'English, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T23:35:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gor