ia artists in painting, sculpture, photography, drawing, collage, film and video and installation art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2011/06/01/arts/design/GREAT.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition of 100 works by nearly 50 Southern California artists in painting, sculpture, photography, drawing, collage, film and video and installation art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An exhibition of 100 works by nearly 50 Southern California artists in painting, sculpture, photography, drawing, collage, film and video and installation art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/design/GREAT-slide-MTBU/GREAT-slide-MTBU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/design/GREAT-slide-MTBU/GREAT-slide-MTBU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/design/GREAT-slide-MTBU/GREAT-slide-MTBU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Greater LA’ in SoHo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T23:36:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c53dd851-f771-57c9-9a71-9d492c96ae2b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c53dd851-f771-57c9-9a71-9d492c96ae2b'}, {'abstract': '“Greater LA” brings a hint of the Southern California art scene to a loft in SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/arts/design/greater-la-california-artists-in-a-soho-loft-review.html', 'snippet': '“Greater LA” brings a hint of the Southern California art scene to a loft in SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who take things into their own hands and try to operate outside the institutional grid deserve our gratitude. So hats off to the organizers of “Greater LA,” a sprawling survey of recent art from Los Angeles arrayed in an immense, unrepentantly raw SoHo loft. It represents a tremendous effort on the part of three temporarily allied art professionals: Benjamin Godsill, a curator moonlighting from the New Museum; Joel Mesler, a partner in Untitled, an art gallery on the Lower East Side who began his art-dealing career in Los Angeles; and Eleanor Cayre, a New York collector and consultant who organized “The Station,” a large group show in Miami during the Basel Miami art fair in 2008.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/GREATER/GREATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/GREATER/GREATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/GREATER/GREATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/GREATER/GREATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/arts/GREATER/GREATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bit of Hollywood, Minus the Tinsel', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bit of Hollywood, Minus the Tinsel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T23:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/95cf4f5d-2c7b-55d1-aac5-9456bc959c51', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95cf4f5d-2c7b-55d1-aac5-9456bc959c51'}, {'abstract': 'The offshoot of Sorella, the restaurant next door, offers savory dishes in addition to its handmade gelato, but the long white marble bar feels more like an ice cream parlor than a lunch counter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/dining/reviews/stellina-nyc-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'The offshoot of Sorella, the restaurant next door, offers savory dishes in addition to its handmade gelato, but the long white marble bar feels more like an ice cream parlor than a lunch counter.', 'lead_paragraph': '95 Allen Street (Delancey Street); (212) 274-9555; stellinanyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stellina-span/01stellina-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop