euvres are suitable for summer cocktails. These are followed by soups, salads, pastas, one-pot stews, fish pies and tarts, an intriguing collections of curry recipes from various Asian sources, and dishes grouped by technique: frying, baking, roasting, poaching, broiling and grilling. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-book/01stuff-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-book/01stuff-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-book/01stuff-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-book/01stuff-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-book/01stuff-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seafood: Read All About It, and How to Cook It', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seafood: Read All About It, and How to Cook It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2011-05-31T23:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0ba273-421b-58d3-9a52-6a9cdb573b69', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0ba273-421b-58d3-9a52-6a9cdb573b69'}, {'abstract': 'A knife for watermelon may not be necessary, but the Kuhn Rikon knife is functional and fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2011/06/01/dining/pink-and-green-and-just-to-cut-watermelon.html', 'snippet': 'A knife for watermelon may not be necessary, but the Kuhn Rikon knife is functional and fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You do not need a special knife for watermelon, but this one, with a watermelon-pink blade and a green handle, is as functional as it is fun. The blade is long (11 inches) and serrated to cut through the rind and the fruit. The little perforations that look like seeds and the blade’s bright silicone coating make slicing effortless. The knife comes in a matching sheath. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-watermelon/01stuff-watermelon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-watermelon/01stuff-watermelon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-watermelon/01stuff-watermelon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/01/dining/01stuff-watermelon/01stuff-watermelon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda